     gene            complement(10643..11356)
                     /gene="yaaW"
                     /locus_tag="b0011"
                     /label=yaaW
     CDS             complement(10643..11356)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yaaW"
                     /locus_tag="b0011"
                     /product="putative enzyme-specific chaperone YaaW"
                     /label=yaaW
                     /note="Mutagenesis experiments performed to study the 
                     <i>htgA</i> open reading frame on the opposite strand 
                     indicated
                     that HtgA may play a role in the regulation of the heat 
                     shock response |CITS: [8478327]|.  However, all mutagenesis
                     experiments disrupted both <i>htgA</i> and <i>yaaW</i>. 
                     Experiments using the <i>E. coli</i> O157:H7 EDL933 
                     <i>yaaW</i> and <i>htgA</i> genes, which are more than 98% 
                     identical to those of <i>E. coli</i> K-12, are reported in 
                     |CITS: [24111745]|.  <i>yaaW</i> is most likely part of an 
                     <i>yaaIWH</i> operon.  Point mutants that selectively knock
                     out either <i>yaaW</i> or <i>htgA</i> were constructed and 
                     tested.  Neither mutant has a heat shock phenotype, and 
                     both mutants show somewhat increased biofilm formation in 
                     minimal medium after 48 hours |CITS: [24111745]|.
                     |CITS: [18226237]| have suggested that the antisense 
                     <i>htgA</i> ORF has originated through overprinting and 
                     have proposed the term ""janolog"" to describe such events.
                     "
