                     /note="IS1 is the smallest insertion sequence in <i>E.
                     coli</i>.  It codes for three proteins, InsA, InsB and 
                     InsAB'.
                     InsAB' is the transposase for IS1 |CITS: [8083181]|. Its 
                     translation depends on a -1 frameshift within the 3' end 
                     region of <i>insA</i> which allows translational 
                     readthrough
                     into <i>insB</i> |CITS: [2543983]|. In the absence of this 
                     frameshift, the IS1 transcriptional repressor protein InsA 
                     is produced instead |CITS: [2543983][8083181][9126837]|."
