     gene            complement(20815..21078)
                     /gene="rpsT"
                     /locus_tag="b0023"
                     /label=rpsT
     CDS             complement(20815..21078)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rpsT"
                     /locus_tag="b0023"
                     /product="trifunctional 30S ribosomal subunit protein S20
                     / 30S ribosomal subunit / ribosome"
                     /label=rpsT
                     /note="The S20 protein is a component of the 30S subunit
                     of the ribosome and appears to be involved in translation 
                     initiation and the association of the 30S and 50S subunits 
                     |CITS: [2207174]|.  S20 was also identified as antizyme 1, 
                     an inhibitor of the biosynthetic ornithine and arginine 
                     decarboxylases; these enzymes are involved in the 
                     biosynthesis of polyamine |CITS: [6392292]|.  S20 is 
                     identical to L26.
                     The synthesis of S20 is regulated at the 
                     post-transcriptional level |CITS: [6187728][7011813]|; in 
                     an <i>in vitro</i> system, S20 represses its own synthesis 
                     |CITS: [6960227]|.  However, S20 doesn't show affinity for 
                     its own mRNA |CITS: [2449659]|.  The UUG initiation codon 
                     appears to be important for regulation |CITS: [3286608]|. 
                     Processing and degradation of <i>rpsT</i> mRNA have been 
                     studied extensively; see for example |CITS: 
                     [12492855][10871599]| and references therein.  <i>rpsT</i> 
                     mRNA stability and translational efficiency are linked 
                     |CITS: [3286608][8106342]|.
                     S20 physically interacts with ornithine and arginine 
                     decarboxylase, and overexpression of S20 decreases the 
                     production of polyamine <i>in vivo</i> |CITS: [7539334]|. 
                     Levels of S20 increase in response to polyamines; the 
                     effect is thought to be due to an increase in the level of 
                     transcription of <i>rpsT</i> |CITS: [2185470]|.
                     S20 binds to the 5' domain and the 3' minor domain of 16S 
                     rRNA |CITS: [386275][3373529][7916699][1717450]|. 
                     C-terminal residues of S20 are required for binding to 16S 
                     rRNA |CITS: [2449659]|.  Hydroxyl radical footprinting 
                     provided evidence that S20 is located near the bottom of 
                     the 30S subunit |CITS: [9848646]|.  Further footprinting 
                     studies provided insight into 30S subunit assembly |CITS: 
                     [18155048]|.  S20 has a local effect on the stability of 
                     the folded structure of 16S rRNA |CITS: [19616559]|.
                     The <i>sup(S20)</i> mutation in <i>rpsT</i> suppresses 
                     defects of an alanyl-tRNA synthetase mutant
                     |CITS: [4614080][796681]|.  A spontaneous mutation in 
                     <i>rpsT</i> causes a temperature-sensitive phenotype and 
                     increases the ability of the ribosome to misread nonsense 
                     stop codons |CITS: [7683367]|.  An <i>rpsT</i> null mutant 
                     shows impaired growth, but is viable |CITS: [17277072]|.
                     A 30S ribosomal subunit lacking S20 shows a reduced rate of
                     mRNA binding and 70S complex formation |CITS: [20149799]|."
