     CDS             25207..25701
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="lspA"
                     /locus_tag="b0027"
                     /product="bifunctional lipoprotein signal peptidase / 
                     prolipoprotein signal peptidase"
                     /EC_number="3.4.23.36"
                     /label=lspA
                     /note="<i>lspA</i> encodes prolipoprotein signal peptidase 
                     (signal peptidase II) |CITS: [6227793][6374664][6373724]| -
                      an inner membrane endopeptidase that cleaves the signal 
                     peptide from glyceride modified prolipoproteins including 
                     |FRAME: EG10544-MONOMER|  |CITS: 
                     [6373799][6368552][3511052][6381496]|. Signal peptidase II 
                     requires a glyceride modified cysteine residue at the 
                     cleavage site |CITS: [11894915][6363408]|. The peptidic 
                     antibiotic, globomycin specifically inhibits signal 
                     peptidase II activity resulting in the accumulation of 
                     glyceride modified prolipoprotein in the inner membrane and
                     cell death |CITS: [6988430][3888977]|.
                     LspA has four predicted membrane-spanning hydrophobic 
                     segments |CITS: [6374664]|. LspA does not have an apparent 
                     signal peptide |CITS: [6374664][6378662]|. LspA contains 
                     four transmembrane domains and both termini are located in 
                     the cytoplasm |CITS: [1894646]|.
                     <i>lspA</i> is part of a five gene operon 
                     (<i>ribF-ileS-lspA-fkpB-ispH</i>) |CITS: [6374664][6373377 
                     ][6378662][2580835][2985604][2432063][3294831][26070674]|. 
                     Reviews: |CITS: [2202727][7674920]|"
