     gene            25826..26275
                     /gene="fkpB"
                     /locus_tag="b0028"
                     /label=fkpB
     CDS             25826..26275
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="fkpB"
                     /locus_tag="b0028"
                     /product="bifunctional peptidyl-prolyl cis-trans isomerase
                     FkpB / peptidyl-prolyl cis-trans isomerase"
                     /EC_number="5.2.1.8"
                     /label=fkpB
                     /note="FkpB is a peptidyl-prolyl <i>cis-trans</i>
                     isomerase (PPIase) of the FK506-binding protein type |CITS:
                     [9188461]|.  FkpB also has chaperone activity; a number of 
                     ribosomal proteins appear to be natural substrates |CITS: 
                     [22735173]|.  Substrates were identified by pull-down assay
                     and binding affinity measurements and include RpoE, RseA, 
                     RpsB and AphC |CITS: [32545723]|.
                     A crystal structure has been solved at 1.35 &Aring; 
                     resolution.  Serendipidously, the linker region of the 
                     purification tag of a different FkpB polypeptide is found 
                     in the chaperone binding groove of the insert-in-flap (IF) 
                     domain of FkpB, mimicing a chaperone substrate.  A proline 
                     residue within the linker peptide appears to be 
                     specifically recognized and is important for binding |CITS:
                     [22735173]|.  A solution structure of FkpB suggested that 
                     the orientation of the F37 residue is a reason for the 
                     moderate PPIase activity of FkpB; domain-swap experiments 
                     support this interpretation |CITS: [29155566]|.
                     Mutants in potential active site residues were assayed for 
                     potential substrate binding and PPIase activity |CITS: 
                     [32545723]|.
                     A strain containing non-polar deletions of all six 
                     cytoplasmic PPIases (&Delta;6<i>ppi</i>) shows a growth 
                     defect at 37&deg;C in rich media and at 43&deg;C in both 
                     rich and minimal media |CITS: [32545723]|.
                     SlpA: ""<b>S</b>lyD-<b>l</b>ike <b>p</b>rotein"" |CITS: 
                     [9188461]|"
