     gene            27293..28207
                     /gene="rihC"
                     /locus_tag="b0030"
                     /label=rihC
     CDS             27293..28207
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rihC"
                     /locus_tag="b0030"
                     /product="multifunctional ribonucleoside hydrolase RihC /
                     uridine nucleosidase / xanthosine nucleosidase / inosine 
                     nucleosidase / adenosine nucleosidase / cytidine 
                     nucleosidase"
                     /EC_number="3.2.2.1; 3.2.2.2; 3.2.2.7; 3.2.2.3"
                     /label=rihC
                     /note="<i>rihC</i> encodes a ribonucleoside hydrolase with
                     a broad substrate specificity.  It has decreasing activity 
                     on substrates in the order uridine > xanthosine > inosine >
                     adenosine > cytidine |CITS: [11027694]|. The enzyme has no 
                     activity with deoxyribonucleosides |CITS: [11027694]|. 
                     <i>E. coli</i> contains two other nucleoside hydrolases 
                     with differing specificities, encoded by <i>rihA</i> and 
                     <i>rihB</i> |CITS: [11027694]|.
                     The transition state of the enzyme has been modeled based 
                     on kinetic isotope effects |CITS: [16027052]|.  Potential 
                     active and catalytic sites and the catalytic mechanism of 
                     RihC have been computationally predicted |CITS: 
                     [20865528]|.
                     An <i>rihA rihB rihC</i> triple mutant does not exhibit an 
                     obvious growth defect |CITS: [11027694]|.
                     The <i>rihA</i> and <i>rihC</i> genes are subject to 
                     catabolite repression |CITS: [11027694]|.  Transcription is
                     induced by nalidixic acid, but not by mitomycin C, and 
                     induction does not require LexA |CITS: [11544210]|.
                     "
