     gene            30817..34038
                     /gene="carB"
                     /locus_tag="b0033"
                     /label=carB
     CDS             30817..34038
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="carB"
                     /locus_tag="b0033"
                     /product="trifunctional carbamoyl-phosphate synthetase
                     large subunit / carbamoyl-phosphate synthetase, 
                     glutamine-hydrolyzing / carbamoyl phosphate synthetase"
                     /EC_number="6.3.5.5"
                     /label=carB
                     /note="The CarB subunit is the synthetase component of 
                     carbamoylphosphate synthetase. It binds the two required 
                     molecules of MgATP and catalyzes the two required 
                     phosphorylation events. The large subunit consists of four 
                     structural units: the carboxyphosphate synthetic component,
                     the oligomerization domain, the carbamoyl phosphate 
                     synthetic component and the allosteric domain |CITS: 
                     [10089390]|. The large subunit alone can catalyze carbamyl 
                     phosphate synthesis from ammonia, but not from glutamine 
                     |CITS: [3549732]|. It uses NH3 and HCO3- in an 
                     ATP-dependent reaction to form carbamoyl phosphate |CITS: 
                     [2682645]|. This subunit has two catalytic 
                     nucleotide-binding domains, one involved in the activation 
                     of HCO3- and the second in phosphorylation of carbamate. 
                     Glu841 is an essential residue for the phosphorylation of 
                     carbamate in the terminal step of the catalytic mechanism 
                     |CITS: [1737023]|.
                     CarB: ""<b>car</b>bamoyl phosphate"" |CITS: [4373646]| 
                     <i>cap</i>: |CITS: [5327652]| (do not use as name/synonym; 
                     name has been labeled ""misleading"" by the original author
                     |CITS: [4373646]|)"
