                     /product="crotonobetainyl-CoA hydratase"
                     /EC_number="4.2.1.149"
                     /label=caiD
                     /note="CaiD is a member of the crotonase superfamily; the
                     enzyme purified from <i>E. coli</i> O44:K74 catalyzes
                     the hydration of crotonobetainyl-CoA to carnitinyl-CoA and 
                     can use crotonyl-CoA, but not crotonobetaine,
                     as an alternative substrate |CITS: [11551212]|.
                     CaiD was originally also described as a carnitine racemase;
                     however, only overexpressing both CaiD and
                     CaiE together led to measurable carnitine racemase activity
                     |CITS: [7815937]|."
