                     /product="carnitine--CoA ligase"
                     /EC_number="6.2.1.48"
                     /label=caiC
                     /note="Carnitine-CoA ligase (CaiC) catalyzes the transfer
                     of CoA to carnitine.  CaiC was initially predicted to have 
                     CoA ligase activity by |CITS: [7815937]|.
                     <i>In vitro</i>, the enzyme can utilize both L- and 
                     D-carnitine as well as crotonobetaine and 
                     &gamma;-butyrobetaine as substrates.  CaiC also exhibits a 
                     CoA-transferase-like activity <i>in vitro</i>,
                     which can not substitute for CaiB activity <i>in vivo</i> 
                     |CITS: [18266698]|.
                     "
