     CDS             complement(39244..40386)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="caiA"
                     /locus_tag="b0039"
                     /product="crotonobetainyl-CoA reductase"
                     /EC_number="1.3.8.13"
                     /label=caiA
                     /note="Although <i>E. coli</i> K-12 does contain the
                     <i>cai</i> genes, it can not utilize carnitine as a carbon 
                     or nitrogen source.  However, under anaerobic conditions, 
                     carnitine can be metabolized to &gamma;-butyrobetaine.
                     The CaiA enzyme has been purified from the O44 K74 strain 
                     |CITS: [7815937][8060125][10209289][10978161]|.  In that 
                     strain, CaiA appears to be a homotetramer and forms a 
                     complex with CaiB, &gamma;-butyrobetaine-CoA:carnitine CoA 
                     transferase |CITS: [10209289]|.
                     Expression of the <i>cai</i> operon is induced by carnitine
                     and crotonobetaine under anaerobic conditions |CITS: 
                     [9573142]|.
                     |CITS: [23718679]| demonstrated production of 
                     &gamma;-butyrobetaine in an engineered 
                     L-carnitine-overproducing mutant of K-12 BW25113 and 
                     abolition of &gamma;-butyrobetaine formation upon 
                     <i>caiA</i> deletion."
