     gene            complement(53416..54702)
                     /gene="surA"
                     /locus_tag="b0053"
                     /label=surA
     CDS             complement(53416..54702)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="surA"
                     /locus_tag="b0053"
                     /product="bifunctional chaperone SurA / peptidyl-prolyl
                     cis-trans isomerase"
                     /EC_number="5.2.1.8"
                     /label=surA
                     /note="SurA is a periplasmic chaperone involved in the 
                     biogenesis of outer membrane proteins (OMPs).
                     SurA is required for proper assembly of the outer membrane 
                     proteins |FRAME: EG10669-MONOMER OmpA|, |FRAME: CPLX0-7534 
                     OmpF|, and |FRAME: CPLX0-7655 LamB| |CITS: [8626309]|; loss
                     of SurA is associated with a defective outer membrane and 
                     induction of |FRAME: RPOE-MONOMER ""&sigma;<sup>E</sup>""| 
                     activity; <i>surA</i> null mutants show increased 
                     sensitivity to detergents, bile salts and some antibiotics 
                     |CITS: [8626309][8878048][8985185]| (see further |CITS: 
                     [16267292]|). Depletion of SurA reduces the density of the 
                     outer membrane |CITS: [17908933]|. The purified protein has
                     (low) peptidyl-prolyl isomerase (PPI) activity on model 
                     substrates |CITS: [8878048][8985185]|. SurA is required for
                     growth at pH 9 |CITS: [9791122]|.
                     Combining null mutations in |FRAME: G7320 ""<i>bamB</i>""| 
                     and <i>surA</i> is synthetically lethal |CITS: [15968066]|.
                     SurA interacts with the |FRAME: CPLX0-3933 ""Bam complex""|
                     at the outer membrane |CITS: [17908933][18165306]| (further
                     |CITS: [27298319][35676411]|). SurA interacts with the 
                     |FRAME: G6093-MONOMER BamA| POTRA-1 domain through a 
                     &beta;-augmentation mechanism; this interaction is 
                     necessary for efficient OMP biogenesis and a stable OM 
                     |CITS: [39218969]|. SurA and the Bam complex facilitate 
                     |FRAME: EG10673-MONOMER OmpT| assembly in proteoliposomes 
                     |CITS: [20378773]|. SurA interacts with the |FRAME: 
                     SEC-SECRETION-CPLX|; modeling predicts an interaction 
                     between SecDF and SurA |CITS: [36701201]|.
                     The majority of OMPs are not affected by <i>surA</i> 
                     deletion; loss of <i>surA</i> decreases the abundance of 8 
                     &beta;-barrel proteins (FadL, LptD, FhuA, OmpX, FecA, OmpA,
                     OmpF and LamB); this decreased abundance likely results 
                     from both decreased expression (due to increased 
                     &sigma;<sup>E</sup> activity) and defective assembly, 
                     except in the case of LptD where decreased levels result 
                     solely from defective assembly |CITS: [19343722]| (see 
                     further |CITS: [22589188]|). Loss of <i>surA</i> increases 
                     the abundance of some OMPS likely due to increased 
                     &sigma;<sup>E</sup> activity |CITS: [19343722]|. SurA is 
                     unable to break-up aggregated OmpC <i>in vitro</i> |CITS: 
                     [29543429]|. SurA cooperates with the thiol:disulfide 
                     oxidoreductase |FRAME: DISULFOXRED-MONOMER DsbA| and the 
                     protein disulfide isomerase |FRAME: DSBC-CPLX DsbC| in the 
                     folding of LptB |CITS: [20615876]|. SurA stabilizes the 
                     unfolded state of FhuA and promotes the insertion and 
                     folding of &beta;-hairpins in a lipid membrane <i>in 
                     vitro</i> |CITS: [26344570]|. SurA is the primary chaperone
                     for |FRAME: G7080-MONOMER Ag43| biogenesis |CITS: 
                     [34995984]|.
                     SurA can be found in soluble form and associated with the 
                     outer membrane |CITS: [15840585]|.
                     SurA is a member of the parvulin family of peptidyl-prolyl 
                     isomerases |CITS: [7878731]|. SurA contains a large 
                     N-terminal domain followed by two parvulin-like PPI domains
                     and a small C-terminal tail |CITS: [12429090]|. SurA has 
                     chaperone-like activity <i>in vitro</i>; this activity is 
                     associated with the large N-terminal domain coupled to the 
                     C-terminal tail and appears to be separate to the PPI 
                     activity which is associated with the 2 parvulin-homology 
                     domains |CITS: [11226178]|. The role of the PPI domains in 
                     SurA activity has been investigated |CITS: 
                     [23943764][26728192][30716334]|.
                     SurA displays selectivity for peptides enriched in aromatic
                     residues in specific configurations |CITS: 
                     [11546789][14506253][15840585][17825319]| (also |CITS: 
                     [15196927][17894549][18498364]|; the peptide binding 
                     activity is located in the first PPIase domain |CITS: 
                     [17825319]|. Multiple sites, predominantly located in the 
                     core domain (composed of the N and C-terminal regions) are 
                     involved in substrate binding; the conformation of SurA 
                     alters in response to OMP binding |CITS: [32358557]|. SurA 
                     contains two OMP-binding ""hotspots"", one located in the 
                     core domain, and the other in the P1 domain |CITS: 
                     [39277579]|.
                     SurA is implicated in the assembly of pili |CITS: 
                     [16267292]|. Assembly of the outer membrane |FRAME: 
                     EG10311-MONOMER FimD| usher is dependant on SurA and the 
                     Bam complex |CITS: [21784935]|.
                     Combining null mutations in |FRAME: G6242 ppiD| and 
                     <i>surA</i> is synthetically lethal |CITS: [9670013]| 
                     (however see also |CITS: [16267292]|). &Delta;|FRAME: 
                     EG10455 <i>skp</i>| <i>surA::kan</i> and |FRAME: EG10463 
                     <i>degP</i>|::Tn10 <i>surA::kan</i> double mutations 
                     produce a synthetically lethal phenotype |CITS: [11698367]|
                     (also |CITS: [15968066]|). &Delta;|FRAME: G7644 
                     <i>yraP</i>| <i>surA::Cm</i>, and &Delta;|FRAME: EG12371 
                     <i>nlpI</i>| <i>surA::Cm</i> double mutations produce a 
                     synthetically lethal phenotype |CITS: [15968066]|. Unfolded
                     OmpA and LamB accumulate in <i>skp surA</i> and <i>degP 
                     surA</i> double-mutant depletion strains; SurA and DegP/Skp
                     have redundant chaperone function |CITS: [17908933]| - this
                     concept has been challenged |CITS: [33947759]|.
                     A <i>surA</i> null mutation activates the |FRAME: PWY0-1493
                     ""Rcs signaling pathway""| in in an RcsC- and an 
                     RcsF-dependent manner |CITS: [16740933]|. An in-frame 
                     <i>surA</i> knockout mutant is defective for biofilm 
                     formation; a <i>surA</i> |FRAME: EG10015 <i>rodZ</i>| 
                     double deletion is synthetically lethal |CITS: [18180259]|.
                     An in-frame <i>surA</i> knockout mutant is unable to grow 
                     in medium lacking aromatic amino acids |CITS: [17519022]|. 
                     An in-frame <i>surA</i> knockout mutant shows a significant
                     reduction in persister cell formation compared to wild-type
                     |CITS: [18519731]|. The Keio collection <i>surA</i> mutant 
                     is sensitive to lithium (<90% growth at 200mM Li) |CITS: 
                     [39983623]|.
                     Expression of <i>surA</i> increases in cultures of high 
                     density |CITS: [15774865]| and is lowest at neutral pH but 
                     higher at high and low pH |CITS: [15601715]|.
                     <i>surA</i>: <u>sur</u>vival in stationary phase |CITS: 
                     [2165476]| (see also |CITS: [9791122]|)
                     Related reviews: |CITS: [12429086][15546662][20447864][312 
                     14987][36613738][39008906]|"
