     gene            complement(59687..60346)
                     /gene="rluA"
                     /locus_tag="b0058"
                     /label=rluA
     CDS             complement(59687..60346)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rluA"
                     /locus_tag="b0058"
                     /product="trifunctional 23S rRNA pseudouridine(746) and
                     tRNA pseudouridine(32) synthase / tRNA pseudouridine(32) 
                     synthase / 23S rRNA pseudouridine(746) synthase"
                     /EC_number="5.4.99.28; 5.4.99.29"
                     /label=rluA
                     /note="RluA is the pseudouridine synthase that catalyzes 
                     formation of pseudouridine at position 746 in 23S rRNA and 
                     at position 32 in tRNA<sup>Phe</sup> |CITS: 
                     [7493321][10383384]|.  <i>In vitro</i>, the enzyme acts on 
                     free 23S rRNA fragments (bases 1-847) and 
                     tRNA<sup>Phe</sup> |CITS: [7493321]|.  Synthetic anticodon 
                     stem-loop containing RNAs are substrates of the enzyme 
                     |CITS: [17002302]|.
                     RNA containing 5-fluorouridine forms a covalent complex 
                     with and inhibits RluA stoichiometrically |CITS: 
                     [14730018]|.  The chemical fate of the complex has been 
                     probed using kinetic and labelling studies |CITS: 
                     [17002302]|.  Pre-steady-state kinetic analysis showed that
                     at low RluA concentrations, substrate binding is 
                     rate-limiting, while at higher enzyme concentrations, 
                     catalysis is the rate-limiting step |CITS: [21998096]|.
                     A crystal structure of RluA bound to substrate RNA has been
                     solved at 2.05 &Aring; resolution.  The enzyme induces 
                     significant reorganization of the RNA stem-loop structure, 
                     which may contribute to sequence recognition. The side 
                     chain of the R62 residue plays a key role in RluA activity 
                     by enabling the flipping of the U32 base into the active 
                     site of the enzyme |CITS: [17188032]|.
                     An <i>rluA</i> null, D64N, or D64T mutant does not show 
                     pseudouridylation of position 746 in 23S rRNA or position 
                     32 in tRNA<sup>Phe</sup>; a null mutant appears to have no 
                     growth defect in single culture, but shows a competitive 
                     disadvantage during growth in a mixed culture |CITS: 
                     [10383384]|.  Mutations at cysteine residues do not affect 
                     enzyme activity |CITS: [10529181]|.  Mutations at Motif I 
                     Lys and Pro residues cause structural instability and cause
                     a small defect in activity |CITS: [10924141]|. Reviews: 
                     |CITS: [17113994][17085441][22905870][25616362]|"
