     gene            67838..68602
                     /gene="yabI"
                     /locus_tag="b0065"
                     /label=yabI
     CDS             67838..68602
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yabI"
                     /locus_tag="b0065"
                     /product="DedA family protein YabI"
                     /label=yabI
                     /note="YabI is a member of the DedA family of inner
                     membrane proteins |CITS: [18456815][23086209]|. <i>E. 
                     coli</i> K-12 contains 7 other DedA family members, namely 
                     |FRAME: EG10216 ""DedA""|, |FRAME: EG11824 ""YghB""|, 
                     |FRAME: G7609-MONOMER ""YqjA""|, |FRAME: EG12017 ""YohD""|,
                     |FRAME: G7407 ""YqaA""|, |FRAME: G6945-MONOMER ""YdjX""| 
                     and |FRAME: G6947 ""YdjZ""|. Collectively, the DedA family 
                     is essential in <i>E. coli</i> K-12 |CITS: [22301910]|.
                     YabI is predicted to be an inner membrane protein with five
                     transmembrane domains; topology analysis suggests the 
                     C-terminus is located in the periplasm |CITS: [15919996]|. 
                     The <i>yabI</i> gene may have a 
                     &sigma;<sup>54</sup>-dependent promoter |CITS: [11528004]|.
                     Expression of <i>yabI</i> is induced by AI-2 quorum 
                     signaling |CITS: [11514505]|. A <i>yghB yqjA</i> double 
                     mutant is temperature sensitive for growth, forms chains of
                     cells at permissive temperatures, and can be complemented 
                     by <i>yghB, yqjA, yohD,</i> or <i>yabI</i> expressed from a
                     plasmid |CITS: [18456815]|.
                     <i>yabI</i> insertion mutants were identified in a genetic 
                     screen for genes that are important for survival of 
                     exposure to ionizing radiation (IR). A <i>yabI</i> deletion
                     mutant has a modest decrease in IR survival |CITS: 
                     [25049088]|."
