     CDS             74108..75286
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="setA"
                     /locus_tag="b0070"
                     /product="sugar exporter SetA"
                     /label=setA
                     /note="SetA is an efflux transporter capable of exporting
                     a number of sugars and sugar analogues; the physiological 
                     role of SetA is not clear.
                     Overexpression of <I>setA</I> decreases the amount of 
                     protein produced form IPTG-responsive promoters and 
                     suppresses the growth inhibition that is associated with 
                     over-expression of membrane proteins; inside-out membrane 
                     vesicles prepared from cells overexpressing <I>setA</I> 
                     accumulate significant amounts of lactose in a manner that 
                     is sensitive to the proton ionophore, carbonyl cyanide 
                     m-chlorophenylhydrazone (CCCP) |CITS: [10209755]|.
                     SetA can transport lactose and glucose; SetA also 
                     transports some glucosides and galactosides with alkyl or 
                     aryl substituents and overexpression of <i>setA</i> 
                     protects cells from the toxic sugar analog 
                     2-nitrophenyl-beta-D-thiogalactopyranoside (ONPTG) |CITS: 
                     [10438463]|. Under stress conditions induced by the 
                     presence of the non-metabolizable glucose analog |FRAME: 
                     CPD-3582 ""&alpha;-methyl glucoside""|, <i>setA</i> is 
                     coexpressed with |FRAME: RNA0-241 ""<i>sgrS</i>""| in an 
                     |FRAME: EG12094-MONOMER ""SgrR""| dependent manner |CITS: 
                     [20971900]|. However, efflux assays using labelled 
                     &alpha;-methyl glucoside suggest that SetA does not have a 
                     role in pumping out this sugar analog |CITS: [20971900]|. 
                     In the Transporter Classification Database |CITS: 
                     [26546518]|, SetA is a member of the Sugar Efflux 
                     Transporter (SET) Family within the Major Facilitator 
                     Superfamily (MFS).
                     <i>setA</i>: <U>s</U>ugar <U>e</U>fflux <U>t</U>ransporter 
                     A |CITS: [10438463]|"
