                     /locus_tag="b0072"
                     /label=leuC
     CDS             complement(75951..77351)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="leuC"
                     /locus_tag="b0072"
                     /product="trifunctional 3-isopropylmalate dehydratase
                     subunit LeuC / 3-isopropylmalate dehydratase / 
                     (2S)-2-isopropylmalate hydro-lyase 
                     (2-isopropylmaleate-forming)"
                     /EC_number="4.2.1.33"
                     /label=leuC
                     /note="Isopropylmalate (IPM) isomerase catalyzes the
                     second step in leucine biosynthesis, converting 
                     2-isopropylmalate to 3-isopropylmalate. LeuC and LeuD are 
                     both required for the activity of IPM isomerase |CITS: 
                     [4587614][23636690]|.
                     Based on the IPM isomerase in <i>Salmonella typhimurium</i>
                     and cross-species complementation studies with the 
                     <i>Salmonella</i> |CITS: [7026530][374346]| and <i>S. 
                     cerevisiae</i> |CITS: [23636690]| enzymes, <i>E. coli</i> 
                     IPM isomerase is likely to be a protein complex consisting 
                     of a 1:1 pairing of the of <i>leuC</i> and <i>leuD</i> gene
                     products |CITS: [7026530][374346]|.
                     LeuC protein levels are increased in a 
                     threonine-overproducing mutant |CITS: [15104539]|; LeuC 
                     leves are decreased after 30 minutes of excess zinc stress 
                     |CITS: [17122063]|.
                     <i>leuC</i> insertion mutants, which cause leucine 
                     auxotrophy, lead to increased antibiotic tolerance in 
                     biofilms under leucine starvation conditions |CITS: 
                     [23300476]|."
