                     /product="leu operon leader peptide"
                     /label=leuL
                     /note="Based on a putative adjacent terminator, observed 
                     transcription termination <i>in vitro</i>, demonstrated 
                     regulation by attenuation of the similar <i>Salmonella</i> 
                     operon, and the presence of four leucines within its 
                     sequence, LeuL is presumed to be a leader peptide involved 
                     in attenuation of transcription of the <i>leuLABCD</i> 
                     operon in response to leucine abundance |CITS: [6171647]|. 
                     Reviews: |CITS: [40210524]|"
