                     /label=ftsO
     misc_RNA        88972..89145
                     /gene="ftsO"
                     /locus_tag="b4810"
                     /product="small regulatory RNA FtsO"
                     /note="FtsO is a small RNA encoded internal to the
                     <i>ftsI</i> open reading frame.  Both the 5' and 3' end of 
                     FtsO is likely generated by RNase processing of the 
                     <i>ftsI</i> mRNA.  Expression of FtsO is high across growth
                     and in rich and minimal medium |CITS: [33460557]|. FtsO 
                     overexpression leads to decreased levels of the |FRAME: 
                     RYBB-RNA| and |FRAME: RNA0-389|; FtsO acts as a sponge for 
                     RybB |CITS: [33460557]|."
     gene            89653..91140
                     /gene="murE"
                     /locus_tag="b0085"
                     /label=murE
     CDS             89653..91140
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="murE"
                     /locus_tag="b0085"
                     /product="UDP-N-acetylmuramoyl-L-alanyl-D-glutamate--2,6-d 
                     iaminopimelate ligase"
                     /EC_number="6.3.2.13"
                     /label=murE
                     /note="UDP-<i>N</i>-acetylmuramoylalanyl-D-glutamate 
                     2,6-diaminopimelate ligase (MurE) catalyzes the addition of
                     the third amino acid, meso-diaminopimelate, to the peptide 
                     moiety of the monomer unit of peptidoglycan |CITS: 
                     [2269304]|. The enzyme's ability to use the LL-DAP isomer 
                     at a low level leads to the incorporation of LL-DAP into 
                     peptidoglycan in a |FRAME: DIAMINOPIMEPIM-MONOMER| 
                     (<i>dapF</i>) mutant |CITS: [3283102]|.
                     A crystal structure of the enzyme has been solved at 
                     2&Aring; resolution, allowing the identification of 
                     residues involved in catalysis. The Lys224 residue within 
                     the active site is carbamylated |CITS: [11124264]|, and 
                     this modification appears to be required for enzymatic 
                     activity |CITS: [11722566]|.
                     Temperature-sensitive <i>murE</i> mutants have been 
                     isolated |CITS: [4553000]|, and the genetic defects of the 
                     <i>murE1</i> allele has been identified |CITS: [9166795]|. 
                     In a <i>dapA</i> mutant, cystathionine or lanthionine will 
                     substitute for diaminopimelate |CITS: [8021219]|. 
                     Repression of <i>murE</i> expression with a synthetic small
                     RNA leads to increased production of cadaverine in an 
                     engineered strain |CITS: [23334451]|. A 
                     temperature-sensitive mutation in this gene was identified 
                     that showed potential as a growth-switch for genetic 
                     engineering |CITS: [37642940]|.
                     MurE is a potential antimicrobial drug target; inhibitors 
                     of MurE activity have been identified |CITS: 
                     [3072305][8706910][18506905][19804894]|.
                     Reviews: |CITS: [12492849][22203377]|"
