     gene            93574..94890
                     /gene="murD"
                     /locus_tag="b0088"
                     /label=murD
     CDS             93574..94890
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="murD"
                     /locus_tag="b0088"
                     /product="UDP-N-acetylmuramoyl-L-alanine--D-glutamate
                     ligase"
                     /EC_number="6.3.2.9"
                     /label=murD
                     /note="UDP-<i>N</i>-acetylmuramoyl-L-alanine:D-glutamate
                     ligase (MurD) catalyzes the addition of the second amino 
                     acid to the peptide moiety of the monomer unit of 
                     peptidoglycan.  There are estimated to be less than 1000 
                     copies of MurD in the cell |CITS: [1765076]|.
                     Biosynthesis of the cytoplasmic precursor subunit of 
                     peptidoglycan has been reconstituted <i>in vitro</i> |CITS:
                     [24389752]|.
                     The reaction mechanism and specific inhibitors of the 
                     enzyme have been studied |CITS: 
                     [9158722][11667046][9873406][12699754][16271472]|.  <i>In 
                     vitro</i> in the absence of D-glutamate, MurD can catalyze 
                     the formation of p<sub>4</sub>A from ATP via an acyl 
                     phosphate intermediate |CITS: [10403366]|.
                     Crystal structures of the enzyme alone and in complex with 
                     substrates, product or inhibitors have been solved, and a 
                     catalytic mechanism involving an acyl phosphate 
                     intermediate was deduced |CITS: 
                     [9218784][10356330][10966819][17507028]|.  Results from 
                     site-directed mutagenesis of conserved amino acid residues 
                     within the active site correlated with their assigned 
                     function based on the crystal structures |CITS: 
                     [10493791]|.  The K198 residue is present as a carbamate 
                     derivative |CITS: [10356330]|; the modification is 
                     important for catalytic activity |CITS: [11722566]|. 
                     Molecular dynamics (MD) simulations were performed to 
                     provide insight into structural changes during substrate 
                     binding and transition into the active conformation |CITS: 
                     [17427948]|.  Three reaction paths to the formation of the 
                     tetrahedral reaction intermediate have been investigated by
                     hybrid QM/MM molecular modeling |CITS: [18704940]|.  MD 
                     simulations were also used for antibacterial drug design 
                     |CITS: [24724969]|.
                     <i>murD</i> is an essential gene |CITS: [16738554]|, and is
                     therefore an antibacterial drug target.  Novel inhibitors 
                     of MurD activity have been identified |CITS: [1 
                     8259126][18506905][18651694][19007109][19014883][19358612][
                     19403924][19804894][20804196][21524830][21591605][21703731]
                     [22705647][24900523][23990043][24724969][24952377][24953950
                     ]|. Reviews: |CITS: [12492849][22203377][25436755]|"
