     CDS             107531..107920
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="mutT"
                     /locus_tag="b0099"
                     /product="8-oxo-dGTP diphosphatase"
                     /EC_number="3.6.1.58; 3.6.1.55"
                     /label=mutT
                     /note="The MutT protein hydrolyzes 
                     8-oxo-7,8-dihydrodeoxyguanosine-triphosphate (8-oxo-dGTP) 
                     and 8-oxo-7,8-dihydroguanosine triphosphate (8-oxo-GTP) to 
                     the monophosphate form, thus avoiding the misincorporation 
                     of mutagenic nucleotides into DNA and mRNA during 
                     replication and transcription |CITS: [3033442],[1309939], 
                     [9311918]|. MutT also hydrolyses 8-oxo-GDP and 8-oxo-dGDP 
                     to their monophosphate form |CITS: [15850400]|. The absence
                     of <i>mutT</i> increases the spontaneous occurrence of A:T 
                     to C:G transversion a thousandfold over the wild type level
                     |CITS:[797306][1851162][10954591]|, and further increases 
                     the occurrence of transcriptional errors |CITS: 
                     [10811907]|. 8-oxo-dGTP is inserted opposite dATP and dCTP 
                     residues of template DNA <i>in vitro</i> with almost equal 
                     efficiency |CITS: [1309939]|. MutT works cooperatively with
                     |FRAME: EG10329-MONOMER ""MutM""| and |FRAME: 
                     EG10627-MONOMER ""MutY""| which function to excise 
                     8-oxyguanine incorporated in DNA |CITS: [7739614]|. Earlier
                     studies showed that the enzyme can catalyze the hydrolysis 
                     of all eight canonical nucleotides, but it shows a marked 
                     preference for oxidized forms of dGTP |CITS:[3033442] 
                     [3288626]|."
