     gene            complement(108136..108333)
                     /gene="yacG"
                     /locus_tag="b0101"
                     /label=yacG
     CDS             complement(108136..108333)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yacG"
                     /locus_tag="b0101"
                     /product="DNA gyrase inhibitor YacG"
                     /label=yacG
                     /note="The YacG protein blocks DNA binding by |FRAME: 
                     CPLX0-2425|, thereby inhibiting its function.
                     YacG inhibits the supercoiling activity of DNA gyrase, as 
                     well as partially inhibiting its intrinsic ATPase activity.
                      It does so via direct binding to the GyrB component of the
                     gyrase holoenzyme and disrupting DNA binding by the enzyme.
                      This inhibition is specific to gyrase, as neither 
                     topoisomerase I nor topoisomerase IV are affected by the 
                     presence of YacG |CITS: [18586829]|. The structure of YacG 
                     has been analyzed via NMR.  It appears to contain a classic
                     zinc finger domain, including a tetrahedrally coordinated 
                     Zn<sup>2+</sup> |CITS: [12211008]|.
                     Based on a deletion analysis, <i>yacG</i> appears to be 
                     dispensible for normal growth in minimal and rich medium 
                     |CITS: [11160101]|.  A <i>yacL</i> in-frame deletion strain
                     has been constructed |CITS: [12142427]|. Overexpression of 
                     <i>yacG</i> leads to growth inhibition and abnormally low 
                     levels of DNA supercoiling |CITS: [18586829]|."
                     /translation="MSETITVNCPTCGKTVVWGEISPFRPFCSKRCQLIDLGEWAAEEK
