                     /product="dephospho-CoA kinase"
                     /EC_number="2.7.1.24"
                     /label=coaE
                     /note="Dephospho-CoA kinase catalyzes the final step in
                     coenzyme A biosynthesis |CITS: [11292795]|.
                     The enzyme appeared to be a monomer in solution |CITS: 
                     [11292795]|; subsequent analysis of the crystal
                     structure, where it appears as a trimer, led to the 
                     discovery that the presence of sulfate ions stabilizes a 
                     trimeric state in solution as well.  The biological role of
                     the trimeric form is unclear |CITS: [12538896]|. Crystal 
                     structures of the enzyme have been solved |CITS: 
                     [12538896][16021622]|.
                     <i>coaE</i> is essential for growth |CITS: [11160101]|."
