     CDS             complement(111009..112211)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="hofC"
                     /locus_tag="b0106"
                     /product="inner membrane protein HofC"
                     /label=hofC
                     /note="HopC (now called HofC) is predicted to be a
                     polytopic inner membrane protein; <i>hofC</i> is part of a 
                     putative three gene operon (<i>ppdD hofB hofC</i>) whose 
                     members all show sequence similarity to genes involved in 
                     type IV fimbrial assembly systems of pathogenic bacteria 
                     |CITS: [7959070]|.
                     <i>ppdD hofB hofC</i> has sequence similarity to the type 
                     IV piliation genes (<i>pilABC</i>) of <i>Pseudomonas 
                     aeruginosa</i> |CITS: [10633126]|. The <i>ppdD hofB 
                     hofC</i> genes are poorly expressed; overexpression of 
                     <i>ppdD, hofB</i> and <i>hofC</i> in <i>E. coli</i> K-12 
                     does not result in the production of detectable type IV 
                     pili |CITS: [10633126]|.
                     The HopC (<U>ho</U>st function of <U>p</U>lasmid 
                     maintenance) mutation characterized by |CITS: [3053654]| is
                     unrelated to the <i>hofC/hopC</i> gene sequenced by |CITS: 
                     [7959070]|. The <i>hopC</i> mutation characterized by 
                     |CITS: [3053654]| maps in the <i>thr-dnaC</i> region. 
                     <i>hop</i>: <U>ho</U>mology to <i><U>p</U>il</i> |CITS: 
                     [7934814][7959070]|
                     "
