     gene            complement(113596..114036)
                     /gene="ppdD"
                     /locus_tag="b0108"
                     /label=ppdD
     CDS             complement(113596..114036)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ppdD"
                     /locus_tag="b0108"
                     /product="prepilin-type N-terminal cleavage/methylation 
                     domain-containing protein PpdD"
                     /label=ppdD
                     /note="<i>ppdD</i> encodes a putative Type IV major pilin 
                     subunit; <i>ppdD</i> is poorly expressed under standard 
                     conditions. Expression of cloned <i>ppdD</i> or cloned 
                     <i>ppdD-hofB-hofC</i> does not result in the production of 
                     detectable pili, but immunogold labeling suggests that PpdD
                     is exposed on the cell surface. PpdD is able to form type 
                     IV pili when expressed in <i>Pseudomonas aeruginosa</i> 
                     |CITS: [10633126]|. PpdD shares over 95% identity with the 
                     major type IV pilin subunit, HcpA from enterohemorrhagic 
                     <i>E. coli</i> O157:H7 |CITS: [XICOHTENCATI-CORTES07]|.
                     <i>ppdD</i> is not required for spontaneous plasmid 
                     transformation on nutrient plates with high agar 
                     concentration |CITS: [19011021]|."
