     gene            115220..115771
                     /gene="ampD"
                     /locus_tag="b0110"
                     /label=ampD
     CDS             115220..115771
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ampD"
                     /locus_tag="b0110"
                     /product="1,6-anhydro-N-acetylmuramoyl-L-alanine amidase"
                     /EC_number="3.5.1.28"
                     /label=ampD
                     /note="AmpD is a cytosolic N-acetylmuramyl-L-alanine
                     amidase responsible for breakdown of anhMurNAc-linked 
                     peptides, releasing the peptides for recycling |CITS: 
                     [7925310][19309146]|.
                     Unlike in <i>Citrobacter freundii</i> or <i>Enterobacter 
                     cloacae</i>, the native |FRAME: EG10040-MONOMER AmpC| 
                     &beta;-lactamase of <i>E. coli</i> is not inducible by 
                     &beta;-lactam antibiotics due to lack of the AmpR 
                     regulator.  In <i>Enterobacter cloacae</i>, the signal 
                     molecule for AmpR-dependent induction of <i>ampC</i> 
                     expression is anhMurNAc-pentapeptide |CITS: [9333034]|.
                     In an <i>ampD</i> mutant, 1,6-anhydro-<i>N</i>-acetylmuram 
                     yl-L-alanyl-D-glutamyl-meso-diaminopimelic acid 
                     (anhMurNAc-tripeptide) accumulates in the cytoplasm |CITS: 
                     [7925310]| and, after export, in the periplasm |CITS: 
                     [8878601]|.
                     <i>ampD</i> is a member of the <i>ampDE</i> operon |CITS: 
                     [2607970]|.
                     Reviews: |CITS: 
                     [8452343][8559061][9158731][18535144][29185941]|"
