     CDS             complement(138495..139157)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="can"
                     /locus_tag="b0126"
                     /product="bifunctional carbonic anhydrase 2 / carbonic
                     anhydrase"
                     /EC_number="4.2.1.1"
                     /label=can
                     /note="<i>E. coli</i> encodes two carbonic anhydrases,
                     CynT (|FRAME: CARBODEHYDRAT-MONOMER|) and Can (carbonic 
                     anhydrase 2).  The enzymes belong to Clade A and Clade B of
                     the &beta; class of carbonic anhydrases, respectively 
                     |CITS: [10978542]|.  Carbonic anhydrase 2 is essential for 
                     growth at amospheric pCO<sub>2</sub> |CITS: 
                     [12784642][14563877][16738554]|.  Enzymatic activity of 
                     carbonic anhydrase 2 is pH-dependent |CITS: [11316870]|. 
                     Inhibition of Can activity by sulfonamides and various 
                     clinically used drugs has been investigated |CITS: 
                     [32486444][32545297][35899716]|.
                     Crystal structures of carbonic anhydrase 2 have been 
                     solved.  The crystal structure data as well as size 
                     exclusion chromatography indicate that the protein exists 
                     as a homotetramer in solution |CITS: [11316870]|.  There is
                     structural evidence for a noncatalytic binding site for 
                     bicarbonate |CITS: [16584170]|.
                     A <i>can</i> mutant does not grow under normal atmospheric 
                     conditions, but the mutant can grow under conditions with a
                     high exogenous or endogenous supply of CO<sub>2</sub>. 
                     Expression of <i>cynT</i> suppresses phenotypes of a 
                     <i>can</i> mutant |CITS: [14563877]|.  A <i>can cynT</i> 
                     double mutant is only viable under high CO<sub>2</sub> 
                     conditions |CITS: [12784642]|.
                     Expression of <i>can</i> is inversely proportional to the 
                     growth rate and does not depend on CO<sub>2</sub> levels 
                     |CITS: [14563877]|.  Under anaerobiosis, FNR represses 
                     <i>can</i> gene expression, but it is not known if this 
                     regulation is direct or indirect |CITS: [12754220]|. 
                     Carbonic anhydrase 2 belongs to a set of native <i>E. 
                     coli</i> proteins that is a common contaminant during 
                     recombinant His-tagged protein purification using 
                     immobilized metal affinity chromatography |CITS: 
                     [16814929]| and was also found during crystal structure 
                     determination of a presumed recombinant survivin |CITS: 
                     [26660914]|.
                     Can: ""<b>c</b>arbonic <b>an</b>hydrase"" |CITS: 
                     [14563877]|
                     Reviews: |CITS: 
                     [10978542][11268536][11696553][21779249][38506448]|"
                     /translation="MKDIDTLISNNALWSKMLVEEDPGFFEKLAQAQKPRFLWIGCSDS
