                     /product="recombination-promoting nuclease RpnC"
                     /label=rpnC
                     /note="RpnC is one of five proteins in <i>E. coli</i> that 
                     belong to the ""transposase_31"" family |CITS: [28096446]|,
                     which is distantly related to the PD-(D/E)XK nuclease 
                     superfamily |CITS: [17584917]|.
                     Overexpression of <i>rpnC</i> increases RecA-independent 
                     recombination, reduces cell viability, and induces 
                     expression of the DNA damage-inducible gene <i>dinD</i> 
                     |CITS: [28096446]|.  An insertion mutation in <i>rpnC</i> 
                     does not affect the ability to grow on glucose minimal 
                     medium |CITS: [8837478]|.
                     RpnC: ""<b>r</b>ecombination-<b>p</b>romoting 
                     <b>n</b>uclease <b>C</b>"" |CITS: [28096446]|
                     "
