     CDS             complement(144431..145282)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="panC"
                     /locus_tag="b0133"
                     /product="pantothenate synthetase"
                     /EC_number="6.3.2.1"
                     /label=panC
                     /note="Pantothenate synthetase (PanC) catalyzes the ATP 
                     hydrolysis-dependent synthesis of pantothenate from 
                     &beta;-alanine and pantoate |CITS: [7037743]|.
                     The enzyme from strains W or B requires both monovalent and
                     divalent cations |CITS: [12999714][374975]|.  The 
                     pantothenate:&beta;-alanine exchange reaction depends on 
                     the presence of AMP, which supports the two-step Bi Uni Uni
                     Bi reaction mechanism with pantoyl adenylate as the 
                     reaction intermediate |CITS: [17040917]|.
                     Crystal structures of the full length enzyme |CITS: 
                     [11377204]| and its N-terminal domain |CITS: [20059543]| 
                     have been solved.  Pantothenate synthetase is dimeric both 
                     in solution and the crystal structure.  It is a member of 
                     the cytidylyltransferase superfamily, with an N-terminal 
                     Rossmann fold domain containing the active site and a 
                     C-terminal domain that forms a hinged lid |CITS: 
                     [11377204]|.  The substrate pantoate is able to bind within
                     the ATP-binding pocket of the N-terminal domain |CITS: 
                     [20059543]|.  Molecular dynamics simulations suggest that 
                     motions of the C-terminal domain dominate the functional 
                     dynamics of the <i>E. coli</i> enzyme |CITS: [21425349]|.
                     <i>panC</i> mutants are auxotrophic for pantothenate |CITS:
                     [7037743]|.
                     Various inhibitors of pantothenate synthetase have been 
                     tested |CITS: [16990935]|.
                     PanC: ""<b>pan</b>tothenate"""
