     gene            complement(146202..147440)
                     /gene="yadC"
                     /locus_tag="b0135"
                     /label=yadC
     CDS             complement(146202..147440)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yadC"
                     /locus_tag="b0135"
                     /product="fimbrial tip-adhesin YadC"
                     /label=yadC
                     /note="<i>yadNVhtrEyadMLKC</i> is a putative
                     chaperone-usher fimbrial operon in <i>E. coli</i> K-12 
                     |CITS: [20345943]|.  The operon is cryptic under normal 
                     laboratory conditions but when constitutive expression is 
                     induced in a strain that lacks the type 1 fimbrial complex 
                     the <i>yad</i> operon promotes biofilm formation in minimal
                     media on a variety of abiotic surfaces and produces surface
                     fimbrial structures that can be observed microscopically 
                     |CITS: [20345943]|. Constitutive expression of the 
                     <i>yad</i> operon results in increased adhesion of cells to
                     xylose; constitutive expression of the <i>yad</i> operon 
                     results in increased adherence to intestinal epithelial 
                     cells and can modulate the inflammatory reponse of host 
                     cells |CITS: [27696649]|. A strain producing Yad fimbriae 
                     outcompetes both the wild type and a &Delta;<i>yad</i> 
                     strain for corn rhizosphere colonisation |CITS: [27696649]|
                     YadC is predicted to contain two domains (a C-terminal 
                     pilin domain and an N-terminal lectin domain) similar to 
                     the type 1 fimbrial tip-adhesin FimH. Constitutive 
                     expression of the <i>yad</i> operon results in increased 
                     adhesion to xylose; YadC binds to xylose |CITS: 
                     [27696649]|.
                     Sequence similarity suggests that YadC may contain 
                     &beta;-barrel structure(s) |CITS: [12192075]|.
                     Expression of the <i>yad</i> operon is negatively regulated
                     by |FRAME: PD00288 ""H-NS""| |CITS: [20345943]|. <i>yad</i>
                     operon expression is subject to complex regulation; 
                     affected by different environmental conditions (eg. 
                     temperature, oxygen and others) and involves multiple 
                     regulatory proteins (eg. ArcA, Fnr, RpoS and others) |CITS:
                     [27696649]|.
                     A <i>yadC</i> insertion mutant is more sensitive than wild 
                     type to mitomycin C and other stresses, but less 
                     susceptible to killing by 10% SDS |CITS: [20128927]|. <i>E.
                     coli</i> K-12 contains 12 chaperone-usher fimbrial operons,
                     including <i>yadNVhtrEyadMLKC</i>; a fimbria-lacking mutant
                     - strain WQM026 - created by deleting all 12 operons has 
                     been characterised |CITS: [33863704]|.
                     "
