     gene            complement(149316..151913)
                     /gene="htrE"
                     /locus_tag="b0139"
                     /label=htrE
     CDS             complement(149316..151913)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="htrE"
                     /locus_tag="b0139"
                     /product="putative fimbrial usher protein HtrE"
                     /label=htrE
                     /note="HtrE has similarity to PapC, which is a type II
                     pilin porin |CITS: [8102362]|. <i>yadNVhtrEyadMLKC</i> is a
                     putative chaperone-usher fimbrial operon in <i>E.coli 
                     K-12</i> |CITS:[20345943]|. The operon is cryptic under 
                     normal laboratory conditions but when constitutive 
                     expression is induced in a strain that lacks the type 1 
                     fimbrial complex the <i>yad</i> operon promotes biofilm 
                     formation in minimal media on a variety of abiotic surfaces
                     and produces surface fimbrial structures that can be 
                     observed microscopically |CITS: [20345943]|. Constitutive 
                     expression of the <i>yad</i> operon results in increased 
                     adhesion of cells to xylose; constitutive expression of the
                     <i>yad</i> operon results in increased adherence to 
                     intestinal epithelial cells and can modulate the 
                     inflammatory reponse of host cells |CITS: [27696649]|. A 
                     strain producing Yad fimbriae outcompetes both the wild 
                     type and a &Delta;<i>yad</i> strain for corn rhizosphere 
                     colonisation |CITS: [27696649]|.
                     HtrE binds human complement component C3 <i>in vitro</i>; 
                     HtrE is implicated in a pathway of glycine-promoted 
                     complement-dependent cell death |CITS: [31346171]|
                     An <i>htrE</i> insertion mutant exhibits heat sensitivity 
                     |CITS: [8102362]|. HtrE is subject to posttranslational 
                     processing; the mature form of the protein is 92kDa whereas
                     the translation product is 95 kDa |CITS: [8102362]|.
                     Expression of the <i>yad</i> operon is negatively regulated
                     by |FRAME: PD00288 ""H-NS""| |CITS: [20345943]|. <i>yad</i>
                     operon expression is subject to complex regulation; 
                     affected by different environmental conditions (eg. 
                     temperature, oxygen and others) and involves multiple 
                     regulatory proteins (eg. ArcA, Fnr, RpoS and others) |CITS:
                     [27696649]|. CRP-cAMP, FlhC and CsgD regulate the 
                     expression of <i>htrE</i> during glycine dependent serum 
                     mediated cell death |CITS: [31346171]|.
                     <i>E. coli</i> K-12 contains 12 chaperone-usher fimbrial 
                     operons, including <i>yadNVhtrEyadMLKC</i>; a 
                     fimbria-lacking mutant - strain WQM026 - created by 
                     deleting all 12 operons has been characterised |CITS: 
                     [33863704]|.
                     <i>htrE</i>: <U>h</U>igh <U>t</U>emperature 
                     <U>r</U>equirement |CITS: [8102362]|
                     "
