                     /label=sfsA
     CDS             complement(157269..157973)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="sfsA"
                     /locus_tag="b0146"
                     /product="sugar fermentation stimulation protein A"
                     /label=sfsA
                     /note="SfsA may be a transcription factor involved in
                     regulation of maltose metabolism.
                     Overexpression of SfsA yields a 10-fold increase in 
                     amylomaltose (MalQ) activity as well as an increase in 
                     maltose-binding protein (MalE) levels |CITS: 
                     [2013578][11272834]|.  This MalT-dependent increase occurs 
                     at the level of transcription |CITS: [2013578][11272834]|. 
                     <i>In vitro</i>, SfsA binds DNA nonspecifically |CITS: 
                     [11272834]|.  It contains a PD-(D/E)XK domain, which is 
                     found in a number of DNA-related proteins |CITS: 
                     [16011798]|.
                     There is no apparent phenotypic consequence of disrupting 
                     <i>sfsA</i> |CITS: [11272834]|.
                     The <i>sfsA</i> ORF contains an out-of-frame internal 
                     translation initiation site that is able to direct 
                     translation initiation <i>in vivo</i> |CITS: [30904393]|. 
                     SfsA: ""<b>s</b>ugar <b>f</b>ermentation 
                     <b>s</b>timulation"" |CITS: [2013578]|"
