     gene            158592..161021
                     /gene="hrpB"
                     /locus_tag="b0148"
                     /label=hrpB
     CDS             158592..161021
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="hrpB"
                     /locus_tag="b0148"
                     /product="RNA-dependent NTPase HrpB"
                     /label=hrpB
                     /note="HrpB belongs to the DEAH/RHA subfamily of nucleic 
                     acid-dependent NTPases |CITS: [30174149][30190128]|. 
                     Nuclease activity of HrpB is highest with CTP and UTP and 
                     is stimulated by the presence of single-stranded RNA.
                     HrpB did not show RNA helicase activity with any of the 
                     tested substrates |CITS: [30174149]|.
                     HrpB was initially named based on its similarity to HrpA. 
                     However, it differs in that it lacks some conserved 
                     residues found in in DEAH-box RNA helicases and HrpA |CITS:
                     [7899078]|.
                     Crystal structures of HrpB have been solved |CITS: 
                     [30174149][30190128]|.  The protein comprises a ""head"" 
                     module consisting of two RecA-like domains, a WH domain, an
                     HB domain, and an OB domain, followed by a connector and a 
                     unique C-terminal region |CITS: [30174149][30190128]|.
                     In a large genetic interaction screen, <i>hrpB</i> showed 
                     genetic interactions with a number of proteins involved in 
                     translation |CITS: [27732863]|.  <i>hrpB</i> deletion 
                     mutants did not show obvious phenotypes under the tested 
                     conditions |CITS: [30174149]|. The Keio collection 
                     <i>hrpB</i> mutant exhibits a 'high level' of resistance to
                     lithium exposure |CITS: [39983623]|.
                     HrpB: ""DEA<b>H</b>-family <b>R</b>NA helicase-like 
                     <b>p</b>rotein <b>B</b>"" |CITS: [7899078]|"
