                     /label=fhuA
     CDS             163971..166214
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="fhuA"
                     /locus_tag="b0150"
                     /product="trifunctional ferrichrome outer membrane 
                     transporter/phage receptor / ferrichrome outer membrane 
                     transport complex / transport of ferrichrome"
                     /label=fhuA
                     /note="FhuA is an outer membrane protein that mediates
                     binding and |FRAME: EG11012-MONOMER TonB|-dependent active 
                     transport of ferrichrome and its close analogs across the 
                     outer membrane; it also transports the antibiotics 
                     albomycin and rifamycin CGP 4832, and serves as the 
                     receptor for phages T1, T5, UC-1, &Phi;80 (and others 
                     |CITS: [37310294][34784345]|), and the peptides colicin M 
                     and microcin J25 (see |CITS: [1096882][136550][353030][629 
                     3371][3079747][3332686][2549378][8244949]|). Early studies 
                     characterized <i>fhuA</i> (formerly <i>tonA</i>) mutants 
                     which are deficient in ferrichrome uptake and resistant to 
                     phages T1, T5 and &Phi;80, to colicin M and to the 
                     antibiotic albomycin |CITS: [1089064][6249788][7026976]|. 
                     FhuA synthesis increases rapidly upon iron deprivation 
                     before decreasing as a function of time |CITS: [6174499]|. 
                     FhuA-mediated transport across the outer membrane is the 
                     rate-limiting step of ferrichrome uptake |CITS: [ 
                     9613584]|.
                     FhuA is a monomeric protein composed of a C-terminal 
                     &beta;-barrel domain and an N-terminal 'cork' or 'plug' 
                     domain which fills the barrel interior; crystal structures 
                     of FhuA complexed with ferrichrome-iron and in a ligand 
                     free state have been reported |CITS: [9856937][9865695]| 
                     (and see |CITS: [10209114]|). Crystal structures of FhuA 
                     bound to rifamycin CGP 4832 |CITS: [11587645]|, to 
                     albomycin |CITS: [10850805]|, and in complex with the TonB 
                     carboxyl-terminal domain |CITS: [16741125]| are also 
                     available.
                     A FhuA 'gating loop' mutant (FhuA &Delta;322-355) forms 
                     stable diffusion channels in lipid membranes and iron 
                     transport into cells expressing the mutant protein is 
                     TonB-independent |CITS: [7688295]| (see also |CITS: 
                     [8955314][8617231][12383253]|). Purified FhuA undergoes 
                     conformational change upon binding to ferrichrome |CITS: 
                     [8939430]| (see also |CITS: [9457864]|). Ligand binding to 
                     FhuA enhances its physical association with TonB |CITS: 
                     [9353297]|.
                     <i>fhuA</i> exhibits mosaic evolution patterns in <i>E. 
                     coli</i> |CITS: [30150258][35285711][40444982]|. 
                     <i>tonA</i>: phage <U>T-on</U>e (see |CITS: 
                     [136550]|)<BR><i>fhu</i>: <U>f</U>erric <U>h</U>ydroxamate 
                     <U>u</U>ptake |CITS: [6249788]|
                     Rview: |CITS: [19329642]|"
