     gene            complement(170089..171369)
                     /gene="hemL"
                     /locus_tag="b0154"
                     /label=hemL
     CDS             complement(170089..171369)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="hemL"
                     /locus_tag="b0154"
                     /product="glutamate-1-semialdehyde 2,1-aminomutase"
                     /EC_number="5.4.3.8"
                     /label=hemL
                     /note="Glutamate-1-semialdehyde 2,1-aminomutase (HemL)
                     catalyzes the pyridoxal 5'-phosphate-dependent transfer of 
                     the amino group from C2 of glutamate-1-semialdehyde (GSA) 
                     to C1, thereby forming &delta;-aminolevulinate (ALA).  ALA 
                     is the first common precursor of porphyrin biosynthesis 
                     |CITS: [2045363]|.
                     HemL forms a tight complex with |FRAME: 
                     GLUTRNAREDUCT-MONOMER|, the preceding enzyme in the 
                     pathway, suggesting metabolic channeling of the highly 
                     reactive pathway intermediate GSA |CITS: [15757895]|. 
                     Transcription of <i>hemL</i> is regulated by 
                     Mg<sup>2+</sup> and PhoP |CITS: [12813061]|.  <i>hemL</i> 
                     mRNA contains RNA G-quadruplex (rG4) structures that appear
                     to increase expression of <i>hemL</i> |CITS: [31964733]|.
                     <i>hemL</i> point mutants show leaky ALA auxotrophy |CITS: 
                     [5340314][2045363][1643048]|.  A K265R point mutant is 
                     nearly catalytically inactive |CITS: [1643048]|. 
                     <i>hemL</i> belongs to a network of genes which facilitate 
                     stress-induced mutagenesis (SIM) in <i>E. coli</i> K-12 
                     |CITS: [23224554]|.
                     An RNA G-quadruplex structure, formed by guanine-rich 
                     sequences located in the coding sequence region of the <i> 
                     hemL</i> gene, regulates positively the expression of the 
                     gene |CITS: [31964733]|.
                     PopC: ""<b>po</b>r<b>p</b>hyrin biosynthesis"" |CITS: 
                     [4598342]|
                     HemL: ""<b>hem</b>e biosynthesis"" |CITS: [2045363]| 
                     Review: |CITS: [26443580]|"
