                     /product="tetrahydrodipicolinate succinylase"
                     /EC_number="2.3.1.117"
                     /label=dapD
                     /note="Tetrahydrodipicolinate succinylase (DapD) catalyzes
                     the formation of <i>N</i>-succinyl-2-amino-6-ketopimelate 
                     from succinyl-CoA and tetrahydrodipicolinate, and is a key 
                     enzyme in the <i>E. coli</i> lysine biosynthetic pathway 
                     |CITS: [6365916]|.
                     A crystal structure of DapD from <i>E. coli</i> O157:H7 has
                     been solved |CITS: [18242192]|.
                     Expression of <i>dapD</i> is repressed by lysine |CITS: 
                     [6094577][18213406]| via ArgP |CITS: [21890697]|.
                     DapD: ""<b>d</b>i<b>a</b>mino<b>p</b>imelate biosynthesis 
                     <b>D</b>"" |CITS: [4926684]|"
