                     /label=tff
     misc_RNA        186199..186334
                     /gene="tff"
                     /locus_tag="b4414"
                     /product="putative small RNA T44"
                     /note="A computational screen for conserved RNA secondary 
                     structures identified t44, a region upstream of 
                     <i>rpsB</i>.  An RNA of approximately 135 nt in length was 
                     detected, and the authors identified t44 as a
                     possible attenuator |CITS: [11553332]|. Posttranscriptional
                     autoregulation of <i>rpsB</i> expression was
                     found to require the <i>rpsB</i> 5' UTR, which is 
                     phylogenetically conserved.  It is thus likely that t44 
                     represents secondary structure conservation due to a 
                     conserved regulatory mechanism rather than a small
                     RNA |CITS: [18648071]|.
                     "
     gene            186361..187086
                     /gene="rpsB"
                     /locus_tag="b0169"
                     /label=rpsB
     CDS             186361..187086
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rpsB"
                     /locus_tag="b0169"
                     /product="trifunctional 30S ribosomal subunit protein S2 /
                     30S ribosomal subunit / ribosome"
                     /label=rpsB
                     /note="The S2 protein, a component of the 30S subunit of
                     the ribosome, is essential in <i>E. coli</i> |CITS: 
                     [161328]|. S2 is required for S1 binding to the ribosome 
                     |CITS: [12068815]|. Overexpression of <i>csdA</i>, a 
                     DEAD-box RNA helicase, supresses the defect of a 
                     temperature-sensitive allele of <i>rpsB</i> |CITS: 
                     [2045359]| by restoring assembly of both S1 and S2 with the
                     ribosome at the non-permissive temperature |CITS: 
                     [12068815]|.
                     Expression of S2 is autoregulated, involving conserved 
                     elements located in the 5' UTR of the <i>rpsB-tsf</i> mRNA.
                     Regulation may also involve the S1 protein |CITS: 
                     [18648071]|.
                     Purified S2 protein binds to inorganic polyphosphate 
                     (polyP). In the presence of polyP, S2 forms a complex with 
                     the Lon protease and is degraded by it |CITS: 
                     [11474114][16337203]|. S2 was also shown to crosslink to 
                     IF3 |CITS: [7020604]|.
                     A protein-enzyme interactions (PEIs) study that examined 
                     the connection between protein-protein interactions (PPIs) 
                     and metabolomics networks studied in 22 different 
                     environmental conditions found that the PEI RpsB-|FRAME: 
                     ADHE-MONOMER AdhE| may have a previously unknown role in 
                     regulating metabolism, in part because the PEI is conserved
                     across many other bacterial taxa |CITS: [39903745]|.
                     A low-resolution cryo-electron microscopy map of the 
                     ribosome containing S2 has been analyzed |CITS: 
                     [12809609]|."
