                     /label=cdsA
     CDS             192164..193021
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="cdsA"
                     /locus_tag="b0175"
                     /product="trifunctional CDP-diglyceride synthetase / 
                     CTP:phosphatidate cytidyltransferase / CTP:2,3,4-saturated 
                     L-phosphatidate cytidylyltransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.7.7.41"
                     /label=cdsA
                     /note="CDP-diglyceride synthetase catalyzes the synthesis
                     of |FRAME: CDPDIACYLGLYCEROL|, the activated form of 
                     |FRAME: L-PHOSPHATIDATE| (phosphatidic acid). |FRAME: 
                     CDPDIACYLGLYCEROL ""CDP-diacylglycerol""| is positioned at 
                     a branchpoint in the lipid biosynthetic pathway where it 
                     reacts with |FRAME: GLYCEROL-3P| to form |FRAME: 
                     L-1-PHOSPHATIDYL-GLYCEROL-P|, or with |FRAME: SER| to form 
                     |FRAME: L-1-PHOSPHATIDYL-SERINE|. It is the source of the 
                     phosphatidyl group for all of the major phospholipids in 
                     <i>E. coli</i> |CITS: [14213340][ 
                     5336962][4879388][4567788][4574544][4551982][30751]|.
                     The properties of both the partially purified |CITS: 
                     [30751]| and purified |CITS: [2995359]| enzyme have been 
                     studied. Mutants in <i>cdsA</i> contain significantly 
                     elevated levels of |FRAME: L-PHOSPHATIDATE| (phosphatidic 
                     acid) <i>in vivo</i> |CITS: [6243645][6273438][6296051]|. 
                     CdsA is implicated in the synthesis of the glycolipid 
                     |FRAME: CPD-15878| |CITS: [30718729]|.
                     Reviews: |CITS: [9370328]|, and Cronan, J.E. Jr., and C.O. 
                     Rock (2008) ""Biosynthesis of Membrane Lipids"" EcoSal 
                     3.6.4 |CITS: [ecosal]|"
