     gene            206166..208307
                     /gene="ldcC"
                     /locus_tag="b0186"
                     /label=ldcC
     CDS             206166..208307
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ldcC"
                     /locus_tag="b0186"
                     /product="bifunctional lysine decarboxylase 2 / lysine 
                     decarboxylase"
                     /EC_number="4.1.1.18"
                     /label=ldcC
                     /note="There are two lysine decarboxylases in <i>E.
                     coli</i>, encoded by the <i>cadA</i> and <i>ldcC</i> genes.
                      The <i>ldcC</i> gene product, lysine decarboxylase 2 
                     (LdcC), differs from the <i>cadA</i>-encoded enzyme in that
                     it is weakly expressed, is more thermosensitive and has 
                     activity over a broad range of pH with a higher pH optimum 
                     than CadA |CITS: 
                     [6767710][6349639][9339543][9226257][9534244]|.
                     A 3D cryo-EM reconstruction of LdcC has been compared to 
                     that of CadA; the C-terminal &beta;-sheet provides a 
                     sequence signature that allows classification of enzymes 
                     into LdcC-like vs. CadA-like and explains why only CadA, 
                     but not LdcC, can interact with RavA |CITS: [27080013]|. 
                     <i>ldcC</i> is expressed at very low levels |CITS: 
                     [9534244]| and shows RpoS-dependent induction during 
                     stationary phase |CITS: [9692215][9829938]|.  The alarmone 
                     (p)ppGpp inhibits LdcC activity |CITS: [21957966]|. 
                     Expression of <i>ldcC</i> is downregulated under simulated 
                     microgravity conditions |CITS: [23472115]|.
                     A mutant that is missing all eight genes involved in 
                     polyamine biosynthesis, &Delta;<i>speABCDEF cadA ldcC</i>, 
                     grows aerobically at a reduced rate.  However, polyamines 
                     are required for growth under anaerobic conditions and at 
                     very high oxygen levels |CITS: [19542271]|.
                     LdcC: ""<b>l</b>ysine <b>d</b>e<b>c</b>arboxylase, 
                     <b>c</b>onstitutive"" |CITS: [9339543]|
                     Review: |CITS: [22812515]|"
