     CDS             208818..210116
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="tilS"
                     /locus_tag="b0188"
                     /product="tRNA(Ile)-lysidine synthetase"
                     /EC_number="6.3.4.19"
                     /label=tilS
                     /note="TilS is a tRNA<sup>Ile</sup>-lysidine synthetase,
                     the enzyme responsible for modifying the wobble base of the
                     CAU anticodon of tRNA<sup>Ile</sup> at the keto group in 
                     position 2 of C34 such that it exhibits proper recognition 
                     of the AUA codon rather than the AUG codon |CITS: 
                     [14527414]|.  This modification is necessary and sufficient
                     for correct charging of the tRNA with isoleucine (not 
                     methionine) |CITS: [3054566][14527414][19233850]|.
                     TilS recognizes and modifies the precursor form of 
                     tRNA<sup>Ile</sup>, thus ensuring the fidelity and avoiding
                     errors in translation.  Unmodified C34 is only found in 
                     pre-tRNA<sup>Ile</sup>; mature tRNA<sup>Ile</sup> contains 
                     the modified L34 base.  Thus, it is not possible to 
                     generate mischarged Met-tRNA<sup>Ile</sup><sub>CAU</sub> 
                     |CITS: [19847269]|. TilS recognizes the anticodon loop, the
                     anticodon stem, and the acceptor stem of tRNA, allowing it 
                     to discriminate between tRNA<sup>Ile</sup> and 
                     tRNA<sup>Met</sup>, which are structurally similar and 
                     share the same anticodon loop |CITS: [16039592]|.  
                     t<sup>6</sup>A-modified tRNA<sup>Ile</sup><sub>CAU</sub> is
                     a better substrate for TilS than the unmodified tRNA |CITS:
                     [26337258]|.  Various analogs of L-lysine have been tested 
                     as inhibitors or alternative substrates for the enzyme 
                     |CITS: [19233850]|. <i>tilS</i> is an essential gene |CITS:
                     [14527414][16738554]|.  A <i>tilS</i> reduction-of-function
                     mutation causes defects in translation of AUA codons |CITS:
                     [14527414]|.
                     TilS: <b>t</b>RNA(<b>I</b>le)-<b>l</b>ysidine 
                     <b>s</b>ynthetase |CITS: [14527414]|
                     Reviews: |CITS: [15124629][19944692][22905870]|"
