     gene            complement(210165..210419)
                     /gene="rof"
                     /locus_tag="b0189"
                     /label=rof
     CDS             complement(210165..210419)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rof"
                     /locus_tag="b0189"
                     /product="modulator of Rho-dependent transcription
                     termination"
                     /label=rof
                     /note="Rof interacts with the Rho terminator protein.  It 
                     inhibits binding of Rho to ssDNA <i>in vitro</i> and shows 
                     antiterminator activity <i>in vivo</i> |CITS: 
                     [9723924][17565995]|.
                     The Rho transcription termination factor co-purifies with 
                     Rof.  Expression of Rof reduces termination at the 
                     Rho-dependent terminator t<sub>L1</sub> and <i>rho</i> 
                     itself <i>in vivo</i> |CITS: [9723924]|.
                     A solution structure of Rof has been determined.  A docked 
                     model of the Rof-Rho complex based on NMR titrations 
                     suggests that Rof acts as a competitive inhibitor of Rho 
                     RNA binding.  <i>In vitro</i>, Rof inhibits Rho binding to 
                     ssDNA |CITS: [17565995]|.
                     <i>rof</i> is a multicopy suppressor of 
                     temperature-sensitive alleles of genes such as <i>ftsA</i>,
                     <i>ftsQ</i>, <i>groEL</i>, <i>grpE</i>, a <i>malE-minE</i> 
                     fusion allele |CITS: [9723924]|, and an <i>rpoB</i> allele 
                     |CITS: [15836776]|.  Suppression appears to be due to 
                     antitermination |CITS: [9723924]|. Expression of 
                     <i>yaeP-rof</i> is growth rate-regulated |CITS: 
                     [9723924]|."
                     /translation="MNDTYQPINCDDYDNLELACQHHLMLTLELKDGEKLQAKASDLVS
