     gene            211756..212466
                     /gene="nlpE"
                     /locus_tag="b0192"
                     /label=nlpE
     CDS             211756..212466
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="nlpE"
                     /locus_tag="b0192"
                     /product="sensor lipoprotein NlpE"
                     /label=nlpE
                     /note="NlpE is an outer membrane lipoprotein |CITS:
                     [7635808]|. NlpE acts as a 'sentry protein' for envelope 
                     stress signals; NlpE specifically activates the |FRAME: 
                     PWY0-1485 ""Cpx signaling pathway""| to provide a 
                     protective response when lipoprotein transport to the outer
                     membrane is disturbed or when oxidative folding is 
                     impaired; NlpE mislocalization at the inner membrane 
                     signals lipoprotein sorting stress to the Cpx system; NlpE 
                     interacts physically with |FRAME: CPLX0-8270 CpxA| |CITS: 
                     [28416660][30833359]| (and see further |CITS: 
                     [31138744][36920223]|). NlpE activates the Cpx system in 
                     response to copper stress |CITS: [31138744]|).
                     NlpE is a <i>bona fide</i> OM sensor; NlpE interacts with 
                     the major outer membrane protein |FRAME: EG10669-MONOMER 
                     OmpA|; both NlpE and OmpA are required to activate the Cpx 
                     response in surface-adhered cells; NlpE senses 
                     overexpression of OmpA, but not other OMPs |CITS: 
                     [37022159]|.
                     NlpE consists of two globular, &beta;-barrrel containing 
                     domains (N-terminal and C-terminal) joined by a linker and 
                     may exist as a monomer <i>in vivo</i>; a conserved CXXC 
                     metal-binding motif is located in the N-terminal domain 
                     (the cysteines of this motif are reduced in solution but 
                     form a disulfide bond in the crystal structure); an 
                     intramolecular disulfide bond is formed in the C-terminal 
                     domain |CITS: [17698001]|.
                     NlpE, mislocalized to the inner membrane, induces |FRAME: 
                     CPLX0-2921 ""DegP""|; a non-lipidated derivative of NlpE 
                     which is mostly found in the periplasm, does not induce 
                     DegP |CITS: [15252048]|. NlpE, mislocalized to the inner 
                     membrane, activates the Cpx system more strongly than 
                     overproduction of the wild-type protein; the C-terminal 
                     domain is dispensable for Cpx activation when NlpE is 
                     mislocalized at the inner membrane; the disulfide 
                     containing C-terminal  domain is implicated in Cpx 
                     activation when oxidative folding is impaired |CITS: 
                     [26908573]| (see further |CITS: [31138744]|). 
                     Overexpression of NlpE suppresses the extracytoplasmic 
                     toxicity of a LamB-LacZ-PhoA fusion protein and a mutant 
                     LamB protein |CITS: [7635808]|, and the 
                     temperature-sensitive phenotypes of a |FRAME: RPOE-MONOMER 
                     ""sigma E""| null mutation (<i>rpoE::</i>&Omega;Cm) |CITS: 
                     [9271123]| and a <i>degP</i> null mutation 
                     (<i>degP::kan</i>) |CITS: [11514504]|, by activating the 
                     Cpx system. Overexpression of <i>nlpE</i> induces 
                     transcription of <i>degP</i> and <i>dsbA</i> though the Cpx
                     pathway |CITS: [7883164][9159399]|. NlpE is required for 
                     induction of the Cpx pathway during surface adhesion; 
                     transcriptional activation of <i>cpxR</i> in response to 
                     adhesion is abolished in &Delta;<i>nlpE</i> cells |CITS: 
                     [11830644]| although this result may have been affected by 
                     the presence of copper |CITS: [30412611]|. NlpE is not 
                     required for induction of the Cpx pathway in response to a 
                     variety envelope stresses (eg. accumulation of misfolded 
                     pilus subunits in the periplasm) |CITS: [12670966]|. 
                     Adhesion to hydrophobic surfaces is impaired in an 
                     <i>nlpE</i> mutant (<i>nlpE::spc</I>) |CITS: [11830644]|. 
                     <i>nlpE</i>: ""new lipoprotein E"" |CITS: 
                     [7635808]|<BR><i>cutF</i>: copper tolerance (see |CITS: 
                     [7635807][25030700]|)"
