     CDS             complement(215374..216081)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="trmO"
                     /locus_tag="b0195"
                     /product="tRNA m(6)t(6)A37 methyltransferase"
                     /label=trmO
                     /note="tRNA m<sup>6</sup>t<sup>6</sup>A37
                     methyltransferase (TrmO) catalyzes methylation of 
                     <i>N</i><sup>6</sup> of the A37 nucleotide adjacent to the 
                     anticodon of tRNAs |FRAME: thrT-tRNA| and |FRAME: 
                     thrV-tRNA|.  The presence of the 
                     <i>N</i><sup>6</sup>-threonylcarbamoyl modification at A37 
                     is required for activity of the enzyme |CITS: [25063302]|. 
                     TrmO is able to discriminate between the four Thr-specific 
                     tRNAs in <i>E. coli</i>, only modifying the ACY-specific 
                     tRNAs containing the GGU anticodon.  The major specificity 
                     determinants within these tRNAs are C31-G39 and G34 |CITS: 
                     [25063302]|.
                     TrmO is the founding member of a novel class of 
                     SAM-dependent methyltransferases.  Site-directed 
                     mutagenesis of conserved residues that were expected to be 
                     involved in SAM binding confirmed that Arg92 and Lys136 are
                     critical for TrmO activity |CITS: [25063302]|.
                     tRNA in a strain carrying the <i>tsaA1</i> allele, which 
                     maps to 4.6 min on the <i>E. coli</i> chromosome, lacks 
                     m<sup>6</sup>t<sup>6</sup>A.  Lack of the methyl group of 
                     m<sup>6</sup>t<sup>6</sup>A37 in 
                     tRNA<sub>GGU</sub><sup>Thr</sup> reduces the efficiency of 
                     this tRNA to read its cognate codon ACC |CITS: [9537379]|. 
                     TsaA: ""<b>t</b>hreonylcarbamoyl-6(<b>s</b>ix)-<b>a</b>den 
                     osine""
                     TrmO: ""<b>tR</b>NA <b>m</b>ethyltransferase <b>O</b>"" 
                     |CITS: [25063302]|"
