     gene            complement(216078..216482)
                     /gene="rcsF"
                     /locus_tag="b0196"
                     /label=rcsF
     CDS             complement(216078..216482)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rcsF"
                     /locus_tag="b0196"
                     /product="sensor lipoprotein RcsF"
                     /label=rcsF
                     /note="RcsF is a surface exposed outer membrane
                     lipoprotein which detects perturbations or defects in the 
                     cell envelope and activates the |FRAME: PWY0-1493 ""Rcs 
                     signal transduction system""|.
                     RcsF contains a lipidated N-terminal Cys, a proline rich 
                     linker domain and a C-terminal periplasmic domain |CITS: 
                     [21454485][21471196]|; RcsF is a surface exposed 
                     lipoprotein; experimental topology analysis suggests RcsF 
                     is a transmembrane protein with the lipidated N terminus 
                     and the linker domain surface exposed and the core domain 
                     in the periplasm |CITS: [25267629]|. RcsF contains two 
                     disulfide bonds formed between non-consecutive cysteines 
                     (Cys74-Cys118 and  Cys109-Cys124); the formation of these 
                     bonds depends on the periplasmic disulfide oxidoreductase 
                     |FRAME: DISULFOXRED-MONOMER ""DsbA""| and isomerase |FRAME:
                     DSBC-CPLX ""DsbC""| |CITS: [14739460][21454485]|. The 
                     length and disordered character of the linker domain play 
                     key roles in targeting RcsF to the outer membrane |CITS: 
                     [34326538]|.
                     RcsF interacts with BamA and with the outer membrane 
                     proteins (OMPs), OmpA, OmpC and OmpF; RcsF traverses the 
                     outer membrane via the &beta;-barrel lumen of an OMP; this 
                     structure is formed during OMP folding by the |FRAME: 
                     CPLX0-3933 ""Bam complex""| |CITS: [25267629]| (see also 
                     |CITS: [25525882][32572278]|). RcsF-OMP complexes are 
                     required for sensing lipopolysaccharide (LPS) defects; 
                     mutants unable to assemble RcsF-OMP complexes cannot 
                     activate the Rcs system in response to Polymyxin B induced 
                     LPS stress; RcsF-OMP complexes sense LPS defects directly; 
                     the surface-exposed domain of RcsF is necessary for sensing
                     LPS defects |CITS: [27282389]| (and further |CITS: 
                     [34349021]|).
                     In the BamA-RcsF crystal structure determined by |CITS: 
                     [32572278]| RcsF lodges deep within the lumen of the BamA 
                     &beta;-barrel.
                     RcsF interacts with the inner membrane protein |FRAME: 
                     G7741-MONOMER ""IgaA""| <i>in vivo</i>; RcsF-IgaA complex 
                     levels increase in response to peptidoglycan stress 
                     (mecillinam treatment); under stress conditions RcsF 
                     interacts with IgaA resulting in activation of the Rcs 
                     system; in the absence of stress IgaA is implicated in 
                     inhibiting the Rcs system |CITS: [25525882][29852010]|. 
                     RcsF interacts with the periplasmic domains of RcsC and 
                     IgaA; RcsF-RcsC interaction is required for activation of 
                     the Rcs system even when RcsF interacts with IgaA |CITS: 
                     [28691662]|. RcsF interacts with the C-terminal, 
                     periplasmic region of |FRAME: EG10669-MONOMER OmpA|; IgaA 
                     and OmpA may compete for RcsF binding in the periplasm 
                     |CITS: [32985973]|. Conformational change in RcsF-OMP 
                     complexes may facilitate interaction with IgaA |CITS: 
                     [36706155]|.
                     RcsF acts upstream of RcsC and RcsD in the Rcs signaling 
                     pathway; induction of signal via RcsF is independent of 
                     <i>rcsF</i> transcription |CITS: [16166540]|. RcsF is 
                     required to activate the Rcs phosphorelay in response to 
                     inhibition of peptidoglycan synthesis |CITS: [18192383]|. 
                     RcsF is required to activate the Rcs phosphorelay when 
                     cells are grown at low temperature (20 &deg;C) with glucose
                     and zinc |CITS: [13129944]|.  Activation of the Rcs pathway
                     in |FRAME: EG10985 ""<i>surA</i>""| null mutants is 
                     dependent upon RcsF; activation of the Rcs pathway by 
                     |FRAME: EG11570-MONOMER ""DjlA""| overproduction is RcsF 
                     independent |CITS: [16740933]| Mislocalised RcsF 
                     constitutively activates the Rcs signaling pathway |CITS: 
                     [22563052][22322964]| (see also |CITS: [23813676]|).
                     <i>rcs</i>: <U>r</U>egulator of <U>c</U>apsule 
                     <U>s</U>ynthesis |CITS: [1459951][3888955]|.
                     Related reviews: |CITS: 
                     [28674071][16153174][27839654][36892778]|."
