     gene            complement(226454..227368)
                     /gene="yafC"
                     /locus_tag="b0208"
                     /label=yafC
     CDS             complement(226454..227368)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yafC"
                     /locus_tag="b0208"
                     /product="DNA-binding transcriptional regulator YafC"
                     /label=yafC
                     /note="YafC, which contains a helix-turn-helix motif to
                     bind DNA in its N-terminal domain, appears to belong to the
                     LysR family of transcription factors (TFs), and it was 
                     predicted to regulate genes related to metabolism and 
                     chlorine resistance |CITS: [35880217]|.
                     YafC was confirmed as a TF through an integrated workflow 
                     comprised of computational prediction, knowledge-based 
                     classification, and experimental validation of candidate 
                     TFs at the genome scale |CITS: [30137486]|.
                     Compared to known global TFs, YafC exhibits some 
                     interesting regulatory features. First, it has more 
                     intragenic binding peaks and fewer peaks located within 
                     putative regulatory regions. Second, it has fewer binding 
                     peaks than global TFs, such as CRP, Lrp, Fnr, and ArcA. 
                     Third, it binds to more genes with putative functions. 
                     Finally, its expression level is lower relative to that of 
                     the majority of global TFs |CITS: [30137486]|. The most 
                     common binding mode for YafC is downstream of the RNAP 
                     binding region |CITS: [30137486]|.
                     Upstream of the <i>yafC</i> gene, a sequence was found that
                     could work as a transcriptional promoter, and the 
                     transcription of the <i>yafC</i> gene is affected by 
                     temperature |CITS: [35880217]|.
                     <i>yafC</i> insertion mutants were identified in a genetic 
                     screen for genes that are important for survival of 
                     exposure to ionizing radiation (IR).  A <i>yafC</i> 
                     deletion mutant has a moderate decrease in IR survival 
                     |CITS: [25049088]|.
                     The YafC binding landscape was globally mapped in vivo by 
                     standardized ChIP-seq and quantitatively modeled using 
                     BoltzNet, a biophysically informed neural network that 
                     infers binding energy from sequence data |CITS:[40335485]|.
                     The resulting ChIP-seq binding regions are available in 
                     RegulonDB (<a href=""https://regulondb.cc 
                     g.unam.mx/ht/dataset/TFBINDING/source=GALAGAN"">Galagan 
                     collection</a>), and the corresponding energy matrix and 
                     genomic binding profiles can be accessed at <a 
                     href=""http://boltznet.bu.edu"">boltznet.bu.edu</a> 
                     |CITS:[40335485]|."
