     gene            complement(241552..242292)
                     /gene="dpaA"
                     /locus_tag="b0224"
                     /label=dpaA
     CDS             complement(241552..242292)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="dpaA"
                     /locus_tag="b0224"
                     /product="trifunctional peptidoglycan meso-diaminopimelic
                     acid protein amidase A / peptidoglycan meso-diaminopimelic 
                     acid protein amidase / glycine carboxypeptidase"
                     /label=dpaA
                     /note="DpaA (formerly LdtF) is a murein endopeptidase that 
                     cleaves peptidoglycan-|FRAME: EG10544-MONOMER Lpp| 
                     cross-links; the protein also has glycine-specific 
                     carboxypeptidase activity |CITS: [33947763][33941679]|. 
                     DpaA hydrolyzes amide bonds between the L-center of 
                     <i>meso</i>-diaminopimelate in peptidoglycan stem peptides 
                     and the C-terminal lysine of Lpp, and between the L-center 
                     of <i>meso</i>-diaminopimelate and a terminal glycine 
                     residue in peptidoglycan stem tetrapeptides |CITS: 
                     [33947763][33941679]|.
                     LdtF and LdtD are implicated in incorporating the 
                     fluorescent D-amino acid NADA, into peptidoglycan at acid 
                     pH; muropetides isolated from &Delta;(ldtA, ldtB, ldtC, 
                     ldtD, ldtE, ldtF) cells coexpressing <i>ldtD</i> and 
                     <i>ldtF</i> and grown at pH 5.0 contain a small proportion 
                     DAP<sup>3</sup>-DAP<sup>3</sup> cross-links (those 
                     expressing <i>ldtD</i> alone or <i>ldtF</i> alone do not 
                     show any 3-3 cross links at pH 5) |CITS: [30233559]|. 
                     Ectopic expression of LdtF alone (in a strain lacking 
                     <i>ldtABCDEF</i>; BW25113&Delta;6LDT) does not restore the 
                     presence of DAP<sup>3</sup>-DAP<sup>3</sup> cross-links 
                     however coexpression of LdtF with LdtE or LdtD increases 
                     the level of DAP<sup>3</sup>-DAP<sup>3</sup> cross-links 
                     (compared to LdtD or LdtE alone) |CITS: [30723128]|. 
                     Purified DpaA is not an L,D-transpeptidase nor an 
                     L,D-carboxypeptidase |CITS: [33947763]|.
                     YafK of enteroaggregative <i>E. coli</i> is required for 
                     development of biofilms and for wild-type transcription of 
                     genes for type II aggregative adherence fimbriae components
                     |CITS: [11555281]|. YafK of enteroaggregative <i>E. 
                     coli</i> may be secreted |CITS: [11555281]|. <I>dpaA</I> 
                     expression is &sigma;<sup>S</sup>-dependent; the  
                     <i>dpaA</i> promoter is maximally expressed in stationary 
                     phase cells |CITS: [30723128]|.
                     <i>dpaA</i>: peptidoglycan 
                     <i>meso</i>-<U>d</U>iaminopimelic acid <U>p</U>rotein 
                     <U>a</U>midase A |CITS: [33947763]|"
