                     /locus_tag="b0228"
                     /product="REP-associated tyrosine transposase"
                     /label=rayT
                     /note="TnpA<sub>REP</sub> (RayT) is closely related to 
                     IS<i>200</i>/IS<i>605</i> transposases and is associated 
                     with a <u>r</u>epetitive <u>e</u>xtragenic 
                     <u>p</u>alindromic (REP) sequence |CITS: 
                     [20085626][22199259]|.  It catalyzes cleavage and 
                     recombination of <u>b</u>acterial <u>i</u>nterspersed 
                     <u>m</u>osaic <u>e</u>lements (BIMEs) <i>in vitro</i> 
                     |CITS: [22199259]|.
                     TnpA<sub>REP</sub> binds single-stranded REP sequences 
                     containing the conserved 5' GATG tetranucleotide and 
                     catalyzes BIME cleavage both upstream and downstream of the
                     REP sequence |CITS: [22199259]|.  A crystal structure of 
                     TnpA<sub>REP</sub> bound to a REP has been solved at 2.6 
                     &Aring; resolution.  Unlike the IS<i>200</i>/IS<i>605</i> 
                     transposases, TnpA<sub>REP</sub> is momoneric and 
                     specifically requires Mn<sup>2+</sup> for cleavage and the 
                     formation of a covalent intermediate |CITS: [22885300]|.
                     RayT: ""<b>R</b>EP-<b>a</b>ssociated t<b>y</b>rosine 
                     <b>t</b>ransposase"" |CITS: [20085626]|"
