     gene            248492..248785
                     /gene="yafN"
                     /locus_tag="b0232"
                     /label=yafN
     CDS             248492..248785
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yafN"
                     /locus_tag="b0232"
                     /product="antitoxin YafN"
                     /label=yafN
                     /note="YafN is the antitoxin for the ribosome-associated
                     mRNA interferase toxin YafO |CITS: 
                     [19617347][19837801][19943910]|.
                     <i>yafN</i> is essential when <i>yafO</i> is present.  The 
                     <i>yafN</i> mutant strain of the Keio collection, JW0222 
                     |CITS: [16738554]|, also contains a frameshift mutation in 
                     <i>yafO</i>, thus making it viable |CITS: [19837801]|. 
                     Expression of <i>yafN</i> is increased by UV irradiation 
                     |CITS: [11333217]|; the <i>dinB</i> promoter is 
                     SOS-regulated |CITS: [19943910]|.  The promoter upstream of
                     <i>yafN</i> appears to be autorepressed by YafN; Lon 
                     protease is required for activation of transcription. 
                     Transcription is induced by chloramphenicol treatment, 
                     amino acid starvation induced by serine hydroxamate, and 
                     glucose starvation |CITS: [19943910]|.
                     Polar <i>dinB</i> mutations affecting the 
                     <i>dinB-yafNOP</i> operon reduce spontaneous mutagenesis 
                     |CITS: [12813093]|; however, only DinB is required for 
                     stress-induced mutagenesis |CITS: [19837801]|.
                     The YafN binding landscape was globally mapped in vivo by 
                     standardized ChIP-seq and quantitatively modeled using 
                     BoltzNet, a biophysically informed neural network that 
                     infers binding energy from sequence data |CITS:[40335485]|.
                     The resulting ChIP-seq binding regions are available in 
                     RegulonDB (<a href=""https://regulondb.cc 
                     g.unam.mx/ht/dataset/TFBINDING/source=GALAGAN"">Galagan 
                     collection</a>), and the corresponding energy matrix and 
                     genomic binding profiles can be accessed at <a 
                     href=""http://boltznet.bu.edu"">boltznet.bu.edu</a> 
                     |CITS:[40335485]|.
                     Review: |CITS: [22060041][31932311]|"
