     CDS             complement(250746..252203)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="pepD"
                     /locus_tag="b0237"
                     /product="multifunctional peptidase D / alanylglutamate
                     dipeptidase / nonspecific dipeptidase / cysteinylglycine 
                     dipeptidase"
                     /EC_number="3.4.13.18"
                     /label=pepD
                     /note="Peptidase D (PepD) is a dipeptidase capable of
                     breaking down a number of dipeptides with unblocked N 
                     termini |CITS: [355237][7988883]|, including 
                     cysteinylglycine, a breakdown product of glutathione |CITS:
                     [11157967]|. Neither proline nor non-protein amino acids 
                     are accepted in the C-terminal position |CITS: [7988883]|.
                     Transcription of <i>pepD</i> increases five fold during 
                     phosphate starvation |CITS: [1313142]|. Overexpression of 
                     <i>pepD</i> negatively affects biofilm formation |CITS: 
                     [14523117]|.
                     Using a method that distinguishes N-phosphorylation from 
                     O-phosphorylation, N-phosphorylation was detected <i>in 
                     vitro</i> |CITS: [33277485]|."
