     gene            253014..254258
                     /gene="frsA"
                     /locus_tag="b0239"
                     /label=frsA
     CDS             253014..254258
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="frsA"
                     /locus_tag="b0239"
                     /product="fermentation-respiration switch protein"
                     /label=frsA
                     /note="The FrsA protein was found to bind specifically to
                     the unphosphorylated form of enzyme IIA<sup>Glc</sup> of 
                     the PEP-sugar phosphotransferase system and is suggested to
                     aid IIA<sup>Glc</sup> in regulating the flux between 
                     respiration and fermentation pathways |CITS: [15169777]|. 
                     Esterase activity of FrsA was discovered in a 
                     high-throughput screen of purified proteins |CITS: 
                     [15808744]|.  FrsA from <i>Vibrio vulnificus</i> is a 
                     pyruvate decarboxylase |CITS: [21623357]|.
                     Mutation of the <i>frsA</i> gene results in increased 
                     respiration on sugars including glucose.  Overexpression of
                     FrsA, on the other hand, results in increased fermentation 
                     of these sugars, leading to the accumulation of mixed-acid 
                     fermentation products |CITS: [15169777]|. Orthologs of the 
                     <i>frsA</i> gene have so far only been found in facultative
                     anaerobes belonging to the &gamma; proteobacteria |CITS: 
                     [15169777]|.
                     FrsA: ""<b>f</b>ermentation/<b>r</b>espiration 
                     <b>s</b>witch protein"" |CITS: [15169777]|"
                     /translation="MTQANLSETLFKPRFKHPETSTLVRRFNHGAQPPVQSALDGKTIP
