     gene            complement(274525..274873)
                     /pseudo
                     /gene="afuB"
                     /locus_tag="b0263"
                     /label=afuB
                     /note="AfuB is a pseudogene candidate in <i>E. coli</i>
                     K-12. The orthologous gene from <i>E. coli</i> O157:H7 
                     encodes a protein of  692 amino acid residues; <i>afuB</i> 
                     from strain K-12 contains an N-terminal deletion compared 
                     to the O157 encoded ortholog |CITS: [12234664]|. 
                     <i>afuBC</i> is a remnant operon; a complete <i>afuABC</i> 
                     gene cluster is present in a wide range of bacteria and 
                     encodes a binding-protein dependent transport system 
                     initially implicated in Fe<sup>3+</sup> uptake (<i>afu</i>:
                     <u>A</u>ctinobacillus <u>f</u>erric <u>u</u>ptake) |CITS: 
                     [8807793]|, but now believed to transport sugar phosphates 
                     |CITS: [26295949]|. <i>E. coli</i> K-12 does not contain an
                     <i>afuA</i> ortholog. Comment from ASAP: The coordinates of
                     afuB have been changed from those reported in the GenBank 
                     entry (GBAN:U00096.2) to correspond to the region of 
                     similarity to Escherichia coli EDL933 (ASAP:ABH-0024350), 
                     removing 14 nucleotides from the N-terminus."
     CDS             complement(274525..274873)
                     /pseudo
                     /gene="afuB"
                     /locus_tag="b0263"
                     /product="CP4-6 prophage; ABC transporter membrane protein
                     AfuB"
                     /label=afuB
