                     /product="bifunctional CP4-6 prophage; D-xylonate
                     dehydratase / D-xylonate dehydratase"
                     /EC_number="4.2.1.82"
                     /label=yagF
                     /note="The YagF protein has D-xylonate dehydratase
                     activity |CITS: [29392388]|.
                     A <i>yjhG yagF</i> double mutant can not use D-xylonate as 
                     the sole source of carbon, and crude cell extracts do not 
                     contain D-xylonate dehydratase activity |CITS: 
                     [21917451][23233208]|.  Both phenotypes are complemented by
                     providing <i>yjhG</i> on a plasmid |CITS: [23233208]|. 
                     Overexpression of <i>yagF</i> alleviates a bottleneck in 
                     the engineered production of glycolate |CITS: [29392388]|. 
                     A <i>yagF</i> mutant is more resistant to the plant 
                     essential oil thymol than wild type |CITS: [17949301]|."
