     CDS             282500..284110
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yagH"
                     /locus_tag="b0271"
                     /product="CP4-6 prophage; putative
                     xylosidase/arabinosidase"
                     /label=yagH
                     /note="YagH is a member of the glycosyl hydrolase family
                     43 with predicted &beta;-xylosidase activity |CITS: 
                     [10486968]|.
                     <i>yagGH</i> is predicted to be a member of the |FRAME: 
                     EG20253-MONOMER ""XylR""| regulon; its products may mediate
                     transport (YagG) and hydrolysis (YagH) of 
                     xylooligosaccharides; putative XylR and CRP binding sites 
                     are identified upstream of <i>yagGH</i> |CITS: [11750821]| 
                     Based on the anomalous codon usage pattern and GC content, 
                     the <i>yagH</i> gene originates from a horizontal gene 
                     transfer event; the gene lies within the CP4-6 prophage 
                     |CITS: [10486968]|."
