                     /product="50S ribosomal subunit protein L36B"
                     /label=ykgO
                     /note="YkgO is a paralog of RpmJ, the |FRAME:
                     EG11232-MONOMER|, but lacks its zinc binding motif |CITS: 
                     [19121005]|.  YkgO is the prevalent paralog present in 
                     stationary phase ribosomes |CITS: [30359641]|.  L36B 
                     functionally substitutes for L36 |CITS: [32559334]|.
                     YkgO is not expressed during growth in rich medium, but 
                     expression is strongly induced during stationary phase in 
                     minimal medium |CITS: [19121005]|.
                     Reviews: |CITS: [36834855]|"
