     gene            complement(308225..308488)
                     /gene="ykgM"
                     /locus_tag="b0296"
                     /label=ykgM
     CDS             complement(308225..308488)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ykgM"
                     /locus_tag="b0296"
                     /product="50S ribosomal subunit protein L31B"
                     /label=ykgM
                     /note="Ribosomal protein L31B (YkgM) was first identified
                     as a precursor of RpmE, the |FRAME: EG10889-MONOMER|, in 
                     <i>E. coli</i> strain W3110 |CITS: [2181444]| and then 
                     recognized as a paralog of RpmE |CITS: [11574053]|. It is 
                     present in stationary phase ribosomes |CITS: [30359641]|, 
                     in ribosomes prepared from a &Delta;<i>rpmE zur::IS2</i> 
                     mutant, and it functionally substitutes for L31 |CITS: 
                     [32559334]|. Under lower-temperature growth conditions and 
                     in growth competition experiments, L31 confers higher 
                     fitness than L31B. In addition, L31B-containing ribosomes 
                     show reduced processivity and increased frame shifting 
                     |CITS: [32669635]|.
                     The expression of the gene <i>ykgM</i> is repressed by the 
                     protein YkgM, but it is not clear at which expression level
                     this regulation happens; it could be at the level of 
                     transcription, mRNA stability, or translation at more than 
                     one level |CITS:[36533433]|. This regulation involves a 
                     hairpin structure in the <i>ykgM</i> mRNA and the 
                     N-terminal domain of YkgM |CITS:[36533433]|.
                     YkgM has lost the predicted metal-binding ""zinc ribbon"" 
                     motif |CITS: [11574053]| and was shown to lack bound 
                     Zn<sup>2+</sup>, in contrast to L31 |CITS: [22196016]|. The
                     authors propose a model where YkgM can provide the function
                     of L31 in the ribosome under zinc-limited conditions.
                     Under Zn<sup>2+</sup>-deficient conditions, expression of 
                     <i>ykgM</i> is upregulated |CITS: [19377097][22196016]|, 
                     and a <i>ykgM</i> mutant grows more poorly than wild-type 
                     |CITS: [19377097]|. Transcription of <i>ykgMO</i> is 
                     repressed by the zinc uptake repressor Zur |CITS: 
                     [19734316]|; a binding site for Zur was predicted to be 
                     present upstream of <i>ykgM</i> |CITS: [12904577]|. 
                     Reviews: |CITS: [36834855]|"
