                     /product="hypochlorite stress response protein RclB"
                     /label=rclB
                     /note="An <i>rclB</i> deletion mutant is more sensitive to
                     HOCl treatment than wild type, and <i>rclB</i> expression 
                     is upregulated under RCS (reactive chlorine species) stress
                     conditions |CITS: [24078635]|. The expression of 
                     <i>rclB</i> is also upregulated in bacteria phagocytosed by
                     neutrophils, probably due to HOCl produced by neutrophils 
                     |CITS: [33351093]|.
                     RNAseq analysis in response to HOSCN exposure revealed the 
                     log-fold increase in <i>|FRAME: G6174|</i> was 
                     significantly higher than for <i>|FRAME: G6173|</i> and 
                     <i>|FRAME: G6171|</i>. Deletion mutants of each 
                     <i>rclABC</i> gene individually and the three genes 
                     together resulted in zinc depletion along with upregulation
                     of <i>|FRAME: G6167|</i> and <i>|FRAME: G7061|</i>, in 
                     addition to a variety of general stress response genes and 
                     some poorly characterized genes, such as <i>|FRAME: 
                     G6253|</i>. Expression of genes that responded differently 
                     to the different <i>rcl</i> mutants, such as <i>|FRAME: 
                     G6570|</i> and <i>|FRAME: EG10670|</i> were also examined 
                     |CITS: [40298396]|.
                     RclB: ""<b>r</b>eactive <b>c</b>h<b>l</b>orine resistance 
                     <b>B</b>"" |CITS: [24078635]|"
