                     /product="putative lactate utilization oxidoreductase
                     YkgE"
                     /label=ykgE
                     /note="While their physiological role in <i>E. coli</i>
                     remains unknown, the <i>ykgEFG</i> genes are homologous to 
                     newly identified lactate utilization genes in <i>Shewanella
                     oneidensis</i>.  Low-copy expression of <i>E. coli 
                     ykgEFG</i> in <i>S. oneidensis</i> complements the ability 
                     of the &Delta;<i>dld-II</i> &Delta;<i>lldF</i> double 
                     mutant for growth on L-lactate, but not D-lactate |CITS: 
                     [19196979]|.
                     Overexpression of <i>ykgEFG</i> in <i>E. coli</i> restores 
                     the ability of a |FRAME: EG10231 <i>dld</i>| mutant to grow
                     on D-lactate; crude extracts of an overexpressing strain 
                     contain elevated levels of both L- and D-lactate 
                     dehydrogenase activity |CITS: [19196979]|."
