                     /EC_number="1.2.1.8"
                     /label=betB
                     /note="Betaine aldehyde dehydrogenase (BADH) catalyzes the 
                     second step in the biosynthesis of the osmoprotectant 
                     glycine betaine from choline |CITS: [3512525][2194570]|. 
                     Expression of the <i>bet</i> operon is regulated by oxygen,
                     choline, osmotic stress, and temperature |CITS: 
                     [3141381][8626294]|.
                     Inactivation of six genes encoding aldehyde dehydrogenases 
                     (|FRAME: EG12292|, |FRAME: EG10036|, |FRAME: EG10110|, 
                     |FRAME: G6755|, |FRAME: G7961|, and |FRAME: EG11329|) 
                     resulted in a strain with greatly reduced aromatic aldehyde
                     oxidation activity (the strain was named ROAR for reduced 
                     oxidation and reduction of aromatic aldehydes) |CITS: [ 
                     37100193]|.
                     BetB: ""<b>bet</b>aine"" |CITS: [3065456]|"
