     gene            344393..345283
                     /gene="prpB"
                     /locus_tag="b0331"
                     /label=prpB
     CDS             344393..345283
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="prpB"
                     /locus_tag="b0331"
                     /product="2-methylisocitrate lyase"
                     /EC_number="4.1.3.30"
                     /label=prpB
                     /note="2-Methylisocitrate lyase (PrpB) catalyzes the
                     cleavage of 2-methylisocitrate to succinate and pyruvate, 
                     which is the final step in propionate metabolism via the 
                     methylcitrate cycle |CITS: [11422389][12473114]|.  The 
                     enzyme activity is sensitive to oxidation and is 
                     inactivated by 3-bromopyruvate alkylation |CITS: 
                     [11422389]|.
                     Crystal structures of the wild type and mutant enzyme in 
                     the apo- and product-bound forms have been solved |CITS: 
                     [12706720][15723538]|.  The structures enabled modeling of 
                     the active site and proposal of a catalytic mechanism 
                     involving an &alpha;-carboxy-carbanion transition state 
                     |CITS: [12706720][15723538]|.
                     Protein production is observed during growth on propionate,
                     but not acetate |CITS: [12473114]| or glucose |CITS: 
                     [11422389]|.  Expression of <i>prpBCDE</i> is regulated by 
                     PrpR and catabolite repression |CITS: [15805526]| and is 
                     downregulated in the presence of a variety of sugars |CITS:
                     [22579471]|."
