     CDS             350633..351892
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="codB"
                     /locus_tag="b0336"
                     /product="cytosine transporter"
                     /label=codB
                     /note="CodB is a cytosine transporter which probably
                     functions as a cytosine/proton symporter. Whole cell 
                     transport assays have shown that the cloned <I>codB</I> 
                     gene can complement mutants with cytosine transport defects
                     which had mapped to a locus near the <I>codA</I> gene 
                     |CITS: [1640834]|. The <I>codB</I> gene is located in a 
                     cytosine-inducible operon with the <I>codA</I> gene 
                     encoding cytosine deaminase |CITS: [7500333] [1640834]|. 
                     Consistent with this, CodB belongs to the NCS1 family of 
                     purine and pyrimidine transporters |CITS: [10082980]|. 
                     Analysis of alkaline phosphatase and &beta;-galactosidase 
                     fusions has suggested that CodB consists of twelve TMS 
                     |CITS: [8535518]|. Imported cytosine can be metabolised via
                     hydrolytic deamination by CodA to yield uracil and 
                     ammonia."
