                     /product="cyanate transporter"
                     /label=cynX
                     /note="CynX is a putative cyanate transporter. CynX is a
                     member of the major facilitator superfamily (MFS) of 
                     transporters |CITS: [9529885]|, and the <I>cynX</I> gene 
                     has been shown to be part of a cyanate-induced operon with 
                     <I>cynS</I> and <I>cynT</I>, encoding cyanase and carbonic 
                     anhydrase, respectively |CITS: [8444806] [3049588]|. 
                     However, no phenotype has been observed for a knockout 
                     mutation in <I>cynX</I> |CITS: [8444806]|. Overexpression 
                     of <i>cynX</i> confers resistance to bromoacetate |CITS: 
                     [20921376]|."
