                     /product="bifunctional acetaldehyde dehydrogenase
                     (acetylating) MhpF / acetaldehyde dehydrogenase 
                     (acetylating)"
                     /EC_number="1.2.1.10"
                     /label=mhpF
                     /note="<i>mhpF</i> encodes an acetylating acetaldehyde 
                     dehydrogenase |CITS: [9098055]|.  MhpF is active as a 
                     monomer; the rate-limiting step of the reaction appears to 
                     be transthioesterification |CITS: [23237860]|.
                     MhpF is involved in synthesis of <i>n</i>-butanol in an 
                     engineered reversal of the &beta;-oxidation pathway |CITS: 
                     [21832992]|.
                     The expression of MhpE is translationally coupled to MhpF, 
                     and interaction between the two proteins appears to be 
                     required for solubility of MhpE |CITS: [16782065]|."
