                     /product="4-hydroxy-2-oxovalerate aldolase"
                     /EC_number="4.1.3.39"
                     /label=mhpE
                     /note="4-hydroxy-2-ketopentanoate aldolase (MhpE) is a 
                     stereospecific class I aldolase |CITS: [9758851]|.
                     The expression of MhpE is translationally coupled to MhpF, 
                     and interaction between the two proteins appears to be 
                     required for solubility of MhpE |CITS: [16782065]|.
                     <i>E. coli</i> is able to utilize certain aromatic acids as
                     carbon and energy sources.  A meta-cleavage pathway 
                     involving MhpE is used for the catabolism of 
                     3-phenylpropionate |CITS: [6345502]|.
                     MhpE: ""<b>m</b>-<b>h</b>ydroxyphenyl<b>p</b>ropionate"""
