                     /gene="frmA"
                     /locus_tag="b0356"
                     /product="S-(hydroxymethyl)glutathione dehydrogenase"
                     /EC_number="1.1.1.284"
                     /label=frmA
                     /note="Glutathione-dependent formaldehyde dehydrogenase
                     (GS-FDH) belongs to the family of class III alcohol 
                     dehydrogenases. Glutathione and formaldehyde combine 
                     non-enzymatically to form hydroxymethylglutathione, the 
                     true substrate of the GS-FDH catalyzed reaction. The 
                     product, S-formylglutathione, is further metabolized to 
                     formic
                     acid. The functional role of GS-FDH may be in the 
                     metabolism of endogenously formed formaldehyde and 
                     detoxifying
                     exogenous formaldehyde |CITS: [1731906] [9333139]|. 
                     Transcription of the <i>frmRAB</i> operon is induced by 
                     formaldehyde, but not <i>S</i>-nitrosoglutathione
                     |CITS: [9333139][15466022]|."
