     CDS             377130..378035
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="insD1"
                     /locus_tag="b0361"
                     /product="IS2 element protein"
                     /label=insD1
                     /note="No specific function has been identified for this
                     protein that is coded for by the IS2 insertion sequence 
                     element.
                     IS2 is an insertion sequence present in from 0-12 copies in
                     various strains of
                     <i>E. coli</i> |CITS: [4577900][6282688][2830172]|.
                     Though it can cause activation and suppression of adjacent 
                     genes, activation
                     appears to be due to generation of novel promoters during 
                     the insertion process
                     rather than to the presence of promoters carried within IS2
                     |CITS: [4610339][329104][6291000]|.
                     In addition to autoregulation by
                     InsA, transcription of IS2 genes is negatively regulated by
                     |FRAME: CPLX0-226| |CITS: [9573153]|.
                     IS2 locations in the <i>E. coli</i> genome correlate with 
                     Hfr origins and F' factor
                     crossover points |CITS: [2553981]|."
