     gene            393328..394422
                     /gene="yaiW"
                     /locus_tag="b0378"
                     /label=yaiW
     CDS             393328..394422
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yaiW"
                     /locus_tag="b0378"
                     /product="surface-exposed outer membrane lipoprotein"
                     /label=yaiW
                     /note="YaiW possesses an N-terminal lipobox sequence which
                     lacks the inner membrane retention signal; YaiW is surface 
                     exposed; the highly similar YaiW protein from <i>Salmonella
                     typhimurium</i> is a surface exposed outer membrane 
                     lipoprotein |CITS: [24214946]|.
                     An <i>E. coli &Delta;yaiW</i> strain has moderately 
                     stronger growth in the presence of sublethal concentrations
                     of two truncated species of the antimicrobial peptide Bac7 
                     and a decreased internalisation of the peptide species. 
                     Deletion of <i>yaiW</i> does not affect sensitivity to 
                     other antimicrobial peptides species such as bleomycin 
                     sulfate and microcin B17 |CITS: [24214946]|.
                     A &Delta;<i>yaiW</i> strain shows enhanced secretion of the
                     extracellular protein |FRAME: EG11807-MONOMER ""YebF""| and
                     of YebF fusion proteins possibly due to defects in the 
                     outer membrane; a &Delta;<i>yaiF</i> strain shows signs of 
                     envelope instability |CITS: [28182400]|. The <i>yaiW</i> 
                     gene is a member of the &sigma;<sup>E</sup> regulon |CITS: 
                     [12900013]|. <i>yaiW</i> is cotranscribed with <i>sbmA</i> 
                     |CITS: [24214946]|.
                     "
