                     /label=ddlA
     CDS             complement(395285..396379)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ddlA"
                     /locus_tag="b0381"
                     /product="bifunctional D-alanine--D-alanine ligase A / 
                     D-alanine--D-alanine ligase"
                     /EC_number="6.3.2.4"
                     /label=ddlA
                     /note="DdlA is one of two D-alanine&mdash;D-alanine
                     ligases in <i>E. coli</i> |CITS: [1993184]|. 
                     D-alanine&mdash;D-alanine ligase, along with alanine 
                     racemase, makes up the D-alanine branch of peptidoglycan 
                     biosynthesis.  The enzyme combines two molecules of 
                     D-alanine to form D-alanyl-D-alanine, which is then added 
                     to the growing cell wall precursor. 
                     D-alanine&mdash;D-alanine ligase is an antibacterial drug 
                     target; it was long known to be the target of D-cycloserine
                     |CITS: [14188160]|.
                     The Keio collection <i>ddlA</i> mutant is 8-fold more 
                     sensitive to X-ray radiation than wild type |CITS: 
                     [27718375]|."
