     gene            396842..397102
                     /gene="iraP"
                     /locus_tag="b0382"
                     /label=iraP
     CDS             396842..397102
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="iraP"
                     /locus_tag="b0382"
                     /product="anti-adaptor protein IraP"
                     /label=iraP
                     /note="IraP is one of several small anti-adaptor proteins;
                     it is required for stabilization of the alternative sigma 
                     factor |FRAME: RPOS-MONOMER &sigma;<sup>S</sup>| during 
                     phosphate starvation and plays a role in stationary phase 
                     and nitrogen starvation.  The |FRAME: EG12121-MONOMER RssB|
                     adaptor protein binds to &sigma;<sup>S</sup> and targets it
                     to the ClpXP protease for degradation.  IraP does not 
                     affect the level or stability of RssB, but interferes 
                     directly with RssB-mediated degradation of 
                     &sigma;<sup>S</sup> by interacting with RssB |CITS: 
                     [16600914]|.  Each anti-adaptor protein interacts with RssB
                     in a unique way |CITS: [24352426][25988182]|.  IraP does 
                     not inactivate ClpXP |CITS: [16600914]|.
                     Expression of <i>iraP</i> is induced by phosphate 
                     starvation; the effect is mediated by ppGpp and requires 
                     SpoT, but not RelA |CITS: [17640895]|.  CsgD was also shown
                     to induce <i>iraP</i> expression |CITS: 
                     [16513732][17873038]|.
                     IraP is one of a number of proteins with <b>h</b>igh 
                     <b>U</b>UX <b>L</b>eucine <b>c</b>odon usage (HULC 
                     proteins).  tRNA modification by |FRAME: EG10595-MONOMER 
                     MiaA| is required for efficient decoding of UUX-leucine 
                     codons, and thus is at least in part responsible for 
                     efficient translation of both RpoS and IraP |CITS: 
                     [26979278]|.
                     IraP: ""<b>i</b>nhibitor of <b>R</b>ssB <b>a</b>ctivity 
                     during <b>p</b>hosphate starvation"" |CITS: [16600914]| 
                     Review: |CITS: [31197038]|"
                     /translation="MKNLIAELLFKLAQKEEESKELCAQVEALEIIVTAMLRNMAQNDQ
                     QRLIDQVEGALYEVKPDASIPDDDTELLRDYVKKLLKHPRQ"
