                     /product="protein AroM"
                     /label=aroM
                     /note="AroM is encoded in an operon together with AroL, 
                     shikimate kinase II |CITS: [3001024][3001025]|.  AroM is 
                     not required for growth on minimal medium, and its function
                     is unknown |CITS: [3001024]|.
                     In a random transposon mutagenesis screen, <i>aroM</i> was 
                     indentified as a gene whose inactivation is beneficial for 
                     anaerobic hydrogen production from glycerol in early log 
                     phase.  A &Delta;<i>aroM</i> mutant strain grows slightly 
                     faster than the parent strain under anaerobic conditions 
                     |CITS: [25567513]|."
