     CDS             complement(404564..405475)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rdgC"
                     /locus_tag="b0393"
                     /product="nucleoid-associated protein RdgC"
                     /label=rdgC
                     /note="RdgC is a 34 kDa nucleoid-associated protein |CITS: 
                     [10368163]| believed to function as a regulator of |FRAME: 
                     EG10823-MONOMER RecA| activity. RdgC inhibits RecA-mediated
                     strand exchange <i>in vitro</i>, probably by competing with
                     RecA for DNA binding sites |CITS: [16377615]|.
                     RdgC binds non-specifically to both ssDNA and dsDNA and is 
                     expressed at high levels in the exponential growth phase 
                     |CITS: [12554673]|. RdgC is essential for growth in 
                     recombination-deficient <i>E. coli</i> strains |CITS: 
                     [8807285]| and in strains lacking the primosome factor 
                     |FRAME: EG10763-MONOMER PriA| |CITS: [12554673]|. 
                     Double-strand DNA breaks accumulate in an 
                     &Delta;<i>rdgC</i> strain; <i>Tn</i>-seq data indicates 
                     that <i>rdgC</i> has enhanced importance when <i>priB</i> 
                     is deleted |CITS: [36326440]|.
                     RdgC exists in solution as a mixture of monomers, dimers 
                     and tetramers |CITS: [16377615]|. RdgC crystallises as a 
                     dimer and forms a toroidal ring structure proposed to 
                     encircle DNA |CITS: [17308310][20525790]|.
                     <i>rdgC</i>: <U>r</U>ecombination-<U>d</U>ependent 
                     <U>g</U>rowth |CITS: [8807285]|.
                     "
