     CDS             complement(406753..407937)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="araJ"
                     /locus_tag="b0396"
                     /product="putative transport protein AraJ"
                     /label=araJ
                     /note="AraJ is predicted to be an inner membrane protein
                     with 12 transmembrane domains |CITS: [15919996][1744033]|. 
                     Expression of <i>araJ</i> is induced in the presence of 
                     arabinose and transcription requires AraC and CRP-cAMP 
                     |CITS: [7047752][2231717]|. Disruption of <i>araJ</i> does 
                     not have an apparent effect on arabinose uptake or 
                     utilisation |CITS: [1744033]|. AraJ is not required for the
                     intracellular arabinose depletion that is associated with 
                     'off-switching' of the inducible arabinose utilization 
                     system |CITS: [24586851]|. Heterologous expression of 
                     <i>araJ</i> enhances arabinose transport in a |FRAME: 
                     TAX-1142| strain engineered to utilize arabinose |CITS: 
                     [34387784]|.
                     In the Transporter Classification Database |CITS: 
                     [33170213]| AraJ is a member of the Drug:H<sup>+</sup> 
                     Antiporter-1 family within the Major Facilitator 
                     Superfamily |CITS: [9529885]|."
