                     /locus_tag="b0401"
                     /label=brnQ
     CDS             415047..416366
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="brnQ"
                     /locus_tag="b0401"
                     /product="branched chain amino acid transporter BrnQ"
                     /label=brnQ
                     /note="BrnQ is a probable branched chain amino acid
                     transporter. BrnQ is highly similar to the <I>Salmonella 
                     typhimurium</I> BrnQ branched chain amino acid transporter 
                     |CITS: [3078876]| and very probably corresponds to the 
                     LIV-II branched chain amino acid transport system in <I>E. 
                     coli</I>, which has been shown to transport leucine, 
                     valine, and isoleucine |CITS: [4590465][4945181][361686]|. 
                     In the Transporter Classification Database |CITS: 
                     [33170213]| BrnQ is a member of the LIVCS family of 
                     branched chain amino acid transporters and probably 
                     functions as a branched chain amino acid:Na<sup>+</sup> 
                     symporter.
                     BrnQ is a low-affinity threonine transporter that is of 
                     minor relevance for normal cell physiology |CITS: 
                     [37025642]|."
