     CDS             complement(419793..420374)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="acpH"
                     /locus_tag="b0404"
                     /product="acyl carrier protein phosphodiesterase"
                     /EC_number="3.1.4.14"
                     /label=acpH
                     /note="Acyl carrier protein (ACP) phosphodiesterase is 
                     responsible for the cleavage of |FRAME: PANTETHEINE-P| 
                     (4'-PP) from |FRAME: ACP| by hydrolysis of the 
                     phosphodiester linkage between 4'-PP and the hydroxyl group
                     of a serine residue of the ACP apoprotein 
                     |CITS:[16107329]|. This reaction requires divalent cations 
                     |CITS:[4290442]|.
                     Monomeric and trimeric forms of the purified protein are 
                     present in solution |CITS:[16107329]|.
                     AcpH is responsible for turnover of the ACP prosthetic 
                     group <i>in vivo</i>, but is not essential for growth. The 
                     physiological role of AcpH is unknown |CITS:[16107329]|. 
                     Review: |CITS: [37345808]|"
