     CDS             422743..423075
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yajC"
                     /locus_tag="b0407"
                     /product="trifunctional Sec translocon accessory complex
                     subunit YajC / Sec translocon accessory complex / Sec 
                     Holo-Translocon"
                     /label=yajC
                     /note="YajC is is part of the heterotrimeric Sec
                     translocon accessory complex.
                     Early studies characterized the <i>secD</i> locus (composed
                     of <i>yajC-secD-secF</i>), implicating the products of 
                     <i>secD</i> and <i>secF</i> in protein export and defining 
                     YajC as a dispensable membrane protein with unknown 
                     function |CITS:[3029032][2170107][8428584][7507921]|. Under
                     conditions of over production YajC forms a complex with 
                     both SecYEG and SecDF |CITS: [12068816]|. YajC is not 
                     essential for cell viability or protein export |CITS: 
                     [8190079], [7507921]|. Membrane topology experiments 
                     indicate that the C-terminus of YajC is located in the 
                     cytoplasm and the N-terminus is buried in the membrane 
                     |CITS: [21235483]|. The purified C-terminal portion of YajC
                     exists as a trimer and forms a structure rich in 
                     &beta;-strands |CITS: [21235483]|."
                     /translation="MSFFISDAVAATGAPAQGSPMSLILMLVVFGLIFYFMILRPQQKR
                     TKEHKKLMDSIAKGDEVLTNGGLVGRVTKVAENGYIAIALNDTTEVVIKRDFVAAVLPK
                     GTMKAL"
