                     /locus_tag="b0415"
                     /product="6,7-dimethyl-8-ribityllumazine synthase"
                     /EC_number="2.5.1.78"
                     /label=ribE
                     /note="The <i>ribE</i> gene encodes lumazine synthase, an
                     enzyme that catalyzes the penultimate step in the 
                     riboflavin
                     biosynthesis pathway.  The protein forms a hollow 
                     icosahedral capsid composed of 60 subunits.  Unlike 
                     lumazine
                     synthase from <i>Bacillus subtilis</i>, the <i>E. coli</i> 
                     enzyme is not physically associated with any other enzyme 
                     of
                     the riboflavin biosynthetic pathway, including riboflavin 
                     synthase |CITS: [8969176]|.
                     <i>ribE</i> is an essential gene |CITS: [16738554]|."
