     CDS             431090..432067
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="thiL"
                     /locus_tag="b0417"
                     /product="thiamine monophosphate kinase"
                     /EC_number="2.7.4.16"
                     /label=thiL
                     /note="Thiamine phosphate kinase (ThiL) is involved in the
                     final step of thiamine biosynthesis. ThiL catalyzes the 
                     phosphorylation of thiamine monophosphate to yield thiamine
                     diphosphate in the presence of ATP and Mg<sup>2+</sup> 
                     |CITS: [4567662][4550824][6284709]|. Mutations in 
                     <i>thiL</i> resulted in a requirement for thiamine 
                     pyrophosphate for growth |CITS: [10382260]|. In 
                     <i>Salmonella typhimurium</i>, altered ThiL activity 
                     resulted in decreased repression of transcription of 
                     thiamine pyrophosphate-regulated genes |CITS: [9188462]|. 
                     The ThiL structure with substrate and product complexes in 
                     <i>Aquifex aeolicus</i> was determined |CITS: [18311927]|."
