     gene            complement(432617..433591)
                     /gene="yajO"
                     /locus_tag="b0419"
                     /label=yajO
     CDS             complement(432617..433591)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yajO"
                     /locus_tag="b0419"
                     /product="bifunctional 1-deoxyxylulose-5-phosphate
                     synthase YajO / D-ribulose 5-phosphate 1-dehydrogenase"
                     /label=yajO
                     /note="YajO is able to synthesize 1-deoxy-D-xylulose
                     5-phosphate (DXP) from ribulose 5-phosphate, providing a 
                     novel route from a pentose phosphate to DXP |CITS: 
                     [25326299]|.  Overexpression of YajO from a multicopy 
                     plasmid leads to resistance to the 
                     4-amino-2-methyl-5-hydroxymethylpyrimidine (HMP) analog 
                     bacimethrin.  The resistance mechanism is undetermined, but
                     does not involve biosynthesis of HMP |CITS: [15292217]|; 
                     increased synthesis of DXP, a precursor of thiamine, is one
                     of the possibilities |CITS: [25326299]|. YajO is similar to
                     the AKR7 family of aldo-keto reductases.  Purified YajO 
                     showed 2-carboxybenzaldehyde reductase activity, but not 
                     methylglyoxal reductase activity |CITS: 
                     [16077126][23990306]|.
                     Growth of a <i>yajO gloA</i> double mutant is inhibited by 
                     0.3 mM methylglyoxal, but expression of <i>yajO</i> is not 
                     increased in response to methylglyoxal |CITS: [16077126]|. 
                     Overexpression of <i>yajO</i> from a plasmid supports cell 
                     viability in the absence of the essential 
                     <i>dxs</i>-encoded |FRAME: DXS-MONOMER| |CITS: [25326299]|.
                     Review: |CITS: [23103600]|
                     "
