     gene            complement(439060..439971)
                     /gene="panE"
                     /locus_tag="b0425"
                     /label=panE
     CDS             complement(439060..439971)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="panE"
                     /locus_tag="b0425"
                     /product="2-dehydropantoate 2-reductase"
                     /EC_number="1.1.1.169"
                     /label=panE
                     /note="2-Dehydropantoate 2-reductase catalyzes the 
                     NADPH-dependent reduction of ketopantoate to pantoate.
                     The enzyme does not require added divalent metal ions 
                     |CITS: [10736170]|.
                     Kinetic data is consistent with an ordered sequential 
                     reaction mechanism, with NADPH binding followed by 
                     ketopantoate binding |CITS: [10736170]|.  Residues involved
                     in catalysis and substrate binding were identified by 
                     site-directed mutagenesis |CITS: 
                     [11123955][15966718][16884311][17229734]|.  The enzyme has 
                     relatively high substrate specificity |CITS: [14503879]|. 
                     Crystal structures of the enzyme have been solved |CITS: 
                     [11724562][15966718][17229734][17242510]|.  The enzyme is a
                     monomer in solution |CITS: [10736170][11724562]| and is 
                     comprised of an N-terminal Rossmann fold domain and a 
                     C-terminal &alpha;-helical domain |CITS: [11724562]|.
                     The enzyme was used as a target for fragment-based drug 
                     discovery |CITS: [16884311][17305325]|.
                     A <i>panE</i> mutant alone is not auxotrophic for 
                     pantothenate, because in both <i>E. coli</i> and <i>S. 
                     typhimurium</i>, the reaction can also be carried out by 
                     IlvC (|FRAME: CPLX0-7643|) |CITS: 
                     [10553653][6401279][9721324]|.
                     ApbA: ""<b>a</b>lternative <b>p</b>yrimidine 
                     <b>b</b>iosynthetic pathway"" |CITS: [7519593]| 
                     (<i>Salmonella typhimurium</i>)
                     PanE: ""<b>pan</b>tothenate"""
