     gene            440139..440630
                     /gene="yajQ"
                     /locus_tag="b0426"
                     /label=yajQ
     CDS             440139..440630
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yajQ"
                     /locus_tag="b0426"
                     /product="nucleotide binding protein YajQ"
                     /label=yajQ
                     /note="YajQ is a nucleotide binding protein |CITS:
                     [12381839]|.  Under conditions that induce MazEF-mediated 
                     cell death, YajQ is required for survival of a 
                     subpopulation of cells |CITS: [19282968]|.
                     An NMR structural characterization has been performed 
                     |CITS: [12381839][11519751]|, and domain architecture is 
                     discussed |CITS: [12381839]|.
                     YajQ has similarity to other bacterial proteins, but is not
                     conserved in eukaryotes |CITS: [12381839]|.  The YajQ 
                     homolog in <i>Pseudomonas syringae pv. phaseolicola</i> 
                     activates the transcription of late genes in the 
                     bacteriophage &Phi;6 |CITS: [18836083]|.  The YajQ ortholog
                     in the plant pathogen <i>Xanthomonas campestris</i> binds 
                     c-di-GMP and contributes to virulence |CITS: [25329577]|.
                     The <i>yajQ</i> mRNA is a target for cleavage by |FRAME: 
                     EG10857-MONOMER|; cleavage within the 5' UTR leads to 
                     stabilization of the transcript |CITS: [28351917]|.
                     A <i>yajQ</i> deletion mutant is more sensitive to 
                     spectinomycin |CITS: [19282968]| and to the DNA damaging 
                     agent nalidixic acid than wild type |CITS: [23308060]|. 
                     Overexpression of <i>yajQ</i> from an ASKA plasmid leads to
                     a more than 3-fold increase in the MIC of hydrogen peroxide
                     |CITS: [34072091]|."
