     gene            complement(440758..442122)
                     /gene="yajR"
                     /locus_tag="b0427"
                     /label=yajR
     CDS             complement(440758..442122)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yajR"
                     /locus_tag="b0427"
                     /product="putative transport protein YajR"
                     /label=yajR
                     /note="The YajR protein is an uncharacterised member of
                     the Sugar Porter (SP) Family within the Major Facilitator 
                     Superfamily (MFS) of transporters |CITS: 
                     [9529885][26546518]|. The crystal structure of YajR in an 
                     outward facing conformation has been resolved. The 12 
                     transmembrane regions form an N-terminal domain (residues 
                     3-184) and a C-terminal domain (215 - 386) connected by a 
                     30 residue helical linker. YajR also contains a small 65 
                     amino acid (residues 389 - 454) cytoplasmic domain which 
                     contains a ferredoxin-like fold. The N and C termini are 
                     located in the cytoplasm and the structure contains a 
                     central cavity which is open to the periplasm and closed to
                     the cytoplasm |CITS: [23950222]|. The signature motif A, 
                     which is conserved in MFS transporters, is located in the 
                     loop connecting TM 2 and 3 |CITS: [23950222]|. 
                     Overexpression of cloned <I>yajR</I> in a K-12 strain which
                     lacks the major efflux pump permease AcrB (<i>E. coli</i> 
                     KAM3; see |CITS: [12618449]|) does not impact the 
                     resistance to a range of antibiotics, dyes and toxic 
                     compounds |CITS:[11566977]|.
                     <i>yajR</i> is one of 35 efflux-encoding genes that have 
                     been deleted or inactivated in 'Efflux KnockOut-35' 
                     (EKO-35) -  a K-12 BW25133-derived strain that lacks 35 
                     efflux pumps and can be used as a platform to study their 
                     function |CITS: [36065018][36318669]|."
