     gene            459858..460256
                     /gene="fadM"
                     /locus_tag="b0443"
                     /label=fadM
     CDS             459858..460256
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="fadM"
                     /locus_tag="b0443"
                     /product="bifunctional long-chain acyl-CoA thioesterase
                     FadM / acyl-CoA thioesterase"
                     /label=fadM
                     /note="Thioesterase III (FadM) is a long-chain acyl-CoA 
                     thioesterase that is involved in the &beta;-oxidation of 
                     oleic acid. The enzyme is able to hydrolyze a number of 
                     related substrates. The best substrate is 
                     3,5-tetradecadienoyl-CoA, which is a minor side product of 
                     oleate &beta;-oxidation that is resistant to further 
                     degradation. The hydrolysis product, 3,5-tetradecadienoate,
                     is released into the growth medium |CITS: 
                     [14707139][18576672]|.
                     Thioesterase III is expressed upon growth on oleic acid as 
                     the sole source of carbon |CITS: [14707139][18576672]|. 
                     <i>fadM</i> is a member of the <i>fad</i> regulon; 
                     expression is induced by a number of fatty acids, with 
                     C<sub>18:1</sub> as the best inducer |CITS: [19684132]|. 
                     Reports disagree on whether |CITS: [18702504]| or not 
                     |CITS: [19684132]| conjugated linoleic acid (CLA) induces 
                     an even higher level of expression of <i>fadM</i>."
