                     /product="7-cyano-7-deazaguanine synthase"
                     /EC_number="6.3.4.20"
                     /label=queC
                     /note="QueC appears to be the 7-cyano-7-deazaguanine
                     synthase that catalyzes an early step of queuosine 
                     biosynthesis, leading from GTP to the formation of 
                     preQ<sub>0</sub> |CITS: [16199558]|.  Queuosine is one of 
                     the most complex tRNA modifications, occurring at the 
                     wobble position of the GUN anticodon in the Asn, Asp, Tyr, 
                     and His tRNAs.
                     <i>queC</i> rescues the queuosine deficiency phenotype of a
                     mutant <i>E. coli</i> B strain |CITS: [16199558]|.
                     The biochemical activity of QueC was studied using the 
                     orthologous |FRAME: BSU13720-MONOMER| from |FRAME: 
                     TAX-1423| |CITS: [19354300]|.
                     "
