                     /product="trifunctional HMP-PP phosphatase / HMP-PP
                     hydrolase / pyridoxal phosphatase"
                     /EC_number="3.1.3.74"
                     /label=cof
                     /note="Cof is a phosphatase belonging to the superfamily
                     of haloacid dehalogenase (HAD)-like hydrolases.  The enzyme
                     is
                     involved in the hydrolysis of HMP-PP, an intermediate in 
                     thiamin biosynthesis |CITS: [15292217]|.  In a screen using
                     a variety of compounds, its preferred substrate is 
                     pyridoxal phosphate; purine and pyrimidine nucleotides are 
                     secondary substrates |CITS: [16990279]|.
                     Overexpression of Cof from a multicopy plasmid leads to 
                     resistance to the HMP 
                     (4-amino-2-methyl-5-hydroxymethylpyrimidine) analog 
                     bacimethrin (MeO-HMP) |CITS: [15292217]|.
                     "
