     CDS             464327..466099
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="mdlA"
                     /locus_tag="b0448"
                     /product="ABC transporter family protein MdlA"
                     /label=mdlA
                     /note="In the Transporter Classification Database MdlAB is 
                     annotated as a putative multidrug resistance-like ABC 
                     exporter |CITS: [26546518]|. MdlA and MdlB each contain a 
                     TMD-ABC domain |CITS: [9593292]|. MdlA contains 6 putative 
                     transmembrane regions and a single nucleotide-binding 
                     domain; overexpression of <i>mdlA</i> (cloned from <i>E. 
                     coli</i> W3104) in the drug supersensitive strain KAM3 did 
                     not alter its resistance phenotype against a large number 
                     of different drug and toxic compounds |CITS: [11566977] 
                     [11544226]|. MdlA is a member of the Rob regulon - an 
                     <i>mdlA-lacZ</i> transcriptional fusion (generated by MudJ)
                     shows Rob-induced expression |CITS: [10850996]|. 
                     <i>mdlA</i> is one of 35 efflux-encoding genes that have 
                     been deleted or inactivated in 'Efflux KnockOut-35' 
                     (EKO-35) -  a K-12 BW25133-derived strain that lacks 35 
                     efflux pumps and can be used as a platform to study their 
                     function |CITS: [36065018][36318669]|.
                     <i>mdl</i>: <U>m</U>ulti<U>d</U>rug resistance-<U>l</U>ike 
                     |CITS: [7904973]|"
