     gene            complement(471438..471827)
                     /gene="ybaZ"
                     /locus_tag="b0454"
                     /label=ybaZ
     CDS             complement(471438..471827)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ybaZ"
                     /locus_tag="b0454"
                     /product="DNA base-flipping protein"
                     /label=ybaZ
                     /note="YbaZ (Atl) belongs to a family of
                     alkyltransferase-like (ATL) proteins which show sequence 
                     similarity to known 
                     <i>O</i><sup>6</sup>-alkylguanine-DNA-alkyltransferases but
                     lack an otherwise conserved cysteine residue at the 
                     predicted active site; YbaZ has sequence similarity with 
                     the <i>O</i><sup>6</sup>-methylguanine-DNA 
                     methyltransferase |FRAME: EG10668-MONOMER Ogt|. Purified 
                     YbaZ binds <i>O</i><sup>6</sup>-methylguanine containing 
                     DNA <I>in vitro</i> but does does not have alkyltransferase
                     activity; mutagenesis of W83 at the predicted active site 
                     to cysteine does not result in catalytic activity |CITS: 
                     [16027108]|.
                     YbaZ binds preferentially to double-stranded DNA probes 
                     with an abasic site; purified YbaZ exhibits base-flipping 
                     activity on 2-aminopyrine (Ap)-modified DNA; YbaZ may 
                     interact with |FRAME: EG10426-MONOMER| |CITS: [18084297]|. 
                     Overexpression of <i>ybaZ</i> increases sensitivity to the 
                     toxic effect of the methylating agent MNNG |CITS: 
                     [16027108]|.
                     YbaZ enhances repair of O<sup>6</sup>-hydroxyethylguanine 
                     and O<sup>6</sup>-hydroxypropylguanine adducts by the 
                     nucleotide excision repair pathway; a pull-down assay 
                     indicates that YbaZ interacts physically with |FRAME: 
                     EG11061-MONOMER UvrA| |CITS: [19269902]|; YbaZ interacts 
                     with |FRAME: EG11063-MONOMER UvrC| |CITS: [19516334]|). 
                     YbaZ also decreases the methyl-mismatch repair 
                     (MMR)-mediated genotoxicity of these larger alkylguanine 
                     adducts; YbaZ interferes with |FRAME: EG10625-MONOMER MutS|
                     binding to hydroxypropylG:T (and to a lesser extent 
                     hydroxyethylG:T) containing substrates <i>in vitro</i> 
                     |CITS: [ 20921378]|. YbaZ recruits UvrA to alkyl lesions; 
                     YbaZ may search for alkyl lesions in an oligomeric assembly
                     that scans DNA |CITS: [32273391]|.
                     Atl: ""<b>a</b>lkyl<b>t</b>ransferase-<b>l</b>ike"" |CITS: 
                     [16027108]|
                     Reviews: |CITS: [17500045]|"
