                     /product="putative inner membrane protein"
                     /label=ylaC
                     /note="YlaC is an inner membrane protein with two
                     predicted transmembrane domains. The C-terminus is located 
                     in the cytoplasm |CITS: [15919996]|.
                     A knockout mutant of this gene was sensitive to boric acid 
                     exposure; a complementation assay restored its intrinsic 
                     boric acid resistance. Double and triple knockout mutants 
                     (<i>&Delta;|FRAME: EG12760|&Delta;ylaC, 
                     &Delta;ylaC&Delta;garP&Delta;|FRAME: G7261| and 
                     &Delta;ylaC&Delta;garP&Delta;|FRAME: G6994|</i>) exhibited 
                     increasing sensitivity, respectively |CITS: [38466471]|."
