     gene            481992..485354
                     /gene="mscK"
                     /locus_tag="b0465"
                     /label=mscK
     CDS             481992..485354
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="mscK"
                     /locus_tag="b0465"
                     /product="potassium dependent, small conductance
                     mechanosensitive channel"
                     /label=mscK
                     /note="MscK is a potassium-dependent, mechanosensitive
                     channel of small conductance.
                     <i>mscK</i> encodes a mechanosensitive channel with similar
                     or slightly lower conductance to the |FRAME: 
                     EG11160-MONOMER ""MscS""| channel of small conductance (0.8
                     - 1nS) |CITS: [10202137][17493135]|; MscK does not 
                     desensitize upon extended pressure application; 
                     &Delta;<i>mscK</i> cells survive the transition to low 
                     osmolarity media as do &Delta;(<i>mscK mscS</i>) double 
                     mutants |CITS: [10202137]|.
                     <i>E. coli</i> strain RQ2 carrying the <i>kefA2</i> allele 
                     is unable to grow in high (0.6M) K<sup>+</sup> medium in 
                     the presence of compatible solutes; the mutant strain 
                     exhibits a complex K<sup>+</sup> specific phenotype that 
                     likely results from aberrant gating of the MscK channel 
                     |CITS: [11985727]| (see further |CITS: 
                     [12374733][17493135]|). MscK is highly regulated; normal 
                     gating requires both membrane tension and high external 
                     K<sup>+</sup> concentration; smaller ions such as 
                     Li<sup>+</sup> and Na<sup>+</sup> cannot substitute for 
                     K<sup>+</sup>, while larger ions such as NH4<sup>+</sup>, 
                     Rb<sup>+</sup>, and Cs<sup>+</sup> can |CITS: [12374733]|. 
                     MscK is predicted to consist of a large amino terminal 
                     domain located in the periplasm, an inner membrane domain 
                     with11 transmembrane regions and a cytoplasmic C-terminus; 
                     MscK contains a 33 residue signal sequence, that is 
                     required to organize the large hydrophilic domain in the 
                     periplasm |CITS: [10202137][11985727]|.
                     MscK fluorescent fusion proteins, expressed at basal 
                     levels, are evenly distributed and mobile throughout the 
                     membrane |CITS: [27596282]|.
                     A strain lacking MscS, MscK and MscL exhibits defects in 
                     Z-ring placement in the presence of the septation 
                     inhibitor, cephalexin |CITS: [21810996]|.
                     Early studies implicated MscK (formerly KefA) in a system 
                     of potassium efflux that responded to osmotic downshock 
                     |CITS: [7595939][8661775][3301813]|.
                     Seven mechanosensitive ion channels have been characterised
                     in <i>E. coli</i> K-12: |FRAME: CPLX0-7627 ""MscL""|, MscS,
                     MscK, |FRAME: CPLX0-7985 ""MscM""|, |FRAME: CPLX0-7982 
                     ""YnaI""|, |FRAME: CPLX0-7983 ""YbiO""| and |FRAME: 
                     CPLX0-7981 ""YbdG""|.  A strain lacking all seven of these 
                     proteins fails to demonstrate channel opening in patch 
                     clamp experiments |CITS: [22874652]|. Related reviews: 
                     |CITS: [24819593][23947546][22404681][229 
                     15507][22000509][20825352]|."
