                     /note="YbaM is a conserved protein that is involved in 
                     regulating virulence in enterobacterial phytophathogens 
                     |CITS: [30872786]|.
                     In growth competition experiments, a <i>ybaM</i> deletion 
                     mutant is much more sensitive to cell envelope stress than 
                     the wild type |CITS: [19734312]|."
