     CDS             join(487548..488831,488831..488842)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /ribosomal_slippage
                     /gene="dnaX"
                     /locus_tag="b0470"
                     /product="multifunctional DNA polymerase III subunit gamma
                     / DNA polymerase III, clamp-loader complex / DNA polymerase
                     III, holoenzyme / replisome"
                     /label=dnaX
                     /note="The &gamma; (gamma) subunit of DNA polymerase III
                     is generated by a programmed frameshift that occurs about 
                     half the time and leads to early termination of translation
                     resulting in a protein that lacks the final two domains 
                     found in tau. The frameshift occurs in a poly(A) tract and 
                     yields a new stop codon immediately following the 
                     frameshift signal |CITS: [2181440][2187190][2186364]|. 
                     Frameshift depends on base pairing between the 3' end of 
                     the 16S rRNA and a sequence upstream from the poly(A) 
                     tract, as well as the presence of a stable stem loop 3' 
                     from the shift point |CITS: [7961443][9300054]|.
                     The third domain of gamma, which is shared with the tau 
                     subunit, is required for oligomerization of both gamma and 
                     tau, and also includes the binding sites for delta, delta',
                     chi and psi |CITS: [11463787][11078742]|.
                     Crystal structures of the amino-terminal half of gamma in 
                     ATP-bound and unbound states show that ATP binding induces 
                     a conformational change that should disrupt dimerization of
                     gamma |CITS: [12623013]|.
                     A temperature-sensitive mutation in this gene was 
                     identified that showed potential as a growth-switch for 
                     genetic engineering |CITS: [37642940]|.
                     Review: |CITS: [31222875]|"
