     CDS             493511..494473
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="hemH"
                     /locus_tag="b0475"
                     /product="ferrochelatase"
                     /EC_number="4.98.1.1"
                     /label=hemH
                     /note="Ferrochelatase is the terminal enzyme in the heme 
                     biosynthesis pathway and catalyzes the insertion of 
                     Fe<sup>2+</sup> into protoporphyrin IX.
                     Both eukaryotic and some microbial ferrochelatases have 
                     been shown to contain a [2Fe-2S] cluster |CITS: 
                     [11948160]|; however, no studies have been performed with 
                     the <i>E. coli</i> enzyme.
                     A <i>hemH</i> mutant is sensitive to visible light due to 
                     the accumulation of protoporphyrin IX.  This is similar to 
                     the defect observed in human protoporphyria |CITS: 
                     [1835790][1397280]|.  The defect in iron incorporation into
                     protoporphyrin IX in a <i>hemH</i> mutant results in a 
                     defect in assembly of membrane-associated 
                     succinate-ubiquinone reductase |CITS: [11405622]|. 
                     Expression of <i>hemH</i> is mildly regulated in response 
                     to heme availability |CITS: [8997718]| and is activated by 
                     OxyR |CITS: [11443091]|.
                     VisA: ""<b>vis</b>ible light-sensitive"" |CITS: 
                     [2051480]|<br>HemH: ""<b>hem</b>e biosynthesis""
                     Reviews: |CITS: [11215517][12073655]|"
