                     /product="putative transporter YbaL"
                     /label=ybaL
                     /note="The YbaL protein is an uncharacterised member of
                     the CPA2 family of monovalent cation:proton antiporters 
                     |CITS: [26546518]|.
                     <i>ybaL</i> has supercoiling-dependent transcription, which
                     is associated with the osmotic stress response and acts 
                     through <i>rpoS</i> |CITS: [12566398]|.
                     In experimental evolution experiments requiring adaptation 
                     of <i>E. coli</i> to high growth temperature (45.9&deg;C or
                     42.2&deg;C), <i>ybaL</i> is frequently mutated |CITS: 
                     [20975944][22282810]|."
