     gene            complement(498932..500152)
                     /gene="fsr"
                     /locus_tag="b0479"
                     /label=fsr
     CDS             complement(498932..500152)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="fsr"
                     /locus_tag="b0479"
                     /product="fosmidomycin efflux pump"
                     /label=fsr
                     /note="Fsr is a putative fosmidomycin efflux protein.
                     Expression of cloned <i>fsr</i> in a wild-type strain of 
                     <i>E. coli</i> K-12 confers resistance to this antibiotic; 
                     Fsr contains 12 putative transmembrane regions |CITS: 
                     [8917080]|. Expression of cloned <I>mdtG</I> in a K-12 
                     strain which lacks the major efflux pump permease AcrB 
                     (<i>E. coli</i> KAM3; see |CITS: [12618449]|) results in a 
                     32-fold increase in resistance to fosmidomycin and a 
                     two-fold increase in resistance to trimethoprim but does 
                     not impact the resistance to a range of other antibiotics, 
                     dyes and toxic compounds |CITS:[11566977]|.
                     In the Transporter Classification Database, Fsr is a member
                     of the Fosmidomycin Resistance (Fsr) Family within the 
                     Major Facilitator Superfamily |CITS: [26546518]|. 
                     <i>fsr</i> is one of 35 efflux-encoding genes that have 
                     been deleted or inactivated in 'Efflux KnockOut-35' 
                     (EKO-35) -  a K-12 BW25133-derived strain that lacks 35 
                     efflux pumps and can be used as a platform to study their 
                     function |CITS: [36065018][36318669]|."
