     gene            508032..509324
                     /gene="ybaT"
                     /locus_tag="b0486"
                     /label=ybaT
     CDS             508032..509324
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ybaT"
                     /locus_tag="b0486"
                     /product="putative transporter YbaT"
                     /label=ybaT
                     /note="<i>ybaT</i> encodes a putative transporter that is 
                     implicated in copper tolerance.
                     <i>ybaT</i> is induced when a &Delta;<i>copA</i> strain is 
                     grown in copper supplemented medium (ie. under conditions 
                     of copper stress); YbaT and |FRAME: CPLX0-7694| are 
                     required for the protective effect of exogenous glutamine 
                     in rescuing a &Delta;<i>copA</i> mutant from copper stress 
                     at acid pH |CITS: [28611214]|. An increase in intracellular
                     copper impairs acid tolerance by disrupting glutamate 
                     synthesis via |FRAME: GLUTAMATESYN-CPLX|; in the presence 
                     of exogenous glutamine, YbaT and glutaminase I may function
                     to alleviate this block in glutamate synthesis |CITS: 
                     [28611214]|.
                     YbaT is a putative transporter belonging to the 
                     Archaeal/Bacterial Transporter (ABT) Family within the 
                     Amino Acid-Polyamine-Organocation (APC) Superfamily |CITS: 
                     [16397293][24225317]|.
                     <i>ybaT</i> is a member of the acid induced GadX regulon 
                     |CITS: [12426343][12730179]|.
                     "
