                     /product="NfeD-like family protein YbbJ"
                     /label=ybbJ
                     /note="YbbJ is an inner membrane protein with three
                     predicted transmembrane domains.  The C terminus is located
                     in the cytoplasm |CITS:[15919996]|.
                     When included with the upstream <I>qmcA</I> gene, 
                     <I>ybbJ</I> improves the multicopy suppression of an 
                     <I>ftsH htpX</I> double disruption mutant compared to 
                     <I>qmcA</I> alone |CITS:[16573693]|."
