     gene            complement(513796..514605)
                     /gene="ybbO"
                     /locus_tag="b0493"
                     /label=ybbO
     CDS             complement(513796..514605)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ybbO"
                     /locus_tag="b0493"
                     /product="trifunctional NADP(+)-dependent aldehyde
                     reductase YbbO / NADP(+)-dependent aldehyde reductase / 
                     isobutyraldehyde reductase"
                     /EC_number="1.1.1.2"
                     /label=ybbO
                     /note="YbbO is an NADP<sup>+</sup>-dependent aldehyde
                     reductase that showed broad substrate activity toward 
                     aldehydes |CITS: [25108218]| with a preference for 
                     long-chain fatty aldehydes |CITS: [27134112]|.  Among the 
                     substrates tested by |CITS: [25108218]|, it has the highest
                     activity toward hexanal and octanal |CITS: [25108218]|; 
                     |CITS: [27134112]| showed that the enzyme has maximal 
                     activity with C16 and C18 chain length aldehydes. A broad 
                     survey of aldehyde reductases showed that YbbO was one of 
                     several endogenous aldehyde reductases that contribute to 
                     the degradation of desired aldehyde end products of 
                     metabolic engineering |CITS: [25108218]|.  In recombinant 
                     <i>E. coli</i> expressing a &beta;-carotene biosynthesis 
                     pathway and &beta;-carotene 15',15'-monooxygenase, 
                     production of retinol can be increased by overexpressing 
                     <i>ybbO</i> |CITS: [25726762]|.  Deletion of <i>ybbO</i> 
                     reduces long chain fatty alcohol production from externally
                     added substrates by 90% |CITS: [27134112]|."
