                     /gene="selU"
                     /locus_tag="b0503"
                     /product="tRNA 2-selenouridine synthase"
                     /EC_number="2.9.1.3"
                     /label=selU
                     /note="tRNA 2-selenouridine synthase (SelU) is responsible
                     for formation of the special selenium-containing wobble 
                     base of the three tRNAs tRNA<sup>Lys</sup>, 
                     tRNA<sup>Glu</sup>, and tRNA<sup>Gln</sup> |CITS: 
                     [6345544][14594807]|. The enzyme catalyzes formation of 
                     5-methylaminomethyl-2-selenouridine 
                     (mnm<sup>5</sup>se<sup>2</sup>U) from 
                     5-methylaminomethyl-2-thiouridine and SePO<sub>3</sub>. 
                     Purified SelU was shown to contain tRNA |CITS: [14594807]|.
                     SelU was found to have high substrate specificity, using 
                     the geranyl (C10) pyrophosphate most efficiently and in the
                     micromolar range to add a prenyl group to the sulfur atom 
                     in the first anticodon position of 
                     tRNA<sup>Glu</sup><sub>UUC</sub>, 
                     tRNA<sup>Lys</sup><sub>UUU</sub> and 
                     tRNA<sup>Gln</sup><sub>UUG</sub> 
                     (carboxy)5-methylaminomethyl-2-thiouridine-modified 
                     nucleotides. The enzyme is less discriminant for the 
                     selenation reaction |CITS: [22983156]|.
                     A crystal structure of SelU in complex with tRNA has been 
                     obtained; two complexes were found with electron-density 
                     mapping |CITS: [39783014]|.
                     SelU residue C97, which lies within the rhodanese homology 
                     domain, is important for the tRNA 2-selenouridine synthase 
                     activity |CITS: [14594807]|. The G67E mutant increases the 
                     relative geranylation activity of SelU |CITS: [22983156]|. 
                     A <i>selU</i> deletion mutant has no obvious growth defect 
                     |CITS: [14594807]|, but contains no geranyl-modified 
                     (mnm5ges2U nor cmnm5ges2U) tRNAs |CITS: [22983156]|. The 
                     geranylation activity of SelU appears to affect 
                     codon-specific translation efficiency and frameshifting 
                     |CITS: [22983156]|.
                     <i>In vitro</i> analysis of SelU indicates it carries out 
                     two consecutive reactions with S-geranyl-2-thiouridine in 
                     tRNA (R5geS2U-tRNA) being the intermediate |CITS: 
                     [29862510]|. A maltose binding protein (MBP)-SelU fusion 
                     protein, that is stable and exhibits higher geranylation 
                     and selenation activities was made for more robust <i>in 
                     vitro</i> analyses, confirmed that R5geS2U-tRNA is the 
                     intermediate in the overall reaction and found that 
                     Mg<sup>2+</sup> is a required for enzymatic activity |CITS:
                     [35306417]|.
                     SelU: |CITS: [22983156]|
                     Comment: |CITS: [23042566]|"
