     CDS             527907..528389
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="allA"
                     /locus_tag="b0505"
                     /product="ureidoglycolate lyase"
                     /EC_number="4.3.2.3"
                     /label=allA
                     /note="Ureidoglycolate lyase catalyzes the conversion of 
                     ureidoglycolate to glyoxylate and urea |CITS: 
                     [10601204][19935661][24107613]|.
                     <i>E. coli</i> is able to utilize allantoin as a sole 
                     source of nitrogen under anaerobic conditions, but can not 
                     utilize it as a sole source of carbon.  An <i>allA</i> 
                     mutant is not impaired in the utilization of allantoin 
                     |CITS: [10601204]|.
                     Ureidoglycolate lyase activity is slightly induced by 
                     growth on allantoin as the sole source of nitrogen |CITS: 
                     [10601204]|.  Transcription of <i>allA</i> is induced by 
                     growth on glyoxylate |CITS: [12460564]|."
