                     /product="bifunctional tartronate semialdehyde reductase 2
                     / tartronate semialdehyde reductase"
                     /label=glxR
                     /note="Tartronate semialdehyde reductase 2 (GlxR)
                     catalyzes the reversible reactions of 
                     NAD<sup>+</sup>-dependent
                     oxidation of <i>D</i>-glycerate and the NADH-dependent 
                     reduction of tartronate semialdehyde |CITS: [10978349]|. 
                     Expression of tartronate semialdehyde reductase is induced 
                     by anaerobic growth with allantoin as the sole source of 
                     nitrogen |CITS: [10601204]| and is induced more than 
                     100-fold by growth on glyoxylate as the sole source of 
                     carbon
                     |CITS: [10978349]|.  A <i>glxR</i> mutant lacks the ability
                     to utilize glyoxylate |CITS: [10601204]|.
                     Review: |CITS: [11306094]|"
