     CDS             533089..534543
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="allW"
                     /locus_tag="b0511"
                     /product="allantoin transporter"
                     /label=allW
                     /note="<i>E. coli</i> is able to utilize allantoin as a
                     source of nitrogen under anaerobic conditions |CITS: 
                     [10601204]|. <i>allW</i>, located within an allantoin 
                     utilization gene cluster, encodes an allantoin transporter 
                     that relies on binding to <i>allB</i>-encoded |FRAME: 
                     CPLX-64| for activity; AllW-AllB physical association is 
                     enhanced in the presence of glyoxylate |CITS: [37147430]|. 
                     AllW and AllB constitute a functional 'membrane transport 
                     metabolon' |CITS: [22705263]|.
                     AllW (formerly YbbW) has sequence similarity to the 
                     allantoin permease of <i>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</i> 
                     |CITS: [10601204]|. Accumulation of the cationic 
                     fluorescent dye 3,3'-dipropylthiadicarbocyanine iodide 
                     (diS-C3) is greater in <i>ybbW</i> knockout cells compared 
                     to wild type |CITS: [31438868]|.
                     In the Transporter Classification Database |CITS: 
                     [10082980]| AllW is a member of the Nucleobase:Cation 
                     Symporter-1 (NCS1) family within the Amino 
                     Acid-Polyamine-Organocation (APC) superfamily."
