                     /product="putative purine transporter"
                     /label=ybbY
                     /note="YbbY is predicted to be an inner membrane protein
                     with 11 transmembrane domains; topology analysis suggests 
                     the C-terminus is located in the cytoplasm |CITS: 
                     [15919996]|.
                     YbbY has sequence similarity to xanthine permease of 
                     <i>Bacillus subtilis</i> and to uracil permease of 
                     <i>Bacillus caldolyticus</i> |CITS: [10601204]|. In the 
                     Transporter Classification Database, YbbY is a member of 
                     the nucleobase:cation symporter-2 (NCS2) family within the 
                     Amino Acid-Polyamine-Organocation (APC) superfamily |CITS: 
                     [24225317]|."
