                     /note="(S)-ureidoglycine aminohydrolase catalyzes the
                     second, stereospecific hydrolysis reaction of the allantoin
                     degradation pathway, producing |FRAME: CPD-1091| and 
                     ammonia from |FRAME: CPD0-2298| |CITS: 
                     [19935661][20038185]|.  Although hydrolysis of 
                     ureidoglycine can proceed spontaneously, the spontaneous 
                     reaction appears to be slow and not stereospecific |CITS: 
                     [20038185]|.
