     gene            542136..543803
                     /gene="allF"
                     /locus_tag="b0518"
                     /label=allF
     CDS             542136..543803
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="allF"
                     /locus_tag="b0518"
                     /product="bifunctional oxamate carbamoyltransferase
                     subunit AllF / oxamate carbamoyltransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.1.3.5"
                     /label=allF
                     /note="Using genome and metabolic context methods, |CITS: 
                     [22693442]| hypothesize that <i>fdrA</i> encodes an 
                     oxamate:CoA ligase which continues the degradation of 
                     oxamate produced by the |FRAME: PWY0-41 ""anaerobic 
                     allantoin degradation pathway""|. The fate of oxamate is 
                     not clear; |CITS: [34494882]| suggest that oxamate is not 
                     degraded further and they provide evidence that FdrA is 
                     critical for oxamate production during anaerobic allantoin 
                     degradation and may be the orphan enzyme |FRAME: 
                     OXAMATE-CARBAMOYLTRANSFERASE-RXN oxamate 
                     carbomoyltransferase| (OXTCase). The OXTCase activity was 
                     subsequently found to require the first 3 genes in the 
                     |FRAME: TU0-12962| operon; all three of which are required 
                     to complement the triple mutant, &Delta;<i>allFGH</i> 
                     |CITS: [38888336]|.
                     The complex of three distinct subunits has not been 
                     observed for other enzymes of the transcarbamylase family 
                     in other organisms; also, the protein sequences for all 
                     three enzymes lack similarity to others in the 
                     transcarbamylase family |CITS: [38888336]|.
                     In contrast to the wild-type, a &Delta;<i>fdrA</i> mutant 
                     does not produce oxamate during glycerol fermentation with 
                     allantoin as the sole nitrogen source |CITS: [34494882]|. 
                     |FRAME: OXALATE Oxalate| production increases under these 
                     same conditions via an alternate pathway involving the 
                     |FRAME: G6275-MONOMER|-catalysed conversion of 
                     ureidoglycolate to urea and glycolate and subsequent 
                     oxidation of glycolate to oxalate likely by 
                     <i>ldhA</i>-encoded |FRAME: DLACTDEHYDROGNAD-MONOMER 
                     lactate dehydrogenase| |CITS: [34494882]|.
                     An <i>fdrA-lacZ</i> transcriptional fusion is induced by 
                     allantoin under anaerobic conditions |CITS: [34494882]|. An
                     N-terminally truncated version of <i>fdrA</i> acts as a 
                     multicopy suppressor of the phenotypes of a dominant 
                     negative <i>ftsH</i> mutation |CITS: [7500942]|. 
                     Overexpression of <i>fdrA</i> leads to reduced motility and
                     decreased levels of biofilm formation |CITS: [12900028]|, 
                     while a knockout mutation in <i>fdrA</i> leads to repressed
                     swarming motility |CITS: [17122336]|. FdrA: 
                     ""<i><b>f</b>tsH</i> <b>d</b>ominant <b>r</b>escue"" |CITS:
                     [7500942]|"
