     gene            543813..545072
                     /gene="allG"
                     /locus_tag="b4572"
                     /label=allG
     CDS             543813..545072
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="allG"
                     /locus_tag="b4572"
                     /product="bifunctional oxamate carbamoyltransferase
                     subunit AllG / oxamate carbamoyltransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.1.3.5"
                     /label=allG
                     /note="Resequencing of multiple isolates of the MG1655
                     strain has identified several genetic variations, including
                     a single-nucleotide polymorphism and a single-nucleotide 
                     insertion in the former <i>ylbE_1</i> pseudogene fragment 
                     in strain ATCC700926 |CITS: [22081388]|, which is the 
                     source of the genome sequence within EcoCyc (U00096.3). 
                     This insertion repairs the frameshift and results in an 
                     intact <i>ylbE</i> gene |CITS: [22081388]|.
                     Using mutational analyses and purified proteins, this gene 
                     product, renamed AllG, was shown to be required for oxamate
                     carbamoyltransferase (OXTCase) activity along with AllF and
                     AllH subunits |CITS: [38888336]|. The complex of three 
                     distinct subunits has not been observed for other enzymes 
                     of the transcarbamylase family in other organisms; also, 
                     the protein sequences for all three enzymes lack similarity
                     to others in the transcarbamylase family |CITS: 
                     [38888336]|.
                     Expression of the <i>ylbE</i> ortholog of the avian 
                     pathogenic <i>E. coli</i> strain CH2 is induced during 
                     infection of chickens |CITS: [22344666]|."
