                     /label=ybcJ
     CDS             complement(552117..552329)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ybcJ"
                     /locus_tag="b0528"
                     /product="putative RNA-binding protein YbcJ"
                     /label=ybcJ
                     /note="A solution structure of YbcJ has been determined.
                     YbcJ has an S4-like RNA binding domain that is expected to 
                     bind to structured regions of RNAs. Amino acids that are 
                     predicted to be involved in RNA binding were identified 
                     |CITS: [12837795]|.
                     YbcJ associates weakly with the 50S subunit of the ribosome
                     |CITS: [17337586]| and interacts with several components of
                     the degradosome |CITS: [19402753]|. In a large genetic 
                     interaction screen, <i>ybcJ</i> showed genetic interactions
                     with a number of proteins involved in translation and 
                     ribosome biogenesis |CITS: [27732863]|. Deletion of 
                     <i>ybcJ</i> appears to decrease the rate of protein 
                     synthesis and translational fidelity |CITS: [19402753]|; a 
                     &Delta;<i>yhbY</i> mutant shows increased levels of stop 
                     codon readthrough |CITS: [27732863]|.
                     This minimally characterized enzyme was found to interact 
                     with the |FRAME: ENOLASE-MONOMER| enzyme in glycolysis in a
                     large assessment of protein-protein interactions (PPIs) 
                     |CITS: [33917325]|."
