     gene            complement(552331..553197)
                     /gene="folD"
                     /locus_tag="b0529"
                     /label=folD
     CDS             complement(552331..553197)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="folD"
                     /locus_tag="b0529"
                     /product="trifunctional bifunctional
                     methylenetetrahydrofolate dehydrogenase / 
                     methenyltetrahydrofolate cyclohydrolase / 
                     methenyltetrahydrofolate cyclohydrolase / 
                     methylenetetrahydrofolate dehydrogenase"
                     /EC_number="3.5.4.9; 1.5.1.5"
                     /label=folD
                     /note="The <i>folD</i> gene product is a bifunctional
                     enzyme that catalyzes the NADP<sup>+</sup>-dependent 
                     dehydrogenation of <i>N</i><sup>5</sup>,<i>N</i><sup>10</s 
                     up>-methylenetetrahydrofolate and the subsequent 
                     cyclohydrolysis reaction that generates 
                     <i>N</i><sup>10</sup>-formyltetrahydrofolate |CITS: 
                     [1748668][25988590]|. 
                     <i>N</i><sup>10</sup>-formyltetrahydrofolates are involved 
                     in tetrahydrofolate and purine biosynthesis and supply the 
                     formyl group for the initiator tRNA<sup>fMet</sup>.
                     The macrolide carboxylate carolacton inhibits both 
                     activities of FolD; mutant enzymes that confer resistance 
                     to carolacton have been isolated |CITS: [29142318]|. 
                     Crystal structures of FolD and the FolD-carolacton complex 
                     have been solved |CITS: [10386884][29142318]|.  Each 
                     monomer comprises two domains that form an interdomain 
                     cleft.  The homodimeric form appears to be stabilized by an
                     intersubunit disulfide bond between the Cys132 residues of 
                     each subunit |CITS: [10386884]|.  Random and site-directed 
                     mutagenesis of residues predicted to play a role in 
                     catalysis confirmed their importance and enabled separation
                     of the dehydrogenase and cyclohydrolase activities; an 
                     R191E mutant is specifically impaired in the dehydrogenase 
                     activity, while a K54S mutant is specifically lacks the 
                     cyclohydrolase activity of FolD |CITS: 
                     [18288206][25988590]|.  Binding of the inhibitor carolacton
                     to FolD likely prevents the binding of substrates |CITS: 
                     [29142318]|.
                     A <i>folD122</i> mutant shows decreased steady-state levels
                     of methionine and SAM |CITS: [18288206]|.  Several 
                     <i>folD</i> point mutants are defective in initiator tRNA 
                     formylation, thereby affecting the fidelity of translation 
                     initiation |CITS: [32795532]|.
                     FolD: |CITS: [1885508]|
                     "
