                     /product="putative fimbrial protein SfmA"
                     /label=sfmA
                     /note="<i>sfmACDHF</i> is a putative chaperone-usher
                     fimbrial operon in <i>E.coli K-12</i> |CITS: [20345943]|. 
                     The operon is cryptic under normal laboratory conditions 
                     but when constitutive expression is induced in a strain 
                     that lacks the type 1 fimbrial complex the <i>sfm</i> 
                     operon promotes adhesion to eukaryotic epithelial cells 
                     (T<sub>4</sub> bladder cells) |CITS: [20345943]|. 
                     Expression of the <i>sfm</i> operon is regulated by the 
                     global regulators |FRAME: PD00288 ""H-NS""| and |FRAME: 
                     CPLX0-226 ""CRP cAMP""| |CITS: [20345943]| and by the 
                     transcription factor |FRAME: EG11103-MONOMER FimZ| |CITS: 
                     [36057789]|.
                     <i>E. coli</i> K-12 contains 12 chaperone-usher fimbrial 
                     operons, including <i>sfmACDHF</i>; a fimbria-lacking 
                     mutant - strain WQM026 - created by deleting all 12 operons
                     has been characterised |CITS: [33863704]|."
