     CDS             complement(join(569985..570042,571242..572281))
                     /pseudo
                     /gene="nmpC"
                     /locus_tag="b0553"
                     /product="DLP12 prophage; putative outer membrane porin
                     NmpC"
                     /label=nmpC
                     /note="NmpC is a member of the General Bacterial Porin
                     (GBP) Family |CITS: [12192075]|. It is believed to be a 
                     water filled outer membrane porin, with an effective 
                     diameter of 1.2nm |CITS: [6384178]|. It is a silent gene 
                     within <I>E. coli</I> K-12 |CITS: [6384178]|. Mutational 
                     studies which activate the gene show that the porin 
                     associates itself with the peptidoglycan |CITS: [357416]|. 
                     Expression of these porins increases sensitivity to several
                     colicins and phages |CITS: [357416]|. However, whether this
                     sensitivity is specific or not, is unknown. <i>nmpC</i>: 
                     <U>n</U>ew <U>m</U>embrane <U>p</U>orin C |CITS: 
                     [357416]|."
