     gene            572854..573069
                     /gene="essD"
                     /locus_tag="b0554"
                     /label=essD
     CDS             572854..573069
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="essD"
                     /locus_tag="b0554"
                     /product="DLP12 prophage; putative phage lysis protein"
                     /label=essD
                     /note="EssD is a predicted class II holin of the cryptic 
                     lambdoid prophage DLP12.  The protein has two potential 
                     transmembrane domains |CITS: [17914239]|. EssD has also 
                     been predicted to be a bitopic inner membrane protein 
                     |CITS: [27510400]|.
                     The effect of an <i>essD</i> deletion on biofilm formation 
                     is dependent on the strain background.  In the BW25113 
                     background, an <i>essD</i> mutation increases biofilm 
                     formation |CITS: [19458652]|, while an <i>essD</i> mutant 
                     is impaired in curli-based biofilm formation, which may be 
                     an indirect effect due to altered peptidoglycan (PG) 
                     metabolism |CITS: [21415116]|. Deletion of the lysis module
                     of DLP12 defective prophage (<i>essD, rrrD</i>, 
                     <i>rzpD/rzoD</i>) induces an hypervesiculation phenotype 
                     (possibly due to an excess of PG fragments in the 
                     periplasmic space); expression of the module is sensitive 
                     to environmental stress factors (low temperature, high 
                     osmolarity and acidic pH) |CITS: [33673345]|.
                     "
