                     /note="YbcH is predicted to be a periplasmic protein that
                     is anchored to the inner membrane; the protein may be an 
                     auxiliary component of a secretion system for an 
                     uncharacteized exopolysaccharide that impedes flagellar 
                     activity and serves as the primary receptor for lytic 
                     bacteriophage N4 |CITS: [34903052]|. <i>ybcH</i> is located
                     together with |FRAME: EG11739 <i>nfrB</i>|, encoding a 
                     |FRAME: C-DI-GMP|-activated glycosyltransferase, and 
                     |FRAME: EG11740 <i>nfrA</i>| encoding an outer membrane 
                     protein, and the three proteins likely constitute an 
                     exopolysaccharide production/secretion system |CITS: 
                     [34903052]|.
                     "
