     gene            complement(583438..586410)
                     /gene="nfrA"
                     /locus_tag="b0568"
                     /label=nfrA
     CDS             complement(583438..586410)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="nfrA"
                     /locus_tag="b0568"
                     /product="exopolysaccharide secretion system outer
                     membrane protein NfrA"
                     /label=nfrA
                     /note="NfrA is an outer membrane protein required for the 
                     secretion of an uncharacterized exopolysaccharide (termed 
                     N4 glycan receptor or NGR) that impedes flagellar activity 
                     and serves as the primary receptor for lytic bacteriophage 
                     N4 |CITS: [34903052][34903045]|. <i>nfrA</i> is located 
                     together with |FRAME: EG11739 <i>nfrB</i>|, encoding a 
                     |FRAME: C-DI-GMP|-activated glycosyltransferase, and 
                     |FRAME: EG12448 <i>ybcH</i>| encoding a periplasmic 
                     protein, and the three proteins likely constitute an 
                     exopolysaccharide production/secretion system |CITS: 
                     [34903052][34903045]|.
                     Early studies characterized <i>nfrA</i> mutations which 
                     conferred N4 resistance in <i>E. coli</i> K-12 strain 
                     SC1100 |CITS: [2670887]|. Sequence analysis indicates that 
                     it contains no significant hydrophobic regions apart from 
                     the signal peptide, and no significant &beta;-sheet 
                     structure |CITS: [2670887][8226649]|. NfrA is predicted to 
                     be an outer membrane, TPR-rich, &beta;-barrel protein 
                     |CITS: [34903052][34903045]|.
                     NfrA (<i>E. coli</i> K-12 strain W3350) interacts 
                     physically with phage N4 tail sheath protein gp65 <i>in 
                     vitro</i> and <i>in vivo</i> |CITS: [19011026]|.
                     NfrA binds human complement component C3 <i>in vitro</i>; 
                     NfrA is implicated in a pathway of glycine-promoted, 
                     complement-dependent, cell death |CITS: [31346171]|. 
                     CRP-cAMP, FlhC and CsgD regulate the expression of 
                     <i>nfrA</i> during glycine dependent serum mediated cell 
                     death |CITS: [31346171]|
                     <i>nfrA</i>: <U>N f</U>our <U>r</U>esistance |CITS: 
                     [2670887]|"
