     gene            complement(586397..588634)
                     /gene="nfrB"
                     /locus_tag="b0569"
                     /label=nfrB
     CDS             complement(586397..588634)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="nfrB"
                     /locus_tag="b0569"
                     /product="cyclic di-3',5'-guanylate-activated
                     glycosyltransferase"
                     /label=nfrB
                     /note="NfrB is a |FRAME: C-DI-GMP|-activated
                     glycosyltransferase which produces an uncharacterized 
                     exopolysaccharide (termed N4 glycan receptor or NGR) that 
                     impedes flagellar motility and acts as an initial (primary)
                     receptor for the lytic bacteriophage N4; <i>nfrB</i> is 
                     located together with |FRAME: EG11740 <i>nfrA</i>|, 
                     encoding an outer membrane protein, and |FRAME: EG12448 
                     <i>ybcH</i>| encoding a periplasmic protein, and the three 
                     proteins likely constitute an exopolysaccharide 
                     production/secretion system |CITS: [34903052][34903045]|.
                     NfrB contains an N-terminal glycosyltransferase domain and 
                     a C-terminal MshEN domain that binds cyclic 
                     di-3',5'-guanylate with high affinity; the two domains are 
                     linked by two predicted alpha-helices which likely anchor 
                     NfrB in the inner membrane; binding of cyclic 
                     di-3',5'-guanylate to the MshEN domain allosterically 
                     activates glycosyltransferase activity |CITS: [34903052]|. 
                     NfrB interacts directly with the |FRAME: G6972-MONOMER| and
                     this interaction provides a localized source of cyclic 
                     di-3',5'-guanylate |CITS: [34903052]|.
                     <i>nfrB</i> expression increases transiently during late 
                     exponential growth and is also affected by temperature; 
                     transcription is regulated by the the |FRAME: CPLX0-3930 
                     FlhDC|-|FRAME: EG11355-MONOMER FliA| flagellar control 
                     cascade |CITS: [34903052]|.
                     Early studies characterized mutations in <i>nfrB</i> which 
                     conferred N4 resistance in <i>E. coli</i> K-12 strain 
                     SC1100 |CITS: [2670887]| (and further |CITS: [8226649]|). 
                     <i>nfrB</i>: <U>N f</U>our <U>r</U>esistance |CITS: 
                     [2670887]|"
