     CDS             591056..592429
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="cusC"
                     /locus_tag="b0572"
                     /product="bifunctional copper/silver export system outer
                     membrane channel / copper/silver export system"
                     /label=cusC
                     /note="CusC is an outer membrane lipoprotein involved in
                     the detoxification of copper and silver ions in <i>E. 
                     coli</i> as part of the CusCFBA copper/silver efflux 
                     system.
                     A crystal structure of CusC has been solved to 2.3 &Aring;.
                     The CusC trimer forms a large continuous internal cavity 
                     with a cylindrical shape. Each monomer contributes 4 &beta;
                     strands to the outer membrane &beta; barrel structure and 4
                     &alpha; helices to the periplasmic &alpha; barrel. The 
                     structure also suggests that CusC is triacylated at the 
                     N-terminal cysteine residue of each monomer |CITS: 
                     [21249122]|.
                     <i>cusC</i> exhibits mosaic evolution patterns in <i>E. 
                     coli</i> |CITS: [40444982]|."
