     gene            complement(603189..603248)
                     /gene="sokE"
                     /locus_tag="b4835"
                     /label=sokE
     misc_RNA        complement(603189..603248)
                     /gene="sokE"
                     /locus_tag="b4835"
                     /product="small RNA SokE"
                     /note="<i>sokE</i> encodes a small RNA similar to that of
                     other hok/sok systems |CITS: [10361310]|.
                     The <i>hokE-sokE</i> locus of <i>E. coli</i> K-12 encodes a
                     hok/sok toxin/antitoxin system that appears to have been 
                     inactivated by the nearby insertion of an IS186 insertion 
                     sequence |CITS: [10361310]|.
                     Comment from EcoGene: ""Antisense sRNA at remnant mokE/hokE
                     locus.  Although sokE and hokE are intact, the start of the
                     regulatory peptide gene mokE is missing from this remnant 
                     hok/mok locus, so the mokE (and hence hokE) is not 
                     expressed and the frame cannot be determined to annotate a 
                     pseudogene.""
                     In the plasmid R1 hok/sok system, Sok antisense RNA binds 
                     with <i>hok</i> mRNA, allowing cleavage by RNase III |CITS:
                     [10473621][1380562]|.
                     Reviews: |CITS: [9442888][17376733][23131729][32213244]|"
     gene            603190..603248
                     /gene="b4700"
                     /locus_tag="b4700"
                     /label=b4700
                     /note="/phantom"
     gene            603292..603444
                     /gene="hokE"
                     /locus_tag="b4415"
                     /label=hokE
     CDS             603292..603444
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="hokE"
                     /locus_tag="b4415"
                     /product="small toxic polypeptide HokE"
                     /label=hokE
                     /note="Sequence analysis indicates that the <i>hokE</i>
                     gene is a homolog of the <i>hok</i> (host killing) gene 
                     which is responsible for mediating plasmid stabilization by
                     post-segregational killing (PSK) in plasmid R1. <i>hok</i> 
                     encodes a stable mRNA whose translation is inhibited by a 
                     less stable mRNA encoded by <i>sok</i>. The stable mRNA 
                     encodes a toxic polypeptide. The <i>hokE</i> system is 
                     inactive probably due to insertion of the insertion element
                     IS186 21 bp downstream of the <i>hokE</i> gene. Sequence 
                     analysis shows that after the removal of the IS186 element 
                     sequence, the <i>hokE</i> system contains regulatory 
                     elements described for the <i>hok/sok</i> system from 
                     plasmid R1, including a fold-back inhibition element 
                     (<i>fbi</i>), a translational activation element 
                     (<i>tac</i>), a promoter, an overlapping open reading frame
                     named <i>mokE</i>, and an antisense RNA complementary to 
                     the <i>hokE</i> mRNA leader in the <i>mokE</i> reading 
                     frame. The antisense RNA is homologous to Sok RNA from 
                     plasmid R1, and is believed to regulate <i>hokE</i> 
                     translation by inhibiting translation of the overlapping 
                     <i>mokE</i>. The only element missing is the start codon of
                     the <i>mokE</i> reading frame |CITS: [10361310]|.
                     Expression of <i>hokE</i> appears to be regulated by LexA 
                     |CITS: [10760155]|.
                     Reviews: |CITS: [9442888][17376733][23131729]|"
