                     /product="polysaccharide co-polymerase family protein
                     FepE"
                     /label=fepE
                     /note="The <i>fepE</i> locus was originally defined by an 
                     enterobactin transport lesion; a 
                     <i>fepE</i>::mini<i>-kan-9</i> strain is able to produce 
                     enterobactin but is unable to grow in either iron-depleted 
                     medium or with addition of purified enterobactin 
                     |CITS:[2956250]|. A <I>fepE</I> homolog in |FRAME: 
                     TAX-90371| is responsible for very long O antigen 
                     polymerization in lipopolysaccharide, providing minor 
                     complement resistance and significant serum resistance in 
                     mouse infection models |CITS:[12603743],[16027021]|, and is
                     upregulated during swarming |CITS:[15049819]|. <I>fepE</I> 
                     is regulated by the FlhDC flagellar transcriptional 
                     regulator |CITS:[15941987]|.
