     gene            complement(619010..619966)
                     /gene="fepB"
                     /locus_tag="b0592"
                     /label=fepB
     CDS             complement(619010..619966)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="fepB"
                     /locus_tag="b0592"
                     /product="trifunctional ferric enterobactin ABC
                     transporter periplasmic binding protein / ferric 
                     enterobactin ABC transporter / transport of ferric 
                     enterobactin"
                     /EC_number="7.2.2.17"
                     /label=fepB
                     /note="FepB is the periplasmic binding protein of a ferric 
                     enterobactin ABC transport system.
                     Purified FepB binds ferric enterobactin and enterobactin 
                     with high affinity (K<sub>d</sub> = 30nM and 60nM 
                     respectively). Varying the periplasmic concentration of 
                     FepB does not affect the rate of uptake of labeled ferric 
                     enterobactin suggesting that the rate limiting step in 
                     ferric enterobactin uptake is transport across the outer 
                     membrane. FepB is synthesized at relatively low levels - 
                     approximately 3800 molecules per cell |CITS: [10986237]|. 
                     Solution structures of FepB with and without bound gallium 
                     enterobactin suggest that ligand binding does not induce 
                     large conformational changes |CITS: [25173704]|.
                     FepB is synthesized with a cleavable signal sequence |CITS:
                     [3011753]|. Isoforms of FepB have been observed in several 
                     studies |CITS: [3011753], [2956250]| but this may be an 
                     artifact of overexpression |CITS: [10986237]|. <i>fepB</i> 
                     is a member of the Fur regulon |CITS: [2139473], 
                     [2529253]|. The <i>fepB</i> transcript contains an AU rich 
                     translational enhancer (TE) located upstream (-29 to -20) 
                     of the non-canonical GUG start codon. This TE element is 
                     associated with increased ribosome binding and increased 
                     translation efficiency.  The presence of the TE element 
                     enhances FepB protein synthesis <i>in vitro</i> |CITS: 
                     [17400738]|.
                     Cultivation with nTiO<sub>2</sub> resulted in increased 
                     production of proteins involved in siderophore biosynthesis
                     (EntA, EntB, EntC, and EntE), siderophore recognition 
                     (FepA, CirA) and transport (FepB) |CITS: [35325859]|."
                     /translation="MRLAPLYRNALLLTGLLLSGIAAVQAADWPRQITDSRGTHTLESQ
                     PQRIVSTSVTLTGSLLAIDAPVIASGATTPNNRVADDQGFLRQWSKVAKERKLQRLYIG
