     gene            620341..621516
                     /gene="entC"
                     /locus_tag="b0593"
                     /label=entC
     CDS             620341..621516
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="entC"
                     /locus_tag="b0593"
                     /product="bifunctional isochorismate synthase EntC /
                     isochorismate synthase"
                     /EC_number="5.4.4.2"
                     /label=entC
                     /note="There are two isochorismate synthase enzymes
                     present in <i>E. coli</i>, encoded by <i>entC</i> and 
                     <i>menF</i>. EntC is specific to the enterobactin 
                     biosynthetic pathway, while MenF is specific to the 
                     menaquinone biosynthetic pathway |CITS: 
                     [8655506][9795253]|.
                     Macromolecular crowding appears to increase the intrinsic 
                     activity of the enzyme by inducing structural changes 
                     |CITS: [17243787]|.
                     The crystal structure of EntC in complex with isochorismate
                     and Mg<sup>2+</sup> has been determined at 2.3 &Aring; 
                     resolution. Also in this report, activity analysis of the 
                     wild-type enzyme and EntC mutants produced by site-directed
                     mutagenesis provided insights into the catalytic mechanism 
                     |CITS: [20079748]|.
                     EntB has been shown to form a specific, intracellular 
                     pairwise interaction with EntC, and computational analysis 
                     indicates the EntB-EntC complex may provide a substrate 
                     channeling surface |CITS: [35952947]|.
                     Expression of <i>entC</i> is induced by low iron 
                     concentration both aerobically and anaerobically |CITS: 
                     [2521621][8655506]|. Cultivation with nTiO<sub>2</sub> 
                     resulted in increased production of proteins involved in 
                     siderophore biosynthesis (EntA, EntB, EntC, and EntE), 
                     siderophore recognition (FepA, CirA) and transport (FepB) 
                     |CITS: [35325859]|.
                     Studies in the biofuel metabolic engineering field showed 
                     that overexpression of several <i>E. coli</i> genes 
                     conferred an increase in n-butanol tolerance, including 
                     EntC and FeoA (|FRAME: EG12101-MONOMER|) which showed 
                     increases of 32.8% and 49.1% respectively, as compared with
                     wild-type |CITS: [21408113]|. Studies in the drug 
                     development field showed that a &Delta;<i>entC</i> mutant, 
                     as well as some other enterobactin biosynthesis, uptake or 
                     utilization mutants, were hypersensitive to an 
                     antimicrobial peptide that appears to act in part by 
                     disrupting iron metabolism |CITS: [22096151]|.
                     FepF: ""<b>f</b>erric <b>e</b>nterobactin 
                     trans<b>p</b>ort"" |CITS: [2956250]|
                     EntC: ""<b>ent</b>erobactin"""
