                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="cstA"
                     /locus_tag="b0598"
                     /product="bifunctional pyruvate transporter CstA /
                     pyruvate:H(+) symporter"
                     /label=cstA
                     /note="<i>cstA</i> encodes a specific, moderate affinity 
                     pyruvate transporter which mediates the proton-dependent 
                     uptake of pyruvate; expression of the transporter from a 
                     plasmid enables the growth of a triple mutant strain 
                     (&Delta;|FRAME: G7942 <i>btsT</i>| &Delta;<i>cstA</i> 
                     &Delta;|FRAME: EG12268 <i>yhjX</i>|) that is otherwise 
                     unable to grow with pyruvate as a sole carbon and energy 
                     source |CITS: [33260635]|.
                     <i>cstA</i> is induced during carbon (succinate, glycerol 
                     or glucose) starvation or upon entry into stationary phase;
                     expression is dependent on |FRAME: RPOD-MONOMER 
                     &sigma;<sup>70</sup>| and positively regulated by cAMP-CRP 
                     |CITS: [1848300][2163388]|. The growth impairment of 
                     <i>cstA opp</i> double null mutants is evident only when 
                     peptides serve as carbon and energy source implicating 
                     <i>cstA</i> in peptide utilization |CITS: [1848300]|. 
                     <i>cstA</i> expression is negatively regulated by |FRAME: 
                     CPLX0-7705 Fis| and by |FRAME: CPLX0-7956 CsrA|; CsrA binds
                     specifically to <i>cstA</i> mRNA and the interaction is 
                     highly cooperative |CITS: [12867454][33260635]|.
                     The inner membrane protein CstA and the small protein 
                     |FRAME: MONOMER0-2660 YbdD| are implicated in constitutive 
                     pyruvate import; <i>cstA</i> and <i>ybdD</i> transposon 
                     mutants are enriched in the presence of the toxic pyruvate 
                     analog, 3 fluoropyruvate (3FP); &Delta;<i>cstA</i> and 
                     &Delta;<i>ybdD</i> strains avoid 3FP-induced growth 
                     inhibition (under pyruvate non-induced conditions) and 
                     import significantly less pyruvate than wild-type strains 
                     (under pyruvate induced conditions) |CITS: [29358499]|.
                     In the Transporter Classification Database |CITS: 
                     [26546518]| CstA is a member of the Peptide Transporter 
                     Carbon Starvation CstA Family within the Amino 
                     Acid-Polyamine-Organocation (APC) Superfamily.
                     "
