     CDS             complement(639013..639423)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rnk"
                     /locus_tag="b0610"
                     /product="nucleoside diphosphate kinase regulator"
                     /label=rnk
                     /note="The Rnk protein was first identified as a regulator
                     of |FRAME: NUCLEOSIDE-DIP-KIN-CPLX| (Ndk) protein levels 
                     |CITS: [7565093]|.  Rnk shows sequence and structural 
                     similarity to the C terminal domain of the Gre factors and 
                     competes with the Gre factors and DksA for binding to core 
                     RNA polymerase <i>in vitro</i>.  It may thus function as an
                     anti-Gre factor <i>in vivo</i>, although this has not yet 
                     been shown |CITS: [18760284]|.
                     A mutation in <i>rnk</i> leads to a significant reduction 
                     in the level of Ndk |CITS: [8596442]|.  Overexpression of 
                     <i>rnk</i> suppresses the oxidative stress sensitivity 
                     caused by a rifampicin-resistant <i>rpoB</i> mutation; UTP,
                     CTP, GTP, and ATP concentrations are restored to normal 
                     levels in the suppressed strain |CITS: [15836776]|. A 
                     crystal structure of Rnk has been solved at 1.91 &Aring; 
                     resolution |CITS: [18760284]|.
                     Expression of <i>rnk</i> is catabolite repressed |CITS: 
                     [7565093]|.
                     Rnk: ""<b>r</b>egulator of <b>n</b>ucleoside diphosphate 
                     <b>k</b>inase"" |CITS: [7565093]|"
