                     /EC_number="2.4.2.52"
                     /label=citG
                     /note="CitG catalyzes the synthesis of the citrate lyase 
                     prosthetic group precursor, 
                     2'-(5''-triphosphoribosyl)-3'-dephospho-CoA, from 
                     dephospho-CoA and ATP.  The enzyme does not catalyze the 
                     conversion of AMP-ACP to holo-ACP |CITS: 
                     [10924139][11042274]|.
                     Overexpression of <i>citG</i> from an ASKA plasmid leads to
                     a more than 3-fold increase in the MIC of hydrogen peroxide
                     |CITS: [34072091]|."
