     gene            complement(650039..651424)
                     /gene="dcuC"
                     /locus_tag="b0621"
                     /label=dcuC
     CDS             complement(650039..651424)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="dcuC"
                     /locus_tag="b0621"
                     /product="multifunctional anaerobic C4-dicarboxylate
                     transporter DcuC / succinate:H(+) symporter / 
                     succinate:fumarate antiporter / fumarate:H(+) symporter"
                     /label=dcuC
                     /note="DcuC is a C4-dicarboxylate transporter which may
                     function primarily as a succinate efflux transporter during
                     glucose fermentation.
                     When grown under anaerobic conditions <i>E. coli</i> K-12 
                     displays transport activities for uptake, efflux and 
                     exchange of C4-dicarboxylates. Fumarate:succinate exchange 
                     is required for fumarate respiration while succinate efflux
                     (without exchange) occurs during glucose fermentation; net 
                     uptake of C4-dicarboxylates is observed experimentally when
                     no counter substrate is present. The exchange reaction is 
                     electroneutral while uptake and efflux are electrogenic 
                     symport reactions probably of the dicarboxylate with 3 
                     H<sup>+</sup> (|CITS: [1512189][8020497]| and see review by
                     |CITS: [11803016]|). <i>E. coli</i> K-12 contains 3 
                     C4-dicarboxylate transporters (DcuA, DcuB and DcuC) that 
                     are active under anaerobic conditions; a strain lacking all
                     three (<i>dcuA</i>::Spc <i>dcuB</i>::Kan 
                     <i>dcuC</i>::mini-Tn10) is not able to grow anaerobically 
                     on fumarate plus glycerol; all three are active in both 
                     exchange and uptake |CITS: [8955408]|. Increased expression
                     of <i>dcuC</i> (due to an IS5 promoter mutation) is able to
                     compensate for DcuA and DcuB in fumarate-succinate exchange
                     and fumarate uptake |CITS: [10368146]|.
                     <I>dcuC</I> is expressed under anaerobic conditions and 
                     repressed in the presence of O<sub>2</sub>; anaerobic 
                     induction of expression is affected primarily by FNR with 
                     some contribution from ArcA |CITS:[10368146]|. <i>dcuC</i> 
                     is not subject to glucose repression and may function 
                     primarily in succinate efflux during glucose fermentation 
                     |CITS:[10368146]|. A <I>dcuC</I> deletion mutant has 
                     increased uptake and exchange of 
                     C<sub>4</sub>-dicarboxylates through DcuA and DcuB 
                     |CITS:[10368146]|.  The low rates of DcuC mediated 
                     C4-carboxylate exchange are inadequate for normal levels of
                     fumarate respiration, but are adequate for succinate export
                     during glucose fermentation |CITS:[8955408],[10368146]|. 
                     Succinate efflux during glucose fermentation is not 
                     diminished in strains lacking the aerobic and anaerobic 
                     C4-carboxylate transporters (DctA, DcuA, DcuB, DcuC, DcuD 
                     or CitT) suggesting the presence of another transporter 
                     active under these condtions |CITS:[11511871]|.
                     Related reviews: |CITS: [27415771]|
                     "
