     CDS             join(653487..653681,653681..654274)
                     /pseudo
                     /gene="ybeM"
                     /locus_tag="b4581"
                     /product="deamidated glutathione amidase, N-terminal
                     fragment"
                     /label=ybeM
                     /note="YbeM_1 and YbeM_2 are the N- and C-terminal
                     fragments of a pseudogene.  The sequence from <i>E. 
                     coli</i> MG1655 contains a nucleotide deletion at codon 66 
                     which results in a framshift error when compared to the 
                     full length allele in <i>E. coli</i> BL21(DE3), <i>E. 
                     coli</i> O157:H7 str. TW14359 and others.
                     Full-length YbeM from <i>E. coli</i> BL21 is a deamidated 
                     glutathione (dGSH) amidase that may function as a 
                     metabolite repair enzyme.  The purified recombinant protein
                     showed high activity toward dGSH |CITS: [28373563]|."
     gene            654403..654606
                     /gene="tatE"
                     /locus_tag="b0627"
                     /label=tatE
     CDS             654403..654606
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="tatE"
                     /locus_tag="b0627"
                     /product="bifunctional twin arginine protein translocation
                     system - TatE protein / twin arginine protein translocation
                     system"
                     /label=tatE
                     /note="TatE is an inner membrane component of the twin
                     arginine translocation (Tat) complex for the export of 
                     folded proteins.
                     TatE is predicted to contain an N-terminal transmembrane 
                     domain followed by an amphipathic helix and a cytoplasmic 
                     domain; TatE has 53% amino acid identity to TatA |CITS: 
                     [9649434]|. &Delta;<i>tatA</i> &Delta;<i>tatE</i> knockout 
                     mutants are unable to export a number of redox cofactor 
                     containing proteins; a &Delta;<i>tatA</i> strain is 
                     significantly more compromised for export than a 
                     &Delta;<i>tatE</i> strain |CITS: [9649434]|.
                     <i>tatE</i> forms a monocistronic unit which is transcribed
                     consititutively; TatE is synthesized at a much lower level 
                     than TatA |CITS: [11160116]|. TatE supports a lower level 
                     of Tat mediated transport than TatA |CITS: [24003141]|.
                     TatE: <u>t</u>win <u>a</u>rginine <u>t</u>ranslocation 
                     |CITS: [9649434]|
                     "
