     gene            complement(659558..660646)
                     /gene="rlpA"
                     /locus_tag="b0633"
                     /label=rlpA
     CDS             complement(659558..660646)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rlpA"
                     /locus_tag="b0633"
                     /product="rare lipoprotein RlpA"
                     /label=rlpA
                     /note="<i>rlpA</i> encodes a minor lipoprotein; the
                     unprocessed protein has an apparent molecular weight of 54 
                     kDa (by SDS-PAGE) despite a calculated molecular weight of 
                     ~36 kDa; <i>in vitro</i> expression of a mature protein is 
                     inhibited by treatment with the signal peptidase II 
                     inhibitor, globomycin; the protein incorporates 
                     <sup>3</sup>H-labeled palmitate and <sup>3</sup>H-labeled 
                     glycerol <i>in vitro</i> |CITS: [3316191]|.
                     A truncated version of RlpA (first 102 residues) suppresses
                     the conditional lethal phenotype of a |FRAME: EG10760 
                     <i>prc</i>| null mutation by an unknown mechanism |CITS: 
                     [8576052]|.
                     An RlpA fluorescent fusion protein (RlpA-RFP) accumulates 
                     at cell division sites, but is also localized elsewhere in 
                     the cell envelope; the isolated, labeled SPOR domain of 
                     RlpA (residues 281-362) accumulates at division sites and 
                     not in any other nonhomogenous pattern; deletion of 
                     <i>rlpA</i> does not result in cell growth or division 
                     defects |CITS: [19684127]| (see also |CITS: [19880599]|). 
                     The isolated, labeled SPOR domain of RlpA localizes to 
                     septal peptidoglycan in purified <i>E. coli</i> sacculi; 
                     septal accumulation is greatly reduced in sacculi (from 
                     amidase mutants) that lack |FRAME: a-denuded-peptidoglycan 
                     denuded glycans| and is increased in sacculi (from lytic 
                     transglycosylase mutants) that contain a higher level of 
                     denuded glycans |CITS: [26305949]|.
                     RlpA interacts physically with a functionally essential 
                     |FRAME: G6464-MONOMER FtsK| periplasmic loop; deletion of 
                     <i>rlpA</i> partially alleviates the growth and morphology 
                     defects associated with the temperature sensitive, loss of 
                     function, <i>ftsK44</i> mutation |CITS: [30154462]|.  An 
                     <i>rlpA</i> deletion mutant shows increased susceptibility 
                     to the &beta;-lactam antibiotic cefsulodin |CITS: 
                     [33144379]|.
                     <i>rlpA</i>: <u>r</u>are <u>l</u>ipo<u>p</u>rotein A |CITS:
                     [3316191]|"
