     gene            complement(663704..664171)
                     /gene="rlmH"
                     /locus_tag="b0636"
                     /label=rlmH
     CDS             complement(663704..664171)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rlmH"
                     /locus_tag="b0636"
                     /product="23S rRNA m(3)psi1915 methyltransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.1.1.177"
                     /label=rlmH
                     /note="RlmH is a methyltransferase that catalyzes the
                     addition of a methyl group in the N3 position of the 
                     pseudouridine (&Psi;) residue at nucleotide 1915 in 23S 
                     rRNA |CITS: [18755835][18755836]|.  The enzyme requires the
                     intact ribosome and the presence of pseudouridine at 
                     position 1915 in 23S rRNA for activity |CITS: 
                     [18755836][20817755]|.  m<sup>3</sup>&Psi;1915 is the only 
                     currently known methylated pseudouridine residue in 
                     bacterial RNAs.
                     Computational docking between RlmH and the ribosome shows 
                     contacts with both ribosomal subunits |CITS: [18755835]|, 
                     consistent with the requirement for intact ribosomes for 
                     <i>in vitro</i> activity |CITS: [18755836]|.
                     RlmH is a member of the SPOUT superfamily of 
                     methyltransferases |CITS: [11763972][17338813]| and belongs
                     to the &alpha;/&beta; knot superfamily of proteins |CITS: 
                     [17169371][17338813]|.  Thermodynamic and kinetic analysis 
                     of folding of RlmH shows that the protein folds via a 
                     simple three-state sequential mechanism |CITS: [17169371]|.
                      Folding may involve a slipknot intermediate |CITS: 
                     [19211785]|.  The RlmH polypeptide chain has a trefoil knot
                     conformation even in the denatured state |CITS: 
                     [20393125]|, but its overall structure is random coil-like 
                     |CITS: [25848882]|.  A circularly permuted RlmH that lacks 
                     the trefoil knot forms a domain-swapped dimer that is less 
                     stable and does not bind SAH |CITS: [31104814]|.
                     RlmH is a dimer in solution |CITS: 
                     [16848900][17169371][20393125]|.  Backbone NMR assignments 
                     for urea-denatured RlmH have been reported |CITS: 
                     [23821130]|.  Crystal structures of the homodimeric RlmH 
                     showed that the SAM-binding pocket is composed of residues 
                     in the knotted core of one monomer; the C-terminal tail of 
                     the second monomer completes the active site. Site-directed
                     mutagenesis of conserved residues within the predicted 
                     active showed that mutation of E138 or residues in the C 
                     terminus led to loss of catalytic activity |CITS: 
                     [28428565]|.
                     RlmH activity is influenced by the presence of specific 
                     nucleotides in stem-loop 69 (H69) surrounding &Psi;1915 in 
                     23S RNA |CITS: [22586702]|.
                     An <i>rlmH</i> deletion mutant lacks the 
                     m<sup>3</sup>&Psi;1915 modification |CITS: 
                     [18755835][18755836]| and has a slightly lower growth rate 
                     than wild type |CITS: [18755835]|.
                     RlmH: ""<b>r</b>RNA <b>l</b>arge subunit 
                     <b>m</b>ethyltransferase <b>H</b>"" |CITS: 
                     [18755835][18755836]|"
