     gene            complement(664175..664492)
                     /gene="rsfS"
                     /locus_tag="b0637"
                     /label=rsfS
     CDS             complement(664175..664492)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rsfS"
                     /locus_tag="b0637"
                     /product="ribosomal silencing factor RsfS"
                     /label=rsfS
                     /note="RsfS is a ribosomal silencing factor that inhibits 
                     assembly of the functional 70S ribosome.  It interacts 
                     directly with the |FRAME: EG10875-MONOMER| |CITS: 
                     [22829778]|.  RsfS may act as an anti-association factor in
                     both ribosome assembly and silencing |CITS: [33639093]|.
                     RsfS was found to associate with the 50S subunit of the 
                     ribosome |CITS: [16980477]|.  Cryo-EM reconstructions of 
                     50S ribosomal subunit precursors revealed a network of 
                     interacting ribosomal biogenesis factors that consists of 
                     RsfS, RluD, YjgA, and |FRAME: G7656-MONOMER ObgE|.  RsfS 
                     interacts directly with pre-50S subunit-associated ObgE at 
                     helix H95 of 23S rRNA and slightly enhances the GTPase 
                     activity of ObgE |CITS: [33639093]|.  RsfS is similar to 
                     the Lojap protein of <i>Zea mays</i>, which is involved in 
                     the stability of chloroplast ribosomes |CITS: [16592664]|. 
                     A transposon insertion in <i>rsfS</i> has a synthetic 
                     lethal phenotype with <i>minCDE</i>; this is likely due to 
                     its effect on the expression of one of the downstream 
                     genes, <i>mrdA</i> or <i>mrdB</i> |CITS: [15165230]|.
                     In a competitive growth experiment, an <i>rsfS</i> mutant 
                     has only a modest growth disadvantage under exponential 
                     growth conditions in rich medium.  However, <i>rsfS</i> 
                     mutants adapt slowly to poor growth conditions, and 
                     viability in stationary phase is decreased |CITS: 
                     [22829778]|.  An <i>rsfS</i> deletion mutant is more 
                     sensitive to ampicillin and kasugamycin than wild type 
                     |CITS: [23308060]|.
                     RsfS (RsfA): ""<b>r</b>ibosomal <b>s</b>ilencing 
                     <b>f</b>actor, <b>S</b>tationary phase"" |CITS: [22829778]|
                     Review: |CITS: [30476446]|"
