     CDS             670474..670956
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ybeL"
                     /locus_tag="b0643"
                     /product="DUF1451 domain-containing protein YbeL"
                     /label=ybeL
                     /note="YbeL is subject to C-terminal tagging with the SsrA 
                     degradation signal while the ribosome stalls at the stop 
                     codon |CITS: [11373298]|.  The C-terminal proline residue 
                     and the preceding glutamate residue were identified as 
                     determinants for efficient SsrA tagging |CITS: [12105207]|.
                     A peptide consisting of the N-terminal 120 amino acids of 
                     YbeL has been used as a translational fusion tag |CITS: 
                     [20525689]| as well as in a transcriptional fusion strategy
                     |CITS: [25451035]| to facilitate overexpression and 
                     purification of properly folded membrane proteins.
                     "
