                     of contact-dependent growth inhibition (CDI) systems in 
                     gram-negative bacteria; <i>gltK</i> transposon insertion 
                     mutants and <i>gltK</i> in-frame deletion mutants are 
                     resistant to the CdiA-CT<sup>TT01</sup> toxin; inner 
                     membrane proteins such as GltK are thought to act as 
                     receptors which bring the nuclease domain of CDI toxins 
                     into close proximity with the inner membrane of target 
                     cells |CITS: [26305955]|."
