     gene            complement(682137..682299)
                     /gene="sroC"
                     /locus_tag="b4763"
                     /label=sroC
     misc_RNA        complement(682137..682299)
                     /gene="sroC"
                     /locus_tag="b4763"
                     /product="small regulatory RNA SroC"
                     /note="SroC is encoded by the intergenic region between 
                     <i>gltI</i>, the first gene of a proposed alternative 
                     glutamate transport operon, and <i>gltJKL</i>.  A 5' end 
                     was identified by RACE.  Lacking <i>E. coli</i> promoter 
                     motifs upstream, it may be generated by transcription 
                     attenuation or processing.  The half life of SroC during 
                     stationary phase is 32 minutes |CITS: [14602901]|.
                     SroC destabilizes the |FRAME: GCVB-RNA| and may act as a 
                     ""sponge"" |CITS: [25630703][30447071]|.  In <i>E. coli</i>
                     W |CITS: [10972807]| and <i>Salmonella</i> |CITS: 
                     [17974919]|, the <i>gltI-sroC-gltJKL</i> mRNA is a 
                     regulatory target of GcvB.
                     SroC is most highly expressed in stationary phase |CITS: 
                     [30447071]|.  Overexpression of SroC decreases biofilm 
                     formation |CITS: [26469694]|.
                     The interaction of SroC with Hfq has been demonstrated 
                     |CITS: [36328526]|.
                     Reviews: |CITS: [32213244][32475775]|"
