                     transport of L-glutamate"
                     /EC_number="7.4.2.1"
                     /label=gltI
                     /note="GltI is the periplasmic binding protein of a 
                     glutamate/aspartate ABC transport system.
                     Purified GltI (released from <i>E. coli</i> K-12 strains by
                     osmotic shock treatment) binds L-glutamate and L-aspartate 
                     with &micro;M affinity; binding is competitively inhibited 
                     by L-glutamine and L-asparagine |CITS: [1091635][236016]|.
                     The amount of GltI is significantly reduced when E. coli W 
                     strain D<sub>2</sub>W is grown with glucose rather than 
                     succinate [Willis75]. Synthesis of GltI is repressed when 
                     the small regulatory RNA, |FRAME: GCVB-RNA ""GcvB""| is 
                     expressed from a plasmid in a &Delta;<i>gcvA</i> 
                     &Delta;<i>gcvB</i> background |CITS: [10972807]|."
