     gene            complement(688987..690411)
                     /gene="miaB"
                     /locus_tag="b0661"
                     /label=miaB
     CDS             complement(688987..690411)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="miaB"
                     /locus_tag="b0661"
                     /product="bifunctional isopentenyl-adenosine A37 tRNA 
                     methylthiolase / isopentenyl-adenosine tRNA methylthiolase"
                     /EC_number="2.8.4.3"
                     /label=miaB
                     /note="MiaB is an isopentenyl-adenosine tRNA
                     methylthiolase. Most <i>E. coli</i> tRNAs that read codons 
                     starting with U contain the modified base 
                     2-methylthio-<i>N</i><sup>6</sup>-isopentenyladenosine-37 
                     (ms<sup>2</sup>i<sup>6</sup>A37) |CITS: [3898020]|. MiaB is
                     required for both sulfur insertion and methylation at 
                     carbon 2 of <i>N</i><sup>6</sup>-isopentenyladenosine-37 in
                     tRNA, yielding the final modified 
                     ms<sup>2</sup>i<sup>6</sup>A37 tRNA |CITS: 
                     [7536729][10572129][11882645]|.
                     MiaB is a member of the Radical SAM protein superfamily 
                     |CITS: [11222759]| and was originally reported to bind two 
                     4Fe-4S clusters |CITS: [17910062][23543739]|. From studies 
                     in <i>E. coli</i> strain C6, the reaction is thought to 
                     take place in two steps: thiolation followed by methylation
                     |CITS: [49880]|. It is thought that the |FRAME: G7511 
                     ""YgfZ protein""| is involved in the repair/exchange of the
                     spent cluster of both MiaB and the homologous enzyme 
                     |FRAME: G6435 RimO| |CITS: [36902159]|. MiaB interacts with
                     |FRAME: CPLX0-7682 ""NfuA""| and |FRAME: EG12181-MONOMER 
                     ""GrxD""|. NfuA, but not GrxD, can transfer a 4Fe-4S 
                     cluster to apo-MiaB <i>in vitro</i>, and both proteins 
                     affect MiaB activity <i>in vivo</i> |CITS: [23543739]|.
                     A <i>miaB</i> mutant accumulates under-modified 
                     i<sup>6</sup>A tRNA |CITS: [10572129]|. However, unlike 
                     mutants in the associated gene <i>miaA</i>, <i>miaB</i> 
                     mutants do not have a mutator phenotype or a drop in 
                     tetracycline resistance |CITS: [11160115][9449261]|. 
                     Reviews: |CITS: [17936058][22178611][22846545][22905870]|"
