     CDS             complement(697059..698207)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="nagA"
                     /locus_tag="b0677"
                     /product="N-acetylglucosamine-6-phosphate deacetylase"
                     /EC_number="3.5.1.25"
                     /label=nagA
                     /note="N-acetylglucosamine-6-phosphate deacetylase
                     catalyzes the first cytoplasmic reaction in the metabolism 
                     of
                     N-acetyl-D-glucosamine.  N-acetylglucosamine can serve as 
                     the sole source of carbon for <i>E. coli</i> and is 
                     transported into the cell via phosphotransferase transport 
                     systems.  It thus reaches the cytoplasm in the 
                     phosphorylated form, N-acetylglucosamine-6-phosphate.
                     A catalytic mechanism of NagA involving the formation of a 
                     tetrahedral intermediate has been proposed
                     |CITS: [17567047]|, and the function of amino acids and the
                     Zn<sup>2+</sup> within the active site has been modelled 
                     |CITS: [17567048]|.  The rate-limiting step is the cleavage
                     of the amide bond |CITS: [17567047]|.
                     Crystal structures of the apoenzyme, the 
                     Zn<sup>2+</sup>-containing enzyme, and a mutant have been 
                     solved
                     |CITS: [16630633][17567048]|.  The enzyme is a homotetramer
                     both in solution |CITS: [9143339]| and in the crystal
                     structure |CITS: [16630633]|.
                     <i>nagA</i> mutants are unable to grow on 
                     N-acetylglucosamine as the sole source of carbon and energy
                     |CITS: [4866432][4591481]|.
                     NagA: ""<b>N</b>-<b>a</b>cetyl<b>g</b>lucosamine"" |CITS: 
                     [4591481]|
                     Review: |CITS: [18535144]|"
