                     /product="esterase"
                     /label=ybfF
                     /note="Thioesterase activity of YbfF with large substrates
                     such as palmitoyl-CoA and malonyl-CoA was discovered in a 
                     high-throughput screen of purified proteins |CITS: 
                     [15808744]|.  The enzyme also has general esterase activity
                     with
                     triacylglycerol substrates with short fatty acid chain 
                     lengths (C4, C8, C10), but not long chain lengths such as 
                     C18
                     |CITS: [18258174]|.
                     Crystal structures of the enzyme have been solved, 
                     revealing a canonical &alpha;/&beta; hydrolase domain and a
                     helical bundle cap domain.  The potential active site 
                     catalytic tetrad was identified.  Note that the 
                     crystallized protein
                     contained four point mutations resulting in amino acid 
                     changes |CITS: [18215690]|.
                     "
