     gene            complement(712402..713721)
                     /gene="potE"
                     /locus_tag="b0692"
                     /label=potE
     CDS             complement(712402..713721)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="potE"
                     /locus_tag="b0692"
                     /product="trifunctional putrescine transporter PotE / 
                     putrescine:H(+) symporter / putrescine:L-ornithine 
                     antiporter"
                     /label=potE
                     /note="PotE is a putrescine transporter which mediates 
                     putrescine efflux by a putrescine:ornithine antiport 
                     reaction and putrescine import by proton symport. 
                     <i>potE</i> is located in an operon with <i>speF</i> 
                     encoding an inducible ornithine decarboxylase; production 
                     and excretion of putrescine may be beneficial for growth 
                     under acidic conditions (see |CITS: [21796432][14982633]|).
                     Overexpression of <i>potE</i> in a polyamine-requiring 
                     strain increases putrescine uptake |CITS: [1939141]|. PotE 
                     mediated putrescine uptake (measured in a polyamine 
                     requiring strain lacking the putrescine uptake systems 
                     PotABCD and PotFGHI) is dependent on membrane potential; 
                     uptake stimulates growth in the polyamine requiring mutant;
                     uptake is inhibited by carbonyl cyanide 
                     <i>m</i>-chlorophenylhydrazone (CCCP), and by high 
                     concentrations of ornithine after putrescine accumulates in
                     cells |CITS: [9045651]|. PotE mediates the excretion of 
                     excess putrescine from intact cells; PotE mediates 
                     putrescine efflux via a 1:1 putrescine/ornithine antiport 
                     reaction; PotE also mediates putrescine:putrescine and 
                     ornithine:ornithine exchange reactions <i>in vitro</i> 
                     |CITS: [1584788]|.
                     PotE is an inner membrane protein with twelve predicted 
                     transmembrane domains; experimental topology analysis 
                     suggests both termini are located in the cytosol |CITS: 
                     [1939141][9045651]|.
                     <i>potE</i> expression is low at neutral pH |CITS: 
                     [9045651]|.
                     PotE is a member of the Basic Amino 
                     Acid/Polyamine-Antiporter (APA) family of transporters 
                     within the Amino Acid-Polyamine-Organocation (APC) 
                     superfamily |CITS: [10931886][26546518]|."
