                     /locus_tag="b0693"
                     /label=speF
     CDS             complement(713718..715916)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="speF"
                     /locus_tag="b0693"
                     /product="bifunctional inducible ornithine decarboxylase / 
                     ornithine decarboxylase"
                     /EC_number="4.1.1.17"
                     /label=speF
                     /note="<i>E. coli</i> encodes two ornithine decarboxylase 
                     enzymes, the biosynthetic (constitutive) |FRAME: 
                     ORNDECARBOX-BIO-CPLX SpeC| and the degradative (inducible) 
                     SpeF |CITS: [3157043][1939141]|.  SpeF is activated by the 
                     guanosine nucleotides GTP, GDP, pppGpp and ppGpp |CITS: 
                     [15587][21957966]|.
                     SpeF enzymatic activity is induced by growth at low pH 
                     (5.5) |CITS: [318645]|.  SpeF is overproduced from a 
                     <i>speF</i>-containing plasmid when cells are grown at pH 
                     5.2, but not at pH 7 |CITS: [1939141]|.  Overexpression of 
                     RNase III from a plasmid increases expression from the 
                     <i>speF</i> promoter, perhaps by processing of the 5' UTR 
                     |CITS: [8166735]|.
                     Expression of SpeF is also regulated by attenuation in 
                     response to ornithine |CITS: [32094585]|; see the summary 
                     for the |FRAME: MONOMER0-4532|."
