     CDS             complement(719863..720435)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="kdpC"
                     /locus_tag="b0696"
                     /product="trifunctional K(+) transporting P-type ATPase
                     subunit KdpC / K(+) transporting P-type ATPase / K(+) 
                     transporting ATPase"
                     /EC_number="7.2.2.6"
                     /label=kdpC
                     /note="KdpC is an inner membrane subunit of a potassium
                     ion transporting P-type ATPase complex.
                     A non-polar &Delta;<i>kdpC</i> strain is unable to grow 
                     under low potassium (<0.1mM) conditions |CITS: [11248697]|.
                     KdpC contains a conserved motif that is also present in ABC
                     transporters; KdpC binds ATP; coordination of ATP occurs 
                     via the formation of a transient KdpB/KdpC/ATP complex 
                     |CITS: [21711450]|.
                     KdpC is predicted to be a bitopic inner membrane protein 
                     |CITS: [27510400]|. In the x-ray structure of 
                     KdpFA<sub>(G116R)</sub>BC, KdpC has a single transmembrane 
                     helix and a soluble domain located on the periplasmic side 
                     of the membrane |CITS: [28636601]|."
