     gene            725039..729232
                     /gene="rhsC"
                     /locus_tag="b0700"
                     /label=rhsC
     CDS             725039..729232
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rhsC"
                     /locus_tag="b0700"
                     /product="rhs element protein RhsC"
                     /label=rhsC
                     /note="There are five homologous rhs loci |CITS:
                     [2644231]| that encode hydrophilic proteins with repetitive
                     sequence elements and divergent C-termini |CITS: 
                     [2403547]|. RhsA, RhsB, and RhsC define one subfamily, and 
                     RhsD and RhsE define a second subfamily of Rhs elements 
                     |CITS: [1766878]|.  Additional rhs elements and subfamilies
                     have been characterized in other strains (not K-12) |CITS: 
                     [7868617], [8536964], [9696756]|.
                     Some of the rhs loci are reported to contain multiple open 
                     reading frames: rhsA |CITS: [7721712]|, rhsB |CITS: 
                     [8387990]|, and rhsC |CITS: [8387990]|.
                     RhsA, RhsB, RhsC, and RhsD include 28 copies of the core 
                     repeat element |CITS: [2403547]| and RhsB, RhsC, and RhsE 
                     also include H-rpt (Hinc repeat) elements, which may be 
                     nonfunctional in RhsC |CITS: [8387990]|.
                     Overproduction of an RhsA fragment causes decreased 
                     survival at stationary phase; this effect is suppressed by 
                     co-overproduction of another part of the element and RpoS 
                     plays a role in moderation of toxicity |CITS: [7721712]|."
