                     /product="bifunctional 5-oxoprolinase component A /
                     5-oxoprolinase"
                     /EC_number="3.5.2.9"
                     /label=pxpA
                     /note="Overexpression of <i>pxpBCA</i> leads to the
                     presence of detectable oxoprolinase activity in cell 
                     lysates.  A <i>pxpA</i> deletion mutant grows to a lower OD
                     than wild type in minimal medium with ammonium as the sole 
                     source of nitrogen |CITS: [28830929]|.
                     While wild-type <i>E. coli</i> shows significantly 
                     decreased swarming motility upon exposure to volatile 
                     organic compounds (VOCs) produced by <i>Bacillus 
                     subtilis</i>, a <i>pxpA</i> null mutant shows no 
                     significant difference in swarming motility upon VOC 
                     treatment |CITS: [23651997]|.
                     PxpA: ""<b>p</b>rokaryotic 5-o<b>x</b>o<b>p</b>rolinase 
                     <b>A</b>"" |CITS: [28830929]|"
