                     operons, including <i>ybgOPQD</i>. When this operon is 
                     removed, the cells are larger, produce 
                     polyhydroxyalkanoates (PHAs) and grows better, particularly
                     in M9G media. A  fimbrial-lacking mutant - strain WQM026 - 
                     created by deleting all 12 operons has been characterised; 
                     it also grows faster and produces PHAs and had higher 
                     efficiency of glucose utilization |CITS: [33863704]|."
