     gene            751363..753129
                     /gene="sdhA"
                     /locus_tag="b0723"
                     /label=sdhA
     CDS             751363..753129
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="sdhA"
                     /locus_tag="b0723"
                     /product="trifunctional succinate:quinone oxidoreductase,
                     FAD binding protein / succinate:quinone oxidoreductase 
                     subcomplex / succinate:quinone oxidoreductase"
                     /EC_number="1.3.5.1"
                     /label=sdhA
                     /note="This is one of two catalytic subunits in the four
                     subunit succinate dehydrogenase (SQR) enzyme. This subunit 
                     contains the FAD cofactor |CITS: [2659351]| and the 
                     substrate-binding site |CITS: [12560550]|. The redox 
                     potential of SdhA-bound FAD cofactor is -55.5 mV |CITS: 
                     [33659541]|.
                     Succinate, fumarate, citrate, and isocitrate appear to 
                     cause increased flavinylation of overproduced SdhA in cell 
                     extracts, indicating the existence of an activation 
                     mechanism involving TCA cycle intermediates |CITS: 
                     [2659351]|.
                     This protein has similarity to the FrdA subunit of fumarate
                     reductase |CITS: [6383359]|.  A 2.2 &Aring; crystal 
                     structure of L-aspartate oxidase suggests that an unusual 
                     tertiary structure is shared by L-aspartate oxidase, the 
                     SdhA subunit of succinate dehydrogenase, and the FrdA 
                     subunit of fumarate reductase  |CITS: [10425677]|.
                     SdhA may play a role in bacteriophage T4 infection |CITS: 
                     [38675830]|."
