                     /locus_tag="b0729"
                     /label=sucD
     CDS             759636..760505
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="sucD"
                     /locus_tag="b0729"
                     /product="bifunctional succinyl-CoA synthetase subunit
                     alpha / succinyl-CoA synthetase"
                     /EC_number="6.2.1.5"
                     /label=sucD
                     /note="SucD is the &alpha; subunit of succinyl-CoA
                     synthetase.
                     His246 is the phosphorylated residue of the reaction 
                     intermediate. A His246Asp mutant can not autophosphorylate 
                     and has no catalytic activity |CITS: 
                     [2548486][1986797][1993168]|. A His142 mutant is 
                     catalytically inactive for the overall reaction, but the 
                     enzyme can be phosphorylated with ATP and dephosphorylated 
                     with succinate |CITS: [1939128]|. Glu208 is essential for 
                     phosphorylation and dephosphorylation of His246 |CITS: 
                     [11781092]|. The conserved Cys123 is not required for 
                     catalytic activity |CITS: [17642514]|.
                     Based on a new quantitative top-down proteomics method 
                     using iodo-tandem mass tags, 16 proteoforms of SucD were 
                     found to respond differently when grown in glucose as 
                     compared to acetate, pointing to possible different 
                     functions |CITS: [39885717]|.
                     Cysteine sites in peptides of this SucD subunit were 
                     significantly oxidized in a redox proteomics study in a 
                     &Delta;|FRAME: CPLX0-245 Ahp| mutant |CITS: [37725887]|."
