     gene            760506..760606
                     /gene="sdhX"
                     /locus_tag="b4764"
                     /label=sdhX
     misc_RNA        760506..760606
                     /gene="sdhX"
                     /locus_tag="b4764"
                     /product="small regulatory RNA SdhX"
                     /note="The small regulatory RNA SdhX connects the
                     expression of TCA cycle genes to acetate metabolism.  SdhX 
                     represses expression of AckA |CITS: [30541135][30591570]|, 
                     FdoG and KatG in <i>E. coli</i> |CITS: [30541135]|.
                     SdhX was originally detected as a 103 nt Hfq-interacting 
                     small RNA |CITS: [14622403]|.  SdhX is processed from the 
                     3' UTR of the <i>sdhCDAB-sucABCD</i> mRNA by |FRAME: 
                     EG10859-MONOMER RNase E|; |FRAME: EG10438-MONOMER Hfq| 
                     appears to play a role in processing |CITS: [30591570]|. 
                     SdhX and 33 potential targets were also identified by 
                     applying a small RNA prediction algorithm to RIL-seq data 
                     |CITS: [34093460]|.
                     SdhX expression is regulated at the transcriptional level 
                     identically to the <i>sdh</i> operon promoter, |FRAME: 
                     PM00143|, and is not affected by posttranscriptional 
                     regulation exerted by the small RNA regulators RybB, RyhB 
                     and Spot 42 |CITS: [30591570]|.
                     Overexpression of SdhX increases resistance to hydroxyurea 
                     via its effect on <i>ackA</i> expression, and deletion of 
                     <i>sdhX</i> reduces the growth lag during exposure to 
                     hydrogen peroxide, likely due to its effect on <i>katG</i> 
                     expression |CITS: [30591570]|.
                     Review: |CITS: [32213244]|"
