     gene            761440..763416
                     /gene="mngA"
                     /locus_tag="b0731"
                     /label=mngA
     CDS             761440..763416
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="mngA"
                     /locus_tag="b0731"
                     /product="2-O-alpha-mannosyl-D-glycerate specific PTS
                     enzyme II"
                     /EC_number="2.7.1.195"
                     /label=mngA
                     /note="MngA, a PTS permease, belongs to the functional 
                     superfamily of the phosphoenolpyruvate (PEP)-dependent, 
                     sugar transporting phosphotransferase system 
                     (PTS<sup>sugar</sup>). The PTS<sup>sugar</sup> transports 
                     and simultaneously phosphorylates its substrates in a 
                     process called group translocation (reviewed in |CITS: 
                     [8246840]|. MngA takes up exogenous 
                     2-<i>O</i>-&alpha;-mannosyl-D-glycerate (MG), releasing the
                     phosphate ester into the cell cytoplasm for hydrolysis by 
                     the <i>mngB</i> encoded |FRAME: EG13236-MONOMER| |CITS: 
                     [14645248]|.
                     <i>E. coli</i> K-12 can use MG as the sole source of 
                     carbon. An <i>E. coli &Delta;mngA</i> strain cannot grow 
                     with MG as sole carbon source. MG induces expression of 
                     <i>mngA</i>. Membranes containing MngA are able to 
                     phosphorylate MG <i>in vitro</i> in the presence of PEP, 
                     PtsI and PtsH |CITS: [14645248]|.
                     <i>mngA</i> formerly known as <i>hsrA</i> was initially 
                     identified during a study of thermoresponsive genes in 
                     <i>E. coli</i> K-12 |CITS: [9063979]|. <i>mngA</i> contains
                     IIA, IIB and IIC PTS domains in a single polypeptide chain 
                     and shows sequence similarity with the fructose specific 
                     PTS proteins. MngA contains two putative phosphorylation 
                     sites at His<sup>87</sup> and Cys<sup>192</sup> |CITS: 
                     [9063979], [9092011]|. MngA is a member of the PTS 
                     Fructose-Mannitol (Fru) family of transporters |CITS: 
                     [24225317]|.
                     The overall PTS-mediated phosphoryl transfer reaction, 
                     requiring the two general energy coupling proteins of the 
                     PTS, |FRAME: CPLX0-7938 ""Enzyme I""| (PtsI) and |FRAME: 
                     PTSH-MONOMER ""HPr""| (PtsH), as well as the three domains 
                     of the Enzyme II<sup>MngA</sup> complex can be represented 
                     as:
                     PEP &rarr; Enzyme I-P<sup>his189</sup> &rarr; 
                     HPr-P<sup>his15</sup> &rarr; Enzyme IIA-P<sup>his87</sup> 
                     &rarr; Enzyme IIB-P<sup>cys192</sup>-(Enzyme IIC) &rarr; 
                     2-<i>O</i>-6-phospho-&alpha;-mannosyl-D-glycerate"
                     /translation="MVLFYRAHWRDYKNDQVRIMMNLTTLTHRDALCLNARFTSREEAI
