     CDS             763434..766067
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="mngB"
                     /locus_tag="b0732"
                     /product="bifunctional alpha-mannosidase / 
                     2-O-(6-phospho-alpha-mannosyl)-D-glycerate hydrolase"
                     /label=mngB
                     /note="MngB is an &alpha;-mannosidase that appears to be 
                     responsible for the conversion of 
                     2-<i>O</i>-(6-phospho-&alpha;-mannosyl)-D-glycerate (MG-P) 
                     to mannose-6-phosphate and glycerate in the |FRAME: 
                     PWY0-1300| pathway |CITS: [14645248]|.  The enzyme has not 
                     yet been purified and assayed <i>in vitro</i>.
                     Expression of <i>mngAB</i> is repressed by MngR and induced
                     when cells are grown in 
                     2-<i>O</i>-&alpha;-mannosyl-D-glycerate (MG).  <i>mngB</i> 
                     mutants are unable to grow in medium containing high levels
                     of MG (without secondary mutations in <i>mngA</i>), likely 
                     due to the toxicity of accumulating MG-P within the cells 
                     |CITS: [14645248]|.
                     MngB: ""<b>m</b>a<b>n</b>nosyl<b>g</b>lycerate catabolism 
                     <b>B</b>"" |CITS: [14645248]|"
