     gene            766914..768482
                     /gene="cydA"
                     /locus_tag="b0733"
                     /label=cydA
     CDS             766914..768482
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="cydA"
                     /locus_tag="b0733"
                     /product="bifunctional cytochrome bd-I subunit 1 /
                     cytochrome bd-I ubiquinol:oxygen oxidoreductase"
                     /EC_number="7.1.1.7"
                     /label=cydA
                     /note="<i>cydA</i> encodes subunit I of the cytochrome 
                     <i>bd</i>-I complex; it contains all three heme cofactors 
                     (heme <i>b<sub>558</sub></i>, heme <i>b<sub>595</sub></i> 
                     and heme <i>d</i>) and is the site of ubiquinol oxidation 
                     and oxygen reduction |CITS: [31604309][31723136]|.
                     CydA contains the heme <i>b<sub>558</sub></i> component of 
                     cytochrome <i>bd</i>-I and is the site of ubiquinol 
                     oxidation |CITS: [6376497][3301837][3013298]|. Purified, 
                     reconstituted CydA can be reduced by ubiquinol but it does 
                     not reduce molecular oxygen |CITS: [3013298]|. The CydA 
                     protein has nine transmembrane helices, the N-terminus is 
                     located in the periplasm and the C-terminus in the 
                     cytoplasm |CITS: [10076013][15013751]|; in the <i>bd</i>-I 
                     complex, the subunit forms two four-helix bundles with an 
                     additional peripheral helix |CITS: [31604309]| (see also 
                     |CITS: [31723136]|). A dynamic periplasmic loop (the 
                     Q-loop) located between transmembrane regions VI and VII is
                     implicated in ubiquinol binding |CITS: [1689724][1707310], 
                     [10076013][16299377]| (further |CITS: 
                     [31604309][31723136]|). The axial ligands for heme 
                     <i>b<sub>558</sub></i> are His-186 and Met-393 |CITS: 
                     [2656671][7577938][7772053]|; heme <i>b<sub>595</sub></i> 
                     is penta-coordinated with Glu-445 as the axial ligand while
                     His-19 is the axial ligand for heme <i>d</i> |CITS: 
                     [2656671][31604309]|. The three heme cofactors are 
                     organized in a triangular geometry near the periplasmic 
                     surface of CydA |CITS: [31604309][31723136]|."
