     gene            768498..769637
                     /gene="cydB"
                     /locus_tag="b0734"
                     /label=cydB
     CDS             768498..769637
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="cydB"
                     /locus_tag="b0734"
                     /product="bifunctional cytochrome bd-I subunit 2 /
                     cytochrome bd-I ubiquinol:oxygen oxidoreductase"
                     /EC_number="7.1.1.7"
                     /label=cydB
                     /note="<i>cydB</i> encodes subunit II of the cytochrome 
                     <i>bd</i>-I complex. Subunit II has eight predicted 
                     transmembrane helices; the N and C-termini are located in 
                     the cytoplasm |CITS: [10076013]|; in the <i>bd</i>-I 
                     complex, the subunit forms two four-helix bundles with an 
                     additional peripheral helix |CITS: [31604309]|. Subunit I 
                     (encoded by <i>cydA</i>) and subunit II are both required 
                     for binding of the heme <i>b<sub>595</sub></i> and heme 
                     <i>d</i> components of cytochrome <i>bd</i>-I |CITS: 
                     [1851043]|. In the cryo-EM structure of the <i>bd</i>-I 
                     complex reported by |CITS: [31604309]|, CydB binds a 
                     structural ubiquinone-8 cofactor that may have a role in 
                     CydAB dimer assembly (see also |CITS: [31723136]|)."
