     CDS             770208..770612
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ybgC"
                     /locus_tag="b0736"
                     /product="esterase/thioesterase"
                     /label=ybgC
                     /note="Esterase/thioesterase activity of YbgC was
                     discovered in a high-throughput screen of purified proteins
                     |CITS: [15808744]|.  The <i>Haemophilus influenzae</i> 
                     ortholog YbgC was shown to be an acyl-coenzyme A 
                     thioesterase |CITS: [11959124]|.  The <i>Synechocystis</i> 
                     ortholog is a 1,4-dihydroxy-2-naphthoyl-CoA (DHNA-CoA) 
                     thioesterase which generates 1,4-dihydroxy-2-naphthoate, an
                     intermediate in menaquinone biosynthesis |CITS: 
                     [20643650]|.  However, YbgC has no detectable activity with
                     DHNA-CoA or aryl-CoA analogues |CITS: [23564174]|. YbgC 
                     interacts with ACP and may be involved in phospholipid 
                     metabolism |CITS: [16294310]|.
                     <i>ybgC</i> is the first gene in an operon together with 
                     <i>tolQRA</i> |CITS: [8763928][9068659]|; however, a 
                     <i>ybgC</i>::Cm insertion strain does not have an obvious 
                     phenotype and does not appear to have a polar effect on 
                     <i>tolQ</i> |CITS: [3294803]|.
                     "
