     gene            770609..771301
                     /gene="tolQ"
                     /locus_tag="b0737"
                     /label=tolQ
     CDS             770609..771301
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="tolQ"
                     /locus_tag="b0737"
                     /product="trifunctional energy transducing Tol complex
                     motor protein TolQ / energy transducing Tol complex / 
                     Tol-Pal Cell Envelope Complex"
                     /label=tolQ
                     /note="TolQ is an inner membrane component of the Tol-Pal
                     system - a group of interacting proteins which span the 
                     cell envelope of <i>E. coli</i> K-12. The Tol-Pal system 
                     plays a role in outer membrane invagination and septal 
                     peptidoglycan processing during cell division and is 
                     important for maintaining outer membrane integrity via 
                     lipid homeostasis. It also has a role in facilitating phage
                     infection and colicin uptake
                     TolQ is an inner membrane protein containing three 
                     transmembrane regions; its C-terminus is located in the 
                     cytoplasm, as is a large loop between the first and second 
                     transmembrane regions, and the N-terminus is in the 
                     periplasm |CITS: [8331075][8300535]|. TolQ accumulates at 
                     the site of constriction in dividing cells; this 
                     localisation is dependent on |FRAME: EG11529-MONOMER 
                     ""FtsN""| |CITS: [17233825]| (and further |CITS: [ 
                     34748387]|).
                     TolQ interacts with TolR and TolA |CITS: 
                     [7744737][7853390][9851983][10419942]|. TolQ is required 
                     for TolA-Pal interaction |CITS:[11722743]|. The second and 
                     third transmembrane domains of TolQ and the TolR 
                     transmembrane domain interact and may consititute an ion 
                     conducting channel |CITS: [17222427][11722743]|. TolQ forms
                     multimers <i>in vivo</i> and <i>in vitro</i> |CITS: 
                     [21285349]|.
                     Mutations in <i>tolQ</i> render (F-plasmid-containing) 
                     cells tolerant to the group A colicins and prevent 
                     infection by filamentous bacteriophage |CITS: 
                     [3001021][3294803]|.
                     <i>tolQ</i> and |FRAME: EG10271 ""<i>exbB</i>""| have 51.2%
                     nucleotide sequence homology |CITS: [2670903]|. TolQ has 
                     protein sequence similarity with |FRAME: 
                     MOTA-FLAGELLAR-MOTOR-STATOR-PROTEIN ""MotA""| |CITS: 
                     [11722743]|
                     <i>tol</i>: colicin <U>tol</U>erant |CITS: 
                     [4167587][4860908]|<BR><i>fii</i>: filamentous phage 
                     infection |CITS: [3001021]|"
