     gene            777541..778584
                     /gene="nadA"
                     /locus_tag="b0750"
                     /label=nadA
     CDS             777541..778584
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="nadA"
                     /locus_tag="b0750"
                     /product="quinolinate synthase"
                     /EC_number="2.5.1.72"
                     /label=nadA
                     /note="Quinolinate synthase catalyzes the second reaction
                     in the <i>de novo</i> biosynthesis of NAD from aspartate, 
                     the condensation of |FRAME: IMINOASPARTATE| with |FRAME: 
                     DIHYDROXY-ACETONE-PHOSPHATE| to form |FRAME: QUINOLINATE|. 
                     NadA was shown to contain an oxygen-sensitive [4Fe-4S] 
                     cluster that is required for its activity |CITS: 
                     [15898769][15967443]|, explaining the NAD auxotrophy of an 
                     |FRAME: G7325| mutant.  Reaction mechanisms involving the 
                     [4Fe-4S] cluster have been proposed |CITS: [15898769]|. The
                     conserved C113, C200 and C297 residues are involved in 
                     [4Fe-4S] cluster binding |CITS: [18674537]|.  The C291 and 
                     C294 residues appear to undergo reversible disulfide bond 
                     formation that regulates the activity of the enzyme |CITS: 
                     [18651751][18674537]|.  The midpoint potential of -264 mV 
                     is similar to that of thioredoxin and of the cytosol |CITS:
                     [18651751]|.
                     Overexpression of NadA of <i>E. coli</i> BL21 (DE3) used in
                     a microbial fuel cell using L-aspartate as the substrate 
                     increased production of NAD(H), and resulted in 
                     substantially increased voltage (an increase of 360%) 
                     |CITS: [36877035]|.
                     NadA: ""<b>NAD</b> biosynthesis"" |CITS: [4315893]|."
