                     /gene="modF"
                     /locus_tag="b0760"
                     /product="ABC family protein ModF"
                     /label=modF
                     /note="ModF contains sequence motifs conserved in
                     ATP-binding cassette (ABC) proteins; ModF contains an 
                     ABC-ABC domain |CITS: [9593292]|. <i>modF</i> is not 
                     essential for synthesis of molybdenum cofactor or for 
                     molybdenum uptake and is not involved in regulation of the 
                     <i>mod</i> operon: insertional inactivation of <i>modF</i> 
                     does not affect the activity of molybdoenzymes (nitrate 
                     reductase, formate dehydrogenase, trimethylamine-N-oxide 
                     reductase) |CITS: [8564363]|. <i>modF</i> expression may be
                     repressed by molybdate: expression of a plasmid borne 
                     &phi;(<i>modF-lacZ</i>) fusion increases when cells are 
                     grown in low molybdate glucose minimal media |CITS: 
                     [8550508]|.
                     <i>modE</i> and <i>modF</i> form a two-gene operon |CITS: 
                     [8550508]|
                     |CITS: [18634750]| suggests that ModF is a component of a 
                     molybdate ABC transporter - ModABCF.
                     <i>phrA</i>: <U>ph</U>oto<U>r</U>epair |CITS: 
                     [8310005][7791009]|"
