     gene            complement(793069..793887)
                     /gene="ybhA"
                     /locus_tag="b0766"
                     /label=ybhA
     CDS             complement(793069..793887)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ybhA"
                     /locus_tag="b0766"
                     /product="trifunctional pyridoxal 
                     phosphate/fructose-1,6-bisphosphate phosphatase / pyridoxal
                     phosphatase / fructose 1,6-bisphosphatase"
                     /EC_number="3.1.3.74; 3.1.3.11"
                     /label=ybhA
                     /note="YbhA is a pyridoxal phosphate phosphatase that 
                     contributes to PLP homeostasis within the cell. Addition of
                     pyridoxal to a wild-type strain grown in minimal medium 
                     leads to an extended lag phase, and cells accumulate PLP. 
                     Overexpression of YbhA alleviates this phenotype. 
                     Conversely, overexpression of YbhA in cells grown in 
                     minimal medium leads to a reduced growth rate and decreased
                     levels of intracellular PLP; the growth defect can be 
                     rescued by addition of pyridoxal to the growth medium 
                     |CITS: [29187681]|.
                     The phosphatase activity of YbhA was first discovered in a 
                     high-throughput screen of purified proteins |CITS: 
                     [15808744]|. YbhA is a promiscuous phosphatase belonging to
                     the superfamily of haloacid dehalogenase (HAD)-like 
                     hydrolases. Its preferred substrates are pyridoxal 
                     phosphate and fructose 1,6-bisphosphate |CITS: [16990279]|.
                     In addition, YbhA appears to have a low level of 
                     phosphotransferase activity using monophosphates as the 
                     phosphate donor |CITS: [16889420]| and a low 
                     &beta;-phosphoglucomutase activity |CITS: [16990279]|. YbhA
                     may exist as a homodimer in solution; gel filtration 
                     analysis of purified recombinant protein showed the 
                     presence of both a monomer and a homodimer |CITS: 
                     [16889420]|.
                     <i>E. coli</i> encodes several enzymes with fructose 
                     1,6-bisphosphate phosphatase activity; YbhA appears to be a
                     less efficient fructose 1,6-bisphosphate phosphatase than 
                     Fbp, GlpX and YggF |CITS: [19073594]|.
                     An open reading frame downstream of and in the same 
                     orientation as <i>modABC</i>, <i>modD</i>, was originally 
                     annotated at this genome location |CITS: [7860583]|."
