     gene            complement(795078..796031)
                     /gene="ybhD"
                     /locus_tag="b0768"
                     /label=ybhD
     CDS             complement(795078..796031)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ybhD"
                     /locus_tag="b0768"
                     /product="putative DNA-binding transcriptional regulator
                     YbhD"
                     /label=ybhD
                     /note="YbhD was predicted to be a LysR-type transcription
                     factor |CITS: [34428301] [35880217]|; it contains a 
                     helix-turn-helix DNA-binding motif in its N-terminal domain
                     |CITS: [35880217]| and is probably involved in regulation 
                     of L-malate utilization |CITS:[35508583]|. However, the 
                     effect of YbhD on the transcription of any gene has not yet
                     been demonstrated |CITS: [34428301] [35508583]|.
                     YbhD DNA-binding activity was probed in vivo in glucose M9 
                     minimal medium by the chromatin immunoprecipitation method 
                     combined with lambda exonuclease digestion (ChIP-exo) 
                     |CITS: [34428301]|.
                     YbhD was found transcriptionally upregulated in the 
                     presence of threonine (Thr) in M9 medium |CITS:[35508583]|.
                     The transcriptional response for the deletion of YbdH has 
                     been characterized by RNA-seq in M9 minimal medium 
                     supplemented with 7 mM l-threonine |CITS:[35508583]|. In 
                     the YbdH knockout strain, the gene <i>ybhH</i>, which is 
                     adjacent and divergently oriented from <i>ybhD</i>, was 
                     strongly upregulated. It was then proposed that YbdH 
                     negatively regulates it; however, binding was not detected 
                     under the growth conditions used in ChIP-exo studies 
                     |CITS:[34428301] [35508583]|.
                     A YbhD knockout strain is able to grow in M9 minimal medium
                     with glycerol only when L-malate is supplemented 
                     |CITS:[35508583]|.
                     Upstream of the <i>ybhD</i> gene, a sequence was found that
                     could work as a transcriptional promoter, and the 
                     transcription of the <i> ybhD</i> gene is affected by 
                     glucose-lactose shift |CITS: [35880217]|.
                     The YbhD binding landscape was globally mapped in vivo by 
                     standardized ChIP-seq and quantitatively modeled using 
                     BoltzNet, a biophysically informed neural network that 
                     infers binding energy from sequence data |CITS:[40335485]|.
                     The resulting ChIP-seq binding regions are available in 
                     RegulonDB (<a href=""https://regulondb.cc 
                     g.unam.mx/ht/dataset/TFBINDING/source=GALAGAN"">Galagan 
                     collection</a>), and the corresponding energy matrix and 
                     genomic binding profiles can be accessed at <a 
                     href=""http://boltznet.bu.edu"">boltznet.bu.edu</a> 
                     |CITS:[40335485]|."
                     /translation="MKHELSSMKAFVILAESSSFNNAAKLLNITQPALTRRIKKMEEDL
                     HVQLFERTTRKVTLTKAGKRLLPEARELIKKFDETLFNIRDMNAYHRGMVTLACIPTAV
