     gene            complement(801454..802737)
                     /gene="ybhC"
                     /locus_tag="b0772"
                     /label=ybhC
     CDS             complement(801454..802737)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ybhC"
                     /locus_tag="b0772"
                     /product="outer membrane lipoprotein YbhC"
                     /label=ybhC
                     /note="YbhC is an outer membrane lipoprotein |CITS:
                     [10806384]|. Sequence similarity suggests that it is a 
                     member of the Outer Membrane Porin (OPR) Family |CITS: 
                     [12192075]|. Phylogenetic analysis places YbhC into a 
                     distinct subclade of the carbohydrate esterase 8 (CE8) 
                     family |CITS: [19452549]|.
                     Esterase/thioesterase activity of YbhC was discovered in a 
                     high-throughput screen of purified proteins |CITS: 
                     [15808744]|. This activity could not be reproduced by 
                     |CITS: [19452549]|.
                     YbhC is enriched in the membrane fraction of minicells 
                     (versus rod cells) purifed from an <i>E. coli</i> minicell 
                     mutant and is a polar protein candidate |CITS: [15130122]|.
                     A crystal structure of a truncated form of YbhC lacking the
                     membrane anchor has been solved at 1.7 &Aring; resolution 
                     |CITS: [19452549]|.
                     Overexpression of <i>yhbC</i> from an ASKA plasmid leads to
                     a more than 3-fold increase in the MIC of hydrogen peroxide
                     |CITS: [34072091]|."
