                     /locus_tag="b0780"
                     /product="putative transferase YbhK"
                     /label=ybhK
                     /note="The function of YbhK in <i>E. coli</i> is not
                     known.  The <i>ybhK</i> gene can functionally substitute 
                     for its homolog in <i>Bacillus subtilis</i>, <i>yvcK</i>, 
                     which is essential for growth on Krebs cycle intermediates 
                     and carbon sources that are metabolized via the pentose 
                     phosphate pathway |CITS: [16272399]|."
