     gene            complement(817954..819195)
                     /gene="clsB"
                     /locus_tag="b0789"
                     /label=clsB
     CDS             complement(817954..819195)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="clsB"
                     /locus_tag="b0789"
                     /product="trifunctional cardiolipin synthase B /
                     cardiolipin synthase / phosphatidylglycerol synthase"
                     /EC_number="2.7.8.41"
                     /label=clsB
                     /note="ClsB is the second cardiolipin synthase in <i>E.
                     coli</i> |CITS: [10634942][27760827]|.  Synthesis of 
                     cardiolipin during exponential growth is due to the 
                     activity of |FRAME: CARDIOLIPSYN-MONOMER ClsA|, while all 
                     three cardiolipin synthases, ClsA, ClsB and |FRAME: 
                     G6551-MONOMER ClsC|, contribute to cardiolipin synthesis in
                     stationary phase |CITS: [22988102]|.  ClsB is able to 
                     catalyze synthesis of phosphatidylglycerol from 
                     phosphatidylethanolamine and glycerol |CITS: [27760827]| 
                     and appears to be involved in the biosynthesis of 
                     6-phosphatidyltrehalose and 6,6'-diphosphatidyltrehalose in
                     certain <i>E. coli</i> strains |CITS: [30804000]|. Cells 
                     with deletions of all three of the genes encoding 
                     cardiolipin synthases, &Delta;<i>clsABC</i>, completely 
                     lack cardiolipin |CITS: [22988102]|.  Upon overexpression 
                     of AtpF (as well as other membrane proteins), formation of 
                     intracellular membranes (ICMs) is observed; the inverted 
                     hexagonal phase of ICMs is absent in a &Delta;<i>clsABC</i>
                     mutant, and thus requires cardiolipin |CITS: [28284722]|.
                     The effect of deletion and overexpression of <i>clsB</i> on
                     lipid class distribution has been measured |CITS: 
                     [29933046]|.  Overexpression of <i>clsB</i> in growth 
                     medium supplemented with glycerol can complement the growth
                     phenotype of a &Delta;<i>pgsA</i> mutant |CITS: 
                     [27760827]|.  Overexpression of <i>clsB</i> in the presence
                     of ethanol or n-butanol leads to production of 
                     phosphatidylethanol or phosphatidylbutanol |CITS: 
                     [29933046]|."
