                     /product="trifunctional ABC exporter membrane subunit YbhR
                     / ABC exporter YbhFSR / cefoperazone ABC exporter"
                     /EC_number="7.6.2.2"
                     /label=ybhR
                     /note="<i>ybhR</i> encodes one of two the integral
                     membrane subunits of a putative ABC exporter.
                     <i>ybhR</i> is part of the <i>cecR-ybhGFSR</i> operon which
                     contains genes encoding a putative ABC exporter 
                     (<i>ybhFSR</i>), a putative membrane fusion protein 
                     (<i>ybhG</i>) and a transcriptional regulator (<i>cecR</i>)
                     |CITS: [16397293][18634750][27112147]|. YbhFSR is 
                     implicated in the efflux of of the third generation 
                     cephalosporin - cefoperazone |CITS: [27112147]|, 
                     tetracycline drugs and the cationic compounds ethidium 
                     bromide and Hoechst33342 |CITS: [32390957]|. YbhFSR may 
                     also function as a Na<sup>+</sup> / (Li<sup>+</sup>):proton
                     antiporter |CITS: [32390957]|. Transcription of 
                     <i>cecR-ybhGFSR</i> is negatively regulated by |FRAME: 
                     EG12406-MONOMER CecR|  |CITS: [27112147]|.
                     In the Transporter Classification Database YbhGFSR is 
                     annotated as a 4-component system within the ATP-binding 
                     Cassette (ABC) superfamily |CITS: [26546518]|. 
                     Overexpression of <i>ybhR</i> from an ASKA plasmid leads to
                     a more than 3-fold increase in the MIC of hypochlorous acid
                     |CITS: [34072091]|."
