     CDS             complement(827924..828406)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ybiA"
                     /locus_tag="b0798"
                     /product="bifunctional N-glycosidase YbiA / 
                     5-amino-6-(D-ribitylamino)uracil glycosidase"
                     /label=ybiA
                     /note="YbiA catalyzes the hydrolysis of the
                     <i>N</i>-glycosidic bond in |FRAME: 
                     DIAMINO-OH-PHOSPHORIBOSYLAMINO-PYR| and |FRAME: CPD-602|, 
                     highly reactive metabolites which are the first two 
                     intermediates in the |FRAME: RIBOSYN2-PWY| pathway |CITS: 
                     [25431972]|.
                     Comparative genomics suggests that the YbiA family of 
                     proteins may play a role in NAD metabolism |CITS: 
                     [22399070]|.
                     Site-directed mutagenesis of conserved residues resulted in
                     reduced or abolished catalytic activity.  A 
                     &Delta;<i>ybiA</i> mutant contains reduced amounts of FAD 
                     and FMN |CITS: [25431972]|.  A <i>ybiA</i> mutant has a 
                     defect in swarming, but not swimming motility |CITS: 
                     [17122336]|."
