     gene            828526..830676
                     /gene="dinG"
                     /locus_tag="b0799"
                     /label=dinG
     CDS             828526..830676
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="dinG"
                     /locus_tag="b0799"
                     /product="bifunctional ATP-dependent DNA helicase DinG / 
                     ATP-dependent 5' -> 3' helicase"
                     /EC_number="5.6.2.3"
                     /label=dinG
                     /note="DinG is a superfamily 2 DNA helicase implicated in
                     DNA repair; DinG may be a structure specific DNA helicase. 
                     Purified DinG has DNA dependent ATPase activity and 
                     ATP-dependent 5' &rarr; 3' DNA helicase activity; the 
                     helicase activity is supported by either ATP or dATP, and 
                     exhibits a requirement for divalent cation that is 
                     satisfied by Mg<sup>2+</sup>, Ca<sup>2+</sup>, or 
                     Mn<sup>2+</sup>, but not by Zn<sup>2+</sup> |CITS: 
                     [12748189]|.
                     DinG is active on D-loops <i>in vitro</i> |CITS: 
                     [17416902]| and on on R-loops (unique DNA/RNA duplexes that
                     form when an RNA transcript binds to DNA behind the site of
                     transcription) <i>in vitro</i> and <i>in vivo</i> |CITS: 
                     [17416902], [19851282]|. Inversion of highly transcribed 
                     rRNA operons renders <i>dinG</i> essential for growth in 
                     rich medium. DinG facilitates progression of replication 
                     forks through inverted rRNA operons |CITS: [19851282]|. 
                     Purified DinG unwinds a variety of DNA G-quadruplex (G4) 
                     structures |CITS: [23935105][37537265]|. A mutation in DinG
                     (<i>E. coli</i> BW25113 &Delta;<i>dinG771::kan</i>) 
                     increases the genetic instability associated with some G4 
                     structures |CITS: [37761860]|.
                     DinG is monomeric |CITS: [12748189]|. DinG contains a 
                     [4Fe-4S] cluster; reduction of the iron-sulfur cluster 
                     reversibly inactivates helicase activity <i>in vitro</i> 
                     |CITS: [19074432]|. DNA bound DinG has a high potential 
                     [4Fe-4S]<sup>3+/2+</sup> cluster (80mV vs. NHE) |CITS: 
                     [24738733]|. The [4Fe-4S] cluster is involved in DNA charge
                     transfer |CITS: [20214403]| - which may be used by DinG to 
                     search for R-loops to repair |CITS: [24738733]|. DinG 
                     preferentially redistributes onto DNA strands where charge 
                     transfer is inhibited by single base mismatches; DinG and 
                     |FRAME: EG10662-MONOMER Endo III| cooperate using 
                     DNA-mediated charge transfer to localise to regions of DNA 
                     damage |CITS: [24738733][28817778]| (and reviewed in |CITS:
                     [31220976]|).
                     |FRAME: CPLX0-8165 SSB| affects the helicase activity of 
                     DinG in a substrate-dependent manner |CITS: 
                     [23036643][40442115]|.
                     The DinG iron-sulfur cluster is reversibly modified by 
                     nitric oxide with concomitant loss of helicase activity 
                     |CITS: [19074432]|.
                     Crystal structures of DinG bound to ssDNA (with and without
                     an ATP analog) are available |CITS: [30520735]|.
                     A &Delta;<i>dinG</i> mutant is viable and somewhat 
                     UV-sensitive, compared to wild type. DinG overproduction 
                     causes some UV sensitivity |CITS: [12748189]|. 
                     Overexpression of <i>dinG</i>, <i>dinI</i>, or <i>lexA</i> 
                     suppresses the cold sensitivity of a <i>dinD</i> mutant 
                     (<i>dinD68</i>) |CITS: [8682790]|.
                     DinG is a superfamily 2 (SF2) helicase (see |CITS: 
                     [20456941]|).
                     Transcription of <i>dinG</i> is induced by nalidixic acid 
                     |CITS: [11544210]| or mitomycin |CITS: [1577702]|. 
                     Transcription is regulated by LexA via an atypical binding 
                     site |CITS: [1577702], [1629168]|."
