     gene            complement(834705..836987)
                     /gene="fiu"
                     /locus_tag="b0805"
                     /label=fiu
     CDS             complement(834705..836987)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="fiu"
                     /locus_tag="b0805"
                     /product="trifunctional ferric catecholate outer membrane 
                     transporter Fiu / ferric catecholate outer membrane 
                     transport complex I / ferric catecholate outer membrane 
                     transporter"
                     /label=fiu
                     /note="Fiu is an integral outer membrane protein which
                     mediates the TonB-dependent import of iron-catecholate 
                     complexes.
                     Early work |CITS: [6353165][3072926][2139424]| 
                     characterized an <i>fiu</i> mutant and identified an 83 kDa
                     protein, produced in large amounts under iron limiting 
                     conditions which mediated the TonB dependent uptake of 
                     dihydroxybenzoylserine-iron complexes and |FRAME: 
                     2-3-DIHYDROXYBENZOATE ""dihydroxybenzoate""| (an 
                     enterobactin precursor) (see also |CITS: 
                     [7793861][10806384]|). The physiological function of Fiu 
                     may be to recapture enterobactin hydrolysis products such 
                     as 2,3-dihydroxybenzoylserine and dihydroxybenzoate |CITS: 
                     [2407721]|. Fiu is able to provide the cell with iron when 
                     it is present as the only outer-membrane iron transporter, 
                     likely through the transport of iron-complexed enterobactin
                     breakdown products although this may not be its 
                     physiological (high-affinity) substrate |CITS: [31712312]|.
                     Fiu binds, but does not transport ferric monocatecholates 
                     such as ferric dihydroxybenzoate| (FeDHBA<sub>3</sub>) and 
                     |FRAME: CPD-17082 ferric dihydroxybenzolyserine| (FeDHBS); 
                     Fiu preferentially transports the ferric dicatecholate 
                     |FRAME: CPD-21612 Fe(DHBS)<sub>2</sub>| |CITS: [38601941]|.
                     Fiu serves as a receptor for microcins E492, M and H47 
                     |CITS: [12949180]|, microcin E492 and its modified form, 
                     the siderophore-peptide microcin E492m |CITS: 
                     [15980406][16718603]|. Fiu is the receptor for |FRAME: 
                     Salmochelins ""salmochelin""| (see |CITS: [19214756]|). Fiu
                     is implicated in uptake of the siderophore cephalosporin, 
                     |FRAME: CPD-28221| |CITS: [29061741]|. The class IIb 
                     microcin MccM targets the TonB-dependent siderophore 
                     receptors Fiu, |FRAME: EG10155-MONOMER CirA|, and |FRAME: 
                     EG10293-MONOMER FepA| |CITS: [39172990]| for entry.
                     Fiu consists of a 22-stranded transmembrane &beta;-barrel 
                     with a number of extended extracellular loops; the protein 
                     contains an internal, gated cavity large enough to 
                     accomodate an iron-complexed catecholate complex; Fiu may 
                     import its substrate via a two-step mechanism which avoids 
                     formation of a membrane-spanning channel |CITS: 
                     [31712312]|.
                     In the Transporter Classification Database |CITS: 
                     [26546518]| Fiu is a member of the Outer Membrane Receptor 
                     (OMR) family. Fiu is evolutionarily distinct from the other
                     TonB dependent catecholate siderophore transporters, Cir 
                     and FepA |CITS: [31712312]|.
                     <i>fiu</i> is a member of the Fur regulon |CITS: 
                     [3323834][1804764]|
                     <i>fiu</i>: <U>f</U>erric <U>i</U>ron <U>u</U>ptake / 
                     <U>f</U>unction <U>i</U>s <U>u</U>nknown |CITS: [6353165]|.
                     Related reviews: |CITS: [17186377][20420522]|"
