                     IEA] [GO_REF 0000044]"
                     /go_process="response to stress [goid 0006950] [evidence
                     IBA] [GO_REF 0000033]"
                     /go_process="colanic acid biosynthetic process [goid
                     0009242] [evidence IMP] [PMID 18309357]"
     gene            837788..838714
                     /gene="rlmF"
                     /locus_tag="b0807"
                     /label=rlmF
     CDS             837788..838714
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rlmF"
                     /locus_tag="b0807"
                     /product="23S rRNA m(6)A1618 methyltransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.1.1.181"
                     /label=rlmF
                     /note="RlmF is the methyltransferase responsible for
                     methylation of 23S rRNA at the N6 position of the A1618 
                     nucleotide |CITS: [18021804]|.
                     <i>In vitro</i>, RlmF can methylate A1618 in LiCl ribosomal
                     core particles (a model for early ribosomal assembly 
                     intermediates), but not in protein-free 23S rRNA or more 
                     fully assembled ribosomal particles |CITS: [18021804]|.
                     RlmF is most similar to several m<sup>2</sup>G 
                     methyltransferases and was thus expected to confer 
                     m<sup>2</sup>G1516 methyltransferase activity |CITS: 
                     [11929612][18021804]|.  Predicted catalytic residues and a 
                     predicted reaction mechanism are discussed |CITS: 
                     [11929612]|.
                     Both an <i>rlmF</i> null mutant and a strain overexpressing
                     <i>rlmF</i> show a growth defect |CITS: [18021804]|.
                     RlmF: ""<b>r</b>RNA <b>l</b>arge subunit 
                     <b>m</b>ethyltransferase <b>F</b>"" |CITS: [18021804]|"
