     CDS             complement(842714..843460)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="glnH"
                     /locus_tag="b0811"
                     /product="trifunctional L-glutamine ABC transporter
                     periplasmic binding protein / L-glutamine ABC transporter /
                     transport of L-glutamine"
                     /EC_number="7.4.2.1"
                     /label=glnH
                     /note="GlnH is the periplasmic binding protein of an
                     L-glutamine ABC transport system.
                     Early studies reported the purification of a glutamine 
                     binding protein released by cold osmotic shock treatment of
                     whole cells of <i>E. coli</i> K12 and K10 derived strains 
                     |CITS: [4927558][4614002]|. <i>glnH</i> encodes a 
                     periplasmic L-glutamine binding protein that is required 
                     for growth on L-glutamine as sole carbon source |CITS: 
                     [3027504]|. Purified GlnH binds L-glutamine with &micro;M 
                     affinity (K<sub>D</sub> = 5 x 10<sup>-7</sup>M) |CITS: 
                     [2693744]|; L-glutamine binding induces conformational 
                     change in the protein |CITS: [2693743]|. Purifed, 
                     crystallized GlnH consists of two globular domains 
                     connected by two peptide linkers (hinges); glutamine binds 
                     in a cleft between the two domains; binding induces large 
                     scale movement of the two hinges and the ligand is 
                     completely buried within the protein |CITS: [8831790]|"
