     gene            complement(844666..845553)
                     /gene="rhtA"
                     /locus_tag="b0813"
                     /label=rhtA
     CDS             complement(844666..845553)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rhtA"
                     /locus_tag="b0813"
                     /product="trifunctional L-threonine/L-homoserine exporter
                     / L-homoserine:H(+) antiporter / L-threonine:H(+) 
                     antiporter"
                     /label=rhtA
                     /note="RhtA can mediate export of L-threonine and
                     L-homoserine and likely operates as a substrate:proton 
                     antiporter; the physiological role of the transporter 
                     remains unclear.
                     Increased expression of <i>rhtA</i> confers increased 
                     resistance to L-homoserine, L-threonine and some other 
                     amino acids (proline, serine, cysteine, histidine) and 
                     amino acid analogues |CITS: [12648727]|. Increased 
                     expression of <i>rhtA</i> increases L-threonine production 
                     in a threonine producing strain and L-homoserine production
                     in an L-homoserine producing strain; addition of the 
                     protonophore |FRAME: CPD-7970| results in a significant 
                     reduction in the rate of export |CITS: [12648727]|. 
                     Heterologous expression of <i>rhtA</i> increases 
                     L-threonine and L-homoserine production in a 
                     <i>Corynebacterium glutamicum</i> threonine producing 
                     strain |CITS: [18594129]|.
                     RhtA is a membrane protein with 10 predicted transmembrane 
                     segments |CITS: [12648727]|
                     RhtA is a member of the 10 TMS Drug/Metabolite Exporter 
                     (DME) family of transporters within the Drug/Metabolite 
                     Transporter (DMT) superfamily |CITS: [26546518]|. 
                     <i>rht</i>: <U>r</U>esistance to <U>h</U>omoserine and 
                     <U>t</U>hreonine |CITS: [10386596]|"
