     gene            845906..846421
                     /gene="ompX"
                     /locus_tag="b0814"
                     /label=ompX
     CDS             845906..846421
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ompX"
                     /locus_tag="b0814"
                     /product="outer membrane protein X"
                     /label=ompX
                     /note="OmpX is a small (18 kDa) outer-membrane protein
                     (OMP). Adhesion of <i>E. coli</i> cells to abiotic surfaces
                     via type1 fimbriae leads to a decreased level of OmpX as 
                     well as a number of other outer membrane proteins |CITS: 
                     [11274103]|.  Deletion of <i>ompX</i> leads to an increase 
                     in cell-surface contact in fimbriated strains of <i>E. 
                     coli</i>, and production of type 1 fimbriae is upregulated.
                     Furthermore, <i>ompX</i> mutants show impaired motility, 
                     increased EPS production, and increased tolerance to SDS 
                     and hydrophobic antibiotics. In nonfimbriated strains, 
                     deletion of <i>ompX</i> led to a decrease in cell surface 
                     contact |CITS: [14679242]|. OmpX has been implicated in the
                     secretion of the extracellular protein |FRAME: 
                     EG11807-MONOMER ""YebF""| |CITS: [22658749]|.
                     Expression of OmpX is affected by medium osmolarity and 
                     pressure; the effect is independent of EnvZ and OmpR |CITS:
                     [7765962]|. Both acidic and basic conditions induce OmpX 
                     expression |CITS: [12107143]|. Overproduction of OmpX 
                     causes an increase in E&sigma;E activity |CITS: [8276244]|.
                     The OmpX protein shows similarity to a family of outer 
                     membrane proteins which are involved in virulence, such as 
                     Ail of <i>Yersinia enterocolitica</i> and Rck and PagC of 
                     <i>Salmonella typhimurium</i>. However, the OmpX protein of
                     <i>E. coli</i> does not appear to play a role in adherence 
                     to mammalian cells |CITS: [7836315]|. Purified OmpX protein
                     binds to human antigen-presenting cells, but does not 
                     activate them |CITS: [12922110]|.
                     A crystal structure of OmpX has been determined at 1.9 
                     &Aring; resolution |CITS: [10022352][10545325]|, and 
                     various solution structures using NMR have been reported 
                     (e.g. |CITS: [14744128], [15037080]|). Targeting of OmpX to
                     the Sec-translocase for transport across the inner membrane
                     is SecB-dependent |CITS:[16352602]|. <i>In vitro</i> 
                     studies have investigated the strategies used by a number 
                     of OMPs, including OmpX, to efficiently fold into the 
                     membrane |CITS: [18641391]|.
                     Expression of <i>ompX</i> is posttranscriptionally 
                     regulated by the small RNA CyaR |CITS: [18978044]|."
