     gene            complement(848181..848520)
                     /gene="rybA"
                     /locus_tag="b4416"
                     /label=rybA
     misc_RNA        complement(848181..848520)
                     /gene="rybA"
                     /locus_tag="b4416"
                     /product="small RNA RybA"
                     /note="The ~205 nt small RNA RybA |CITS: [11445539]| was
                     later found to encode the small protein MntS.  Larger RNA 
                     species can also be detected |CITS: 
                     [11445539][21908668][22336764]|. Manganese toxicity upon 
                     overexpression was shown to be due to MntS rather than RybA
                     |CITS: [25774656]|.
                     RybA expression is upregulated under peroxide stress 
                     conditions but downregulated in long-term stationary phase 
                     |CITS: [22336764][24858919]|. Apparently, the mature 207 nt
                     <i>rybA</i> transcript is stabilized under peroxide stress 
                     |CITS: [22336764]|.
                     RybA appears to regulate expression of genes for aromatic 
                     amino acid biosynthesis. Under peroxide stress, it acts as 
                     a negative regulator for expression of <i>aroL</i> and 
                     <i>aroF</i> by an unknown mechanism that involves TyrR. In 
                     addition, gene expression analysis suggests that RybA acts 
                     as a positive regulator for the CusR regulon |CITS: 
                     [22336764]|.
                     An interaction of Hfq with RybA has not been detected 
                     |CITS: [11445539]|.
                     Reviews: |CITS: [12762038][12654996][11445539]|"
     gene            complement(848325..848453)
                     /gene="mntS"
                     /locus_tag="b4705"
                     /label=mntS
     CDS             complement(848325..848453)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="mntS"
                     /locus_tag="b4705"
                     /product="small protein MntS"
                     /label=mntS
                     /note="MntS is a small protein that affects the
                     availability of Mn<sup>2+</sup> within the cell |CITS: 
                     [21908668][25774656]|.  Synthesis of MntS increases the 
                     total intracellular levels of Mn<sup>2+</sup>, likely by 
                     directly or indirectly inhibiting manganese export through 
                     |FRAME: G6999-MONOMER MntP|.  Under 
                     Mn<sup>2+</sup>-limiting conditions, MntS confers 
                     resistance to hydrogen peroxide by facilitating delivery of
                     Mn<sup>2+</sup> to Mn<sup>2+</sup>-dependent enzymes |CITS:
                     [25774656]|.
                     Expression of <i>mntS</i> is high during exponential growth
                     in minimal media and is repressed by MntR in response to 
                     Mn<sup>2+</sup> |CITS: [21908668]|. Overproduction of MntS 
                     in the presence of high levels of Mn<sup>2+</sup> is 
                     detrimental |CITS: [21908668][25774656]| by causing iron 
                     limitation, which leads to failure of |FRAME: 
                     PROTOHEME-FERROCHELAT-MONOMER| activity |CITS: [25774656]|.
                     The mRNA encoding MntS is also known as the ~205 nt small 
                     RNA RybA |CITS: [11445539]|.  Larger RNA species can also 
                     be detected |CITS: [11445539][21908668][22336764]|. 
                     Manganese toxicity upon overexpression was shown to be due 
                     to MntS rather than the small RNA RybA |CITS: [25774656]|. 
                     Under peroxide stress conditions, <i>rybA</i> is 
                     upregulated.  Apparently, the mature 207 nt <i>rybA</i> 
                     transcript is stabilized under peroxide stress |CITS: 
                     [22336764]|.
                     "
