     gene            870791..872119
                     /gene="dgcI"
                     /locus_tag="b0834"
                     /label=dgcI
     CDS             870791..872119
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="dgcI"
                     /locus_tag="b0834"
                     /product="putative diguanylate cyclase DgcI"
                     /label=dgcI
                     /note="DgcI belongs to the core set of eight GGDEF/EAL
                     domain proteins that is absolutely conserved in a set of 61
                     <i>E. coli</i> genomes containing pathogenic, commensal and
                     probiotic strains |CITS: [26303830]|.
                     DgcI is an inner membrane protein with two predicted 
                     transmembrane domains; the C terminus is located in the 
                     cytoplasm |CITS: [15919996]|. DgcI is predicted to be a 
                     bitopic inner membrane protein |CITS: [27510400]|. DgcI 
                     contains an N-terminal GAPES (<u>ga</u>mma-proteobacterial 
                     <u>pe</u>riplasmic <u>s</u>ensory) domain |CITS: 
                     [26148715]|.
                     In a random transposon mutagenesis study, DgcI was found to
                     be required for growth under optimum growth conditions 
                     (rich medium at 37&deg;C), but not under cold conditions 
                     (15&deg;C) or in minimal medium |CITS: [15380559]|.  A 
                     <i>dgcI</i> mutant was found to be a weak suppressor of the
                     synthetic lethal phenotype of a <i>pta recBC</i>(TS) strain
                     |CITS: [15687190]|.
                     Expression of <i>dgcI</i> is downregulated by CsrA |CITS: 
                     [18713317]|.
                     DgcI: ""<b>d</b>i<b>g</b>uanylate <b>c</b>yclase <b>I</b>""
                     |CITS: [26148715]|
                     Review: |CITS: [33640237]|."
