                     [evidence IEP] [PMID 16597943]"
     gene            874198..875313
                     /gene="yliI"
                     /locus_tag="b0837"
                     /label=yliI
     CDS             874198..875313
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yliI"
                     /locus_tag="b0837"
                     /product="bifunctional aldose sugar dehydrogenase YliI /
                     aldose sugar dehydrogenase"
                     /label=yliI
                     /note="YliI is an aldose sugar dehydrogenase that requires
                     the cofactor pyrroloquinoline quinone (PQQ) for activity 
                     |CITS: [16864586]|. <i>E. coli</i> lacks the ability to 
                     synthesize PQQ |CITS: [HOMMES84][9353919]| however, it 
                     exhibits chemotaxis towards environmental PQQ |CITS: 
                     [8576064]|, and may thus use an externally supplied 
                     cofactor |CITS: [16864586]|. PQQ is transported across the 
                     outer membrane by the TonB-dependent transporter |FRAME: 
                     G6762-MONOMER PqqU| |CITS: [36054785]|. The physiological 
                     substrate of YliI is unknown |CITS: [16864586]|.
                     YliI localizes to the the periplasm |CITS: [16864586]| and 
                     is associated with the outer membrane under certain 
                     physiological conditions |CITS: [16522795]|. Sequence 
                     similarity suggests that YliI may contain &beta;-barrel 
                     structures |CITS: [12192075]|; however, the 
                     &beta;-propeller fold of YliI may have led to a 
                     false-positive prediction of a &beta;-barrel structure (von
                     Heijne, pers. comm., 8/8/2006).
                     The crystal structure of YliI has been determined at 1.5 
                     &Aring; resolution |CITS: [16864586]|."
