     gene            complement(878248..878844)
                     /gene="ybjG"
                     /locus_tag="b0841"
                     /label=ybjG
     CDS             complement(878248..878844)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ybjG"
                     /locus_tag="b0841"
                     /product="undecaprenyl pyrophosphate phosphatase"
                     /EC_number="3.6.1.27"
                     /label=ybjG
                     /note="YbjG is similar to the |FRAME: bacitracin|
                     resistance protein BcrC of <i>Bacillus licheniformis</i>. 
                     Disruption of <i>ybjG</i> causes increased bacitracin 
                     sensitivity, and overexpression causes increased resistance
                     to bacitracin |CITS: [10498733][15778224]|. Simultaneous 
                     inactivation of <i>ybjG</i>, |FRAME: EG11665 <i>bacA</i>|, 
                     and |FRAME: EG10705 <i>pgpB</i>| is lethal. Depletion of 
                     BacA in the triple mutant strain causes changes in cell 
                     morphology and lysis. Overexpression of <i>ybjG</i>, 
                     |FRAME: G7146 <i>lpxT</i>|, <i>bacA</i>, or <i>pgpB</i> 
                     leads to increased undecaprenyl diphosphate 
                     (C<sub>55</sub>PP) phosphatase activity in crude membrane 
                     extracts. Expression of C<sub>55</sub>PP phosphatase 
                     activity from one of the three genes <i>ybjG</i>, 
                     <i>bacA</i>, and <i>pgpB</i> appears to be sufficient for 
                     synthesis of undecaprenyl phosphate and survival |CITS: 
                     [15778224]|. <i>bacA ybjG</i> double and <i>bacA ybjG 
                     lpxT</i> triple deletion mutants are hypersensitive to the 
                     undecaprenyl phosphate biosynthesis inhibitor fosmidomycin 
                     |CITS: [17660416]|.
                     YbjG is an inner membrane protein with four transmembrane 
                     domains |CITS: [17660416]|. The C terminus is located in 
                     the cytoplasm |CITS: [15919996][17660416]|. The acid 
                     phosphatase domain of YbjG is located on the periplasmic 
                     side of the plasma membrane |CITS: [17660416]|. <i>ybjG</i>
                     expression is increased in the constitutively active 
                     <i>evgS1</i> mutant and may be directly regulated by PhoP 
                     |CITS: [15126461]|. <i>ybjG</i> is one of a number of genes
                     that are specifcally induced when cells are exposed to the 
                     antimicrobial lactoperoxidase-thiocyanate system |CITS: 
                     [15748988]|. Expression of <i>ybjG</i> displayed 
                     significantly increased variability across populations 
                     adapted to different toxins |CITS: [28217741]|. 
                     Transcription of <i>ybjG</i> (and <i>pgpB</i>) increases 
                     when C<sub>55</sub>PP dephosphorylation activity in cells 
                     is experimentally reduced |CITS: [40509967]|."
