                     /label=ybjI
     CDS             complement(880772..881587)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ybjI"
                     /locus_tag="b0844"
                     /product="bifunctional
                     5-amino-6-(5-phospho-D-ribitylamino)uracil phosphatase / 
                     FMN phosphatase"
                     /EC_number="3.1.3.104; 3.1.3.102"
                     /label=ybjI
                     /note="The identity of the enzyme(s) catalyzing the 
                     dephosphorylation of |FRAME: CPD-1086| in the riboflavin 
                     biosynthesis pathway was long unknown |CITS: 
                     [416855][colisalII]|.  |CITS: [24123841]| have now shown 
                     that at least two enzymes, YbjI and YigB, can catalyze this
                     reaction.
                     YbjI was initially identified as an FMN phosphatase 
                     belonging to the superfamily of haloacid dehalogenase 
                     (HAD)-like hydrolases.  In addition, YbjI has some 
                     phosphatase activity against pyridoxal phosphate |CITS: 
                     [16990279]|.  The phosphatase activity of YbjI was first 
                     discovered in a high-throughput screen of purified proteins
                     |CITS: [15808744]|.
                     Deletion of <i>ybjI</i> alone does not result in riboflavin
                     auxotrophy |CITS: [16738554]|."
