     gene            complement(883435..883513)
                     /gene="rybB"
                     /locus_tag="b4417"
                     /label=rybB
     misc_RNA        complement(883435..883513)
                     /gene="rybB"
                     /locus_tag="b4417"
                     /product="small regulatory RNA RybB"
                     /note="RybB is a small regulatory RNA whose expression
                     increases in stationary phase, when its half life is 8 
                     minutes |CITS: [11445539][14602901]|.  RybB expression is 
                     dependent on the alternative sigma factor 
                     &sigma;<sup>E</sup>, which is activated by cell envelope 
                     stress |CITS: [17007876][17416652]|.  Indirect repression 
                     of &sigma;<sup>E</sup> synthesis by RybB creates an 
                     autoregulatory loop |CITS: [17416652]|.
                     An efficient interaction between RybB RNA and Hfq protein 
                     has been detected |CITS: [11445539]|, and the specific 
                     contacts between RybB and Hfq have been probed using 
                     <i>Salmonella</i> components |CITS: [22645344]|.  RybB also
                     interacts with the RNA chaperone ProQ.  The RbsZ RNA was 
                     discovered in an RNA-RNA interactome screen, where 
                     RybB-RbsZ was the most abundant pair found on ProQ.  RbsZ 
                     appears to act as a sponge that lowers the leves of RybB, 
                     while ProQ protects RybB against downregulation/degradation
                     by Hfq and RNase III |CITS: [31761494]|.
                     A number of regulatory targets of RybB were identified 
                     |CITS: [21768388]|.  Prediction of regulatory targets of 
                     RybB can be improved by considering accessible regions in 
                     both the sRNA and its target |CITS: [22767260]|; 
                     comparative genomics was subsequently used to predict 
                     regulatory targets |CITS: [23980183]|.  A candidate RybB 
                     regulon was inferred by integrating information on 
                     experimentally supported targets and sRNA-mRNA interactions
                     with transcription datasets |CITS: [32487739]|.  New 
                     targets were identified by an affinity purification method 
                     |CITS: [25891076]|.  This method also identified direct 
                     interactions of RybB with the 3' external transcribed 
                     spacer (ETS) sequence of a tRNA-encoding operon, |FRAME: 
                     TU00512|.  In this context, the 3'ETS<sup><i>leuZ</i></sup>
                     is thought to function as a sponge that absorbs 
                     transcriptional noise while RybB expression is not induced 
                     |CITS: [25891076]|.
                     Translation of WaaR may be downregulated by RybB |CITS: 
                     [22021036]|.  Overexpression of <i>rybB</i> causes 
                     increased expression of <i>rpoS</i> in minimal media |CITS:
                     [11445539]| and decreased levels of <i>ompC</i>, 
                     <i>ompW</i> |CITS: [17007876]|, <i>rpoE</i>, and 
                     <i>rybB</i> itself |CITS: [17416652]|.  Overexpression of 
                     either MicA or RybB rescues the growth and viability 
                     phenotypes of &sigma;<sup>E</sup> depletion |CITS: 
                     [21768388]| and also leads to increased cell lysis in 
                     stationary phase |CITS: [22251246]|.  Overexpression of 
                     RybB decreases biofilm formation and expression of type I 
                     fimbriae |CITS: [26469694]|.  A <i>rybB</i> deletion mutant
                     is less sensitive to cell envelope stress than wild type 
                     |CITS: [19734312]|, appears unable to establish long-term 
                     stationary phase |CITS: [23594456]|, and shows increased 
                     frequency of persister cell waking |CITS: [31608580]|.
                     Expression of <i>rybB</i> is induced in complex medium at 
                     stationary phase |CITS: [11445539][14602901]|.  RybB 
                     accumulates in the absence of |FRAME: CPLX0-3521| |CITS: 
                     [18203924]|.  Proper regulation of <i>rybB</i> expression 
                     by &sigma;<sup>E</sup> is critical |CITS: [28373273]|.
                     The transcripts of many RybB targets are decreased after 
                     &sigma;<sup>E</sup> induction as expected  |CITS: 
                     [31992590]|.  The |FRAME: RNA0-413| acts as a sponge for 
                     RybB |CITS: [33460557]|.
                     Reviews: |CITS: [12654996][15487940][17055775][19366629][2 
                     0068355][25916829][26618164][29992897][32213244]|"
