     gene            888413..888889
                     /gene="ybjN"
                     /locus_tag="b0853"
                     /label=ybjN
     CDS             888413..888889
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ybjN"
                     /locus_tag="b0853"
                     /product="protein YbjN"
                     /label=ybjN
                     /note="Both overexpression and mutation of YbjN has
                     pleiotropic effects in the cell involving the production of
                     flagella and fimbriae and acid resistance |CITS: 
                     [21980417]|.  Using a ""fuzzy functional form"" alignment 
                     mechanism, YbjN was predicted to have thiol-disulfide 
                     oxidoreductase activity |CITS: [9743619]|.
                     It was initially found that overexpression of YbjN 
                     suppresses the temperature-sensitive growth defect of 
                     several <i>coaA</i> alleles as well as the <i>ilu-1</i> 
                     allele |CITS: [16701556]|.  The authors hypothesized that 
                     YbjN functions to generally stabilize unstable proteins 
                     |CITS: [16701556]|.
                     Overexpression of <i>ybjN</i> leads to a growth defect in 
                     liquid media, decreased expression of fimbriae, decreased 
                     acid resistance, and induction of many stress response 
                     genes.  A <i>ybjN</i> mutant has increased flagellar 
                     motility and appears to overproduce colanic acid, leading 
                     to a mucoid appearance |CITS: [21980417]|.  <i>ybjN</i> 
                     insertion mutants were identified in a genetic screen for 
                     genes that are important for survival of exposure to 
                     ionizing radiation (IR).  A <i>ybjN</i> deletion mutant has
                     a modest decrease in IR survival |CITS: [25049088]|. 
                     Expression of <i>ybjN</i> is growth stage- and 
                     temperature-dependent |CITS: [21980417]|."
                     /translation="MTSLVVPGLDTLRQWLDDLGMSFFECDNCQALHLPHMQNFDGVFD
