     gene            889240..890352
                     /gene="potF"
                     /locus_tag="b0854"
                     /label=potF
     CDS             889240..890352
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="potF"
                     /locus_tag="b0854"
                     /product="trifunctional putrescine ABC transporter
                     periplasmic binding protein / putrescine ABC transporter / 
                     transport of putresince"
                     /EC_number="7.6.2.11"
                     /label=potF
                     /note="PotF is the periplasmic, putrescine binding protein
                     of an ATP-dependent putrescine uptake system.
                     PotF binds putrescine in a 1:1 ratio; PotF has 35% sequence
                     similarity with |FRAME: POTD-MONOMER PotD| - the spermidine
                     preferential binding protein of the PotABCD polyamine 
                     uptake system |CITS: [8416922]|. PotF binds its endogenous 
                     ligand, putrescine, with high affinity |CITS: [9651355]| 
                     (K<sub>d</sub>=4.8 nM |CITS: [23792166]|; K<sub>d</sub>=68 
                     nM |CITS: [33406388]|). Purified PotF also binds |FRAME: 
                     CADAVERINE| (K<sub>d</sub>=68 nM |CITS: [33406388]|) and 
                     |FRAME: AGMATHINE| (K<sub>d</sub>=0.22 &micro;M |CITS: 
                     [33406388]|), and with less affinity, |FRAME: SPERMIDINE| 
                     and |FRAME: SPERMINE| |CITS: [33406388]|).
                     In the crystal structure reported by |CITS: [9651355]| PotF
                     consists of two globular domains and three interdomain 
                     linker segments; the two domains are divided by a deep 
                     cleft which contains the substrate binding site; bound 
                     putrescine is completely enclosed within the cleft and is 
                     held in place through multiple direct and indirect 
                     (water-mediated) interactions with PotF residues. 
                     Structures of apo-PotF in open and closed conformation and 
                     in complex with various polyamine ligands are also 
                     available |CITS: [33406388]|.
                     Deletion of <i>potF</i> impairs pili-dependent surface 
                     motility (PDSM) in <i>E. coli</i> strain W3110 |CITS: 
                     [40178519]|. The antibiotic plantaricin BM-1 effects were 
                     enhanced in a &Delta;<i>potF</i> mutant, disrupting the 
                     cell membrane, decreasing the biofilm formation, and up- 
                     and down-regulating several hundred proteins, many of which
                     were biofilm-related proteins, such as |FRAME: PD02198|, 
                     |FRAME: RCSC-MONOMER|, |FRAME: EG11355-MONOMER| and |FRAME:
                     G369-MONOMER| |CITS: [40106189]|."
