     gene            complement(907618..909270)
                     /gene="hcp"
                     /locus_tag="b0873"
                     /label=hcp
     CDS             complement(907618..909270)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="hcp"
                     /locus_tag="b0873"
                     /product="bifunctional protein S-nitrosylase /
                     hydroxylamine reductase"
                     /EC_number="1.7.99.1"
                     /label=hcp
                     /note="The hybrid cluster protein (HCP) is a high-affinity
                     NO reductase that is responsible for the majority of NO 
                     detoxification at low concentrations of NO |CITS: 
                     [26879449]|.
                     HCP exhibits hydroxylamine reductase activity, possibly 
                     functioning as a scavenger of toxic by-products of nitrogen
                     metabolism |CITS: [12374823]|.  HCP was originally 
                     suggested to be involved in nitrate-and/or nitrite 
                     respiration based on its regulation |CITS: [10651802]|.
                     HCP contains iron-sulfur clusters of the [2Fe-2S] and 
                     [4Fe-2S-2O] type |CITS: [10381368][10651802]| and is 
                     reduced by the Hcr NADH oxidoreductase |CITS: [10651802]|. 
                     The properties of electron transfer in the Hcr-HCP system 
                     have been studied |CITS: [10651802]|.
                     Growth of an <i>hcp hcr</i> mutant in a strain background 
                     that lacks known NO reductases and nitrite reductases (i.e.
                     &Delta;<i>nirBD, nrfAB, norVW</i>) is inhibited in the 
                     presence of nitrate or nitrite |CITS: [26879449]|.
                     HCP is produced during anaerobic growth in the presence of 
                     nitrate or nitrite |CITS: [10651802]|.  Expression is 
                     induced by NarL, NarP, OxyR and FNR |CITS: 
                     [15667305][16928682][17449618]| and repressed by |FRAME: 
                     EG11212-MONOMER NsrR| |CITS: [17449618]|.  Expression of 
                     <i>hcp</i> is also upregulated by 
                     <i>S</i>-nitrosoglutathione, a nitrosating agent |CITS: 
                     [15647275]|, and by hydrogen peroxide |CITS: [16928682]|. 
                     Hcp: ""<b>h</b>ybrid-<b>c</b>luster <b>p</b>rotein"" 
                     Reviews: |CITS: [9667933][22029434]|"
