     gene            complement(909414..910313)
                     /gene="lysO"
                     /locus_tag="b0874"
                     /label=lysO
     CDS             complement(909414..910313)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="lysO"
                     /locus_tag="b0874"
                     /product="trifunctional L-lysine/thialysine exporter /
                     L-lysine exporter / thialysine exporter"
                     /label=lysO
                     /note="LysO is an L-lysine/thialysine efflux transporter.
                     A <i>&Delta;lysO</i> strain has an increased intracellular 
                     concentration of L-lysine and impaired growth in the 
                     presence of the dipeptide Lys-Ala (but not in the presence 
                     of Arg-Ala); a <i>&Delta;lysO</i> strain is sensitive to 
                     the naturally occurring lysine antimetabolite, thialysine 
                     |CITS: [25845847]|. LysO may export thialysine with higher 
                     affinity than L-lysine; LysO exports thialysine via 
                     proton-coupled antiport |CITS: [34487760]|.
                     Overexpression of <i>lysO</i> from a plasmid mediates 
                     increased export of L-lysine in Lys-Ala containing medium 
                     and mediates increased resistance to thialysine; 
                     overexpression of <i>lysO</i> from a plasmid suppresses the
                     canavanine supersensitive phenotype of a strain lacking the
                     arginine efflux transporter, ArgO possibly because 
                     increased extracellular lysine inhibits canavanine uptake 
                     by the |FRAME: ABC-3-CPLX| |CITS: [25845847]|.
                     The <i>cis</i>-regulatory region of <i>lysO</i> contains an
                     imperfect ArgR binding site; arginine mediates 
                     transcriptional repression of <i>lysO</i> via the ArgR 
                     repressor however this effect may only be evident when the 
                     cytoplasmic level of arginine is high |CITS: [25845847]|. 
                     LysO contains 8 transmembrane regions and adopts an 
                     N<sub>out</sub>-C<sub>out</sub> configuration in the 
                     cytoplasmic membrane |CITS: [25845847][34487760]|. Enhanced
                     expression of <i>lysO</i> (formerly <i>ybjE</i>) results in
                     accumulation of specific L-amino acids in the culture 
                     medium of <i>E. coli</i> strains that are capable of 
                     producing L-amino acids (US patent number 8383363). 
                     <i>lysO</i>: <U>lys</U>ine <U>o</U>utward permease"
