     CDS             936415..938859
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="dmsA"
                     /locus_tag="b0894"
                     /product="bifunctional dimethyl sulfoxide reductase
                     subunit A / dimethyl sulfoxide reductase"
                     /EC_number="1.8.5.3"
                     /label=dmsA
                     /note="The DmsA subunit of DMSO reductase contains a 
                     molybdo-bis(pyranopterin guanine dinucleotide) (Mo-bisPGD) 
                     cofactor and a [4Fe-4S] cluster (known as FS0) |CITS: 
                     [21357619]|.
                     DmsA contains a twin-arginine leader peptide which targets 
                     the protein to the membrane, although DmsA does not
                     appear to be exported to the periplasm. The leader peptide 
                     is also essential for expression of DmsA and stability of 
                     the DmsAB dimer, and is cleaved between residues 45 and 46 
                     |CITS: [3062312][10801884]|. The leader peptide interacts 
                     with the redox enzyme maturation protein (REMP) |FRAME: 
                     G6849-MONOMER ""DmsD""| |CITS: 
                     [11309116][18247574][24093457]|.
                     "
