                     /label=ycaC
     CDS             complement(940387..941013)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ycaC"
                     /locus_tag="b0897"
                     /product="putative hydrolase YcaC"
                     /label=ycaC
                     /note="The crystal structure of YcaC, solved at 1.8
                     &Aring; resolution, indicates that YcaC has similarity to 
                     hydrolases and forms a homooctamer (a dimer of tetrameric 
                     ring structures) |CITS: [9782055]|.  The protein shows 
                     structural similarity to the pyrazinamidase encoded by the 
                     <i>Pyrococcus horikoshii</i> 999 gene |CITS: [11714269]|. 
                     Cys118 is identified as a likely catalytic residue |CITS: 
                     [9782055]|.
                     A &Delta;<i>ycaC</i> mutant shows increased resistance to 
                     the proline-rich antimicrobial peptide (PrAMP) apidaecin 1b
                     and the designer peptide Api88 |CITS: [27405093]|."
