     gene            complement(944116..945024)
                     /gene="ycaN"
                     /locus_tag="b0900"
                     /label=ycaN
     CDS             complement(944116..945024)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ycaN"
                     /locus_tag="b0900"
                     /product="putative DNA-binding transcriptional regulator
                     YcaN"
                     /label=ycaN
                     /note="YcaN was predicted to be a LysR-type transcription
                     factor |CITS: [34428301] [35880217]|, it contains a 
                     helix-turn-helix motif to bind DNA in its N-terminal domain
                     |CITS: [35880217]|, and it is probably involved in 
                     regulation of threonine and formate utilization 
                     |CITS:[35508583]|.  YcaN DNA-binding activity was probed 
                     <i>in vivo</i> in glucose M9 minimal medium by the 
                     chromatin immunoprecipitation method combined with lambda 
                     exonuclease digestion |CITS: [34428301]|. However, the 
                     effect of YcaN on the transcription of any gene has not yet
                     been demonstrated |CITS: [34428301]|.
                     YcaN was found transcriptionally upregulated in the 
                     presence of threonine (Thr) in M9 medium |CITS:[35508583]|.
                     The transcriptional response for the deletion of YcaN has 
                     been characterized by RNA-seq in M9 minimal medium 
                     supplemented with 7 mM l-threonine |CITS:[35508583]|. In 
                     the YbdH knockout strain, the adjacent genes <i>ycaD</i> 
                     and <i>focA</i> were upregulated while the <i>ycaC</i> gene
                     was downregulated; however, binding was not found under the
                     growth conditions used in ChiP-exo studies. Additionally, 
                     in the YcaN knockout strain, various genes involved in 
                     amino acid transport and metabolism were strongly 
                     downregulated |CITS:[35508583]|; moreover, the strain was 
                     unable to grow in minimal medium with formate 
                     |CITS:[35508583]|. It was proposed that YcaN is probably 
                     involved in formate utilization mediated by repression of 
                     the <i>focA</i> gene |CITS:[35508583]|.
                     The transcription of the <i>ycaN</i> gene is affected by 
                     Fe<sup>2+</sup> |CITS: [35880217]|.
                     "
