                     /label=ycaO
     CDS             complement(950328..952088)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ycaO"
                     /locus_tag="b0905"
                     /product="bifunctional ribosomal protein S12
                     methylthiotransferase accessory factor YcaO / ATP 
                     pyrophosphatase"
                     /EC_number="3.6.1.8"
                     /label=ycaO
                     /note="The YcaO protein is involved in the 
                     &beta;-methylthiolation of |FRAME: EG10911-MONOMER|.  YcaO 
                     interacts directly with a ribonucleoprotein complex 
                     containing S12 |CITS: [21169565]|.  The molecular function 
                     of <i>E. coli</i> YcaO is unknown; however, the YcaO domain
                     and its ATP binding motif define the YcaO superfamily which
                     includes proteins that catalyze cyclodehydration, amidation
                     and thioamidation reactions |CITS: [28256131]|.
                     Crystal structures of apo- and nucleotide-bound YcaO have 
                     been solved, showing a circularly symmetric homodimer.
                     The protein consists of an N-terminal domain with a broadly
                     conserved and previously unknown ATP-binding fold and a 
                     C-terminal dimerization domain.  The purified protein 
                     hydrolyzes ATP to AMP and pyrophosphate <i>in vitro</i> 
                     |CITS: [25129028]|.
                     A <i>ycaO</i> deletion mutant contains significantly 
                     reduced levels of &beta;-methylthiolated ribosomal protein 
                     S12 and has an altered transcriptional profile similar to 
                     that of a <i>rimO</i> deletion mutant |CITS: [21169565]|. 
                     Review: |CITS: [28256131]|
                     "
