     gene            964845..966077
                     /gene="ycaQ"
                     /locus_tag="b0916"
                     /label=ycaQ
     CDS             964845..966077
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ycaQ"
                     /locus_tag="b0916"
                     /product="trifunctional interstrand DNA crosslink repair 
                     glycosylase / NM5-interstrand DNA crosslink repair 
                     glycosylase / DNA-N(7)-methyguanine glycosylase"
                     /label=ycaQ
                     /note="YcaQ is an alkylpurine DNA glycosylase which acts
                     on interstrand cross-links (ICLs) formed by alkylation at 
                     purine N<sup>3</sup> or N<sup>7</sup> positions. YcaQ can 
                     unhook chemically diverse ICLs, such as those produced by 
                     the <i>Streptomyces</i> secondary metabolite, |FRAME: 
                     CPD-16517| (|FRAME: CPD-23532 ""AZB-ICLs""|), and from 
                     nitrogen mustard compounds such as |FRAME: CPD-23531| 
                     (|FRAME: A-NM5-ICL ""NM-ICLs""|), <i>in vitro</i>. YcaQ can
                     act on either side of the cross-link and can generate 
                     opposing AP (apurinic) sites which can be incised by 
                     |FRAME: EG10651-MONOMER| <i>in vitro</i> although the <i>in
                     vivo</i> mechanism of downstream repair remains unknown 
                     |CITS: [32409837]|.
                     YcaQ activity provides an alternative to |FRAME: 
                     UVRABC-CPLX ""UvrABC""|-mediated ICL repair |CITS: 
                     [32409837]|.
                     Purified YcaQ also acts on monoadducts and can cleave 
                     N<sup>7</sup>-methylguanine lesions in DNA |CITS: 
                     [32409837]|.
                     <i>ycaQ</i> expression is not induced by exposure to 
                     mechloroethamine or MMS |CITS: [32409837]|.
                     "
