     CDS             966308..967054
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="kdsB"
                     /locus_tag="b0918"
                     /product="3-deoxy-manno-octulosonate cytidylyltransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.7.7.38"
                     /label=kdsB
                     /note="CMP-KDO synthetase activates the 8-carbon sugar KDO
                     for incorporation into lipopolysaccharide.
                     The &beta;-pyranose form of KDO is the preferred substrate 
                     of CMP-KDO synthetase |CITS: [2997221]|.  A nucleophilic 
                     displacement mechanism was proposed for the enzyme |CITS: 
                     [3031027]|.  Based on kinetic, modelling and EPR studies 
                     and the crystal structure of the ternary complex, a 
                     reaction mechanism involving two Mg<sup>2+</sup> ions was 
                     proposed |CITS: [19815542]|.
                     A crystal structure of the enzyme has been solved at 2.6 
                     &Aring; resolution |CITS: [16021622]|; the structure of the
                     ternary complex of KdsB with CTP and 2&beta;-deoxy KDO was 
                     solved at 1.9 &Aring; resolution |CITS: [19815542]|. 
                     Expression of <i>kdsB</i> is growth regulated: it is 
                     highest in early log phase and decreases in stationary 
                     phase |CITS: [7543480]|.  <i>kdsB</i> is an essential gene 
                     |CITS: [16738554]|."
