                     /locus_tag="b0926"
                     /label=mepK
     CDS             978531..979079
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="mepK"
                     /locus_tag="b0926"
                     /product="peptidoglycan L,D-endopeptidase"
                     /label=mepK
                     /note="MepK is an L,D-endopeptidase which cleaves the 
                     cross-bridges between <i>meso</i>-diaminopimelic acid 
                     residues (mDAP-mDAP or 3&rarr;3 cross-links) in 
                     peptidoglycan.
                     Peptidoglycan isolated from a &Delta;<i>mepK</i> strain 
                     contains an increased percentage of soluble muropeptides 
                     containing mDAP-mDAP linkages compared to wild type; 
                     purified MepK cleaves 'tri-tetra' muropeptides (ie. 
                     peptidoglycan dimers containing an 
                     mDAP<sup>3</sup>-mDAP<sup>3</sup> crosslink) to produce 
                     tripeptide and tetrapeptide disaccharides |CITS: 
                     [30940749]|. MepK activity contributes to peptidoglycan 
                     expansion during bacterial growth; &Delta;<i>mepK</i> 
                     strains show decreased peptidoglycan synthesis (assayed by 
                     measuring the incorporation of labeled m-DAP) compared to 
                     wild type; additional deletion of either of the 
                     D,D-endopeptidases, |FRAME: G7147-MONOMER ""MepS""| or 
                     |FRAME: EG10013-MONOMER ""MepM""|, results in a further 
                     decrease in peptidoglycan synthesis, indicating that the 
                     combined activity of these enzymes is required for optimal 
                     peptidoglycan expansion |CITS: [30940749]|. The MepK and 
                     MepM endopeptidases are minimally required for bacterial 
                     growth in strains engineered to produce |FRAME: 
                     EG11253-MONOMER LdtD|-mediated 3&rarr;3 cross-linked 
                     peptidoglycan |CITS: [34382698]|.
                     The composition of peptidoglycan isolated from a strain 
                     lacking both MepK and |FRAME: CPLX0-3201 ""MepA""| is not 
                     significantly different to that isolated from a strain 
                     lacking only MepK; MepK appears to be the only enzyme 
                     cleaving mDAP-mDAP crosslinks under normal laboratory 
                     conditions |CITS: [30940749]|.
                     In the peptidase database MEROPS, MepK is a member of the 
                     M15 family of metallopeptidases |CITS: [29145643]|."
