                     /gene="ssuC"
                     /locus_tag="b0934"
                     /product="bifunctional aliphatic sulfonate ABC transporter
                     membrane subunit / aliphatic sulfonate ABC transporter"
                     /EC_number="7.6.2.14"
                     /label=ssuC
                     /note="SsuC is the predicted integral membrane component
                     of an ATP-dependent aliphatic sulfonate uptake system 
                     |CITS:[10506196]|. A <i>&Delta;ssuBC</i> strain is unable 
                     to grow using a range of aliphatic sulfonates as sulfur 
                     source including ethanesulfonate, hexanesulfonate, 
                     octanesulfonate, decanesulfonate, sulfoacetate, 
                     4-phenyl-1-butanesulfonate, N-phenyltaurine, MOPS and HEPES
                     and growth is significantly reduced with propanesulfonate, 
                     pentanesulfonate, 2-(4-pyridyl)ethanesulfonate or PIPES as 
                     sulfur source. Wild type growth is restored when 
                     <i>ssuB</i> and <i>ssuC</i> are expressed from a plasmid 
                     |CITS: [10781534]|.
                     SsuC is predicted to be an inner membrane protein with 6-7 
                     transmembrane domains; topology analysis suggests the N and
                     C termini are located in the cytoplasm |CITS: [11867724]|."
