                     /product="bifunctional aliphatic sulfonate ABC transporter 
                     periplasmic binding protein / aliphatic sulfonate ABC 
                     transporter"
                     /EC_number="7.6.2.14"
                     /label=ssuA
                     /note="SsuA is the predicted substrate-binding protein of
                     an ATP-dependent aliphatic sulfonate uptake system 
                     |CITS:[10506196]|. A <i>&Delta;ssuA</i> strain is unable to
                     grow using a range of aliphatic sulfonates as sulfur source
                     including ethanesulfonate, hexanesulfonate, 
                     octanesulfonate, decanesulfonate, sulfoacetate, 
                     N-phenyltaurine, 4-phenyl-1-butansulfonate, MOPS and HEPES 
                     and has significantly reduced growth with propanesulfonate,
                     pentanesulfonate, 2-(4-pyridyl)ethanesulfonate or PIPES as 
                     sulfur source. Wild type growth is restored when 
                     <i>ssuA</i> is expressed from a plasmid |CITS: 
                     [10781534]|."
