     CDS             993324..993863
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="elfA"
                     /locus_tag="b0938"
                     /product="putative laminin-binding fimbrial subunit"
                     /label=elfA
                     /note="<i>ycbQRSTUVF</i> is a putative chaperone-usher
                     fimbrial operon in <i>E.coli K-12</i> |CITS: [20345943]|. 
                     The operon is cryptic under normal laboratory conditions 
                     but when constitutive expression is induced in a strain 
                     that lacks the type 1 fimbrial complex the <i>ycb</i> 
                     operon promotes biofilm formation in minimal media on a 
                     variety of abiotic surfaces and produces numerous surface 
                     fimbrial structures that can be observed microscopically 
                     |CITS: [20345943]|. Extraction and purification of these 
                     fimbriae revealed the presence of the YcbQ protein |CITS: 
                     [20345943]|. Expression of the <i>ycb</i> operon is 
                     regulated by the global regulators |FRAME: PD00288 
                     ""H-NS""| and |FRAME: CPLX0-226 ""CRP cAMP""| |CITS: 
                     [20345943]|.
                     Deletion of each gene (with the exception of <i>ycbF</i>) 
                     in the 7 gene <i>ycbQRSTUVF</i> operon (in a K-12 BW25113 
                     background) decreases invasion into a human ileocecal 
                     epithelial cell line compared to wild type |CITS: 
                     [27323865]|.
                     YcbQ was found, in random transposon mutagenesis studies, 
                     to be required for growth in optimum (rich medium at 
                     37&deg;C) growth conditions but not under cold conditions 
                     (15&deg;C) or in minimal medium |CITS: [15380559]|. 
                     <i>ycbQ</i> has been characterized in Shiga-toxigenic <i>E.
                     coli</i> O157:H7 and shown to encode the major subunit of 
                     laminin-binding fimbriae; the N-terminal sequence of the 
                     purified protein matches that of the predicted protein 
                     encoded by <i>ycbQ</i> in <i>E. coli</i> K-12 MG1655; the 
                     <i>ycbQRST</i> operon has been renamed <i>elfADCG</i> 
                     (<i><u>E</u>. coli</i> YcbQ <u>l</u>aminin-binding 
                     <u>f</u>imbriae) |CITS: [19508558]|.
                     <i>E. coli</i> K-12 contains 12 chaperone-usher fimbrial 
                     operons, including <i>ycbQRSTUVF</i>; a fimbria-lacking 
                     mutant - strain WQM026 - created by deleting all 12 operons
                     has been characterised |CITS: [33863704]|."
