                     /note="<i>ycbQRSTUVF</i> is a putative chaperone-usher
                     fimbrial operon in <i>E.coli K-12</i> |CITS:[12192075], 
                     [20345943]|. The operon is cryptic under normal laboratory 
                     conditions but when constitutive expression is induced in a
                     strain that lacks the type 1 fimbrial complex the 
                     <i>ycb</i> operon promotes biofilm formation in minimal 
                     media on a variety of abiotic surfaces and produces 
                     numerous surface fimbrial structures that can be observed 
                     microscopically |CITS: [20345943]|. Expression of the 
                     <i>ycb</i> operon is regulated by the global regulators 
                     |FRAME: PD00288 ""H-NS""| and |FRAME: CPLX0-226 ""CRP 
                     cAMP""| |CITS: [20345943]|.
                     <i>E. coli</i> K-12 contains 12 chaperone-usher fimbrial 
                     operons, including <i>ycbQRSTUVF</i>; a fimbria-lacking 
                     mutant - strain WQM026 - created by deleting all 12 operons
                     has been characterised |CITS: [33863704]|.
