     CDS             1016594..1017223
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="sxy"
                     /locus_tag="b0959"
                     /product="bifunctional transcriptional coactivator for CRP
                     / DNA-binding transcriptional  repressor CRP-Sxy"
                     /label=sxy
                     /note="Sxy is required for transcription from a subset of 
                     |FRAME: PD00257 CRP|-activated promoters.  Sxy is not 
                     thought to bind to DNA itself |CITS: [17068078]|.
                     Genes that are differentially expressed upon overexpression
                     of Sxy were identified by microarray analysis |CITS: 
                     [19502395]|.  Although expression of Sxy induces the 
                     expression of competence gene homologs, natural 
                     transformation was not detected |CITS: [19502395]|.  
                     However, transformation occurs when Sxy is expressed while 
                     recombination functions are provided by the &lambda; Red 
                     recombinase |CITS: [22532864]|. Expression of <i>sxy</i> is
                     autoregulated |CITS: [25491382]|.  The Sxy protein is 
                     unstable and is rapidly degraded by the Lon protease |CITS:
                     [25491382]|.  A <i>sxy</i> null mutant shows reduced 
                     fitness in long-term competitive growth experiments |CITS: 
                     [19502395]|.
                     The Sxy binding landscape was globally mapped in vivo by 
                     standardized ChIP-seq and quantitatively modeled using 
                     BoltzNet, a biophysically informed neural network that 
                     infers binding energy from sequence data |CITS:[40335485]|.
                     The resulting ChIP-seq binding regions are available in 
                     RegulonDB (<a href=""https://regulondb.cc 
                     g.unam.mx/ht/dataset/TFBINDING/source=GALAGAN"">Galagan 
                     collection</a>), and the corresponding energy matrix and 
                     genomic binding profiles can be accessed at <a 
                     href=""http://boltznet.bu.edu"">boltznet.bu.edu</a> 
                     |CITS:[40335485]|."
