     gene            1019927..1021981
                     /gene="helD"
                     /locus_tag="b0962"
                     /label=helD
     CDS             1019927..1021981
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="helD"
                     /locus_tag="b0962"
                     /product="bifunctional DNA helicase IV / DNA helicase"
                     /EC_number="5.6.2.4"
                     /label=helD
                     /note="DNA helicase IV (HelD) is an ATP-dependent 3'->5'
                     DNA helicase belonging to the helicase superfamily I |CITS:
                     [2822720]|.  HelD appears to interact with ssDNA by a 
                     distributed mechanism; addition of SSB stimulates the DNA 
                     unwinding reaction two-fold |CITS: [1321715]|.  The 
                     presence of a protein bound to dsDNA substantially inhibits
                     the helicase activity of HelD |CITS: [1336182]|. The 
                     predicted ATP binding site of HelD was investigated by 
                     site-directed mutagenesis.  Mutants in the conserved Q201 
                     and Y502 residues lead to loss of ATPase activity; the 
                     S224H and S224M mutants showed unaffected ATPase and DNA 
                     binding activities, but severely reduced helicase activity 
                     |CITS: [16442499]|.
                     There appears to be functional overlap between RecQ 
                     helicase, helicase II, and helicase IV |CITS: [7868608]|. 
                     Analysis of combinations of mutants in genes of the RecF 
                     pathway revealed synergistic interactions between 
                     <i>helD</i> and <i>recF</i>/<i>recO</i> in recombinational 
                     repair |CITS: [8647383]|.  In combination with a 
                     <i>uvrD</i> amber allele, <i>helD</i> mutations are 
                     co-suppressors for a mutation in <i>recJ</i>, which encodes
                     a single-strand DNA-specific exonuclease involved in 
                     homologous recombination |CITS: [7635292]|.  However, a 
                     reexamination of the RecF recombination pathway using 
                     well-defined mutants found that HelD is dispensable for 
                     recombination |CITS: [22342069]|.
                     HelD is expressed at low levels in the cell and is not 
                     essential for viability |CITS: [8335623]|.  In one study, 
                     even a modest level of HelD overexpression appeared to be 
                     lethal |CITS: [8335623]|; a later study reports that 
                     overexpression of HelD affects biofilm formation and causes
                     a filamentous cell morphology |CITS: [12900028]|. HelD: 
                     ""<b>hel</b>icase IV"" |CITS: [2542273]|<br>
                     SrjB: ""<b>s</b>uppressor of <i><b>r</b>ec<b>J</b></i> 
                     <b>B</b>"" |CITS: [7635292]|
                     Review: |CITS: [10754547]|"
