     gene            complement(1023860..1024177)
                     /gene="hspQ"
                     /locus_tag="b0966"
                     /label=hspQ
     CDS             complement(1023860..1024177)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="hspQ"
                     /locus_tag="b0966"
                     /product="heat shock protein HspQ"
                     /label=hspQ
                     /note="HspQ binds to hemimethylated DNA at <i>oriC</i>
                     |CITS: [12700277]|.
                     The HspQ protein of <i>Yersinia pestis</i> functions as a 
                     specificity-enhancing factor for the Lon protease |CITS: 
                     [28575662]|.  In <i>Salmonella enterica</i>, HspQ switches 
                     from activating Lon to binding and inhibiting 
                     ClpS-dependent proteolysis upon acetylation |CITS: 
                     [31371438]|.
                     The HspQ protein appeared to form dimers and higher order 
                     multimers in solution |CITS: [15569148]|; in a crystal 
                     structure, HspQ forms a homotrimer |CITS: [29083032]|.
                     An <i>hspQ</i> mutant suppresses the temperature 
                     sensitivity of the <i>dnaA508</i> and <i>dnaA167</i> 
                     alleles |CITS: [15569148]|; reports differ on whether 
                     |CITS: [12700277]| or not |CITS: [15569148]| an <i>hspQ</i>
                     mutant also suppresses the temperature sensitivity of the 
                     <i>dnaA46</i> allele.  Overexpression of HspQ exacerbates 
                     the growth defect of the <i>dnaA508</i> and <i>dnaA167</i> 
                     alleles |CITS: [15569148]|.  Overexpression of the D25A, 
                     D27A, W51A, H53A, or Y67A mutants of HspQ exacerbate the 
                     <i>dnaA508</i> growth defect to a lesser degree than wild 
                     type; thus, these residues appear to be involved in the 
                     <i>in vivo</i> function of HspQ |CITS: [29083032]|.  HspQ 
                     protein stimulates the degradation of the DnaA508 mutant 
                     protein, but not of DnaA46 |CITS: [15569148]|.  In an 
                     <i>hspQ</i> mutant, levels of DnaA appear to be increased 
                     |CITS: [12700277]|.
                     <i>hspQ</i> transcription depends on the heat shock sigma 
                     factor &sigma;<sup>32</sup> |CITS: [15569148]|.
                     HspQ: ""<b>h</b>eat <b>s</b>hock <b>p</b>rotein <b>Q</b>"" 
                     |CITS: [15569148]|"
                     /translation="MIASKFGIGQQVRHSLLGYLGVVVDIDPVYSLSEPSPDELAVNDE
                     LRAAPWYHVVMEDDNGLPVHTYLAEAQLSSELQDEHPEQPSMDELAQTIRKQLQAPRLR
                     N"
