     gene            complement(1024235..1025425)
                     /gene="rlmI"
                     /locus_tag="b0967"
                     /label=rlmI
     CDS             complement(1024235..1025425)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rlmI"
                     /locus_tag="b0967"
                     /product="23S rRNA m(5)C1962 methyltransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.1.1.191"
                     /label=rlmI
                     /note="RlmI is the methyltransferase responsible for
                     methylation of 23S rRNA at the C5 position of the C1962 
                     nucleotide.  The enzyme can methylate naked 23S rRNA, but 
                     not assembled 50S ribosomal subunits or 70S ribosomes 
                     |CITS: [18786544]|.
                     A crystal structure of RlmI has been solved at 2 &Aring; 
                     resolution; domain organization and possible evolutionary 
                     relationships of the enzyme are discussed |CITS: 
                     [18789337]|.
                     A mutant with a deletion of <i>rlmI</i> shows a significant
                     decrease in biofilm formation |CITS: [16385049]|.  However,
                     an <i>rlmI</i> mutant shows only a slight growth defect 
                     compared to wild-type cells during competitive growth 
                     experiments in rich or minimal medium |CITS: [18786544]|.
                     Expression of <i>rlmI</i> increases 17-fold upon deletion 
                     of <i>tqsA</i>, which increases biofilm formation |CITS: 
                     [16385049]|.
                     RlmI: ""<b>r</b>RNA <b>l</b>arge subunit 
                     <b>m</b>ethyltransferase <b>I</b>"" |CITS: [18786544]| 
                     Review: |CITS: [20007150]|
                     "
