     CDS             complement(1025795..1026124)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="tusE"
                     /locus_tag="b0969"
                     /product="bifunctional sulfur transfer protein TusE /
                     TusD:TusE sulfurtransferase"
                     /label=tusE
                     /note="TusE functions as a sulfur mediator during
                     synthesis of 2-thiouridine of the modified wobble base 
                     mnm<sup>5</sup>s<sup>2</sup>U in tRNA.  TusE directly 
                     interacts with both the TusBCD complex and the MnmA-tRNA 
                     complex, but not with tRNA itself |CITS: [16387657]|.
                     TusE accepts the sulfur from the |FRAME: CPLX-3942| and 
                     transfers it to Cys199 of MnmA |CITS: [28098827]|. 
                     2-thiouridine formation <i>in vitro</i> is greatly enhanced
                     in the presence of TusE.  TusE is labeled by <sup>35</sup>S
                     sulfur during 2-thiouridine formation <i>in vitro</i> 
                     |CITS: [16387657]|.
                     A <i>tusE</i> deletion mutant lacks 
                     mnm<sup>5</sup>s<sup>2</sup>U, accumulates mnm<sup>5</sup>U
                     and has a growth defect.  The cysteine residue C108 is 
                     required for sulfur transfer |CITS: [16387657]|.
                     TusE: ""tRNA 2-<b>t</b>hio<b>u</b>ridine 
                     <b>s</b>ynthesizing protein"" |CITS: [16387657]|"
