     gene            complement(1026215..1026874)
                     /gene="yccA"
                     /locus_tag="b0970"
                     /label=yccA
     CDS             complement(1026215..1026874)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yccA"
                     /locus_tag="b0970"
                     /product="modulator of FtsH protease"
                     /label=yccA
                     /note="YccA is a substrate of |FRAME: EG11506-MONOMER
                     ""FtsH""| and a modulator of FtsH-mediated proteolysis 
                     |CITS: [9636708][19661432]|.
                     YccA is predicted to have seven membrane spanning regions 
                     |CITS: [9636708]|.
                     YccA is subject to FtsH-mediated proteolysis |CITS: 
                     [9636708], [10357810]|. The sequence determinants of 
                     protease recognition have been examined in detail |CITS: 
                     [11256624]|. YccA interacts with FtsH and with the 
                     HflK-HflC (HflKC) complex, which modulates FtsH activity 
                     |CITS: [9636708]|.
                     The <i>yccA11</i> mutation causes deletion of eight 
                     residues from the cytoplasmic N terminus; YccA11 mutant 
                     protein exhibits resistance to FtsH-mediated degradation 
                     and a <i>yccA11</i> mutant strain exhibits selective 
                     defects in FtsH-mediated degradation, including a defect in
                     degradation of free SecY protein |CITS: [9636708]|. YccA11 
                     mutant protein does not exhibit a defect in interaction 
                     with FtsH or with HflKC and HflKC is required for the SecY 
                     degradation defect of the <i>yccA11</i> mutant |CITS: 
                     [9636708]|. Over expression of YccA counteracts the 
                     'jamming' of the Sec secretion complex and SecY degradation
                     that occurs with high level production of a LamB-LacZ 
                     fusion protein |CITS: [19661432]|.
                     A <i>yccA</i> mutant is impaired in biofilm formation 
                     |CITS: [14731270]|. Transcription of <i>yccA</i> is induced
                     upon biofilm formation compared to planktonic growth in 
                     exponential phase. Induction of expression is dependent on 
                     the presence of the F plasmid |CITS: [14731270]|.
                     YccA is highly homologous to human Bax Inhibitor I (BI-1), 
                     an anti-apoptotic protein which is upregulated in a variety
                     of different cancers  |CITS: [19661432]| (and see |CITS: 
                     [21663964]|).
                     "
