     gene            1028710..1030503
                     /gene="hyaB"
                     /locus_tag="b0973"
                     /label=hyaB
     CDS             1028710..1030503
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="hyaB"
                     /locus_tag="b0973"
                     /product="trifunctional hydrogenase 1 large subunit /
                     hydrogenase 1 / hydrogenase 1, oxygen tolerant hydrogenase"
                     /EC_number="1.12.5.1"
                     /label=hyaB
                     /note="HyaB is the large subunit of hydrogenase 1 and
                     contains the Ni-Fe active site. The nickel and iron atoms 
                     are coordinated by 4 Cys thiolates plus 3 diatomic ligands 
                     (2 cyano and a carbonyl). Acquisition of the [NiFe] 
                     cofactor, C-terminal processing of HyaB and subsequent 
                     association with the small subunit (HyaA) are required 
                     prior to export by the Tat system |CITS: [1856178] 
                     [8405419][12914940]| (and reviewed in |CITS: [17216401]|. A
                     <i>hyaB</i> in-frame deletion mutant does not have a defect
                     in anaerobic growth with hydrogen and fumarate as sole 
                     energy and carbon sources; a <i>hyaB hybC</i> double mutant
                     does not grow under these conditions |CITS: [DUBINI02]|."
