     gene            1030522..1031229
                     /gene="hyaC"
                     /locus_tag="b0974"
                     /label=hyaC
     CDS             1030522..1031229
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="hyaC"
                     /locus_tag="b0974"
                     /product="trifunctional hydrogenase 1 cytochrome b subunit
                     / hydrogenase 1 / hydrogenase 1, oxygen tolerant 
                     hydrogenase"
                     /EC_number="1.12.5.1"
                     /label=hyaC
                     /note="The <i>hyaC</i> gene product is very hydrophobic,
                     rich in aromatic residues, and has four putative 
                     hydrophobic
                     membrane-spanning regions |CITS: [2180913]|.
                     An in-frame deletion in the <i>hyaC</i> gene results in 
                     wild-type levels of hydrogenase 1 activity and the 
                     appearance of multiple forms of the enzyme during 
                     purification |CITS: [1856178]|. Sequence analysis suggests 
                     that the HyaC subunit contains two heme groups but only one
                     heme could be identified in the crystal structure of the 
                     hydrogenase 1 complex; HyaC's main function may be 
                     anchoring the hydrogenase to the membrane |CITS: 
                     [23260654]|.
                     Overexpression of <i>hyaC</i> from an ASKA plasmid leads to
                     a more than 3-fold increase in the MIC of hypochlorous acid
                     |CITS: [34072091]|."
