     gene            complement(1037486..1039666)
                     /gene="etk"
                     /locus_tag="b0981"
                     /label=etk
     CDS             complement(1037486..1039666)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="etk"
                     /locus_tag="b0981"
                     /product="bifunctional protein-tyrosine kinase Etk / 
                     protein-tyrosine kinase"
                     /label=etk
                     /note="Etk is a protein tyrosine kinase of the inner
                     membrane that autophosphorylates and can be 
                     dephosphorylated by Etp |CITS: 
                     [10369665][11090276][12657060]|.  In contrast to the 
                     related kinase, |FRAME: G7105-MONOMER Wzc|, Etk has minimal
                     effect on biosynthesis of colanic acid |CITS: [11090276]|. 
                     Etk, but not Wzc, plays a role in resistance to polymyxin B
                     |CITS: [16814990]|.  Etk phosphorylates the heat shock 
                     sigma factor &sigma;<sup>32</sup> <i>in vitro</i> |CITS: 
                     [12657060]|.
                     A crystal structure of the C-terminal kinase domain has 
                     been solved at 2.5 &Aring; resolution.  Etk shows 
                     structural similarity to the ATPase MinD |CITS: 
                     [18497741]|.
                     Etk has two predicted transmembrane domains.  The C 
                     terminus is located in the cytoplasm |CITS: [15919996]|. 
                     The operon encoding YmcD, YmcC, YmcB, YmcA, YccZ, Etp, and 
                     Etk was characterized in the enteropathogenic <i>E. 
                     coli</i> strain O127:H6.  There, all seven gene products 
                     are required for the production of the G4C capsule 
                     polysaccharide |CITS: [16030220]|.  That operon may not be 
                     expressed in <i>E. coli</i> K-12, because the promoter 
                     region that was mapped in <i>E. coli</i> O127:H6 is 
                     inactivated in <i>E. coli</i> K-12 by the insertion of an 
                     IS<i>1</i> element 15 bp upstream of the YmcD translation 
                     start site |CITS: [10369665][16030220]|.
                     Reviews: |CITS: [17208443][19525115]|"
