                     /locus_tag="b0991"
                     /product="protein YmcE"
                     /label=ymcE
                     /note="YmcE was mistakenly thought to be a suppressor of 
                     <i>fabA6</i>, a temperature-sensitive unsaturated fatty 
                     acid auxotroph |CITS: [8808925]|; in fact, the suppressor 
                     localizes to the <i>gnsA</i> gene, which is located 
                     immediately downstream of <i>ymcE</i> |CITS: [11544213]|. 
                     YmcE is also predicted to be the antitoxin of a proposed 
                     GnsA-YmcE toxin-antitoxin system |CITS: [21927020]|.
                     YmcE is predicted to be a bitopic inner membrane protein 
                     |CITS: [27510400]|.
                     Expression of <i>ymcE</i> is increased by cold shock |CITS:
                     [14527658]|.  Overexpression of <i>ymcE</i> increases the 
                     tolerance of <i>E. coli</i> to n-butanol |CITS: 
                     [21408113]|.
                     "
