     gene            1053540..1054712
                     /gene="torC"
                     /locus_tag="b0996"
                     /label=torC
     CDS             1053540..1054712
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="torC"
                     /locus_tag="b0996"
                     /product="trifunctional cytochrome c menaquinol
                     dehydrogenase TorC / menaquinol:trimethylamine N-oxide 
                     oxidoreductase I / menaquinol:trimethylamine N-oxide 
                     oxidoreductase"
                     /label=torC
                     /note="TorC is a pentaheme <I>c</I>-type cytochrome that
                     is anchored to the inner membrane |CITS: 
                     [8022286][8039676][11056172]|. The protein is predicted to 
                     be largely hydrophilic but contains a small stretch of 
                     hydrophobic amino acids towards the N-terminus |CITS: 
                     [8022286]|. TorC is required for anaerobic growth in the 
                     presence of trimethylamine N-oxide; TorC shuttles electrons
                     from a membrane quinol to TorA in the periplasm |CITS: 
                     [11056172]|. TorC contains an N-terminal domain 
                     (TorC<sub>N</sub>) and a C-terminal domain 
                     (TorC<sub>C</sub>) of similar size; TorC<sub>N</sub> 
                     contains the membrane anchor followed by 4 heme-binding 
                     sites; TorC<sub>C</sub> contains the fifth heme-binding 
                     site and this domain donates electrons directly to TorA 
                     |CITS: [11056172]|
                     The TorC apoprotein down-regulates transcription of the 
                     <i>torCAD</i> operon |CITS: [10411745]|; apoTorC acts as a 
                     negative regulator after translocation to the periplasm; 
                     the C-terminal domain of the TorC apoprotein is involved in
                     autoregulation of the <i>tor</i> operon; apoTorC interacts 
                     directly with the TorS sensory kinase; apoTorC does not 
                     bind strongly to TorA |CITS: [11562502]|."
