                     /product="stress-induced bacterial acidophilic repeat 
                     motifs-containing protein YmdF"
                     /label=ymdF
                     /note="This |FRAME: G0-10443| gene along with |FRAME:
                     EG11127| gene is homologous to gene STM14_1829 in |FRAME: 
                     TAX-90371| 14028s that belong to a family of proteins 
                     involved in motility |CITS: [30373755]|. These two genes 
                     also show homology to gene PA2146 in |FRAME: TAX-208964|, 
                     shown to contribute to both biofilm formation and 
                     susceptibility to a variety of antimicrobial agents |CITS: 
                     [35798749]|.
                     Deletion of both <i>yciG</i> and <i>ymdF</i> together 
                     exhibited a slight swimming motility defect |CITS: 
                     [30373755]|.
                     <i>ymdF</i> can substitute for PA2146 gene in <i>P. 
                     aeruginosa</i> &Delta;PA2146 mutants. A deletion mutant of 
                     <i>ymdF</i> in <i>E. coli</i> BW25113 was more susceptible 
                     to antimicrobial agents, such as hydrogen peroxide and 
                     ciprofloxacin and not able to form typical 3-D biofilm 
                     architecture compared to wild-type; the deletion mutant 
                     phenotype was rescued by the <i>P. aeruginosa</i> PA2146 
                     gene. <i>ymdF</i> lacks a Walker nucleotide binding motif 
                     present in <i>yciF</i>; the functional significance of this
                     difference was not examined |CITS: [35798749]|.
                     "
                     /translation="MANHRGGSGNFAEDRERASEAGKKGGQHSGGNFKNDPQRASEAGK
                     KGGKSSHGKSDN"
