     CDS             complement(1065316..1065810)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rutF"
                     /locus_tag="b1007"
                     /product="bifunctional FMN reductase RutF / FMN reductase"
                     /EC_number="1.5.1.42"
                     /label=rutF
                     /note="<i>E. coli</i> K-12 contains a previously
                     undescribed pathway for pyrimidine degradation.  RutF 
                     functions as a flavin reductase whose activity is required 
                     for the first catalytic step, the flavin 
                     hydroperoxide-catalyzed ring opening by the RutA pyrimidine
                     oxygenase |CITS: [20369853][20400551]|.  <i>In vitro</i>, 
                     the flavin reductase Fre can substitute for the function of
                     RutF; however, RutF is required for uracil utilization 
                     <i>in vivo</i> |CITS: [20400551]|.
                     Expression of the <i>rutABCDEFG</i> operon is under the 
                     control of nitrogen regulatory protein C (NtrC) |CITS: 
                     [11121068]|.  A <i>rutF</i> insertion mutant loses the 
                     ability to utilize pyrimidine nucleosides and bases as the 
                     sole source of nitrogen at room temperature |CITS: 
                     [16540542]|.
                     RutF: ""py<b>r</b>imidine <b>ut</b>ilization <b>F</b>"" 
                     |CITS: [16540542]|
                     Reviews: |CITS: [16595627][17555842]|"
