     gene            complement(1068319..1069467)
                     /gene="rutA"
                     /locus_tag="b1012"
                     /label=rutA
     CDS             complement(1068319..1069467)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rutA"
                     /locus_tag="b1012"
                     /product="trifunctional pyrimidine monooxygenase RutA /
                     uracil oxygenase / thymine oxygenase"
                     /EC_number="1.14.99.46"
                     /label=rutA
                     /note="<i>E. coli</i> K-12 contains a previously
                     undescribed pathway for pyrimidine degradation.  In the 
                     presence of the flavin reductases Fre or RutF, RutA 
                     catalyzes the first step in this pathway, the ring opening 
                     of uracil at the C4 carbonyl |CITS: [20369853][20400551]|. 
                     The reaction was initially thought to produce 
                     ureidoacrylate peracid, which would convert to 
                     ureidoacrylate either enzymatically or spontaneously |CITS:
                     [20369853][20400551]|.  It was later shown that the 
                     reaction involves formation of a |FRAME: CPD-22328| 
                     intermediate |CITS: [28661684]|.  More recently, |CITS: 
                     [32066967]| used mechanistic and computational studies 
                     together with X-ray crystallography to show that 
                     flavin-N5-peroxide is the oxygen-transferring species. 
                     Expression of the <i>rutABCDEFG</i> operon is under the 
                     control of nitrogen regulatory protein C (NtrC) |CITS: 
                     [11121068]|.  A <i>rutA</i> insertion mutant loses the 
                     ability to utilize pyrimidine nucleosides and bases as the 
                     sole source of nitrogen at room temperature |CITS: 
                     [16540542]|.
                     Crystal structures of RutA have been solved |CITS: 
                     [20369853][32066967]|.
                     <i>rutA</i> levels are increased 3.5-fold by growth on 
                     ZnSO<sub>4</sub>-containing medium, and a <i>rutA</i> null 
                     mutant is hypersensitive to ZnSO<sub>4</sub> |CITS: 
                     [15659689]|.
                     RutA: ""py<b>r</b>imidine <b>ut</b>ilization <b>A</b>"" 
                     |CITS: [16540542]|
                     Reviews: |CITS: [16595627][17555842][28784589]|"
