     gene            complement(1083295..1085313)
                     /gene="pgaB"
                     /locus_tag="b1023"
                     /label=pgaB
     CDS             complement(1083295..1085313)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="pgaB"
                     /locus_tag="b1023"
                     /product="trifunctional
                     poly-beta-1,6-N-acetyl-D-glucosamine N-deacetylase and 
                     beta-1,6 glycoside hydrolase / 
                     poly-beta-1,6-N-acetyl-D-glucosamine N-deacetylase / 
                     endo-poly-beta-1,6-D-glucosamine hydrolase"
                     /label=pgaB
                     /note="PgaB is an outer membrane lipoprotein that is
                     required for the partial de-<i>N</i>-acetylation and 
                     hydrolysis of poly-&beta;-1,6-<i>N</i>-acetyl-D-glucosamine
                     (known as PGA or PNAG) - an exopolysaccharide that is a key
                     component of the biofilm matrix of many pathogenic bacteria
                     |CITS: [15090514][15601723][18359807][29684093]|. PgaB 
                     interacts with the outer membrane porin |FRAME: 
                     G6531-MONOMER PgaA| and this interaction is implicated in 
                     the export of deacetylated PNAG |CITS: [26957546]|.
                     PgaB consists of an N-terminal deacetylase domain that has 
                     a distorted (&beta;/&alpha;)<sub>7</sub> barrel fold and 
                     belongs to the class 4 carbohydrate esterases and a 
                     C-terminal glycoside hydrolase (GH) domain that has a 
                     (&beta;/&alpha;)<sub>8</sub> barrel fold and belongs to a 
                     newly defined GH family - GH153 |CITS: 
                     [22810235][29684093]|. Both domains are necessary for 
                     de-<i>N</i>-acetylation of PNAG; a cleft formed between the
                     N and C-terminal domains is proposed to bind PNAG in an 
                     extended conformation during deacetylation |CITS: 
                     [24994902]|. Full-length constructs of PgaB and the 
                     isolated GH domain both display glycoside hydrolase 
                     activity on partially deacetylated PNAG isolated from <i>S.
                     aureus</i> |CITS: [29684093]|. GH activity has been 
                     characterised in the <i>Bordetella bronchiseptica</i> 
                     isofunctional homolog (44% sequence identity) |CITS: 
                     [29684093]|.
                     PgaB is a metal dependent de-<i>N</i>-acetylase with a 
                     preference for Co<sup>2+</sup>, Ni<sup>2+</sup> and 
                     Fe<sup>2+</sup>; PgaB binds two metal ions per molecule; 
                     PgaB exhibits length dependent de-<i>N</i>-acetylation of 
                     &beta;-1,6-GlcNAc oligomers <i>in vitro</i> [up to 
                     &beta;-1,6-(GlcNAc)<sub>5</sub>]; PgaB has specificity for 
                     &beta;-1,6-GlcNAc oligomers - no activity is observed on 
                     chitotetraose [&beta;-1,4-(GlcNAc)<sub>4</sub>] |CITS: 
                     [22810235]|.
                     Deletion of <i>pgaB</i> results in reduced biofilm 
                     formation and retention of acetylated polymer in the 
                     periplasm; deacetylation of PNAG by PgaB promotes its 
                     export |CITS: [15090514][18359807]|.
                     <i>pgaB</i> is part of a 4 gene locus (<i>pgaABCD</i>) 
                     whose gene products are involved in the synthesis, 
                     modification and export of PNAG. Expression of 
                     <i>pgaABCD</i> is higher at 37&deg;C than at 21&deg;C and 
                     is highest during stationary phase |CITS: [18445167]|. 
                     Expression also increases in response to one-percent NaCl 
                     or ethanol |CITS: [18445167]|.  Expression increases in 
                     response to glucose, ethanol, NaCl, and MnCl<sub>2</sub> in
                     a clinical isolate, and dramatically increases upon 
                     deletion or mutation of <i>csrA</i> in this strain |CITS: 
                     [18445167][16923806]|.  CsrA inhibits translation of 
                     <i>pgaABCD</i> mRNA by binding to six sites within the 
                     <i>pgaABCD</i> leader |CITS: [15916613][16923806]|.  NaCl 
                     and alkaline pH induction are dependent upon <i>nhaR</i> as
                     deletion of this gene prevented induction |CITS: 
                     [16997959][18445167]|.
                     PgaB has similarity to the HmsF protein encoded by the 
                     <i>Yersinia pestis hmsHFRST</i> gene cluster, which is 
                     involved in plague transmission |CITS: [10463178]|. 
                     Comment: |CITS: [25006258]|"
                     /translation="MLRNGNKYLLMLVSIIMLTACISQSRTSFIPPQDRESLLAEQPWP
