     gene            complement(1085322..1087745)
                     /gene="pgaA"
                     /locus_tag="b1024"
                     /label=pgaA
     CDS             complement(1085322..1087745)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="pgaA"
                     /locus_tag="b1024"
                     /product="partially deacetylated 
                     poly-beta-1,6-N-acetyl-D-glucosamine export porin"
                     /label=pgaA
                     /note="The <i>pgaABCD</i> locus is required for the
                     synthesis of a cell-bound hexosamine-rich polysaccharide, 
                     which was identified as a linear polymer of 
                     &beta;-1,6-<i>N</i>-acetylglucosamine residues (PGA), an 
                     adhesin essential in biofilm formation |CITS: 
                     [15090514][15601723]|. PgaA exports PGA across the outer 
                     membrane. <i>N</i>-deacetylation of PGA by PgaB promotes 
                     its transport across the outer membrane.
                     A <i>pgaA</i> mutant has reduced biofilm formation |CITS: 
                     [15090514]|. <i>pgaA</i> mutants do not release significant
                     amounts of PGA into the medium during shaking compared to 
                     wild-type |CITS: [18359807]|. PGA from <i>pgaA</i> mutants 
                     is not externally exposed, showing PgaA is involved in 
                     transport of PGA across the outer membrane |CITS: 
                     [18359807]|.
                     Expression of <i>pgaABCD</i> is higher at 37&deg;C than at 
                     21&deg;C and is highest during stationary phase |CITS: 
                     [18445167]|. Expression increased in response to 1% NaCl or
                     ethanol |CITS: [18445167]|. Expression increased in 
                     response to glucose, ethanol, NaCl, and MnCl<sub>2</sub> in
                     a clinical isolate, and dramatically increased upon 
                     deletion or mutation of <i>csrA</i> in this strain |CITS: 
                     [18445167][16923806]|. CsrA inhibits translation of 
                     <i>pgaABCD</i> mRNA by binding to six sites within the 
                     <i>pgaABCD</i> leader |CITS: [15916613][16923806]|. NaCl 
                     and alkaline pH induction are dependent upon <i>nhaR</i>, 
                     as deletion of this gene prevented induction |CITS: 
                     [16997959][18445167]|.
                     PgaA has similarity to the HmsH protein encoded within the 
                     <i>Yersinia pestis hmsHFRST</i> gene cluster, which is 
                     involved in plague transmission and is required for biofilm
                     formation in vitro |CITS: [10463178]|."
