                     /label=ghrA
     CDS             1093342..1094280
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ghrA"
                     /locus_tag="b1033"
                     /product="trifunctional glyoxylate/hydroxypyruvate
                     reductase A / glyoxylate reductase / hydroxypyruvate 
                     reductase"
                     /EC_number="1.1.1.79"
                     /label=ghrA
                     /note="GhrA is one of two enzymes with glyoxylate
                     reductase activity.  GhrA prefers NADPH as the electron 
                     donor and also catalyzes reduction of hydroxypyruvate, 
                     although at lower catalytic efficiency.  In contrast, the 
                     <i>ghrB</i>-encoded enzyme prefers hydroxypyruvate as the 
                     substrate |CITS: [11237876]|.
                     Expression of <i>ghrA</i> is slightly increased by growth 
                     on medium containing hydroxypyruvate |CITS: [11237876]|. 
                     <i>ghrA</i> was one of only three genes whose expression 
                     changed under all stress conditions tested by |CITS: 
                     [19767843]|.
                     Inactivation of <i>ghrA</i> was investigated as a means to 
                     improve production of 1,2,4-butanetriol in a metabolically 
                     engineered strain |CITS: [27702485]|."
