                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ycdY"
                     /locus_tag="b1035"
                     /product="chaperone protein YcdY"
                     /label=ycdY
                     /note="YcdY is a member of an atypical subfamily of TorD 
                     chaperones |CITS: [15073303]|.  YcdY appears to enable 
                     maturation of YcdX, potentially by facilitating insertion 
                     of Zn<sup>2+</sup> into the catalytic site of YcdX |CITS: 
                     [21965574]|.
                     Phylogenetic analysis of the NarJ subfamily of proteins 
                     suggests that YcdY has only recently evolved from DmsD 
                     |CITS: [26067063]|.
                     A <i>ycdY</i> mutant has a swarming defect |CITS: 
                     [17122336][21965574]|.
                     Review: |CITS: [25157671]|"
