     gene            1100870..1101181
                     /gene="ymdA"
                     /locus_tag="b1044"
                     /label=ymdA
     CDS             1100870..1101181
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ymdA"
                     /locus_tag="b1044"
                     /product="uncharacterized protein YmdA"
                     /label=ymdA
                     /note="Expression of YmdA is posttranscriptionally
                     activated by CsrA.  CsrA binds to two sites in the 5' UTR 
                     of <i>ymdA</i>; both binding sites are required to 
                     destabilize a hairpin structure that sequesters the 
                     ribosome binding site |CITS: [32934077]|.
                     Overexpression of YmdA inhibits biofilm formation |CITS: 
                     [28582517]|.  A &Delta;<i>ymdA</i> strain shows a modest 
                     decrease in biofilm formation |CITS: [32934077]|."
                     /translation="MFRPFLNSLMLGSLFFPFIAIAGSTVQGGVIHFYGQIVEPACDVS
                     TQSSPVEMNCPQNGSIPGKTYSSKALMSGNVKNAQIASVKVQYLDKQKKLAVMNIEYN"
                     /go_component="extracellular region [goid 0005576]
                     [evidence IEA] [PMID 26602691]"
                     /go_process="single-species biofilm formation [goid
                     0044010] [evidence IMP] [PMID 32934077]"
     gene            1101276..1101809
                     /gene="ymdB"
                     /locus_tag="b1045"
                     /label=ymdB
     CDS             1101276..1101809
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ymdB"
                     /locus_tag="b1045"
                     /product="bifunctional 2'-O-acetyl-ADP-ribose deacetylase, 
                     regulator of RNase III activity / 2''-O-acetyl-ADP-ribose 
                     deacetylase"
                     /EC_number="3.1.1.106"
                     /label=ymdB
                     /note="YmdB is a macrodomain family protein with 
                     <i>O</i>-acetyl-ADP-ribose deacetylase activity |CITS: 
                     [21257746]|.  <i>O</i>-acetyl-ADP-ribose is produced by 
                     NAD<sup>+</sup>-dependent protein deacetylation.
                     The YmdB protein inhibits the activity of |FRAME: 
                     CPLX0-3281| by interacting directly with the enzyme. Amino 
                     acids 120-140 in the catalytic region of RNase III are 
                     necessary for YmdB binding |CITS: [19141481]|. The 
                     interaction was modeled, and site-directed mutagenesis 
                     confirmed that residues R40 of YmdB and D128 of RNase III 
                     are important for the interaction |CITS: [25546632]|. A 
                     protein inhibitor of RNase III was first identified by 
                     Makarov and Apirion |CITS: [1378735]|.
                     Crystal structures of YmdB have been solved, and a 
                     catalytic mechanism was proposed |CITS: [26481419]|. 
                     Expression of <i>ymdB</i> increases in early stationary 
                     phase and during cold shock |CITS: [19141481][28582517]|; 
                     this response is dependent on the alternative sigma factor 
                     RpoS (&sigma;<sup>S</sup>) |CITS: [19141481]|. 
                     Downregulation of RNase III activity during cold shock 
                     requires YmdB, while decreased RNase III activity during 
                     stationary phase does not appear to depend on YmdB |CITS: 
                     [19141481]|.
                     Genes whose expression is modulated by YmdB were identified
                     by microarray analysis |CITS: [24267348]|. Overexpression 
                     of YmdB inhibits biofilm formation |CITS: 
                     [24267348][28582517]|. This effect is independent of RNase 
                     III, and may be due to an interaction with RpoS |CITS: 
                     [24267348]|. Overexpression of <i>ymdB</i> increases the 
                     susceptibility to apramycin; this effect depends on the 
                     presence of RNase III |CITS: [28034758]|.
                     A <i>ymdAB-clsC</i> triple knockout mutant showed greater 
                     biofilm formation than a <i>ymdB</i> single mutant. 
                     Resistance to apramycin was increased in <i>ymdB</i> 
                     knockout cells compared with wild-type cells |CITS: 
                     [28582517]|.
                     Full complementation of a <i>clsC</i> mutant requires 
                     co-expression with <i>ymdB</i> |CITS: [22988102]|."
                     /translation="MKTRIHVVQGDITKLAVDVIVNAANPSLMGGGGVDGAIHRAAGPA
