     gene            1109035..1109262
                     /gene="yceK"
                     /locus_tag="b1050"
                     /label=yceK
     CDS             1109035..1109262
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yceK"
                     /locus_tag="b1050"
                     /product="DUF1375 domain-containing lipoprotein YceK"
                     /label=yceK
                     /note="Strong aggravating genetic interactions (measured
                     by relative colony size and fitness in rich medium) were 
                     observed between <i>lptD</i> and <i>yceK</i> |CITS: 
                     [22125496]|. Deletion of <i>yceK</i> results in impaired 
                     outer membrane integrity as evidenced by vancomycin-induced
                     morphological defects and lowered outer membrane protein 
                     (OMP) abundance |CITS: [22125496]|. Deletion of <i>yceK</i>
                     and <i>lptD</i> results in cell wall failure/lysis, lowered
                     OMP abundance and increased levels of the DegP stress 
                     response protease |CITS: [22125496]|.
                     Overexpression of <i>yceK</i> suppresses the essentiality 
                     of |FRAME: EG12691-MONOMER <i>lapB</i>|, which encodes a 
                     protein involved in lipopolysaccharide (LPS) assembly. The 
                     defects in LPS composition that occur in a &Delta;(<i>lapA 
                     lapB</i>) mutant are exacerbated in a &Delta;(<i>lapA lapB 
                     yceK</i>) mutant |CITS: [24722986]|.
                     <i>yceK</i> contains a predicted lipoprotein signal |CITS: 
                     [12876315][15174130]|.  YceK is a verified lipoprotein 
                     according to unpublished data by S. Matsuyama et al. (cited
                     in |CITS: [12876315]|)."
                     /translation="MRLIVVSIMVTLLSGCGSIISRTIPGQGHGNQYYPGVQWDVRDSA
                     WRYVTILDLPFSLVFDTLLLPIDIHHGPYE"
                     /go_process="DNA damage response [goid 0006974] [evidence
                     IEP] [PMID 11967071]"
     gene            complement(1109263..1109637)
                     /gene="msyB"
                     /locus_tag="b1051"
                     /label=msyB
     CDS             complement(1109263..1109637)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="msyB"
                     /locus_tag="b1051"
                     /product="acidic protein MsyB"
                     /label=msyB
                     /note="The <i>msyB</i> gene is a multicopy suppressor of
                     heat sensitivity of a <i>secY24</i> mutant |CITS: 
                     [1537791]|.
                     NMR resonance assignments for MsyB are available |CITS: 
                     [32504338]|.
                     MsyB is rich in acidic amino acids, which may cause 
                     abnormal migration in SDS gels |CITS: [1537791]|. As a 
                     fusion partner for overexpression of heterologous proteins 
                     in <i>E. coli</i>, MsyB improves solubility |CITS: 
