     CDS             complement(1109720..1110946)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="mdtG"
                     /locus_tag="b1053"
                     /product="trifunctional efflux pump MdtG / fosfomycin:H(+) 
                     antiporter / deoxycholate:H(+) antiporter"
                     /label=mdtG
                     /note="Increased expression of <I>mdtG</I> in a K-12
                     strain which lacks the major efflux pump permease AcrB 
                     (<i>E. coli</i> KAM3; see |CITS: [12618449]|) results in a 
                     four-fold increase in resistance to fosfomycin and a 
                     two-fold increase in resistance to deoxycholate but does 
                     not impact the resistance to a range of other antibiotics 
                     and toxic compounds |CITS:[11566977]|. MdtG (formerly YceE)
                     is a member of the Drug:H<sup>+</sup> Antiporter-1 (12 
                     Spanner) (DHA1) family within the Major Facilitator 
                     Superfamily (MFS) |CITS: [8987357][26546518]|. <i>mdtG</i> 
                     is a member of the <I>marA-soxS-rob</i> regulon; a SoxS 
                     binding marbox sequence is located within the <i>mdtG</i> 
                     promoter region; an <i>mdtG-lacZ</i> transcriptional fusion
                     is induced in the presence of paraquat, sodium salicylate 
                     and 2,2'-dipyridyl |CITS: [20008776]|. <i>mdtG</i> is one 
                     of 35 efflux-encoding genes that have been deleted or 
                     inactivated in 'Efflux KnockOut-35' (EKO-35) -  a K-12 
                     BW25133-derived strain that lacks 35 efflux pumps and can 
                     be used as a platform to study their function |CITS: 
                     [36065018][36318669]|."
