     gene            complement(1111118..1112038)
                     /gene="lpxL"
                     /locus_tag="b1054"
                     /label=lpxL
     CDS             complement(1111118..1112038)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="lpxL"
                     /locus_tag="b1054"
                     /product="lauroyl acyltransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.3.1.241"
                     /label=lpxL
                     /note="Lauroyl acyltransferase (LpxL) transfers laurate
                     from lauroyl acyl carrier protein (ACP) to the free OH 
                     group of the 2'-R-3-hydroxymyristoyl chain of the 
                     KDO<sub>2</sub>-lipid IV<sub>A</sub>. This is one of the 
                     last two acylation reactions needed to synthesize 
                     KDO<sub>2</sub>-lipid A |CITS: 
                     [2203778][8662613][18656959]|.
                     LpxL is an inner membrane protein with a predicted single 
                     N-terminal transmembrane helix |CITS: [17362200]|. LpxL 
                     shares sequence homology and functional similarity to LpxM,
                     the final enzyme in the lipid A biosynthetic pathway |CITS:
                     [1732206]|. A third ortholog, LpxP, is induced below 
                     20&deg;C and competes with LpxL to transfer palmitoleate 
                     chain to KDO<sub>2</sub>-lipid IV<sub>A</sub> |CITS: 
                     [11830595]|. Distant sequence homology exists between LpxL 
                     and the glycerol-3-phosphate acyltransferase (GPAT) family 
                     of enzymes |CITS: [18656959]|.
                     <i>lpxL</i>, the gene coding for LpxL was previously 
                     identified as a high-temperature requirement gene 
                     (<i>htrB</i>) because the null mutant was 
                     temperature-sensitive for growth above 33&deg;C. Under 
                     nonpermissive conditions, cell division ceased, the 
                     membrane bulged and the cells slowly lysed |CITS: 
                     [1846149][1656498]|. Recently, <i>lpxL</i> mutants have 
                     been shown to grow at 30, 37 and 42&deg;C. At 37 and 
                     42&deg;C the <i>lpxL</i> mutants generated atypical penta- 
                     and hexaacyl lipid A structures |CITS: [23812252]|. 
                     Mutations in <i>lpxL</i> have caused reduced acylation of 
                     LPS, resulting in constitutive expression of the sigma(E) 
                     regulon above wild-type levels |CITS: [15720549]|. 
                     Conserved residues in LpxL were identified using the 
                     conserved domain database |CITS: [15608175]|. Point 
                     mutations of the residues were generated and two mutations,
                     H132A and E137A, impaired activity the most as compared to 
                     wild-type LpxL |CITS: [18656959]|. Overexpression of 
                     <i>lpxL</i> suppressed the lethality of <i>kdtA</i> (gene 
                     encoding the KDO transferase) deletions |CITS: 
                     [19754149]|."
