     gene            1112263..1113315
                     /gene="trhO"
                     /locus_tag="b1055"
                     /label=trhO
     CDS             1112263..1113315
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="trhO"
                     /locus_tag="b1055"
                     /product="bifunctional tRNA U34 hydroxylase TrhO / tRNA
                     U34 hydroxylase"
                     /label=trhO
                     /note="TrhP is involved in the formation of the 
                     cmo<sup>5</sup>U34 modification on tRNAs during anaerobic 
                     growth conditions, while TrhO-mediated formation of 
                     ho<sup>5</sup>U34 utilizes molecular oxygen as the oxygen 
                     atom donor |CITS: [31253794]|.
                     A &Delta;<i>trhP trhO</i> double mutant has lost all 
                     modification of the U34 wobble base of tRNA<sup>Val1</sup> 
                     and grows more slowly than wild type.  Additional knockout 
                     of |FRAME: EG30094 <i>serU</i>|, |FRAME: EG30104 
                     <i>thrW</i>| or |FRAME: EG30066 <i>proK</i>|, which encode 
                     tRNAs responsible for decoding G-ending codons, results in 
                     further reduction of growth |CITS: [31253794]|. Mutagenesis
                     of the predicted active site residues C200, T201, G203, and
                     R205, and residues K112 and R114 predicted to be involved 
                     in substrate binding of TrhO results in loss of activity in
                     the mutant strain |CITS: [31253794]|. TrhO: ""<b>tR</b>NA 
                     <b>h</b>ydroxylation <b>O</b>"" |CITS: [31253794]|"
