     gene            complement(1114763..1114903)
                     /gene="yceO"
                     /locus_tag="b1058"
                     /label=yceO
     CDS             complement(1114763..1114903)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yceO"
                     /locus_tag="b1058"
                     /product="DUF2770 domain-containing protein YceO"
                     /label=yceO
                     /note="YceO appears to be involved in biofilm formation
                     |CITS: [16385049]| and the acid stress response |CITS: 
                     [19734312]|.  The YceO open reading frame contains a 
                     predicted transmembrane segment |CITS: [19121005]|. 
                     Expression of <i>yceO</i> increases 11-fold upon deletion 
                     of <i>tqsA</i>, which increases biofilm formation |CITS: 
                     [16385049]|.  YceO is expressed during exponential growth 
                     |CITS: [19121005]|.  A mutant with a deletion of 
                     <i>yceO</i> shows a significant decrease in biofilm 
                     formation |CITS: [16385049]|.  In growth competition 
                     experiments, a <i>yceO</i> deletion mutant is more 
                     sensitive to acute acid stress than the wild type |CITS: 
                     [19734312]|."
                     /translation="MRPFLQEYLMRRLLHYLINNIREHLMLYLFLWGLLAIMDLIYVFY
                     F"
