                     IEA] [PMID 26602691]"
                     /go_process="single-species biofilm formation [goid
                     0044010] [evidence IMP] [PMID 16385049]"
                     /go_process="response to acidic pH [goid 0010447]
                     [evidence IMP] [PMID 19734312]"
     gene            complement(1114924..1116042)
                     /gene="solA"
                     /locus_tag="b1059"
                     /label=solA
     CDS             complement(1114924..1116042)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="solA"
                     /locus_tag="b1059"
                     /product="N-methyl-L-tryptophan oxidase"
                     /EC_number="1.5.3.2"
                     /label=solA
                     /note="The <i>solA</i> gene product has 
                     <i>N</i>-methyltryptophan oxidase (MTOX) activity.
                     Despite significant similarity to the <i>Bacillus</i> sp. 
                     sarcosine oxidase, the enzyme has comparatively little 
                     sarcosine oxidase activity |CITS: 
                     [8973328][11170473][15723552]|.  MTOX can catalyze the 
                     demethylation of various <i>N</i>-methyl amino acids, but 
                     has a preference for <i>N</i>-methyltryptophan |CITS: 
                     [8973328]|.  The metabolic role and physiological substrate
                     for the enzyme are unknown.
                     Cys308 is the covalent attachment site for FAD |CITS: 
                     [10220347][18186483]|.  Studies of the reaction mechanism 
                     are consistent with a modified ping pong mechanism |CITS: 
                     [11170473]| and exclude the formation of a covalent adduct 
                     intermediate |CITS: [17542620]|.  Lys259 is the site of 
                     oxygen activation and also plays a role in holoenzyme 
                     biosynthesis and N-methyltryptophan oxidation.  The enzyme 
                     contains separate active sites for N-methyltryptophan 
                     oxidation and oxygen reduction on opposite faces of the 
                     flavin ring |CITS: [21526853]|.
                     A crystal structure of SolA has been solved at 3.2 &Aring; 
                     resolution, identifying Thr239 as a key residue for 
                     substrate side chain recognition |CITS: [18186483]|.
                     SolA expression is increased 3-fold by growth on minimal 
                     media |CITS: [11170472]|.
                     SolA: ""<b>s</b>arcosine <b>o</b>xidase-<b>l</b>ike gene"" 
                     |CITS: [8973328]|"
