     gene            1121018..1121602
                     /gene="rimJ"
                     /locus_tag="b1066"
                     /label=rimJ
     CDS             1121018..1121602
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rimJ"
                     /locus_tag="b1066"
                     /product="ribosomal-protein-S5-alanine
                     N-acetyltransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.3.1.267"
                     /label=rimJ
                     /note="RimJ is an alanine acetyltransferase that is
                     specific for |FRAME: EG10904-MONOMER| |CITS: 
                     [385889][2828880]|.  RimJ also plays a role in maturation 
                     of the 30S ribosomal subunit |CITS: [18466225][20176963]|. 
                     RimJ interacts with pre-30S, but not mature ribosomal 
                     subunits |CITS: [18466225]|.  RimJ has overall similarity 
                     to RimL |CITS: [2671655]| and C-terminal similarity to RimI
                     |CITS: [2828880]|.
                     Overexpression of RimJ, even when lacking its 
                     acetyltransferase activity, suppresses the 16S rRNA 
                     maturation defect of an RpsE G28D mutant |CITS: 
                     [18466225][20176963]|.  Overexpression of RimJ decreases 
                     the levels of the immature long precursor 16S rRNA (lp16S 
                     rRNA) in the RpsE G28D mutant |CITS: [20176963]|.  In a 
                     <i>rimJ</i> mutant, the ribosomal protein S5 is not 
                     acetylated at the N terminus |CITS: [385889]|.  Mutation of
                     the conserved cysteine residues C54 and/or C105 results in 
                     loss of RimJ acetyltransferase activity |CITS: [18466225]|.
                     RimJ acts in transcriptional regulation of the <i>pap</i> 
                     pilin operon by environmental conditions in uropathogenic 
                     <i>E. coli</i> |CITS: [1356970][12142402]|.
                     Tcp: ""<b>t</b>hermoregulatory <b>c</b>ontrol of 
                     <i><b>p</b>ap</i>"" |CITS: [2156803]|
                     RimJ: ""<b>ri</b>bosomal <b>m</b>odification <b>J</b>"" 
                     |CITS: [385889]|
                     Review: |CITS: [21529161]|"
