     CDS             complement(1124870..1125286)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="flgN"
                     /locus_tag="b1070"
                     /product="flagellar biosynthesis protein FlgN"
                     /label=flgN
                     /note="FliT, along with FliS and FlgN, are cytoplasmic, 
                     substrate-specific chaperones of the flagellar export 
                     system.  They share several similarities with other type 
                     III cytoplasmic chaperone family members |CITS:[8028576]|. 
                     Affinity blot analysis showed that FlgN binds <I>in 
                     vitro</I> to hook-filament junction proteins FlgK and FlgL 
                     |CITS:[10320579]| suggesting that FlgN may act as a 
                     chaperone which aids in the export  and prevents premature 
                     aggregation of the FlgK and FlgL hook-filament junction 
                     proteins |CITS:[1169117]|. Gel filtration chromatography 
                     indicate that FlgN exists as a homodimer in the cytosol and
                     that these homodimers bind to monomers of FlgK and FlgL to 
                     form heterotrimeric chaperone-substrate complexes 
                     |CITS:[11169117]|."
