     gene            complement(1125291..1125584)
                     /gene="flgM"
                     /locus_tag="b1071"
                     /label=flgM
     CDS             complement(1125291..1125584)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="flgM"
                     /locus_tag="b1071"
                     /product="anti-sigma factor for FliA (sigma(28))"
                     /label=flgM
                     /note="FlgM is an anti-sigma factor that protects its 
                     corresponding sigma factor, &sigma;<sup>28</sup> (|FRAME: 
                     EG11355-MONOMER FliA|), against degradation by the Lon 
                     protease |CITS: [17537210]|.
                     FlgM is an intrinsically disordered protein that exists in 
                     a pre-molten globule-like conformation |CITS: [23352839]|. 
                     FlgM function has been extensively studied in <i>Salmonella
                     typhimurium</i>.  FlgM is an intrinsically disordered 
                     protein that becomes structured on binding to the 
                     transcription factor &sigma;<sup>28</sup>, regulating 
                     flagellar synthesis |CITS: [9095196]|.  FlgM is produced 
                     from both the class 2 transcript of <i>flgAMN</i> and the 
                     class 3 transcript of <i>flgMN</i>.  FlgM is initially 
                     translated from its class 2, FlhDC-activated, 
                     &sigma;<sup>70</sup>-dependent transcript.  FlgM is the 
                     anti-&sigma;<sup>28</sup> factor responsible for regulation
                     of &sigma;<sup>28</sup> activity and functions in coupling 
                     of flagellar assembly to gene expression.
                     FlgM prevents &sigma;<sup>28</sup> from binding to DNA by 
                     interacting with its promoter -binding domain.  Once the 
                     hook-basal body structure of the flagellum is complete, the
                     cell becomes capable of flagellum-specific type III 
                     secretion of FlgM, and it is secreted.  This reduces the 
                     FlgM in the cytoplasm and derepresses &sigma;<sup>28</sup>,
                     which is responsible for expression of class 3 transcripts 
                     involved in the third and final phase of flagellar 
                     development.  The purpose of expressing FlgM from the class
                     3 promoter only to be secreted is predicted to be to 
                     improve motility by reducing the number and length of 
                     flagella |CITS: [11104815]|.
                     Unfortunately the source of FlgM protein used in various 
                     publications, e.g. |CITS: [9095196][9454599][12271132]|, 
                     was not reported.
                     A complex between &sigma;<sup>28</sup> and the C-terminal 
                     &sigma;<sup>28</sup>-binding fragment of FlgM has been 
                     crystallized |CITS: [17329813]|.
                     Temporal expression of <i>flgM</i> compared to other genes 
                     in the flagellar pathway has been measured |CITS: 
                     [11408658][17537210]|.  Increasing expression of 
                     <i>flgM</i> increases chemotaxis efficiency |CITS: 
                     [16306993]|; a &Delta;<i>flgM</i> mutant has larger 
                     chemotaxis receptor clusters than wild type |CITS: 
                     [18427119][18476921]|.
                     Reviews: |CITS: 
                     [7565101][9891799][11104815][14550943][24396271]|"
