     gene            complement(1125660..1126319)
                     /gene="flgA"
                     /locus_tag="b1072"
                     /label=flgA
     CDS             complement(1125660..1126319)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="flgA"
                     /locus_tag="b1072"
                     /product="flagellar basal body P-ring formation protein
                     FlgA"
                     /label=flgA
                     /note="FlgA and FlgI are required for the assembly of the 
                     flagellar P ring. Experiments with <I>Salmonella 
                     typhimurium</I> show FlgA is produced as a precursor and 
                     transported to the periplasm through the Sec pathway to 
                     assist in the assembly of the flagellar P ring. FlgA, which
                     is normally unstable, has been shown to be stabilized by 
                     the presence of FlgI, suggesting an interaction exists 
                     between the two proteins. FlgA is predicted to act as a 
                     chaperone for polymerization of FlgI onto the P ring 
                     |CITS:[10832645]|.
                     Early studies in <i>E. coli</i> K-12 identified the 
                     <i>flaU</i> gene within the region I <i>fla</i> (flagella) 
                     genes (see |CITS: [6993282]|). Incomplete flagella 
                     structures are detected in mutants with defects in 
                     <i>flaU</i> |CITS: [7007337]|. <i>flgA</i> mutants 
                     ('Ec:flgAi') are non-motile |CITS: [25816013]|. For a 
                     description of flagellar gene nomenclature, including old 
                     (<i>fla, flb</I>) and new (<i>flg, flh</i> and <i>fli</i>) 
                     symbols, see |CITS: [3070322]|.
                     The 'pole-localizer' protein |FRAME: G7087-MONOMER TmaR| 
                     protects and stabilizes <i>flgA</i> transcripts |CITS: 
                     [37934665]|."
