                     /product="trifunctional flagellar basal-body rod protein
                     FlgB / flagellar basal body / flagellum"
                     /label=flgB
                     /note="FlgB is one of four proteins that comprise the rod
                     of the flagellar basal body.
                     FlgB is best characterized in <i>Salmonella</i> Typhimurium
                     (see |CITS: [2181149][2129540][11554792][13705 
                     43][1594581][1640458][10809679][12670972][15136044][1776181
                     4][24946091]|); flagella structure, assembly and motor 
                     function are considered to be widely the same in 
                     <i>Salmonella</i> Typhimurium and <i>E. coli</i>. The FlgB 
                     proteins from these two species share 81% sequence 
                     identity.
                     Early studies in <i>E. coli</i> K-12 identified the 
                     <i>flbA</i> gene within the region I <i>fla</i> (flagella) 
                     genes (see |CITS: [330498][6993282]|). K-12 <i>flbA</i> 
                     mutants lack detectable flagellar structures when examined 
                     by electron microscscopy |CITS: [7007337]|. For a 
                     description of flagellar gene nomenclature, including old 
                     (<i>fla, flb</I>) and new (<i>flg, flh</i> and <i>fli</i>) 
                     symbols, see |CITS: [3070322]|.
                     "
