     gene            1127310..1128005
                     /gene="flgD"
                     /locus_tag="b1075"
                     /label=flgD
     CDS             1127310..1128005
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="flgD"
                     /locus_tag="b1075"
                     /product="flagellar biosynthesis, initiation of hook
                     assembly"
                     /label=flgD
                     /note="Experiments using antibodies raised against the
                     flagellar protein FlgD of <I>Salmonella typhimurium</I> 
                     have identified FlgD as a scaffold where assembly of hook 
                     proteins takes place. Immunoelectron
                     microscopy shows that once the rod is completed, FlgD is 
                     added to its end, allowing assembly of hook
                     proteins. Transport of FlgD occurs via the type III 
                     flagellar export apparatus. Once the hook is formed, the 
                     hook-filament junction proteins FlgK are added to the end 
                     and FlgD dissociates |CITS:[8157595]|.
                     Early studies in <i>E. coli</i> K-12 identified the 
                     <i>flaV</i> gene within the region I <i>fla</i> (flagella) 
                     genes (see |CITS: [330498][6993282]|). Incomplete flagella 
                     structures are detected in mutants with defects in 
                     <i>flaV</i> |CITS: [7007337]|. For a description of 
                     flagellar gene nomenclature, including old (<i>fla, 
                     flb</I>) and new (<i>flg, flh</i> and <i>fli</i>) symbols, 
                     see |CITS: [3070322]|."
                     /translation="MSIAVTTTDPTNTGVSTTSSSSLTGSNAADLQSSFLTLLVAQLKN
                     QDPTNPMENNELTSQLAQISTVSGIEKLNTTLGSISGQIDNSQSLQASNLIGHGVMIPG
