                     /gene="flgE"
                     /locus_tag="b1076"
                     /product="bifunctional flagellar hook protein FlgE /
                     flagellum"
                     /label=flgE
                     /note="FlgE is the basic subunit that polymerizes to form
                     the flexible hook structure which
                     couples the envelope-embedded flagellar rotary motor to the
                     rigid flagellar filament in
                     <I>Escherichia coli</I>.
                     Early studies in <i>E. coli</i> K-12 identified the 
                     <i>flaK</i> gene within the region I <i>fla</i> (flagella) 
                     genes (see |CITS: [330498][6993282]|). For a description of
                     flagellar gene nomenclature, including old (<i>fla, 
                     flb</I>) and new (<i>flg, flh</i> and <i>fli</i>) symbols, 
                     see |CITS: [3070322]|.
                     <i>flgE</i> exhibits mosaic evolution patterns in <i>E. 
                     coli</i> |CITS: [40444982]|."
