     gene            1129258..1130013
                     /gene="flgF"
                     /locus_tag="b1077"
                     /label=flgF
     CDS             1129258..1130013
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="flgF"
                     /locus_tag="b1077"
                     /product="trifunctional flagellar basal-body rod protein
                     FlgF / flagellar basal body / flagellum"
                     /label=flgF
                     /note="FlgF is one of four proteins that comprise the rod
                     of the flagellar basal body.
                     FlgF is best characterized in <i>Salmonella</i> Typhimurium
                     (see |CITS: [2181149][2129540][11554792][13705 
                     43][1594581][1640458][12670972][15136044][17761814][2494609
                     1]|); flagella structure, assembly and motor function are 
                     considered to be widely the same in <i>Salmonella</i> 
                     Typhimurium and <i>E. coli</i>. The FlgF proteins from 
                     these two species share 87% sequence identity.
                     Early studies in <i>E. coli</i> K-12 identified the 
                     <i>flaX</i> gene within the region I <i>fla</i> (flagella) 
                     genes (see |CITS: [330498][6993282]|). K-12 <i>flaX</i> 
                     mutants lack detectable flagellar structures when examined 
                     by electron microscscopy |CITS: [7007337]|. <i>flgF</i> 
                     mutants ('Ec:flgFi') are non-motile |CITS: [25816013]|. For
                     a description of flagellar gene nomenclature, including old
                     (<i>fla, flb</I>) and new (<i>flg, flh</i> and <i>fli</i>) 
                     symbols, see |CITS: [3070322]|.
                     "
