     CDS             1131020..1131718
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="flgH"
                     /locus_tag="b1079"
                     /product="trifunctional flagellar L-ring protein /
                     flagellar basal body / flagellum"
                     /label=flgH
                     /note="FlgH is the basic subunit which makes up the L or 
                     lipopolysaccharide ring of the flagellar basal body. The L 
                     ring lies in the plane of the outer membrane and encircles 
                     the basal body rod |CITS: [12500982]|.
                     FlgH is a verified lipoprotein according to unpublished 
                     data by S. Matsuyama et al. (cited in |CITS: [12876315]|). 
                     Early studies in <i>E. coli</i> K-12 identified the 
                     <i>flaY</i> gene within the region I <i>fla</i> (flagella) 
                     genes (see |CITS: [330498][6993282]|). Incomplete flagella 
                     structures are detected in mutants with defects in 
                     <i>flaY</i> |CITS: [7007337]|. For a description of 
                     flagellar gene nomenclature, including old (<i>fla, 
                     flb</I>) and new (<i>flg, flh</i> and <i>fli</i>) symbols, 
                     see |CITS: [3070322]|."
