     gene            1131730..1132827
                     /gene="flgI"
                     /locus_tag="b1080"
                     /label=flgI
     CDS             1131730..1132827
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="flgI"
                     /locus_tag="b1080"
                     /product="trifunctional flagellar P-ring protein /
                     flagellar basal body / flagellum"
                     /label=flgI
                     /note="FlgI is the structural component of the P
                     (peptidoglycan ring) of the flagellar basal body |CITS: 
                     [3549689][3549690]|. FlgI and FlgH (the structural 
                     component of the L ring) form the L-P ring complex which 
                     assembles around the rod and is thought to act as the 
                     molecular bushing that supports flagellar motor rotation 
                     (see |CITS: [12500982]|).
                     Our knowledge on FlgI in <i>E. coli</i> is based, in part, 
                     on characterization of the homologous protein in 
                     <i>Salmonella</i> typhimurium (see |CITS: [3549691][254456 
                     1][2047860][10049367][2407720][10832645][1594581][27273476]
                     |); the two proteins are 92% identical over their entire 
                     length.
                     <i>E. coli</i> FlgI contains an intramolecular disulfide 
                     bond; the presence of this bond does not appear to be 
                     necessary for P-ring formation but has been implicated in 
                     preventing degradation of the protein in the periplasmic 
                     space |CITS: [8503954][16740925]|. Cross-linking 
                     experiments suggest that FlgI may interact with the stator 
                     protein MotB |CITS: [20576620]|.
                     Early studies in <i>E. coli</i> K-12 identified the 
                     <i>flaM</i> gene within the region I <i>fla</i> (flagella) 
                     genes (see |CITS: [330498][6993282]|). Incomplete flagella 
                     structures are detected in mutants with defects in 
                     <i>flaM</i> |CITS: [7007337]|. <i>flaM</i> mutants are 
                     non-motile |CITS: [3549690]| (see also |CITS: [25816013]|).
                     For a description of flagellar gene nomenclature, including
                     old (<i>fla, flb</I>) and new (<i>flg, flh</i> and 
                     <i>fli</i>) symbols, see |CITS: [3070322]|.
                     "
