     CDS             1132827..1133768
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="flgJ"
                     /locus_tag="b1081"
                     /product="putative peptidoglycan hydrolase FlgJ"
                     /label=flgJ
                     /note="FlgJ has been largely characterized in
                     <i>Salmonella</i> Typhimurium where it is a bifunctional, 
                     periplasmic protein required for flagella rod assembly and 
                     possessing endo &beta;-N-acetylglucosaminidase activity; 
                     this latter activity is associated with the C-terminal 
                     region of the protein and may function to create holes in 
                     the peptidoglycan layer for flagella assembly |CITS: [2544 
                     561][8824596][10049388][11554792][12670972][25248745]|. 
                     FlgJ from <i>E. coli</i> K-12 has 83% identity with FlgJ 
                     from <i>Salmonella</i> Typhimurium.
                     The Keio collection <i>flgJ</i> mutant exhibits a 'low 
                     level' of resistance to lithium exposure |CITS: 
                     [39983623]|.
                     Early studies in <i>E. coli</i> K-12 identified the 
                     <i>flaZ</i> gene within the region I <i>fla</i> (flagella) 
                     genes (see |CITS: [330498][6993282]|). <i>flgJ</i> mutants 
                     ('Ec:flgJi') are non-motile |CITS: [25816013]|. For a 
                     description of flagellar gene nomenclature, including old 
                     (<i>fla, flb</I>) and new (<i>flg, flh</i> and <i>fli</i>) 
                     symbols, see |CITS: [3070322]|."
