                     /product="bifunctional flagellar hook-filament junction
                     protein 1 / flagellum"
                     /label=flgK
                     /note="Experiments in <I>Salmonella typhimurium</I> using 
                     antibodies against the flagellar proteins FlgK and FlgL 
                     identify them as junction proteins which connect the 
                     filament to the hook |CITS:[3546266]|.
                     Early studies in <i>E. coli</i> K-12 identified the 
                     <i>flaS</i> gene within the region I <i>fla</i> (flagella) 
                     genes (see |CITS: [330498][6993282]|). For a description of
                     flagellar gene nomenclature, including old (<i>fla, 
                     flb</I>) and new (<i>flg, flh</i> and <i>fli</i>) symbols, 
                     see |CITS: [3070322]|.
                     The 'pole-localizer' protein |FRAME: G7087-MONOMER TmaR| 
                     protects and stabilizes <i>flgK</i> transcripts |CITS: 
                     [37934665]|."
