     gene            1140396..1141355
                     /gene="rluC"
                     /locus_tag="b1086"
                     /label=rluC
     CDS             1140396..1141355
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rluC"
                     /locus_tag="b1086"
                     /product="23S rRNA pseudouridine(955/2504/2580) synthase"
                     /EC_number="5.4.99.24"
                     /label=rluC
                     /note="RluC catalyzes pseudouridylation of nucleotides
                     U955, U2504, and U2580 in 23S rRNA; all three sites are 
                     located near the peptidyl transferase center of the 
                     ribosome |CITS: [9660827][9843401]|. RluC also shows 
                     activity toward 16S rRNA <i>in vitro</i> |CITS: [9843401]|.
                     RluC associates with a pre-50S ribosomal particle |CITS: 
                     [17337586]|. A proteolytic fragment consisting of amino 
                     acids 89-319 is catalytically active |CITS: [10089432]|. 
                     The crystal structure of the C-terminal catalytic domain 
                     has been determined at 2 &Aring; resolution |CITS: 
                     [15078091]|.
                     An <i>rluC</i> mutant lacks pseudouridylation of 
                     nucleotides U955, U2504, and U2580 in 23S rRNA, but does 
                     not exhibit an obvious growth defect |CITS: 
                     [9660827][9843401]|. It was later shown that an <i>rluC</i>
                     mutant shows some cold sensitivity |CITS: [17337586]|. 
                     Insertion mutations in <i>rluC</i> suppress the 
                     cold-sensitive growth phenotype of a <i>bipA</i> deletion 
                     mutant |CITS: [18820021]|. Inactivation of <i>rluC</i> 
                     leads to increased susceptibility to antibiotics that 
                     target the peptidyl transferase center, such as 
                     clindamycin, linezolid, and tiamulin |CITS: [18554609]|. A 
                     &Delta;<i>rlmE</i> &Delta;<i>rluC</i> double mutant 
                     exhibited a 20&deg;C conditional lethal phenotype but was 
                     permissive at 37&deg;C; a lower tripeptide synthesis rate 
                     compared to the single mutations was also observed. 
                     Knocking out <i>rlmE</i> and <i>rluC</i> in combination 
                     with three other genes, <i>rlmKL</i>, <i>rlmN</i>, and 
                     <i>rlmM</i>, was viable at both temperatures but resulted 
                     in large effects on ribosome assembly and peptidyl 
                     transferase activity at 20&deg;C |CITS: [35260421]|.
                     A study that used a &Delta;10 ribosomal modification 
                     deletion strain lacking nucleoside modifications around the
                     peptidyl-transferase center (PTC) due to deletions of 
                     |FRAME: EG11118|, |FRAME: G6488|, |FRAME: EG12401|, |FRAME:
                     EG11794|, |FRAME: G6581|, |FRAME: EG12433|, |FRAME: 
                     EG11921|, |FRAME: G7845|, |FRAME: G6746| and |FRAME: 
                     EG11507| found that RlmE is the most effective at 
                     alleviating the severe growth defect phenotype of the 
                     &Delta;10 strain and that RluC's pseudouridine modification
                     activity can complement the growth defect as well as the 
                     large ribosomal subunit assembly of the RlmE-containing 
                     mutant at growth temperatures from 37 &deg;C down to 25 
                     &deg;C as determined by sucrose gradient ribosome profile 
                     assay |CITS: [38554109]|.
                     RluC: ""<b>r</b>ibosomal <b>l</b>arge subunit 
                     pseudo<b>u</b>ridine synthase <b>C</b>"" |CITS: [9660827]| 
                     Reviews: |CITS: [17113994][25616362]|"
                     /translation="MKTETPSVKIVAITADEAGQRIDNFLRTQLKGVPKSMIYRILRKG
