     CDS             complement(1141467..1142051)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yceF"
                     /locus_tag="b1087"
                     /product="m(7)GTP pyrophosphatase"
                     /label=yceF
                     /note="YceF shows triphosphatase activity with the
                     modified nucleotide 7-methyl-GTP (m<sup>7</sup>GTP) as a 
                     substrate.  The authors suggest that the <i>in vivo</i> 
                     function of YceF may be to monitor the ribonucleotide pool 
                     and prevent unspecific incorporation of modified bases into
                     cellular RNAs |CITS: [24210219]|.
                     YceF exists as a mixture of monomers and dimers in 
                     solution.  A crystal structure of the protein has been 
                     solved at 1.85 &Aring; resolution |CITS: [24210219]|. 
                     Mutations in predicted active site residues reduce the 
                     catalytic activity.  The unprotonated Asp69 residue is 
                     proposed to function as a general base that produces a 
                     nucleophilic hydroxide ion which attacks the 
                     &alpha;-phosphate of the substrate |CITS: [24210219]|.
                     "
