     CDS             1142823..1142996
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rpmF"
                     /locus_tag="b1089"
                     /product="trifunctional 50S ribosomal subunit protein L32
                     / 50S ribosomal subunit / ribosome"
                     /label=rpmF
                     /note="The L32 protein is a non-essential component of the
                     50S subunit of the ribosome.
                     L32 was found to crosslink to L17 |CITS: 
                     [1104622][2645289][2653827][2665813]| and does not appear 
                     to be exposed on the ribosomal surface |CITS: [9371771]|. 
                     L32 assembles late in the process and does not bind rRNA by
                     itself |CITS: [3298242]|, but can be crosslinked to 
                     nucleotides 2878-90 within 23S rRNA |CITS: [1702198]|.
                     L32 is located within 21 &Aring; of nucleotide C2475 of 23S
                     rRNA, near the peptidyltransferase center |CITS: 
                     [7529559]|.
                     In a &Delta;<i>rpmF</i> mutant, exposure to hydroxyurea 
                     leads to an increased membrane stress response and 
                     increased generation of reactive oxygen species |CITS: 
                     [23292777]|. The Keio collection <i>rpmF</i> mutant is 
                     sensitive to lithium (<90% growth at 200mM Li) |CITS: 
                     [39983623]|."
