     gene            1157341..1157700
                     /gene="hinT"
                     /locus_tag="b1103"
                     /label=hinT
     CDS             1157341..1157700
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="hinT"
                     /locus_tag="b1103"
                     /product="purine nucleoside phosphoramidase"
                     /label=hinT
                     /note="HinT is a purine nucleoside phosphoramidase with a 
                     preference for purine nucleoside phosphoramidates.  The 
                     enzyme is a homolog of the histidine triad 
                     nucleotide-binding proteins (Hint) |CITS: [15703176]|.
                     The presence of a phosphoramidase activity in <i>E. 
                     coli</i> was first shown by |CITS: [13832126]|.   The 
                     catalytic activity of HinT affects the activity of |FRAME: 
                     DALADEHYDROGA-MONOMER| |CITS: [21754980]|.
                     In search of the physiological substrate for HinT, it was 
                     found that HinT can be adenylated by |FRAME: LYSU-MONOMER| 
                     (LysRS) in the presence of Mg<sup>2+</sup> and lysine; the 
                     reaction is inhibited by Zn<sup>2+</sup>, Ap<sub>4</sub>A 
                     and Ap<sub>3</sub>A and enhanced by the presence of 
                     pyrophosphatase.  These experiments suggest that the 
                     lysyl-AMP intermediate that is formed by LysRS is the 
                     natural substrate for HinT |CITS: [17158446]|.
                     The substrate specificity of the enzyme has been 
                     investigated; in contrast with the human enzyme, no 
                     stereochemical preference or preference for substitution at
                     the &alpha; carboxylate was found for the <i>E. coli</i> 
                     enzyme |CITS: [17217311]|.  The divergent C-terminal loop 
                     region of the enzyme appears to be responsible for 
                     substrate specificity |CITS: [17939685]|. Crystal 
                     structures of HinT have been solved.  The C-terminal region
                     appears to be conformationally flexible |CITS: [20934431]|.
                     <i>hinT</i> is essential for growth under high salt 
                     conditions |CITS: [15703176]| and is required for growth on
                     D-alanine as the sole source of carbon and energy |CITS: 
                     [21754980]|.
                     HinT: ""<b>hi</b>stidi<b>n</b>e <b>t</b>riad 
                     nucleotide-binding protein homolog"" |CITS: [15703176]|"
