     gene            1158716..1159540
                     /gene="thiK"
                     /locus_tag="b1106"
                     /label=thiK
     CDS             1158716..1159540
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="thiK"
                     /locus_tag="b1106"
                     /product="thiamine kinase"
                     /EC_number="2.7.1.89"
                     /label=thiK
                     /note="Thiamine kinase (ThiK) catalyzes the
                     phosphorylation of the hydroxyl group of thiamin. This 
                     enzyme is a salvage enzyme and enables the cell to use 
                     recycled thiamin as an alternative to its synthesis <i>de 
                     novo</i>.
                     The <i>thiK</i> locus was mapped |CITS: [6284709]|, and the
                     <i>ycfN</i> open reading frame was identified as the 
                     structural gene encoding thiamine kinase. The gene was 
                     overexpressed as a His10-tagged protein, but the protein 
                     was present primarily in inclusion bodies, was unstable, 
                     and lost all activity during purification, although assays 
                     performed with cell extracts showed significant thiamine 
                     kinase activity |CITS: [15150256]|.
                     The Keio collection <i>thiK</i> mutant is sensitive to 
                     lithium (<90% growth at 100mM Li) |CITS: [39983623]|. 
                     Orthologs of ThiK have so far only been found in the 
                     &gamma; proteobacteria."
