     CDS             1159551..1160576
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="nagZ"
                     /locus_tag="b1107"
                     /product="beta-N-acetylglucosaminidase"
                     /label=nagZ
                     /note="&beta;-<i>N</i>-acetylglucosaminidase (NagZ) is a 
                     cytoplasmic enzyme involved in murein recycling.  NagZ is 
                     specific for hydrolysis of the &beta;-1,4 glycosidic bond, 
                     generating monosaccharides from the disaccharides released 
                     during muropeptide recycling.  The enzyme cleaves 
                     anhydromuropeptides and is also active with muropeptides 
                     |CITS: [1377][10940025][10978324]|.
                     A mutant strain lacking more than 99% of NagZ activity 
                     shows no apparent growth defect |CITS: [1107312]|.  A 
                     <i>nagZ</i> insertion mutant contains much increased 
                     amounts of the GlcNAc-&beta;-1,4-<i>anhydro</i>-MurNAc 
                     disaccharide |CITS: [10940025]|.
                     The <i>nagZ</i> mRNA was predicted to be a regulatory hub 
                     for post-transcriptional regulation by small RNAs. 
                     Overexpression of RyhB and FnrS represses translation 
                     |CITS: [23980183]|.
                     NagZ: ""&beta;-<i><b>N</b></i>-<b>a</b>cetyl<b>g</b>lucosa 
                     minidase"" |CITS: [10940025][10978324]|
                     Reviews: |CITS: [18535144][29185941]|"
