     CDS             1163055..1163594
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ycfJ"
                     /locus_tag="b1110"
                     /product="PF05433 family protein YcfJ"
                     /label=ycfJ
                     /note="YcfJ has similarity to <i>Proteus mirabilis</i>
                     UmoD, which is involved in in flagellar synthesis, 
                     swarming, and cell elongation |CITS: [9723914]|. YcfJ is 
                     predicted to be a bitopic inner membrane protein |CITS: 
                     [27510400]|.
                     Transcription of <i>ycfJ</i> is induced upon biofilm 
                     formation compared to planktonic growth in exponential 
                     phase. Induction of expression was found to be independent 
                     of the presence of the F plasmid |CITS: [14731270]|.
                     A <i>ycfJ</i> mutant is impaired in biofilm formation 
                     |CITS: [14731270]|.
                     <i>ycfJ</i> was in the top 20 genes with increased 
                     translation in response to extreme acid stress (pH 4.4 and 
                     5.8 compared to pH 7.6) and shown to have increased 
                     transcription in response to low pH, H<sub>2</sub>O 
                     oxidative stress and ethanol stress as measured by mRNA 
                     levels by RT-qPCR |CITS: [37909716]|."
