     gene            1164529..1164786
                     /gene="bhsA"
                     /locus_tag="b1112"
                     /label=bhsA
     CDS             1164529..1164786
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="bhsA"
                     /locus_tag="b1112"
                     /product="DUF1471 domain-containing multiple stress
                     resistance outer membrane protein BhsA"
                     /label=bhsA
                     /note="BhsA/ComC is a small outer membrane protein |CITS: 
                     [22089859][17293424]|, involved in biofilm formation |CITS:
                     [17293424]| and response to stress |CITS: [17293424]|. Its 
                     presence appears to reduce the permeability of the outer 
                     membrane to copper |CITS: [22089859]|.
                     Transcription of <i>bhsA</i> is induced upon biofilm 
                     formation compared to planktonic growth in exponential 
                     phase |CITS: [14731270][14727089]| and under various 
                     cellular stress conditions |CITS: 
                     [15774872][15601715][10481021][11395452][11443091]|. 
                     Induction of expression was found to be independent of the 
                     presence of the F plasmid |CITS: [14731270]|. Expression of
                     <i>comC</i> is induced 30-fold in the presence of 3mM 
                     copper in <i>E. coli</i> wild-type but is induced 
                     approximately 270-fold in a <i>comR</i> negative strain 
                     indicating that ComR represses <i>comC</i> expression in 
                     the wild type |CITS: [22089859]|.
                     A <i>comC</i> knockout strain is more sensitive to copper 
                     than the wild type |CITS: [22089859]|. Expression of the 
                     <i>cusCFBA</i> operon, encoding a copper/silver efflux 
                     system, is increased in a <i>comC</i> knockout strain, 
                     possibly due to increased copper leakage across the outer 
                     membrane |CITS: [22089859]|.
                     Different authors have reported that a <i>bhsA</i> mutant 
                     is impaired in biofilm formation |CITS: [14731270]| or 
                     shows 5-fold increased biofilm formation in LB glucose 
                     medium |CITS: [17293424]|.  This discrepancy can be 
                     explained: the <i>bhsA</i> deletion phenotype was shown to 
                     be sensitive to both incubation time and temperature and 
                     may be correlated with curli production |CITS: [17293424]|.
                     Deletion of <i>bhsA</i> induces the expression of stress 
                     response genes in biofilms, increases the sensitivity to 
                     stress, and increases aggregation and cell surface 
                     hydrophobicity |CITS: [17293424]|.
                     Based on a microarray assay to identify genes relevant to 
                     the interaction between the bacterium and lettuce plant, 
                     the <i>bhsA</i> gene, involved in biofilm modulation, was 
                     found to be significantly upregulated |CITS: [22247152]|. 
                     BhsA: ""influencing <b>b</b>iofilm through 
                     <b>h</b>ydrophobicity and <b>s</b>tress response"" |CITS: 
                     [17293424]|.<br>
                     ComC: ""<b>c</b>opper induced <b>o</b>uter <b>m</b>embrane 
                     <b>C</b>omponent"" |CITS: [22089859]|"
                     /translation="MKNVKTLIAAAILSSMSFASFAAVEVQSTPEGQQKVGTISANAGT
                     NLGSLEEQLAQKADEMGAKSFRITSVTGPNTLHGTAVIYK"
