     CDS             1170883..1172082
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="lolC"
                     /locus_tag="b1116"
                     /product="bifunctional lipoprotein release complex - inner
                     membrane subunit / lipoprotein release complex"
                     /label=lolC
                     /note="LolC is an inner membrane subunit of the LolCDE 
                     lipoprotein release complex |CITS: [10783239]|.
                     LolC contains 4 predicted transmembrane regions; a large 
                     loop region between the first and second transmembrane 
                     regions is located in the periplasm |CITS: 
                     [10783239][16585747][19809197]|. The periplasmic domain of 
                     LolC contains structural features that underpin the 
                     mechanotransmission mechanism of the type VII ABC 
                     transporter, |FRAME: MACB ""MacB""| |CITS: [29109272]|. The
                     periplasmic domain of LolC contains a 'hook' (residues P167
                     - P179) and 'pad' (R163, Q181, R182) that mediate 
                     interaction with the lipopotein chaperone |FRAME: 
                     G6465-MONOMER LolA|; the interaction between LolA and 
                     LolCDE occurs exclusively through LolC and is independent 
                     of nucleotide binding and hydrolysis; LolC discriminates 
                     between LolA and LolB |CITS: [30012603]| (see also |CITS: 
                     [33782615]|)."
