                     /locus_tag="b1126"
                     /label=potA
     CDS             complement(1179914..1181050)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="potA"
                     /locus_tag="b1126"
                     /product="trifunctional spermidine preferential ABC
                     transporter ATP binding subunit / spermidine preferential 
                     ABC transporter / putrescine/spermidine ABC transporter"
                     /EC_number="7.6.2.11"
                     /label=potA
                     /note="PotA is the ATP-binding subunit of a high affinity 
                     spermidine uptake system.
                     PotA contains signature motifs conserved in ATP-binding 
                     cassette (ABC) proteins |CITS: [1939142][9593292]|. PotA 
                     binds nucleotides with the following specificity: 
                     ATP>GTP=ADP>CTP=UTP |CITS: [8366082]|. PotA associates with
                     the membrane through its interaction with PotB and PotC; 
                     purified PotA has Mg<sup>2+</sup> dependent ATPase activity
                     which is inhibited by spermidine and spermine but not by 
                     putrescine; the C-terminal domain of PotA (residues 
                     251-378) may contain a spermidine binding site which is 
                     involved in regulation of its ATPase activity |CITS: 
                     [7592703][11976340]|. PotA is able to form dimers but each 
                     PotA subunit appears to function independently (no 
                     cooperativity for ATP during ATP hydrolysis) |CITS: 
                     [11976340]|"
                     /translation="MGQSKKLNKQPSSLSPLVQLAGIRKCFDGKEVIPQLDLTINNGEF
