     gene            complement(1187446..1188087)
                     /gene="hflD"
                     /locus_tag="b1132"
                     /label=hflD
     CDS             complement(1187446..1188087)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="hflD"
                     /locus_tag="b1132"
                     /product="lysogenization regulator"
                     /label=hflD
                     /note="<I>hflD</I> encodes an inner membrane-associated
                     protein that directly interacts with protein CII of 
                     bacteriophage &lambda;, making it more vulnerable to 
                     proteolysis by FtsH |CITS: [11278968]| and inhibiting DNA 
                     binding of CII |CITS: [19853572]|, thus leading to 
                     decreased lysogenization frequency of &lambda; |CITS: 
                     [11278968]|.  What role HflD may have in the uninfected 
                     host is as yet unknown |CITS: [11278968]|.
                     An <i>hflD</i> mutant shows increased &lambda; 
                     CII-dependent transcription, and thus an increased 
                     frequency of lysogenization |CITS: [11278968]|. The Keio 
                     collection <i>hflD</i> mutant exhibits a 'low level' of 
                     resistance to lithium exposure |CITS: [39983623]|.
                     HflD: ""<b>h</b>igh <b>f</b>requency 
                     <b>l</b>ysogenization"" |CITS: [11278968]|"
