     gene            complement(1189754..1190407)
                     /gene="rluE"
                     /locus_tag="b1135"
                     /label=rluE
     CDS             complement(1189754..1190407)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rluE"
                     /locus_tag="b1135"
                     /product="23S rRNA pseudouridine(2457) synthase"
                     /EC_number="5.4.99.20"
                     /label=rluE
                     /note="RluE is the pseudouridine synthase that catalyzes 
                     formation of the universally conserved pseudouridine at 
                     position 2457 in the peptidyltransferase center of 23S 
                     rRNA. RluE belongs to the RsuA family of RNA pseudouridine 
                     synthases |CITS: [11720289]|.
                     Crystal structures of the full-length protein and the 
                     C-terminal catalytic domain have been solved at 1.6 and 1.2
                     &Aring; resolution, respectively. The conserved active site
                     residue Asp79 is essential for activity |CITS: [11720289]|.
                     RluE interacts with the H89 helix and its single-stranded 
                     flanking regions within 23S rRNA; specific regions within 
                     RluE that are involved in rRNA interactions as well as 
                     additional active site residues were identified by 
                     mutagenesis |CITS: [29555553]|.
                     An <i>rluE</i> null mutant exhibits no obvious growth 
                     defect |CITS: [11720289]|.
                     A 20&deg;C conditional lethal with 37&deg;C permissive 
                     phenotype occurred for a &Delta;<i>rluE</i> &Delta;|FRAME: 
                     EG11118 ""<i>rluC</i>""| double mutant along with a lower 
                     tripeptide synthesis rate compared to the single mutations.
                     Double knockout mutants of <i>rluE</i> in combination with 
                     three 23S ribosomal RNA methyltransferase genes, |FRAME: 
                     G6488|, |FRAME: EG11794| and |FRAME: EG12401|, were viable 
                     at both temperatures but resulted in large defects in 
                     ribosome assembly and peptidyl transferase activity at 
                     20&deg;C |CITS: [35260421]|. Reviews: |CITS: 
                     [17113994][25616362]|"
                     /translation="MRQFIISENTMQKTSFRNHQVKRFSSQRSTRRKPENQPTRVILFN
