     CDS             1205141..1205695
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="pinE"
                     /locus_tag="b1158"
                     /product="bifunctional e14 prophage; site-specific DNA
                     recombinase / recombinase"
                     /label=pinE
                     /note="Pin is a site-specific DNA recombinase that is a
                     part of the
                     e14 prophage element.
                     Pin is a site-specific DNA recombinase, similar to the Gin 
                     recombinase
                     of phage Mu. It is responsible for the inversion of the P 
                     region,
                     an adjacent chunk of DNA containing |FRAME: EG12877|, 
                     |FRAME: G6598|, |FRAME: EG11120| and
                     |FRAME: G6599| |CITS: [6310572][3891522][3894006]|.
                     Pin is part of e14, a UV-excisable element that is probably
                     the remains
                     of a prophage |CITS: [6233259][6998954]|.
                     Pin allows phase variation when <i>Salmonella</i> H1 and H2
                     regions
                     are artificially introduced into <i>E. coli</i> |CITS: 
                     [6355064]|."
