     gene            complement(1207136..1207459)
                     /gene="iraM"
                     /locus_tag="b1160"
                     /label=iraM
     CDS             complement(1207136..1207459)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="iraM"
                     /locus_tag="b1160"
                     /product="anti-adaptor protein IraM"
                     /label=iraM
                     /note="IraM is one of several small anti-adaptor proteins.
                     In response to Mg<sup>2+</sup> starvation, IraM inhibits 
                     proteolysis of the stationary phase sigma factor |FRAME: 
                     RPOS-MONOMER &sigma;<sup>S</sup>| by interacting with 
                     |FRAME: EG12121-MONOMER RssB|, which would normally target 
                     &sigma;<sup>S</sup> for degradation by the ClpXP protease 
                     |CITS: [18383615]|.  Each anti-adaptor protein interacts 
                     with RssB in a unique way |CITS: [24352426][25988182]|. 
                     <i>iraM</i> expression is induced during 
                     Mg<sup>2+</sup>/Ca<sup>2+</sup> starvation; regulation is 
                     dependent on PhoP |CITS: [18383615]|.  H-NS inhibits the 
                     expression of <i>iraM</i> |CITS: [22408168]|.
                     When placed on a multicopy plasmid, <i>iraM</i> creates a 
                     mutator phenotype |CITS: [15225322]|.  Expression of 
                     <i>iraM</i> is induced 40-fold upon exposure of cells to 
                     the biocide polyhexamehtylene biguanide (PHMB). 
                     Overexpression of <i>iraM</i> decreases the MIC of PHMB 
                     |CITS: [16549663]|.  IraM contributes to acid resistance 
                     via activation by the EvgSA two-component system and SafA 
                     |CITS: [21193607]|.
                     <i>iraM</i> was identified in a mutant screen designed to 
                     identify genes involved in the biosynthesis of isopentenyl 
                     diphosphate, a precursor of isoprenoids, and improving 
                     heterologous lycopene biosynthesis |CITS: 
                     [9603997][17509919]|.
                     ElbA: ""<b>e</b>nhancing <b>l</b>ycopene 
                     <b>b</b>iosynthesis"" |CITS: [9603997]|
                     IraM: ""<b>i</b>nhibitor of <b>R</b>ssB <b>a</b>ctivity in 
                     response to <b>m</b>agnesium starvation"" |CITS: 
                     [18383615]|
                     Review: |CITS: [31197038]|"
