     gene            complement(1209720..1210931)
                     /gene="bluF"
                     /locus_tag="b1163"
                     /label=bluF
     CDS             complement(1209720..1210931)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="bluF"
                     /locus_tag="b1163"
                     /product="blue light- and temperature-regulated
                     antirepressor BluF"
                     /label=bluF
                     /note="The N-terminal domain of BluF is a member of the
                     family of blue-light sensing proteins that use FAD. BluF 
                     interacts directly with the MerR-like transcription factor 
                     |FRAME: G6602-MONOMER BluR| and interferes with binding of 
                     BluR to the <i>ycgZ</i> promoter in a blue light-dependent 
                     manner |CITS: [19240136]|.
                     The C-terminal EAL domain of BluF is degenerate; the 
                     protein does not bind cyclic di-guanosine monophosphate 
                     (c-di-GMP) and does not have c-di-GMP phosphodiesterase 
                     activity |CITS: [19240136]|. Re-introduction of consensus 
                     amino acids of other EAL domain proteins does not restore 
                     phosphodiesterase activity and reduces the ability of BluF 
                     to antagonize BluR |CITS: [22783906]|. BluF also interacts 
                     directly with the C-terminal domain of the transcriptional 
                     activator MlrA |CITS: [22783906]|.
                     Overexpressed and purified BluF contains FAD |CITS: 
                     [9857073]|. The protein undergoes a reversible photocycle 
                     after exposure to light |CITS: [15453820]|. FTIR difference
                     spectra reveal light-induced structural changes of the BluF
                     protein |CITS: [16533062]|. Photoexcitation leads to 
                     dimerization of BluF |CITS: [17489591]|. Structural changes
                     in the BLUF domain are extremely temperature-dependent and 
                     are influenced by the joining helix between the BLUF and 
                     EAL domains of the protein |CITS: [18792053]|. The 
                     conformation change after dimerization is predominantly 
                     localized to the EAL domain. Temperature sensitivity of the
                     photoreaction and dimer formation suggests that BluF may 
                     also function as a temperature sensor |CITS: [20141167]|.
                     Expression of <i>bluF</i> is strongly increased by growth 
                     at 16&deg;C |CITS: [14527658][19240136]|; the increase is 
                     dependent on Pnp |CITS: [14527658]|. Expression of 
                     <i>bluF</i> in liquid medium is not 
                     &sigma;<sup>S</sup>-dependent |CITS: [19332833]|.
                     Blrp: ""<b>b</b>lue <b>l</b>ight-<b>r</b>egulated 
                     <b>p</b>hosphodiesterase"" |CITS: [15453820]|
                     BluF: ""<b>b</b>lue <b>l</b>ight-<b>u</b>sing 
                     <b>F</b>AD-EAL protein""
                     Review: |CITS: [25229449][37339911]|"
