     gene            1212784..1214307
                     /gene="pdeG"
                     /locus_tag="b1168"
                     /label=pdeG
     CDS             1212784..1214307
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="pdeG"
                     /locus_tag="b1168"
                     /product="putative cyclic di-GMP phosphodiesterase PdeG"
                     /label=pdeG
                     /note="PdeG is a predicted c-di-GMP phosphodiesterase.
                     PdeG is predicted to contain two transmembrane domains 
                     which flank a periplasmic CSS domain containing two highly 
                     conserved cysteines, followed by a cytoplasmic C-terminal 
                     EAL domain with predicted phosphodiesterase activity |CITS:
                     [26148715][29514851]|. PdeG consistently copurifies with 
                     the degradosome |CITS: [16139413]|.
                     PdeG is one of 5 CSS domain containing c-di-GMP 
                     phosphodiesterases in <i>E. coli</i> K-12; redox control 
                     and proteolysis of these enzymes is believed to modulate 
                     their activity and affect matrix production in biofilm (see
                     |CITS: [29514851]|).
                     No expression of <i>pdeG</i> was seen during growth in LB 
                     |CITS: [19332833]|. PdeG is present at very low levels in 
                     wild-type cells grown in tryptone broth at 37 &deg;C and is
                     absent in &Delta;<i>pdeH</i> cells |CITS: [26553851]|. 
                     PdeG: ""<b>p</b>hospho<b>d</b>i<b>e</b>sterase <b>G</b>"" 
                     |CITS: [26148715]|"
