     gene            1214439..1214657
                     /gene="ymgF"
                     /locus_tag="b4520"
                     /label=ymgF
     CDS             1214439..1214657
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ymgF"
                     /locus_tag="b4520"
                     /product="division septum component YmgF"
                     /label=ymgF
                     /note="YmgF is an inner membrane protein with two
                     transmembrane domains; both the N- and the C-terminus are 
                     located in the cytoplasm. YmgF interacts with the cell 
                     division proteins FtsI, FtsN and FtsQ |CITS: [15774864]| as
                     well as other components of the cell division machinery 
                     |CITS: [18978050]|, and it localizes to the septum during 
                     cell division. This localization is dependent on FtsZ, 
                     FtsA, FtsQ and FtsN |CITS: [18978050]|. The N-terminal part
                     of the protein may be required for dimerization and for its
                     interactions with cell division proteins |CITS: 
                     [18978050]|.
                     YmgF is not essential for viability. In low osmolarity 
                     medium, overexpression of <i>ymgF</i> can partially rescue 
                     the growth defect of the <i>ftsQ</i>1(ts) mutant |CITS: 
                     [18978050]|.
                     Expression of <i>ymgF</i> has been detected under standard 
                     growth conditions |CITS: [18978050]|. Expression of 
                     <i>ymgF</i> was significantly though oppositely affected by
                     mioC and gidA, two genes which flank oriC |CITS: 
                     [26074904]|."
