                     /product="inhibitor of g-type lysozyme"
                     /label=pliG
                     /note="The PliG protein inhibits activity of g-type
                     lysozyme <i>in vitro</i> |CITS: [20734102]|. <i>pliG</i> 
                     deletion mutants show increased sensitivity to g-type 
                     lysozyme in the presence of EDTA |CITS: [20734102]|. PliG 
                     contains a conserved bacterial prepeptidase C terminal 
                     (PPC) domain |CITS: [20734102]|. Structural and mutational 
                     data has identified a putative lysozyme interaction 
                     interface |CITS: [22634186]|.
                     Targeting of YcgK to the Sec-translocase for transport 
                     across the inner membrane is SecB-dependent 
                     |CITS:[16352602]|.
                     <i>pliG</i>: <U>p</U>eriplasmic <U>l</U>ysozme 
                     <U>i</U>nhibitor of <U>g</U>-type lysozyme |CITS: 
