                     /locus_tag="b1180"
                     /label=ycgM
     CDS             1223535..1224194
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ycgM"
                     /locus_tag="b1180"
                     /product="bifunctional oxaloacetate tautomerase / OAA
                     tautomerase"
                     /EC_number="5.3.2.2"
                     /label=ycgM
                     /note="This protein belongs to a highly conserved 
                     fumarylacetoacetate hydrolase domain (FAHD)-containing 
                     protein family that carries out oxaloacetate (OAA) 
                     tautomerase (OAT) activity, which can run in reverse to 
                     convert enol-OAA to keto-OAA, thus removing the enol-OAA 
                     inhibition of |FRAME: CPLX0-8160| (SDH) within the |FRAME: 
                     TCA| |CITS: [38287013]|.
                     A <i>&Delta;ycgM</i> mutant showed significant growth 
                     defects and small cell size phenotypes relative to 
                     wild-type strains, whereas a double mutant with the 
                     catalytic subunit, |FRAME: EG10931|, resulted in a similar 
                     phenotype that was less severe because the SDH couldn't 
                     form the SDH inhibitor, enol-OAA. Metabolic profiling 
                     results are consistent with SDH inhibition of the TCA cycle
                     and with YcgM being a metabolite repair enzyme |CITS: 
                     [38287013]|."
