     gene            complement(1227956..1228486)
                     /gene="dsbB"
                     /locus_tag="b1185"
                     /label=dsbB
     CDS             complement(1227956..1228486)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="dsbB"
                     /locus_tag="b1185"
                     /product="protein thiol:quinone oxidoreductase DsbB"
                     /EC_number="1.8.5.9"
                     /label=dsbB
                     /note="DsbB is a protein thiol:quinone oxidoreductase that 
                     functions within a pathway for protein disulfide bond 
                     formation; DsbB catalyses the oxidation of DsbA via the 
                     reduction of membrane quinones; DsbB, in conjunction with 
                     membrane quinones generates disulfide bonds <i>de novo</i> 
                     and is considered to be a disulfide bond manufacturer 
                     within <i>E. coli</i> K-12 (reviewed in |CITS: [11967064][ 
                     19567379]|).
                     DsbB null mutants (<i>dsbB</i>::kan5) synthesize OmpA and 
                     &beta;-lactamase proteins that are deficient in disulfide 
                     bonds and this defect can be rescued by supplementation 
                     with cystine or oxidized glutathione; DsbA is present in 
                     the fully reduced state in DsbB null mutants |CITS: 
                     [8430071]| (see also |CITS: [7688471]|). <i>dsb</i> mutant 
                     strains (&Delta;<i>dsbB</i>, &Delta;<i>dsbA</i> and 
                     &Delta;<i>dsbAB</i>) have unimpaired growth under aerobic 
                     conditions but show a severe growth defect under anaerobic 
                     conditions which can be suppressed by supplementation with 
                     cystine |CITS: [28559299]|. The |FRAME: Polysulfides 
                     polysulfide| compound, octasulfur, can complement the 
                     anaerobic growth defect of a <i>dsbB</i> deletion mutant 
                     |CITS: [39918318]|.
                     DsbB is an inner membrane protein containing 4 
                     transmembrane regions and two periplasmic loops; DsbB 
                     contains 6 cysteine residues, including two essential pairs
                     (Cys41-Cys44 and Cys104-Cys130) which are implicated in 
                     protein disulfide bond formation |CITS: 
                     [7688471][7957076]|. DsbB forms a mixed disulfide with DsbA
                     |CITS: [7568240][7615498][9140064]|; DsbB oxidizes the the 
                     reduced form of DsbA using the oxidative power of membrane 
                     quinones |CITS: [9342327][10428033][10854438]|. The 
                     mechanism of electron transfer from DsbA to DsbB (an 
                     energetically unfavourable reaction), within DsbB and from 
                     DsbB to quinones has been widely investigated using 
                     biochemical, genetic and structural approaches |CITS:[1006 
                     4586][11005861][12072444][12853466][15347648][14634016][171
                     10337][16384917][17267399 
                     ][18922471][19214188][23416557][24145032]| <i>dsbB</i> 
                     shows differential codon adaptation, resulting in 
                     differential translation efficiency signatures, in 
                     thermophilic microbes. It was therefore predicted to play a
                     role in the heat shock response.  A <i>dsbB</i> deletion 
                     mutant was shown to be slightly more sensitive than 
                     wild-type specifically to heat shock, but not other 
                     stresses |CITS: [24580753]|.
                     Reviews: |CITS: [7830566][10535729][19567379][20367276]|"
