     gene            complement(1228632..1230173)
                     /gene="nhaB"
                     /locus_tag="b1186"
                     /label=nhaB
     CDS             complement(1228632..1230173)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="nhaB"
                     /locus_tag="b1186"
                     /product="bifunctional Na(+):H(+) antiporter NhaB /
                     Na(+):H(+) antiporter"
                     /label=nhaB
                     /note="<i>nhaB</i> encodes a Na<sup>+</sup>:H<sup>+</sup> 
                     antiporter |CITS: [1655717][1317851][8093613]| implicated 
                     in alkaline pH homeostasis. <i>E. coli</i> contains other 
                     transporters which mediate active proton uptake for 
                     alkaline pH homeostasis including |FRAME: CPLX0-7629 
                     ""NhaA""| (the prominent Na<sup>+</sup>:H<sup>+</sup> 
                     antiporter), |FRAME: CHAA-MONOMER ""ChaA""|, |FRAME: 
                     CMR-MONOMER ""MdfA""| and |FRAME:  YJIO-MONOMER ""MdtM""|, 
                     each of which may function under varying conditions of 
                     external pH and cation composition (see |CITS: 
                     [16277975][23701827]|)
                     Purified, reconstituted NhaB is an electrogenic antiporter 
                     with a stoichiometry of 3H<sup>+</sup>:2Na<sup>+</sup> 
                     |CITS: [7929345]|. NhaB also contributes to Li<sup>+</sup> 
                     export (Li<sup>+</sup>:H<sup>+</sup> antiport) at high 
                     external Li<sup>+</sup> concentrations (0.2 M LiCl) 
                     |CITS:[8019504]|.
                     The <i>E. coli</i> K-12 mutant strain EP432 
                     (&Delta;<i>nhaA</i> &Delta;<i>nhaB</i>) is Na<sup>+</sup> 
                     sensitive and membrane vesicles isolated from this strain 
                     lack Na<sup>+</sup>:H<sup>+</sup> antiporter activity 
                     |CITS: [7876124]| (see also |CITS: [8093613]|). The <i>E. 
                     coli</i> K-12 mutant strain KNabc (&Delta;<i>nhaA</i> 
                     &Delta;<i>nhaB</i> &Delta;<i>chaA</i>) cannot export 
                     Na<sup>+</sup> and is unable to grow in the presence of of 
                     0.2 M NaCl (or 10 mM LiCl); membrane vesicles prepared from
                     KNabc cells do not show any Na<sup>+</sup>:H<sup>+</sup> 
                     antiporter activity |CITS: [8651921]|.  Characterization of
                     mutant strains containing varying combinations of NhaA, 
                     NhaB and ChaA is also reported in |CITS: 
                     [8021217][9518629]|) (and further |CITS: 
                     [9845336][10652103][23701827]|). NhaB may be the 
                     constitutive Na<sup>+</sup>:H<sup>+</sup> antiporter |CITS:
                     [9518629]|
                     NhaB is an inner membrane protein with 12 predicted 
                     transmembrane segments |CITS:[1317851]|.
                     Under oxygen limitation <I>nhaB</I> expression shows a 
                     complex response to pH; under aerobic conditions expression
                     is highest at acid pH (5.7) |CITS: [17026754]|. Related 
                     reviews:  |CITS:[7823039]|
                     "
