     gene            complement(1235791..1237527)
                     /gene="cvrA"
                     /locus_tag="b1191"
                     /label=cvrA
     CDS             complement(1235791..1237527)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="cvrA"
                     /locus_tag="b1191"
                     /product="putative K(+):H(+) antiporter"
                     /label=cvrA
                     /note="CvrA (formerly YcgO) belongs to the Monovalent 
                     Cation:Proton Antiporter-1 (CPA1) Family - members of which
                     typically catalyse Na<sup>+</sup>:H<sup>+</sup> antiport 
                     |CITS: [24225317]|. CvrA has been implicated in 
                     K<sup>+</sup> efflux and may function as a 
                     K<sup>+</sup>:H<sup>+</sup> antiporter with a role in 
                     adaptive stress relief |CITS: [27137496]|.
                     YcgO is not involved in respiration-driven Na<sup>+</sup> 
                     transport; Na<sup>+</sup> export is not affected in a 
                     &Delta;<i>ycgO</i> strain |CITS: [11700351]|. A 
                     &Delta;<i>ycgO</i> strain is sensitive to low osmolarity; 
                     growth inhibition is observed in low salt media. A 
                     &Delta;<i>ycgO</i> strain has disrupted alkali cation 
                     transport when grown at low osmolarity; a 
                     &Delta;<i>ycgO</i> strain has decreased intracellular 
                     K<sup>+</sup> levels when grown at low osmolarity |CITS: 
                     [11700351]|.
                     Deletion of <i>cvrA</i> suppresses the potassium sensitive 
                     phenotype of a &Delta;<i>ptsN</i> strain; overproduction of
                     CvrA results in a potassium sensitive phenotype that is 
                     similar to that of the &Delta;<i>ptsN</i> strain; the 
                     potassium sensitive phenotype in both cases is associated 
                     with decreased intracellular potassium content. The 
                     &Delta;<i>cvrA</i> strain yields a phenotype only in a 
                     &Delta;<i>ptsN</i> background suggesting that <i>cvrA</i> 
                     may be cryptic under most conditions. Crypticity of 
                     <i>cvrA</i> may be maintained by PtsN (likely in the 
                     dephosphorylated form) |CITS: [27137496]|.
                     CvrA orthologs in <i>Vibrio</i> spp. have been 
                     characterized as K<sup>+</sup>:H<sup>+</sup> antiporters 
                     (see |CITS: [27137496]|).
                     <i>cvrA</i>: <u>c</u>ell <u>v</u>olume <u>r</u>egulation 
                     |CITS: [11700351]|
                     "
