     gene            complement(1244581..1245213)
                     /gene="dhaL"
                     /locus_tag="b1199"
                     /label=dhaL
     CDS             complement(1244581..1245213)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="dhaL"
                     /locus_tag="b1199"
                     /product="bifunctional dihydroxyacetone kinase subunit L / 
                     dihydroxyacetone kinase"
                     /EC_number="2.7.1.121"
                     /label=dhaL
                     /note="DhaL is similar to the C-terminal half of the 
                     ATP-dependent dihydroxyacetone kinase of <i>Citrobacter 
                     freundii</i> and eukaryotes |CITS: 
                     [11021910][11158340][11350937]|.  DhaL contains bound ADP 
                     which is transiently phosphorylated as a cofactor in the 
                     kinase reaction |CITS: [15753087]|.
                     Crystal structures of the DhaL-ADP complex |CITS: 
                     [16647083]| and the DhaK-DhaL complex |CITS: [21209328]| 
                     have been solved.  The proximity of the DHA-binding site in
                     DhaK and the ADP/ATP-binding site in DhaL is consistent 
                     with a direct transfer of the &gamma;-phosphate from ATP to
                     the &gamma;-hydroxyl group of DHA |CITS: [21209328]|. 
                     ADP-bound DhaL is a coactivator of |FRAME: G6628-MONOMER 
                     DhaR|, the transcription factor that controls expression of
                     the <i>dhaKLM</i> operon |CITS: [15616579]|.  A crystal 
                     structure of DhaL bound to DhaR has been solved.  Via a 
                     surface that overlaps with its DhaK-interacting region, 
                     DhaL interacts with the GAF-like domain and the connecting 
                     helix of DhaR, leading to conformational changes in DhaR 
                     |CITS: [24440518]|.  The DhaR-DhaL interaction is 
                     significantly stronger than the DhaR-DhaK interaction 
                     |CITS: [24440518]|.
                     The levels of DhaK and DhaL are increased in a <i>ptsI</i> 
                     mutant |CITS: [11158340]|.
                     DhaL: ""<b>d</b>i<b>h</b>ydroxy<b>a</b>cetone"" |CITS: 
                     [11350937]|
                     Review: |CITS: [16505971]|"
