     gene            1261550..1262383
                     /gene="prmC"
                     /locus_tag="b1212"
                     /label=prmC
     CDS             1261550..1262383
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="prmC"
                     /locus_tag="b1212"
                     /product="protein-(glutamine-N(5)) methyltransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.1.1.297"
                     /label=prmC
                     /note="PrmC is a protein-(glutamine-<i>N</i><sup>5</sup>) 
                     methyltransferase that methylates |FRAME: EG10761-MONOMER| 
                     (RF1) and |FRAME: EG10762-MONOMER| at their GGQ motifs 
                     |CITS: [11805295][11847124]|.  Methylation of these release
                     factors increases termination efficiency |CITS: 
                     [17932046]|.
                     The PrmC/HemK family of proteins shows similarity to the 
                     gamma subfamily of S-adenosyl-methionine-dependent 
                     adenine-specific DNA methyltransferases |CITS: [10690633]|.
                      A crystal structure of PrmC is reported at 3.2 &Aring; 
                     resolution |CITS: [15223314]|.  The C terminus contains a 
                     number of conserved residues surrounding the AdoHcy binding
                     site |CITS: [15223314]|.  The N-terminal domain was 
                     suggested to determine methyltransferase substrate 
                     specificity |CITS: [10690633]| and shows structural 
                     similarity to a number of protein-interacting domains 
                     |CITS: [15223314]|.  The crystal structure of a complex 
                     between RF1 and PrmC shows that the N-terminal domain 
                     interacts with both the GGQ motif and the central domain of
                     RF1 |CITS: [16364916]|.
                     The N-terminal domain of PrmC was used as a model substrate
                     to study co-translational protein folding |CITS: 
                     [26612953]|.
                     A mutant shows a defect in nonsense codon recognition 
                     |CITS: [11805295]| and a growth defect |CITS: 
                     [7883187][11805295][11847124]| that is suppressed by 
                     mutations in <i>prfB</i> |CITS: [11805295][11847124]|. 
                     <i>prmC</i> (<i>hemK</i>) was initially isolated as a 
                     suppressor of the light-sensitive phenotype of a 
                     <i>hemH</i> mutant and thought to encode a putative 
                     protoporphyrinogen oxidase |CITS: [7883187]|.  A mutant 
                     exhibits a global transcription pattern characteristic of 
                     anaerobic growth, which may decrease oxidative stress 
                     |CITS: [11805295]| and may therefore account for the 
                     genetic results originally thought to be indicative of a 
                     PrmC role in heme synthesis |CITS: [7883187]|.
                     PrmC: ""<b>pr</b>otein <b>m</b>ethylation"" |CITS: 
                     [11847124]|
                     Review: |CITS: [11830650]|
                     "
