                     /product="putative antisense regulatory RNA RdlA"
                     /note="<i>rdlA</i> is one of a set of four <i>rdl</i>
                     genes, one of which (<i>rdlD</i>) has been shown to code 
                     for the antisense regulatory RNA component of a 
                     toxin-antitoxin pair.  All of the <i>rdl</i> genes are 
                     associated with a matched <i>ldr</i> gene |CITS: 
                     [12123448]|.  cDNA clones of RdlA RNA have been obtained 
                     |CITS: [15718303]|.
                     RdlA interacts with the protein |FRAME: 
                     EG12866-MONOMER||CITS: [36328526]|.
                     Review: |CITS: [32213244]|"
