     CDS             1279060..1280598
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="narH"
                     /locus_tag="b1225"
                     /product="multifunctional nitrate reductase A subunit beta
                     / nitrate reductase A / menaquinol:nitrate oxidoreductase /
                     ubiquinol:nitrate oxidoreductase / tellurite reductase"
                     /EC_number="1.7.5.1"
                     /label=narH
                     /note="The &beta; subunit (NarH) of nitrate reductase A
                     contains 4 iron-sulfur clusters - one [3Fe-4S] cluster 
                     (FS4) and three
                     [4Fe-4S] clusters (FS1, FS2 and FS3) |CITS: [2985594] 
                     [2674654] [12910261]|. FS1, FS2 and FS3 are coordinated by 
                     4 cysteine residues and FS4 is coordinated by 3 cysteine 
                     residues (reviewed by |CITS: [11289300]|.
                     NarH and NarG are significantly upregulated in a 
                     &Delta;|FRAME: CPLX0-245 Ahp| strain compared to wild type 
                     and redox proteomics indicates that cysteine sites in 
                     peptides (NarH<sub>Cys-217</sub>/NarG<sub>Cys-292</sub>) 
                     are significantly reduced |CITS: [37725887]|.
                     <i>nar</i>: <U>n</U>itr<U>a</U>te <U>r</U>eductase; 
                     <i>chl</i>: <U>ch</U>lorate resistant |CITS: [7047497]|"
