     gene            1280595..1281305
                     /gene="narJ"
                     /locus_tag="b1226"
                     /label=narJ
     CDS             1280595..1281305
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="narJ"
                     /locus_tag="b1226"
                     /product="nitrate reductase 1 molybdenum cofactor assembly 
                     chaperone"
                     /label=narJ
                     /note="NarJ is part of the redox enzyme maturation protein 
                     (REMP) family of chaperones |CITS: [15213747]|.  NarJ acts 
                     as a private chaperone during the incorporation of the 
                     molybdenum cofactor into NarG, the &alpha; subunit of 
                     |FRAME: NITRATREDUCTA-CPLX| |CITS: 
                     [8793883][9305880][9632249][15247236]|, coordinating the 
                     final assembly and cofactor acquisition of nitrate 
                     reductase A.
                     NarJ, encoded by the third gene in the <i>narGHJI</i> 
                     operon, is not part of the final nitrate reductase A 
                     enzyme, but is essential for nitrate reductase activity 
                     |CITS: [3053688][1545706][1732220]|.  NarJ interacts with 
                     the NarG subunit of the apoenzyme complex at two distinct 
                     sites.  One site is located at the N terminus of NarG and 
                     interferes with membrane anchoring of the complex |CITS: 
                     [16286471][16540088][20236317]|, while the second site is 
                     involved in the insertion of the molybdenum cofactor, which
                     precedes membrane anchoring |CITS: [16286471]|.  The 
                     interaction between NarJ and NarG induces a conformational 
                     change within NarJ |CITS: [20236317]|.
                     In a <i>narJ</i> mutant, nitrate reductase A does not 
                     contain the MoCo cofactor |CITS: [9632249]|, the FS0 
                     iron-sulfur cluster of the NarG subunit, or the heme 
                     <i>b</i> cofactor |CITS: [17442677]|.
                     Review: |CITS: [15213747]|"
