     gene            1281305..1281982
                     /gene="narI"
                     /locus_tag="b1227"
                     /label=narI
     CDS             1281305..1281982
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="narI"
                     /locus_tag="b1227"
                     /product="multifunctional nitrate reductase A subunit
                     gamma / nitrate reductase A / menaquinol:nitrate 
                     oxidoreductase / ubiquinol:nitrate oxidoreductase / 
                     tellurite reductase"
                     /EC_number="1.7.5.1"
                     /label=narI
                     /note="The &gamma; subunit (NarI) of nitrate reductase A
                     is a membrane-embedded heme-iron subunit resembling 
                     cytochrome b, which transfers electrons from the quinone 
                     pool to the &beta; subunit (NarH).  There are two hemes 
                     present, a low-potential heme <i>b</i><sub>L</sub> and a 
                     high-potential heme <i>b</i><sub>H</sub> |CITS: [HACKETT82]
                     [9325288] [10504245]|. Electrons are thought to transfer 
                     from the quinol binding site (Q-site) via heme 
                     <i>b</i><sub>L</sub> and heme <i>b</i><sub>H</sub> to the 
                     [3Fe-4S] cluster of NarH |CITS: [9556558], [11318649]|. The
                     Q-site of Nar is periplasmically oriented |CITS: 
                     [15615728]|. NarI contains 5 transmembrane helices; the 
                     first helix appears to facilitate dimer formation. A 
                     C-terminal tail interacts with both NarG and NarH. The two 
                     Fe atoms are coordinated by histidine groups - His 56 and 
                     His 205 coordinate heme <i>b</i><sub>H</sub>, His66 and His
                     187 coordinate heme <i>b</i><sub>L</sub>. NarI contains an 
                     elongated hydrophobic cavity which may provide a protected 
                     interaction site for quinones |CITS: [9325288],[12910261]|.
                     Reviews: |CITS: [11321583]|"
                     /translation="MQFLNMFFFDIYPYIAGAVFLIGSWLRYDYGQYTWRAASSQMLDR
