                     /locus_tag="b4595"
                     /product="uncharacterized protein YciY"
                     /label=yciY
                     /note="A <i>yciY</i> mRNA of ~250 nt length has been
                     detected.  <i>yciY</i> is expressed during exponential 
                     phase in both rich and minimal medium |CITS: [11445539]|. 
                     The <i>yciY</i> gene described in |CITS: [11445539]| lies 
                     in the <i>clsA</i>-<i>kch</i> intergenic region; the 
                     precise position was not reported.  Position information 
                     was obtained from EcoGene."
                     /translation="MKRSRTEVGRWRMQRQASRRKSRWLEGQSRRNMRIHSIRKCILNK
                     QRNSLLFAIYNI"
     gene            complement(1303273..1304526)
                     /gene="kch"
                     /locus_tag="b1250"
                     /label=kch
     CDS             complement(1303273..1304526)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="kch"
                     /locus_tag="b1250"
                     /product="bifunctional K(+) channel Kch / voltage-gated
                     K(+) channel"
                     /label=kch
                     /note="Kch is a member of the Voltage-gated Ion Channel
                     (VIC) Superfamily of transporters |CITS: [7520590]|. The 
                     regulation and functional properties of the protein have 
                     not been extensively studied; however, comparisons have 
                     often been made between Kch and the eukaryotic potassium 
                     channel proteins |CITS: [9657392][8824224][8170937]|.
                     Kch was solubilized and purified, and the biochemical 
                     properties and structure of the protein were examined 
                     |CITS: [9657392][11606201]|. The physiological state of Kch
                     is believed to be homotetrameric |CITS: [11606201]|. Kch 
                     was shown to contain an interacting sequence tag 
                     corresponding to the oligomerization domain of the protein 
                     providing more evidence for oligomerization |CITS: 
                     [14973045]|. The primary structure of Kch as well as 
                     experiments with PhoA fusions show the presence of six 
                     transmembrane helices with low overall sequence similarity 
                     to eukaryotic channels |CITS: [8170937][8824224]|. However,
                     the potassium specific pore region (P-region) is 60-70% 
                     identical to corresponding regions in various eukaryotic 
                     potassium channel proteins |CITS: [8170937]|. <i>kch</i> 
                     gain-of-function mutants have been isolated which are 
                     sensitive to elevated potassium |CITS: [12912904]|.  
                     Suppressor mutations have also been isolated within the 
                     K<sup>+</sup> filter which rescue these mutants |CITS: 
                     [12912904]|.  In an earlier study, toxicity from 
                     overexpression of <i>kch</i> was rescued by supplementing 
                     the medium with K<sup>+</sup>, Rb<sup>+</sup>, 
                     NH<sub>4</sub><sup>+</sup>, or Cs<sup>+</sup> |CITS: 
                     [12220501]|.  Overexpression of <i>kch</i> has also been 
                     shown to lead to decreased intracellular potassium levels 
                     due to leakage |CITS: [11606201]|. Kch was found, in random
                     transposon mutagenesis studies, to be required for growth 
                     in optimum (rich medium at 37&deg;C) growth conditions but 
                     not under cold conditions (15&deg;C) or in minimal medium 
                     |CITS: [15380559]|.
                     RpoS has been reported to be required for expression of 
                     <i>kch</i> |CITS: [14671322]|. Expression of <i>kch</i> is 
                     induced by Lrp |CITS: [12374860]|.  <i>kch</i> has a 
                     predicted &sigma;<sup>54</sup>-binding site, though it is 
                     264 bases from the gene and may not be functional |CITS: 
                     [11528004]|.  <i>kch</i> was found to be not expressed in 
                     rich medium cultures |CITS: [11133948]|.
                     A mini-Tn<i>5</i>Km2 insertion into <i>kch</i> of <i>E. 
                     coli</i> O157:H7 Sakai strain resulted in reduced adherence
                     of the mutant to Caco-2 cells |CITS: [10992506]|.
                     Review: |CITS: [7513423]|
                     "
