     gene            complement(1306608..1307147)
                     /gene="yciB"
                     /locus_tag="b1254"
                     /label=yciB
     CDS             complement(1306608..1307147)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yciB"
                     /locus_tag="b1254"
                     /product="inner membrane protein YciB"
                     /label=yciB
                     /note="YciB has sequence similarity with IspA - a
                     <i>Shigella flexneri</i> protein with a role in cell 
                     division and intracellular spreading |CITS: [8830250]|. 
                     YciB has been implicated in the import of specific toxins 
                     of contact-dependent growth inhibition (CDI) systems in 
                     gram-negative bacteria; <i>yciB</i> transposon insertion 
                     mutants and <i>yciB</i> in-frame deletion mutants are 
                     resistant to the CdiA-CT<sub>o11</sub><sup>EC869</sup> 
                     toxin; inner membrane proteins such as YciB are thought to 
                     act as receptors which bring the nuclease domain of CDI 
                     toxins into close proximity with the inner membrane of 
                     target cells |CITS: [26305955]| (see further |CITS: 
                     [39591464]|).
                     YciB is a multipass inner membrane protein; bacterial 
                     two-hybrid analysis indicates that it interacts with a 
                     number of cell division and cell shape proteins (RodZ, 
                     MurG, MreC, MreD and RodA); a &Delta;<i>yciB</i> mutant is 
                     sensitive to low osmolarity |CITS: [26454142]|
                     <i>yciB</i> exhibits a synthetic lethal phenotype with 
                     |FRAME: G7767 ""<i>dcrB</i>""|; the double deletion mutants
                     have pleiotropic defects including morphological changes, 
                     reduced proton motive force and disrupted outer membrane 
                     protein biogenesis |CITS: [30368949]|."
