                     /product="trp operon leader peptide"
                     /label=trpL
                     /note="The TrpL leader peptide is a key component in the 
                     attenuation system that controls expression of the 
                     <i>trpLEDCBA</i> operon in response to tryptophan 
                     availability |CITS: [7038627]|. <i>trpL</i> occurs within a
                     130-nucleotide region at the beginning of the <i>trp</i> 
                     operon |CITS: [781269]|. The TrpL peptide contains tandem 
                     tryptophan residues that serve as the regulatory region 
                     during attenuation |CITS: [6206069][2991886]|.
                     Review: |CITS: [34651439]|"
