     gene            1321109..1321984
                     /gene="rluB"
                     /locus_tag="b1269"
                     /label=rluB
     CDS             1321109..1321984
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rluB"
                     /locus_tag="b1269"
                     /product="23S rRNA pseudouridine(2605) synthase"
                     /EC_number="5.4.99.22"
                     /label=rluB
                     /note="RluB is the pseudouridine synthase that catalyzes 
                     formation of pseudouridine at position 2605 in 23S rRNA. 
                     RluB belongs to the RsuA family of RNA pseudouridine 
                     synthases |CITS: [11720289]|.
                     RluB is associated with a particle the migrates slightly 
                     slower than the 50S ribosomal subunit, suggesting that it 
                     acts during 50S subunit maturation |CITS: [17337586]|. 
                     Pseudouridine residues outside of helix-loop 69, including 
                     &Psi;<sup>2605</sup>, appear to be made during the early 
                     steps of large ribosome subunit assembly |CITS: 
                     [20719918][23228329]|.
                     Crystal structures of the catalytic domain alone and in a 
                     complex with the substrate stem-loop have been solved, 
                     revealing a covalent bond between the hydroxyl group of the
                     active site Tyr140 and the C6 of the U2605 substrate with 
                     the base flipped into the active site.  The authors propose
                     a Michael addition reaction mechanism for pseudouridine 
                     synthesis |CITS: [24214967]|.
                     The conserved active site residue Asp110 is essential for 
                     activity |CITS: [11720289]|, while a Tyr140Phe mutant 
                     retains 3% of wild-type enzymatic activity |CITS: 
                     [24214967]|.  An <i>rluB</i> null mutant or an <i>rluB 
                     rluF</i> double null mutant exhibits no obvious growth 
                     defect |CITS: [11720289]|.  Deletion of <i>rluB</i> leads 
                     to accumulation of free 30S and 50S ribosomal subunits 
                     |CITS: [17337586]|.
                     Reviews: |CITS: [17113994][25616362]|
                     "
