     gene            complement(1322024..1322614)
                     /gene="btuR"
                     /locus_tag="b1270"
                     /label=btuR
     CDS             complement(1322024..1322614)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="btuR"
                     /locus_tag="b1270"
                     /product="trifunctional cobinamide/cobalamin
                     adenosyltransferase / cobinamide adenosyltransferase / 
                     cobalamin adenosyltransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.5.1.17"
                     /label=btuR
                     /note="<i>E. coli</i> K-12, as well as natural isolates,
                     can synthesize cobalamin only when supplied with the 
                     intermediate cobinamide |CITS: [8770581]|. Sequence 
                     similarity and complementation of a <i>cobA</i> mutant in 
                     <i>Salmonella typhimurium</i> suggests that <i>btuR</i> 
                     encodes the cobinamide adenosyltransferase |CITS: 
                     [2403541][7916712]|. Cobinamide adenosyltransferase 
                     catalyzes the synthesis of adenosylcobalamin from a 
                     cobalamin precursor transported into the cell |CITS: 
                     [2644187]|.
                     A <i>btuR</i> mutation leads to loss of repression of 
                     expression by externally supplied vitamin B<sub>12</sub> 
                     and was therefore initially thought to encode a 
                     transcriptional repressor of <i>btuB</i> |CITS: [3108627]|.
                     However, it was later shown that a <i>btuR</i> mutation 
                     results in a decrease in the pool of intracellular 
                     adenosylcobalamin and is thus more likely involved in the 
                     conversion of vitamin B<sub>12</sub> to adenosylcobalamin 
                     |CITS: [2644187]|. Insertion mutants within <i>btuR</i> 
                     lead to an inability to utilize cobinamide under aerobic 
                     growth conditions |CITS: [7592411]|.
                     Laboratory evolution and overexpression experiments found 
                     that BtuR is required for growth in a |FRAME: 
                     HOMOCYSMETB12-MONOMER| (MetH)-dependent strain with 
                     pseudocobalamin |CITS: [39873498]|.
                     BtuR: ""<b>B</b> <b>t</b>welve <b>u</b>ptake 
                     <b>r</b>egulation"""
