                     /product="S49 peptidase family protein"
                     /label=sohB
                     /note="SohB is an inner membrane protein with similarity
                     to the signal peptide peptidase |FRAME: CPLX0-2941 
                     ""protease IV""| |CITS: [1885549]|.  It contains one 
                     predicted transmembrane domain; the C terminus is located 
                     in the cytoplasm |CITS: [15919996]|.  SohB is subject to 
                     posttranslational processing of a signal sequence; the 
                     precursor is 39 kDa and the mature protein is 37 kDa |CITS:
                     [1885549]|.
                     Multicopy expression of <i>sohB</i> suppresses the heat 
                     sensitivity of an |FRAME: EG10463 <i>htrA</i>| mutant 
                     |CITS: [1885549]|.
                     SohB: ""<b>s</b>uppressor <b>o</b>f <i><b>h</b>trA</i> 
                     <b>B</b>"" |CITS: [1885549]|"
