                     /locus_tag="b1279"
                     /product="lipopolysaccharide assembly protein A"
                     /label=lapA
                     /note="<i>lapA</i> is generally not essential. 
                     <i>&Delta;lapA</i> strains do not grow on MacConkey agar at
                     43&deg;C. LapA copurifies with LapB, DnaK, DnaJ and with 
                     the LPS transport system proteins (LptE/D, LptBFGC, LptA). 
                     Purified LapA contains lipopolysaccharide (LPS) |CITS: 
                     [24722986]|.
                     <i>lapAB</i> transcription is subject to heat shock 
                     induction via an RpoH-regulated promoter located upstream 
                     of <i>lapA</i> |CITS: [24722986]|.
                     LapA is an inner membrane protein with two predicted 
                     transmembrane domains.  The C terminus is located in the 
                     cytoplasm |CITS: [15919996]|.
                     LapA was identified in a phylogenetic screen that found 
                     proteins containing domains that only occur in organisms 
                     that also contain a |FRAME: EG10204-MONOMER Dam| 
                     methyltransferase |CITS: [16787973]|.
                     LapA: <u>l</u>ipopolysaccharide <u>a</u>ssembly 
                     <u>p</u>rotein A"
