                     /product="multifunctional ABC transporter ATP binding
                     protein SapF / putative putrescine ABC exporter / 
                     putrescine ABC exporter / putative antimicrobial peptide 
                     ABC transporter / antimicrobial peptide ABC transporter"
                     /label=sapF
                     /note="SapF is one of two ATP-binding proteins of a
                     predicted ATP-binding cassette (ABC)-family transporter 
                     complex, SapABCDF, that may be involved in the uptake of a 
                     range of molecules, such as antimicrobial peptides, 
                     dipeptides and heme |CITS: [40084591][40387417]|. 
                     Separately, a |FRAME: CPLX0-13226 SapBCDF complex| has been
                     implicated in putrescine efflux at neutral pH |CITS: 
                     [27803167]|. The concentration of putrescine in the culture
                     supernatant of a &Delta;<i>sapF</i> strain is significantly
                     reduced compared to wild type |CITS: [27803167]|. SapF 
                     contains signature motifs conserved in ATP-binding cassette
                     (ABC) proteins |CITS: [9593292]|."
