     CDS             complement(1352059..1353444)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="puuP"
                     /locus_tag="b1296"
                     /product="putrescine:H(+) symporter PuuP"
                     /label=puuP
                     /note="PuuP is a proton dependent putrescine transporter
                     which functions in the exponential growth phase 
                     |CITS:[15590624], [19181795]|. Mutational experiments show 
                     that among all the genes for putrescine transport 
                     (<i>potFGHI, potABCD, potE</i> and <i>puuP</i>) only 
                     <i>puuP</i> is essential to utilise putrescine as a
                     sole carbon or nitrogen source |CITS:[19181795]|. The level
                     of <i>puuP</i> expression increases at low concentrations 
                     of glucose (0.04%). The expression of <i>puuP</i> is not 
                     inhibited by the intracellular accumulation of putrescine 
                     |CITS: [23719730]|.
                     PuuP and |FRAME: YEEF-MONOMER PlaP| are receptors for the 
                     group 5 CDI ionophore toxins |CITS: [39591464]|."
