                     /gene="puuA"
                     /locus_tag="b1297"
                     /product="glutamate-putrescine ligase"
                     /EC_number="6.3.1.11"
                     /label=puuA
                     /note="Glutamate-putrescine ligase is the first enzyme in
                     the primary putrescine utilization pathway of
                     <i>E. coli</i> |CITS: [18495664]|.  It catalyzes the 
                     ATP-dependent &gamma;-glutamylation of putrescine.
                     The function of genes in the <i>puu</i> gene cluster was 
                     initially inferred by similarity with the 
                     <i>ipuABCDEGFH</i> operon in <i>Pseudomonas</i> sp. |CITS: 
                     [15590624]|.  PuuA has similarity to
                     glutamine synthetase; based on this similarity, predicted 
                     active site residues were mutagenized, and the
                     resulting enzymes show little activity |CITS: [18495664]|. 
                     A <i>puuA</i> deletion mutant can not grow on putrescine as
                     the sole source of carbon or nitrogen
                     |CITS: [18495664]|.  Expression of <i>puuA</i> is induced 
                     during the transition of anaerobic to aerobic
                     cultures |CITS: [16857675]| and by putrescine |CITS: 
                     [18495664]|.
                     PuuA: ""<b>pu</b>trescine <b>u</b>tilization pathway"" 
                     |CITS: [15590624]|"
