     CDS             1358489..1359769
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="puuB"
                     /locus_tag="b1301"
                     /product="gamma-glutamylputrescine oxidase"
                     /label=puuB
                     /note="PuuB is probably the &gamma;-glutamylputrescine
                     oxidase in a putrescine utilization pathway; together with 
                     PuuC,
                     &gamma;-glutamyl-&gamma;-aminobutyrate is produced from 
                     &gamma;-glutamylputrescine |CITS: [15590624]|.
                     The function of genes in the <i>puu</i> gene cluster was 
                     initially inferred by similarity with the 
                     <i>ipuABCDEGFH</i>
                     operon in <i>Pseudomonas</i> sp. |CITS: [15590624]|. Loss 
                     of PuuB in a strain without PatA prevents putrescine 
                     utilization |CITS: [22636776]|.
                     The <i>puuC</i>, <i>puuB</i>, and <i>puuE</i> genes may 
                     form an operon |CITS: [9150200][1840553]|."
