                     /product="phage shock protein D"
                     /label=pspD
                     /note="PspD is a peripheral inner membrane protein |CITS: 
                     [12562786]|.
                     PspA, PspB, and PspC are not observed to cross-link with 
                     PspD, whereas PspA, PspB, and PspC form a complex, and PspC
                     is required for PspA to bind to PspB |CITS: [12562786]|.
                     Multi-copy overexpression of the psp operon increases 
                     survival of stress caused by n-hexane treatment |CITS: 
                     [9493373]|.
                     The corresponding psp locus of <i>Yersinia 
                     enterocolitica</i> is virulence-related |CITS: [11136463]|.
                     Regulation has been described |CITS: [1712397][9344746][95 
                     12522][9878422][9987127][9493373][1717346][8606168][7596833
                     ][8134371][7921245]|. The psp operon shows induction upon 
                     phage infection, temperature increase, or exposure to 
                     ethanol, osmotic shock |CITS: [1712397]|, or the organic 
                     solvents n-hexane or cyclooctane |CITS: [9493373]|.   
                     Induction is mediated by sigma54, PspB, PspC |CITS: 
                     [1717346]|, PspF |CITS: [8606168]|, and IHF |CITS: 
                     [7596833]|.  Transcription is induced by conditions that 
                     cause stress related to energy depletion |CITS: [8134371]|.
                      Treatment with the drugs diazaborine or cerulenin, which 
                     inhibit synthesis of fatty acids and phospholipids, or 
                     treatment with globomycin, which disrupts lipoprotein 
                     processing, causes transcriptional induction of pspA |CITS:
                     [7921245]|. Transcription is repressed by PspA and by the 
                     heat shock (sigma32-dependent) system |CITS: [1717346]|.
                     PspD: ""<b>p</b>hage <b>s</b>hock <b>p</b>rotein <b>D</b>""
                     |CITS: [1712397]|
                     Reviews: |CITS: [9159513][16045608]|"
                     /translation="MNTRWQQAGQKVKPGFKLAGKLVLLTALRYGPAGVAGWAIKSVAR
