     CDS             1374405..1375064
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ycjU"
                     /locus_tag="b1317"
                     /product="beta-phosphoglucomutase"
                     /EC_number="5.4.2.6"
                     /label=ycjU
                     /note="YcjU is a &beta;-phosphoglucomutase belonging to
                     the superfamily of haloacid dehalogenase (HAD)-like 
                     hydrolases |CITS: [16990279]|.  Phosphatase activity of the
                     enzyme with the reaction intermediate 
                     &beta;-glucose-1,6-bisphosphate has been measured |CITS: 
                     [25848029]|.
                     <i>ycjU</i> was identified in a screen for genes that 
                     reduce the lethal effects of stress.  A <i>ycjU</i> 
                     insertion mutant is more sensitive than wild type to 
                     mitomycin C and other stresses such as UV irradiation 
                     |CITS: [20128927]|.  A <i>ycjU</i> mutant has reduced 
                     ability to act as a recipient in cell-to-cell transfer of a
                     plasmid and shows reduced transformation efficiency using 
                     the CaCl<sub>2</sub> and electroporation transformation 
                     methods |CITS: [22497891]|."
