     gene            complement(1382562..1383068)
                     /gene="tpx"
                     /locus_tag="b1324"
                     /label=tpx
     CDS             complement(1382562..1383068)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="tpx"
                     /locus_tag="b1324"
                     /product="lipid hydroperoxide peroxidase"
                     /EC_number="1.11.1.24"
                     /label=tpx
                     /note="Tpx is a |FRAME: RED-THIOREDOXIN-MONOMER|-dependent
                     thiol peroxidase that belongs to the family of atypical 
                     2-Cys peroxidases |CITS: [12514184][14506251]|.  <i>In 
                     vivo</i>, Tpx appears to function as a lipid hydroperoxide 
                     peroxidase and acts as the principal antioxidant under 
                     anaerobic conditions |CITS: [14676195]|.
                     Osmotic shock experiments initially indicated that the 
                     enzyme was located in the periplasm |CITS: [7499381]|. 
                     However, no signal sequence for transport into the 
                     periplasm is evident, and <i>in vivo</i> interaction with 
                     |FRAME: RED-THIOREDOXIN-MONOMER| indicates that the enzyme 
                     is located in the cytoplasm |CITS: [19054092]|.
                     Kinetic analysis shows a bisubstrate ping-pong catalytic 
                     mechanism |CITS: [12514184]|.  The enzyme is a dimer in 
                     solution, and this form is independent of the redox state; 
                     electrophoresis data is consistent with intrasubunit 
                     disulfide bond formation |CITS: [12514184]|.  A crystal 
                     structure of Tpx in the oxidized state has been solved at 
                     2.2 &Aring; resolution |CITS: [14506251]|.
                     A <i>tpx</i> deletion mutant is more sensitive to oxidative
                     stress than wild type |CITS: [8824604]|.  Cys61 is the 
                     peroxidatic residue and is essential for catalytic activity
                     |CITS: [9168946][12514184]|.  A Cys95 mutant has partial 
                     activity |CITS: [12514184]|.  Expression of <i>tpx</i> is 
                     induced under aerobic conditions |CITS: 
                     [8630014][10794600]| and by low pH |CITS: [12107143]|, but 
                     not oxidative stress |CITS: [14676195]|.
                     Tpx: ""<b>t</b>hiol <b>p</b>ero<b>x</b>idase"" |CITS: 
                     [8630014]|
                     Reviews: |CITS: [22609271][18498222][12517450][12033427]|"
