     gene            1387484..1389097
                     /gene="mppA"
                     /locus_tag="b1329"
                     /label=mppA
     CDS             1387484..1389097
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="mppA"
                     /locus_tag="b1329"
                     /product="bifunctional murein tripeptide ABC transporter 
                     periplasmic binding protein / murein tripeptide ABC 
                     transporter"
                     /label=mppA
                     /note="MppA is the periplasmic binding protein of an ABC 
                     transporter that mediates the high affinity uptake of 
                     murein tripeptides |CITS: [9495761]|.
                     <i>mppA</i> mutants cannot use murein tripeptide 
                     (L-alanyl-&gamma;-D-glutamyl-<i>meso</i>-diaminopimelate) 
                     as a source of diaminopimelic acid (Dap) in a strain that 
                     requires Dap for growth |CITS: [9495761]|.  MppA (in the 
                     absence of the periplasmic oligopeptide binding protein 
                     OppA) supports growth of a proline auxotroph on Pro-Phe-Lys
                     tripeptide; MppA transports murein tripeptide more 
                     efficiently than Pro-Phe-Lys |CITS: [9495761]|. Purified 
                     MppA binds murein tripeptide with sub micromolar affinity 
                     and the synthetic tripeptide L-Ala-&gamma;-D-Glu-L-Lys with
                     500-fold lower affinity; it does not bind conventional 
                     tripeptides such as Lys-Glu-Lys, Lys-Lys-Lys, Ala-Lys-Lys 
                     and others |CITS: [21705338]|. Crystal structures of MppA 
                     in an open, unliganded conformation and in a closed 
                     conformation with murein tripeptide bound have been 
                     reported; MppA contains two relatively rigid domains 
                     connected by a flexible linker; ligand binding is 
                     associated with large conformational change whereupon the 
                     molecule transitions from an open form with a solvent 
                     accessible cleft to a closed form containing a single 
                     molecule of murein tripeptide completely buried within the 
                     protein |CITS: [21705338][29783769]|.
                     In a recombinant strain of <i>E. coli</i> that expresses an
                     outer membrane heme receptor (HasR from <i>S. 
                     marcescens</i>), MppA supports the uptake of heme and the 
                     heme precursor &gamma;-aminolevulinic acid; heme uptake 
                     requires the membrane components of the dipeptide ABC 
                     transporter (DppBCDF) and either of the periplasmic binding
                     proteins DppA or MppA; purified MppA binds heme; tripeptide
                     is a competitor for heme binding <i>in vitro</i> |CITS: 
                     [16905647]|.
                     <i>mppA</i> is implicated in the adaptive response to 
                     acetate and propionate; <i>mppA</i> expression decreases 
                     after growth in complex medium with acetate or propionate 
                     |CITS: [12620868]|. <i>mppA</i> is a member of the PgrR 
                     regulon; PgrR binds to an upstream site of <i>mppA</i>; 
                     <i>mppA</i> expression is increased in a <i>pgrR</i> 
                     deletion mutant; <i>mppA</i> expression increases under 
                     nitrogen starvation |CITS: [27231238]|.
                     <i>mppA</i>: <U>m</U>urein <U>p</U>eptide <U>p</U>ermease A
                     |CITS: [9495761]|
                     Review: |CITS: [18535144]|"
