     gene            complement(1391929..1392879)
                     /gene="uspE"
                     /locus_tag="b1333"
                     /label=uspE
     CDS             complement(1391929..1392879)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="uspE"
                     /locus_tag="b1333"
                     /product="universal stress protein E"
                     /label=uspE
                     /note="UspC, UspD, and UspE play nonredundant and probably 
                     sequential roles in a pathway involved in resistance to UV 
                     irradiation |CITS: [11849540]|.  The UspE protein promotes 
                     cell motility at the expense of adhesion |CITS: 
                     [16159758]|.
                     UspE consists of two tandemly arranged Usp domains.  A 
                     crystal structure of the protein from <i>E. coli</i> 
                     O157:H7, whose sequence is 100% identical to that of <i>E. 
                     coli</i> K-12 MG1655, has been solved at 3.2 &Aring; 
                     resolution |CITS: [25484216][26865045]|.  The crystal 
                     structure shows an unidentified ligand bound in a 
                     hydrophobic pocket, and the protein was shown to bind 
                     Cd<sup>2+</sup> |CITS: [26865045]|.
                     <i>uspE</i> deletion mutants shows decreased resistance to 
                     UV irradiation |CITS: [11849540]|, lack flagella, are 
                     unable to aggregate |CITS: [16159758]|, and show increased 
                     biofilm formation |CITS: [20209085]|.  Expression of 
                     <i>uspE</i> is induced in stationary phase and by a variety
                     of stress conditions including oxidative stress |CITS: 
                     [11849540][20209085]| and requires ppGpp |CITS: 
                     [11849540]|.
                     UspE: ""<b>u</b>niversal <b>s</b>tress <b>p</b>rotein 
                     <b>E</b>"" |CITS: [11849540]|
                     Reviews: |CITS: [12732303][16159755]|
                     "
