     gene            1403386..1403507
                     /gene="fnrS"
                     /locus_tag="b4699"
                     /label=fnrS
     misc_RNA        1403386..1403507
                     /gene="fnrS"
                     /locus_tag="b4699"
                     /product="small regulatory RNA FnrS"
                     /note="FnrS is a small regulatory RNA that reprograms
                     metabolism in response to anaerobiosis. Potential 
                     regulatory targets were identified by gene expression 
                     analysis and proteomic profiling, and selected targets were
                     validated |CITS: [20070527][20075074]|. Additional targets 
                     of FnrS have been identified by comparative genomics |CITS:
                     [23980183]|. A candidate FnrS regulon was inferred by 
                     integrating information on experimentally supported targets
                     and sRNA-mRNA interactions with transcription datasets 
                     |CITS: [32487739]|.
                     Hfq interacts with and stabilizes FnrS |CITS: 
                     [20075074][36328526]|; in an <i>hfq</i> mutant strain, the 
                     half life of FnrS is decreased 15-fold from 100 minutes in 
                     the wild-type background |CITS: [20075074]|.
                     Expression of FnrS occurs only under anaerobic growth 
                     conditions, is dependent on |FRAME: CPLX0-7797| |CITS: 
                     [20070527][20075074]|, and is affected by ArcA and CRP 
                     |CITS: [20070527]|. CpxR was identified as a putative 
                     regulator of FnrS expression |CITS: [34327153]|. When the 
                     existence of FnrS (RydA) was first proposed, no expression 
                     could be detected on Northern blots |CITS: [11445539]|. 
                     FnrA represses translation of the iron-sulfur cluster 
                     transcriptional regulator |FRAME: CPLX0-8083 ""IscR""| 
                     under anaerobiosis; electrophoretic mobility shift assays 
                     (EMSAs) confirmed the base-pairing site in the 5'-UTR of 
                     IscR, with the presence of Hfq improving the interaction 
                     |CITS: [39495911]|.
                     FnrS: ""<b>FN</b>R-<b>r</b>egulated <b>s</b>RNA"" |CITS: 
                     [20075074]|
                     Review: |CITS: [32213244]|"
