     gene            1431378..1431488
                     /gene="micC"
                     /locus_tag="b4427"
                     /label=micC
     misc_RNA        1431378..1431488
                     /gene="micC"
                     /locus_tag="b4427"
                     /product="small regulatory RNA MicC"
                     /note="MicC is a small RNA that regulates expression of
                     OmpC at the post-transcriptional level |CITS: 
                     [15466019][17264113]|. Overexpression of MicC causes a 60% 
                     reduction of OmpC expression, while deletion of <i>micC</i>
                     causes a 1.5-2 fold increase in OmpC expression. 22 
                     nucleotides at the 5' end of MicC are able to base pair 
                     with a sequence located upstream of the ribosome binding 
                     site in the <i>ompC</i> mRNA and repress OmpC expression by
                     inhibiting binding of the 30S ribosomal subunit to 
                     <i>ompC</i> mRNA |CITS: [15466019]|.
                     Hfq is required for MicC function |CITS: 
                     [15466019][17264113]|.
                     Overexpression of MicC decreases swarming motility |CITS: 
                     [26469694]|.
                     Expression of MicC is induced by growth at low temperature 
                     or on minimal media |CITS: [15466019]|, as well as in the 
                     presence of carbapenems and cephalosporins, members of the 
                     &beta;-lactam class of antibiotics, and by overexpression 
                     of RseA, which depletes &sigma;<sup>E</sup> |CITS: 
                     [29211019]|.
                     Reviews: |CITS: 
                     [15466017][12654996][17055775][29137641][32213244]|"
