     CDS             complement(1435578..1436000)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="hslJ"
                     /locus_tag="b1379"
                     /product="lipoprotein implicated in Novobiocin resistance"
                     /label=hslJ
                     /note="<i>hslJ</i> is a member of the CysB regulon; CysB
                     is a direct repressor of <i>hslJ</i> transcription; 
                     <i>hslJ</i> is also subject to (possibly indirect) 
                     autogenous negative repression |CITS: 
                     [14663078][12892888]|. <i>hslJ</i> is implicated in the 
                     increased resistance to Novobiocin that occurs in 
                     <i>cysB</i><sup>-</sup> mutants. Inactivation of 
                     <i>hslJ</i> (<i>hslJ::lacZ</i> or <i>hslJ</i>::&Omega;Kan) 
                     in a <i>cysB</i><sup>-</sup> background results in 
                     decreased resistance to the antibiotic Novobiocin (compared
                     to the <i>cysB</i><sup>-</sup> parent strain); 
                     overexpression of <i>hslJ</i> from a low copy number 
                     plasmid increases Novobiocin resistance in both a 
                     <i>cysB</i><sup>-</sup> and <i>cysB</i><sup>+</sup> 
                     background |CITS: [12892888]|.
                     HslJ is a lipoprotein |CITS: [12876315]|; HslJ is predicted
                     to be a membrane protein |CITS: [12892888]| <i>hslJ</i> 
                     expression is induced by heat shock (7 mins at 50 &deg;C) 
                     |CITS: [8349564]|. Expression of a <i>hslJ::lacZ</i> gene 
                     fusion (in a <i>cysB<sup>-</sup></i> strain) is not induced
                     by heat shock - maximal expression occurs at 37 &deg;C; no 
                     heat shock promoters are identified in the upstream region 
                     of <i>hslJ</i> |CITS: [12892888]|"
