     gene            1437308..1439947
                     /gene="ydbH"
                     /locus_tag="b1381"
                     /label=ydbH
     CDS             1437308..1439947
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ydbH"
                     /locus_tag="b1381"
                     /product="putative intermembrane phospholipid transport
                     protein YdbH"
                     /label=ydbH
                     /note="YdbH, |FRAME: G7875-MONOMER TamB|, |FRAME:
                     G7690-MONOMER YhdP|, |FRAME: EG11684-MONOMER YicH| and 
                     |FRAME: EG12251-MONOMER YhjG| are |FRAME: EG11361-MONOMER 
                     AsmA|-like paralogs predicted to contain an N-terminal 
                     inner membrane anchor and a large periplasmic region with 
                     chorein-N and AsmA-like domains; the combined loss of YdbH,
                     TamB, and YhdP is lethal; the three proteins are crucial 
                     for maintaining lipid homeostasis at the OM and are 
                     functionally redundant but not equivalent; TamB, YhdP and 
                     YdbH may be intermembrane bridge proteins that facilitate 
                     the movement of phospholipids between the inner and outer 
                     membrane |CITS: [34781743]| (see also |CITS: 
                     [35226662][37455811]|).
                     YdbH interacts with the outer membrane |FRAME: 
                     G6704-MONOMER| to form a periplasmic protein bridge that 
                     connects the inner and outer membranes; <i>ydbH</i> forms 
                     an operon with <i>ynbE</i> and |FRAME: G6705|, and 
                     <i>ydbL</i> is implicated in formation of the YdbH-YnbE 
                     complex |CITS: [38748582]|.
                     Sequence similarity suggests that YdbH is a member of the 
                     Autotransporter (AT) family |CITS: [12192075]|."
