                     /label=paaD
     CDS             1450182..1450679
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="paaD"
                     /locus_tag="b1391"
                     /product="phenylacetate degradation protein"
                     /label=paaD
                     /note="PaaA, PaaB, PaaC, and PaaD were predicted to be
                     subunits of a phenylacetate-CoA oxygenase involved in 
                     phenylacetate catabolism |CITS: [12846838]|.  Recent work 
                     with the enzyme from <i>Pseudomonas</i> sp. has shown that 
                     the PaaA, PaaB, PaaC and PaaE polypeptides copurify as a 
                     complex when overexpressed.  PaaD is not part of the 
                     complex, nor is it required for the enzymatic activity of 
                     the complex.  PaaD is hypothesized to participate in the 
                     formation of a predicted iron-sulfur cluster in the PaaE 
                     subunit |CITS: [20660314]|.
                     PaaD: ""<b>p</b>henyl<b>a</b>cetic <b>a</b>cid 
                     degradation"" |CITS: [9748275]|"
