     gene            1454728..1455150
                     /gene="paaI"
                     /locus_tag="b1396"
                     /label=paaI
     CDS             1454728..1455150
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="paaI"
                     /locus_tag="b1396"
                     /product="bifunctional phenylacetyl-CoA thioesterase / 
                     hydroxyphenylacetyl-CoA thioesterase"
                     /label=paaI
                     /note="PaaI belongs to the acyl-CoA thioesterase subfamily
                     of the hotdog-fold superfamily of enzymes |CITS: 
                     [15307895]|.  Among the relevant phenylacetate degradation 
                     pathway intermediates, its primary substrate appears to be 
                     phenylacetyl-CoA |CITS: [22398448]|, although it was 
                     previously thought that its preferred substrates were 
                     ring-hydroxylated phenylacetyl-CoA thioesters |CITS: 
                     [16464851]|.  It may be involved in detoxification or 
                     salvage reactions for breakdown products of the unstable 
                     early intermediates of the phenylacetate degradation 
                     pathway |CITS: [20660314][22398448]|.
                     A crystal structure of PaaI has been solved at 2 &Aring; 
                     resolution |CITS: [16464851]|.
                     A <i>paaI</i> mutant does not exhibit a defect in 
                     utilization of phenylacetate as a source of carbon |CITS: 
                     [12846838]|.  PaaI activity is increased in cells grown on 
                     phenylacetate |CITS: [22398448]|.
                     PaaI: ""<b>p</b>henyl<b>a</b>cetic <b>a</b>cid 
                     degradation"" |CITS: [9748275]|"
