                     /label=ynbA
     CDS             1471878..1472483
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ynbA"
                     /locus_tag="b1408"
                     /product="CDP-alcohol phosphatidyltransferase
                     domain-containing protein YnbA"
                     /label=ynbA
                     /note="YnbA is an inner membrane protein with five
                     predicted transmembrane domains.  The C terminus is located
                     in the cytoplasm |CITS: [15919996]|.
                     Based on sequence similarity, YnbA was predicted to be a 
                     diacylglycerol cholinephosphotransferase |CITS: 
                     [12952533]|; however, phosphatidylcholine is not a 
                     component of <i>E. coli</i> membranes |CITS: [20656373]|. 
                     <i>ynbA</i> was identified in a screen for genes affecting 
                     Fe-S cluster biogenesis and/or iron homeostasis |CITS: 
                     [24415728]|.
                     Expression of <i>ynbA</i> is activated by BglJ-RcsB |CITS: 
                     [24335284]|."
