     gene            1485159..1485689
                     /gene="cybB"
                     /locus_tag="b1418"
                     /label=cybB
     CDS             1485159..1485689
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="cybB"
                     /locus_tag="b1418"
                     /product="superoxide oxidase"
                     /EC_number="1.10.3.17"
                     /label=cybB
                     /note="CybB or cytochrome <i>b</i><sub>561</sub> is a
                     membrane bound superoxide:ubiquinone oxidoreductase which 
                     catalyses the direct oxidation of superoxide to oxygen 
                     concomitant with the reduction of ubiquinone to ubiquinol; 
                     the primary function of CybB may be to quench superoxide 
                     produced by respiratory chain enzymes in or at the membrane
                     surface |CITS: [29915379]|.
                     CybB is a small inner membrane protein forming a four-helix
                     bundle; it contains two <i>b</i>-type hemes, one of which 
                     has the edge of the porphyrin ring exposed to the periplasm
                     |CITS: [3510204] [29915379]|. Ubiquinone is predicted to 
                     bind in a membrane exposed cavity near the cytosol-membrane
                     interface; the structural and electrochemical features of 
                     the protein suggest that it catalyses an electrogenic 
                     reaction with the electrons derived from the periplasmic 
                     side of the membrane and the protons for ubiquinone 
                     reduction derived from the cytosol |CITS: [29915379]|.
                     <i>cybB</i> transcription is higher in log phase growth 
                     compared to stationary phase and is not influenced by the 
                     presence or absence of oxygen |CITS: [29915379]|. Reduced 
                     detection of superoxide is observed in membranes from cells
                     that overproduce CybB |CITS: [29915379]|.
                     Cytochrome <i>b</i><sub>561</sub> was first identified in a
                     cytochrome <i>b</i><sub>556</sub>-deficient mutant |CITS: 
                     [6237244][6097799]|; its redox potential is estimated to be
                     +20mV |CITS: [3510204]|
                     "
