     gene            complement(1485699..1485763)
                     /gene="rydC"
                     /locus_tag="b4597"
                     /label=rydC
     misc_RNA        complement(1485699..1485763)
                     /gene="rydC"
                     /locus_tag="b4597"
                     /product="small regulatory RNA RydC"
                     /note="RydC is a putative small RNA regulator of the
                     expression of <i>yejABEF</i>, which encodes a predicted ABC
                     permease |CITS: [15618228]|, and of the transcriptional 
                     regulator CsgD |CITS: [24489123]|. However, these targets 
                     did not show differential regulation in response to RydC 
                     overexpression in later experiments |CITS: [30700509]|.  
                     RydC activates the expression of Cfa, promoting survival 
                     during acid shock |CITS: [30700509][31308070]|.  Additional
                     regulatory targets of RydC, encoding genes in aromatic 
                     amino acid biosynthesis pathways, have been identified 
                     |CITS: [30700509]|.
                     Hfq binds to RydC <i>in vivo</i> |CITS: [14622403]| and 
                     stabilizes it <i>in vitro</i> |CITS: [15618228][36328526]|.
                      RydC folds into a pseudoknot structure |CITS: [14622403]|;
                     Hfq facilitates unfolding of the pseudoknot and thereby 
                     enhances the interaction of RydC with its mRNA target 
                     |CITS: [24489123]|.  A crystal structure of the 
                     <i>Salmonella</i> RydC with <i>E. coli</i> Hfq has been 
                     solved |CITS: [25551292]|.  The <i>yejABEF</i> mRNA was 
                     found to bind the RydC-Hfq complex |CITS: [15618228]|.
                     The small RNA OmrB inhibits the activity of RydC 
                     |CITS:[38980083]|.
                     A <i>rydC</i> deletion strain has no detectable growth 
                     defect, but overexpression of RydC leads to a 
                     temperature-sensitive growth defect on minimal medium with 
                     glycerol, maltose, or ribose as the carbon source and leads
                     to degradation of <i>yejABEF</i> mRNA |CITS: [15618228]|.  
                     Overexpression of RydC decreases swarming motility and 
                     expression of curli |CITS: [26469694]|.
                     RydC: ""RNA of unknown function at X position (10 minute) 
                     in the genome""
                     Reviews: |CITS: [25028968][32213244]|"
