     gene            1486376..1486432
                     /gene="sokB"
                     /locus_tag="b4429"
                     /label=sokB
     misc_RNA        1486376..1486432
                     /gene="sokB"
                     /locus_tag="b4429"
                     /product="putative small regulatory RNA antitoxin SokB"
                     /note="<i>sokB</i> encodes a small antisense RNA with a
                     half life of 4 minutes that is predicted to regulate the 
                     translation of MokB and HokB |CITS: [10361310]|.
                     The <i>hokB/sokB</i> locus of <i>E. coli</i> K-12 encodes 
                     an intact hok/sok toxin/antitoxin system.  The <i>hokB</i> 
                     mRNA appears to be processed at its 3' end |CITS: 
                     [10361310]|.
                     In the plasmid R1 hok/sok system, Sok antisense RNA binds 
                     with <i>hok</i> mRNA, allowing cleavage by RNase III |CITS:
                     [10473621][1380562]|.
                     SokB interacts with the protein |FRAME: EG12866-MONOMER| 
                     |CITS: [36328526]|.
                     IS-mediated knockout of <i>hokB-sokB</i> was found in a 
                     long-term evolution experiment with <i>E. coli</i> B |CITS:
                     [11014799]|.
                     SokB: ""<b>s</b>uppression <b>o</b>f <b>k</b>illing 
                     <b>B</b>"" |CITS: [10361310]|
                     Reviews: |CITS: [9442888][17376733][23131729][32213244]|"
