     gene            1493195..1493734
                     /gene="rimL"
                     /locus_tag="b1427"
                     /label=rimL
     CDS             1493195..1493734
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rimL"
                     /locus_tag="b1427"
                     /product="bifunctional ribosomal-protein-L12-serine 
                     N-acetyltransferase / ribosomal-protein-L12-serine 
                     acetyltransferase"
                     /label=rimL
                     /note="RimL is the acetyl transferase that acetylates the 
                     N<sup>&alpha;</sup>-terminal serine residue of ribosomal 
                     protein L12, converting it into its modified form, L7 
                     |CITS: [7038378][2671655][17445774]|.  Acetylation of L12 
                     does not appear to be essential for its function |CITS: 
                     [7038378]|.
                     RimL can also acetylate a mutant ribosomal protein L12 
                     which contains alanine instead of serine at the N-terminal 
                     position (after cleavage of the leading methionine); 
                     substitution of the adjacent amino acid with aspartate 
                     leads to lower catalytic efficiency |CITS: [17445774]|. 
                     RimL is similar to the MccE acetyltransferase that 
                     acetylates and thereby provides resistance to processed 
                     microcin C (McC).  RimL, but not RimI or RimJ, contributes 
                     to <i>E. coli</i>'s basal level of resistance to McC and 
                     some of its analogs |CITS: [25002546]|.
                     A <i>rimL</i> mutant lacks ribosomal protein L7, the 
                     acetylated form of ribosomal protein L12 |CITS: [7038378]|.
                     RimL shows similarity to RimJ |CITS: [2671655]|."
                     /translation="MTETIKVSESLELHAVAENHVKPLYQLICKNKTWLQQSLNWPQFV
