     gene            1494830..1495822
                     /gene="tehA"
                     /locus_tag="b1429"
                     /label=tehA
     CDS             1494830..1495822
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="tehA"
                     /locus_tag="b1429"
                     /product="bifunctional tellurite resistance protein /
                     ethidium exporter"
                     /label=tehA
                     /note="Overexpression of <i>tehAB</i> from a plasmid
                     confers resistance to tellurite through an unknown 
                     mechanism that does not appear to involve reduced uptake or
                     increased efflux |CITS: [8169225], [7728659]|. 
                     Overexpression of <i>tehA</i> results in hypersensitivity 
                     to dequalinium and methyl viologen and resistance to 
                     tetraphenylarsonium, ethidium, crystal violet and proflavin
                     |CITS: [9021204]|.  Whole cell experiments indicated that 
                     TehA confers ethidium resistance via active efflux. Efflux 
                     is inhibited by the ionophore carbonyl cyanide 
                     m-chlorophenylhydrazone (CCCP). The addition of tellurite 
                     has no effect on ethidium transport <i>in vitro</i> |CITS: 
                     [9021204]|. Overexpression of <i>tehAB</i> protects against
                     tellurite induced dissipation of the transmembrane pH 
                     gradient and depletion of intracellular ATP levels |CITS: 
                     [15574934]|.
                     TehA is a member of the tellurite resistance/dicarboxylate 
                     (TDT) family of transporters which includes malate 
                     transporters.  The physiological role of <i>tehA</i> 
                     remains elusive.
                     "
