     CDS             1501038..1502999
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rlhA"
                     /locus_tag="b1435"
                     /product="23S rRNA 5-hydroxycytidine C2501 synthase"
                     /label=rlhA
                     /note="RlhA is the enzyme responsible for generating the 
                     5-hydroxycytidine modification at the C2501 position 
                     (ho<sup>5</sup>C2501) of 23S rRNA.  In addition to RlhA, 
                     prephenate biosynthesis and iron-sulfur cluster biogenesis 
                     proteins are required for generating the 
                     ho<sup>5</sup>C2501 modification |CITS: [29069499]|.
                     RlhA co-fractionates with the 30S subunit of the ribosome 
                     in a sucrose gradient, similar to other 23S rRNA-modifying 
                     enzymes |CITS: [29069499]|.
                     A &Delta;<i>rlhA</i> mutant strain completely lacks the 
                     ho<sup>5</sup>C2501 modification of 23S rRNA.  Mutations in
                     the conserved cysteine residues 169, 176, 580 and 611 
                     abolish the activity of RlhA |CITS: [29069499]|.
                     RlhA: ""<b>l</b>arge subunit <b>r</b>ibosomal RNA 
                     <b>h</b>ydroxylation <b>A</b>"" |CITS: [29069499]|
                     "
