     CDS             1504260..1505666
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ydcR"
                     /locus_tag="b1439"
                     /product="fused putative DNA-binding transcriptional 
                     regulator/putative aminotransferase YdcR"
                     /label=ydcR
                     /note="YdcR is a member of the GntR family of
                     transcriptional regulators |CITS: [35880217] [34428301]|. 
                     This family is known to be associated with regulation of 
                     carbon metabolism |CITS: [10734204] [35880217]|. YdcR has 
                     an HTH motif near its N terminus |CITS: [35880217]| and an 
                     aminotransferase domain.
                     YdcR DNA-binding activity was probed in vivo in glucose M9 
                     minimal medium through chromatin immunoprecipitation assays
                     (ChIP-exo) |CITS: [34428301]|. However, the effect of YdcR 
                     on the transcription of any gene has not yet been 
                     demonstrated |CITS: [34428301]|.
                     The transcription of the <i>ydcR</i> gene is affected by 
                     UV, cadmium, and pH |CITS: [35880217]|.
                     The YdcR binding landscape was globally mapped in vivo by 
                     standardized ChIP-seq and quantitatively modeled using 
                     BoltzNet, a biophysically informed neural network that 
                     infers binding energy from sequence data |CITS:[40335485]|.
                     The resulting ChIP-seq binding regions are available in 
                     RegulonDB (<a href=""https://regulondb.cc 
                     g.unam.mx/ht/dataset/TFBINDING/source=GALAGAN"">Galagan 
                     collection</a>), and the corresponding energy matrix and 
                     genomic binding profiles can be accessed at <a 
                     href=""http://boltznet.bu.edu"">boltznet.bu.edu</a> 
                     |CITS:[40335485]|.
                     The YdcR binding landscape was globally mapped in vivo by 
                     standardized ChIP-seq and quantitatively modeled using 
                     BoltzNet, a biophysically informed neural network that 
                     infers binding energy from sequence data |CITS:[40335485]|.
                     The resulting ChIP-seq binding regions are available in 
                     RegulonDB (<a href=""https://regulondb.cc 
                     g.unam.mx/ht/dataset/TFBINDING/source=GALAGAN"">Galagan 
                     collection</a>), and the corresponding energy matrix and 
                     genomic binding profiles can be accessed at <a 
                     href=""http://boltznet.bu.edu"">boltznet.bu.edu</a> 
                     |CITS:[40335485]|."
