     gene            1505911..1507056
                     /gene="ydcS"
                     /locus_tag="b1440"
                     /label=ydcS
     CDS             1505911..1507056
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ydcS"
                     /locus_tag="b1440"
                     /product="trifunctional putative ABC transporter
                     periplasmic binding protein / polyhydroxybutyrate synthase 
                     / poly-3-hydroxybutyrate synthase / putative transport 
                     complex, ABC superfamily"
                     /EC_number="2.3.1.304"
                     /label=ydcS
                     /note="The periplasmic protein,YdcS is a predicted to be
                     the binding protein of an uncharacterized ABC transporter 
                     |CITS: [16397293] [24225317]|.  YdcS is implicated in 
                     double strand (ds) DNA transport across the inner membrane 
                     during natural and chemical transformation; a <i>ydcS</i> 
                     deletion mutant has significantly decreased rates of 
                     natural and chemical transformation compared to wild type 
                     |CITS: [26826386]|.
                     Purified YdcS has poly-3-hydroxybutyrate (PHB) synthase 
                     activity; a <i>ydcS</i> deletion mutant contains 
                     approximately 30% less PHB complexed to proteins (cPHB) in 
                     the outer membrane compared to wild type; the addition of 
                     PHB to outer membrane proteins in the periplasm may 
                     facilitate their insertion into the outer membrane |CITS: 
                     [18640095]| (see also |CITS: [23702844]|).
                     Deletion of <i>ydcS</i> is associated with significant 
                     changes in the distribution of carbon fluxes in central 
                     metabolism |CITS: [33926117]|
                     <i>ydcS</i> is the first gene in a five gene operon 
                     (<i>ydcSTUVpatD</i>); transcription is initiated by 
                     &sigma;<sup>s</sup> containing RNA polymerase and induced 
                     under nitrogen limited growth |CITS: [15716429] [23531166] 
                     [26826386]|. <i>ydcS</i> is upregulated during adaption to 
                     glucose limitation |CITS: [15576800] [16804185]|"
