                     /locus_tag="b1447"
                     /product="putative transport protein YdcZ"
                     /label=ydcZ
                     /note="YdcZ is predicted to be an inner membrane protein
                     with five transmembrane domains; experimental topology 
                     analysis suggests the C terminus is located in the 
                     cytoplasm |CITS: [15919996]|. YdcZ appears to be required 
                     for normal swarming, but not swimming motility |CITS: 
                     [17122336]|.
                     In the Transporter Classification Database |CITS: 
                     [24225317]|, YdcZ is an uncharacterized member of the 
                     Drug/Metabolite Transporter (DMT) superfamily. A 
                     &Delta;<i>ydcZ</i> strain shows ability to take up 
                     membrane-permeable, cationic fluorescent dyes |CITS: 
                     [31438868]| and increased sensitivity to |FRAME: CPD0-2336|
                     |CITS: [36009997]|."
