     gene            complement(1515220..1517322)
                     /gene="pqqU"
                     /locus_tag="b1451"
                     /label=pqqU
     CDS             complement(1515220..1517322)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="pqqU"
                     /locus_tag="b1451"
                     /product="bifunctional pyrroloquinoline quinone outer
                     membrane transporter / pyrroloquinoline quinone outer 
                     membrane transport complex"
                     /label=pqqU
                     /note="<i>pqqU</i> (formerly <i>yncD</i>) encodes an outer 
                     membrane protein that mediates binding and |FRAME: 
                     CPLX0-1923 TonB|-dependent active transport of 
                     pyrroloquinoline quinone - a redox cofactor required by the
                     dehydrogenases |FRAME: GLUCDEHYDROG-MONOMER Gcd| and 
                     |FRAME: G6437-MONOMER YliI| -  across the outer membrane 
                     |CITS: [36054785]|. PqqU supports the growth of a 
                     PTS-deficient <i>E. coli</i> strain in glucose minimal 
                     medium at low PQQ concentrations (~ 1nmol/L); at higher PQQ
                     concentrations growth of this strain is PqqU-independent 
                     possibly due to porin-mediated PQQ diffusion |CITS: 
                     [36054785]|.
                     PqqU is a member of the Outer Membrane Receptor (OMR) 
                     family of TonB dependent transporters |CITS: 
                     [12192075][26546518]|.
                     A strain with a transposon insertion in <i>yncD</i> shows 
                     increased fitness during selection for thiamine diphosphate
                     (TPP) production in a competitive growth assay; a 
                     <i>yncD</i> null mutant produces a higher extracellular TPP
                     titer |CITS: [28768189]|.
                     Bioinformatic analysis indicates that YncD occurs in 
                     species within the Gammaproteobacteria and 
                     Betaproteobacteria; the majority of YncD-containing 
                     bacteria are environmental isolates |CITS: [32355044]|. 
                     Purified, recombinant YncD consists of a 22-stranded 
                     transmembrane &beta;-barrel with an N-terminal plug domain;
                     the protein contains a compact, positively charged binding 
                     site suggesting it may bind a small negatively charged 
                     molecule |CITS: [32355044]|. YncD is not involved in iron 
                     acquisition under laboratory conditions |CITS: [32355044]|.
                     PqqU is the terminal receptor for a number of small 
                     siphoviruses of the <i>Drexlerviridae</i> genus |CITS: 
                     [34784345]|.
                     <i>pqqU</i> exhibits mosaic evolution patterns in <i>E. 
                     coli</i> |CITS: [40444982]|."
