     gene            1528281..1529126
                     /gene="nhoA"
                     /locus_tag="b1463"
                     /label=nhoA
     CDS             1528281..1529126
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="nhoA"
                     /locus_tag="b1463"
                     /product="bifunctional arylamine N-acetyltransferase / 
                     N-hydroxyarylamine O-acetyltransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.3.1.5; 2.3.1.118"
                     /label=nhoA
                     /note="Arylamine acetyltransferase (NhoA) catalyzes the 
                     acetyl-CoA-dependent <i>N</i>-acetylation of a variety of 
                     arylamine substrates.  It acts via a ping-pong bi bi 
                     mechanism |CITS: [10806332]|.  The physiological role of 
                     NhoA is unknown.
                     Two acetylated lysine residues within NhoA can be 
                     deacetylated by |FRAME: G6577-MONOMER ""CobB""|.  Mutants 
                     of NhoA in which one or both lysine residues have been 
                     mutated have lower N-acetyltransferase activity than 
                     wild-type |CITS: [23452042]|.
                     NhoA may also act as an <i>N</i>-hydroxyarylamine 
                     <i>O</i>-acetyltransferase, although this activity has not 
                     been assayed directly.  However, this activity leads to 
                     metabolic activation and increased toxicity of nitro 
                     compounds.  <i>nhoA</i> mutants were shown to have 
                     increased resistance to the mutagenicity of nitro compounds
                     |CITS: [12222687][23452042]|.  Increased expression of 
                     <i>nhoA</i> in response to a panel of toxic substances has 
                     been measured; exposure to paraquat in particular increases
                     <i>nhoA</i> expression quickly |CITS: [19068836]|."
