     gene            complement(1540545..1541426)
                     /gene="yddG"
                     /locus_tag="b1473"
                     /label=yddG
     CDS             complement(1540545..1541426)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yddG"
                     /locus_tag="b1473"
                     /product="bifunctional amino acid exporter YddG / amino
                     acid exporter"
                     /label=yddG
                     /note="YddG is an amino acid exporter with broad
                     specificity.
                     YddG is a member of the Aromatic Amino Acid/Paraquat 
                     Exporter (ArAA/P-E) Family (TC:  2.A.7.17) within the 
                     Drug/Metabolite Transporter (DMT) superfamily |CITS: 
                     [26546518]|.
                     YddG is predicted to be an inner membrane protein with nine
                     or ten transmembrane domains; experimental topology 
                     analysis supports a model of 10 transmembrane helices with 
                     the N and C-termini located in the cytoplasm |CITS: 
                     [15044727][21042032]|
                     Expression of <I>yddG</I> from a multicopy plasmid results 
                     in increased resistance to phenylalanine, and to the 
                     aromatic amino acid analogues 
                     DL-<I>p</I>-fluorophenylalanine, 
                     DL-<I>o</I>-fluorophenylalanine, and 5-fluorotryptophane 
                     |CITS:[17784858]|. Overexpression of <i>yddG</i> in <i>E. 
                     coli</i> strains engineered to produce aromatic amino acids
                     is associated with accumulation of the respective amino 
                     acid (phenylalanine, tyrosine or tryptophan) in the culture
                     medium; overexpression of <i>yddG</i> enhances 
                     phenylalanine efflux in the Phe-producing strain 
                     |CITS:[17784858]|. Overexpression of <i>yddG</i> enhances 
                     L-tryptophan production in a Trp-producing strain |CITS: 
                     [23775271]|. Purified YddG reconstituted into liposomes 
                     transports L-threonine, L-methionine, L-lysine and 
                     L-glutamic acid; overexpression of <i>yddG</i> (in both 
                     <i>E. coli</i> W3110 wild type and &Delta;<i>yddG</i> 
                     backgrounds) is associated with a consistent increase of 
                     valine, threonine and isolecine in the culture medium 
                     suggesting that YddG transports a range of amino acids 
                     |CITS: [27281193]|."
