                     /product="trifunctional formate dehydrogenase N subunit
                     beta / formate dehydrogenase N, subcomplex / formate 
                     dehydrogenase N"
                     /EC_number="1.17.5.3"
                     /label=fdnH
                     /note="<i>fdnH</i> encodes the &beta; subunit of formate 
                     dehydrogenase N (Fdh-N); it contains four [4Fe-4S] clusters
                     (FS1, FS2, FS3 and FS4) and one C-terminal transmembrane 
                     helix |CITS: [1834669][11884747]|. FdnH serves as a conduit
                     for electrons that are transferred from the formate 
                     oxidation site in the &alpha; subunit (FdnG) to the 
                     menaquinone associated with the &gamma; subunit (FdnI) 
                     |CITS: [11884747]|.
                     FdnH is a putative C-tail-anchored (TA) membrane protein 
                     |CITS: [20406421]|."
