                     /product="trifunctional formate dehydrogenase N subunit
                     gamma / formate dehydrogenase N, subcomplex / formate 
                     dehydrogenase N"
                     /EC_number="1.17.5.3"
                     /label=fdnI
                     /note="<I>fdnI</i> encodes the &gamma; subunit of formate 
                     dehydrogenase-N (Fhd-N); it is an integral membrane protein
                     with four transmembrane helices, which, together with the 
                     single transmembrane helix of FdnH and a cardiolipin 
                     molecule, form a tightly packed trimer in the inner 
                     membrane. The &gamma; subunit contains two heme <i>b</i> 
                     groups - heme <i>b</i><sub>P</sub> located towards the 
                     periplasmic side of the membrane and heme 
                     <i>b</i><sub>C</sub> located towards the cytoplasmic face 
                     of the membrane - and a site for menaquinone reduction 
                     |CITS: [1834669][11884747]|."
