     gene            complement(1546655..1546939)
                     /gene="yddM"
                     /locus_tag="b1477"
                     /label=yddM
     CDS             complement(1546655..1546939)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yddM"
                     /locus_tag="b1477"
                     /product="DNA-binding transcriptional regulator YddM"
                     /label=yddM
                     /note="YddM, which contains a helix-turn-helix motif to
                     bind DNA in its N-terminal domain, appears to belong to the
                     Xre family of transcription factors (TFs), and it was 
                     predicted to regulate genes related to metabolism |CITS: 
                     [35880217]|.
                     YddM was confirmed as a TF through an integrated workflow 
                     comprised of computational prediction, knowledge-based 
                     classification, and experimental validation of candidate 
                     TFs at the genome scale |CITS: [30137486]|.
                     Compared to known global TFs, YddM exhibits some 
                     interesting regulatory features. First, it has more 
                     intragenic binding peaks and fewer peaks located within 
                     putative regulatory regions. Second, it has fewer binding 
                     peaks than global TFs, such as CRP, Lrp, Fnr, and ArcA. 
                     Third, it binds to more genes with putative functions. 
                     Finally, its expression level is lower relative to that of 
                     the majority of global TFs |CITS: [30137486]|.
                     Upstream of the <i>yddM</i> gene, a sequence was found that
                     could work as a transcriptional promoter, and the 
                     transcription of the <i>yddM</i> gene is affected by cold 
                     or heat stress |CITS: [35880217]|.
                     Interconnectivity between the <i>yddM</i> gene and the 
                     stress regulators <i>cspABE</i> and <i>oxyR</i> has been 
                     reported |CITS:[35835781]|.
                     The YddM binding landscape was globally mapped in vivo by 
                     standardized ChIP-seq and quantitatively modeled using 
                     BoltzNet, a biophysically informed neural network that 
                     infers binding energy from sequence data |CITS:[40335485]|.
                     The resulting ChIP-seq binding regions are available in 
                     RegulonDB (<a href=""https://regulondb.cc 
                     g.unam.mx/ht/dataset/TFBINDING/source=GALAGAN"">Galagan 
                     collection</a>), and the corresponding energy matrix and 
                     genomic binding profiles can be accessed at <a 
                     href=""http://boltznet.bu.edu"">boltznet.bu.edu</a> 
                     |CITS:[40335485]|."
