     gene            complement(1550083..1550220)
                     /gene="sra"
                     /locus_tag="b1480"
                     /label=sra
     CDS             complement(1550083..1550220)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="sra"
                     /locus_tag="b1480"
                     /product="ribosome-associated protein Sra"
                     /label=sra
                     /note="Sra is a 30S ribosomal subunit-associated protein
                     that is more abundant at stationary phase than during log 
                     phase growth |CITS: [3553169][11292794]|.
                     Transcription is induced |CITS: [11101804][11292794]| and 
                     protein abundance increases |CITS: [11292794]| under 
                     stationary phase conditions.  &sigma;<sup>S</sup>, cAMP, 
                     ppGpp, Fis, and IHF may be involved in the transcription of
                     <i>sra</i> during stationary phase |CITS: 
                     [11292794][15489429]|.  <i>sra</i> is also cotranscribed 
                     with the <i>bdm</i> gene from a promoter upstream of 
                     <i>bdm</i> which is activated by osmotic shock and 
                     dependent on the RcsCDB phosphorelay system |CITS: 
                     [15901715]|.  Sra protein production is increased during 
                     HipA-induced persistence |CITS: [34427514]|.
                     An <i>sra</i> deletion mutant does not have an obvious 
                     growth defect |CITS: [11292794][17277072]|.  |CITS: 
                     [30211949]| showed that a &Delta;<i>sra</i> mutant had an 
                     increased doubling time and decreased cell size.  A 
                     &Delta;<i>sra</i> mutant shows increased growth inhibition 
                     and lower antibiotic tolerance upon ectopic expression of 
                     HipA compared to wild type |CITS: [34427514]|.
                     Sra: ""<b>s</b>tationary-phase-induced 
                     <b>r</b>ibosome-<b>a</b>ssociated"" |CITS: [11292794]| 
                     Review: |CITS: [30476446]|"
                     /translation="MKSNRQARHILGLDHKISNQRKIVTEGDKSSVVNNPTGRKRPAEK
                     "
