     gene            complement(1550322..1550537)
                     /gene="bdm"
                     /locus_tag="b1481"
                     /label=bdm
     CDS             complement(1550322..1550537)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="bdm"
                     /locus_tag="b1481"
                     /product="biofilm-dependent modulation protein"
                     /label=bdm
                     /note="Bdm appears to be involved in regulating flagellar 
                     biosynthesis |CITS: [25398323]|.
                     <i>bdm</i> is a member of the Rcs regulon |CITS: 
                     [13129944][15901715]|.  It was originally reported that 
                     expression of <i>bdm</i> is reduced within biofilms and 
                     decreased by high osmolarity |CITS: [10498711]|.  However, 
                     other studies agree that expression is increased by high 
                     osmolarity |CITS: [12218039][15901715][18793315]| and that 
                     the increase is RcsB-dependent |CITS: [15901715]|. 
                     Expression of <i>bdm</i> is also upregulated by acid 
                     treatment |CITS: [18302792]|.  In addition, overexpression 
                     of <i>bdm</i> from a multicopy plasmid leads to enhanced 
                     biofilm formation |CITS: [19943899]|.
                     <i>bdm</i> mRNA is degraded by |FRAME: CPLX0-3281|; the 
                     sustained increase in <i>bdm</i> mRNA levels upon osmotic 
                     upshift requires downregulation of RNase III activity 
                     |CITS: [19943899]|.
                     Gene expression analysis of a <i>bdm</i> mutant compared to
                     wild type shows downregulation of a number of genes 
                     involved in flagellar biosynthesis, chemotaxis and 
                     motility.  A <i>bdm</i> deletion strain does not have a 
                     growth defect, but shows impaired motility |CITS: 
                     [25398323]|.
                     Bdm: ""<b>b</b>iofilm-<b>d</b>ependent <b>m</b>odulation"" 
                     |CITS: [15901715]|"
                     /translation="MFTYYQAENSTAEPALVNAIEQGLRAQHGVVTEDDILMELTKWVE
                     ASDNDILSDIYQQTINYVVSGQHPTL"
                     /go_process="positive regulation of bacterial-type
                     flagellum assembly [goid 1902210] [evidence IMP] [PMID 
                     25398323]"
