     gene            complement(1561761..1563080)
                     /gene="digH"
                     /locus_tag="b1491"
                     /label=digH
     CDS             complement(1561761..1563080)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="digH"
                     /locus_tag="b1491"
                     /product="divisome localized glycosyl hydrolase"
                     /label=digH
                     /note="DigH is a |FRAME: a-denuded-peptidoglycan denuded
                     glycan| specific hydrolase with either glucosaminidase or 
                     muramidase activity |CITS: [32152098]|. DigH-mediated 
                     hydrolysis of denuded glycans contributes to peptidoglycan 
                     degradation at the division septum |CITS: [40492729]|. DigH
                     contains a single glycosyl hydrolase-like 10 (GHL10) domain
                     and a predicted lipoprotein signal sequence; the protein 
                     localizes to the outer membrane. In a reaction containing 
                     the N-acetylmuramyl-L-alanine amidase |FRAME: G6452-MONOMER
                     ""AmiD""|, purified, soluble DigH cleaves peptidoglycan 
                     sacculi to produce a large fraction of disaccharides 
                     containing N-acetylglucosamine (GlcNAc) and N-acetylmuramic
                     acid (MurNAc) without a 1,6-anhydro linkage, and a small 
                     fraction of GlcNAc-1,6-anhydroMurNAc; no cleavage is 
                     observed in the absence of AmiD |CITS: [32152098]|.
                     Overexpression of <i>digH</i> suppresses the growth and 
                     division defect of a &Delta;<i>tol-pal</i> mutant (in LB 
                     lacking NaCL at 42&deg;C); suppressed cells continue to 
                     produce outer membrane vesicles when grown in minimal 
                     medium |CITS: [32152098]|. Overexpression of <i>digH</i> 
                     suppresses the chaining defect in '&Delta;LT' 
                     (&Delta;<i>mltACDE</i>&Delta;<i>slt</i>&Delta;<i>rlpA</i>) 
                     cells which lack lytic transglycosylase activity and would 
                     otherwise accumulate denuded glycans; deletion of 
                     <i>digH</i> in '&Delta;LT' cells produces a strong 
                     synthetic phenotype |CITS: [40492729]|.
                     DigH accumulates in cells lacking |FRAME: EG10760-MONOMER 
                     ""Prc protease""| (&Delta;<i>prc</i>); a DigH fluorescent 
                     fusion protein accumulates at midcell in dividing cells 
                     |CITS: [32152098]|.
                     <i>digH</i>: <U>di</U>visome-localized <U>g</U>lycosyl 
                     <U>h</U>ydrolase |CITS: [32152098]|"
