     gene            complement(1563211..1564746)
                     /gene="gadC"
                     /locus_tag="b1492"
                     /label=gadC
     CDS             complement(1563211..1564746)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="gadC"
                     /locus_tag="b1492"
                     /product="L-glutamate:4-aminobutyrate antiporter"
                     /label=gadC
                     /note="GadC, a glutamic acid:&gamma;-aminobutyrate
                     antiporter, is part of the glutamate-dependent acid 
                     resistance system 2 (AR2) which confers resistance to 
                     extreme acid conditions. When cells are grown at pH 2.5 
                     with glutamate, the internal pH reaches 4.2 which reflects 
                     the pH optimum of the glutamate decarboxylases |CITS: 
                     [15342572]|. Insertional inactivation of <I>gadC</I> 
                     results in sensitivity to extreme acid conditions (pH 2-3) 
                     and eliminates glutamate-dependent acid resistance |CITS: 
                     [8682809]|. GadC mediates export of &gamma;-aminobutyrate 
                     in exchange for glutamic acid. GadC is a member of the APC 
                     superfamily of amino acid transporters. AR2 also protects 
                     the cell during anaerobic phosphate starvation when 
                     glutamate is available by preventing damage from weak acids
                     produced from carbohydrate fermentation. <I>gadABC</I> 
                     mutants have reduced viability after anaerobic phosphate 
                     starvation compared to wild-type |CITS:[17209032]|.
                     GadC, together with |FRAME: CPLX0-7694|, constitutes a 
                     glutamine-mediated acid resistance system |CITS: 
                     [23337585]|.
                     GadC is implicated in maintaining antibiotic tolerance 
                     under starvation; <i>gadC</i> is upregulated during 
                     nutrient starvation and the starvation-induced ampicillin 
                     tolerance levels of a <i>gadC</i> knockout strain are 
                     significantly reduced over both a 6 and 30 day period 
                     |CITS: [34787438]|.
                     The identical protein derived from <i>E. coli</i> strain 
                     O157:H7 has been purified and characterized |CITS: 
                     [22407317]|.
                     <i>xasA</i>: e<U>x</U>treme <U>a</U>cid <U>s</U>ensitive 
                     |CITS: [8682809]|"
                     /translation="MATSVQTGKAKQLTLLGFFAITASMVMAVYEYPTFATSGFSLVFF
