     gene            complement(1566664..1569459)
                     /gene="pqqL"
                     /locus_tag="b1494"
                     /label=pqqL
     CDS             complement(1566664..1569459)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="pqqL"
                     /locus_tag="b1494"
                     /product="periplasmic metalloprotease"
                     /label=pqqL
                     /note="PqqL is a periplasmic protein; a 26 residue signal 
                     peptide is cleaved <i>in vivo</i>. Purified recombinant 
                     PqqL, crystallized in the absence of substrate, contains 
                     two M16 protease domains each of which forms one half of an
                     extended 'clam-shell like' structure; the N-terminal domain
                     contains a putative zinc ion in the protease active site. 
                     PqqL is flexible in solution. Purified PqqL cleaves a small
                     subset of peptides within a combinatorial peptide library; 
                     it does not show proteolytic activity towards human 
                     ferredoxins and globins, or plant ferredoxin |CITS: 
                     [31613892]|.
                     <i>pqqL</i> is located in a 3 gene cluster 
                     (<i>yddA-yddB-ppqL</i>) which may represent a 3-component 
                     iron-uptake system |CITS: [12746439][25222563]|. Distant 
                     homologs (<i>fusD, fusA</i> and <i>fusC</i> respectively) 
                     encode a ferredoxin uptake system (Fus) in plant pathogenic
                     <i>Pectobacterium</i> spp. |CITS: [31613892]|. <i>pqqL</i> 
                     expression increases under iron-limiting conditions; PqqL 
                     does not support growth during iron limitation in LB media 
                     but may have a niche specific role in iron acquisition from
                     a distinct protein substrate |CITS: [31613892]|.
                     PqqL is a putative zinc peptidase; <i>pqqL</i> is part of a
                     5 ORF fragment that is able to complement 
                     <i><u>p</u></i>yro<i><u>q</u></i>uinoline 
                     <i><u>q</u></i>uinone (<i>ppqE</i> and <i>ppqF</i>) mutants
                     of <i>Methylobacterium organophilum</i> |CITS: [9116051]|.
                     In a large genetic interaction screen, <i>pqqL</i> showed 
                     genetic interactions with a number of proteins involved in 
                     translation and ribosome biogenesis |CITS: [27732863]|.
                     In uropathogenic <i>E. coli</i> (UPEC) strain CFT073, 
                     <i>pqqL</i> plays a role in fitness during systemic 
                     infection in a mammalian host |CITS: [24339777]|.
                     "
