     gene            complement(1569504..1571876)
                     /gene="yddB"
                     /locus_tag="b1495"
                     /label=yddB
     CDS             complement(1569504..1571876)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yddB"
                     /locus_tag="b1495"
                     /product="putative TonB-dependent receptor YddB"
                     /label=yddB
                     /note="YddB is an outer membrane protein; YddB forms a
                     22-strand &beta;-barrel with an N-terminal globular domain 
                     that folds into the barrel plugging the pore; the protein 
                     contains 11 extracellular loops which are predicted to form
                     an external binding site |CITS: [31613892]|
                     YddB is a distant homologue of FusA - the TonB-dependent 
                     outer membrane receptor of a ferredoxin uptake system (Fus)
                     in plant pathogenic <i>Pectobacterium</i> spp.; YddB is 
                     structurally analagous to FusA |CITS: [31613892]|. 
                     <i>yddB</i> is located in a 3 gene cluster with Fus 
                     homologs - <i>yddA</i> (<i>fusD</i>) predicted to be encode
                     an inner membrane transporter and and <i>ppqL</i> 
                     (<i>fusC</i>) predicted to encode a substrate processing 
                     protein |CITS: [31613892]|; the cluster may represent a 
                     3-component iron-uptake system |CITS: 
                     [12746439][25222563]|. YddB does not support growth during 
                     iron limitation in LB media but may have a niche specific 
                     role in iron acquisition from a distinct protein substrate 
                     |CITS: [31613892]|. In uropathogenic <i>E. coli</i> (UPEC) 
                     strain CFT073, <i>yddB</i> plays a role in fitness during 
                     systemic infection in a mammalian host |CITS: [24339777]|. 
                     Screening of a random transposon mutant library suggests 
                     that YddB is required for growth under optimum growth 
                     conditions (rich medium at 37&deg;C), but not under cold 
                     conditions (15&deg;C) or in minimal medium |CITS: 
                     [15380559]|."
