     gene            complement(1578019..1578216)
                     /gene="safA"
                     /locus_tag="b1500"
                     /label=safA
     CDS             complement(1578019..1578216)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="safA"
                     /locus_tag="b1500"
                     /product="two-component system connector SafA"
                     /label=safA
                     /note="SafA is a small membrane protein that functions to 
                     connect the the |FRAME: PWY0-1490 ""EvgS/EvgA""| and 
                     |FRAME: PWY0-1458 ""PhoQ/PhoP""| two component systems; 
                     activation of the EvgS/EvgA system induces SafA which in 
                     turn activates the PhoQ/PhoP system to induce PhoP 
                     regulated genes (see |CITS: [18832064]|). SafA contributes 
                     to a complex network of acid resistance gene regulation 
                     (see |CITS: [21193607][20603130]|).
                     <i>safA</i> forms an operon with <i>ydeO</i>; 
                     <i>safA-ydeO</i> is a member of the EvgA regulon |CITS: 
                     [12399493][12694615]|; <i>safA-ydeO</i> is up-regulated 
                     when the EvgS/EvgA two-component system is activated |CITS:
                     [19352034]|. Deletion of <i>safA</i> results in a slight 
                     decrease in survival at pH 2.5 |CITS: [12399493]|. 
                     Expression of <i>safA</i> from a heterologous promoter 
                     activates expression of PhoP regulon genes (eg <i>mgtA, 
                     mgrB, rstAB, slyB</i> and others) in a PhoQ/PhoP dependent 
                     manner |CITS: [17998538]|. SafA interacts with, and 
                     activates PhoQ |CITS: [17998538][ 22651704]| (see also 
                     |CITS: [30632929]|); SafA activates the autophosphorylation
                     of PhoQ |CITS: [23563556]|.
                     SafA is a Type II membrane protein that spans the membrane 
                     once with its N-terminus in the cytoplasm |CITS: 
                     [17998538][2275815]|.
                     SafA: <b>S</b>ensor-<b>a</b>ssociating <b>f</b>actor 
                     <b>A</b> |CITS: [21193607]|"
