     gene            1600357..1601232
                     /gene="lsrF"
                     /locus_tag="b1517"
                     /label=lsrF
     CDS             1600357..1601232
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="lsrF"
                     /locus_tag="b1517"
                     /product="3-hydroxy-2,4-pentadione 5-phosphate thiolase"
                     /EC_number="2.3.1.245"
                     /label=lsrF
                     /note="LsrF is the final enzyme in the pathway for
                     degradation of the intercellular signaling molecule AI-2. 
                     It acts as a 3-hydroxy-2,4-pentadione 5-phosphate (P-HPD) 
                     thiolase, catalyzing the transfer of the acetyl group of 
                     P-HPD to coenzyme A |CITS: [25225400]|.  LsrF was noted to 
                     have similarity to class I aldolases |CITS: 
                     [17274596][19714241]|, and the activity described in |CITS:
                     [25225400]| is novel for this family of enzymes. Kinetic 
                     measurements showed a positive Hill coefficient for both 
                     substrates, P-HPD and coenzyme A, indicating cooperativity 
                     |CITS: [25225400]|.
                     Crystal structures of LsrF were solved in both the apo form
                     and in complex with phospho-AI-2 analogs.  The protein is a
                     homodecamer of (&alpha;&beta;)<sub>8</sub> barrels with 
                     domain-swapped N termini, and the structure is similar to 
                     that of class I aldolases that process phosphorylated 
                     sugars.  The structural conservation extends to the 
                     predicted ligand binding sites and catalytic residues such 
                     as Lys203 |CITS: [19714241]|.  The K203A, D251A and D57A 
                     mutants show no catalytic activity; based on these results,
                     a reaction mechanism was proposed |CITS: [25225400]|.
                     LsrF is expressed as part of the <i>lsr</i> operon involved
                     in AI-2 transport and processing |CITS: [17274596]|.  
                     Deletion of <i>lsrF</i> leads to accumulation of 
                     phospho-AI-2 |CITS: [25225400]|.
                     LsrF: ""<b>L</b>ux<b>S</b> <b>r</b>egulated"""
