     CDS             complement(1603486..1604937)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="uxaB"
                     /locus_tag="b1521"
                     /product="tagaturonate reductase"
                     /EC_number="1.1.1.58"
                     /label=uxaB
                     /note="Altronate oxidoreductase is the second enzyme of
                     the galacturonate catabolism pathway, catalyzing the 
                     reversible NADH-dependent reduction of D-tagaturonate to 
                     D-altronate |CITS: [4402917]|.
                     The reaction proceeds via an ordered bi-bi mechanism with 
                     NADH as the first substrate |CITS: [4351434]|.
                     Expression of <i>uxaB</i> is repressed by ExuR |CITS: 
                     [6997263][7026975]|, induced by galacturonate |CITS: 
                     [6296052]|, and is sensitive to catabolite repression 
                     |CITS: [7026975]|.
                     In a <i>crp</i> mutant selected for increased acetate 
                     tolerance, expression of <i>uxaB</i> is decreased during 
                     exposure to acetate.  Overexpression of <i>uxaB</i> in a 
                     wild type strain decreases its growth rate under acetate 
                     stress |CITS: [24124618]|."
