                     /product="bifunctional glutaminase 2 / glutaminase"
                     /EC_number="3.5.1.2"
                     /label=glsB
                     /note="GlsB (YneH) is a glutaminase that is highly
                     selective for L-glutamine.  Based on the pH profile of the 
                     enzymatic activity, GlsB was proposed to correspond to the 
                     previously identified |FRAME: GLUTAMINB-CPLX| of <i>E. 
                     coli</i> B.  Glutamine binding exhibits positive 
                     cooperativity |CITS: [18459799]|.
                     A <i>glsB</i> deletion mutant grows two times slower than 
                     wild-type on glutamine as the sole source of carbon and 
                     nitrogen |CITS: [18459799]|.  A &Delta;<i>glsB</i> mutant 
                     has no defect in glutamine-dependent acid resistance |CITS:
                     [23337585]|.
                     Review: |CITS: [NANDAKUMAR03]|
