                     /gene="ydeA"
                     /locus_tag="b1528"
                     /product="bifunctional putative exporter YdeA /
                     L-arabinose exporter"
                     /label=ydeA
                     /note="YdeA is a member of the major facilitator
                     superfamily (MFS) of transporters |CITS: [9529885]|. 
                     Overexpression of <I>ydeA</I> interferes with the 
                     intracellular accumulation of arabinose and this effect is 
                     dependent on the proton motive force; mutational activation
                     of the <i>ydeA</i> promoter inhibits activation of the 
                     arabinose-inducible P<sub>BAD</sub> promoter |CITS: 
                     [10094697]| (see also |CITS: [10438792]|). Deletion of 
                     <i>ydeA</i> (in strain MG1655) does not affect the 
                     intracellular concentration of arabinose; overexpression of
                     <i>ydeA</i> reduces the intracellular concentration of 
                     arabinose; expression of <i>ydeA</i> is induced by 
                     arabinose |CITS: [22952739]|. YdeA may function to limit 
                     the acumulation of toxic sugar phosphates |CITS: 
                     [22952739]|.
                     Crystal structures of YdeA (from <i>E. coli</i> strain 
                     BL21) in different conformations have been determined and 
                     are informative of the alternating access mechanism of 
                     transport |CITS: [33280821]|.
                     Overexpression of cloned <I>ydeA</I> in a K-12 strain which
                     lacks the major efflux pump permease AcrB (<i>E. coli</i> 
                     KAM3; see |CITS: [12618449]|) does not impact resistance to
                     a range of antibiotics, dyes and toxic compounds 
                     |CITS:[11566977]|.
                     <i>ydeA</i> is one of 35 efflux-encoding genes that have 
                     been deleted or inactivated in 'Efflux KnockOut-35' 
                     (EKO-35) -  a K-12 BW25133-derived strain that lacks 35 
                     efflux pumps and can be used as a platform to study their 
                     function |CITS: [36065018][36318669]|."
