     gene            complement(1612500..1613165)
                     /gene="marC"
                     /locus_tag="b1529"
                     /label=marC
     CDS             complement(1612500..1613165)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="marC"
                     /locus_tag="b1529"
                     /product="inner membrane protein MarC"
                     /label=marC
                     /note="MarC is an inner membrane protein with six
                     predicted transmembrane domains.  The C terminus is located
                     in the periplasm |CITS: [11867724][15919996]|. MarC is not 
                     involved in multiple antibiotic resistance |CITS: 
                     [17954692]|.
                     MarC, YchE and YhgN are paralogs.  Neither a <i>marC</i> 
                     single deletion mutant nor a triple <i>marC ychE yhgN</i> 
                     deletion mutant shows a difference in susceptibility to 
                     various antibiotics compared to wild type |CITS: 
                     [17954692]|.  Overexpression of MarC also has no effect on 
                     antibiotic susceptibility |CITS: [17954692]|.
                     Although <i>marC</i> mRNA levels are increased by 
                     tetracycline and chloramphenicol |CITS: 
                     [8383113][17954692]|, this is likely due to mRNA 
                     stabilization |CITS: [17954692]|.  <i>marC</i> expression 
                     is not regulated by MarR |CITS: [17954692]|. Non-synonymous
                     SNPs |CITS: [21364744]| and an IS1 insertion |CITS: 
                     [21435272]| in <i>marC</i> were identified in adaptive 
                     laboratory evolution (ALE) experiments selecting for 
                     increased isobutanol tolerance. <i>marC</i> mutants were 
                     also identified in ALE experiments selecting for increased 
                     isoprenol tolerance |CITS: [33292484]|.  A <i>marC</i> 
                     deletion mutant increases isobutanol tolerance |CITS: 
                     [21435272]|. Overexpression of <i>marC</i> from an ASKA 
                     plasmid leads to a more than 3-fold increase in the MIC of 
                     hypochlorous acid |CITS: [34072091]|.
                     MarC: |CITS: [8723480]|
                     Note:  The <i>marC</i>/<i>soxR</i> mutation maps at 92 min 
                     |CITS: [7986007]| and is therefore distinct from
                     the <i>marC</i>/<i>b1529</i> gene.
                     "
