                     /note="<I>marB</I> is part of the <I>marRAB</I> operon,
                     which is known to have a role in multiple antibiotic 
                     resistance |CITS:[8383113]|. MarB is located in the 
                     periplasm |CITS: [23710538]|. Deletion of <i>marB</i> 
                     results in increased expression of <i>marA</i> |CITS: 
                     [21185072], [23710538]|."
