                     /product="dipeptide exporter"
                     /label=ydeE
                     /note="YdeE is a member of the Drug:H<sup>+</sup>
                     Antiporter-1 (DHA) family within the Major Facilitator 
                     Superfamily (MFS) of transporters |CITS: [26546518]|. YdeE 
                     has been implicated in arabinose efflux |CITS: [22952739]|.
                     YdeE is able to transport dipeptides (Ala-Gln and 
                     L-alanyl-L-branched chain amino acids) in a dipeptide 
                     overproducing strain |CITS: [20067529]|. Overexpression of 
                     cloned <I>ydeE</I> (<i>ydeF</i>) in a K-12 strain which 
                     lacks the major efflux pump permease AcrB (<i>E. coli</i> 
                     KAM3; see |CITS: [12618449]|) does not impact resistance to
                     a range of antibiotics, dyes and toxic compounds 
                     |CITS:[11566977]|.
                     <i>ydeE</i> (<i>ydeF</i>) is one of 35 efflux-encoding 
                     genes that have been deleted or inactivated in 'Efflux 
                     KnockOut-35' (EKO-35) -  a K-12 BW25133-derived strain that
                     lacks 35 efflux pumps and can be used as a platform to 
                     study their function |CITS: [36065018][36318669]|.
                     "
