     gene            1616903..1616998
                     /gene="mgtS"
                     /locus_tag="b4599"
                     /label=mgtS
     CDS             1616903..1616998
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="mgtS"
                     /locus_tag="b4599"
                     /product="small protein MgtS"
                     /label=mgtS
                     /note="MgtS is a small, inner membrane protein which
                     interacts with the Mg<sup>2+</sup> transporter, |FRAME: 
                     MGTA-MONOMER ""MgtA""| and the |FRAME: PITA-MONOMER ""PitA 
                     low-affinity phosphate transporter""| to promote 
                     intracellular Mg<sup>2+</sup> accumulation; the 
                     interactions are implicated in regulatory cross-talk 
                     between Mg<sup>2+</sup> and phosphate homeostasis
                     When grown under Mg<sup>2+</sup> limitation and compared to
                     the wild-type, a &Delta;<i>mgtS</i> mutant has lower 
                     intracellular Mg<sup>2+</sup> levels and displays a growth 
                     defect; MgtS and MgtA co-purify in a reciprocal manner 
                     |CITS: [28512220]|. MgtA accumulates normally in a 
                     &Delta;<i>mgtS</i> strain that overexpresses a known FtsH 
                     substrate (phage lambda cII protein), indicating that MgtS 
                     may act to stabilize MgtA by inhibiting FtsH proteolysis of
                     MgtA |CITS: [28512220]|.
                     Overexpression of <i>mgtS</i> activates the |FRAME: 
                     PWY0-1483 ""PhoRB two-component system""| during growth in 
                     rich media and this activation requires the |FRAME: 
                     PITA-MONOMER ""PitA low-affinity phosphate transporter""|; 
                     MgtS interacts physically with PitA and this interaction 
                     contributes to an increase in intracellular Mg<sup>2+</sup>
                     levels |CITS: [30276893]|.
                     MgtS contains a predicted transmembrane segment, and the 
                     protein can be found in the membrane fraction |CITS: 
                     [19121005]|. Using a sucrose fractionation protocol the 
                     majority of MgtS partitions into the inner membrane 
                     fraction |CITS: [21778229]|. Topology assays using GFP and 
                     PhoA fusion proteins suggest that MgtS is oriented with the
                     C-terminus in the cytoplasm |CITS: [21778229]|. <i>mgtS</i>
                     mRNA has been detected |CITS: [11445539]|. <i>mgtS</i> is 
                     expressed during stationary phase (data not shown) |CITS: 
                     [19121005]|.  Expression of <i>mgtS</i> is lower in minimal
                     glucose medium than in rich medium, increases upon heat 
                     shock and SDS/EDTA treatment, and decreases upon diamide 
                     treatment |CITS: [19734316]| and in stationary phase |CITS:
                     [30837344]|.
                     Expression of <i>mgtS</i> is induced by low Mg<sup>2+</sup>
                     in a PhoPQ-dependent manner |CITS: [19889087][28512220]|.
                     Review: |CITS: [30810554]|"
