     gene            complement(1617074..1617171)
                     /gene="mgrR"
                     /locus_tag="b4698"
                     /label=mgrR
     misc_RNA        complement(1617074..1617171)
                     /gene="mgrR"
                     /locus_tag="b4698"
                     /product="small regulatory RNA MgrR"
                     /note="MgrR is a conserved small regulatory RNA that may
                     affect lipopolysaccharide composition |CITS: [19889087]|. 
                     Potential regulatory targets of MgrR were identified by 
                     RIL-seq |CITS: [27588604]|. MgrR negatively regulates the 
                     levels of SoxS |CITS: [27137887]| and the cation-phosphate 
                     symporter PitA |CITS: [30276893]|.
                     A combination of data suggests that base pairing of MgrR 
                     with the <i>eptB</i> mRNA promotes Rho-dependent 
                     transcription termination and may protect the 5' mRNA 
                     fragment from degradation |CITS: [33460557]|.
                     MgrR was first identified in an intergenic region with a 
                     high Hfq co-immunoprecipitation signal on microarrays 
                     |CITS: [14622403]|. MgrR is highly expressed in rich growth
                     media and may be stabilized by Hfq; expression is 
                     positively regulated by the PhoPQ system in response to 
                     Mg<sup>2+</sup> concentration |CITS: [19889087]|. At high 
                     Ca<sup>2+</sup> levels, expression of MgrR is significantly
                     decreased |CITS: [23659637]|.
                     MgrR was classified as a Class II small RNA, which 
                     accumulate to higher levels in the rim mutants and to 
                     reduced levels in distal face mutants of Hfq |CITS: 
                     [26373314]|. Small RNAs compete for binding to Hfq. 
                     Expression of OxyS at physiologically relevant levels 
                     reduces the abundance of other small RNAs including MgrR 
                     and reduces their association with Hfq. Increased levels of
                     Hfq overcome this competition effect |CITS: [22040174]|. 
                     The interaction of MgrR with Hfq |CITS: [30217864] 
                     [36328526]| and its effect on the interaction of MgrR with 
                     target mRNAs has been studied in more detail |CITS: 
                     [30217864]|.
                     An <i>mgrR</i> mutant is ten times more resistant to 
                     Polymyxin B than wild type, likely due to the effect of 
                     MgrR on <i>eptB</i> expression |CITS: [19889087]|.
                     MgrR: ""<b>Mg</b><sup>2+</sup> <b>r</b>esponsive 
                     <b>R</b>NA"" |CITS: [19889087]|
                     Reviews: |CITS: [19906183][26618164][29992897][32213244]|"
