                     /gene="ydfJ"
                     /locus_tag="b1543"
                     /product="putative transporter YdfJ"
                     /label=ydfJ
                     /note="The YdfJ protein is an uncharacterised member of
                     the Metabolite:H<sup>+</sup> Symporter (MHS) family within 
                     the Major Facilitator Superfamily (MFS) of transporters 
                     |CITS: [9529885][26546518]|.
                     Heterologous expression of cloned <i>ydfJ</i> (expressed in
                     the mammalian cell line, HEK-293) produces a functional 
                     K<sup>+</sup> channel |CITS: [21744086]|.
                     <i>ydfJ</i> may constitute the C-terminal portion of an 
                     ancestral gene disrupted by an insertion of the cryptic 
                     prophage Qin/Kim.  The N-terminal fragment may be |FRAME: 
                     G0-10559 <i>ynfP</i>|."
