     gene            complement(1632712..1632924)
                     /gene="cspI"
                     /locus_tag="b1552"
                     /label=cspI
     CDS             complement(1632712..1632924)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="cspI"
                     /locus_tag="b1552"
                     /product="Qin prophage; cold shock-like protein CspI"
                     /label=cspI
                     /note="CspI is a cold shock protein with complex
                     regulation. CspI protein levels are highest between 
                     10-15&deg;C |CITS: [10049393]|. <i>cspI</i> belongs to a 
                     small set of genes whose expression is upregulated and 
                     whose absence is a competitive disadvantage in long-term 
                     stationary phase (LTSP) |CITS: [32753505]|.
                     Expression of <i>cspI</i> is transiently induced upon cold 
                     shock. In addition, at 37&deg;C, <i>cspI</i> mRNA is 
                     unstable, with a half life of ~20 seconds; after 1 hour of 
                     temperature downshift, the <i>cspI</i> half life increases 
                     dramatically to 14 minutes. The 5' UTR of the <i>cspI</i> 
                     mRNA negatively affects its own expression at 37&deg;C 
                     |CITS: [10049393]|. In defined rich medium at 37&deg;C, 
                     expression of <i>cspI</i> is highest in mid-log phase. 
                     Transcription of <i>cspI</i> is induced by cold shock in 
                     both defined rich and defined minimal media |CITS: 
                     [24952137]|. Regulation of <i>cspI</i> expression by CRP 
                     appears to be indirect |CITS: [25637299]|.
                     Expression of <i>cspI</i> is upregulated in LTSP, and it is
                     expressed at higher levels in LTSP than in any other growth
                     phase. A <i>cspI</i> mutant has a competitive disadvantage 
                     compared to wild-type in LTSP |CITS: [32753505]|.
                     An <i>in-silico</i> comparative study of evolution, 
                     structure and function was carried out for the 9 CspA 
                     family of proteins in <i>E. coli K-12</i>. Despite high 
                     homology (>70% amino acid sequence similarity), it was 
                     determined that 4 paralogous pairs could be identified and 
                     served as the focus for the comparative analyses: 
                     CspA/CspB, CspC/CspE, CspG/CspI and CspF/CspH |CITS: 
                     [37333716]|. A follow-up study conducted mutational 
                     analysis and molecular modeling to determine selection 
                     pressure on the paralogous pairs |CITS: [39779584]|. 
                     Review: |CITS: [9484881][17437059]|"
                     /translation="MSNKMTGLVKWFNPEKGFGFITPKDGSKDVFVHFSAIQSNDFKTL
                     TENQEVEFGIENGPKGPAAVHVVAL"
