     gene            complement(1639376..1639531)
                     /gene="hokD"
                     /locus_tag="b1562"
                     /label=hokD
     CDS             complement(1639376..1639531)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="hokD"
                     /locus_tag="b1562"
                     /product="Qin prophage; toxic protein HokD"
                     /label=hokD
                     /note="Sequence analysis indicates that the <i>hokD</i>
                     gene is a homologue of the <i>hok</i> (host killing) gene 
                     which is responsible for mediating plasmid stabilization by
                     post-segregational killing (PSK) in plasmid R1. <i>hok</i> 
                     encodes a stable mRNA whose translation is inhibited by a 
                     less stable mRNA encoded by <i>sok</i>. The stable mRNA 
                     from <i>hokD</i> encodes a polypeptide that induction 
                     experiments have shown to be toxic to <i>E. coli</i>, 
                     resulting in loss of membrane potential, cell respiration 
                     arrest, morphological changes, and host cell death |CITS: 
                     [3019679]|.
                     The <i>hokD</i> gene is post-transcriptionally regulated in
                     <i>E. coli</i> |CITS: [2693900]|. Sequence analysis has 
                     also shown that the <i>hokD</i> locus has a fold-back 
                     inhibition element downstream of the <i>hokD</i> reading 
                     frame, but lacks the upstream regulatory elements of a 
                     <i>hok</i>-homologous gene system. The <i>hokD</i> system 
                     is therefore believed to have been inactivated by genetic 
                     rearrangement |CITS: [10361310]|.
                     Experiments for the development of biological containment 
                     systems have been performed by using the <i>hokD</i> gene 
                     as part of a suicide mechanism to prevent the survival of 
                     bacteria outside of the laboratory |CITS: 
                     [2036024][7793926]|.
                     Hok: ""<b>ho</b>st <b>k</b>illing""
                     Review: |CITS: [2101633]|"
                     /translation="MKQQKAMLIALIVICLTVIVTALVTRKDLCEVRIRTGQTEVAVFT
                     AYEPEE"
