                     /product="Qin prophage; protein YdfW"
                     /label=ydfW
                     /note="Overexpression of <i>ydfW</i> increases fitness as
                     well as resistance to several antibiotics, including 
                     spiramycin and erythromycin |CITS: [21173244]|.
                     A <i>ydfW</i> null mutant was reported to produce less 
                     hydrogen than wild type under fermentation conditions.  A 
                     <i>ydfW</i> expression clone from the ASKA library does not
                     complement the phenotype |CITS: [24025676]|. <i>ydfW</i> 
                     may represent a significantly truncated allele of a phage 
                     integrase.  Note in ASAP: ""N-terminal deletion of 1129 
                     nucleotides relative to Escherichia coli ATCC 8739 
                     (ASAP:AEM-0007804)."""
