                     /note="YnfP was identified as an expressed small protein;
                     low levels of expression were detected at stationary phase 
                     |CITS: [29645342]|.
                     <i>ynfP</i> may constitute the N-terminal fragment of a 
                     gene disrupted by an insertion of the cryptic prophage 
                     Qin/Kim.  The C-terminal fragment may be |FRAME: G6817 
                     <i>ydfJ</i>|, which, upon heterologous expression, was able
                     to produce a functional protein even without this 
                     N-terminal fragment."
