     gene            1658763..1659377
                     /gene="dmsD"
                     /locus_tag="b1591"
                     /label=dmsD
     CDS             1658763..1659377
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="dmsD"
                     /locus_tag="b1591"
                     /product="redox enzyme maturation protein DmsD"
                     /label=dmsD
                     /note="DmsD binds to the twin-arginine leaders of certain 
                     proteins, including dimethylsulfoxide (DMSO) reductase and 
                     trimethylamine N-oxide (TMAO) reductase that are 
                     translocated to the cytoplasmic membrane or the periplasm 
                     by the Sec-independent system that is termed Mtt (membrane 
                     targeting and transport) or more frequently Tat 
                     (twin-arginine translocation) |CITS: [11309116], 
                     [19151138]|. DmsD interacts with the membrane-associated 
                     Tat complex under anaerobic but not aerobic growth |CITS: 
                     [12813051]| and is essential for the biogenesis of DMSO 
                     reductase
                     |CITS: [12527378]|. DmsD interacts with the TatB and TatC 
                     subunits of the Tat complex |CITS: [12813051]|. DmsD has 
                     been purified, yielding a mixture of at least five 
                     different folding forms, three of which bind to the 
                     twin-arginine leader sequence of DmsA |CITS: [14766221]|. 
                     The DmsD residues important for this association have been 
                     identified |CITS: [18247574]|.
                     DmsD also binds to the twin arginine leader peptide of YnfE
                     and YnfF, both components of a putative selenate reductase 
                     (YnfEFGH) |CITS:[19151138], [19415239]|. An <i>E.coli 
                     dmsD</i> null mutant is unable to reduce selenate to 
                     selenium |CITS:[19415239]|. DmsD interacts with the 
                     molecular chaperones DnaK, DnaJ, GrpE, GroEL, TF and Ef-Tu 
                     and with the MoeAB proteins of the molybdopterin 
                     biosynthesis pathway |CITS: [20153451]|.
                     X-ray crystal structures of DmsD have been determined 
                     |CITS:[19361518], [19652330]|. DmsD has an &alpha;-helical 
                     structure composed of 10 helices |CITS: [19652330]|. 
                     Molecular dynamics simulation experiments have predicted a 
                     model for the DmsD-DmsA leader peptide complex 
                     |CITS:[19361518]|."
