     CDS             1659572..1660828
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="clcB"
                     /locus_tag="b1592"
                     /product="bifunctional putative chloride:H(+) antiporter
                     ClcB / chloride:H(+) antiporter"
                     /label=clcB
                     /note="ClcB is a member of the ubiquitous ClC family of 
                     Cl<sup>-</sup> channels which promote the the selective 
                     flow of Cl<sup>-</sup> ions across cell membranes |CITS: 
                     [10539975]|. <i>E. coli</i> K-12 contains two chloride 
                     channels, one of which - |FRAME: EG12331 ""ClcA""| - has 
                     been characterized as a chloride:H<sup>+</sup> antiporter 
                     |CITS: [14985752]|.
                     Cells lacking both ClcB and ClcA do not survive acid shock 
                     conditions (pH2.5, 2 hrs at 37&deg;C in minimal medium) and
                     a biological role for them in the extreme acid resistance 
                     (XAR) response has been proposed |CITS: [12384697]|."
