     gene            1663956..1665209
                     /gene="ynfM"
                     /locus_tag="b1596"
                     /label=ynfM
     CDS             1663956..1665209
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ynfM"
                     /locus_tag="b1596"
                     /product="putative transporter YnfM"
                     /label=ynfM
                     /note="Expression of cloned <I>ynfLM</I> in a K-12 strain
                     which lacks the major efflux pump permease AcrB (<i>E. 
                     coli</i> KAM3; see |CITS: [12618449]|) confers 
                     hypersensitivity to acriflavine (minimum inhibitory 
                     concentration, 12.5 &micro;g/mL for KAM3 versus 3.13 
                     &micro;g/mL for KAM3/pUCynfLM) but does not impact the 
                     resistance to a range of other antibiotics, dyes and toxic 
                     compounds; expression of cloned <i>ynfM</i> (pTrcHynfM) 
                     cannot be detected and KAM3 cells harbouring this 
                     expression vector do not exhibit the acriflavine 
                     hypersensitivity phenotype |CITS:[11566977]|.
                     In the Transporter Classification Database, YnfM is a 
                     member of the Acriflavin-sensitivity family within the 
                     Major Facilitator Superfamily (MFS) |CITS: 
                     [9529885][26546518]|. YnfM has been implicated in arabinose
                     efflux |CITS: [22952739]|.
                     <i>ynfM</i> is one of 35 efflux-encoding genes that have 
                     been deleted or inactivated in 'Efflux KnockOut-35' 
                     (EKO-35) -  a K-12 BW25133-derived strain that lacks 35 
                     efflux pumps and can be used as a platform to study their 
                     function |CITS: [36065018][36318669]|."
