                     /label=mdtU
     CDS             complement(1667865..1667966)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="mdtU"
                     /locus_tag="b4777"
                     /product="protein MdtU"
                     /label=mdtU
                     /note="MdtU was identified as a previously unannotated
                     small protein; it is expressed in both exponential and 
                     stationary phase in rich media |CITS: [30837344]|. 
                     Transcription of <i>mdtUJI</i> is induced by spermidine at 
                     pH 9; translation of MdtU is required for 
                     spermidine-mediated expression of MdtJ.  Rho-dependent 
                     transcription termination between the MdtU and MdtJ coding 
                     regions was discovered by RNA 3' end mapping |CITS: 
                     [33460557]|.
                     MdtU: ""<b>Mdt u</b>pstream ORF"" |CITS: [33460557]|"
                     /translation="MDNLFRTLFSTFTHLRTSSTILLVGEQHWRNAL"
     gene            1668170..1669204
                     /gene="tqsA"
                     /locus_tag="b1601"
                     /label=tqsA
     CDS             1668170..1669204
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="tqsA"
                     /locus_tag="b1601"
                     /product="autoinducer 2 exporter"
                     /label=tqsA
                     /note="TqsA has been implicated in autoinducer 2 (AI-2) 
                     transport - it may be involved in exporting AI-2 or 
                     inhibiting its uptake.  A <i>tqsA</I> knockout mutant (K-12
                     BW25113 &Delta;<i>tqsA::kan</i>) has significantly less 
                     extracellular AI-2 activity and signficantly more 
                     intracellular AI-2 activity compared to the wild-type 
                     strain, and is more resistant than wild-type to a number of
                     drugs. The <i>tqsA</I> knockout increases biofilm formation
                     in M9 glucose media - a phenotype that is complemented by 
                     the expression of <i>tqsA</i> in <i>trans</i> |CITS: 
                     [16385049]|. The protein product is predicted to be a 
                     mostly &alpha;-helical membrane protein with seven or eight
                     transmembrane segments |CITS: [16385049]|.
                     TqsA is a member of the Autoinducer-2 Exporter (AI-2E) 
                     Family of transporters |CITS: [24225317]|.
                     <i>tqsA</I>: <U>t</U>ransporter of 
                     <U>q</U>uorum-<U>s</U>ensing signal <U>A</U>I-2
                     Review: |CITS: [20559013]|"
