                     transhydrogenase"
                     /EC_number="7.1.1.1"
                     /label=pntB
                     /note="<i>pntB</i> encodes the &beta; subunit of
                     membrane-bound proton-translocating pyridine nucleotide 
                     transhydrogenase.
                     The &beta; subunit contains an N-terminal domain with 6 - 8
                     transmembrane regions and a cytosolic C-terminal domain 
                     that binds NADP(H) |CITS: 
                     [3525165][1932078][1551908][8011636][9015388]|.
                     Early studies characterized the <i>pnt-1</i> mutation (PntB
                     G314E |CITS: [1633824]|) which causes loss of both 
                     energy-dependent and energy-independent pyridine nucleotide
                     transhydrogenase activity |CITS: [363055][378938]|."
