     gene            complement(1688517..1690328)
                     /gene="uidA"
                     /locus_tag="b1617"
                     /label=uidA
     CDS             complement(1688517..1690328)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="uidA"
                     /locus_tag="b1617"
                     /product="bifunctional beta-glucuronidase /
                     beta-D-glucuronidase"
                     /EC_number="3.2.1.31; 3.1.1.93"
                     /label=uidA
                     /note="&beta;-D-glucuronidase catalyzes the cleavage of a
                     wide variety of &beta;-glucuronides |CITS: [3534890]|.
                     The enzyme is a homotetramer |CITS: [21051639]|, but 
                     higher-order multimers have also been shown to be active 
                     |CITS: [26121040]|.  A number of crystal structures of the 
                     enzyme alone and bound to specific inhibitors have been 
                     solved |CITS: [21051639][23690068][26364932]|.  Reaction 
                     kinetics of single molecules have been measured and 
                     compared to values measured in bulk assays |CITS: 
                     [24684619]|.
                     &beta;-D-glucuronidase and |FRAME: BETAGALACTOSID-CPLX| 
                     belong to the same protein family and thus probably share a
                     common evolutionary ancestor |CITS: [1747104]|. Wild-type 
                     &beta;-D-glucuronidase has very weak &beta;-galactosidase 
                     activity.  Mutations that change the substrate specificity 
                     of the enzyme have been identified |CITS: 
                     [10404164][11124909][12972256][15069062][21548964][ 
                     24116038]|. Thermostable variants have been isolated |CITS:
                     [11786015][17557766]|.
                     &beta;-D-glucuronidase activity has been used both as a 
                     means of detection and enumeration of <i>E. coli</i> cells 
                     (e.g. in |CITS: [2202252]|) as well as a reporter gene for 
                     measurement and localization of gene expression in a wide 
                     variety of systems |CITS: [16739584]|. 
                     &beta;-D-glucuronidase produced by bacteria in the human 
                     gut was identified as the source of toxicity of the common 
                     colon cancer drug |FRAME: CPD-21277| (CPT-11) by restoring 
                     its active drug metabolite |FRAME: CPD-27827| from the 
                     inactive form |FRAME: CPD0-2376| |CITS: [21051639]|. 
                     Specific inhibitors of the bacterial enzyme were identified
                     and found to alleviate CPT-11 toxicity |CITS: 
                     [21051639][23690068]|. The enzyme was also shown to act on 
                     the glucuronated form of the drugs |FRAME: CPD-20606| 
                     |CITS: [22328575]| and |FRAME: CPD-14601| |CITS: [ 
                     38857657]|.
                     Methyl-&beta;-glucoronide and fructuronate induce 
                     production of the enzyme |CITS: [4607717][322730]|.  A 
                     <i>uidA</i> mutant is unable to grow on 
                     methyl-&beta;-D-glucoronide |CITS: [4568840]|.
                     UidA: |CITS: [4568840]|"
