     gene            1693612..1695204
                     /gene="malX"
                     /locus_tag="b1621"
                     /label=malX
     CDS             1693612..1695204
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="malX"
                     /locus_tag="b1621"
                     /product="trifunctional PTS enzyme IIBC component MalX /
                     transport of maltose / transport of glucose"
                     /label=malX
                     /note="The deduced amino acid sequence of MalX displays
                     35% identity with |FRAME: PTSG-MONOMER ""PtsG""| (Enzyme 
                     IIBC<sup>glc</sup> of the glucose PTS). The constitutive 
                     expression of chromosomal <i>malX</i> (through a 
                     <I>malI::Tn10</I> mutation) restores growth on glucose in 
                     an <i>E. coli &Delta;ptsG &Delta;ptsM</i> strain provided 
                     cytoplasmic glucokinase (encoded by <i>glk</i>) is present.
                     This suggests that the MalX protein can transport glucose 
                     via facilitated diffusion |CITS: [1856179]|. Overexpression
                     of <i>malX</i> from a plasmid restores growth on glucose in
                     a <i>&Delta;ptsG &Delta;ptsM &Delta;glk</i> strain which 
                     suggests that MalX also functions, albeit inefficiently, in
                     vectorial phosphorylation of glucose possibly in 
                     conjunction with |FRAME: CRR-MONOMER ""Crr""| (Enzyme 
                     IIA<sup>glc</sup>) |CITS: [1856179]|. MalX may also 
                     transport maltose by facilitated diffusion |CITS: 
                     [1856179]|. The physiological function of MalX is not clear
                     |CITS: [1856179]|. MalX/Crr is a member of the PTS 
                     Glucose-Glucoside family of transporters |CITS: 
                     [24225317]|.
                     <i>malX</i> forms an operon with |FRAME: CPLX0-8092 
                     ""<i>malY</i>""|. |FRAME: PD00361 ""MalI""| regulates the 
                     expression of <i>malXY</i>. Putative MalI binding sites 
                     have been identified in the intergenic <i>malI-malX</I> 
                     region |CITS: [1856179]|.
                     <i>malX</i> is a virulence associated gene in <i>E. 
                     coli</i> strains causing extraintestinal infections |CITS: 
                     [9712795], [21317254]|.
                     "
