     gene            1698808..1698933
                     /gene="blr"
                     /locus_tag="b4409"
                     /label=blr
     CDS             1698808..1698933
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="blr"
                     /locus_tag="b4409"
                     /product="beta-lactam resistance protein"
                     /label=blr
                     /note="Blr is a small membrane protein that appears to be 
                     involved in stabilization of the divisome under certain 
                     stress conditions |CITS: [22885295]| and in resistance to a
                     number of antibiotics which inhibit peptidoglycan synthesis
                     |CITS: [10931331]|.  Blr does not affect beta-lactamase 
                     activity; resistance may be due to enhancement of drug exit
                     from the cell or to prevention of drug entry into the cell.
                      Blr is predicted to have a single transmembrane segment; 
                     the C-terminus is located in the periplasm |CITS: 
                     [10931331]|.
                     Blr interacts with FtsL as well as other cell division 
                     proteins, including FtsI, FtsK, FtsN, FtsQ, FtsW, and YmgF.
                      Its localization to the cell division site is dependent on
                     FtsQ and FtsN |CITS: [22885295]|.
                     A strain with a Tn<i>phoA</i> insertion in <i>blr</i> has 
                     increased susceptibility to beta-lactam antibiotics, 
                     D-cycloserine, and bacitracin |CITS: [10931331]|.  In 
                     growth competition experiments, a <i>blr</i> deletion 
                     mutant is more resistant to cell envelope stress than the 
                     wild type |CITS: [19734312]|.  These phenotypes were not 
                     observed by |CITS: [22885295]|.  Overproduction of 
                     <i>blr</i> suppresses the sensitivity to low osmolarity of 
                     a <i>ftsQ1</i>(Ts) mutant, while a <i>blr</i> null mutation
                     enhances this phenotype |CITS: [22885295]|.
                     Blr: ""<b>b</b>eta-<b>l</b>actam <b>r</b>esistance"" |CITS:
                     [10931331]|
                     Review: |CITS: [21342783]|"
