     gene            1700024..1700605
                     /gene="rsxA"
                     /locus_tag="b1627"
                     /label=rsxA
     CDS             1700024..1700605
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rsxA"
                     /locus_tag="b1627"
                     /product="trifunctional SoxR [2Fe-2S] reducing system
                     protein RsxA / SoxR [2Fe-2S] reducing system, Rsx complex /
                     SoxR [2Fe-2S] reducing system"
                     /label=rsxA
                     /note="Products of the <i>rsxABCDGE</i> cluster and
                     |FRAME: G7347 <i>rseC</i>| are implicated in a pathway that
                     functions to reduce the |FRAME: PD04132 SoxR| iron-sulfur 
                     cluster; in-frame deletion of any gene within the cluster 
                     results in SoxR-mediated constitutive activation of |FRAME:
                     EG10958 <i>soxS</i>| transcription in the absence of 
                     oxidative stress |CITS: [12773378]|. SoxR exists in a more 
                     oxidized form in <i>rsx</i> and <i>rseC</i> mutants |CITS: 
                     [12773378]|. The periplasmic flavin transferase |FRAME: 
                     EG12073-MONOMER ApbE| (renamed Ftp |CITS: [26626129]|) is 
                     also a component of this system; the RsxABCDGE, RseC and 
                     AbpE proteins likely form a complex that uses NAD(P)H to 
                     reduce SoxR |CITS: [35344189]|.
                     The proteins encoded by the <i>rsxABCDGE</i> gene cluster 
                     are predicted to form a membrane-associated complex |CITS: 
                     [12773378]|. RsxA is predicted to be an inner membrane 
                     protein with a 6 (or possibly more) transmembrane 
                     N<sub>out</sub>-C<sub>out</sub> topology |CITS: 
                     [12773378][10411911]|. RsxA and RsxE are homologous 
                     membrane proteins with opposite topologies and they may 
                     form a 'quasi-symmetrical' complex across the membrane 
                     |CITS: [10411911]| (see also |CITS: [16429150]|).
                     The <i>rsxABCDGE</i> gene cluster has similarity to the 
                     <i>Rhodobacter capsulatus rnf</i> gene cluster 
                     (<i>rnfABCDGEH</i> |CITS: [ 8264535][9492268]|), which 
                     plays a role in nitrogenase reduction |CITS: [12773378]| 
                     (see further |CITS: [21072677]|). Proton-motive force (PMF)
                     driven Rnf complexes are one mechanism by which diazotrophs
                     can maintain reduced ferredoxin production from NAD(P)H 
                     (see |CITS: [37154716]|); the Rsx complex of <i>E. coli</i>
                     may couple periplasmic redox signals to ion transport and 
                     reduction of the SoxR iron-sulfur cluster |CITS: 
                     [35344189]|.
                     <i>rsxA</i> insertion mutants were identified in a genetic 
                     screen for genes that are important for survival of 
                     exposure to ionizing radiation (IR).  An <i>rsxA</i> 
                     deletion mutant has a moderate decrease in IR survival 
                     |CITS: [25049088]|.
                     Rsx: <U>r</U>educer of <U>S</U>o<U>x</U>R |CITS: 
                     [12773378]|"
