     CDS             1701176..1703398
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rsxC"
                     /locus_tag="b1629"
                     /product="trifunctional SoxR [2Fe-2S] reducing system
                     protein RsxC / SoxR [2Fe-2S] reducing system, Rsx complex /
                     SoxR [2Fe-2S] reducing system"
                     /label=rsxC
                     /note="Products of the <i>rsxABCDGE</i> cluster and
                     |FRAME: G7347 <i>rseC</i>| are implicated in a pathway that
                     functions to reduce the |FRAME: PD04132 SoxR| iron-sulfur 
                     cluster; in-frame deletion of any gene within the cluster 
                     results in SoxR-mediated constitutive activation of |FRAME:
                     EG10958 <i>soxS</i>| transcription in the absence of 
                     oxidative stress |CITS: [12773378]|. SoxR exists in a more 
                     oxidized form in <i>rsx</i> and <i>rseC</i> mutants |CITS: 
                     [12773378]|. The periplasmic flavin transferase |FRAME: 
                     EG12073-MONOMER ApbE| (renamed Ftp |CITS: [26626129]|) is 
                     also a component of this system; the RsxABCDGE, RseC and 
                     AbpE proteins likely form a complex that uses NAD(P)H to 
                     reduce SoxR |CITS: [35344189]|.
                     The proteins encoded by the <i>rsxABCDGE</i> gene cluster 
                     are predicted to form a membrane-associated complex |CITS: 
                     [12773378]|. RsxC has an NAD(P)H binding motif and a 
                     ferredoxin domain with two [4Fe-4S] binding motifs |CITS: 
                     [12773378][35344189]|. RsxC interacts with SoxR |CITS: 
                     [35344189]|.
                     The <i>rsxABCDGE</i> gene cluster has similarity to the 
                     |FRAME: TAX-1061| <i>rnf</i> cluster (<i>rnfABCDGEH</i> 
                     |CITS: [8264535][9492268]|), which plays a role in 
                     nitrogenase reduction |CITS: [12773378]| (see further 
                     |CITS: [21072677]|). Proton-motive force (PMF) driven Rnf 
                     complexes are one mechanism by which diazotrophs can 
                     maintain reduced ferredoxin production from NAD(P)H (see 
                     |CITS: [37154716]|); the Rsx complex of <i>E. coli</i> may 
                     couple periplasmic redox signals to ion transport and 
                     reduction of the SoxR iron-sulfur cluster |CITS: 
                     [35344189]|.
                     Rsx: <U>r</U>educer of <U>S</U>o<U>x</U>R |CITS: 
                     [12773378]|"
