     gene            1734168..1735379
                     /gene="punC"
                     /locus_tag="b1660"
                     /label=punC
     CDS             1734168..1735379
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="punC"
                     /locus_tag="b1660"
                     /product="bifunctional purine nucleoside transporter PunC
                     / purine nucleoside transporter"
                     /label=punC
                     /note="PunC is a purine nucleoside transporter that
                     supports growth under nitrogen-limiting conditions; a 
                     <i>punC</i> deletion strain from the Keio collection is 
                     unable to grow with adenosine or 2-deoxyadenosine as the 
                     nitrogen source; the <i>punC</i> mutant also shows a growth
                     defect with inosine or guanosine as nitrogen source |CITS: 
                     [34413462]|. PunC is implicated in the uptake of some 
                     sulfonamide antibiotics |CITS: [34413462]|.
                     PunC is a member of the Drug:H<sup>+</sup> Antiporter (DHA)
                     Family within the Major Facilitator Superfamily (MFS) of 
                     transporters |CITS: [8438231][26546518]|. PunC is 
                     implicated in arabinose efflux |CITS: [22952739]|. PunC is 
                     implicated in adenosine transport; a &Delta;<i>punC</i> 
                     strain shows a growth defect with adenosine as the sole 
                     carbon source; <i>punC</i> transcript levels increase when 
                     adenosine is supplied as the sole carbon source |CITS: 
                     [32994326]|.
                     Overexpression of cloned <I>punC</I> in a K-12 strain which
                     lacks the major efflux pump permease AcrB (<i>E. coli</i> 
                     KAM3; see |CITS: [12618449]|) does not impact the 
                     resistance to a range of antibiotics, dyes and toxic 
                     compounds |CITS:[11566977]|.
                     PunC expression is regulated by the nitrogen assimilation 
                     control protein, |FRAME: G7072-MONOMER Nac|, and the LysR 
                     family transcriptional regulator, |FRAME: EG12140-MONOMER 
                     PunR| |CITS: [34413462]|.
                     <i>ydhC</i> (<i>punC</i>) is one of 35 efflux-encoding 
                     genes that have been deleted or inactivated in 'Efflux 
                     KnockOut-35' (EKO-35) -  a K-12 BW25133-derived strain that
                     lacks 35 efflux pumps and can be used as a platform to 
                     study their function |CITS: [36065018][36318669]|."
