     CDS             complement(1745985..1748087)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ydhV"
                     /locus_tag="b1673"
                     /product="putative oxidoreductase YdhV"
                     /label=ydhV
                     /note="YdhV contains a redox-active |FRAME: CPD-15874 
                     bis-Mo-MPT| cofactor.  Bis-Mo-MPT, which lacks the linked 
                     GMP moieties of |FRAME: CPD-15873|, has not previously been
                     observed as the cofactor of a molybdoenzyme |CITS: 
                     [30945846]|.
                     YdhV is a putative member of the aldehyde ferredoxin 
                     oxidoreductase family of molybdoenzymes |CITS: [17349664]|.
                      Based on sequence similarity, the <i>ydhYVWXUT</i> operon 
                     may encode components of an oxidoreductase |CITS: 
                     [18227264]|.
                     A <i>ydhY-T</i> mutant does not show a growth defect under 
                     anaerobic conditions, although utilization of certain 
                     sources of sulfur is impaired |CITS: [18227264]|.
                     In a &Delta;<i>tusA</i> strain, expression of <i>ydhV</i> 
                     is decreased in mid-exponential phase and under aerobic 
                     conditions |CITS: [23281480]|.
                     Reviews: |CITS: [23201473][32239579]|
                     "
