     gene            1765328..1766542
                     /gene="ydiM"
                     /locus_tag="b1690"
                     /label=ydiM
     CDS             1765328..1766542
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ydiM"
                     /locus_tag="b1690"
                     /product="putative exporter YdiM"
                     /label=ydiM
                     /note="Deletion of <i>ydiM</i> results in reduced
                     tolerance to isoprenol (12 hr exposure to 0.5% isoprenol) 
                     compared to wild-type and over-expression of <i>ydiM</i> 
                     improves resistance to isoprenol; isoprenol exposure 
                     induces up-regulation of <i>ydiM</i> |CITS: [26563610]|. 
                     <i>ydiM</i> is one of 35 efflux-encoding genes that have 
                     been deleted or inactivated in 'Efflux KnockOut-35' 
                     (EKO-35) -  a K-12 BW25133-derived strain that lacks 35 
                     efflux pumps and can be used as a platform to study their 
                     function |CITS: [36065018][36318669]|.
                     Deletion of <i>ydiM</i> in a strain (&Delta;<i>cydB</i>::K 
                     m<sup>S</sup>/&Delta;<i>appB</i>::Km<sup>R</sup>) that is 
                     dependent solely on |FRAME: CYT-O-UBIOX-CPLX| for 
                     respiratory growth, results in an aerobic growth defect; 
                     cytochrome <i>bo</i><sub>3</sub> oxidase activity is 
                     significantly reduced and its <i>b</i>- and <i>o</i>-type 
                     hemes cannot be detected |CITS: [37862358]|. Deletion of 
                     <i>ydiM</i> in an otherwise wild-type background perturbs 
                     copper (but not iron) homeostasis |CITS: [37862358]|.
                     In the Transporter Classification Database, YdiM is a 
                     member of the Aromatic Acid:H<sup>+</sup> Symporter (AAHS) 
                     family within the Major Facilitator Superfamily (MFS) 
                     |CITS: [9529885][26546518]|."
                     /translation="MKNPYFPTALGLYFNYLVHGMGVLLMSLNMASLETLWQTNAAGVS
