     gene            complement(1772647..1773558)
                     /gene="ydiP"
                     /locus_tag="b1696"
                     /label=ydiP
     CDS             complement(1772647..1773558)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ydiP"
                     /locus_tag="b1696"
                     /product="DNA-binding transcriptional regulator YdiP"
                     /label=ydiP
                     /note="YdiP is an AraC-type transcription factor |CITS: 
                     [34428301] [35880217]|, involved in the cold shock response
                     |CITS:[35835781]|. It contains a helix-turn-helix motif to 
                     bind DNA in its C-terminal domain |CITS: [35880217]|.
                     YdiP DNA-binding activity was probed in vivo in glucose M9 
                     minimal medium through chromatin immunoprecipitation assays
                     (ChIP-exo) |CITS: [34428301]|. It was predicted that this 
                     protein regulates genes related to metabolism |CITS: 
                     [35880217]|. However, the effect of YdiP on the 
                     transcription of any gene has not yet been demonstrated 
                     |CITS: [34428301]|.
                     In LB medium, the YdiP protein abundance was increased 
                     after 2 h of shifting to cold shock at 15&deg;C relative to
                     activity at 37&deg;C |CITS:[35835781]|. At 15&deg;C but not
                     at 37&deg;C, YdiP binds with CspA, CspB, CspE, CspG, and 
                     CspI proteins in rich medium and with CspE in minimal 
                     medium |CITS:[35835781]|.
                     A <i>ydiP</i> knockout mutant showed impaired growth at 
                     15&deg;C but not at 37&deg;C compared to wild type 
                     |CITS:[35835781]|. This defect was exacerbated when 
                     <i>cspABEGI</i> was also deleted |CITS:[35835781]|. YdiP 
                     protein abundance was increased after adaptation to 
                     10&deg;C relative to that at 37&deg;C |CITS:[35835781]|. 
                     <i>ydiP</i> transcript level was increased 4 h after a 
                     shift to 15&deg;C relative to abundance at 37&deg;C 
                     |CITS:[35835781]|.  At 15&deg;C but not at 37&deg;C, a 
                     <i>ydiP</i> mutant grown in LB medium or M9 minimal medium 
                     formed long filamentous cells; <i>ydiP</i> overexpression 
                     in a <i>ydiP</i> mutant rescued the filamentous phenotype 
                     |CITS:[35835781]|.
                     Interconnectivity between <i>ydiP</i> gene and the gene 
                     encoding the TF CspA has been reported |CITS:[35835781]|. 
                     The <i>ydiP</i> gene is affected by stress and conditions 
                     that lead to biofilm formation |CITS: [35880217]|."
