                     /product="putative electron transfer flavoprotein subunit
                     YdiQ"
                     /label=ydiQ
                     /note="YdiQ and YdiR are predicted to be subunits of an
                     electron transport flavoprotein.  YdiO, YdiQ, YdiR, YdiS, 
                     and YdiT may play a role in electron transport between the 
                     anaerobic fatty acid oxidation pathway and the respiratory 
                     chain |CITS: [12535077]|.
                     <i>fixA</i>, <i>fixB</i>, <i>ydiQ</i>, <i>ydiR</i>, 
                     <i>ygcR</i>, and <i>ygcQ</i> form a subsystem based on 
                     genome context methods, and may represent a previously 
                     uncharacterized electron transfer pathway |CITS: 
                     [21775308]|."
