     gene            complement(1784065..1785501)
                     /gene="selO"
                     /locus_tag="b1706"
                     /label=selO
     CDS             complement(1784065..1785501)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="selO"
                     /locus_tag="b1706"
                     /product="bifunctional protein adenylyltransferase SelO /
                     protein adenylyltransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.7.7.108"
                     /label=selO
                     /note="SelO is a widely conserved member of the SELO
                     family of pseudokinases |CITS: [22359664]| that catalyzes 
                     the transfer of AMP from ATP to Ser, Thr, and Tyr residues 
                     on protein substrates (AMPylation) |CITS: [30270044]|. 
                     Protein substrates for SelO include |FRAME: E1O-MONOMER 
                     SucA| and |FRAME: RED-GLUTAREDOXIN GrxA| |CITS: 
                     [30270044]|.
                     Active site residues were predicted based on the crystal 
                     structure of the <i>Pseudomonas syringae</i> enzyme; 
                     mutagenesis of these residues - K107, E130, R170, R177, 
                     D246, N247, and D256 - to alanine lead to loss of catalytic
                     activity.  Under non-reducing conditions, the formation of 
                     an intramolecular disulfide bond between Cys272 and Cys476 
                     reduces the AMPylation activity of SelO |CITS: [30270044]|.
                     A <i>selO</i> mutant shows a modest decrease in global 
                     protein S-glutathionylation; after treatment with |FRAME: 
                     OXIDIZED-GLUTATHIONE oxidized glutathione|, the mutant 
                     shows a larger decrease in protein S-glutathionylation 
                     compared to wild type |CITS: [30270044]|.
                     Expression of <i>selO</i> is positively regulated by 
                     apo-IscR |CITS: [16677314][19361432]|.
                     SelO: ""<b>sel</b>enoprotein-<b>O</b>"" |CITS: [30270044]| 
                     (note that the <i>E. coli</i> protein does not contain a 
                     selenocysteine residue)
                     Experiments reported in |CITS: [30270044]| used <i>E. 
                     coli</i> Rosetta, which is a BL21 (DE3) derivative, as the 
                     source of the gene/protein and for the gene disruption 
                     experiments.  The SelO protein sequence is approximately 
                     98% identical to that of the K-12 strain."
