                     /label=hxpB
     CDS             1803637..1804305
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="hxpB"
                     /locus_tag="b1727"
                     /product="multifunctional hexitol phosphatase B / 
                     sorbitol-6-phosphatase / mannitol-1-phosphatase / 
                     2-deoxyglucose-6-phosphate phosphatase"
                     /EC_number="3.1.3.50; 3.1.3.22; 3.1.3.68"
                     /label=hxpB
                     /note="The hexitol phosphatase activity of HxpB was
                     discovered in a large-scale metabolomics screen for 
                     enzymatic activities of uncharacterized proteins in <i>E. 
                     coli</i> |CITS: [27941785]|.
                     HxpB is a sugar phosphatase belonging to the superfamily of
                     haloacid dehalogenase (HAD)-like hydrolases.  Its preferred
                     substrate is 2-deoxyglucose-6-phosphate |CITS: [16990279]|.
                      The phosphatase activity of HxpB was
                     first discovered in a high-throughput screen of purified 
                     proteins |CITS: [15808744]|.
                     Phosphatase activity of HxpB is dependent on the presence 
                     of a divalent cation such as Mg<sup>2+</sup>, which appears
                     to affect substrate binding |CITS: [16990279]|. Mutagenesis
                     of the predicted catalytic Asp residues in HxpB results in 
                     loss of phosphatase activity.  A <i>hxpB</i>
                     deletion mutant is more sensitive to the presence of 
                     2-deoxyglucose in the growth medium than wild type, while a
                     strain overexpressing <i>hxpB</i> tolerates higher 
                     concentrations of 2-deoxyglucose |CITS: [16990279]|. 
                     2-deoxyglucose is taken up by <i>E. coli</i> and is 
                     phosphorylated to 2-deoxyglucose-6P, a toxic analog of 
                     glucose-6P |CITS: [4928893]|.
                     HxpB: ""<b>h</b>e<b>x</b>itol <b>p</b>hosphatase <b>B</b>""
                     |CITS: [27941785]|"
