     CDS             complement(1810643..1811392)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="chbG"
                     /locus_tag="b1733"
                     /product="bifunctional chitooligosaccharide
                     monodeacetylase ChbG / N,N'-diacetylchitobiose 6'-phosphate
                     monodeacetylase"
                     /EC_number="3.5.1.136"
                     /label=chbG
                     /note="ChbG is a chitooligosaccharide monodeacetylase
                     encoded as part of the <i>chb</i> operon, which encodes 
                     enzymes involved in growth on |FRAME: CHITOBIOSE| as the 
                     sole source of carbon |CITS: 
                     [9405618][22797760][33794535]|.
                     A &Delta;<i>chbG</i> strain is unable to grow on 
                     diacetylchitobiose |CITS: [22797760][33794535]| or 
                     triacetylchitobiose |CITS: [22797760]| as the sole source 
                     of carbon and energy.  A &Delta;<i>chbF</i> mutant 
                     accumulates monoacetylchitobiose-phosphate; recombinant 
                     ChbF degrades this accumulated compound to 
                     glucosamine-6-phosphate and <i>N</i>-acetylglucosamine. 
                     This, together with additional evidence, shows that ChbG 
                     deacetylates diacetylchitobiose at the non-reducing 
                     (phosphorylated) end |CITS: [33794535]|.
                     Mutations in conserved residues of a predicted metal 
                     binding site negatively affect the activity of ChbG |CITS: 
                     [22797760]|.  ChbG has promiscuous phosphonoesterase 
                     activity with 3-phosphopropyl-<i>p</i>-nitrophenyl 
                     methylphosphonate and other xenobiotic phosphorylated 
                     phosphonates |CITS: [21332126]|.
                     Expression of <i>chbG</i> is upregulated in a strain 
                     containing the <i>ompR234</i> up-mutation |CITS: 
                     [14523117]|.
                     ChbG: ""<i>N,N</i>'-diacetyl<b>ch</b>ito<b>b</b>iose 
                     <b>G</b>"" |CITS: [9405618]|
                     "
