     gene            complement(1811405..1812757)
                     /gene="chbF"
                     /locus_tag="b1734"
                     /label=chbF
     CDS             complement(1811405..1812757)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="chbF"
                     /locus_tag="b1734"
                     /product="bifunctional monoacetylchitobiose-6-phosphate
                     hydrolase / 6-phospho-beta-D-glucosyl-(1,4)-D-glucose 
                     glucohydrolase"
                     /EC_number="3.2.1.86"
                     /label=chbF
                     /note="ChbF is a monoacetylchitobiose-6-phosphate
                     hydrolase encoded as part of the <i>chb</i> operon, which 
                     encodes enzymes involved in growth on |FRAME: CHITOBIOSE| 
                     as the sole source of carbon and energy |CITS: 
                     [9405618][33794535]|.
                     ChbF belongs to family 4 of the glycosylhydrolase 
                     superfamily |CITS: [10572139]|.  ChbF hdrolyzes the 
                     reaction product of ChbG to glucosamine-6-phosphate and 
                     <i>N</i>-acetylglucosamine and also cleaves 
                     diacetylchitotriose-phosphate to diacetyl-chitobiose and 
                     glucosamine-6-phosphate.  ChbF is unable to utilize 
                     diacetylchitobiose-phosphate, the product of the ChbBCA PTS
                     transporter |CITS: [33794535]|.
                     Substrate specificity of the enzyme was investigated by 
                     |CITS: [10572139]|; unfortunately, chitobiose derivatives 
                     were not among the tested substrates.
                     A &Delta;<i>chbF</i> strain is unable to grow on 
                     diacetylchitobiose as the sole source of carbon and energy 
                     |CITS: [33794535]|.
                     ChbF: ""<i>N,N</i>'-diacetyl<b>ch</b>ito<b>b</b>iose 
                     <b>F</b>"" |CITS: [9405618]|
                     "
