     gene            complement(1813712..1814062)
                     /gene="chbA"
                     /locus_tag="b1736"
                     /label=chbA
     CDS             complement(1813712..1814062)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="chbA"
                     /locus_tag="b1736"
                     /product="bifunctional N,N'-diacetylchitobiose-specific
                     PTS enzyme IIA component / N,N'-diacetylchitobiose-specific
                     PTS enzyme II"
                     /EC_number="2.7.1.196"
                     /label=chbA
                     /note="ChbA contains a PTS Enzyme IIA domain.
                     IIA<sup>chb</sup> has been shown to form stable homodimers 
                     |CITS: [10913118]|, though the solution structure of a 
                     mutant IIA<sup>Chb</sup> determined by NMR spectroscopy 
                     suggests that a homotrimer is the primary oligomeric state 
                     of IIA<sup>chb</sup>. The active site histidine (His89) is 
                     located within a crevice formed at the interface of two 
                     adjacent subunits of the EIIA<sup>Chb</sup> trimer |CITS: 
                     [15654077]|. A solution structure of a ChbA-ChbB complex 
                     has been obtained and the interaction sites mapped. The 
                     protruding active site of ChbB containing the active site 
                     cysteine residue (Cys10) is buried within the cleft formed 
                     by the adjacent subunits of the ChbA trimer |CITS: 
                     [19959833]|. The solution structure of a ChbA-HPr complex 
                     shows the active site histidine (His15) of HPr buried 
                     within this same cleft |CITS: [22593574]|. HPr and CbhB 
                     have no similarity in either overall structure or local 
                     structure at their active site; despite this they bind to 
                     highly overlapping binding sites on ChbA.
                     Stable complexes with a 1:1 ratio of IIA<sup>chb</sup> and 
                     IIB<sup>chb</sup> subunits have been identified which 
                     dissociate when IIB<sup>chb</sup> is phosphorylated |CITS: 
                     [10913119][10913122]|.
                     <i>chbA</i>: <i>N,N'</i>-diacetyl<u>ch</u>ito<u>b</u>iose 
                     A"
