     gene            1816715..1817542
                     /gene="nadE"
                     /locus_tag="b1740"
                     /label=nadE
     CDS             1816715..1817542
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="nadE"
                     /locus_tag="b1740"
                     /product="bifunctional NH3-dependent NAD(+) synthetase /
                     NAD(+) synthetase, NH3-dependent"
                     /EC_number="6.3.1.5"
                     /label=nadE
                     /note="NAD<sup>+</sup> synthetase is an essential enzyme 
                     involved in both the <i>de novo</i> biosynthesis and 
                     salvage of NAD<sup>+</sup>, catalyzing the final step of 
                     both pathways.
                     The enzyme shows a strong preference for ammonia over 
                     glutamine as the amino group donor |CITS: [13717628]| and 
                     may even have no glutamine-dependent NAD<sup>+</sup> 
                     synthetase activity at all |CITS: [8195100]|.
                     The enzyme contains a P-loop-like pyrophosphatase motif 
                     |CITS: [7731953]|.  Crystal structures of the enzyme alone 
                     and in complex with substrates and the reaction product 
                     NAD<sup>+</sup> have been solved.  The catalytic cycle 
                     appears to involve significant structural reorganization 
                     |CITS: [10544053][15699042]|.
                     <i>nadE</i> is essential for growth |CITS: 
                     [1512214][12142426]|.  In the presence of a heterologous 
                     NAD<sup>+</sup> transporter, a &Delta;<i>nadE</i> mutant is
                     able to grow with externally supplied NAD<sup>+</sup> 
                     |CITS: [21742902]|.  Expression of <i>nadE</i> is 
                     posttranscriptionally regulated by the small RNA CyaR 
                     |CITS: [18978044]|.
                     Efg: ""essential for growth"" |CITS: [1512214]|
                     NadE: ""<b>NAD</b> biosynthesis <b>E</b>"" |CITS: 
                     [8195100]|
                     Reviews: |CITS: [11153263][26443758]|"
