                     /gene="astA"
                     /locus_tag="b1747"
                     /product="arginine N-succinyltransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.3.1.109"
                     /label=astA
                     /note="Arginine succinyltransferase (AstA) catalyzes the
                     first reaction in the ammonia-producing arginine catabolic 
                     pathway, |FRAME: AST-PWY|.  The activity has only been 
                     assayed in crude cell extracts, and thus there is little 
                     direct evidence for the function of the <i>astA</i> gene 
                     product |CITS: [9696779]|.
                     AstA is a member of the acyl-CoA <i>N</i>-acyltransferase 
                     superfamily |CITS: [14675764]|.
                     Expression of the enzymes of the AST pathway is regulated 
                     by arginine and nitrogen availability |CITS: [9696779]| via
                     ArgR and NtrC |CITS: [12003934]|."
