     gene            complement(1825019..1826239)
                     /gene="astC"
                     /locus_tag="b1748"
                     /label=astC
     CDS             complement(1825019..1826239)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="astC"
                     /locus_tag="b1748"
                     /product="bifunctional succinylornithine transaminase / 
                     N-acetylornithine aminotransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.6.1.81; 2.6.1.11"
                     /label=astC
                     /note="Succinylornithine transaminase (AstC) catalyzes the
                     third reaction in the ammonia-producing arginine catabolic 
                     pathway, |FRAME: AST-PWY|.  The <i> astC</i> gene is 60% 
                     identical to |FRAME: EG10066 ""<i>argD</i>""|, which 
                     encodes the arginine-repressible <i>N</i>-acetylornithine 
                     aminotransferase |CITS: [9696779][9696780]|.
                     Four enzymes, ArgD, AstC, GabT, and PuuE, show some level 
                     of <i>N</i>-acetylornithine aminotransferase (ACOAT) 
                     activity involved in arginine biosynthesis.  On minimal 
                     medium lacking arginine, single <i>argD</i> or <i>astC</i> 
                     mutants have subtle growth defects, and an <i>argD astC</i>
                     double mutant has a slower doubling time than wild type.  
                     An <i>argD astC gabT</i> triple mutant does not grow on 
                     medium lacking arginine.  Accumulation of suppressor 
                     mutations eventually allows growth of the triple mutant; an
                     additional deletion of <i>puuE</i> eliminates this effect 
                     |CITS: [25243376]|.
                     The normal activities of two enzymes, ArgD and SerC, are 
                     sufficient for succinyldiaminopimelate (SDAP) and lysine 
                     biosynthesis; AstC is a third enzyme that is sufficient for
                     SDAP biosynthesis, but alone can not fulfill the cell's 
                     requirement for lysine.  Expression of <i>argD</i>, 
                     <i>astC</i>, <i>serC</i>, <i>aspC</i>, <i>gabT</i>, 
                     <i>hisC</i>, <i>ilvE</i>, <i>patA</i>, <i>puuE</i>, or 
                     <i>tyrB</i> from a plasmid allow growth of the triple 
                     &Delta;<i>argD serC astC</i> mutant on minimal medium 
                     |CITS: [25243376]|.
                     Crystal structures of AstC from <i>E. coli</i> BL21(DE3) 
                     have been solved.  The enzyme is 99% identical to the <i>E.
                     coli</i> K-12 enzyme |CITS: [23484010]|.
                     Expression of the enzymes of the AST pathway is regulated 
                     by arginine and nitrogen availability |CITS: 
                     [9696779][15289551]| via ArgR and NtrC |CITS: [12003934]|. 
                     An <i>astC</i> mutant is unable to utilize arginine as the 
                     sole source of nitrogen and is impaired in the utilization 
                     of ornithine |CITS: [9696779][9696780]|.
                     CstC: ""<b>c</b>arbon <b>st</b>arvation protein <b>C</b>"" 
                     |CITS: [9696780]|"
