                     /label=nudG
     CDS             1835747..1836154
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="nudG"
                     /locus_tag="b1759"
                     /product="multifunctional 5-hydroxy-CTP diphosphatase /
                     oxidized nucleoside triphosphate pyrophosphohydrolase / 
                     5-hydroxy-CTP diphosphohydrolase / ppGpp phosphohydrolase"
                     /EC_number="3.6.1.56"
                     /label=nudG
                     /note="NudG is a member of the Nudix hydrolase family and
                     shows high specificity for hydrolysis of pyrimidine 
                     (deoxy)nucleoside triphosphates |CITS: [11053429]|.  The 
                     enzyme hydrolyzes oxidized nucleotides and is therefore 
                     expected to function in DNA damage avoidance |CITS: 
                     [11676470]|.  Its preferred substrate appears to be 
                     5-hydroxy-CTP |CITS: [12509230]|.
                     A solution structure of NudG has been obtained, enabling 
                     identification of the substrate binding pocket |CITS: 
                     [21553121][22414689]|.
                     A <i>nudG</i> deletion strain exhibits a 2-3-fold elevated 
                     rate of |FRAME: HYDROGEN-PEROXIDE|-induced mutations, while
                     overexpression of <i>nudG</i> suppressed mutations |CITS: 
                     [14750949]|.  Site-directed mutagenesis of various 
                     conserved amino acid residues has been performed |CITS: 
                     [15381107]|, and residues involved in substrate binding 
                     have been identified |CITS: [15823026]|."
