                     /product="putative oxidoreductase YdjA"
                     /label=ydjA
                     /note="Crystal structures of YdjA alone and with the FMN 
                     cofactor have been solved.  The enzyme forms a homodimer in
                     the crystal, and two molecules of FMN are bound at the 
                     dimer interface |CITS: [18241886]|.
                     Overexpressed YdjA does not appear to reduce the prodrugs 
                     CB1954 and PR-104A |CITS: [23399641]| and was used by 
                     |CITS: [24996412]| as a negative control for nitroreductase
                     activity.
                     A <i>ydjA</i> null mutant was reported to produce less 
                     hydrogen than wild type under fermentation conditions 
                     |CITS: [MOHDYUSOFF12]|.  No attempt to complement the 
                     mutant phenotype with wild-type <i>ydjA</i> was reported."
