                     /product="bifunctional methylglyoxal reductase YeaE /
                     methylglyoxal reductase"
                     /EC_number="1.1.1.21"
                     /label=yeaE
                     /note="YeaE has been shown to have methylglyoxal reductase 
                     activity |CITS: [16077126]|.
                     The subunit structure of YeaE has not been determined, but 
                     its amino acid sequence similarity to the aldo-keto 
                     reductases DkgA (YqhE) and DkgB (YafB) suggests that it may
                     be monomeric |CITS: [23103600]|.
                     Growth of a <i>yeaE gloA</i> double mutant is inhibited by 
                     0.3 mM methylglyoxal |CITS: [16077126]|.  A <i>yeaE</i> 
                     mutant is more sensitive to glyoxal than wild type in plate
                     assays, although the IC<sub>50</sub> in a liquid assay is 
                     quite similar to that of wild type |CITS: [23990306]|.  
                     Expression of <i>yeaE</i> is not increased in response to 
                     methylglyoxal |CITS: [16077126]| or glyoxal |CITS: 
                     [23990306]|.
                     Review: |CITS: [23103600]|
                     "
