     gene            complement(1859983..1860729)
                     /gene="mipA"
                     /locus_tag="b1782"
                     /label=mipA
     CDS             complement(1859983..1860729)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="mipA"
                     /locus_tag="b1782"
                     /product="MltA-interacting protein"
                     /label=mipA
                     /note="MipA, <U><B>M</B></U>ltA-<U><B>i</B></U>nteracting 
                     <U><B>p</B></U>rotein, is a scaffolding protein that forms 
                     a trimer with PBP1B, a murein polymerase, and MltA, a 
                     murein hydrolase |CITS:[10037771]|.
                     MipA is found in the membrane fraction |CITS:[10037771]| 
                     and has been identified as an integral outer membrane 
                     protein by 2D electrophoresis and peptide mass 
                     fingerprinting |CITS:[10806384]|.  It shares low sequence 
                     similarity with the porin-like protein Omp26La of 
                     <I>Listonella anguillarum</I> and is predicted to contain 
                     &beta;-barrel structure |CITS: [12192075]|.  MipA binds 
                     specifically to MltA and PBP1B |CITS:[10037771]|. 
                     Overexpression of <I>mipA</I> results in cell lysis due to 
                     compromised membrane integrity |CITS:[10037771]|. Multicopy
                     expression results in increased 
                     &sigma;<sup>E</sup>-dependent expression of <I>degP</I> and
                     <I>rybB</I> |CITS:[17416652]|.
                     <I>mipA</I> is predicted to be a member of the CRP regulon 
                     |CITS:[11282972]|.  Expression of <I>mipA</I> is induced by
                     addition of the conjugative plasmid R1<I>drd</I>19 
                     |CITS:[18344336]| and decreased upon exposure to acetate 
                     |CITS:[11244055]|."
