     gene            1861165..1863099
                     /gene="yeaG"
                     /locus_tag="b1783"
                     /label=yeaG
     CDS             1861165..1863099
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yeaG"
                     /locus_tag="b1783"
                     /product="bifunctional protein kinase YeaG / protein
                     kinase"
                     /EC_number="2.7.11.1"
                     /label=yeaG
                     /note="YeaG plays a role in the adaptation to sustained
                     nitrogen (N) starvation |CITS: [26621053]|. YeaG is a 
                     member of the PrkA family of serine protein kinases. 
                     Purified YeaG has autokinase and casein kinase activity 
                     |CITS: [18276156]|. YeaG may phosphorylate an unknown 65 
                     kDa cytoplasmic protein |CITS: [TAGOURTI11]|.
                     Comparison of the phosphoproteomes of wild-type and a 
                     &Delta;<i>yeaG</i> mutant during the shift from glucose to 
                     malate metabolism shows several differentially 
                     phosphorylated proteins, including |FRAME: 
                     ISOCIT-LYASE-MONOMER| (AceA). <i>In vitro</i>, YeaG is able
                     to phosphorylate |FRAME: ISOCIT-LYASE-MONOMER| only in the 
                     presence of malate |CITS: [33889145]|.
                     Expression of <i>yeaG</i> is increased during stationary 
                     phase, acid and salt stress |CITS: [15716429]|. A 
                     <i>yeaG</i> mutant shows a growth defect in stationary 
                     phase |CITS: [TAGOURTI11]| and reduced viability during 
                     sustained nitrogen starvation |CITS: [26621053]|. 
                     Expression of the |FRAME: CPLX0-7822 MqsRA| and |FRAME: 
                     G6109-MONOMER YafQ|-|FRAME: G6110-MONOMER DinJ| 
                     toxin-antitoxin systems is increased in a <i>yeaG</i> 
                     mutant |CITS: [26621053]|. Under sustained N starvation 
                     conditions, a &Delta;<i>yeaG</i> mutant shows dysregulated 
                     expression of |FRAME: PD04032 MetJ|-regulated methionine 
                     biosynthesis genes |CITS: [29957170]|. During the shift 
                     from glucose to malate metabolism, a &Delta;<i>yeaG</i> 
                     mutant shows a shorter lag phase than the wild type |CITS: 
                     [33889145]|.
                     The |FRAME: CPLX0-1461|-dependent |FRAME: RYEB-RNA| was 
                     found to downregulate the translation of YeaG and YeaH 
                     under long term (24 hrs) N-starved conditions. Recovery 
                     from N-starvation has a shorter lag time in 
                     <i>&Delta;yeaG</i>, <i>&Delta;yeaH</i> and 
                     <i>&Delta;yeaG&Delta;yeaH</i> mutants, whereas a longer lag
                     time was observed in <i>&Delta;sdsR</i> mutants; thus, SdsR
                     translational downregulation of YeaG and |FRAME: 
                     G6970-MONOMER YeaH| allows for optimal recovery from 
                     N-starvation |CITS: [38142457]|."
                     /translation="MNIFDHYRQRYEAAKDEEFTLQEFLTTCRQDRSAYANAAERLLMA
                     IGEPVMVDTAQEPRLSRLFSNRVIARYPAFEEFYGMEDAIEQIVSYLKHAAQGLEEKKQ
