     gene            1864642..1866117
                     /gene="cdgI"
                     /locus_tag="b1785"
                     /label=cdgI
     CDS             1864642..1866117
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="cdgI"
                     /locus_tag="b1785"
                     /product="putative c-di-GMP binding protein CdgI"
                     /label=cdgI
                     /note="CdgI contains an N-terminal MASE4
                     (Membrane-Associated SEnsor) domain with eight predicted 
                     transmembrane domains followed by a C-terminal degenerate 
                     diguanylate cyclase (GGDEF) domain that is located in the 
                     cytoplasm |CITS: [15919996][26148715]|.  CdgI belongs to 
                     the core set of eight GGDEF/EAL domain proteins that is 
                     absolutely conserved in a set of 61 <i>E. coli</i> genomes 
                     containing pathogenic, commensal and probiotic strains 
                     |CITS: [26303830]|.
                     A <i>cdgI</i> deletion mutant shows 30-fold increased early
                     biofilm formation and 4-fold increased swimming motility.  
                     The motility phenotype is complemented by wild type 
                     <i>cdgI</i>, but not a mutant where the degenerate GGDEF 
                     motif, EGEVF in CdgI, was changed to EGAVF, suggesting that
                     CdgI may indeed be a functional diguanylate cyclase.  
                     Deletion of <i>cdgI</i> does not alter the concentration of
                     c-di-GMP inside the cell |CITS: [21181144]|.
                     Expression of <i>cdgI</i> may be dependent on 
                     &sigma;<sup>S</sup> under high salt, but not other stress 
                     conditions |CITS: [17010156]|.  No expression was seen in 
                     LB medium |CITS: [19332833]|. |FRAME: G6971| was 
                     significantly upregulated in simulated microgravity |CITS: 
                     [35940684]|.
                     CdgI: ""<b>c</b>-<b>d</b>i-<b>G</b>MP binding protein 
                     <b>I</b>"" |CITS: [26148715]|
                     "
