     gene            1866298..1867788
                     /gene="dgcJ"
                     /locus_tag="b1786"
                     /label=dgcJ
     CDS             1866298..1867788
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="dgcJ"
                     /locus_tag="b1786"
                     /product="bifunctional diguanylate cyclase DgcJ /
                     diguanylate cyclase"
                     /EC_number="2.7.7.65"
                     /label=dgcJ
                     /note="DgcJ contains an N-terminal GAPES
                     (GAmma-proteobacterial PEriplasmic Sensory) domain 
                     predicted to be periplasmic |CITS: [26148715]| and a 
                     C-terminal cytoplasmic GGDEF domain with predicted 
                     diguanylate cyclase activity |CITS: [19332833]|. DgcJ 
                     interacts directly with the |FRAME: C-DI-GMP|-activated 
                     glycosyltransferase |FRAME: EG11739-MONOMER NfrB| and is 
                     required for NfrAB-dependent phage N4 infection; DgcJ 
                     functions to provide cyclic di-3',5'-guanylate to NrfB wth 
                     resultant activation of glycosyltransferase activity |CITS:
                     [34903052][34903045]|. The periplasmic domain of DgcJ 
                     likely senses a nutritional signal |CITS: [34903045]|.
                     A <i>dgcJ</i> null mutant partially suppresses the loss of 
                     motility phenotype of a <i>pdeH</i> mutant at 37&deg;C 
                     |CITS: [18765794]|. Deletion of <i>dgcJ</i> increases 
                     swimming motility |CITS: [21181144]|; complementation by 
                     overexpressing <i>dgcJ</i> reduced swimming and swarming 
                     back to wild-type levels |CITS: [36400010]|. <i>dgcJ</i> is
                     expressed during exponential growth |CITS: [19332833]|. 
                     DgcJ is active during vegetative growth at at 37&deg;C; 
                     DgcJ, |FRAME: G7049-MONOMER DgcQ|, and |FRAME: CPLX0-8535 
                     DgcE| all contribute to inhibiting motility of a 
                     &Delta;<i>pdeH</i> mutant at 37&deg;C |CITS: [34903052]|. 
                     Deletion of <i>dgcJ</i> provides strong protection against 
                     phage N4 |CITS: [34903045]|.
                     Kanamycin resistant (K<sup>R</sup>), <i>dgcJ</i> mutants 
                     were only obtained from wild-type cells plated on swarm 
                     media that crossed into Kan swim media (i.e. edge mutants) 
                     but not from cells plated in swim media; mutations were in 
                     DgcJ active site residues and periplasmic sensory domain at
                     residue V330 |CITS: [36400010]|.
                     <i>dgcJ</i> transcription is significantly reduced at 
                     30&deg;C compared to 37&deg;C |CITS: [34903045]|.
                     DgcJ: <b>d</b>i<b>g</b>uanylate <b>c</b>yclase <b>J</b> 
                     |CITS: [26148715]|
                     Reviews: |CITS: [19318291][22226726][27498163][33640237]|"
