                     /label=yeaK
     CDS             1867831..1868334
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yeaK"
                     /locus_tag="b1787"
                     /product="multifunctional mischarged aminoacyl-tRNA
                     deacylase / L-seryl-[tRNA(Thr)] deacylase / 
                     L-homoseryl-[tRNA(Lys)] deacylase / L-seryl-[tRNA(Ala)] 
                     deacylase / L-seryl-[tRNA(Lys)] deacylase / 
                     L-threonyl-[tRNA(Ile)] deacylase / L-threonyl-[tRNA(Val)] 
                     deacylase / L-threonyl-[tRNA(Lys)] deacylase"
                     /label=yeaK
                     /note="The YeaK protein (""ProXp-ST1"") has aminoacyl-tRNA 
                     editing activity.  It is able to deacylate tRNAs mischarged
                     with serine or threonine, such as Thr-tRNA<sup>Lys</sup>, 
                     Thr-tRNA<sup>Val</sup>, and Thr-tRNA<sup>Ile</sup> as well 
                     as, to a lesser extent, Ser-tRNA<sup>Lys</sup>, 
                     Ser-tRNA<sup>Ala</sup>, homoseryl-tRNA<sup>Lys</sup>, and 
                     Ser-tRNA<sup>Thr</sup>. It does not deacylate cognate 
                     Lys-tRNA<sup>Lys</sup>, Ala-tRNA<sup>Ala</sup>, 
                     Val-tRNA<sup>Val</sup>, or Ile-tRNA<sup>Ile</sup> |CITS: 
                     [25918376]|.
                     YeaK has similarity to the editing active site (INS domain)
                     of |FRAME: PROS-CPLX|, which functions in editing 
                     mischarged Ala-tRNA<sup>Pro</sup> |CITS: [14663147]|.
                     A <i>yeaK</i> null mutant shows growth defects under 
                     conditions that increase mischarging of certain tRNAs, such
                     as overexpression of |FRAME: LYSS-CPLX LysS|, |FRAME: 
                     LYSU-CPLX LysU| or |FRAME: SERS-CPLX SerRS| together with 
                     growth in the presence of excess serine, homoserine or 
                     threonine |CITS: [25918376]|."
