                     /product="bifunctional 2-nitroimidazole exporter /
                     nitroimidazole exporter"
                     /label=nimT
                     /note="A <i>&Delta;nimT</i> mutant is more sensitive to
                     the natural antibiotic, 2-nitroimidazole, than wild type 
                     under both aerobic and anaerobic conditions. <i>nimT</i> 
                     appears to be the single target gene of the |FRAME: 
                     G6976-MONOMER ""NimR""| transcriptional regulator |CITS: 
                     [25790494]|. Overexpression of <I>nimT</I> from a plasmid 
                     confers resistance to the toxic chemical, bromoacetate 
                     |CITS: [20921376]|.
                     NimT (formerly YeaN) is a member of the Cyanate Porter (CP)
                     family within the Major Facilitator Superfamily (MFS) of 
                     transporters |CITS: [9529885] [25790494]|."
