     CDS             1873131..1873205
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yoaJ"
                     /locus_tag="b4675"
                     /product="uncharacterized protein YoaJ"
                     /label=yoaJ
                     /note="The <i>yoaJ</i> open reading frame was predicted
                     based on sequence similarity to a number of other enteric 
                     bacteria.  YoaJ contains a predicted transmembrane segment,
                     and the protein can be found in the membrane fraction.  
                     YoaJ is more highly expressed during stationary phase than 
                     during exponential growth |CITS: [19121005]|. Topology 
                     assays using GFP and PhoA fusion proteins suggest that YoaJ
                     is oriented with the C-terminus in the periplasm |CITS: 
                     [21778229]|. Translocation of YoaJ is impaired in both SecE
                     depleted and YidC depleted <i>E. coli</i> strains |CITS: 
                     [21778229]|."
