                     /product="multifunctional carnitine monooxygenase subunit
                     YeaW / gamma-butyrobetaine monooxygenase / choline 
                     monooxygenase / carnitine monooxygenase / 2Fe-2S 
                     cluster-containing protein YeaW"
                     /EC_number="1.14.13.239"
                     /label=yeaW
                     /note="Partially purified YeaW protein was shown to
                     contain a [2Fe-2S] iron-sulfur cluster that can be reduced 
                     by dithionite,
                     but not ascorbate, identifying it as a low-potential Rieske
                     iron-sulfur cluster protein |CITS: [18286376]|. When 
                     incubated together in the presence of NADH, YeaWX liberated
                     |FRAME: TRIMETHYLAMINE| from several substrates, including 
                     |FRAME: CARNITINE|, |FRAME: GAMMA-BUTYROBETAINE| and 
                     |FRAME: CHOLINE| |CITS: [25440057]|.  It has not yet been 
                     determined whether a physical YeaWX complex exists.
                     "
