     gene            complement(1885582..1887492)
                     /gene="yoaA"
                     /locus_tag="b1808"
                     /label=yoaA
     CDS             complement(1885582..1887492)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yoaA"
                     /locus_tag="b1808"
                     /product="bifunctional ATP-dependent DNA helicase YoaA / 
                     ATP-dependent 5' -> 3' helicase"
                     /EC_number="5.6.2.3"
                     /label=yoaA
                     /note="YoaA is an Fe-S cluster containing, ATP-dependent,
                     5' to 3' DNA helicase that functions in DNA repair; YoaA 
                     interacts directly with |FRAME: EG11413-MONOMER HolC| (the 
                     &chi; subunit of DNA polymerase III) and this complex is 
                     likely the physiologically relevant form of the helicase 
                     |CITS: [36509145][33582602][26544712]|.
                     YoaA and &chi; form a complex <i>in vitro</i>; YoaA-&chi; 
                     has DNA-dependent helicase activity and requires a 5' 
                     single-stranded overhang or ssDNA gap for DNA unwinding; 
                     YoaA-&chi; unwinds DNA with a 5' flap and various types of 
                     damaged DNA (see |CITS: [36509145]|). |FRAME: CPLX0-8165 
                     SSB| interacts with YoaA-&chi; and affects the helicase 
                     activity of YoaA-&chi; in a substrate-dependent manner; 
                     YoaA-&chi; may pull SSB along while it translocates on DNA 
                     |CITS: [40442115]|.
                     Overexpression of <i>yoaA</i> increases tolerance to the 
                     chain terminating nucleoside analog, azidothymidine (AZT) 
                     in a wild-type background and in a variety of genetic 
                     backgrounds (<i>lexA3, recA, xthA</i>); &Delta;<i>yoaA</i> 
                     mutants are sensitive to AZT |CITS: [26544712]|. YoaA-&chi;
                     mediates tolerance to AZT |CITS: [26544712][33582602]|. 
                     |FRAME: EG11414-MONOMER HolD|, |FRAME: CPLX0-8165 SSB| and 
                     |FRAME: EG10243-MONOMER DnaQ| are implicated in the 
                     YoaA-mediated tolerance to AZT |CITS: [26544712]|.
                     YoaA is a superfamily 2 (SF2) helicase (see |CITS: 
                     [20456941]|).
                     Mutations in <i>yoaA</i> are synergistic with mutations in 
                     |FRAME: EG11296 <i>radA</i>| for sensitivity to AZT |CITS: 
                     [25484163]|. Double <i>yoaA</i> |FRAME: EG11357 
                     <i>dinG</i>| mutants exhibit strong synergistic sensitivity
                     to AZT |CITS: [26544712]|."
