     gene            1891189..1892553
                     /gene="sdaA"
                     /locus_tag="b1814"
                     /label=sdaA
     CDS             1891189..1892553
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="sdaA"
                     /locus_tag="b1814"
                     /product="bifunctional L-serine deaminase I / L-serine
                     deaminase"
                     /EC_number="4.3.1.17"
                     /label=sdaA
                     /note="L-serine deaminase I (SdaA) is one of three enzymes 
                     carrying out the sole step in the
                     pathway of L-serine degradation, converting serine into a 
                     basic
                     cellular building block, pyruvate.
                     SdaA catalyzes the conversion of L-serine into pyruvate and
                     ammonia |CITS: [2504697][8436113][15155761]|.
                     SdaA contains a catalytically critical 4Fe-4S cluster that 
                     interacts directly with the L-serine substrate |CITS: 
                     [15155761]|.
                     This cluster is only present when the enzyme is synthesized
                     under anaerobic conditions |CITS: [2504697][8436113]|. 
                     Oxidatively inactivated serine deaminase can be activated 
                     <i>in vitro</i> with a combination of iron sulfate and 
                     dithiothreitol |CITS: [3888962][8436113][15155761]|. 
                     Activation <i>in vivo</i>, presumably involving 
                     construction
                     of the 4Fe-4S cluster, appears to require multiple 
                     additional
                     gene products |CITS: [3888962]|."
