                     /product="TerC family inner membrane protein YoaE"
                     /label=yoaE
                     /note="YoaE is predicted to be an inner membrane protein
                     with seven transmembrane domains; experimental topology 
                     analysis suggests that the C terminus is located in the 
                     cytoplasm |CITS: [15919996]|.
                     In <i>Salmonella Enteritidis</i>, YoaE was found to be 
                     required for survival in egg white |CITS: [31915212]|. 
                     Overexpression of <i>yoaE</i> from an ASKA plasmid leads to
                     a more than 3-fold increase in the MIC of hypochlorous acid
                     |CITS: [34072091]|."
