     CDS             1897339..1898139
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="manY"
                     /locus_tag="b1818"
                     /product="bifunctional mannose-specific PTS enzyme IIC
                     component / mannose-specific PTS enzyme II"
                     /EC_number="2.7.1.191; 2.7.1.199; 2.7.1.193"
                     /label=manY
                     /note="ManY is a hydrophobic integral membrane protein
                     which together with ManZ forms the transmembrane channel of
                     the <i>E. coli</i> ManXYZ mannose permease |CITS: 
                     [2951378]|. ManY contains a PTS Enzyme IIC domain. The ManY
                     and ManZ proteins alone are sufficient for penetration of  
                     &lambda; phage DNA |CITS: [2951378]|. Engineered expression
                     of |FRAME: EG10227-MONOMER ""DicB""| (encoded on the Qin 
                     prophage) inhibits ManYZ-mediated phage uptake and 
                     transport of the PTS sugars, mannose and glucosamine; the 
                     new phenotypes (phage &lambda; resistance and growth 
                     inhibition on plates with mannose or glucosamine as carbon 
                     source) are dependent on DicB-MinC interaction |CITS: 
                     [31527115]|.
                     The ManY (and ManZ) structure consists of core, arm and 
                     V-motif domains; the core domains form the substrate 
                     binding site of a ManYZ protomer |CITS: [31209249]|.
                     "
