                     /locus_tag="b1819"
                     /product="bifunctional mannose-specific PTS enzyme IID
                     component / mannose-specific PTS enzyme II"
                     /EC_number="2.7.1.191; 2.7.1.199; 2.7.1.193"
                     /label=manZ
                     /note="ManZ is a moderately hydrophobic membrane protein
                     which together with ManY forms the transmembrane channel of
                     the <i>E. coli</i> ManXYZ mannose permease |CITS: 
                     [2999119][2951378]|. ManZ contains a PTS Enzyme IID domain.
                     The ManZ and ManY proteins alone are sufficient for 
                     penetration of  &lambda; phage DNA |CITS: [2951378]|. 
                     Engineered expression of |FRAME: EG10227-MONOMER ""DicB""| 
                     (encoded on the Qin prophage) inhibits ManYZ mediated phage
                     uptake and transport of the PTS sugars, mannose and 
                     glucosamine; the new phenotypes (phage &lambda; resistance 
                     and growth inhibition on plates with mannose or glucosamine
                     as carbon source) are dependent on DicB-MinC interaction 
                     |CITS: [31527115]|.
                     The ManZ (and ManY) structure consists of core, arm and 
                     V-motif domains; the core domains form the substrate 
                     binding site of a ManYZ protomer |CITS: [31209249]|."
