     gene            1899945..1900511
                     /gene="mntP"
                     /locus_tag="b1821"
                     /label=mntP
     CDS             1899945..1900511
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="mntP"
                     /locus_tag="b1821"
                     /product="Mn(2+) exporter"
                     /label=mntP
                     /note="<i>mntP</i> encodes the primary manganese exporter.
                     An <i>mntP</i> deletion strain exhibits increased 
                     sensitivity to manganese and accumulates approximately 
                     2-fold more intracellular manganese than the wild type 
                     |CITS: [21908668]|. MntP confers robust manganese 
                     resistance; MntP expression affects resistance to reactive 
                     oxygen species; ectopic production of MntP halts the growth
                     of a strain (&Delta;<i>ahpCF</i> &Delta;<i>katG</i>) that 
                     accumulates high levels of hydrogen peroxide |CITS: 
                     [29440394]|. Inactivation of MntP increases the recovery of
                     DNA replication after H<sub>2</sub>O<sub>2</sub> exposure 
                     |CITS: [37493920]|. Exposure to 10 &micro;M manganese 
                     chloride results in increased expression of <i>mntP</i> and
                     increased levels of a chromosomal MntP fusion protein; this
                     induction is attenuated in an <i>mntR</i> deletion strain 
                     |CITS: [21908668]|. <i>mntP</i> expression is regulated by 
                     manganese levels through the transcription factors MntR and
                     Fur; <i>mntP</i> expression is regulated 
                     post-transcriptionally by a manganese-responsive, 
                     <i>yybP-ykoYY</i> family riboswitch located in the 5' 
                     untranslated region of <i>mntP</i> |CITS: [25794618]|. The 
                     <i>mntP</i> riboswitch is also responsive to intracellular 
                     pH; alkaline pH favors the interaction between manganese 
                     and the riboswitch which results in enhanced manganese 
                     efflux |CITS: [36190429]| (see also |CITS: [38869303]|). A 
                     crystal structure of the Mn<sup>2+</sup> responsive 
                     <i>yybP-ykoY</i> family riboswitch at 3.8 &Aring; revealed 
                     the binding domain and its ability to change conformation 
                     under alkaline conditions but not across other pH 
                     conditions |CITS: [40252020]|.
                     The <i>mntP</i> riboswitch also serves as a platform for 
                     Rho-dependent transcription termination; Rho-dependent 
                     termination acts to moderate MntP levels in both the 
                     presence and absence of manganese stress and this protects 
                     the cell from membrane protein toxicity |CITS: [39510182]|.
                     MntP contains 6 predicted transmembrane helices and belongs
                     to the LysE superfamily of transporters |CITS: 
                     [29440394][26546518]|.
                     Deletion of <i>mntP</i> fully phenocopies overproduction of
                     |FRAME: MONOMER0-4216 ""MntS""|; MntS may inhibit MntP 
                     function |CITS: [25774656]|."
