     gene            complement(1901705..1901848)
                     /gene="yobF"
                     /locus_tag="b1824"
                     /label=yobF
     CDS             complement(1901705..1901848)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yobF"
                     /locus_tag="b1824"
                     /product="DUF2527 domain-containing protein YobF"
                     /label=yobF
                     /note="YobF is a small protein that belongs to the DUF2527 
                     family of proteins of unknown function.
                     YobF expression is post-transcriptionally regulated by the 
                     |FRAME: RYEE-RNA| |CITS: [23980183]|.  <i>yobF</i> was 
                     predicted to be a target of the |FRAME: OXYS-RNA|. 
                     Overexpression of OxyS decreases the expression of 
                     <i>yobF</i> |CITS: [16717284]|.  YobF is expressed during 
                     stationary phase |CITS: [19121005]|.  Levels of YobF 
                     protein increases after heat shock; induction occurs at the
                     post-transcriptional level |CITS: [19734316]|.
                     In growth competition experiments, a <i>yobF</i> deletion 
                     mutant is more sensitive to cell envelope stress and acute 
                     acid stress than the wild type |CITS: [19734312]|.
                     The |FRAME: G7000| gene was found to be commonly mutated in
                     a laboratory evolution study aimed to increase tolerance to
                     several industrial chemicals. The authors defined YobF as a
                     stress signaling protein |CITS: [36738854]|.
                     Review: |CITS: [30810554]|"
