     gene            complement(1902880..1903023)
                     /gene="mgrB"
                     /locus_tag="b1826"
                     /label=mgrB
     CDS             complement(1902880..1903023)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="mgrB"
                     /locus_tag="b1826"
                     /product="PhoQ kinase inhibitor"
                     /label=mgrB
                     /note="MgrB is a small, inner membrane protein that
                     mediates a negative feedback loop in the PhoQP two 
                     component system.
                     MgrB negatively regulates the activity of the |FRAME: 
                     PHOQ-MONOMER| |CITS: [20041203]|. PhoQ is involved in 
                     sensing external magnesium concentrations and then 
                     activating |FRAME: PHOP-MONOMER|. Thus, by negatively 
                     regulating PhoQ activity, MgrB downregulates PhoP activity 
                     and the transcription of a wide range of genes whose 
                     expression is controlled by PhoP regulation. This set of 
                     genes includes <i>mgrB</i> itself |CITS: [20041203]|. MgrB 
                     inhibits the kinase activity of PhoQ; this inhibition 
                     drives the partial adaption response that PhoPQ exhibits in
                     response to strong activating stimuli such as a major 
                     downward shift in extracellular Mg<sup>2+</sup> levels 
                     |CITS: [27447896]|.
                     MgrB localizes to the inner membrane, in accord with prior 
                     predictions that it would have a transmembrane segment; 
                     MgrB directly interacts with PhoQ |CITS: 
                     [19121005][20041203][32482726]|. MgrB may act to mediate a 
                     pathway that senses disruptions to the oxidizing 
                     environment of the periplasm and activates the PhoQP 
                     two-component system |CITS: [22267510]|.
                     Transcription of <i>mgrB</i> is induced by low magnesium 
                     and is controlled by the PhoP/PhoQ two-component system 
                     |CITS: [10464230]|. PhoP binds to the <i>mgrB</i> promoter 
                     region <i>in vitro</i> |CITS: [12813061]|.
                     An <i>mgrB</i> deletion causes a ""glycogen-excess"" 
                     phenotype in cells entering stationary phase |CITS: 
                     [17543954]|. In growth competition experiments, an 
                     <i>mgrB</i> deletion mutant is more sensitive to acute acid
                     stress than the wild type |CITS: [19734312]|. As would be 
                     expected from its regulatory relationship with the PhoQP 
                     system, deletion of <i>mgrB</i> leads to a 3-9-fold 
                     increase in expression of genes regulated by the system 
                     |CITS: [20041203]|. Mutation of MgrB's predicted 
                     periplasmic cysteine residues C28 and C39 blocks the effect
                     of a <i>dsbA</i> null mutation on PhoQ activity |CITS: 
                     [22267510]|.
                     Adaptive laboratory evolution of <i>E. coli</i> MG1655 in 
                     the presence of trimethoprim resulted in loss-of-function 
                     mutations in <i>mgrB</i>, which causes derepression of 
                     PhoPQ signaling thus enabling resistance to trimethoprim. A
                     &Delta;<i>mgrB</i> mutant strain confirmed resistance to 
                     trimethoprim was due to <i>mgrB</i>, but the mutant strain 
                     also resulted in elevated |FRAME: 
                     DIHYDROFOLATEREDUCT-MONOMER DHFR| levels which is linked to
                     antibiotic resistance  |CITS: [34591012]|.
                     MgrB: ""<b>Mg</b><sup>2+</sup>-<b>r</b>esponsive gene"" 
                     |CITS: [10464230]|
                     Review: |CITS: [30810554]|"
                     /translation="MKKFRWVVLVVVVLACLLLWAQVFNMMCDQDVQFFSGICAINQFI
