     gene            complement(1905952..1906833)
                     /gene="htpX"
                     /locus_tag="b1829"
                     /label=htpX
     CDS             complement(1905952..1906833)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="htpX"
                     /locus_tag="b1829"
                     /product="protease HtpX"
                     /label=htpX
                     /note="HtpX is a heat shock protein that may be involved
                     in degrading misfolded proteins |CITS: [1826904]|. 
                     Expression of HtpX is controlled by the CpxR-CpxA signal 
                     system, which senses abnormal proteins. The Cpx pathway has
                     been shown to become activated by abnormal folding of 
                     proteins at the periplasmic surface of the cytoplasmic 
                     membrane |CITS:[11285215]|.
                     Overexpression of HtpX leads to enhanced degradation of 
                     partial-length puromycyl peptides |CITS: 
                     [12081643][1826904]|.
                     The putative zinc metalloproteinase active site of HtpX is 
                     located on the cytosolic side of the
                     inner membrane. Mutations in this site abrogate HtpX 
                     function |CITS: [12081643]|. HtpX is integrated into the 
                     inner membrane with two N-terminally located transmembrane 
                     segments |CITS: [12081643]|.
                     Review: |CITS: [19454621]|"
