     CDS             1910515..1911798
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="letA"
                     /locus_tag="b1833"
                     /product="intermembrane transport protein LetA"
                     /label=letA
                     /note="LetA is an inner membrane protein with six
                     transmembrane regions |CITS: [27795327]|.
                     <i>letAB</I>, <i>pqiABC</i> and |FRAME: ABC-45-CPLX 
                     ""<i>mlaFEDCB""|</i> are related loci; <i>letAB</i> (and 
                     <i>pqiABC</I>) are predicted to encode inter-membrane 
                     transport pathways that contribute to membrane integrity; 
                     simultaneous deletion of <i>letAB</I> and <i>pqiABC</i> in 
                     a &Delta;<i>mlaD</i> background increases sensitivity to 
                     EDTA and SDS; the substrate for transport is not known 
                     |CITS: [27795327]| (see also |CITS: [32359438]|). 
                     <i>letA</i> shows differential codon adaptation, resulting 
                     in differential translation efficiency signatures, in 
                     thermophilic microbes.  It was therefore predicted to play 
                     a role in the heat shock response.  A <i>letA</i> deletion 
                     mutant was shown to be more sensitive than wild-type 
                     specifically to heat shock, but not other stresses |CITS: 
                     [24580753]|. A <i>letA'-'lacZ</i> fusion is induced in 
                     cells that produce truncated lipopolysaccharide or have 
                     other membrane defects |CITS: [27795327]|.
                     <i>letA</i>: <U>l</U>ipophilic <U>e</U>nvelope-spanning 
                     <U>t</U>unnel |CITS: [32359438]|"
