     gene            1914480..1915919
                     /gene="rsmF"
                     /locus_tag="b1835"
                     /label=rsmF
     CDS             1914480..1915919
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rsmF"
                     /locus_tag="b1835"
                     /product="bifunctional 16S rRNA m(5)C1407 and tRNA-Tyr
                     m(5)C49 methyltransferase / 16S rRNA m(5)C1407 
                     methyltransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.1.1.178"
                     /label=rsmF
                     /note="RsmF is a dual-substrate RNA-modifying
                     methyltransferase responsible for methylation of 16S rRNA 
                     at the C5 position of the C1407 nucleotide |CITS: 
                     [16678201]| and for m<sup>5</sup>c modification to the 
                     anticodon of |FRAME: TYR-tRNAs tRNA<sup>Tyr</sup>| at 
                     position C49 |CITS: [39495928]|. <i>In vitro</i>, the 
                     enzyme methylates 16S rRNA within the 30S ribosomal 
                     subunit, but not naked 16S rRNA or 70S ribosomes |CITS: 
                     [16678201]|.
                     The enzyme was identified by similarity to the RsmB 
                     methyltransferase, which is responsible for methylation of 
                     C967 of 16S rRNA |CITS: [10454610][16678201]|.
                     A crystal structure of RsmF has been solved at 2.9 &Aring; 
                     resolution. The enzyme has an N-terminal catalytic domain 
                     that binds S-adenosylmethionine; the C-terminal domain has 
                     structural similarity to PUA domains of pseudouridine 
                     synthases and archaeosine-specific transglycosylases. A 
                     mechanism for substrate specificity and recognition has 
                     been proposed |CITS: [16793063]|.
                     Methylation of G1405 by the aminoglycoside resistance 
                     methyltransferases Sgm |CITS: [19509304]|, ArmA, RmtB, and 
                     RmtC |CITS: [22330907]| interferes with methylation of 
                     C1407 by RsmF.
                     A strain carrying a null mutation in <i>rsmF</i> contains 
                     16S rRNA with unmethylated C1407 |CITS: [16678201]|. The 
                     mutant exhibits a growth defect and reduced fitness in 
                     competition with wild-type cells |CITS: 
                     [16678201][22330907]| and has increased resistance to a 
                     number of aminoglycoside antibiotics |CITS: [22330907]|. An
                     <i>rsmF</i> deletion mutant allows some translation 
                     initiation by a mutant initiator tRNA |CITS: [18288206]|. 
                     Both transcription of <i>rsmF</i> and tRNA modification by 
                     RsmF are induced in response to reactive oxygen species 
                     (ROS) from the Fenton reaction; tRNA modification is also 
                     induced by heat shock |CITS: [39495928]|.
                     RsmF: ""<b>r</b>RNA <b>s</b>mall subunit 
                     <b>m</b>ethyltransferase <b>F</b>"" |CITS: [16678201]| 
                     Review: |CITS: [20007150]|"
