     gene            complement(1921036..1923096)
                     /gene="ptrB"
                     /locus_tag="b1845"
                     /label=ptrB
     CDS             complement(1921036..1923096)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ptrB"
                     /locus_tag="b1845"
                     /product="bifunctional oligopeptidase B / oligopeptidase"
                     /EC_number="3.4.21.83"
                     /label=ptrB
                     /note="Oligopeptidase B, originally called protease II, is
                     a serine protease that hydrolyzes peptide bonds following 
                     arginines and lysines |CITS: [1769955]|.  The enzyme is 
                     very efficient at cleaving after paired basic amino acid 
                     residues such as Arg-Arg |CITS: [9223183]|.  Its 
                     specificity for artificial peptide substrates has been 
                     compared with |FRAME: EG11441-MONOMER| |CITS: [16515865]| 
                     and oligopeptidases from other organisms |CITS: 
                     [23123472]|.  PtrB is able to degrade and thereby 
                     inactivate several short antimicrobial peptides (AMPs) 
                     |CITS: [24225368]|.
                     The enzyme belongs to the prolyl oligopeptidase family of 
                     serine peptidases |CITS: [1953688][9223183]|.
                     A noncanonical translation initiation mechanism was 
                     discovered for PtrB.  The <i>ptrB</i> mRNA begins with an 
                     AUG codon at its very 5' end (5'-uAUG).  Although 
                     translation of the potential 5' ORF is poor, the 5'-uAUG is
                     required for efficent translation of PtrB |CITS: 
                     [27467758]|.  The 5'-uAUG functions as a ribosome 
                     recognition signal that compensates for the poor 
                     Shine-Dalgarno sequence upstream of the <i>ptrB</i> ORF 
                     |CITS: [28484048]|.
                     Overexpression of <i>ptrB</i> from a plasmid confers 
                     increased resistance to the proline-rich antimicrobial 
                     peptide Bac7(1-16) and certain other AMPs |CITS: 
                     [24225368]|.
                     OpdB: ""<b>o</b>ligo<b>p</b>epti<b>d</b>ase <b>B</b>"" 
                     |CITS: [24225368]|
                     Reviews: |CITS: [18029266][28484051]|
                     "
