     gene            complement(1933479..1934450)
                     /gene="lpxM"
                     /locus_tag="b1855"
                     /label=lpxM
     CDS             complement(1933479..1934450)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="lpxM"
                     /locus_tag="b1855"
                     /product="bifunctional Lipid A biosynthesis
                     myristoyltransferase / myristoyl-acyl carrier 
                     protein-dependent acyltransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.3.1.243"
                     /label=lpxM
                     /note="Myristoyl-acyl carrier protein (ACP)-dependent 
                     acyltransferase (LpxM) catalyzes the transfer of myristate 
                     from myristoyl-ACP to the 3'-R-3-hydroxymyristoyl chain of 
                     KDO<sub>2</sub>-(lauroyl)-lipid IV<sub>A</sub>. This is one
                     of the last two acylation reactions needed to synthesize 
                     KDO<sub>2</sub>-lipid A. LpxM functions optimally after 
                     laurate incorporation by LpxL has taken place |CITS: 
                     [9099672]|. LpxM shares sequence homology and functional 
                     similarity to LpxL |CITS: [1732206]|.
                     Mutants of <i>lpxM</i> are characterized by attenuated 
                     cytokine induction and with an LPS that lacked the 
                     myristoyl fatty acid moiety of the lipid A |CITS: 
                     [8567955]|. Overexpression of <i>lpxM</i> (<i>msbB</i>) 
                     suppresses the temperature sensitive growth associated with
                     mutations in the <i>lpxL</i> gene. Mutations in <i>lpxM</i>
                     have caused reduced acylation of LPS, resulting in 
                     constitutive expression of the sigma(E) regulon above 
                     wild-type levels |CITS: [15720549]|. Strains overexpressing
                     LpxM and with a deleted <i>kdtA</i>, the gene encoding the 
                     KDO transferase, accumulated pentaacylated lipid A |CITS: 
                     [19754149]|.
                     Mutational analysis has shown that the <i>lpxM</i> gene is 
                     not essential for growth |CITS: [1732206]|.
                     When <i>E. coli</i> cells are subjected to cold shock or 
                     grown at low temperatures, palmitoleate is incorporated 
                     into lipid A instead of laurate |CITS: [10092655]|."
