                     /locus_tag="b1864"
                     /product="putative transcriptional regulator YebC"
                     /label=yebC
                     /note="At 20&deg;C and in the absence of the protein
                     |FRAME: EG11837-MONOMER BipA|, YebC appears to regulate 
                     genes involved in biofilm formation, LPS synthesis, capsule
                     production, and resistance to bile salts |CITS: [37152896]|
                     <i>yebC</i> insertion mutants were identified in a genetic 
                     screen for genes that are important for survival of 
                     exposure to ionizing radiation (IR).  A <i>yebC</i> 
                     deletion mutant has a substantial decrease in IR survival 
                     |CITS: [25049088]|.  A <i>yebC</i> null mutant grows 
                     normally at 37&deg;C |CITS: [10572302]|, but is more 
                     sensitive to nalidixic acid and kasugamycin than wild type 
                     |CITS: [23308060]|.
                     YebC has a similar phylogenetic distribution as the RuvABC 
                     resolvasome complex |CITS: [23046553]|."
