                     /product="cytochrome c quinol dehydrogenase TorY"
                     /label=torY
                     /note="The periplasmic oxidoreductase |FRAME:
                     G7022-MONOMER ""TorZ""| and membrane anchored pentaheme 
                     <I>c</I>-type cytochrome TorY constitute an anaerobic 
                     respiratory system that can use several <i>N</i> and 
                     <i>S</i>-oxides, including TMAO and biotin sulfoxide as 
                     terminal electron acceptors |CITS: [11004177]|.
                     TorY is a <i>c</i>-type cytochrome that is anchored to the 
                     inner membrane; 5 predicted heme binding sites (CXXCH) have
                     been identified. TorY has 36% identity with |FRAME: 
                     EG11815-MONOMER | |CITS: [11004177]|.
                     <i>torYZ</i> expression is very low and is not induced by 
                     TMAO or DMSO |CITS: [11004177]|."
