     gene            complement(1952698..1953004)
                     /gene="micL"
                     /locus_tag="b4717"
                     /label=micL
     misc_RNA        complement(1952698..1953004)
                     /gene="micL"
                     /locus_tag="b4717"
                     /product="small regulatory RNA MicL"
                     /note="MicL is a small RNA that negatively regulates
                     translation of |FRAME: EG10544 <i>lpp</i>|, one of the most
                     highly expressed genes in <i>E. coli</i>. Binding of Hfq to
                     MicL and MicL-S stabilizes both small RNAs |CITS: 
                     [25030700]|. MicL (SlrA) was isolated as a suppressor of 
                     the &Delta;<i>lapAB</i> mutant phenotype |CITS: 
                     [24722986]|.
                     The 307 |CITS: [24722986]| (or 308 |CITS: [25030700]|) nt 
                     primary transcript is processed to yield the 80 nt MicL-S 
                     non-coding RNA |CITS: [24722986][25030700]|. Correct 
                     processing of MicL to MicL-S by RNase E requires stable 
                     tandem stem-loops that are located 3' to the cleavage site 
                     |CITS: [30462307]|.
                     MicL appears to have many genetic interactions with other 
                     sRNAs under different growth conditions |CITS: [35920556]|.
                     Expression of MicL is &sigma;<sup>E</sup>-dependent and 
                     induced during transition to stationary phase |CITS: 
                     [25030700][31992590]|. The transcript of <i>micL</i> is 
                     increased after &sigma;E induction, but no effect on 
                     expression was observed for its target, based on 
                     high-throughput analysis of gene expression |CITS: 
                     [31992590]|. Expression of MicL on a medium-copy plasmid 
                     rescues the growth defect of the &Delta;<i>lapAB</i> 
                     deletion strain on rich medium and MacConkey agar. 
                     Constitutive expression of MicL rescues the growth defect 
                     of a &Delta;<i>degP</i> strain at 42&deg;C |CITS: 
                     [24722986]|. Overexpression of RyeF (MicL) decreases 
                     swarming motility |CITS: [26469694]|. A &Delta;<i>micL</i> 
                     mutant is sensitive to cell envelope stress |CITS: 
                     [19734312]|. Single mutation of <i>micL</i> slightly 
                     enhances cell growth when ribose is used as a sole carbon 
                     source |CITS: [35920556]|.
                     SlrA: ""<b>s</b>uppressing <i><b>l</b>ap</i> <b>R</b>NA"" 
                     |CITS: [24722986]|
                     MicL: ""<b>m</b>RNA-<b>i</b>nterfering <b>c</b>omplementary
                     RNA regulator of <b>L</b>pp"" |CITS: [25030700]|
                     Reviews: |CITS: [26618164][29992897]|"
