     CDS             complement(1957229..1959307)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="flhA"
                     /locus_tag="b1879"
                     /product="bifunctional flagellar biosynthesis protein FlhA
                     / flagellar export assembly apparatus"
                     /label=flhA
                     /note="FlhA is one of six integral membrane components of
                     the flagellar export apparatus.
                     FlhA has two regions: the hydrophobic N-terminal 
                     transmembrane region
                     with eight membrane-spanning segments and the C-terminal 
                     cytoplasmic domain |CITS:[8002586]|.
                     The structures of the C-terminal domain of FlhA and a 
                     fragment of the domain have been
                     determined by X-ray crystallography to a resolution of 2.9 
                     and 3.2 &Aring;, respectively |CITS:[16511106]|. 
                     Temperature-sensitive mutations in the cytoplasmic region 
                     of FlhA can prevent flagellar export |CITS:[10712687]|. 
                     FlhA is osmosensitive and is involved in the stress 
                     response at pH 6.5 or lower |CITS:[24060380]|."
