     CDS             complement(1967617..1969290)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="cheA"
                     /locus_tag="b1888"
                     /product="chemotaxis protein CheA(S)"
                     /label=cheA
                     /note="<i>Escherichia coli</i> expresses CheA as both a
                     full length molecule |FRAME: CHEA-CPLX ""(CheAL)""| and as 
                     a shorter version (CheAS) translated from an alternative 
                     start codon; CheAS lacks the N-terminal 97 amino acids of 
                     CheAL including the site of autophosphorylation |CITS: 
                     [6449010][2002011]|. CheAS can mediate <i>in vitro</i> 
                     phosphorylation of kinase-deficient CheAL mutant proteins 
                     which retain the site of autophosphorylation; CheAS can 
                     restore kinase function and chemotactic ability to cells 
                     expressing kinase deficient or truncated CheAL variants 
                     |CITS: [8434013][8045878]|. Mutants which do not express 
                     CheAS retain chemotactic ability under laboratory 
                     conditions |CITS: [7751280]|. CheAS interacts with CheZ 
                     <i>in situ</i>; CheAS forms a complex with CheZ <i>in 
                     vitro</i> only under reducing conditions; CheAS-CheZ 
                     complexes enhance the rate of dephosphorylation of CheY-P 
                     <i>in vitro</i> |CITS: [8820640]|. Polar localisation of 
                     the CheZ phosphatase requires CheA(S) |CITS: 
                     [12644507][19502407]|. Co-expression of CheAL, CheAS and 
                     CheZ occurs widely in motile isolates of the 
                     Enterobacteriaceae |CITS: [9045846]|."
