     gene            complement(1971465..1971559)
                     /gene="motR"
                     /locus_tag="b4828"
                     /label=motR
     misc_RNA        complement(1971465..1971559)
                     /gene="motR"
                     /locus_tag="b4828"
                     /product="small RNA MotR"
                     /note="The Hfq-dependent small RNA MotR and 19 potential
                     targets were identified by applying a small RNA prediction 
                     algorithm to RIL-seq data |CITS: [34093460]|.
                     MotR is most highly expressed during the exponential phase 
                     and under iron limitation |CITS: [34093460][37843988]|. 
                     Notably, the expression of MotR experiences a decline in 
                     the presence of glucose phosphate (G6P) |CITS: [37843988]|.
                     Computational analysis indicates the presence of strong 
                     stem-loops at the 3A' end of MotR |CITS: [37843988]|. 
                     Intriguingly, overexpressing MotR results in a substantial 
                     increase in the number of flagella, albeit with only a 
                     slight enhancement in bacterial motility |CITS: 
                     [37843988]|. Comprehensive RIL-seq and RNA-seq analyses 
                     unveil the regulatory role of MotR, revealing potential 
                     targets primarily associated with ribosomal proteins and 
                     genes within the late and middle stages of the flagella 
                     regulon |CITS: [37843988]|.
                     Review: |CITS: [32213244]|"
