     gene            complement(1975068..1975868)
                     /gene="otsB"
                     /locus_tag="b1897"
                     /label=otsB
     CDS             complement(1975068..1975868)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="otsB"
                     /locus_tag="b1897"
                     /product="trehalose-6-phosphate phosphatase"
                     /EC_number="3.1.3.12"
                     /label=otsB
                     /note="<i>otsB</i> encodes the biosynthetic 
                     trehalose-6-phosphate phosphatase, which belongs to the 
                     superfamily of haloacid dehalogenase (HAD)-like hydrolases 
                     |CITS: [1310094][7966317]|.  The phosphatase activity of 
                     OtsB was also found in a high-throughput screen of purified
                     proteins |CITS: [15808744]|.
                     Accumulation of trehalose at low temperatures enhances cell
                     viability |CITS: [12105274]|.  An <i>otsBA</i> double 
                     mutant is more sensitive than wild type to heat shock 
                     during stationary phase, but not during exponential growth 
                     |CITS: [1744047]|.
                     Expression of <i>otsB</i> is increased under osmotic stress
                     |CITS: [3131312][16420371][17015655]| and induced during 
                     the transition to stationary phase and by low temperature 
                     in a &sigma;<sup>S</sup>-dependent manner |CITS: 
                     [1744047][12105274][18174134]|.  Stability of <i>otsBA</i> 
                     mRNA is increased approximately 10-fold at 16&deg;C 
                     compared to 37&deg;C |CITS: [12105274]|.  Under 
                     nutrient-limiting conditions in an RpoS mutant strain 
                     background, an adaptive mutation that allows 
                     RpoS-independent transcription of <i>otsBA</i> arises 
                     spontaneously and increases fitness |CITS: [19798444]|. 
                     OtsB: ""<b>o</b>smoregulatory <b>t</b>rehalose 
                     <b>s</b>ynthesis <b>B</b>"" |CITS: [3131312]|
                     Reviews: |CITS: [8391102][12626396][23302511][24068238]|"
