                     /label=sdsN
     misc_RNA        1990402..1990538
                     /gene="sdsN"
                     /locus_tag="b4719"
                     /product="small regulatory RNA SdsN"
                     /note="The <i>sdsN</i> locus produces two small RNAs, 
                     SdsN<sub>137</sub> and SdsN<sub>178</sub>, from different 
                     promoters.  The smaller RNA, SdsN<sub>137</sub>, negatively
                     regulates the synthesis of |FRAME: EG11261-MONOMER|, 
                     |FRAME: EG10456-MONOMER| and |FRAME: NARP-MONOMER NarP| and
                     confers resistance to nitrofurans |CITS: [27166377]|.
                     Due to its unusual interaction with Hfq |CITS: [36328526]|,
                     the larger product of the <i>sdsN</i> locus, 
                     SdsN<sub>178</sub> does not regulate expression of NfsA or 
                     NarP.  However, a shorter cleavage product of 
                     SdsN<sub>178</sub>, SdsN<sub>124</sub>, is able to repress 
                     expression of NfsA and HmpA |CITS: [27166377]|.
                     This small RNA was first identified by RNA-Seq |CITS: 
                     [21665928]|.
                     Expression of <i>sdsN</i> is induced in stationary phase 
                     and is dependent on &sigma;<sup>S</sup> |CITS: [27166377]|.
                      During logarithmic growth in either LB or glucose minimal 
                     medium, approximately equal expression of an ~75 nt 
                     fragment has been detected |CITS: [27190161]|. SdsN: 
                     ""&sigma;<sup><b>S</b></sup>-<b>d</b>ependent 
                     <b>s</b>R<b>N</b>A |CITS: [27166377]|
                     Review: |CITS: [32213244]|"
