     gene            complement(1993066..1993866)
                     /gene="tcyJ"
                     /locus_tag="b1920"
                     /label=tcyJ
     CDS             complement(1993066..1993866)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="tcyJ"
                     /locus_tag="b1920"
                     /product="multifunctional cystine ABC transporter
                     periplasmic binding protein / cystine ABC transporter / 
                     L-cystine ABC transporter / diaminopimelate ABC transporter
                     / djenkolate ABC transporter / lanthionine ABC transporter 
                     / D-cystine ABC transporter / homocystine ABC transporter"
                     /EC_number="7.4.2.12"
                     /label=tcyJ
                     /note="TcyJ (formerly FliY) is the periplasmic binding
                     protein of a cystine ABC transport system in <i>E. coli</i>
                     K-12 |CITS: [11421275][25139244]|.
                     Purified FliY binds cystine <i>in vitro</i> |CITS: 
                     [8450713]| (see further |CITS: [32144203]|). FliY is a 
                     member of the extracellular bacterial solute-binding family
                     3; FliY is exported to the periplasm |CITS: [8550423]|.
                     <i>fliY</i> forms an operon with |FRAME: EG11355 
                     ""<i>fliA</i>""| and |FRAME: EG11356 ""<i>fliZ</i>""| 
                     |CITS: [8550423]|.   The corresponding gene in 
                     <i>Salmonella typhimurium</i> is transcribed from both the 
                     flagellar promoter upstream of <i>fliA</i> and from a 
                     non-flagellar promoter upstream of <i>fliY</i> suggesting 
                     that <i>fliY</i> may not be a flagellar gene |CITS: 
                     [10411266]|. Overproduction does not affect motility |CITS:
                     [8550423]|.  A <i>fliZ fliY</i> double mutant shows a 
                     partial defect in motility |CITS: [8550423]|, probably due 
                     to the <i>fliZ</I> mutation |CITS: [10411266]|. Protein 
                     abundance is increased by acetate supplementation of the 
                     media |CITS: [11591692]| or by sulfate starvation |CITS: 
                     [8774726]|. <i>tcyJ</i> is expressed as a monocistronic 
                     transcript; expression is dependent on CysB and is induced 
                     during growth in sulfate medium |CITS: [26350134]|.
                     Wild-type strains are able to grow aerobically with 
                     djenkolate or lanthionine as the sole sulfur source but 
                     &Delta;<i>tcyJ</i> mutants cannot. Wild-type strains, 
                     &Delta;<i>tcyJ</i> mutants and &Delta;<i>tcyP</i> mutants 
                     are able to grow aerobically and anaerobically with 
                     L-cystine or D-cystine as sole sulfur source but 
                     &Delta;<i>tcyJ</i>&Delta;<i>tcyP</i> double mutants cannot.
                     Wild-type strains, &Delta;<i>tcyJ</i> mutants and 
                     &Delta;<i>tcyP</i> mutants are able to use homocystine as a
                     methionine precursor but 
                     &Delta;<i>tcyJ</i>&Delta;<i>tcyP</i> double mutants cannot 
                     |CITS: [26350134]|.
                     &Delta;<i>tcyJ</i> mutants show increased sensitivity to 
                     H<sub>2</sub>O<sub>2</sub> and are unable to grow in the 
                     presence of 0.5 mM H<sub>2</sub>O<sub>2</sub>; uptake of 
                     labelled L-cystine is significantly impaired in 
                     &Delta;<i>tcyJ</i> mutants |CITS: [20351115]|. 
                     Transcription of <i>tcyJ</i> is induced by 
                     H<sub>2</sub>O<sub>2</sub> and to a lesser extent by 
                     exogenous L-cysteine |CITS: [20351115]|.
                     FliY has similarity to <i>E. coli</i> PheC |CITS: 
                     [8550423]|, to the L-cystine uptake protein of 
                     <i>Lactobacillus fermentum</i> BR11, BspA, |CITS: 
                     [10094698]|, and to the <i>Salmonella typhimurium</i> FliY 
                     protein |CITS: [10411266]|.
                     Ssi7: ""sulfate starvation-induced"" |CITS: [8774726]|"
