                     /product="putative selenium transporter YedE"
                     /label=yedE
                     /note="YedE is predicted to be an inner membrane protein 
                     containing ten transmembrane domains; experimental topology
                     analysis suggests the C terminus is located in the 
                     cytoplasm |CITS: [15919996]|.
                     Comparative genomics implicates <i>yedE</i> in selenium 
                     transport |CITS: [25638258]|.
                     <i>E. coli</i> YedE is a member of the YedE/YeeE (YeeE) 
                     family of uncharacterized transporters |CITS: [24225317]|. 
                     <i>yedE</i> is downregulated under multiple stress 
                     conditions (heat, cold, oxidative stress, and antibiotic 
                     treatment) |CITS: [36144394]|."
