     gene            2003302..2003970
                     /gene="yedK"
                     /locus_tag="b1931"
                     /label=yedK
     CDS             2003302..2003970
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yedK"
                     /locus_tag="b1931"
                     /product="genome maintenance protein"
                     /label=yedK
                     /note="YedK is a genome maintenance protein that forms
                     covalent cross-links to abasic (apurinic/apyrimidinic) (AP)
                     sites in ssDNA; YedK is proposed to sense and bind to AP 
                     sites at stalled replication forks, forming a stable 
                     structure that shields these lesions from endonucleases and
                     error-prone polymerases.
                     Purified YedK binds DNA with a strong preference for ssDNA 
                     over dsDNA; YedK binds to ssDNA containing an AP site 
                     |CITS: [30554877]| (see also |CITS: [31504793]|).
                     YedK forms a stable thiazolidine linkage between its 
                     catalytic Cys-2 residue and a ring-opened AP site in ssDNA 
                     |CITS: [30554877][31235915]|.
                     YedK contains a positively charged channel or groove that 
                     binds the ssDNA phosphate backbone; crystal structures 
                     suggest the protein could accommodate dsDNA on the 3' side 
                     of the AP site but not on the 5' side and thus YedK may 
                     target DNA structures formed when polymerases stall at 
                     abasic sites |CITS: [31235915]| (see also |CITS: 
                     [31504793]|).
                     YedK contains a single SOS response associated peptidase 
                     (SRAP) domain. Single SRAP domain proteins are found in all
                     three domains of life and YedK is a homolog of the human 
                     genome maintenance protein known as HMCES |CITS: 
                     [30554877]|."
