     gene            2008361..2009356
                     /gene="fliG"
                     /locus_tag="b1939"
                     /label=fliG
     CDS             2008361..2009356
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="fliG"
                     /locus_tag="b1939"
                     /product="trifunctional flagellar motor switch protein
                     FliG / flagellar basal body / flagellum"
                     /label=fliG
                     /note="FliG is one of three components of the flagellar
                     motor's ""switch complex.""
                     FliG proteins consist of N-terminal (N), middle (M) and 
                     C-terminal (C) domains separated by short flexible linkers 
                     (helix<sub>NM</sub> and helix<sub>MC</sub>); the M and C 
                     domains each contain an Armadillo-repeat motif 
                     (ARM<sub>M</sub> and ARM<sub>C</sub>). FliG is monomeric in
                     solution but forms a multimeric ring structure during 
                     assembly of the flagellar complex; FliG monomers are linked
                     together by intermolecular ARM<sub>M</sub>-ARM<sub>C</sub> 
                     interactions; the FliG ring assembles using a domain-swap 
                     polymerization mechanism (see |CITS: [26854663]|).
                     For a description of flagellar gene nomenclature, including
                     old (<i>fla, flb</I>) and new (<i>flg, flh</i> and 
                     <i>fli</i>) symbols, see |CITS: [3070322]|."
