     gene            complement(2023929..2024399)
                     /gene="vsr"
                     /locus_tag="b1960"
                     /label=vsr
     CDS             complement(2023929..2024399)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="vsr"
                     /locus_tag="b1960"
                     /product="DNA mismatch endonuclease Vsr"
                     /label=vsr
                     /note="Vsr is an endonuclease that specifically recognizes
                     and exhibits strand-specific nicking at T:G DNA mismatches,
                     which arise from spontaneous deamination at 
                     5-methylcytosine, the product of Dcm (cytosine) methylation
                     |CITS: [1944537]|. Vsr activity counterbalances the 
                     mutagenesis associated with dcm activity |CITS: [1829427], 
                     [9324251]|.
                     Vsr is an essential component of the very short patch (VSP)
                     mismatch repair pathway, as is PolA |CITS: [1944537]|, 
                     whereas MutL and MutS are involved but not essential |CITS:
                     [1944537], [9461452], [22846989]|. A minimal VSP pathway 
                     containing the purified components Vsr, PolA, DNA ligase I 
                     (LigA) and a plasmid substrate has been reconstituted <i>in
                     vitro</i> |CITS: [22846989]|. Vsr binding to MutL 
                     antagonizes MutL homodimerization and decreases 
                     interactions among MutL, MutS, and MutH |CITS: [11585365]|.
                     <i>In vitro</i> stimulation of Vsr requires MutS, MutL and 
                     ATP hydrolysis |CITS:[19474347]|.
                     Crystal structures of Vsr are presented |CITS: [10612397], 
                     [12626704]|.  Vsr substrate recognition and substrate 
                     specificity has been examined in detail |CITS: [7823316], 
                     [7836300], [10612397], [10871403], [11124025], [11439018], 
                     [12626704]|.
                     A <i>vsr</i> mutation exhibits increased mutagenesis at the
                     C2 of CCAGG sequences, compared to wild type |CITS: 
                     [8349541], [7506360]|.  Vsr overproduction also results in 
                     increased mutagenesis |CITS: [8763960], [9324251], 
                     [9537396]|.
                     Regulation has been described |CITS: [2198248], [7694036], 
                     [10400606], [11371527]|.  The <i>vsr</i> and <i>dcm</i> 
                     genes overlap and are cotranscribed |CITS: [2198248], 
                     [7694036]|.  However, abundance of the Dcm and Vsr proteins
                     are subject to distinct regulation, and the abundance of 
                     Vsr is regulated by growth phase |CITS: [10400606]|.  The 
                     Dam (adenine) methylase affects regulation of Vsr abundance
                     |CITS: [11371527]|.
                     Reviews: |CITS: [8736526], [10946233], [10957969], 
                     [12067333], [12760037]|."
                     /translation="MADVHDKATRSKNMRAIATRDTAIEKRLASLLTGQGLAFRVQDAS
