     gene            complement(2024380..2025798)
                     /gene="dcm"
                     /locus_tag="b1961"
                     /label=dcm
     CDS             complement(2024380..2025798)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="dcm"
                     /locus_tag="b1961"
                     /product="DNA-cytosine methyltransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.1.1.37"
                     /label=dcm
                     /note="Dcm is a DNA cytosine methyltransferase that 
                     preferentially methylates sites of sequence 5' C-MeC-T 3' 
                     |CITS: [1097428]|.  This modification interferes with 
                     cleavage by the EcoRII restriction enzyme |CITS: 
                     [770462][14921][3011742][12399478]|, but does not offer the
                     cell full protection from EcoRII |CITS: [2104830]|. Not all
                     Dcm methylation sites are modified <i>in vivo</i> |CITS: 
                     [1584789]|.  The reaction catalyzed by Dcm has been 
                     characterized |CITS: [14921][6336735][6143811][8441638]|. 
                     Methylated cytosines are subject to deamination, which 
                     causes mutation of the C to a T, and Dcm and the product of
                     the adjacent gene, Vsr, are associated with a corrective 
                     mismatch repair activity, very short patch (VSP) repair 
                     |CITS: 
                     [2956428][3038536][2959653][3049557][1829427][7506360]|. 
                     Dcm has also affects transposition by Tn3 |CITS: 
                     [2561572]|.
                     Dcm is non-essential; a <i>dcm</i> mutant is viable |CITS: 
                     [375073]|.
                     Dcm also has utility as a modification enzyme that 
                     interferes with cleavage by several restriction enzymes 
                     used in the molecular biology laboratory |CITS: [2825125][ 
                     2825126][2834695][2657665][1945846][1314209][8371990]|. 
                     Regulation has been described |CITS: 
                     [2198248][7694036][10400606][11371527]|.
                     Dcm: ""<b>D</b>NA <b>c</b>ytosine <b>m</b>ethylase"" |CITS:
                     [4576399]|
                     Mec: ""5-<b>me</b>thyl-<b>c</b>ytosine"" |CITS: [4353870]| 
                     Reviews: |CITS: [8200522][8736526]|"
