     gene            complement(2026600..2026902)
                     /gene="drpB"
                     /locus_tag="b1963"
                     /label=drpB
     CDS             complement(2026600..2026902)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="drpB"
                     /locus_tag="b1963"
                     /product="cell division protein DrpB"
                     /label=drpB
                     /note="DrpB is a non-essential protein involved in cell
                     division that localizes to the septal ring.  Localization 
                     requires FtsZ, but not FtsEX, and is dependent on growth in
                     a medium with low osmotic strength |CITS: [32900831]|. 
                     Proteins interacting with DrpB were identified by BACTH 
                     assays and include DamX, FtsI, FtsN, FtsQ, YmgF, DedD, 
                     FtsA, as well as MalF, MalG and PBP2; however, the 
                     likelihood of false positives in this assay is high |CITS: 
                     [32900831]|.
                     DrpB is predicted to contain two transmembrane helices, 
                     with both the N- and C-terminus of the protein located in 
                     the cytoplasm |CITS: [32900831]|.
                     DrpB was identified as a multicopy suppressor of the 
                     &Delta;<i>ftsEX</i> mutant.  A &Delta;<i>drpB</i> mutant 
                     shows no obvious growth or cell division defect; however, a
                     &Delta;<i>drpB</i> &Delta;<i>dedD</i> double mutant shows 
                     lower plating efficiency and increased filamentation during
                     growth in rich media at 42&deg;C |CITS: [32900831]|.
                     <i>drpB</i> was in the top 20 genes with increased 
                     translation in response to extreme acid stress (pH 4.4 
                     compared to pH 7.6) as measured by ribosome coverage of its
                     transcripts using RNA-Seq |CITS: [37909716]|.
                     DrpB: ""<b>d</b>ivision <b>r</b>ing <b>p</b>rotein 
                     <b>B</b>"" |CITS: [32900831]|"
