     gene            2047124..2048440
                     /gene="shiA"
                     /locus_tag="b1981"
                     /label=shiA
     CDS             2047124..2048440
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="shiA"
                     /locus_tag="b1981"
                     /product="shikimate:H(+) symporter"
                     /label=shiA
                     /note="ShiA has been implicated in the high affinity
                     transport of shikimate, an intermediate in the aromatic 
                     amino acid biosynthetic pathway |CITS: [9524262][6050]|. 
                     Chromosomal mutants in <i>shiA</i> are unable to transport 
                     shikimate, and introduction of the cloned <i>shiA</i> gene 
                     restores shikimate transport |CITS: [9524262]|.  The ShiA 
                     protein has twelve predicted TMS and is a member of the 
                     major facilitator superfamily of transporters (MFS) |CITS: 
                     [9529885]| and hence is likely to function as a 
                     proton/shikimate symporter.  Analysis of a <i>shiA-lacZ</i>
                     fusion has suggested that <i>shiA</i> expression is 
                     constitutive and is not regulated by the TyrR repressor 
                     |CITS: [9524262]|.  The <i>shiA</i> gene probably 
                     constitutes a monocistronic operon.  Imported shikimate 
                     presumably serves as a substrate for biosynthesis of 
                     aromatic compounds."
