                     /product="nicotinate-nucleotide--dimethylbenzimidazole 
                     phosphoribosyltransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.4.2.21"
                     /label=cobT
                     /note="<i>E. coli</i> K-12, as well as natural isolates,
                     can synthesize cobalamin only when supplied with the 
                     intermediate
                     cobinamide |CITS: [8770581]|.  <i>cobT</i> encodes a 
                     predicted dimethylbenzimidazole phosphoribosyltransferase. 
                     In addition to its predicted phosphoribosyltransferase 
                     activity, it is likely that CobT also participates directly
                     in the
                     synthesis of DMB |CITS: [7592411]|.
                     Expression of the <i>cobUST</i> operon is induced by 
                     cobinamide |CITS: [7592411]|."
