     gene            2070593..2070961
                     /gene="cbeA"
                     /locus_tag="b2004"
                     /label=cbeA
     CDS             2070593..2070961
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="cbeA"
                     /locus_tag="b2004"
                     /product="CP4-44 prophage; cytoskeleton bundling-enhancing 
                     antitoxin CbeA"
                     /label=cbeA
                     /note="CbeA is the antitoxin of the CbtA-CbeA
                     toxin-antitoxin system.  Unlike other antitoxins, CbeA does
                     not interact directly with the toxin CbtA.  Instead, it 
                     antagonizes action of the toxin by interacting directly 
                     with MreB and FtsZ, the targets of CbtA, and enhances 
                     filament bundling.  CbeA is also able to neutralize toxic 
                     effects of other inhibitors of MreB and FtsZ |CITS: 
                     [22515815]|.
                     Episomal expression of <i>cbtA</i> causes inhibition of 
                     cell growth and decreased viability, compared to wild type,
                     and this phenotype is suppressed by coexpression of 
                     <i>cbeA</i>.  Antitoxin production appeared to reduce toxin
                     abundance |CITS: [14594833]|.
                     CbeA antitoxin activity appeared to require the 
                     <i>cbeA-cbtA</i> intergenic region |CITS: [14594833]|, 
                     although in other experiments, only the protein-coding 
                     region was required for activity |CITS: [22515815]|.
                     CbtA, YkfI, and YpjF have similarity to each other and 
                     define a protein family of cellular toxins |CITS: 
                     [14594833]|, with CbeA, YafW, and YfjZ defining a protein 
                     family of cognate antitoxins |CITS: [28257056]|.  The YafW 
                     and CbeA antitoxins are partially interchangeable with 
                     respect to inhibition of toxicity caused by YkfI, CbtA, and
                     YpjF production |CITS: [14594833][28257056]|.
                     A crystal structure of CbeA has been solved.  The protein 
                     shows structural similarity to the ribosome-interacting 
                     toxins YoeB and RelE |CITS: [20696400]|.
                     CbeA: ""<b>c</b>ytoskeleton <b>b</b>undling 
                     <b>e</b>nhancing factor <b>A</b>"" |CITS: [22515815]|"
                     /translation="MSDTLPGTTLPDDNHDRPWWGLPCTVTPCFGARLVQEGNRLHYLA
                     DRAGIRGLFSDADAYHLDQAFPLLMKQLELMLTSGELNPRHQHTVTLYAKGLTCKADTL
                     SSCDYVYLAVYPTPEMKN"
