     gene            complement(2072513..2072842)
                     /gene="tmaR"
                     /locus_tag="b2007"
                     /label=tmaR
     CDS             complement(2072513..2072842)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="tmaR"
                     /locus_tag="b2007"
                     /product="pole-localizer protein"
                     /label=tmaR
                     /note="TmaR controls the localization of the general PTS
                     system component |FRAME: CPLX0-7938| (EI). TmaR localizes 
                     to one cell pole mainly during the early log phase of 
                     growth; polar localization depends on phosphorylation of 
                     Tyr-72. TmaR-regulated clustering of EI at the cell pole 
                     negatively correlates with EI-mediated sugar uptake |CITS: 
                     [33376208]|.
                     TmaR forms phase-separated condensates at the poles that 
                     compartmentalize EI; formation of TmaR condensates depends 
                     on phosphorylation of Tyr-72 and requires (non-specific) 
                     RNA; TmaR recruits and stabilizes flagella-related 
                     transcripts to polar condensates, thus controlling flagella
                     formation |CITS: [37934665]|.
                     TmaR recruits the RNA chaperone |FRAME: CPLX0-1461| to 
                     polar condensates in cells under certain stresses; TmaR is 
                     also required for Hfq condensate formation in the cytoplasm
                     |CITS: [36577380]|.
                     A &Delta;<i>tmaR</i> mutant shows increased metabolism of 
                     PTS sugars; conversely, overexpression of TmaR reduces 
                     metabolism of PTS sugars. A <i>tmaR</i> mutant shows 
                     impaired survival under mildly acidic conditions when grown
                     on PTS sugars |CITS: [33376208]|. Levels of the 
                     flagella-related transcripts <i>motA, fliA, flgK, flgA,</i>
                     and <i>fliC</i> are significantly decreased in <i>tmrA</i> 
                     knockout cells |CITS: [37934665]|. <i>tmaR</i>: 
                     ""<b>t</b>argeting of sugar 
                     <b>m</b>etabolism-<b>a</b>ssociated <b>r</b>egulator"" 
                     |CITS: [33376208]|"
                     /translation="METTKPSFQDVLEFVRLFRRKNKLQREIQDVEKKIRDNQKRVLLL
                     DNLSDYIKPGMSVEAIQGIIASMKGDYEDRVDDYIIKNAELSKERRDISKKLKAMGEMK
                     NGEAK"
