     gene            complement(2074270..2074743)
                     /gene="sbmC"
                     /locus_tag="b2009"
                     /label=sbmC
     CDS             complement(2074270..2074743)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="sbmC"
                     /locus_tag="b2009"
                     /product="DNA gyrase inhibitor"
                     /label=sbmC
                     /note="SbmC is an inhibitor of DNA gyrase-mediated DNA 
                     supercoiling |CITS: [9442027]| that inhibits the enzyme 
                     activity
                     at an early step |CITS: [11850398]|.  Because this 
                     inhibitor interferes with DNA binding by gyrase, it also 
                     protects
                     the cell from toxins that act via DNA damage caused by 
                     DNA-bound gyrase (e.g. the extrachromosomal CcdB
                     and microcin B17 toxins and quinoline drugs) |CITS: 
                     [11850398][13680098]|. In addition, SbmC mitigates
                     DNA damage from alkylating agents that are not known to act
                     by disrupting gyrase function |CITS: [13680098]|. 
                     Overproduction causes filamentous cell morphology and 
                     growth defects, as does antisense expression |CITS: 
                     [9442027]|.  High-copy expression results in resistance to 
                     the DNA-damage- and SOS-response-inducing toxin mitomycin C
                     (MMC) |CITS: [11244065]|.  High-copy expression also 
                     results in resistance to the DNA gyrase toxin microcin B17 
                     (MccB17) and causes decreased microcin B17 extrusion |CITS:
                     [8709849]|.
                     SbmC binds to DNA gyrase and also exhibits a small amount 
                     of binding to the individual components of the gyrase 
                     holoenzyme, as measured by immunoprecipitation and by 
                     surface plasmon resonance |CITS: [11777918]|.  This binding
                     does not require ATP |CITS: [11777918]|.  An SbmC peptide 
                     composed of only residues 89 to 96 also exhibits gyrase 
                     binding and inhibition activity |CITS: [11777918]|. A 
                     crystal structure is presented |CITS: [11948793]|.
                     The protein has been overproduced and purified |CITS: 
                     [9442027]|.
                     Regulation has been described |CITS: [8709849], 
                     [11689018]|.  Gene expression is increased at stationary 
                     phase and by treatment with compounds that cause DNA damage
                     |CITS: [8709849]|.  SOS induction of sbmC gene expression 
                     is regulated by H-NS protein (the product of the hns gene),
                     which binds to the promoter, and induction also shows 
                     dependence on RpoS |CITS: [11689018]|.
                     The binding of the transcription factor |FRAME: CPLX0-226 
                     CRP| to a predicted CRP DNA binding site around the start 
                     of the <i>sbmC</i> gene has been demonstrated; however an 
                     effect of this binding on gene expression has not been 
                     analyzed |CITS: [37114659]|.
                     GyrI: ""DNA gyrase inhibitory protein"" |CITS: [9442027]|. 
                     Review (in Japanese): |CITS: [10432838]|."
