     gene            complement(2074862..2076028)
                     /gene="dacD"
                     /locus_tag="b2010"
                     /label=dacD
     CDS             complement(2074862..2076028)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="dacD"
                     /locus_tag="b2010"
                     /product="trifunctional D-alanyl-D-alanine
                     carboxypeptidase DacD / beta-lactamase / D-alanyl-D-alanine
                     carboxypeptidase"
                     /EC_number="3.5.2.6"
                     /label=dacD
                     /note="Penicillin-binding protein 6b (PBP6b), the product
                     of the <i>dacD</i> gene, is a penicillin-sensitive, 
                     membrane-bound D-alanyl D-alanine carboxypeptidase 
                     (DD-carboxypeptidase) which cleaves the carboxy-terminal 
                     D-alanine from peptidoglycan pentapeptides |CITS: 
                     [8955390]|. PBP6b DD-carboxypeptidase activity contributes 
                     to the maintenance of cell shape at low pH |CITS: 
                     [27329754]|.
                     The predicted amino acid sequence of PBP6b is 47.4% 
                     identical to |FRAME: CPLX0-8252 ""PBP5""| and 47.7% 
                     identical to |FRAME: CPLX0-8254 ""PBP6""| |CITS: 
                     [8955390]|. Increased expression of <i>dacD</i> in a strain
                     that contains <i>dacA</i> and <i>dacC</i> null alleles 
                     reduces the amount of pentapeptide muropeptides in 
                     peptidoglycan |CITS: [8955390]|.
                     DacD contains the conserved motif sequences, SxxK (SLTK), 
                     [S/Y]xN (SGN) and [K/H][T/S]G (KTG), of the serine 
                     acyltransferase superfamily |CITS: [8955390][12456788]|; 
                     DacD binds benzylpenicillin |CITS: [8955390]|. DacD does 
                     not contribute to intrinsic &beta;-lactam resistance in 
                     <i>E. coli</i> K-12, however overexpression of <i>dacD</i> 
                     partially complements the &beta;-lactam sensitivity of a 
                     &Delta;<i>dacA</i> mutant |CITS: [21719544]|. Purified, 
                     soluble DacD binds Bocillin FL penicillin and has moderate 
                     deacylation activity; it also exhibits DD-carboxpeptidase 
                     activity with the model substrate diacetyl-Lys-D-Ala-D-Ala 
                     and with the the peptidoglycan mimetic pentapeptide 
                     substrate, L-Ala-&gamma;-D-Glu-L-Lys-D-Ala-D-Ala |CITS: 
                     [22978571]|.
                     Single <i>dacD</i> insertion mutants grow normally under 
                     typical laboratory condiition as do <i>&Delta;dacA 
                     dacD::</i>Cm, <i>&Delta;dacA &Delta;dacC dacD::</i>Cm and 
                     <i>&Delta;dacA &Delta;dacB &Delta;dacC dacD::</i>Cm strains
                     |CITS: [8955390]| (see also |CITS: [10383966]|). Genetic 
                     interaction implicates <i>dacD</i> in the maintenance of 
                     normal morphology |CITS: [11325933][15576782]|. 
                     Overexpression of DacD in early exponential growth leads to
                     cell lysis |CITS: [11325933]|. PBP5/DacD hybrid proteins, 
                     in which the C-terminal membrane anchor of PBP5 is replaced
                     by the homologous membrane anchor of PBP6, bind to the 
                     membrane and like PBP5, can complement the morphological 
                     defects of a strain lacking seven PBPs (PBPs 4, 5, 6, and 
                     7, DacD, AmpC and AmpH) |CITS: [12057958]|.
                     PBP6b has strong DD-carboxypeptidase activity at pH 5.0; 
                     <i>dacD</i> transcription and translation increase at pH 
                     5.0; purified PBP6b binds a penicillin derivative faster at
                     pH 5.0 than at pH 7.5 and has increased DD-carboxypeptidase
                     activity against pentapeptide-rich peptidoglycan at pH 5.0;
                     this higher activity is due to both enhanced protein 
                     stability and enhanced substrate binding at acidic pH 
                     |CITS: [27329754]|. At pH 5.0, active PB6b is required to 
                     produce cells with normal morphology |CITS: [27329754]|,
                     <i>dacD</i> is implicated in the productive biogenesis of 
                     the GOB-18 metallo-&beta;-lactamase (<i>Elizabethkingia 
                     meningoseptica pre-apo-gob-18</i> expressed in trans in 
                     <i>E. coli</i>); &Delta;<i>dacD</i> mutants show increased 
                     ability to develop biofilm |CITS: [24145538]|.
                     Related reviews: |CITS: [18539032][22126997]|"
