     gene            complement(2079185..2080543)
                     /gene="plaP"
                     /locus_tag="b2014"
                     /label=plaP
     CDS             complement(2079185..2080543)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="plaP"
                     /locus_tag="b2014"
                     /product="putrescine:H(+) symporter PlaP"
                     /label=plaP
                     /note="PlaP is a low-affinity putrescine importer |CITS: 
                     [21266585]|. PlaP is a member of the APC (amino 
                     acid/polyamine/organocation) superfamily and functions as a
                     putrescine:proton symporter |CITS: [21266585]|. PlaP is 
                     required for the induction of type-I pili driven motility 
                     induced by putrescine as a signaling molecule |CITS: 
                     [21266585]| (see also |CITS: [40178519]|).
                     Expression of <I>plaP</I> decreased in response to 
                     treatment with acetate |CITS:[11244055]| and sodium 
                     salicylate |CITS:[11395452]|. CRP was identified as a 
                     repressor for <I>plaP</I> expression using run-off 
                     transcription/microarray analysis |CITS:[15520470]|. The 
                     binding site of CRP overlaps the binding site of RNA 
                     polymerase |CITS:[15520470]|.
                     <I>plaP</I> has also shown to be repressed under anaerobic 
                     conditions |CITS:[15659690]|.
                     PlaP and |FRAME: B1296-MONOMER PuuP| are receptors for the 
                     group 5 CDI ionophore toxins |CITS: [39591464]|.
                     plaP: <U>p</U>utrescine <U>l</U>ow <U>a</U>ffinity 
                     <U>p</U>ermease"
