                     YeeY"
                     /label=yeeY
                     /note="YeeY, which contains a helix-turn-helix motif to
                     bind DNA in its N-terminal domain, appears to belong to the
                     LysR family of transcription factors, and it was predicted 
                     to regulate genes related to metabolism and toxin-antitoxin
                     systems |CITS: [35880217]|. Upstream of the <i>yeeY</i> 
                     gene, a sequence was found that could work as a 
                     transcriptional promoter, and the transcription of the 
                     <i>yeeY</i> gene is affected by conditions that lead to 
                     biofilm formation |CITS: [35880217]|."
