                     /product="his operon leader peptide"
                     /label=hisL
                     /note="The HisL leader peptide controls by attenuation the 
                     transcription of the <i>hisLGDCBHAFI</i> operon (which 
                     encodes the enzymes of the histidine biosynthesis pathway).
                      HisL contains seven histidine residues as its attenuation 
                     regulatory points within a 16 amino acid long peptide 
                     |CITS: [360216][4582195]|. Moreover, the <i>hisL</i> and 
                     the tRNA<sup>His</sup> sequences have been detected to be 
                     homologs, implying that both can interact with or be the 
                     target of the same regulatory effects |CITS: [6351055]|, 
                     which may have important effects in the operon expression.
                     Reviews: |CITS: [40210524]|"
