                     /note="N-(5'-phospho-L-ribosyl-formimino)-5-amino-1-(5'-ph 
                     osphoribosyl)-4-imidazolecarboxamide isomerase (HisA) 
                     carries out the fourth step in histidine biosynthesis. HisA
                     catalyzes an internal redox reaction known as an Amadori 
                     rearrangement |CITS: [12356303]|.
                     Spontaneous <i>hisA</i> mutants were investigated |CITS: 
                     [2270088]|."
