     CDS             complement(2090802..2091782)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="wzzB"
                     /locus_tag="b2027"
                     /product="O-antigen co-polymerase"
                     /label=wzzB
                     /note="<i>wzzB</i> encodes the O-antigen co-polymerase
                     (also called the O-antigen chain length regulator) of a 
                     Wzx/Wzy-dependent pathway of O-antigen synthesis; Wzz 
                     family proteins are required to regulate the length 
                     distribution of lipid-linked polysaccharides during 
                     polymerization at the periplasmic face of the inner 
                     membrane (see |CITS: [32424042][31778182]|). WzzB is a 
                     group 1a polysaccharide co-polymerase (PCP1a); E. coli K-12
                     also contains a group 1b PCP - |FRAME: EG11295-MONOMER 
                     WzzE| - which regulates the length of enterobacterial 
                     common antigen (see |CITS: [19058968]|). <i>E. coli</i> 
                     K-12 is phenotypically rough and does not express O-antigen
                     due to mutations in the <i>rfb</i> region; an engineered 
                     strain of <i>E. coli</i> K-12 with all <i>rfb</i> genes 
                     intact synthesizes |FRAME: CPD0-2249 O16 antigen| |CITS: 
                     [7517391][7512872][7517390]|. Early studies identified 
                     <i>wzz</i> genes (formerly <i>rol</i> for ""regulator of O 
                     length"" or <i>cld</i> for ""chain length determinant"") in
                     O-antigen producing <i>E. coli</i> strains |CITS: 
                     [1715860][1379582][7682279]|. In K-12 strains engineered to
                     produced O specific polysaccharide WzzB functions together 
                     with the corresponding  |FRAME: RFBX-MONOMER Wzx family 
                     flippase| and |FRAME: EG11982-MONOMER Wzy family 
                     polymerase| for translocation and synthesis of lipid-linked
                     O16 antigen (see |CITS: [15583162][16816184]|).
                     WzzB appears to be present as a dimer in the membrane 
                     |CITS: [16079137]|. In the cryo-electron microscopy 
                     structure reported by |CITS: [33446644]| purified WzzB 
                     forms a bell-shaped octameric complex consisting of a large
                     periplasmic domain and 8 transmembrane domains encircling a
                     transmembrane chamber.
                     For information on bacterial polysaccharide gene 
                     nomenclature see |CITS: [9004408]|."
