                     /label=wbbJ
                     /note="<i>wbbJ</i> is predicted to encode an 
                     <i>O</i>-acetyltransferase involved in the biosynthesis of 
                     O-antigen repeat units (see |CITS: [37792901]|). <i>E. 
                     coli</i> K-12 is phenotypically rough and does not express 
                     O-antigen due to mutations in the <i>rfb</i> region; <i>E. 
                     coli</i> K-12 MG1655 contains the <i>rfb-50</i> mutation - 
                     an IS5 element which disrupts |FRAME: EG11986 <i>wbbL</i>| 
                     encoding rhamnose transferase; an engineered strain of 
                     <i>E. coli</i> K-12 with all <i>rfb</i> genes intact 
                     synthesizes |FRAME: CPD0-2249 O16 antigen| |CITS: 
                     [7517391][7512872][7517390]|.
                     For information on bacterial polysaccharide gene 
                     nomenclature see |CITS: [9004408]|."
