     gene            complement(2099541..2100707)
                     /gene="wbbH"
                     /locus_tag="b2035"
                     /label=wbbH
     CDS             complement(2099541..2100707)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="wbbH"
                     /locus_tag="b2035"
                     /product="O-antigen polymerase"
                     /label=wbbH
                     /note="<i>wzyB</i> (also called <i>wbbH</i>) encodes the 
                     O-antigen polymerase of a Wzx/Wzy-dependent pathway of 
                     O-antigen synthesis; Wzy family polymerases are integral 
                     membrane proteins that transfer growing lipid-linked 
                     O-polysaccharides onto the non-reducing end of a newly 
                     flipped Und-PP-linked repeat unit (see |CITS: 
                     [32424042][31778182]|).
                     <i>E. coli</i> K-12 is phenotypically rough and does not 
                     express O-antigen due to mutations in the <i>rfb</i> 
                     region; <i>E. coli</i> K-12 MG1655 contains the 
                     <i>rfb-50</i> mutation - an IS5 element which disrupts 
                     |FRAME: EG11986 <i>wbbL</i>| encoding rhamnose transferase;
                     an engineered strain of <i>E. coli</i> K-12 with all 
                     <i>rfb</i> genes intact synthesizes |FRAME: CPD0-2249 O16 
                     antigen| |CITS: [7517391][7512872][7517390]|. In K-12 
                     strains engineered to produced O specific polysaccharide 
                     WzyB functions together with the |FRAME: RFBX-MONOMER Wzx 
                     family flippase| and the Wzz family |FRAME: G7090-MONOMER| 
                     for translocation and synthesis of lipid-linked O16 antigen
                     (see |CITS: [16816184]|).
                     For information on bacterial polysaccharide gene 
                     nomenclature see |CITS: [9004408]|."
