     gene            complement(2104558..2105457)
                     /gene="rfbD"
                     /locus_tag="b2040"
                     /label=rfbD
     CDS             complement(2104558..2105457)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rfbD"
                     /locus_tag="b2040"
                     /product="dTDP-4-dehydrorhamnose reductase"
                     /EC_number="1.1.1.133"
                     /label=rfbD
                     /note="dTDP-4-dehydrorhamnose reductase (RfbD) is the
                     final enzyme of the |FRAME: DTDPRHAMSYN-PWY| pathway, which
                     synthesizes one of the precursors for the O antigen of 
                     lipopolysaccharide.  RfbD catalyzes the stereospecific 
                     reduction of the 4-keto group of 
                     dTDP-4-dehydro-6-deoxy-L-mannose to generate the final 
                     product, dTDP-L-rhamnose.  The <i>E. coli</i> enzyme has 
                     not been biochemically characterized.
                     <i>E. coli</i> K-12 strains carry mutations in the 
                     <i>rfb</i> gene cluster and do not produce O antigen.  In 
                     MG1655, the <i>rfb-50</i> allele, an IS<i>5</i> insertion, 
                     interrupts the <i>wbbL</i> gene, which would encode the 
                     dTDP-rhamnose transferase |CITS: 
                     [7512872][7517390][7517391]|.
                     Deletion of <i>rfbD</i> enables increased production of 
                     quercetin 3-<i>O</i>-(6-deoxytalose) in an engineered <i>E.
                     coli</i> strain |CITS: [22492444]|. dTDP-4-dehydrorhamnose 
                     reductase has primarily been investigated in <i>Salmonella 
                     enterica</i>.  The enzyme was purified and crystal 
                     structures have been obtained.  A reaction mechanism was 
                     proposed, and predicted catalytic residues were tested by 
                     site-directed mutagenesis |CITS: 
                     [10455186][10666586][12057193]|.
                     For information on bacterial polysaccharide gene 
                     nomenclature see |CITS: [9004408]|.
                     Review: |CITS: [11114506]|"
