     gene            complement(2105457..2106542)
                     /gene="rfbB"
                     /locus_tag="b2041"
                     /label=rfbB
     CDS             complement(2105457..2106542)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rfbB"
                     /locus_tag="b2041"
                     /product="bifunctional dTDP-glucose 4,6-dehydratase 1 / 
                     dTDP-glucose 4,6-dehydratase"
                     /EC_number="4.2.1.46"
                     /label=rfbB
                     /note="dTDP-glucose 4,6-dehydratase (RfbB) is involved in
                     the dTDP-rhamnose biosynthesis pathway, which is important 
                     for the synthesis of O-specific LPS. This enzyme catalyzes 
                     the conversion of dTDP-&alpha;-D-glucose into 
                     dTDP-4-keto-6-deoxyglucose. This reaction occurs in three 
                     steps: dehydrogenation, dehydration, and rereduction. The 
                     coenzyme NAD<sup>+</sup> mediates the dehydrogenation and 
                     rereduction steps of the reaction |CITS: [11601973]|. The 
                     reduction of enzyme-bound NAD<sup>+</sup> to NADH results 
                     in a conformational change in the protein such that the 
                     substrate cannot be released at a significant rate from 
                     this form of the enzyme, thus the intermediates in the 
                     normal catalytic process remain tightly bound to the enzyme
                     |CITS: [GlaserMethEnzXXVIII,446]|.
                     The genes encoding the enzymes involved in the biosynthesis
                     of O-specific polysaccharides are clustered in the 
                     <i>rfb</i> region. <i>E. coli</i> K-12 does not normally 
                     express O-specific LPS due to mutations in the <i>rfb</i> 
                     region. However, genes in the <i>rfb</i> cluster have been 
                     identified. |CITS: [7517391]| dTDP-glucose 4,6-dehydratase 
                     is encoded by the <i>rfbB</i> gene which is paralogous to 
                     <i>rffG</i> |CITS: [7517390]|. The product of <i>rffG</i> 
                     is another dTDP-glucose 4,6-dehydratase which catalyzes the
                     same reaction as RfbB, but functions in the enterobacterial
                     common antigen (ECA) pathway |CITS: [7559340][7517391]|.
                     RfbB in <i>E. coli</i> B has been crystallized |CITS: 
                     [4307450]|. The crystal structure in <i>Salmonella 
                     enterica</i> has been resolved to 2.8 &Aring; resolution 
                     |CITS: [10666612]|.
                     For information on bacterial polysaccharide gene 
                     nomenclature see |CITS: [9004408]|."
