                     /note="<i>wcaM</i> is located in a cluster of genes that
                     are responsible for production of the extracellular 
                     polysaccharide, |FRAME: CPD-21504 ""colanic acid""| (CA); 
                     an insertion mutation in <i>wcaM</i> ('orf20') does not 
                     affect the mucoid phenotype of a CA-producing strain of 
                     <i>E. coli</i> K-12 (|CITS: [8759852]| and later |CITS: 
                     [34159784]|). The <i>Salmonella enterica </i> LT2 homolog 
                     has been implicated in biofilm formation |CITS: 
                     [15838049]|.
                     Nomenclature for genes involved in bacterial polysaccharide
                     synthesis is discussed in |CITS: [9004408]| "
