                     polysaccharide, |FRAME: CPD-21504 colanic acid| (CA or M 
                     antigen) |CITS: [8759852]|. <i>wzxC</i> encodes a predicted
                     integral membrane protein which may be involved in export 
                     of the lipid-linked CA repeat unit |CITS: [8759852]|. The 
                     &Delta;<i>wzxC</i> mutant of an <i>rcsA</i> overexpressing,
                     CA producing strain of <i>E. coli</i> K-12 MG1655 grows as 
                     misshapen rods and spheres and accumulates the pyruvylated 
                     hexasaccharide |FRAME: CPD-21522 repeat unit of CA| |CITS: 
                     [34159784]|.
                     WzxC single amino acid substitution mutants which have lost
                     substrate specificity and are able to transport lipid II 
                     and O-antigen precursors in addition to CA precursors have 
                     been isolated; the changes map to regions of the protein 
                     located near the periplasmic face of the membrane and may 
                     exert their effect through destabilizing the inward-open 
                     conformation of the transporter |CITS: [29907971]|. WzxC 
                     may mediate the translocation of lipid III in the absence 
                     of functional |FRAME: EG11486-MONOMER WzxE| |CITS: 
                     [16199561]| (and see |CITS: [40207904]|). WzxC is a member 
                     of the Polysaccharide Transporter (PST) family within the 
                     MultiDrug/Oligosaccharidyl-lipid/Polysaccharide (MOP) 
                     Flippase Superfamily |CITS: [9274022][26546518]|. 
                     Nomenclature for genes involved in bacterial polysaccharide
                     synthesis is discussed in |CITS: [9004408]|"
