     gene            complement(2118004..2119227)
                     /gene="wcaI"
                     /locus_tag="b2050"
                     /label=wcaI
     CDS             complement(2118004..2119227)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="wcaI"
                     /locus_tag="b2050"
                     /product="bifunctional colanic acid biosynthesis
                     fucosyltransferase WcaI / GDP-Fuc:alpha-D-Glc-PP-Und 
                     alpha-(1,3)-fucosyltransferase"
                     /label=wcaI
                     /note="WcaI is the fucosyltransferase that catalyzes the 
                     transfer of unmodified fucose to |FRAME: CPD-12773 UPP-Glc|
                     in the biosynthesis of the extracellular polysaccharide 
                     |FRAME: CPD-21504 colanic acid| (CA) |CITS: [30821147]|.
                     <i>wcaI</i> is located within a cluster of genes that are 
                     responsible for production of CA; <i>wcaI</i> was predicted
                     to encode a glycosyl transferase involved in the process 
                     |CITS: [8759852]|.
                     Expression of <i>wcaI</i> is higher in wild-type biofilms 
                     than in biofilms formed by an <i>rpoS</i> mutant |CITS: 
                     [17979199]|.
                     The Keio collection <i>wcaI</i> mutant is sensitive to 
                     lithium (<90% growth at 200mM Li) |CITS: [39983623]|. 
                     Nomenclature for genes involved in bacterial polysaccharide
                     synthesis is discussed in |CITS: [9004408]|."
