     gene            complement(2119224..2119703)
                     /gene="gmm"
                     /locus_tag="b2051"
                     /label=gmm
     CDS             complement(2119224..2119703)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="gmm"
                     /locus_tag="b2051"
                     /product="bifunctional GDP-mannose mannosyl hydrolase /
                     GDP-glucose glucosyl hydrolase"
                     /EC_number="3.2.1.42"
                     /label=gmm
                     /note="GDP-mannose mannosyl hydrolase (GDPMH) is able to 
                     hydrolyze both GDP-mannose and GDP-glucose.
                     Its biological role is as yet unknown, though it may 
                     participate in the regulation of cell wall biosynthesis by 
                     influencing the cell concentration of GDP-mannose or 
                     GDP-glucose |CITS: [7592609]|.
                     The enzyme was first identified as a member of the Nudix 
                     hydrolase family |CITS: [8810257]|.  However,
                     unlike other Nudix hydrolases, GDPMH catalyzes the 
                     nucleophilic substitution at C1' rather than
                     phosphorus |CITS: [10913267]| and requires one divalent 
                     cation per active site to facilitate the departure of
                     GMP |CITS: [11926828]|.  The divalent cation binding site, 
                     the general base catalyst, and other residues
                     important for catalytic activity were identified by 
                     site-directed mutagenesis |CITS: [12196023][16981689]|. 
                     Crystal structures of GDPMH have been solved, and a 
                     reaction mechanism with a four-stage catalytic
                     cycle was suggested |CITS: [15274914][16981689]|.
                     Review: |CITS: [16378245]|"
