                     /label=wcaE
                     /note="<i>wcaE</i> is located within a cluster of genes
                     that are responsible for production of |FRAME: CPD-21504 
                     ""colanic acid""| (CA); <i>wcaE</i> was predicted to encode
                     a glycosyltransferase involved in CA biosynthesis |CITS: 
                     [8759852]|.
                     WcaE was later shown to be a fucosyltransferase that 
                     catalyzes transfer of a fucosyl residue to the UPP-linked 
                     acetylated disaccharide during biosynthesis of the 
                     extracellular polysaccharide |FRAME: CPD-21504 ""colanic 
                     acid""| |CITS: [30821147]|. The Keio collection <i>wcaE</i>
                     mutant is sensitive to lithium (<90% growth at 100mM Li) 
                     |CITS: [39983623]|.
                     Nomenclature for genes involved in bacterial polysaccharide
                     synthesis is discussed in |CITS: [9004408]|."
