     CDS             complement(2123142..2124359)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="wcaD"
                     /locus_tag="b2056"
                     /product="colanic acid polymerase"
                     /label=wcaD
                     /note="<i>wcaD</i> is located within a cluster of genes
                     that are responsible for production of the extracellular 
                     polysaccharide, |FRAME: CPD-21504 ""colanic acid""| (CA); 
                     WcaD is predicted to be an integral inner membrane protein 
                     and it may have a role in polymerising the CA 
                     hexasaccharide unit |CITS: [8759852]|.
                     A &Delta;<i>wcaD</i> mutant of an <i>rcsA</i> 
                     overexpressing, CA producing strain of <i>E. coli</i> K-12 
                     MG1655 grows as misshapen rods and spheres and accumulates 
                     the pyruvylated hexasaccharide |FRAME: CPD-21522 repeat 
                     unit of CA|; further deletion of |FRAME: EG11424 
                     <i>waaL</i>|, encoding O-antigen ligase, in this strain 
                     results in extensive cell lysis |CITS: [34159784]|. The 
                     Keio collection <i>wcaD</i> mutant is sensitive to lithium 
                     (<90% growth at 200mM Li) |CITS: [39983623]|."
