     gene            complement(2129136..2129579)
                     /gene="wzb"
                     /locus_tag="b2061"
                     /label=wzb
     CDS             complement(2129136..2129579)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="wzb"
                     /locus_tag="b2061"
                     /product="protein-tyrosine phosphatase"
                     /EC_number="3.1.3.48"
                     /label=wzb
                     /note="Wzb is a protein-tyrosine phosphatase with activity 
                     towards autophosphorylated |FRAME: G7105-MONOMER ""Wzc""| 
                     protein |CITS: [10348860]|.  Autophosphorylation of Wzc 
                     negatively regulates colanic acid biosynthesis, and Wzb 
                     activity counteracts this negative regulation |CITS: 
                     [11090276]|.
                     Wzb acts on the phosphorylated tyrosine residues of the 
                     C-terminal tyrosine cluster in Wzc, but has little 
                     phosphatase activity toward the phosphorylated Y568 residue
                     in Wzc |CITS: [12851388]|.  Wzb also does not exhibit 
                     significant phosphatase activity toward UDP-glucose 
                     dehydrogenase, a substrate of the Wzc kinase |CITS: 
                     [12851388]|.  The majority of the binding energy for the 
                     interaction between Wzb and the catalytic domain of Wzc 
                     appears to be provided by a region distinct from the 
                     phosphorylated C-tail of Wzc, instead overlapping with a 
                     region that plays a role in Wzc oligomerization and 
                     trans-phosphorylation |CITS: [23543749]|.
                     Analysis of site-directed mutants indicate that the C9 
                     residue is required for Wzb activity, the Y115 residue 
                     within the D-loop of Wzb is involved in the phosphatase 
                     activity, while L40 may play a secondary role in 
                     interacting with the phospho-tyrosine substrate |CITS: 
                     [23543749]|.
                     A solution structure of Wzb revealed differences in the 
                     active site P-loop between Wzb and eukaryotic low molecular
                     weight protein-tyrosine phosphatases, perhaps indicating a 
                     different mechanism for substrate recognition |CITS: 
                     [16651264]|.  A crystal structure of the Wzb protein from 
                     the O9a:K30 strain has been solved |CITS: [19616007]|.
                     In some <i>E. coli</i> strains, including O9a:K30, the 
                     <i>wzb</i> gene is found in a cluster involved in the 
                     biosynthesis of the capsule |CITS: 
                     [10094716][10200954][11053445][12426330]|.  Expression of 
                     <i>E. coli</i> K-12 <i>wzb</i> can complement the capsular 
                     polysaccharide biosynthesis defect of a <i>wzb</i> mutant 
                     in O9a:K30 |CITS: [16030241]|.
                     Expression of <i>wzb</i> is induced by the quorum signal 
                     AI-2 |CITS: [11514505]|.
                     Review: |CITS: [16756484]|"
