     CDS             complement(2133240..2135093)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="asmA"
                     /locus_tag="b2064"
                     /product="putative assembly protein AsmA"
                     /label=asmA
                     /note="AsmA is involved in the assembly of outer membrane 
                     proteins, possibly by affecting outer membrane structure. 
                     Null mutations of <i>asmA</i> suppress the assembly defects
                     of mutant OmpF and OmpC outer membrane proteins |CITS: 
                     [7476172][8576061]|. The OmpF assembly step that is 
                     affected by this suppression occurs in the outer membrane 
                     |CITS: [8866482]|. LPS levels in the outer membrane are 
                     lowered in <i>asmA</i> null mutants |CITS: [8866482]|. AsmA
                     is predicted to be a bitopic inner membrane protein |CITS: 
                     [27510400]|
                     <i>asmA</i> null mutations do not affect the assembly of 
                     wild-type OmpF |CITS: [7476172]|.
                     An <i>asmA</i> nonsense mutation contributes to colistin 
                     resistance in a laboratory evolved strain |CITS: 
                     [35680894]|."
