     CDS             complement(2135788..2136429)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="udk"
                     /locus_tag="b2066"
                     /product="trifunctional uridine/cytidine kinase / uridine
                     kinase / cytidine kinase"
                     /EC_number="2.7.1.48"
                     /label=udk
                     /note="Uridine-cytidine kinase phosphorylates both uridine
                     and cytidine; GTP and dGTP are the most efficient phosphate
                     donors |CITS: [211379]|.
                     Uridine-cytidine kinase was found to have a molecular 
                     weight of 90,000 by gel filtration and is thus likely not 
                     monomeric |CITS: [211379]|.
                     Overexpression of uridine-cytidine kinase inhibits growth 
                     of the bacteriophage T7, particularly in a T7 gp0.7 mutant 
                     |CITS: [17135349]|, due to inadequate inhibition of host 
                     RNA polymerase |CITS: [18067538]|.  Overexpression of Udk 
                     mimics the absence of Gp2 during T7 infection |CITS: 
                     [23242801]|."
