     gene            2146792..2146935
                     /gene="sibA"
                     /locus_tag="b4436"
                     /label=sibA
     misc_RNA        2146792..2146935
                     /gene="sibA"
                     /locus_tag="b4436"
                     /product="small RNA SibA"
                     /note="The SibA small RNA was first detected during a 
                     comparative genomics screen for sequence conservation 
                     |CITS: [11445539]|.  The <i>yegL-yegM</i> intergenic region
                     was initially shown to contain two copies of a repeat 
                     sequence element (initially termed QUAD1 and later renamed 
                     SIB) that occurs five times in the <i>E. coli</i> K-12 
                     genome |CITS: [10673004][18710431]|.  Many sequence regions
                     conserved between the SIB elements are predicted to form 
                     stem-loop structures |CITS: [18710431]|.
                     Two RNA products arising from <i>sibA</i> have been 
                     detected |CITS: [11445539][18710431]|; the shorter RNA 
                     product may be derived by processing of the longer 
                     transcript |CITS: [18710431]|.  A small open reading frame,
                     <i>ibsA</i>, is encoded on the opposite strand; the Ibs-Sib
                     pairs may be toxin-antitoxin systems |CITS: [18710431]|.
                     SibA interacts with the protein |FRAME: EG12866-MONOMER| 
                     |CITS: [36328526]|.
                     SibA is expressed at varying levels throughout growth in 
                     both rich and minimal medium |CITS: [11445539][18710431]|. 
                     Neither deletion nor overexpression of <i>sibA</i> has a 
                     detectable effect on cell growth |CITS: [18710431]|.
                     Ryx: ""RNA of unknown function at X position (10 minute) in
                     the genome"" |CITS: [11445539]|
                     SibA: ""<b>s</b>hort, <b>i</b>ntergenic, a<b>b</b>undant 
                     sequence"" |CITS: [18710431]|
                     Reviews: |CITS: [12762038][12654996][32213244]|"
