     gene            2148744..2151866
                     /gene="mdtB"
                     /locus_tag="b2075"
                     /label=mdtB
     CDS             2148744..2151866
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="mdtB"
                     /locus_tag="b2075"
                     /product="multifunctional multidrug efflux pump RND
                     permease subunit MdtB / multidrug efflux pump MdtABC-TolC /
                     novobiocin efflux pump / deoxycholate efflux pump / SDS 
                     efflux pump"
                     /label=mdtB
                     /note="MdtBC is the resistance-nodulation-division (RND)
                     family permease of a tripartite efflux pump that is 
                     implicated in resistance to antibiotics, bile salt 
                     derivatives and SDS.
                     MdtB contains 6 predicted transmembrane domains |CITS: 
                     [12107133]|. MdtB and MdtC comprise a heteromultimeric 
                     transmembrane complex; the purified active complex contains
                     MdtB and MdtC in a 2:1 ratio |CITS: [20038594]|. 
                     <i>mdtB</i> is one of 35 efflux-encoding genes that have 
                     been deleted or inactivated in 'Efflux KnockOut-35' 
                     (EKO-35) -  a K-12 BW25133-derived strain that lacks 35 
                     efflux pumps and can be used as a platform to study their 
                     function |CITS: [36065018][36318669]|. The <i>mdtB</i> Keio
                     collection mutant (BW25113 &Delta;<i>mdtB::kan</i>) shows a
                     significant increase in swimming motility |CITS: 
                     [39529380]|."
