     gene            2154945..2156360
                     /gene="mdtD"
                     /locus_tag="b2077"
                     /label=mdtD
     CDS             2154945..2156360
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="mdtD"
                     /locus_tag="b2077"
                     /product="putative multidrug efflux pump MdtD"
                     /label=mdtD
                     /note="In the Transporter Classification Database, MdtD is
                     a member of the Drug:H<sup>+</sup> Antiporter-2 (DHA2) 
                     family within the major facilitator superfamily (MFS) 
                     |CITS: [26546518]|.
                     Overexpression of cloned <I>mdtD</I> in a K-12 strain which
                     lacks the major efflux pump permease AcrB (<i>E. coli</i> 
                     KAM3; see |CITS: [12618449]|) does not impact resistance to
                     a range of toxic compounds (dyes, detergents, antibiotics 
                     and others) compared to the mutant parent 
                     |CITS:[11566977]|.
                     Intracellular arabinose concentration (measured indirectly 
                     though <i>araBAD</i> promoter activity) is increased in a 
                     &Delta;<i>mdtD</i> strain compared to wild type; 
                     overexpression of <i>mdtD</i> does not affect intracellular
                     arabinose levels |CITS: [22952739]|. Accumulation of the 
                     cationic fluorescent dyes 3,3'-dipropylthiadicarbocyanine 
                     iodide (diS-C3) and SYBR Green is greater in <i>mdtD</i> 
                     knockout cells compared to wild type |CITS: [31438868]|.
                     <i>mdtABCD</i> and <i>baeSR</i> form an operon; 
                     overexpression of BaeR increases transcription of <i>mdtA, 
                     mdtB, mdtC</i> and <i>mdtD</i> and confers a drug resistant
                     phenotype against bile salt derivatives, sodium dodecyl 
                     sulfate and novobiocin; BaeR induced drug-resistance is 
                     dependent on |FRAME: TRANS-CPLX-202 ""MdtABC""|; disruption
                     of <i>mdtD</i> does not affect the BaeR induced drug 
                     resistance phenotype |CITS: [12107134][12107133]|.
                     <i>mdtD</i> is one of 35 efflux-encoding genes that have 
                     been deleted or inactivated in 'Efflux KnockOut-35' 
                     (EKO-35) -  a K-12 BW25133-derived strain that lacks 35 
                     efflux pumps and can be used as a platform to study their 
                     function |CITS: [36065018][36318669]|.
                     "
