     gene            2160595..2160681
                     /gene="cyaR"
                     /locus_tag="b4438"
                     /label=cyaR
     misc_RNA        2160595..2160681
                     /gene="cyaR"
                     /locus_tag="b4438"
                     /product="small regulatory RNA CyaR"
                     /note="CyaR is a small RNA that promotes degradation of
                     the <i>ompX</i> |CITS: [18619465][18978044]|, <i>yqaE</i>, 
                     <i>nadE</i>, <i>luxS</i> |CITS: [18978044]| and <i>rpoS</i>
                     |CITS: [31552789]| mRNAs.  Additional targets of CyaR have 
                     been identified by comparative genomics |CITS: [23980183]| 
                     and by an affinity purification method |CITS: [29294085]|. 
                     A candidate CyaR regulon was inferred by integrating 
                     information on experimentally supported targets and 
                     sRNA-mRNA interactions with transcription datasets |CITS: 
                     [32487739]|.  Regulation depends on the presence of Hfq 
                     |CITS: [18619465]|.  Hfq and CyaR interact |CITS: 
                     [11445539][36328526]|, and Hfq may stabilize CyaR |CITS: 
                     [18619465]|.  CyaR also impacts the function of RyhB by 
                     competing for Hfq |CITS: [34210798]|.
                     In an <i>hfq</i> mutant, significantly less CyaR 
                     accumulates than in wild type |CITS: [22040174]|; CyaR is 
                     also more unstable in a |FRAME: EG10743 <i>pnp</i>| mutant 
                     |CITS: [21527671][36409892]|.  |FRAME: EG10743-MONOMER 
                     PNPase| and |FRAME: EG10863-MONOMER| together stabilize 
                     CyaR during exponential growth; during stationary phase, 
                     CyaR is relatively stable independent of PNPase or RNase PH
                     |CITS: [27698082]|.  In the absence of PNPase, the RNase E,
                     through its AR2 region, degrades CyaR bound to Hfq, and 
                     most probably at the same time the targets of CyaR are 
                     degraded by the RNase |CITS: [36409892]|.
                     The processed form of the |FRAME: SRAH-RNA| downregulates 
                     CyaR levels by base-pairing and mediating its RNase 
                     E-dependent degradation |CITS: [31552789]| or by acting as 
                     a ""sponge"" |CITS: [32356726]|.
                     CyaR expression is increased by cAMP-CRP and subject to 
                     catabolite repression |CITS: [18619465][18978044]| and is 
                     regulated by the CpxAR two-component system |CITS: 
                     [25246476]|.  CyaR is expressed at higher levels when cells
                     are grown in pyruvate compared to glucose |CITS: 
                     [31363904]|.  |CITS: [18619465]| observed that CyaR 
                     expression was upregulated by the alternative sigma factor 
                     of the envelope stress response, &sigma;<sup>E</sup>; 
                     however, this regulatory effect was not observed by |CITS: 
                     [25030700]|.
                     Overexpression of CyaR decreases curli expression |CITS: 
                     [26469694]|.
                     Ryx: ""RNA of unknown function at X position (10 minute) in
                     the genome"" |CITS: [11445539]|
                     CyaR: ""<b>cy</b>clic AMP-<b>a</b>ctivated <b>R</b>NA"" 
                     |CITS: [18619465]|
                     Reviews: |CITS: [12762038][12654996][19366629][20068355][2 
                     1843668][29992897][32213244]|"
