     gene            2179396..2180220
                     /gene="rcnA"
                     /locus_tag="b2106"
                     /label=rcnA
     CDS             2179396..2180220
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rcnA"
                     /locus_tag="b2106"
                     /product="trifunctional Ni(2+)/Co(2+) exporter / Co(2+)
                     exporter / Ni(2+) exporter"
                     /label=rcnA
                     /note="RcnA is an inner membrane efflux system for nickel
                     and cobalt ions. Under aerobic growth conditions deletion 
                     of <i>rcnA</i> results in decreased resistance to nickel 
                     and cobalt and increased intracellular accumulation of 
                     Ni<sup>2+</sup> can be directly demonstrated |CITS: 
                     [15805538], [17120142]|. <i>rcnA</i> expressed in 
                     <i>trans</i> in a strain lacking chromosomal <i>rcnA</i> 
                     results in increased resistance to Ni<sup>2+</sup> and 
                     Co<sup>2+</sup> compared to wild type |CITS: [15805538]|. 
                     RcnA is involved in Ni<sup>2+</sup> homeostasis under 
                     anaerobic conditions and at low nickel concentrations (10nM
                     Ni<sup>2+</sup>). Under these conditions deletion of 
                     <i>rcnA</i> results in reduced nickel accumulation and 
                     decreased |FRAME: HYDROG3-CPLX| activity. Deletion of 
                     <i>rcnA</i> results in increased |FRAME: EG11519-MONOMER 
                     ""NikR""| activity which impacts nickel import via the high
                     affinity |FRAME: ABC-20-CPLX| |CITS: [16956381]|. RcnA 
                     contains 6 predicted transmembrane regions and a histidine 
                     rich domain in the center of the protein that may be 
                     associated with nickel binding |CITS: [15805538]| Exposure 
                     of <i>rcnA</i> mutants to subinhibitory concentrations of 
                     nickel promotes the formation of biofilm structure |CITS: 
                     [19168650]|.
                     <i>rcnA</i> expression is regulated by the |FRAME: 
                     G7137-MONOMER ""RcnR transcritional repressor""| 
                     |CITS:[16956381], [17120142], [21040754]|.<BR><i>rcnA</i> 
                     forms an operon with |FRAME: G7139-MONOMER ""<i>rcnB</i>""|
                     |CITS: [21665978]|.
                     RcnA is a member of the Nickel-Cobalt (NicO) family of 
                     transporters |CITS: [24225317]|."
