     gene            2180439..2180777
                     /gene="rcnB"
                     /locus_tag="b2107"
                     /label=rcnB
     CDS             2180439..2180777
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rcnB"
                     /locus_tag="b2107"
                     /product="periplasmic protein involved in Ni/Co export"
                     /label=rcnB
                     /note="Deletion of <i>rcnB</i> in the K-12 derived strain
                     W3110, results in increased resistance to nickel and cobalt
                     and <i>&Delta;rcnB</i> mutants show reduced intracellular 
                     levels of nickel and cobalt; a <i>&Delta;rcnB</i> strain 
                     has increased rates of nickel efflux compared to wild type 
                     |CITS: [21665978]|. RcnB may act to regulate RcnA mediated 
                     nickel efflux |CITS: [21665978]|.
                     RcnB is located in the periplasm; purified RcnB does not 
                     bind nickel or cobalt |CITS: [21665978]|. RcnB binds copper
                     <i>in vitro</i> and <i>in vivo</i>; purified RcnB binds one
                     atom of Cu per monomer with micromolar affinity |CITS: 
                     [24658095]|. <i>rcnB</i> is not induced by copper and does 
                     not appear to be involved in copper homeostasis |CITS: 
                     [24658095]|. Disruption of a conserved potential copper 
                     binding motif renders the RcnAB efflux system ineffective 
                     with respect to nickel and cobalt resistance which suggests
                     that copper binding by RcnB is essential for function 
                     |CITS: [24658095]|.
                     <i>rcnB</i> forms an operon with |FRAME: G7138 
                     ""<i>rcnA</i>""| (which encodes a nickel/cobalt efflux 
                     protein); expression is induced by nickel and cobalt via 
                     the RcnR regulator |CITS: [21665978]|. <i>rcnB</i> is 
                     expressed constitutively probably from a promoter located 
                     in the <i>rcnArcnB</i> intergenic region |CITS: 
                     [24658095]|.
                     <i>rcnB</i> expression is upregulated in response to 
                     challenge by three cationic amphipathic antimicrobial 
                     peptides (AMPs) of natural origin. A <i>&Delta;rcnB</i> 
                     strain is more sensitive than wild type to the natural AMPs
                     Magainin 2 and LL-37 |CITS: [24789011]|.
                     In contrast to later results, |CITS: [17120142]| report 
                     that deletion of <i>rcnB</i> in <i>E. coli</i> K-12 W3110 
                     has no effect on cobalt or nickel resistance and expression
                     of an <i>rcnB::lacZ</i> fusion is not altered by cobalt or 
                     nickel.
                     A knockout mutant of this gene was sensitive to boric acid 
                     exposure compared to most other gene knockouts; a 
                     complementation assay restored its intrinsic boric acid 
                     resistance |CITS: [38466471]|."
                     /translation="MTIKNKMLLGALLLVTSAAWAAPATAGSTNTSGISKYELSSFIAD
