                     /locus_tag="b2108"
                     /product="putative fimbrial adhesin YehA"
                     /label=yehA
                     /note="<i>yehDCBA</i> is a putative chaperone-usher
                     fimbrial operon in <i>E.coli K-12</i> |CITS:[20345943]|. 
                     The operon is cryptic under normal laboratory conditions 
                     but when constitutive expression is induced in a strain 
                     that lacks the type 1 fimbrial complex the <i>yeh</i> 
                     operon promotes biofilm formation in minimal media on a 
                     variety of abiotic surfaces |CITS: [20345943]|. Expression 
                     of the <i>yeh</i> operon is regulated by the global 
                     regulators |FRAME: PD00288 ""H-NS""| and |FRAME: CPLX0-226 
                     ""CRP cAMP""| |CITS: [20345943]|.
                     YehA shares a low sequence similarity to members of the 
                     Autotransporter (AT) Family |CITS: [12192075]|.
                     <i>E. coli</i> K-12 contains 12 chaperone-usher fimbrial 
                     operons, including <i>yehDCBA</i>; a fimbria-lacking mutant
                     - strain WQM026 - created by deleting all 12 operons has 
                     been characterised |CITS: [33863704]|.
                     "
