                     /locus_tag="b2115"
                     /product="PF05406 family protein YehF"
                     /label=yehF
                     /note="Expression of <i>yehF</i> appears to be regulated
                     by LexA |CITS: [10760155]|.  A mini-Tn<i>10</i> insertion 
                     mutant in ""<i>molR</i>"" is defective in the reduction of 
                     selenate |CITS: [12480890]|.
                     In <i>E. coli</i> K-12, the <i>yehFGH</i> open reading 
                     frames may in fact represent a single gene that is 
                     interrupted by a frameshift mutation.  However, the size of
                     the <i>yehF</i> mRNA, ~ 1 kb, is consistent with encoding 
                     the ""interrupted"" N-terminal 274 amino acid gene product 
                     of <i>yehF</i> |CITS: [10760155]|.
                     The <i>molR</i> gene has been assigned to this region, 
                     although in the original publication on <i>molR</i> |CITS: 
                     [2156810]|, the gene was mapped between <i>metC</i> and 
                     <i>argG</i> at ~65 min.  A <i>molR</i> mutant is defective 
                     in utilization of molybdate; it is thought to regulate the 
                     synthesis of ModE, a transcription factor regulating the 
                     expression of a molybdate-specific transporter |CITS: 
                     [2156810]|.
                     "
