                     /note="OsmF is the periplasmic binding component of a low 
                     affinity glycine betaine ABC transporter; OsmF binds the 
                     osmoprotectants glycine betaine, choline-<i>0</i>-sulfate 
                     and dimethylsulfopropionate with low (mM) affinities |CITS:
                     [26325238]|.
                     apoYehZ contains a type II periplasmic binding fold 
                     consisting of two domains (A and B) with two connecting 
                     loops |CITS: [26325238]|. Expression of an <i>osmF-phoA</i>
                     fusion is induced by growth in a medium of high osmolarity 
                     |CITS: [2821274]|. An <i>osmFlacZ</i> transcriptional 
                     fusion is induced by both osmotic shock and entry into 
                     stationary phase |CITS: [15251200]|."
