                     /gene="bglX"
                     /locus_tag="b2132"
                     /product="bifunctional putative periplasmic glycoside
                     hydrolase / periplasmic glycoside hydrolase"
                     /EC_number="3.2.1.23"
                     /label=bglX
                     /note="<i>bglX</i> is predicted to encode a periplasmic 
                     &beta;-glucosidase/&beta;-galactosidase; the purified 
                     enzyme can hydrolyse artifical substrates 
                     (<i>o</i>-nitrophenyl-&beta;-D-glucopyranoside, 
                     <i>p</i>-nitrophenyl-&beta;-D-glucopyranoside, and 
                     <i>o</i>-nitrophenyl-&beta;-D-galactopyranoside) with 
                     varying kinetics; it can also hydrolyse lactose (but not 
                     cellobiose, maltose or laminarin) |CITS: 
                     [8757730][37736388]|. No obvious phenotype is associated 
                     with deletion or overexpression |CITS: 
                     [8757730][37736388]|, and the physiological function of the
                     enzyme remains uncertain.
                     In the CAZy database, BglX is a Glycoside Hydrolase Family 
                     3 (GH3) enzyme |CITS: [34850161]|."
