     gene            2224103..2224501
                     /gene="yohJ"
                     /locus_tag="b2141"
                     /label=yohJ
     CDS             2224103..2224501
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yohJ"
                     /locus_tag="b2141"
                     /product="putative 3-hydroxypropanoate export protein
                     YohJ"
                     /label=yohJ
                     /note="<i>yohJ</i> and <i>yohK</i> encode two inner
                     membrane proteins implicated in the export of |FRAME: 
                     3-HYDROXY-PROPIONATE| (3-HP) |CITS: [33149261]|. 
                     <i>yohJK</i> belongs to the |FRAME: EG11733-MONOMER YieP| 
                     regulon; YieP downregulates expression of <i>yohJK</i>; 
                     deletion of <i>yieP</i> improves tolerance to 3-HP in a 
                     number of <i>E. coli</i> strains including K-12 |CITS: 
                     [33149261]|.
                     The growth of an <i>E. coli</i> W &Delta;<i>yohJK</i> 
                     mutant is significantly reduced in the presence of 300mM 
                     3-HP; over-expression of <i>yohJK</i> (in <i>E. coli</i> W)
                     improves tolerance to 3-HP; the intracellular concentration
                     of 3-HP is significantly reduced when <i>yieP</i> is 
                     deleted or when <i>yohJK</i> is overexpressed |CITS: 
                     [33149261]|.
                     YohJ is predicted to be an inner membrane protein with four
                     transmembrane domains; experimental topology analysis 
                     suggests the C-terminus is located in the periplasm |CITS: 
                     [15919996]|."
