                     the FMN-binding subunit |CITS: [34097066]|.
                     Based on sequence similarity, PreA was predicted to be a 
                     dihydrothymine/dihydropyrimidine dehydrogenase |CITS: 
                     [12952533][11574054]|.  PreA has similarity to the 
                     C-terminal half of mammalian dihydropyrimidine 
                     dehydrogenase |CITS: [18482579]|.
                     PreA is required for swarming motility |CITS: [17122336]|. 
                     PreA: |CITS: [21169495]|"
