     gene            complement(2232829..2233827)
                     /gene="mglB"
                     /locus_tag="b2150"
                     /label=mglB
     CDS             complement(2232829..2233827)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="mglB"
                     /locus_tag="b2150"
                     /product="multifunctional D-galactose/methyl-galactoside
                     ABC transporter periplasmic binding protein / D-galactose /
                     methyl-beta-D-galactoside ABC transporter / transport of 
                     beta-D-galactose / transport of methyl-beta-D-galactoside"
                     /label=mglB
                     /note="MglB is the periplasmic binding protein of a
                     D-galactose / methyl-D-galactoside ABC transport system; 
                     ligand bound MglB also interacts with the |FRAME: EG11018 
                     ""Trg""| sensory protein to mediate taxis to galactose and 
                     glucose.
                     <i>mglB</i> mutants are defective in both galactose 
                     transport and galactose taxis |CITS: [4359648]|. 
                     <i>mglB</i> mutants are unable to accumulate labeled 
                     methyl-&beta;-D-galactopyranoside |CITS: [6807987]|. 
                     <i>mglB</i><sup>+</sup> plasmids synthesize both the 
                     precursor and the mature form of galactose binding protein 
                     in minicells; chemotaxis towards galactose requires MglB 
                     but not MglA or MglC |CITS: [6294056]|. MglB (purified from
                     <i>E. coli</I> W3092) has a single binding site and binds 
                     galactose and glucose with &micro;M affinity |CITS: 
                     [319823]|.
                     Purified MglB consists of two globular domains joined by 
                     three separate peptide segments |CITS: [6993475][6340108]|.
                     D-glucose and D-galactose bind in a cleft between the two 
                     domains; bound sugars are detected in their &beta; anomeric
                     form |CITS: [3057628][8161535]|. Purified MglB binds a 
                     Ca<sup>2+</sup> ion |CITS: [3600760]|. MglB has a 
                     preference for the &beta; form of D-glucose |CITS: 
                     [17473016]|. Ligand bound MglB interacts with the Trg 
                     chemoreceptor |CITS: [4927373][370826]|.
                     MglB has been used in the development of a glucose 
                     biosensor (reviewed by |CITS: [23439161]|).
                     Review: |CITS: [4940020]|<BR>Related reviews: |CITS: 
                     [8336670][8861200]|"
