                     /product="putative pseudouridine transporter"
                     /label=psuT
                     /note="PsuT is a member of the Concentrative Nucleoside 
                     Transport (CNT) family |CITS: [26546518]| and is a 
                     predicted pseudouridine transport protein in <i>E. coli</i>
                     K-12. <i>psuT</i> is located directly downstream from 
                     <i>psuG</i> and <i>psuK</i> which encode proteins involved 
                     in pseudouridine degradation. These proteins have been 
                     experimentally characterised in uropathogenic <i>E. 
                     coli</i> |CITS: [18591240]|. Additionally pyrimidine 
                     auxotrophs of <i>E. coli</i> strains B and W are able to 
                     grow with pseudouridine as a sole pyrimidine source |CITS: 
                     [4334133]|. The three proteins have not been characterised 
                     in <i>E. coli</i> K-12."
