     gene            complement(2254906..2255844)
                     /gene="fruK"
                     /locus_tag="b2168"
                     /label=fruK
     CDS             complement(2254906..2255844)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="fruK"
                     /locus_tag="b2168"
                     /product="1-phosphofructokinase"
                     /EC_number="2.7.1.56"
                     /label=fruK
                     /note="1-phosphofructokinase is essential for the
                     utilization of fructose as a carbon source. The enzyme is 
                     highly specific for fructose-1-phosphate |CITS: 
                     [femsletbusch29-231-85]|.
                     FruK has some sequence similarity to the minor form of 
                     6-phosphofructokinase (PfkB), but not the major form (PfkA)
                     |CITS: [1981619]|. FruK belongs to the ribokinase family of
                     sugar kinases |CITS: [8382990]|.
                     A <i>fruK</i> mutant is unable to grow on fructose or 
                     fructose-1-phosphate as the sole source of carbon |CITS: 
                     [4579702]|. A &Delta;<i>fruK</i> mutant results in 
                     increased lag phase when grown on preferred carbon sources,
                     and increased growth delays on non-preferred carbon 
                     sources, such as glycerol |CITS: [38723750]|.
                     FruK can carry out the reverse reaction to form 
                     fructose-1-phosphate (F1P) from physiological 
                     concentrations of fructose-1,6-bisphosphate (FBP), thus 
                     creating the effector molecule of |FRAME: PD00521|. FruK 
                     can also form higher-order heterocomplexes with Cra in 
                     crude cell extracts and
                     <i>in vitro</i> with purified FruK |CITS: [38723750]|. 
                     Review: |CITS: [11361065]|"
