                     /locus_tag="b2169"
                     /label=fruB
     CDS             complement(2255844..2256974)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="fruB"
                     /locus_tag="b2169"
                     /product="bifunctional fructose-specific PTS
                     multiphosphoryl transfer protein FruB / fructose-specific 
                     PTS enzyme II"
                     /EC_number="2.7.1.202"
                     /label=fruB
                     /note="<i>fruB</i> encodes a tridomain protein in which a
                     IIA domain is linked to an HPr-like domain called FPr 
                     (fructose-inducible HPr) or H by a central domain (M) of 
                     unknown function |CITS: [8013873], [3528748], [2546043]|. 
                     Phosphate transfer to fructose by the fructose PTS occurs 
                     via the FPr domain of FruB rather than by HPr as is typical
                     for other PTS pathways |CITS: [3510127]|. Phosphate 
                     transfer is predicted to occur from Enzyme I (PtsI) to 
                     histidine residue 299 in the FruB H domain to histidine 
                     residue 62 in the FruB IIA domain.
                     FruB is also known as the diphosphoryl transfer protein 
                     (DTP)."
