     gene            2257342..2258523
                     /gene="setB"
                     /locus_tag="b2170"
                     /label=setB
     CDS             2257342..2258523
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="setB"
                     /locus_tag="b2170"
                     /product="sugar exporter SetB"
                     /label=setB
                     /note="Early work |CITS: [10209755][10438463]|
                     characterized SetB as a sugar transporter; a later study 
                     |CITS: [14617174]| implicated SetB in chromosome 
                     segregation.
                     Inside-out membrane vesicles prepared from cells 
                     overexpressing <I>setB</I> accumulate significant amounts 
                     of lactose in a manner that is sensitive to the proton 
                     ionophore, carbonyl cyanide m-chlorophenylhydrazone (CCCP) 
                     |CITS: [10209755]|. SetB can transport lactose and glucose 
                     but does not export the sugar analogs isopropyl 
                     &beta;-D-thiogalactoside (IPTG) and 
                     2-nitrophenyl-beta-D-thiogalactopyranoside (ONPTG); SetB 
                     has a narrower substrate specificity than |FRAME: 
                     B0070-MONOMER ""SetA""| |CITS: [10438463]|.
                     SetB has been implicated in chromosome segregation |CITS: 
                     [14617174]|. Overexpression of of <i>setB</i> suppresses 
                     the growth defect of a mutation in <i>parC</i> 
                     (<i>parC1215</i>), encoding a subunit of topoisomerase IV*;
                     deletion of SetB produces a delay in chromosome segregation
                     while overproduction results in cell elongation, 
                     filamentation, and stretched or fragmented nucleoids; 
                     &Delta;<i>setB ftsk::cam</i> double mutants have a 
                     synthetic phenotype; a SetB-GFP fusion protein localizes in
                     a helical pattern in the cell and SetB interacts physically
                     with MreB |CITS: [14617174]|.
                     In the Transporter Classification Database |CITS: 
                     [26546518]|, SetB is a member of the Sugar Efflux 
                     Transporter (SET) Family within the Major Facilitator 
                     Superfamily (MFS).
                     <i>setB</i>: <u>s</u>ugar <u>e</u>fflux <u>t</u>ransporter 
                     B |CITS: [10438463]|
                     * |CITS: [14617174]| states ""The original suppressor 
                     plasmid.... which rescued 
                     C600<i>parC1215</i>......contained <i>E. coli</i> 
                     chromosomal sequences from nucleotide 3,877,467 to nt 
                     4,187,000 (Blattner et al., 1997). This region included 
                     three complete ORFs in the following order: <i>yeiO, 
                     yeiP</i> and <i>yeiQ</i>.""<BR>However <i>yeiO, yeiP</i> 
                     and <i>yeiQ</i> are located at map position 2,263,863 to 
                     2,267,711.<BR>SetB's role in chromosome segregation is also
                     referred to in |CITS: 
                     [15130115][15866039][17200598][16983190][20862359]|."
