     gene            2262333..2263046
                     /gene="lpxT"
                     /locus_tag="b2174"
                     /label=lpxT
     CDS             2262333..2263046
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="lpxT"
                     /locus_tag="b2174"
                     /product="trifunctional lipid A-core phosphotransferase / 
                     Kdo2-lipid A phosphotransferase / undecaprenyl diphosphate 
                     phosphatase"
                     /EC_number="2.7.4.29; 3.6.1.27"
                     /label=lpxT
                     /note="LpxT transfers a phosphate group from 
                     undecaprenyl-pyrophosphate (Und-PP or C<sub>55</sub>-PP) to
                     the position 1 phosphate of approximately one-third of 
                     lipid A-core oligosaccharide molecules to create lipid 
                     A-core 1-diphosphate. LpxT activity enhances the net 
                     negative charge of LPS and contributes to recycling of the 
                     carrier lipid |FRAME: CPD-9646| that is required for 
                     biosynthesis of a number of cell wall polymers such as 
                     peptidoglycan and lipopolysaccharide.
                     LpxT activity contributes to |FRAME: DEOXYCHOLATE| 
                     resistance; <i>lpxT</i> inactivation impairs the initial 
                     stages of gut colonization in a mouse model of infection; 
                     inhibition of LpxT by the small membrane protein |FRAME: 
                     MONOMER0-4214 PmrR| results in sensitivity to deoxycholate 
                     in the polymyxin-resistant |FRAME: EG11615 
                     BasR(PmrA)|-constitutive strain WD101 |CITS: 
                     [34017319][20384697]| (see also |CITS: [16428424]|). <i>In 
                     trans</i> expression of <i>lpxT</i> in WD101 restores 
                     deoxycholate resistance and confers polymyxin B 
                     susceptibility |CITS: [34017319]|.
                     LpxT is a membrane protein with its C-terminus in the 
                     cytoplasm |CITS: [17660416]|. The catalytic acid 
                     phosphatase domain is located in the periplasm |CITS: 
                     [17660416][18047581]|.
                     LpxT transfers a phosphate from Und-PP to 
                     Kdo<sub>2</sub>-lipid A <i>in vitro</i> |CITS: [18047581]|.
                     The antibiotic |FRAME: bacitracin bacitracin| sequesters 
                     Und-PP and prevents lipid A-core diphosphate formation 
                     <i>in vivo</i>  |CITS: [18047581]|. Activation of the 
                     |FRAME: PWY0-1482 ""BasSR two-component system""| by 
                     Fe<sup>3+</sup> results in the post-translational 
                     inhibition of LpxT-dependent lipid A-core modification 
                     |CITS: [20384697]|.
                     <i>lpxT</i> mutants do not produce lipid A-core 
                     1-diphosphate |CITS: [18047581]|. LpxT contributes to the 
                     residual Und-PP phosphatase activity in a strain that lacks
                     the major Und-PP phosphatase |FRAME: EG11665-MONOMER BacA|;
                     LpxT-mediated Und-PP phosphatase activity alone is not 
                     sufficient to sustain growth |CITS: [15778224]|. <i>bacA 
                     lpxT</i> double deletion mutants and <i>bacA lpxT ybjG</i> 
                     triple deletion mutants are hypersensitive to |FRAME: 
                     CPD0-441| - an antibiotic that inhibits the <i>de novo</i> 
                     synthesis of Und-P |CITS: [17660416]|.
                     Expression of <i>lpxT</i> is increased by exposure to 
                     sodium salicylate |CITS: [11395452]|. <i>lpxT</i> is a 
                     'core pH-dependent gene' - its expression varies between 
                     acid and base growth conditions under both aerobic and 
                     anaerobic growth |CITS: [17026754]|. LpxT expression is 
                     reduced in a <i>phoP</i> null mutant grown in rich nutrient
                     broth; LpxT expression is increased at 37&deg;C and 
                     42&deg;C compared to 25&deg;C |CITS: [34017319]|. Related 
                     review: |CITS: [18086187]|"
                     /translation="MIKNLPQIVLLNIVGLALFLSWYIPVNHGFWLPIDADIFYFFNQK
