     gene            2264205..2265761
                     /gene="pdeN"
                     /locus_tag="b2176"
                     /label=pdeN
     CDS             2264205..2265761
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="pdeN"
                     /locus_tag="b2176"
                     /product="putative c-di-GMP phosphodiesterase PdeN"
                     /label=pdeN
                     /note="PdeN is a predicted c-di-GMP phosphodiesterase; the 
                     protein is predicted to contain two transmembrane domains 
                     flanking a periplasmic CSS domain containing two highly 
                     conserved cysteines, followed by a cytoplasmic C-terminal 
                     EAL domain with predicted phosphodiesterase activity |CITS:
                     [19332833][26148715][29514851]|.
                     PdeN is one of 5 CSS domain containing c-di-GMP 
                     phosphodiesterases in <i>E. coli</i> K-12; redox control 
                     and proteolysis of these enzymes is believed to modulate 
                     their activity and affect matrix production in biofilm (see
                     |CITS: [29514851]|).
                     A screen for suppressors of the motility defect of a 
                     |FRAME: EG12252 &Delta;<i>pdeH</i>| mutant identified 
                     activating mutations in <i>E. coli</i>'s alternative 
                     c-di-GMP phosphodiesterases (PDEs), including PdeN. This 
                     supports the view that many of the candidate c-di-GMP 
                     phosphodiesterases encoded in the <i>E. coli</i> genome 
                     require an appropriate stimulus to become active. 
                     Suppressor mutations in <i>pdeN</i> consisted of single 
                     amino acid substitutions in either the N-terminal membrane 
                     sensory domain of PdeN or the EAL catalytic domain and 
                     resulted in increased swimming motility and reduced levels 
                     of intracellular c-di-GMP |CITS: [26553851]|.
                     <i>pdeN</i> is expressed during exponential growth in rich 
                     media at both 37 and 28&deg;C |CITS: [19332833]| (see also 
                     |CITS: [29514851]|).
                     <i>rtn</i> was originally misidentified as a gene of 
                     another organism, <i>Proteus vulgaris</i> |CITS: 
                     [9079933]|.
                     PdeN: ""<b>p</b>hospho<b>d</b>i<b>e</b>sterase <b>N</b>"" 
                     |CITS: [26148715]|"
