     gene            complement(2272049..2273239)
                     /gene="bcr"
                     /locus_tag="b2182"
                     /label=bcr
     CDS             complement(2272049..2273239)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="bcr"
                     /locus_tag="b2182"
                     /product="multidrug efflux pump Bcr"
                     /label=bcr
                     /note="Expression of <i>bcr</i> from a high-copy number
                     plasmid confers resistance to the antibiotic bicyclomycin 
                     |CITS: [8486276 ]|; increased expression of <i>bcr</i> 
                     contributes to sulfathiazole resistance in an <i>E. 
                     coli</i> strain that also contains a 
                     sulfathiazole-resistant |FRAME: H2PTEROATESYNTH-MONOMER| 
                     |CITS: [2694948][9449266]|. Multicopy expression of 
                     <i>bcr</i> in a K-12 strain which lacks the major efflux 
                     pump permease AcrB (<i>E. coli</i> KAM3; see |CITS: 
                     [12618449]|), confers moderate resistance to tetracycline, 
                     fosfomycin, kanamycin and acriflavine but does not impact 
                     the resistance to a range of other antibiotics and toxic 
                     compounds |CITS: [11566977]|. Bcr is able to transport 
                     dipeptides (Ala-Gln and L-alanyl-L-branched chain amino 
                     acids) in a dipeptide overproducing strain |CITS: 
                     [20067529]| and promotes L-cysteine export in cells 
                     engineered for L-cysteine overproduction |CITS: 
                     [16820466]|.
                     <i>bcr</i> is one of 35 efflux-encoding genes that have 
                     been deleted or inactivated in 'Efflux KnockOut-35' 
                     (EKO-35) -  a K-12 BW25133-derived strain that lacks 35 
                     efflux pumps and can be used as a platform to study their 
                     function |CITS: [36065018][36318669]|.
                     Bcr is a member of the Drug:H<sup>+</sup> Antiporter-1 (12 
                     Spanner) (DHA1) family within the Major Facilitator 
                     Superfamily (MFS) |CITS: [8440470][8987357][26546518]|. 
                     <i>bcr</i>: <U>b</U>i<U>c</U>yclomycin <U>r</U>esistance 
                     |CITS: [8486276]|<BR><i>sur</i>:<U>su</U>lfathiazole 
                     <U>r</U>esistance |CITS: [9449266]|"
