     gene            2274111..2275871
                     /gene="radD"
                     /locus_tag="b2184"
                     /label=radD
     CDS             2274111..2275871
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="radD"
                     /locus_tag="b2184"
                     /product="bifunctional DNA repair helicase RadD / RadD
                     ATPase"
                     /label=radD
                     /note="Genetic studies have implicated RadD in the repair
                     of double strand DNA breaks; strains lacking <i>radD</i> 
                     have increased sensitivity to conditions (UV irradiation, 
                     ionising radiation) or agents (ciprofloxacin) that cause 
                     double strand DNA breaks |CITS: [25049088] [25425430]|. The
                     &Delta;<i>radD</i> &Delta;|FRAME: EG11296 ""<i>radA</i>""| 
                     double mutant shows a synergistic increase in sensitivity 
                     to DNA damaging agents/conditions and the two proteins may 
                     have an overlapping or complementary function in the repair
                     of breaks |CITS: [25425430]|. RadD is implicated in the 
                     avoidance or destabilization of R-loops; RadD counteracts 
                     the R-loop formation that leads to double strand DNA breaks
                     upon sub-lethal treatment with the aminoglycoside 
                     antibiotic, tobramycin |CITS: [31266870]|. RadD is 
                     implicated in the resolution of branched DNA intermediates 
                     which can arise from template switching (see |CITS: 
                     [28641943]|) at postreplication gaps |CITS: [31665437]|.
                     Purified RadD has DNA-independent ATPase activity; RadD 
                     physically interacts with single strand DNA binding protein
                     (SSB) <i>in vitro</i> and <i>in vivo</i> and SSB stimulates
                     the ATPase activity of RadD <i>in vitro</i>; RadD interacts
                     with ssDNA <i>in vitro</i> |CITS: [27519413]| (see also 
                     |CITS: [36614183][37142225]|).
                     RadD contains all 7 of the helicase superfamily 2 motifs; 
                     RadD contains a cluster of cysteines in the C-terminal 
                     region that may be involved in binding zinc |CITS: 
                     [25425430]|. RadD is monomeric in solution; RadD is a 
                     multidomain protein consisting of 2 RecA-like domains (RD1 
                     and RD2), a 4-Cys zinc finger domain, and a C-terminal 
                     domain |CITS: [31035307]|.
                     Overexpression of RadD<sub>1-461</sub> (cloned from a 
                     DH5&alpha; strain) causes a filamentous phenotype |CITS: 
                     [23565292]|.
                     <i>rad</i>: <U>rad</U>iation sensitive"
