     gene            2275996..2276280
                     /gene="rplY"
                     /locus_tag="b2185"
                     /label=rplY
     CDS             2275996..2276280
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rplY"
                     /locus_tag="b2185"
                     /product="trifunctional 50S ribosomal subunit protein L25
                     / 50S ribosomal subunit / ribosome"
                     /label=rplY
                     /note="The L25 protein is a component of the 50S subunit
                     of the ribosome and binds to 5S rRNA. L25 is not an 
                     essential protein |CITS: [17198710]|.
                     Binding of L25 to 5S rRNA has been studied in detail |CITS:
                     [354687][365228][379819][380994][393829][6278442][6 
                     364140][6347250][6372859][6383867][3892485][2429677][353588
                     6][3542026][8925931]|. Solution structures of L25 alone and
                     in complex with a segment of 5S rRNA have been determined 
                     |CITS: [9799245][10454606][10562563]|, and a crystal 
                     structure of L25 bound to a loop E-containing fragment of 
                     5S rRNA has been solved at 1.8 &Aring; resolution |CITS: 
                     [10696113]|. The interaction of L25 with 5S rRNA is not 
                     required for incorporation of L25 into the ribosome, 
                     although it is important for its retention |CITS: 
                     [25365493]|. Molecular dynamics of the main polypeptide 
                     C&alpha;-atoms in the &alpha;-helices and &beta;-sheets 
                     were simulated; the latter have much lower dynamics and 
                     higher stability |CITS: [39403096]|.
                     L25 can be crosslinked to 23S rRNA in the initiation 
                     complex |CITS: [2495985]| and to ribosomal protein L19 
                     |CITS: [2645289][2653827][2665813]|. L25 is important for 
                     retention of ribosomal protein L16 |CITS: [26885579]|.
                     A truncated form of L25 can be detected in 2-D gels |CITS: 
                     [9868784]|. L25 is not posttranslationally modified |CITS: 
                     [10094780]|.
                     Although <i>rplY</i> has a non-canonical ribosome binding 
                     site, the gene is translated with high efficiency. 
                     Conserved elements in the 5' UTR play a role in autogenous 
                     translation control |CITS: [25749694]|.
                     An <i>rplY</i> deletion mutant is viable, but has a slower 
                     growth rate than wild type. Mutant ribosomes are impaired 
                     in protein biosynthesis |CITS: [17198710]|. The mutant 
                     ribosomes appeared to lack only L25 |CITS: [17198710]|; 
                     however, subsequent experiments showed that these ribosomes
                     contained an inactive fraction of dissociated subunits, in 
                     which the 50S subunit also lacked the essential |FRAME: 
                     EG10877-MONOMER L16| subunit |CITS: [26885579]|. A 
                     &Delta;<i>rplY</i> mutant shows increased sensitivity to 
                     the alkylating agent methyl methanesulfonate |CITS: 
                     [18824089]|."
                     /translation="MFTINAEVRKEQGKGASRRLRAANKFPAIIYGGKEAPLAIELDHD
