     gene            2277855..2279615
                     /gene="lapC"
                     /locus_tag="b2188"
                     /label=lapC
     CDS             2277855..2279615
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="lapC"
                     /locus_tag="b2188"
                     /product="lipopolysaccharide signal transducer LapC"
                     /label=lapC
                     /note="<i>lapC</i> (formerly <i>yejM</i>) encodes an
                     essential inner membrane protein that is implicated in 
                     lipopolysaccharide (LPS) homeostasis. LapC functions in a 
                     regulatory pathway that controls |FRAME: EG11506-MONOMER 
                     ""FtsH""|/|FRAME: EG12691-MONOMER ""LapB""| mediated 
                     proteolysis of the lipid A biosynthesis protein |FRAME: 
                     UDPACYLGLCNACDEACETYL-MONOMER ""LpxC""| |CITS: 
                     [32291302][32430473][33260377]|. LapC senses LPS within the
                     inner membrane and controls LPS biosynthesis through LapB 
                     and FtsH-mediated regulation of LpxC levels |CITS: 
                     [32540932]|; LapC (purified from |FRAME: TAX-199310|) 
                     senses LPS in the inner membrane and acts to sequester LapB
                     from FtsH and thus regulate LpxC degradation |CITS: 
                     [35931690]|.
                     In uropathogenic <i>E. coli</i> (UPEC CFT073) the LapC 
                     ortholog, PbgA binds LPS directly |CITS: [32788728]|.  A 
                     LapC<sub>2</sub>LapB<sub>2</sub> oligomeric complex, 
                     purified from CFT073, is thought to represent the native 
                     state; structural information suggests that binding of LPS 
                     and LapB to LapC are mutually exclusive; 
                     LapC<sub>2</sub>LapB<sub>2</sub> dissociates when LPS is 
                     present |CITS: [35931690]|.
                     LapC has 5 predicted transmembrane domains; topology 
                     analysis suggests the C-terminus is located in the 
                     periplasm |CITS:[15044727],[15919996]|.
                     A <I>lapC</I> null mutation is lethal |CITS:[18245839]| 
                     (see also |CITS: [32788728]|). Strain LH530, which contains
                     a <i>lapC</i> (G570A) nonsense mutation and would express a
                     truncated form of LapC that retains the N-terminal membrane
                     domain but lacks the C-terminal periplasmic domain, is 
                     temperature sensitive, is more sensitive to rifampicin and 
                     erythromycin and is defective for Lipid A synthesis 
                     |CITS:[18245839][9168603][9025280]|. Overexpression of 
                     |FRAME: EG12221-MONOMER ""<I>acpT</I>""| - encoding 
                     holo-[acyl carrier protein] synthase 2 - suppresses the 
                     lethality of a <I>lapC</I> null mutation, as well as the 
                     temperature sensitivity associated with a <i>lapC</i> 
                     (G570A) nonsense mutation |CITS:[18245839][9025280]|. This 
                     suppression does not appear to require phosphopantetheinyl 
                     transferase activity: overexpression of a mutant AcpT 
                     protein which lacks this activity also suppresses the 
                     temperature sensitivity of the <i>lapC</i> (G570A) mutation
                     |CITS:[18245839]| (see also |CITS: [32430473]|).
                     Loss of the LapC periplasmic domain leads to decreased LPS 
                     levels and genetic interaction data indicates that this is 
                     due to increased activity of a LapB-FtsH protease complex 
                     with resultant increased degradation of LpxC which 
                     catalyses the first committed step in lipid A biosynthesis 
                     |CITS: [32291302][32430473]|. LapC is not essential in 
                     cells overproducing LpxC; LapC interacts physically with 
                     LapB and may serve as an antagonist of LapB function |CITS:
                     [32430473][33260377]| (see also |CITS: 
                     [33990960][35931690]|). LapC is not essential when the 
                     FtsH-LapB complex is inactivated; loss of <i>lapC</i> may 
                     hyperactivate the the FtsH-LapB proteolytic machinery 
                     |CITS: [32291302]|.
                     In |FRAME: TAX-99287 ""<i>Salmonella typhimurium</i>""| 
                     <i>yejM</i> (renamed <i>pbgA</i>) encodes a transmembrane 
                     protein that binds cardiolipins and promotes their 
                     trafficking to the outer membrane - a function that is 
                     implicated in the PhoPQ-regulated remodelling of the outer 
                     membrane during host infection |CITS: [25856753]|. Crystal 
                     structures of the the globular periplasmic domain of PbgA 
                     (residues 245-586) from both <i>Salmonella</i> and <i>E. 
                     coli</i> K-12 have been determined |CITS: [27487745]| and a
                     putative cardiolipin binding site identified |CITS: 
                     [27487745]| (see further |CITS: [32047135]|).
                     LapC is implicated in lipid homeostasis independently of 
                     its role in cardiolipin transport; the <i>lapC1163</i> 
                     allele (expressing a C-terminally truncated form of LapC) 
                     increases OM permeability - this phenotype is not affected 
                     by deletion of the cardiolipin synthase genes and thus does
                     not appear to result from a defect in cardiolipin transport
                     |CITS: [31235517]|.
                     <i>lapC</I>: <u>l</u>ipopolysaccharide <u>a</u>ssembly 
                     <u>p</u>rotein C
                     Related review: |CITS: [35008618]|"
                     /translation="MVTHRQRYREKVSQMVSWGHWFALFNILLSLVIGSRYLFIADWPT
