     CDS             complement(2291136..2291738)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="napC"
                     /locus_tag="b2202"
                     /product="bifunctional menaquinol--cytochrome c reductase
                     NapC / menaquinol--[NapB cytochrome c] reductase"
                     /label=napC
                     /note="The |FRAME: EG12060| gene encodes a membrane-bound 
                     tetraheme cytochrome <i>c</i> protein, which passes 
                     electrons either from menaquinone or from the |FRAME: 
                     CPLX0-3241 ""NapGH ubiquinol-cytochrome c reductase 
                     complex""| to the |FRAME: EG12061 NapB| subunit of the 
                     |FRAME: NAP-CPLX ""periplasmic nitrite reductase""| |CITS: 
                     [8039676][8842153][8830238][8919448][14674886]|.
                     NapC is homologous to the |FRAME: G-55066 CymA| protein of 
                     |FRAME: TAX-211586|, which transfers electrons from 
                     menaquinol to a number of terminal oxidases. Heterologous 
                     expression of CymA in <i>E. coli</i> enabled growth with 
                     Fe(III) NTA as the terminal electron acceptor |CITS: 
                     [18394146]|."
