     gene            2297384..2297872
                     /gene="eco"
                     /locus_tag="b2209"
                     /label=eco
     CDS             2297384..2297872
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="eco"
                     /locus_tag="b2209"
                     /product="serine protease inhibitor ecotin"
                     /label=eco
                     /note="Ecotin inhibits trypsin and a number of additional 
                     heterologous proteases |CITS: 
                     [6411724][8142399][7781771][10500122]|. Some endogenous 
                     <i>E. coli</i> proteases are not sensitive to ecotin |CITS:
                     [6411724][3549688]|.
                     Residue Met84 is the reactive site |CITS: [2007606]|. M84K,
                     M84R, and M84L mutant proteins exhibit altered substrate 
                     specificity |CITS: [8143850]|. The activities of various 
                     mutant proteins have been evaluated |CITS: [814385 
                     0][8063835][7744876][8647243][9642073][9642077][10843853][1
                     1352586][11959867]|. Ecotin is implicated in defense from 
                     T6SS-mediated killing by |FRAME: TAX-666| |CITS: 
                     [33892013]|. Knockout mutant and crystal structural studies
                     of ecotin interacting with mannan-binding lectin-associated
                     serine proteases (MASPs), components of the lectin pathway 
                     of the complement system, revealed ecotin's activity as a 
                     microbial defense factor and how binding sites 1 and 2 
                     contribute to ecotin's inhibition of MASP enzymes, thus 
                     providing a potential antibiotic target |CITS: 
                     [31860690][35483450]|.
                     Ecotin is a homodimer |CITS: [6411724]|; each homodimer 
                     binds to two protease monomers |CITS: [6411724]|. The 
                     dimerization and substrate interaction regions have been 
                     examined in detail |CITS: [9642073][10843853][11352586]|. 
                     Ecotin is periplasmic |CITS: [6411724][2007606][1879537]|. 
                     Ecotin exhibits anticoagulant properties |CITS: [8142399]|.
                     Crystal structures of ecotin |CITS: [8931142]|, of an 
                     ecotin-chymotrypsin complex |CITS: [10216315]|, of an 
                     ecotin-trypsin complex |CITS: [10843853]|, of an 
                     ecotin-factor Xa complex |CITS: [12834348]| and of ecotin 
                     complexed with MASPs |CITS: [35483450]| are presented. 
                     Ecotin has been crystallized for structural studies, with 
                     trypsin |CITS: [1960717]| and alone |CITS: [8445642]|. 
                     Regulation has been described |CITS: 
                     [6411724][2007606][9661786]|.
                     Review: |CITS: [7757004]|"
