     gene            2306563..2306655
                     /gene="micF"
                     /locus_tag="b4439"
                     /label=micF
     misc_RNA        2306563..2306655
                     /gene="micF"
                     /locus_tag="b4439"
                     /product="small regulatory RNA MicF"
                     /note="The MicF small RNA |CITS: [2436145]| negatively
                     regulates translation of the OmpF porin |CITS: [2478539]| 
                     and the stability of OmpF mRNA |CITS: [2478539][11029695]|.
                      MicF binds to OmpF mRNA |CITS: [1702997]| and represses 
                     production of OmpF in response to environmental and/or 
                     stress conditions, including conditions of high osmolarity 
                     |CITS: [2439487][2478539]|, low or moderate osmolarity 
                     |CITS: [7519595]|, heat |CITS: [2478539]|, ethanol |CITS: 
                     [2478539]|, salicylate |CITS: 
                     [1715858][11766055][21398557]|, paraquat |CITS: [7679383]|,
                     and membrane perturbation |CITS: [9139902]|. MicF activity 
                     has been implicated in resistance to antibiotic drugs 
                     |CITS: 
                     [2848006][1510409][7679383][7896685][9343820][11353631]|. 
                     MicF is involved in survival of nitric oxide released by 
                     macrophages in response to infection |CITS: [8234347]|. 
                     Additional targets of MicF have been defined and include 
                     regulation of Lrp expression in rich medium.  A double 
                     negative feedback loop of MicF and Lrp regulation has been 
                     proposed |CITS: [22324810]|.
                     The <i>micF</i> gene was originally found to encode a 
                     non-translated 174 nt antisense RNA that regulates OmpF 
                     abundance |CITS: [6201848]|.  It was later found that the 
                     primary transcript is a smaller, 93 nt RNA species |CITS: 
                     [2436145]|.  The secondary structure of the MicF RNA has 
                     been examined |CITS: [7534474][9478198]|.  MicF is cleaved 
                     by RNase E <i>in vitro</i> |CITS: [8522136]| and may be 
                     destabilized by StpA |CITS: [11029695]| and is stabilized 
                     by Hfq |CITS: [17264113]|.
                     MicF was found in a ribonucleoprotein complex |CITS: 
                     [1702997]|; it was later determined that MicF binds Hfq 
                     |CITS: [14622403][18388495]| and that regulation of OmpF 
                     |CITS: [17264113]| and Lrp |CITS: [22324810]| expression by
                     MicF depends on the presence of Hfq.  Regulation of OmpF 
                     does not depend on RNase E |CITS: [17264113]|. 
                     Overexpression of <i>micF</i> from a high-copy-number 
                     plasmid causes reduced OmpF expression, compared to wild 
                     type, while expression of <i>micF</i> from a 
                     low-copy-number plasmid does not appear to affect OmpF 
                     expression |CITS: [3888961][2439487]|.  Deletion of 
                     <i>micF</i> suppresses the OmpF-defective phenotype of a 
                     <i>tolC</i> mutant, probably by upregulating production of 
                     OmpF |CITS: [3007299][2443485]|.  The defect in OmpC 
                     regulation exhibited by a <i>micF</i> mutant is suppressed 
                     by HrsA overproduction |CITS: [9063979]|.
                     Regulation of <i>micF</i> expression has been described 
                     |CITS: [2848006][2478539][1695892][1715858][1723390][15104 
                     09][7679383][7934849][8234347][8034583][7519595][7891555][8
                     002608][7896685][8522515][8825776][8626315][8655567][880974
                     7][8899987][9139902][9192630][10398829][10631293][10802742]
                     [10850996][11029695][11073934][11353631][11724537][11766055
                     ][12713466][15466019]|. Many chemical signals that modulate
                     the transcription of the <i>micF</i> gene have been shown 
                     in |CITS: [40694573]|.
                     Stc: ""<b>s</b>uppressor of <b>T</b>ol<b>C</b>""
                     MicF: ""<b>m</b>RNA-<b>i</b>nterfering <b>c</b>omplementary
                     RNA"" |CITS: [6201848]|
                     Reviews: |CITS: [2450678][7689446][7540245][8809744][92557 
                     88][10068996][11601842][15063850][15487940][15466017][1695 
