     CDS             2306967..2309639
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rcsD"
                     /locus_tag="b2216"
                     /product="RcsD phosphotransferase"
                     /label=rcsD
                     /note="RcsD is a phosphotransferase within the complex Rcs 
                     phosphorelay. RcsD mediates phosphate transfer between the 
                     hybrid histidine kinase RcsC and the transcription 
                     regulator RcsB. RcsD may be the primary interacting partner
                     of the Rcs pathway inhibitor, |FRAME: G7741-MONOMER 
                     ""IgaA""| (see |CITS: [29897834]|).
                     RcsD is an inner membrane protein containing a 
                     pseudo-histidine-kinase domain (lacking a presumed 
                     histidine phosphorylation site) and a phosphotransmitter 
                     domain containing a conserved histidine (His-842); a 
                     non-polar <i>rcsD</i> deletion abolishes activation of the 
                     Rcs signalling response (as measured by induction of a 
                     <i>cps::lacZ</i> transcriptional fusion in response to 
                     osmotic shock or upon DjlA overproduction); the 
                     histidine-containing phosphotransmitter (HPt) domain of 
                     RcsD can be phosphorylated <i>in vitro</i> and is capable 
                     of transferring a phosphate to purified RcsB however a 
                     direct RcsC to RcsD phosphotransfer has not been 
                     demonstrated |CITS: [11309126]|.
                     A solution structure of the Hpt domain of RcsD has been 
                     reported and its interaction with the RcsC and RcsB 
                     proteins studied |CITS: [15476819]| (see also |CITS: 
                     [17005198][19021569]|). RcsD contains an 
                     &alpha;/&beta;/loop (ABL) domain located in the linker 
                     region between the pseudo HK and HPt domains; the RcsD ABL 
                     domain interacts with the DNA-binding domain of RcsB <i>in 
                     vitro</i> |CITS: [21481780]|.
                     The Keio collection <i>rcsD</i> mutant is sensitive to 
                     lithium (<90% growth at 100mM Li) |CITS: [39983623]|. 
                     <i>rcsD</i> transcription increases in a 
                     <i>hns</i>-deficient strain |CITS: [20435136]|."
