     CDS             2319588..2320772
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="atoB"
                     /locus_tag="b2224"
                     /product="acetyl-CoA acetyltransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.3.1.16"
                     /label=atoB
                     /note="AtoB is one of two 3-ketoacyl-CoA thiolases in
                     <i>E. coli</i>.  While |FRAME: FADA-MONOMER FadA| has broad
                     substrate specificity, AtoB is strictly specific for 
                     acetoacetyl-CoA |CITS: [236278][9904]|.
                     Crystal structures of AtoB alone and in a complex with CoA 
                     have been solved; the structure can be described as a 
                     loosely interacting dimer of tight dimers |CITS: 
                     [27380370]|.  The gene for this study was cloned from <i>E.
                     coli</i> BL21 (DE3), but the sequence is identical to that 
                     of the K-12 protein.
                     AtoB expression is induced by growth on acetoacetate |CITS:
                     [4563344]|.
                     AtoB is used for metabolic engineering of 1-butanol |CITS: 
                     [21398484][25866563]| and medium-chain fuel |CITS: 
                     [25645093]| production.
                     AtoB: ""<b>a</b>ce<b>to</b>acetate"" |CITS: [4563344]|"
