                     /locus_tag="b2237"
                     /product="putative lipopolysaccharide kinase InaA"
                     /label=inaA
                     /note="<i>inaA</i> was originally identified as a gene
                     whose expression is induced in the presence of benzoate and
                     other weak acids that are able to traverse the cell 
                     membrane, and is inversely correlated with growth 
                     temperatures between 30 and 45&deg;C |CITS: 
                     [2954947][1537798]|.  Salicylate (via MarA), paraquat, 
                     hydrogen peroxide (via SoxS) |CITS: [7928997][11073934]|, 
                     and dipyridyl (via Rob) |CITS: 
                     [7896685][10850996][11844771]| increase <i>inaA</i> 
                     expression.
                     InaA: ""<b>in</b>ternal <b>a</b>cid-inducible"" |CITS: 
                     [2954947]|"
