                     dehydrogenase subunit A / anaerobic glycerol-3-phosphate 
                     dehydrogenase / glycerol-3-phosphate dehydrogenase, 
                     anaerobic"
                     /EC_number="1.1.5.3"
                     /label=glpA
                     /note="GlpA is the large subunit of a three subunit 
                     glycerol-3-phosphate dehydrogenase complex. In anaerobic 
                     conditions this respiratory enzyme converts 
                     glycerol-3-phosphate to dihydroxyacetone phosphate (DHAP) 
                     using fumarate as a terminal electron acceptor. The GlpA 
                     subunit contains noncovalently bound FAD. |CITS: 
                     [3286606][6282417][6792201][4945192]|."
