                     /note="<i>glpB</i> encodes a subunit of the heterotrimeric 
                     glycerol-3-phosphate dehydrogenase complex.  In anaerobic 
                     conditions this respiratory enzyme converts 
                     glycerol-3-phosphate to dihydroxyacetone phosphate (DHAP) 
                     using fumarate as a terminal electron acceptor. GlpB 
                     contains a predicted flavin mononucleotide-binding domain 
                     |CITS: [3286606][6363389]|
                     <i>glpB</i> was among the genes induced during phosphate 
                     starvation |CITS: [2160940]|."
