                     /product="inactive recombination-promoting nuclease-like
                     protein RpnE"
                     /label=rpnE
                     /note="RpnE is one of five proteins in <i>E. coli</i> that 
                     belong to the ""transposase_31"" family |CITS: [28096446]|,
                     which is distantly related to the PD-(D/E)XK nuclease 
                     superfamily |CITS: [17584917]|.
                     Unlike the other <i>E. coli</i> members of the family, 
                     overexpression of <i>rpnE</i> does not increase 
                     RecA-independent recombination, reduce cell viability, or 
                     induce expression of the DNA damage-inducible gene 
                     <i>dinD</i> |CITS: [28096446]|.
                     RpnE: ""inactive <b>r</b>ecombination-<b>p</b>romoting 
                     <b>n</b>uclease-like protein <b>E</b>"" |CITS: [28096446]|"
