     gene            complement(2351521..2352324)
                     /gene="yfaU"
                     /locus_tag="b2245"
                     /label=yfaU
     CDS             complement(2351521..2352324)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yfaU"
                     /locus_tag="b2245"
                     /product="2-keto-3-deoxy-L-rhamnonate aldolase"
                     /EC_number="4.1.2.53"
                     /label=yfaU
                     /note="YfaU is a 2-keto-3-deoxy-L-rhamnonate aldolase
                     which catalyzes a retro-aldol reaction with somewhat 
                     relaxed substrate specificity |CITS: [18754683][18754693]|.
                     Crystal structures of the enzyme alone and in a product 
                     complex with Mg<sup>2+</sup>-pyruvate have been solved, 
                     showing a trimer of domain-swapped dimers with 
                     (&beta;/&alpha;)<sub>8</sub> barrel subunits typical of the
                     divalent metal ion-dependent class II aldolases.  The 
                     architecture of the active site and a predicted catalytic 
                     mechanism are discussed.  Site-directed mutagenesis 
                     confirmed the importance of Arg74 and His49 for catalysis 
                     |CITS: [18754683]|.
                     The engineered variant W23V/L216A is able to accept larger 
                     pyruvate analogs as substrates in aldol addition reactions 
                     |CITS: [29363239]|."
