                     /note="The YfaV protein is an uncharacterised member of
                     the major facilitator superfamily (MFS) of transporters 
                     |CITS: [9529885]|. Based on sequence similarity, it may 
                     function as a proton-driven metabolite uptake system.
                     YfaV is an inner membrane protein with 12 predicted 
                     transmembrane domains.  The C terminus is located in the 
                     cytoplasm |CITS: [15919996]|."
