                     /gene="rhmD"
                     /locus_tag="b2247"
                     /product="L-rhamnonate dehydratase"
                     /EC_number="4.2.1.90"
                     /label=rhmD
                     /note="YfaW is a L-rhamnonate dehydratase (RhamD) with 
                     promiscuous substrate specificity |CITS: [18754693]|. RhamD
                     is a member of the mandelate racemase (MR) subgroup of the 
                     enolase superfamily.  A crystal
                     structure has been solved at 2.1 &Aring; resolution, where 
                     the enzyme is a tetramer of dimers.  Although
                     the enzyme is also an octamer in solution, based on the 
                     location of the active site, the minimum functional
                     unit appears to be the monomer.  A reaction mechanism and 
                     likely catalytic residues have been proposed,
                     and site-directed mutants were assayed to confirm lack of 
                     activity |CITS: [18754693]|."
