                     /label=yfaY
                     /note="YfaY contains a C-terminal domain that belongs to a 
                     family of NMN deamidases |CITS: [24340054]|, but the 
                     protein does not have NMN deamidase activity |CITS: 
                     [21953451]|.  The N-terminal domain of YfaY belongs to 
                     COG1058, a novel pyrophoshatase family, members of which 
                     were shown to have ADP-ribose pyrophosphatase activity 
                     |CITS: [23776507]|."
