     gene            2361518..2363500
                     /gene="arnA"
                     /locus_tag="b2255"
                     /label=arnA
     CDS             2361518..2363500
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="arnA"
                     /locus_tag="b2255"
                     /product="multifunctional fused
                     UDP-4-amino-4-deoxy-L-arabinose 
                     formyltransferase/UDP-glucuronate dehydrogenase / 
                     UDP-4-amino-4-deoxy-L-arabinose 
                     formyltransferase/UDP-glucuronate dehydrogenase / 
                     UDP-4-amino-4-deoxy-L-arabinose formyltransferase / 
                     UDP-glucuronate dehydrogenase"
                     /EC_number="2.1.2.13; 1.1.1.305"
                     /label=arnA
                     /note="ArnA is a bifunctional enzyme that acts within a
                     pathway that modifies lipid A phosphates with 
                     4-amino-4-deoxy-L-arabinose (L-Ara4N), which causes 
                     increased resistance to polymyxin |CITS: [11706007]|.
                     ArnA exhibits UDP-glucuronic acid (UDP-GlcA) 
                     C-4""-dehydrogenase and UDP-4-amino-4-deoxy-L-arabinose 
                     (UDP-L-Ara4N) formyltransferase activities <i>in vitro</i> 
                     |CITS: [11706007]|.  The two activities are separable, and 
                     both are required for polymyxin resistance |CITS: 
                     [15695810]|.
                     The N-terminal domain is similar to 
                     methionyl-tRNA<sup>fMet</sup> formyltransferase and 
                     catalyzes the 
                     <i>N</i><sup>10</sup>-formyltetrahydrofolate-dependent 
                     formylation of the 4'' amine of UDP-L-Ara4N |CITS: 
                     [15695810]|.  Crystal structures of this domain have been 
                     solved at 1.7, 1.2 and 2.5 &Aring; resolution |CITS: 
                     [15807526][15809294][27171345]|.  The 
                     <i>N</i><sup>10</sup>-formyltetrahydrofolate binding site 
                     has been identified and a reaction mechanism has been 
                     proposed; point mutations in the proposed catalytic 
                     residues abolish activity |CITS: [15807526][15809294]|. The
                     structure of the N-terminal domain in complex with both the
                     UDP-sugar substrate and 
                     <i>N</i><sup>5</sup>-formyltetrahydrofolate has provided 
                     additional insight into the substrate binding site |CITS: 
                     [27171345]|.
                     The C-terminal domain contains the 
                     NAD<sup>+</sup>-dependent dehydrogenase/decarboxylase 
                     activity which catalyzes the oxidative decarboxylation of 
                     UDP-GlcA.  Crystal structures of this domain have been 
                     solved at 2.4 and 2.3 &Aring; resolution |CITS: 
                     [15491143][15809294]|, and active site residues have been 
                     identified |CITS: [15809294][15939024]|.  The C-terminal 
                     domain is also able to inefficiently catalyze the reduction
                     of UDP-&alpha;-D-4-ketoxylose to UDP-&alpha;-D-xylose in an
                     overall reaction similar to the human UDP-&alpha;-D-xylose 
                     synthase.  Local unfolding of the active site is proposed 
                     to direct formation of the preferred product |CITS: 
                     [23072385]|.
                     Crystal structures of the full-length protein in the apo- 
                     and substrate-bound forms have been solved |CITS: 
                     [15939024][25760615]|.  The enzyme forms a homohexamer in a
                     dimer-of-trimers configuration.  The dehydrogenase domain 
                     undergoes a large conformational change upon binding of the
                     substrate UDP-GlcA; a catalytic mechanism was proposed 
                     |CITS: [15939024]|.  A central pocket present in the 
                     unliganded structure is proposed to bind a small-molecule 
                     effector |CITS: [25760615]|.
                     ArnA was also identified as a protein that copurifies with 
                     the SsrA-SmpB complex |CITS: [11248028]| and is often a 
                     contaminant during purification of recombinant His-tagged 
                     proteins |CITS: [16814929]|.
                     SAF: ""<b>S</b>srA-<b>a</b>ssociated <b>f</b>actor"" |CITS:
                     [11248028]|
                     ArnA: ""L-<b>Ar</b>a4<b>N</b> (4-amino-4-deoxy-L-arabinose)
                     biosynthesis"" |CITS: [11706007]|
                     PmrI: ""<b>p</b>oly<b>m</b>yxin <b>r</b>esistance"" Review:
                     |CITS: [17362200]|"
