     gene            2364387..2366039
                     /gene="arnT"
                     /locus_tag="b2257"
                     /label=arnT
     CDS             2364387..2366039
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="arnT"
                     /locus_tag="b2257"
                     /product="lipid IVA
                     4-amino-4-deoxy-L-arabinosyltransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.4.2.43"
                     /label=arnT
                     /note="ArnT is a transferase that catalyzes the addition
                     of |FRAME: 4-AMINO-4-DEOXY-L-ARABINOSE| (L-Ara4N) residues 
                     from |FRAME: CPD0-1189| to lipid A. This modification 
                     confers on the organism resistance to |FRAME: Polymyxins 
                     ""polymyxin antibiotics""| |CITS:[11535604][11535605]| 
                     (similar to the effect of lipid A modification by |FRAME: 
                     PHOSPHORYL-ETHANOLAMINE|, which is catalyzed by |FRAME: 
                     EG11613-MONOMER|). It should be noted that K-12 derived 
                     strains express ArnT, but do not synthesize  |FRAME: 
                     CPD0-1189| under normal conditions, and thus are sensitive 
                     to polymyxin.
                     The enzyme from <i>E. coli</i> has not been studied much, 
                     but the <i>Salmonella typhimurium</i> enzyme has been 
                     purified and characterized |CITS:[11535604][16226890]|.
                     It has been suggested, although not proven, that the enzyme
                     is involved not only in the attachment of L-Ara4N to lipid 
                     A but also in the transport of L-Ara4N from the cytoplasm, 
                     where it is synthesized, to the periplasmic side of the 
                     inner membrane, where the attachment takes place. However, 
                     deletion of <I>arnT</I> results in defective attachment of 
                     L-Ara4N to the lipid A core, but does not affect the 
                     transport of undecaprenyl phosphate-&alpha;-L-Ara4N across 
                     the inner membrane |CITS:[17928292]|.
                     A |FRAME: EG10614| mutant lacking the secondary linked 
                     myristoyl group of lipid A is unable to attach L-Ara4N to 
                     lipid A |CITS:[15951433]|.
                     It was found that in a |FRAME: EG10224| mutant, which is 
                     polymyxin-sensitive due to inhibition of |FRAME: 
                     EG11613-MONOMER|, resistance to polymyxin is restored by 
                     mutations that affect formation of the |FRAME: CPLX0-226 
                     ""cAMP-CRP complex""| (such as deletion of |FRAME: EG10170|
                     or |FRAME: EG10164|). In the absence of the cAMP-CRP 
                     complex ArnT activity was enhanced significantly, with the 
                     fraction of unmodified lipid A decreasing from ~40% to
                     ~12%. While the reason for this effect is still not fully 
                     understood, the authors suggest that loss of the complex 
                     results in increased synthesis of glutamate, a substrate of
                     ArnT |CITS: [37070977]|.
                     Expression of the |FRAME: TU0-13569| operon increases 
                     during growth with elevated FeSO<sub>4</sub>, 
                     FeCl<sub>3</sub>, or ZnSO<sub>4</sub> and is dependent upon
                     the |FRAME: EG11614 BasS|/|FRAME: EG11615 BasR| 
                     two-component signal transduction system 
                     |CITS:[15322361][15659689]|. <i>arnT</i> transcript levels 
                     increase under growth conditions with low Mg<sup>2+</sup> 
                     concentrations, but these expression levels decrease 
                     significantly in a |FRAME: G7172| mutant strain compared 
                     with the wild-type strain |CITS: [25605366]|."
