     gene            complement(2366751..2367017)
                     /gene="pmrD"
                     /locus_tag="b2259"
                     /label=pmrD
     CDS             complement(2366751..2367017)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="pmrD"
                     /locus_tag="b2259"
                     /product="signal transduction protein PmrD"
                     /label=pmrD
                     /note="PmrD is similar to the <i>Salmonella enterica</i>
                     serovar Typhimurium PmrD, which confers resistance to 
                     polymyxin B when it is overexpressed |CITS: 
                     [8206837][8524935]|; in <i>Salmonella</i>, PmrD controls 
                     the activity of the PmrA-PmrB two-component system at a 
                     post-transcriptional level |CITS: [10775270][17615238]|. 
                     <i>E. coli</i> PmrD is functional as a PhoP/PhoQ - 
                     PmrA/PmrB connector in <i>Salmonella</i>, but does not 
                     function in <i>E. coli</i> |CITS: [21811415]|.
                     The <i>E. coli</i> and <i>Salmonella</i> PmrD proteins have
                     functionally diverged.  In <i>E. coli</i>, PmrD is produced
                     under conditions of low Mg<sup>2+</sup> concentration in a 
                     PhoP-dependent manner; however, unlike in 
                     <i>Salmonella</i>, PmrD does not activate the PmrA-PmrB 
                     two-component system (known as |FRAME: PWY0-1482 ""BasSR""|
                     in <i>E. coli</i> K-12) |CITS: [15569938]|. This may 
                     explain why <i>E. coli</i> is unable to modify its LPS to 
                     become resistant to polymyxin B in medium containing low 
                     concentrations of Mg<sup>2+</sup>, such as LB |CITS: 
                     [10373459]|.  In addition, PmrA does not repress 
                     transcription of <i>E. coli pmrD</i> |CITS: [15569938]|. 
                     Nevertheless, a recent study showed that <i>pmrD</i> 
                     expression was partially reduced in a <i>phoP phoQ</i> 
                     double mutant and <i>phoP phoQ pmrA</i> and <i>phoP phoQ 
                     pmrB</i> triple mutants. Furthermore the <i>pmrD</i> gene 
                     is important to the expression of the PmrA regulon genes, 
                     since the expression levels of <i>prmA</i> decreased 
                     significantly in a <i>pmrD</i> mutant strain compared with 
                     a wild-type strain, indicating that <i>pmrD</i> plays an 
                     important role in the survival of cells exposed to 
                     polymyxin B under growth conditions with low 
                     Mg<sup>2+</sup> concentrations |CITS: [25605366]|.
                     A solution structure of PmrD has been solved |CITS: 
                     [17686460]|, and molecular dynamics simulations suggest 
                     that a leucine-rich cluster stabilizes the protein |CITS: 
                     [19428472]|.  A crystal structure of PmrD has been solved 
                     at 2 &Aring; resolution, showing an intramolecular 
                     disulfide bond between Cys9 and Cys81 that might contribute
                     to stabilization of the &alpha; helix |CITS: [25480013]|.
                     PmrD: ""<b>p</b>oly<b>m</b>yxin <b>r</b>esistance"" Review:
                     |CITS: [15691651]|"
                     /translation="MEWLVKKSCCNKQDNRHVLMLCDAGGAIKMIAEVKSDFAVKVGDL
