     gene            complement(2370313..2371071)
                     /gene="menH"
                     /locus_tag="b2263"
                     /label=menH
     CDS             complement(2370313..2371071)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="menH"
                     /locus_tag="b2263"
                     /product="bifunctional 
                     2-succinyl-6-hydroxy-2,4-cyclohexadiene-1-carboxylate 
                     synthase / (1R,6R)-2-succinyl-6-hydroxy-2,4-cyclohexadiene 
                     -1-carboxylate synthase"
                     /EC_number="4.2.99.20"
                     /label=menH
                     /note="MenH catalyzes the third step in the menaquinone 
                     biosynthesis pathway, a proton abstraction reaction that 
                     results in 2,5-elimination of pyruvate from |FRAME: 
                     CPD-9924| and the formation of |FRAME: CPD-9923| |CITS: 
                     [18284213]|.  SHCHC synthase activity was first detected in
                     crude extracts |CITS: [17760421]|.
                     Structural modelling and site-directed mutagenesis allowed 
                     identification of active site residues |CITS: 
                     [18284213][19545176]|.  Crystal structures of the wild type
                     protein and two active site mutants have been solved |CITS:
                     [23637813]|.
                     MenH was initially suggested to catalyze a thioesterase 
                     step in the menaquinone biosynthetic pathway |CITS: 
                     [11153266]|.  However, the purified protein lacks 
                     thioesterase activity, but has efficient SHCHC synthase 
                     activity |CITS: [18284213][19545176]|.  Conflicting with 
                     this result, esterase activity of MenH with palmitoyl-CoA 
                     as the substrate was discovered in a high-throughput screen
                     of purified proteins |CITS: [15808744]|."
