     gene            complement(2374201..2374506)
                     /gene="elaB"
                     /locus_tag="b2266"
                     /label=elaB
     CDS             complement(2374201..2374506)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="elaB"
                     /locus_tag="b2266"
                     /product="tail-anchored inner membrane protein ElaB"
                     /label=elaB
                     /note="ElaB is a C-tail anchored inner membrane protein
                     that is implicated in various stress reponses; deletion of 
                     <i>elaB</i> reduces cell survival under heat and oxidative 
                     stress; deletion of <i>elaB</i> also increases persister 
                     cell formation |CITS: [28242719]|.
                     Overexpressed ElaB is present in the ribosome fraction 
                     |CITS: [22661687]|.
                     ElaB is predicted to be a bitopic inner membrane protein 
                     |CITS: [27510400]|. An ElaB-YFP fusion protein localizes 
                     mainly at the cell poles; the tail anchor domain of ElaB 
                     localizes to regions enriched in phosphatidic acid |CITS: 
                     [34644400]|.
                     <i>elaB</i> is a member of the RpoS regulon; transcription 
                     is induced during stationary phase and when cells are grown
                     in nutrient limited minimal medium |CITS: [28242719]|. 
                     |FRAME: EG11447-MONOMER CsrA| regulates <i>elaB</i> 
                     expression both transcriptionally and 
                     post-transcriptionally; CsrA mediates the direct 
                     translational repression of <i>elaB</i> during exponential 
                     growth |CITS: [37943032]|.
                     ElaB, |FRAME: G7612-MONOMER ""YqjD""| and |FRAME: 
                     B0899-MONOMER ""YgaM""| are paralogs |CITS: [22661687]|; 
                     ElaB, YqjD and YgaM contain similar C-terminal 
                     transmembrane domains |CITS: [28242719]|; <i>E. coli</i> 
                     K-12 contains 11 chromosomally encoded C-tail anchored 
                     proteins |CITS: [20406421]|. ElaB, YqjD, and YgaM are 
                     ribosome associated factors implicated in stress-associated
                     translation modulation (see |CITS: [30476446]|)"
                     /translation="MSNQFGDTRIDDDLTLLSETLEEVLRSSGDPADQKYVELKARAEK
