     gene            complement(2388821..2389375)
                     /gene="nuoJ"
                     /locus_tag="b2280"
                     /label=nuoJ
     CDS             complement(2388821..2389375)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="nuoJ"
                     /locus_tag="b2280"
                     /product="multifunctional NADH:quinone oxidoreductase
                     subunit J / NADH:quinone oxidoreductase I / NADH:ubiquinone
                     oxidoreductase (H(+)-transporting) / NADH:menaquinone 
                     oxidoreductase (H(+)-transporting)"
                     /EC_number="7.1.1.2"
                     /label=nuoJ
                     /note="NuoJ is part of the inner membrane component of
                     NADH dehydrogenase I |CITS: [7607227]|.  The protein has 
                     five predicted transmembrane domains; the C terminus is 
                     located in the cytoplasm |CITS: [15919996]|.  A crystal 
                     structure of the membrane component at higher resolution 
                     has allowed better identification of the interactions 
                     between the subunits |CITS: [21822288]|.
                     Point mutations at conserved residues have been analyzed; 
                     mutation of Val65, which is located in the most conserved 
                     transmembrane segment, causes significant reduction of 
                     coupled electron transfer activity |CITS: [15736965]|. 
                     Among other site-directed mutants, a V65G mutation had the 
                     most deleterious effect on growth on malate and on 
                     enzymatic activity |CITS: [17894548]|.
                     In the presence of NADH, crosslinking between NuoA and NuoJ
                     in the intact Complex I is abolished, indicating that the 
                     conformational change involving the hydrophilic subunits in
                     the presence of NADH extends to the membrane domain |CITS: 
                     [18771280]|.
                     The similarity between NDH-1 and the mitochondrial Complex 
                     I has been exploited to study the effects of pathogenic 
                     mutations and polymorphisms found in the human proteins on 
                     enzymatic activity.  A Y59F mutation (analogous to the Y59C
                     mutation in human ND6, which is associated with LHON) in 
                     NuoJ decreases proton translocation |CITS: [25747201]|. 
                     Null mutants of all individual <i>nuo</i> genes have a 
                     growth defect under aerobic conditions in rich medium 
                     |CITS: [22063474]|.
                     <i>nuoJ</i> belongs to a network of genes which facilitate 
                     stress-induced mutagenesis (SIM) in <i>E. coli</i> K-12 
                     |CITS: [23224554]|.
                     NuoJ: ""<b>N</b>ADH:<b>u</b>biquinone 
                     <b>o</b>xidoreductase"" |CITS: [8387992]|"
