     CDS             complement(2389387..2389929)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="nuoI"
                     /locus_tag="b2281"
                     /product="multifunctional NADH:quinone oxidoreductase
                     subunit I / NADH:quinone oxidoreductase I, peripheral arm /
                     NADH:quinone oxidoreductase I / NADH:ubiquinone 
                     oxidoreductase (H(+)-transporting) / NADH:menaquinone 
                     oxidoreductase (H(+)-transporting)"
                     /EC_number="7.1.1.2"
                     /label=nuoI
                     /note="NuoI is part of the connecting fragment of NADH 
                     dehydrogenase I |CITS: [7607227]| and is required for 
                     efficient assembly of NDH-1 |CITS: [22474289]|.  The Fe-S 
                     clusters of NuoI conduct electrons from NuoG to the Fe-S 
                     cluster of NuoB |CITS: [22474289]|.
                     Based on sequence similarity, this subunit was predicted to
                     contain the two 4Fe-4S clusters N6a and N6b |CITS: 
                     [7690854][9593861][11352750]|.  EPR signals for both N6a 
                     and N6b have now been detected |CITS: [22700653]|. Although
                     N6a and N6b are located close to each other, they display 
                     no spin-spin interaction |CITS: [22474289]|.  The location 
                     and identity of EPR spectra for the N4 and N5 Fe-S clusters
                     were subject of some controversy.  The 4Fe-4S cluster N4, 
                     located on the NuoG subunit, was thought to be identical to
                     either N6a or N6b |CITS: [17640900]|.  Recent reevaluation 
                     of the data |CITS: [18486592]| and mutational analysis of 
                     the N5 His(Cys)<sub>3</sub> ligands confirmed the location 
                     of both N4 and N5 in the NuoG subunit |CITS: [18603533]|.
                     In the presence of NADH or reducing agents, crosslinking 
                     between NuoB and NuoI in the intact Complex I is abolished,
                     indicating a conformational change involving the 
                     hydrophilic subunits in the presence of NADH |CITS: 
                     [18771280]|.
                     Point mutants in the cysteine residues predicted to 
                     coordinate the Fe-S clusters and in highly conserved acidic
                     residues have been studied |CITS: [22474289]|.
                     Null mutants of all individual <i>nuo</i> genes have a 
                     growth defect under aerobic conditions in rich medium 
                     |CITS: [22063474]|.
                     NuoI: ""<b>N</b>ADH:<b>u</b>biquinone 
                     <b>o</b>xidoreductase"" |CITS: [8387992]|"
