     gene            complement(2389944..2390921)
                     /gene="nuoH"
                     /locus_tag="b2282"
                     /label=nuoH
     CDS             complement(2389944..2390921)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="nuoH"
                     /locus_tag="b2282"
                     /product="multifunctional NADH:quinone oxidoreductase
                     subunit H / NADH:quinone oxidoreductase I / NADH:ubiquinone
                     oxidoreductase (H(+)-transporting) / NADH:menaquinone 
                     oxidoreductase (H(+)-transporting)"
                     /EC_number="7.1.1.2"
                     /label=nuoH
                     /note="NuoH is part of the inner membrane component of
                     NADH dehydrogenase I |CITS: [7607227]|.  The protein has 
                     eight predicted transmembrane domains; the C terminus is 
                     located in the periplasm |CITS: [15919996]|.
                     This subunit was thought to contain the ubiquinone binding 
                     site |CITS: [7690854][9593861]|, which has since been 
                     proposed to be located in the NuoM subunit |CITS: 
                     [12730198]|.  However, an E36Q mutant shows higher apparent
                     K<sub>m</sub> for ubiquinone, suggesting proximity to the 
                     ubiquinone binding domain |CITS: [22079202]|.  The charged 
                     residues of the cytoplasmic loops are highly conserved; 
                     mutagenesis of these residues results in loss of enzymatic 
                     activity and a low content of the peripheral subunits NuoB 
                     and NuoCD, indicating that the cytoplasmic loops are 
                     essential for assembly of the peripheral arm of NDH-1 
                     |CITS: [19189973]|.
                     The similarity between NDH-1 and the mitochondrial Complex 
                     I has been exploited to study the effects of pathogenic 
                     mutations and polymorphisms found in the human proteins on 
                     enzymatic activity |CITS: [19616643][20197120][25747201]|. 
                     An E36K mutation in NuoH (analogous to an E24K mutation in 
                     the human mitochondrial protein that is associated with the
                     LHON/MELAS disease phenotype) almost completely abolishes 
                     NDH-1 activity |CITS: [22079202]|.  The D213G mutation 
                     (analogous to the D199G mutation in human mitochondrial ND1
                     of a patient) decreases NDH-1 activity |CITS: 
                     [34135385][34026733]|. A triple mutation in residues 
                     199-201, a region associated with a 7 nt inversion 
                     associated with human mitochondrial dysfunction, assembles 
                     stably but shows no enzymatic activity |CITS: [35234296]|.
                     Null mutants of all individual <i>nuo</i> genes have a 
                     growth defect under aerobic conditions in rich medium 
                     |CITS: [22063474]|.
                     <i>nuoH</i> belongs to a network of genes which facilitate 
                     stress-induced mutagenesis (SIM) in <i>E. coli</i> K-12 
                     |CITS: [23224554]|.
                     NuoH: ""<b>N</b>ADH:<b>u</b>biquinone 
                     <b>o</b>xidoreductase"" |CITS: [8387992]|"
