     gene            complement(2395031..2395531)
                     /gene="nuoE"
                     /locus_tag="b2285"
                     /label=nuoE
     CDS             complement(2395031..2395531)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="nuoE"
                     /locus_tag="b2285"
                     /product="multifunctional NADH:quinone oxidoreductase
                     subunit E / NADH:quinone oxidoreductase I, peripheral arm /
                     NADH:quinone oxidoreductase I / NADH:ubiquinone 
                     oxidoreductase (H(+)-transporting) / NADH:menaquinone 
                     oxidoreductase (H(+)-transporting)"
                     /EC_number="7.1.1.2"
                     /label=nuoE
                     /note="NuoE is part of the soluble fragment of NADH 
                     dehydrogenase I (NDH-1), which represents the electron 
                     input part of the enzyme |CITS: [7607227][9485311]|.
                     Based on sequence similarity, this subunit is predicted to 
                     contain the N1a 2Fe-2S cluster |CITS: 
                     [7690854][9593861][15683249][15922336]|.  The location of 
                     the conserved N1a cluster suggests that it does not 
                     participate in electron transfer chain through NDH-1. 
                     Site-directed mutagenesis of the cysteine residues expected
                     to coordinate the N1a cluster resulted in the loss of N1a 
                     and significantly reduced the amount of the N1b cluster 
                     coordinated by the NuoG subunit.  Only the C97A mutant 
                     retained most of the N1a cluster.  The mutants showed 
                     reduced NHD-1 activity, but severely affected the stability
                     of the NDH-1 complex |CITS: [28509551]|.  A V96P/N142M 
                     double mutant switches the N1a cluster from its 
                     high-potential to a low-potential state |CITS: [23980528]|.
                      NDH-1 containing the NuoE G135D mutant is stable, but 
                     loses most NADH oxidase activity; the loss is attributed to
                     the inability to release NAD<sup>+</sup>, i.e. product 
                     inhibition.  The production of reactive oxygen species in 
                     the mutant is significantly reduced |CITS: [31186428]|.
                     Null mutants of all individual <i>nuo</i> genes have a 
                     growth defect under aerobic conditions in rich medium 
                     |CITS: [22063474]|.  In a strain lacking the alternative 
                     NADH dehydrogenase NDH-2, <i>nuoE</i> site-directed mutants
                     showed significantly decreased growth rates |CITS: 
                     [28509551]|.
                     A potential +1 frameshift site was identified 
                     computationally; a fluorescent reporter system confirmed 
                     that frameshifting occurred at approximately 5% efficiency 
                     |CITS: [19783813]|.
                     NuoE: ""<b>N</b>ADH:<b>u</b>biquinone 
                     <b>o</b>xidoreductase"" |CITS: [8387992]|
                     Review: |CITS: [26944855]|"
