     gene            complement(2404918..2405568)
                     /gene="hxpA"
                     /locus_tag="b2293"
                     /label=hxpA
     CDS             complement(2404918..2405568)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="hxpA"
                     /locus_tag="b2293"
                     /product="multifunctional hexitol phosphatase A / 
                     sorbitol-6-phosphatase / mannitol-1-phosphatase / sugar 
                     phosphatase / glycerol-3-phosphatase"
                     /EC_number="3.1.3.50; 3.1.3.22; 3.1.3.23; 3.1.3.21"
                     /label=hxpA
                     /note="The hexitol phosphatase activity of HxpA was
                     discovered in a large-scale metabolomics screen for 
                     enzymatic activities of uncharacterized proteins in <i>E. 
                     coli</i> |CITS: [27941785]|.
                     HxpA is a sugar phosphatase belonging to the superfamily of
                     haloacid dehalogenase (HAD)-like hydrolases. It shows a low
                     level of substrate discrimination among its preferred 
                     substrates, although it does selectively hydrolyze 
                     &beta;-D-glucose-1-phosphate and has no activity with the 
                     &alpha; form |CITS: [16990279]|. Overexpression of 
                     <i>hxpA</i> results in increased glycerol-3-phosphatase 
                     activity in crude extract |CITS: [22353596]|. The 
                     phosphatase activity of HxpA was first discovered in a 
                     high-throughput screen of purified proteins |CITS: 
                     [15808744]|.
                     Phosphatase activity of HxpA is dependent on the presence 
                     of a divalent cation such as Mg<sup>2+</sup>, which appears
                     to affect substrate binding |CITS: [16990279]|. HpxA 
                     coexpressed with the D-tagatose 6-phosphate 4-epimerases 
                     |FRAME: G7128-MONOMER GatZ| or |FRAME: G7631-MONOMER| 
                     enables the production of D-tagatose, indicating that HpxA 
                     carries out the final dephosphorylation of D-tagatose 
                     6-phosphate |CITS: [39999377]|.
                     HxpA: ""<b>h</b>e<b>x</b>itol <b>p</b>hosphatase <b>A</b>""
                     |CITS: [27941785]|"
