                     carboxylase complex"
                     /EC_number="2.1.3.15"
                     /label=accD
                     /note="The Zn<sup>2+</sup>-binding domain of AccD is
                     required both for catalytic activity and for binding to 
                     mRNA |CITS: [19965770]|.
                     Transcription of <i>accD</i> is growth rate-regulated 
                     |CITS: [7678242]|.
                     A temperature-sensitive mutation in this gene was 
                     identified that showed potential as a growth-switch for 
                     genetic engineering |CITS: [37642940]|.
                     A lesson in gene naming:<BR>DedB: ""<b>d</b>ownstream 
                     <i><b>E</b>. coli</i> <b>D</b>NA (from <i>hisT</i>)"" 
                     |CITS: [3040734]|<BR>Usg: ""<b>u</b>p<b>s</b>tream 
                     <b>g</b>ene"" |CITS: [3040739]|<BR>AccD: 
                     ""<b>a</b>cetyl-<b>C</b>oA <b>c</b>arboxylase <b>D</b>"" 
                     |CITS: [1355086]|"
