     gene            complement(2428303..2429115)
                     /gene="truA"
                     /locus_tag="b2318"
                     /label=truA
     CDS             complement(2428303..2429115)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="truA"
                     /locus_tag="b2318"
                     /product="tRNA pseudouridine(38-40) synthase"
                     /EC_number="5.4.99.12"
                     /label=truA
                     /note="TruA is the tRNA pseudouridine synthase responsible
                     for catalyzing pseudouridine formation in the anticodon 
                     loop of a subset of tRNAs |CITS: [3276686]|.
                     TruA-mediated pseudouridylation contributes to structural 
                     stability of this region of the tRNA |CITS: [2021615]| and 
                     to reading frame maintenance by tRNA<sup>Leu</sup> |CITS: 
                     [11532950]|.
                     Results from site-directed mutagenesis indicate that the 
                     reaction mechanism likely does not involve a covalent 
                     cysteine intermediate |CITS: [8999885]|.  Instead, the D60 
                     residue is essential for catalytic activity |CITS: 
                     [9425056]|, forming a covalent adduct that can undergo 
                     <i>O</i>-acyl hydrolytic cleavage to form the pseudouridine
                     product |CITS: [10588695]|.  The Arg58 residue facilitates 
                     flipping of the substrate base into the active site |CITS: 
                     [17466622]|.
                     Pre-steady-state kinetic analysis showed that catalysis, 
                     but not substrate binding, is the rate-limiting step |CITS:
                     [21998096]|.
                     Crystal structures of the enzyme have been solved |CITS: 
                     [10625422][17466622]|.  TruA is a dimer in the crystal as 
                     well as in solution |CITS: [10625422]|.  Modeling of the 
                     substrate recognition pathway indicates that the enzyme 
                     utilizes the intrinsic flexibility of the tRNA anticodon 
                     loop |CITS: [17466622]|.
                     A <i>truA</i> mutant exhibits a tRNA pseudouridine synthase
                     defect |CITS: [323237]| and increased translation errors 
                     under conditions of low histidine |CITS: [6757659]|.  A 
                     mutant exhibits a growth defect that is rescued by addition
                     of adenine, uracil, and isoleucine to the growth medium 
                     |CITS: [323237]|.  A <i>truA</i> insertion mutant has a 
                     severe growth defect in minimal medium which can be rescued
                     by addition of uracil |CITS: [1938930]|.  In a large-scale 
                     TraDIS screen, <i>truA</i> was found to be essential in 
                     late-stage biofilms |CITS: [34783647]|.
                     <i>truA</i> is encoded in an operon downstream of 
                     <i>usg</i>, a gene of unknown function |CITS: 
                     [2991861][3029016]|.  Expression of <i>truA</i> is growth 
                     rate-regulated and increases in stationary phase |CITS: 
                     [1938930]|.
                     AsuC: ""<b>a</b>nti<b>su</b>ppressor"" |CITS: 
                     [3918006]|<br>TruA: ""<b>tR</b>NA pseudo<b>u</b>ridine 
                     formation <b>A</b>"" |CITS: [7489483]|
                     Reviews: |CITS: [17113994][17085441][25616362][40210524]|"
