                     /locus_tag="b2326"
                     /product="EF-P-Lys34 hydroxylase"
                     /label=epmC
                     /note="EpmC catalyzes the hydroxylation of the &gamma;
                     (C4) or &delta; (C5) position of Lys34 in |FRAME: 
                     EG12099-MONOMER|.  The 5-hydroxyllysine form of EF-P 
                     appears to be present <i>in vivo</i>.  EpmC is the final 
                     enzyme in the pathway generating the fully modified Lys34 
                     residue |CITS: [22706199]|.
                     A crystal structure of EpmC has been solved at 1.45&Aring; 
                     resolution |CITS: [25195899][25274739]|.  A 
                     metal-coordinating 2-His-1-carboxylate motif similar to 
                     that of non-heme iron enzymes forms the catalytic site .
                     A catalytic mechanism has been proposed |CITS: [25274739]|.
                     EpmC: ""<b>E</b>F-P <b>p</b>ost-translational 
                     <b>m</b>odification <b>C</b>"" |CITS: [22706199]|"
                     /translation="MNSTHHYEQLIEIFNSCFADDFNTRLIKGDDEPIYLPADAEVPYN
