                     /product="bifunctional ribosomal protein L3 N(5)-glutamine 
                     methyltransferase / protein-glutamine N-methyltransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.1.1.298"
                     /label=prmB
                     /note="PrmB is an N<sup>5</sup>-glutamine
                     methyltransferase that specifically methylates |FRAME: 
                     EG10866-MONOMER ribosomal protein L3| |CITS: 
                     [331083][11847124]|.
                     PrmB and PrmC have sequence similarity to each other; PrmB 
                     is active toward ribosomal protein L3, whereas PrmC is 
                     active toward polypeptide chain release factors RF1 and RF2
                     |CITS: [11847124]|.
                     A <i>prmB</i> mutant lacks methylation of L3, has a 
                     cold-sensitive growth phenotype and accumulates abnormal 
                     ribosomal particles, indicating a defect in ribosome 
                     assembly |CITS: [372746][6173216][11847124]|.
                     PrmB: ""<b>pr</b>otein <b>m</b>ethylation <b>B</b>"" |CITS:
                     [372746]|"
