     gene            complement(2443530..2444069)
                     /gene="yfcP"
                     /locus_tag="b2333"
                     /label=yfcP
     CDS             complement(2443530..2444069)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yfcP"
                     /locus_tag="b2333"
                     /product="putative fimbrial protein YfcP"
                     /label=yfcP
                     /note="<i>yfcOPQRSTUV</i> is a putative chaperone-usher
                     fimbrial operon |CITS: [20345943]|. The operon is cryptic 
                     under normal laboratory conditions but when constitutive 
                     expression is induced in a strain that lacks the type 1 
                     fimbrial complex the <i>yfc</i> operon promotes adhesion to
                     eukaryotic epithelial cells (T<sub>4</sub> bladder cells) 
                     |CITS: [20345943]|. Expression of the <i>yfc</i> operon is 
                     regulated by the global regulators |FRAME: PD00288 
                     ""H-NS""| and |FRAME: CPLX0-226 ""CRP cAMP""| |CITS: 
                     [20345943]|.
                     <i>E. coli</i> K-12 contains 12 chaperone-usher fimbrial 
                     operons, including <i>yfcOPQRSTUV</i>; a fimbria-lacking 
                     mutant - strain WQM026 - created by deleting all 12 operons
                     has been characterised |CITS: [33863704]|."
