                     /product="putative fimbrial chaperone YfcS"
                     /label=yfcS
                     /note="<i>yfcOPQRSTUV</i> is a putative chaperone-usher
                     fimbrial operon; <i>yfcS</i> is predicted to encode a 
                     fimbrial chaperone |CITS: [12192075][20345943]|. The operon
                     is cryptic under normal laboratory conditions but when 
                     constitutive expression is induced in a strain that lacks 
                     the type 1 fimbrial complex the <i>yfc</i> operon promotes 
                     adhesion to eukaryotic epithelial cells (T<sub>4</sub> 
                     bladder cells) |CITS: [20345943]|. Expression of the 
                     <i>yfc</i> operon is regulated by the global regulators 
                     |FRAME: PD00288 ""H-NS""| and |FRAME: CPLX0-226 ""CRP 
                     cAMP""| |CITS: [20345943]|.
                     <i>E. coli</i> K-12 contains 12 chaperone-usher fimbrial 
                     operons, including <i>yfcOPQRSTUV</i>; a fimbria-lacking 
                     mutant - strain WQM026 - created by deleting all 12 operons
                     has been characterised |CITS: [33863704]|.
                     "
