                     /product="putative outer membrane usher protein YfcU"
                     /label=yfcU
                     /note="Sequence analysis indicates that the b2337 gene 
                     (<i>yfcT</i>) and the b2338 gene (<i>yfcU</i>) are two 
                     parts of a putative fimbrial usher protein interrupted by a
                     stop codon. The <i>yfcTU</i> genes are found in a predicted
                     operon with other putative fimbrial genes and have sequence
                     similarity with fimbrial usher proteins |CITS: [20345943]|.
                     <i>yfcOPQRSTUV</i> is cryptic under normal laboratory 
                     conditions, but when constitutive expression is induced in 
                     a strain that lacks the type 1 fimbrial complex, the 
                     <i>yfc</i> operon promotes adhesion to eukaryotic 
                     epithelial cells (T<sub>4</sub> bladder cells) |CITS: 
                     [20345943]|. Expression of the <i>yfc</i> operon is 
                     regulated by the global regulators |FRAME: PD00288 
                     ""H-NS""| and |FRAME: CPLX0-226 ""CRP cAMP""| |CITS: 
                     [20345943]|.
                     <i>E. coli</i> K-12 contains 12 chaperone-usher fimbrial 
                     operons, including <i>yfcOPQRSTUV</i>; a fimbria-lacking 
                     mutant - strain WQM026 - created by deleting all 12 operons
                     has been characterised |CITS: [33863704]|.
                     "
