                     /gene="intS"
                     /locus_tag="b2349"
                     /product="CPS-53 (KpLE1) prophage; prophage CPS-53
                     integrase"
                     /label=intS
                     /note="IntS is the integrase required for both integration
                     and excision of the prophage KpLE1 |CITS: [17545146]|.  A 
                     narrow concentration range of IntS enables excisive 
                     recombination |CITS: [20949106]|.
                     IntS binds DNA at the KplE1 attachment site <i>attL</i> 
                     |CITS: [17545146]|.  In the presence of their DNA target 
                     sites, IntS oligomers are stabilized |CITS: [20494389]|. 
                     The <i>attL</i> site overlaps with the <i>intS</i> promoter
                     region, thereby enabling negative autoregulation of 
                     <i>intS</i> expression by IntS |CITS: [20949106]|.
                     "
