     gene            2469789..2469989
                     /gene="torI"
                     /locus_tag="b4501"
                     /label=torI
     CDS             2469789..2469989
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="torI"
                     /locus_tag="b4501"
                     /product="CPS-53 (KpLE1) prophage; prophage CPS-53
                     recombination directionality factor and response regulator 
                     inhibitor"
                     /label=torI
                     /note="TorI is the recombination directionality factor
                     (RDF) for KplE1 (or CPS-53) prophage excision.  TorI was 
                     shown to be required for prophage excision <i>in vivo</i> 
                     and <i>in vitro</i> |CITS: [16079126][17545146]|.  DnaJ 
                     interacts with |CITS: [21908845]| and stabilizes |CITS: 
                     [22378785]| TorI and stimulates prophage excision |CITS: 
                     [21908845]|.
                     A solution structure of TorI has been solved.  TorI is a 
                     winged-helix protein that is structurally highly similar to
                     the phage &lambda; Xis protein, the Mu bacteriophage 
                     repressor MuR, and Mu transposase, and may represent the 
                     structural ""missing link"" between &lambda;Xis and MuR. 
                     Conserved residues that are involved in DNA binding have 
                     been identified and confirmed by site-directed mutagenesis 
                     |CITS: [16079126]|.  The binding sites of TorI in the KplE1
                     prophage region have been mapped |CITS: [17545146]|. The 
                     presence of their DNA target sites stabilizes TorI 
                     oligomers |CITS: [20494389]|, and DnaJ stimulates binding 
                     of TorI to the target sites |CITS: [21908845]|.
                     Binding of TorI in the |FRAME: G7218 <i>intS</i>| promoter 
                     region negatively regulates IntS expression |CITS: 
                     [20949106]|.  The TorI protein was initially identified as 
                     a negative regulator of the <i>torCAD</i> operon.  The 
                     effect is dependent on the response regulator TorR.  TorI 
                     binds to the C-terminal effector domain of TorR <i>in 
                     vitro</i>, but does not appear to affect the ability of 
                     TorR to bind to the <i>torR</i> and <i>torC</i> promoters 
                     specifically |CITS: [15197250]|.
                     TorI is 100% identical to the <i>hkaC</i> gene product of 
                     the coliphage HK620 and gene 18 of the <i>Shigella 
                     flexneri</i> phage Sf6 |CITS: [15197250]|.
                     Overexpression of TorI leads to excision of the KplE1 
                     prophage |CITS: [16079126]|.  The termination factor 
                     |FRAME: EG10845-MONOMER Rho| keeps expression of TorI low, 
                     leading to maintenance of the KplE1 prophage |CITS: 
                     [23940369]|.
                     TorI: ""<b>Tor i</b>nhibition"" |CITS: [15197250]|"
