                     /gene="emrY"
                     /locus_tag="b2367"
                     /product="trifunctional tripartite efflux pump membrane
                     subunit EmrY / tripartite efflux pump EmrKY-TolC / 
                     deoxycholate efflux pump"
                     /label=emrY
                     /note="EmrY is the inner membrane subunit of a putative 
                     tripartite efflux pump complex.
                     EmrY is a member of the Drug:H+ Antiporter-2 (14 Spanner) 
                     (DHA2) Family within the Major Facilitator Superfamily 
                     (MFS) |CITS: [8987357][26546518]|. EmrY has 63.3 % sequence
                     identity with the efflux pump protein |FRAME: EMRB-MONOMER 
                     ""EmrB""| |CITS: [12501312]|.
                     <i>emrY</i> was identified in a screen for genes that 
                     reduce the lethal effects of stress; an <i>emrY</i> 
                     insertion mutant is more sensitive than wild type to 
                     mitomycin C and other stresses such as UV irradiation 
                     |CITS: [20128927]|.
                     <i>emrY</i> is one of 35 efflux-encoding genes that have 
                     been deleted or inactivated in 'Efflux KnockOut-35' 
                     (EKO-35) -  a K-12 BW25133-derived strain that lacks 35 
                     efflux pumps and can be used as a platform to study their 
                     function |CITS: [36065018][36318669]|.
                     "
