     gene            complement(2485483..2486733)
                     /gene="frc"
                     /locus_tag="b2374"
                     /label=frc
     CDS             complement(2485483..2486733)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="frc"
                     /locus_tag="b2374"
                     /product="formyl-CoA transferase"
                     /EC_number="2.8.3.16"
                     /label=frc
                     /note="YfdW (Frc) is a formyl-CoA transferase with
                     sequence and structural similarity to Frc from 
                     <i>Oxalobacter
                     formigenes</i>, a strictly anaerobic bacterium found in the
                     mammalian gut |CITS: [12844490][18245280]|.  Unlike the
                     <i>O. formigenes</i> enzyme, the <i>E. coli</i> enzyme 
                     shows high substrate specificity |CITS: [18245280]|. 
                     Crystal structures of apo-YfdW and YfdW with CoA, 
                     acetyl-CoA, or both acetyl-CoA and oxalate have been 
                     solved.
                     YfdW is a homodimer; the ring-shaped monomers are 
                     concatenated like links of a chain
                     |CITS: [12844490][14993676]|.
                     The enzymatic reaction mechanism is predicted by structural
                     similarity to related enzymes; residue D169 is predicted
                     to catalyze the reaction |CITS: [12844490]|.  Biochemical 
                     data indicates that the kinetic mechanism is ordered bi-bi 
                     sequential |CITS: [18245280]|.
                     Frc is required during the adaption phase of an 
                     oxalate-induced acid tolerance response |CITS: [23335415]|.
                      Expression of <i>frc</i> is increased when the EvgAS 
                     two-component regulatory system is overexpressed |CITS: 
                     [12399493]|.
                     "
