     gene            2488177..2488452
                     /gene="ypdI"
                     /locus_tag="b2376"
                     /label=ypdI
     CDS             2488177..2488452
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ypdI"
                     /locus_tag="b2376"
                     /product="colanic acid synthesis putative lipoprotein
                     YpdI"
                     /label=ypdI
                     /note="YpdI is a putative membrane lipoprotein which has
                     been shown to play a role in colonic acid synthesis. 
                     Colanic acid is the main extracellular polysaccharide in 
                     <i>Escherichia coli</i> and its synthesis involves at least
                     two pathways of induction and 20 different genes |CITS: 
                     [8759852]|. Capsular polysaccharide production is effected 
                     by both a two-component signal transduction system, RcsC 
                     and RcsB and a positive transcription regulator, RcsA 
                     |CITS: [10200953]|. YpdI plasmid overexpression was shown 
                     to confer a mucoid colony phenotype to <i>E. coli</i>  
                     |CITS: [15183873]|. Extracts of plasmid-bearing cells were 
                     subjected to SDS-PAGE analysis and an excess of a protein 
                     corresponding to the predicted size of the <i>ypdI</i> gene
                     product was observed |CITS: [15183873]|."
                     /translation="MKVNLILFSLFLLVSIMACNVFAFSISGGGSERSYKETEKTSAMT
