                     /gene="lpxP"
                     /locus_tag="b2378"
                     /product="palmitoleoyl acyltransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.3.1.242"
                     /label=lpxP
                     /note="In wild-type <i>E. coli</i> grown at 12&deg;C,
                     two-thirds of the lipid A molecules contain palmitoleate 
                     instead of laurate |CITS: [11830594]|.  Palmitoleoyl 
                     acyltransferase (LpxP) is the sole enzyme that catalyzes 
                     the incorporation of palmitoleate into lipid A in <i>E. 
                     coli</i> |CITS: [10092655][11830594]|.
                     <i>lpxP</i> expression is induced by cold shock |CITS: 
                     [10092655]|.  An <i>lpxP</i> mutant does not exhibit an 
                     obvious growth defect even when grown at 12&deg;C; however,
                     the mutant is hypersensitive to certain antibiotics at low 
                     temperatures |CITS: [11830594]|.  A triple <i>lpxL lpxM 
                     lpxP</i> mutant lacking all secondary acyl chains of lipid 
                     A grows slowly in minimal medium, but is not viable at 
                     temperatures above 32&deg;C in rich medium |CITS: 
                     [11830595]|.  Overexpression of <i>msbA</i> suppresses the 
                     growth defect of the triple mutant under fast-growing 
                     conditions |CITS: [19346244]|.
                     Reviews: |CITS: [12045108][15052329][15466018][17362200]|"
