     CDS             2494609..2495466
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ypdC"
                     /locus_tag="b2382"
                     /product="putative AraC-type DNA-binding transcriptional
                     regulator YpdC"
                     /label=ypdC
                     /note="YpdC contains a predicted C-terminal AraC-type 
                     DNA-binding domain |CITS: [11361063][23222720] [35880217]|.
                     It was predicted that this protein regulates genes related 
                     to metabolism |CITS: [35880217]|.
                     Upstream of the <i>ypdC</i> gene, a sequence was found that
                     could work as a transcriptional promoter, and the 
                     transcription of the <i>ypdC</i> gene is affected by 
                     conditions that lead to biofilm formation |CITS: 
                     [35880217]|.
                     The YpdC binding landscape was globally mapped in vivo by 
                     standardized ChIP-seq and quantitatively modeled using 
                     BoltzNet, a biophysically informed neural network that 
                     infers binding energy from sequence data |CITS:[40335485]|.
                     The resulting ChIP-seq binding regions are available in 
                     RegulonDB (<a href=""https://regulondb.cc 
                     g.unam.mx/ht/dataset/TFBINDING/source=GALAGAN"">Galagan 
                     collection</a>), and the corresponding energy matrix and 
                     genomic binding profiles can be accessed at <a 
                     href=""http://boltznet.bu.edu"">boltznet.bu.edu</a> 
                     |CITS:[40335485]|."
