     gene            complement(2504947..2506185)
                     /gene="mntH"
                     /locus_tag="b2392"
                     /label=mntH
     CDS             complement(2504947..2506185)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="mntH"
                     /locus_tag="b2392"
                     /product="bifunctional Mn(2+):H(+) symporter / Mn(2+):H(+) 
                     symporter"
                     /label=mntH
                     /note="Early studies indicated that <i>E. coli</i> is able
                     to accumulate manganese by means of a highly-specific 
                     active transport system |CITS: [16559107][16559108]|. 
                     <i>mntH</i> encodes a proton-dependent divalent metal ion 
                     transporter with a marked preference for Mn<sup>2+</sup>; 
                     MntH does transport ferrous iron but this is not expected 
                     to be physiologically relevant; Cd<sup>2+</sup> is an 
                     alternative, non-physiological substrate |CITS: 
                     [10844693][10712688]|.
                     &Delta;<i>mntH</i> cells grow normally, but their manganese
                     content is minimal and activity of the manganese-dependent 
                     superoxide dismutase |FRAME: SUPEROX-DISMUTMN-CPLX SodA| is
                     virtually absent; manganese import is essential in 
                     H<sub>2</sub>O<sub>2</sub>-stressed cells; manganese is not
                     an efficient scavenger of reactive oxygen species; 
                     manganese may substitute for iron in some metalloenzymes 
                     making them less vulnerable to to oxidative damage |CITS: 
                     [19400769]|. Manganese import protects |FRAME: 
                     RIBULP3EPIM-MONOMER| from irreversible damage during 
                     H<sub>2</sub>O<sub>2</sub> stress |CITS: [21402925]|. 
                     MntH-mediated manganese import facilitates the recovery of 
                     DNA replication after H<sub>2</sub>O<sub>2</sub> exposure; 
                     accumulation of intracellular manganese increases cell 
                     survival to acute oxidative stress |CITS: [37493920]| (see 
                     also |CITS: [31570529][33591320]|).
                     In the Transporter Classification Database |CITS: 
                     [33170213]|, MntH is a member of the Metal Ion 
                     (Mn<sup>2+</sup>-iron) transporter (Nramp) family. 
                     <i>mntH</i>: manganese transport system |CITS: [10712688]|;
                     <U>H</U><sup>+</sup>-stimulated <U>m</U>a<U>n</U>ganese 
                     <U>t</U>ransport |CITS: [10844693]|
                     Reviews: |CITS: [12829271]|"
