     gene            2506521..2507723
                     /gene="nupC"
                     /locus_tag="b2393"
                     /label=nupC
     CDS             2506521..2507723
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="nupC"
                     /locus_tag="b2393"
                     /product="bifunctional nucleoside:H(+) symporter NupC / 
                     nucleoside:H(+) symporter"
                     /label=nupC
                     /note="Early studies in <i>E. coli</i> K-12 reported the 
                     presence of two different nucleoside transport systems, one
                     of which (<i>cru/nupC</i>) transports pyrimidine and 
                     adenine nucleosides and is inhibited by the nucleoside 
                     antibiotic showdomycin, and the other (<i>gru/|FRAME: 
                     NUPG-MONOMER nupG</i>|) which transports all nucleosides 
                     and is not affected by showdomycin |CITS: 
                     [4354132][827549]|.
                     NupC mediates proton-dependent uptake of the nucleosides, 
                     (deoxy)cytidine, thymidine, uridine and (deoxy)adenosine 
                     but does not transport guanosine; it is also able to 
                     transport inosine and the nucleoside drugs 
                     3'-azido-3'-deoxythymidine (AZT) and 5'-azacytidine |CITS: 
                     [374403][14668133][8022285]|. Structural motifs important 
                     for ligand binding to NupC and NupG have been investigated 
                     |CITS: [15678184]|. Under conditions of envelope stress, 
                     NupC mediates uptake of ADP-glucose in a cAMP/CRP-regulated
                     process |CITS: [30341391]|.
                     In the Transporter Classification Database |CITS: 
                     [33170213]| NupC is a member of the Concentrative 
                     Nucleoside Transporter (CNT) family.
                     <i>nup</i>: <U>n</U>ucleoside <U>up</U>take"
