     CDS             2507810..2508922
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="insL3"
                     /locus_tag="b2394"
                     /product="putative IS186/IS421 transposase"
                     /label=insL3
                     /note="IS186 is an insertion sequence element that appears
                     three times in a typical <i>E. coli</i> genome.
                     IS186 is an insertion sequence element with an apparent 
                     preference for GC-rich sequences |CITS: 
                     [2997142][2996940]|.
                     As a consequence, it can insert at the tail end of cDNA 
                     clones |CITS: [2996940]|. At the DNA level,
                     the various IS186 genes have terminal inverted repeats and 
                     produce variable-length DNA duplications at the insertion 
                     site (10,
                     12 or 13 bp) |CITS: [2997142][2996940]|.
                     "
