     gene            complement(2537191..2537982)
                     /gene="ucpA"
                     /locus_tag="b2426"
                     /label=ucpA
     CDS             complement(2537191..2537982)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ucpA"
                     /locus_tag="b2426"
                     /product="bifunctional oxidoreductase UcpA / diacetyl
                     reductase"
                     /EC_number="1.1.1.304"
                     /label=ucpA
                     /note="Based on sequence similarity, UcpA was predicted to
                     be an acetoin dehydrogenase (diacetyl reductase) |CITS: 
                     [12952533]|.  Recent data show that UcpA is in fact able to
                     reduce diacetyl to acetoin |CITS: [27931827]|.  A range of 
                     potential substrates, including diacetyl and acetoin, was 
                     previously tested in cell extracts of a strain 
                     overexpressing UcpA, and no increased activity compared to 
                     control extracts was found |CITS: [22267665]|.
                     Crp, FruR and IHF are involved in the regulation of 
                     <i>ucpA</i> |CITS: [9241368]|.  Expression of <i>ucpA</i> 
                     is upregulated by furfural, and overexpression of 
                     <i>ucpA</i> increases furan tolerance in an engineered 
                     <i>E. coli</i> strain and in the wild-type <i>E. coli</i> W
                     strain |CITS: [22267665][23431191]|.
                     A knockout mutation of <i>ucpA</i> negatively affected 
                     conjugation efficiency after 24-48 hrs; UcpA's putative 
                     role in fermentation may help restore intracellular pH thus
                     improving conjugation efficiency |CITS: [35336183]|. UcpA: 
                     ""<b>u</b>pstream of <b>c</b>ys<b>P</b>"" |CITS: [9241368]|
                     "
