     gene            2539132..2540028
                     /gene="murQ"
                     /locus_tag="b2428"
                     /label=murQ
     CDS             2539132..2540028
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="murQ"
                     /locus_tag="b2428"
                     /product="N-acetylmuramic acid 6-phosphate etherase"
                     /EC_number="4.2.1.126"
                     /label=murQ
                     /note="MurQ catalyzes the cleavage of the lactyl ether
                     moiety of <i>N</i>-acetylmuramic acid 6-phosphate 
                     (MurNAc-6-P), acting in one of the pathways that recycle 
                     murein components |CITS: [15983044]|.  MurQ is
                     the only MurNAc-6-P etherase in <i>E. coli</i> |CITS: 
                     [16452451]|.
                     A reaction mechanism involving &beta;-elimination/hydration
                     has been proposed |CITS: [15983044]|.
                     Further studies support a mechanism involving <i>syn</i> 
                     elimination of lactate followed by <i>syn</i>
                     addition of water.  Structural modelling and site-directed 
                     mutagenesis implicated the Glu83 and Glu114
                     residues in catalysis and suggested that Glu83 is required 
                     for protonation of the departing lactate
                     |CITS: [18837509]|.
                     A <i>murQ</i> null mutant strain that is non-polar on 
                     <i>murP</i> can not grow on <i>N</i>-acetylmuramic
                     acid as the sole source of carbon and energy.  When grown 
                     on other carbon sources, a <i>murQ</i> null
                     mutant accumulates MurNAc 6-phosphate |CITS: [15983044]|. 
                     Review: |CITS: [18535144]|"
