                     /product="trifunctional N-acetylmuramic acid-specific PTS
                     enzyme IICB component / anhydro-N-acetylmuramic acid 
                     transporter / anhydro-N-acetylmuramic acid permease / 
                     N-acetylmuramic acid-specific PTS enzyme II"
                     /EC_number="2.7.1.192"
                     /label=murP
                     /note="<i>murP</i> encodes the permease component of the 
                     <i>N</i>-acetylmuramic acid PTS transport system. MurP 
                     contains PTS Enzyme IIB and IIC domains |CITS: [15060041]|.
                     MurP is required for the uptake of anhydrous 
                     N-acetylmuramic (anhMurNAc) acid from the medium. MurP 
                     transports but does not phosphorylate anhMurNAc. The 
                     <i>anmK</i> encoded |FRAME: G6880-MONOMER 
                     ""anhydro-N-acetylmuramic acid kinase""| is required to 
                     convert imported anhMurNAc to MurNAc-P. <i>E. coli</i> K-12
                     cannot use anhMurNAc as the sole source of carbon |CITS: 
                     [15901686][16452451]|."
