                     /gene="eutH"
                     /locus_tag="b2452"
                     /product="putative ethanolamine permease EutH"
                     /label=eutH
                     /note="Sequence analysis has identified EutH as a membrane 
                     protein |CITS: [7868611]| with 11 transmembrane helices 
                     |CITS: [10464203]|.  A possible ethanolamine transport 
                     function for EutH has been suggested |CITS: [7868611]|. 
                     Although it was initially found that a <i>eutH</i> mutant 
                     in <i>Salmonella enterica</i> is not defective for 
                     ethanolamine utilization |CITS: [10464203]|, further 
                     studies showed a pH-dependent effect, and it is now thought
                     that EutH facilitates diffusion of protonated ethanolamine 
                     across the cytoplasmic membrane |CITS: [15466042]|."
