     CDS             complement(2565122..2565409)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="eutN"
                     /locus_tag="b2456"
                     /product="putative ethanolamine catabolic microcompartment
                     shell protein EutN"
                     /label=eutN
                     /note="Several genes of the <i>eut</i> operon are involved
                     in the ability to utilize ethanolamine as the sole source 
                     of carbon and nitrogen in <i>Salmonella typhimurium</i>; 
                     the operon is conserved between <i>Salmonella</i> and <i>E.
                     coli</i>.  EutN has not been shown to be involved in 
                     ethanolamine utilization in either <i>Salmonella</i> or 
                     <i>E. coli</i> |CITS: [10464203]|.  EutN is similar to the 
                     carboxysomal shell protein CcmL of <i>Synechococcus</i> sp.
                     strain PCC7942 |CITS: [8491708][10464203]|.
                     A crystal structure of EutN has been solved at 2.4 &Aring; 
                     resolution.  The protein forms a tight hexamer with a 
                     central hole that is predominantly covered by acidic 
                     residues, suggesting a pore with a transport function 
                     |CITS: [17588214]|.
                     EutN: ""<b>e</b>thanolamine <b>ut</b>ilization""
                     CchB: ""<b>c</b>arbon dioxide <b>c</b>oncentration 
                     <b>h</b>omolog <b>B</b>"" |CITS: [7868611]|"
