     gene            2572025..2572975
                     /gene="talA"
                     /locus_tag="b2464"
                     /label=talA
     CDS             2572025..2572975
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="talA"
                     /locus_tag="b2464"
                     /product="bifunctional transaldolase A / transaldolase"
                     /EC_number="2.2.1.2"
                     /label=talA
                     /note="Transaldolase is an enzyme of the pentose phosphate 
                     pathway, where it catalyzes the reversible interconversion 
                     of glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate and sedoheptulose-7-phosphate
                     to fructose-6-phosphate and erythrose-4-phosphate.  The 
                     reversibility of this reaction and carbon flux through the 
                     pentose phosphate pathway has been addressed both 
                     experimentally (summarized in |CITS: [6049456]|) and 
                     theoretically |CITS: [6049456][9546650][16176270]|.
                     There are two closely related transaldolases in <i>E. 
                     coli</i>, encoded by <i>talA</i> and <i>talB</i>. 
                     Transaldolase A has not been biochemically characterized. 
                     Under aerobic growth conditions with glucose as the sole 
                     source of carbon, a <i>talA</i> mutant shows a similar 
                     growth rate, but a decreased acetate production and 
                     increased biomass yield compared to wild type |CITS: 
                     [18213409]|.  A <i>talA</i> mutant is more sensitive to 
                     gentamicin than wild-type |CITS: [25070093]|.
                     Protein levels of TalA are induced by osmotic stress only 
                     under aerobic conditions |CITS: [17015655]| and by exposure
                     to mercury |CITS: [23771180]|.  <i>talA</i> belongs to the 
                     &sigma;<sup>S</sup> regulon |CITS: [15716429]|; its 
                     expression increases in early stationary phase just as 
                     expression of <i>talB</i> decreases |CITS: [18175070]|.  
                     Expression is negatively regulated by ArcA |CITS: 
                     [15699038]| and positively regulated by ppGpp |CITS: 
                     [18532980]|.  Transcription of <i>talA</i> is induced by 
                     the CreBC two-component system in minimal media growth 
                     conditions |CITS: [11350954]|.
                     TalA: ""<b>t</b>rans<b>al</b>dolase <b>A</b>"" |CITS: 
                     [8396116]|
                     Reviews: |CITS: [8572885][19401148]|"
