     gene            complement(2576905..2578884)
                     /gene="aegA"
                     /locus_tag="b2468"
                     /label=aegA
     CDS             complement(2576905..2578884)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="aegA"
                     /locus_tag="b2468"
                     /product="putative oxidoreductase AegA"
                     /label=aegA
                     /note="Under anaerobic and microaerobic conditions, <i>E. 
                     coli</i> is able to utilize urate as its sole source of 
                     nitrogen.  AegA or YgfT play a role in the 
                     formate-dependent catabolism of urate |CITS: [30885932]|. 
                     AegA contains an N-terminal Fe-S cluster domain and 
                     C-terminal similarity to the GltD subunit of glutamate 
                     synthase |CITS: [8955321]|.
                     An <i>aegA</i> mutant does not have obvious phenotypes with
                     respect to respiration or fermentation and shows no defect 
                     in metabolizing ammonium or various amino acids (L-alanine,
                     L-arginine, L-glutamate, glycine, or DL-serine) as a source
                     of nitrogen, or in use of various sources of carbon |CITS: 
                     [8955321]|.  An <i>aegA ygfT</i> double mutant lacks urate 
                     degradation activity |CITS: [30885932]|.
                     Expression of <i>aegA</i> is regulated by Fnr, NarXL, and 
                     NarQ (but not ArcA) |CITS: [8955321]|, and is induced under
                     anaerobic |CITS: [8955321][30885932]| and microaerobic 
                     conditions |CITS: [30885932]|.  Results differ on whether 
                     expression of <i>aegA</i> under anaerobic conditions is 
                     repressed in the presence of nitrate |CITS: [8955321]|, or 
                     whether there is no effect of nitrate addition; differences
                     may be due to differences in the presence or absence of 
                     regulatory elements |CITS: [30885932]|.
                     AegA: ""<b>a</b>naerobically <b>e</b>xpressed <b>g</b>ene 
                     <b>A</b>"" |CITS: [8955321]|"
