                     /note="Overexpression of <i>ypfN</i> (in 'wild-type'
                     strain MG1655 &Delta;<i>hsdR</i>)  increases ampicillin 
                     resistance; deletion of <i>ypfN</i> increases 
                     susceptibility to ampicillin in the presence of a 
                     &beta;-lactamase expressing plasmid but does not impact 
                     susceptibility to ampicillin in the wild-type |CITS: 
                     [40231449]|. <i>ypfN</i> is highly conserved in <i>E. 
                     coli</i> |CITS: [40231449]|."
