     gene            2593837..2594307
                     /gene="bcp"
                     /locus_tag="b2480"
                     /label=bcp
     CDS             2593837..2594307
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="bcp"
                     /locus_tag="b2480"
                     /product="thiol peroxidase"
                     /EC_number="1.11.1.24"
                     /label=bcp
                     /note="Bcp is a |FRAME: RED-THIOREDOXIN-MONOMER|-dependent
                     thiol peroxidase that belongs to the family of atypical 
                     2-Cys peroxidases |CITS: [19298085]|.  The enzyme can 
                     utilize a variety of peroxides and reducing substrates, 
                     including Trx1, Trx2, Grx1, and Grx3.  The redox potential 
                     of Bcp is very high, at -145.9 mV |CITS: [21910476]|.
                     The reaction mechanism has been investigated.  Utilizing an
                     atypical two-cysteine peroxiredoxin pathway, a sulfenic 
                     acid is transiently formed on Cys45, followed by formation 
                     of an intramolecular disulfide bond between Cys45 and 
                     Cys50.  This oxidized form of Bcp is a substrate for 
                     reduction by thioredoxin.  In a C50S mutant, the sulfenic 
                     acid intermediate is resolved by formation of an 
                     intermolecular disulfide bond |CITS: [19298085]|.
                     Both the oxidized and the reduced form of the Bcp protein 
                     is monomeric in solution |CITS: [21910476]|.
                     A Cys45 mutant loses all catalytic activity.  A <i>bcp</i> 
                     insertion mutant grows slower than wild type and is 
                     hypersensitive to peroxides.  Expression of <i>bcp</i> is 
                     induced by oxidative stress |CITS: [10644761]|.
                     Bcp: ""<b>b</b>acterioferritin <b>c</b>omigratory 
                     <b>p</b>rotein"" |CITS: [2016588]|
                     Reviews: |CITS: [12517450][12033427][22609271]|"
                     /translation="MNPLKAGDIAPKFSLPDQDGEQVNLTDFQGQRVLVYFYPKAMTPG
