                     /label=focB
     CDS             2607293..2608141
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="focB"
                     /locus_tag="b2492"
                     /product="bifunctional formate channel FocB / formate
                     channel"
                     /label=focB
                     /note="<I>focB</I> is located in an operon 
                     (<i>hyfABCDEFGHIR-focB</i>) with genes encoding a putative 
                     hydrogenase complex; the FocB protein contains 6 predicted 
                     membrane helices and has 50% sequence identity with the 
                     formate channel |FRAME: CPLX0-7843 ""FocA""|; FocB is 
                     predicted to import formate for use in a formate 
                     hydrogenlyase pathway involving the <i>hyf</i> encoded 
                     hydrogenase |CITS: [9387241]|.
                     FocB activity and the direction of formate translocation is
                     affected by electron donor identity and external pH; in the
                     absence of |FRAME: CPLX0-7843 ""FocA""| and FocB an 
                     unidentifed system serves to transport formate |CITS: 
                     [30247527]|. FocB and FocA are implicated in the 
                     maintenance of ion gradients during fermentation |CITS: 
                     [38307245]|.
                     FocB is a member of the FNT family of formate and nitrite 
                     transporters |CITS: [10082980]|."
