                     /note="A <i>yfgI</i> deletion mutant is more sensitive to
                     the DNA damaging agent nalidixic acid than wild type |CITS:
                     [23308060]|.
                     In a random transposon mutagenesis screen, <i>yfgI</i> was 
                     indentified as a gene whose inactivation is beneficial for 
                     anaerobic hydrogen production from glycerol.  A 
                     &Delta;<i>yfgI</i> mutant strain grows slightly faster than
                     the parent strain under anaerobic conditions |CITS: 
                     [25567513]|."
