     gene            complement(2632022..2632642)
                     /gene="yfgM"
                     /locus_tag="b2513"
                     /label=yfgM
     CDS             complement(2632022..2632642)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yfgM"
                     /locus_tag="b2513"
                     /product="ancillary SecYEG translocon subunit"
                     /label=yfgM
                     /note="YfgM interacts with the SecYEG translocon and may 
                     function within a &beta;-barrel trafficking chaperone 
                     network. Deletion of <i>yfgM</i> further compromises outer 
                     membrane integrity in both <i>&Delta;surA</i> and 
                     <i>&Delta;skp</i> backgrounds |CITS: [24855643]|. Proteomic
                     analysis of <i>E.coli</i> membrane preparations suggests 
                     that YfgM forms a stable complex with the periplasmic 
                     chaperone |FRAME: G6242-MONOMER ""PpiD""|. PpiD co-purifies
                     with his-tagged YfgM |CITS: [21210718]|. YfgM is predicted 
                     to contain an N-terminal transmembrane helix and a large 
                     periplasmic domain |CITS: [21210718]|. YfgM interacts with 
                     RcsB and may have a role in the Rcs-mediated stress 
                     response network |CITS: [26092727]| YfgM is degraded by the
                     ATP-dependent metalloendopeptidase, FtsH; degradation is 
                     most rapid in stationary phase |CITS: [23091052]| and is 
                     not influenced by PpiD or RcsB |CITS: [26092727]|. A 
                     dedicated motif - the YfgM degron - comprising the first 14
                     N-terminal amino acids, directs it to FtsH for proteolysis 
                     |CITS: [26092727]|."
