     gene            complement(2636488..2637642)
                     /gene="rlmN"
                     /locus_tag="b2517"
                     /label=rlmN
     CDS             complement(2636488..2637642)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rlmN"
                     /locus_tag="b2517"
                     /product="trifunctional 23S rRNA m(2)A2503
                     methyltransferase/tRNA m(2)A37 methyltransferase / 23S rRNA
                     m(2)A2503 methyltransferase / tRNA m(2)A37 
                     methyltransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.1.1.192"
                     /label=rlmN
                     /note="RlmN is the methyltransferase responsible for
                     methylation of 23S rRNA at the C2 position of the A2503 
                     nucleotide |CITS: [18025251]|. The enzyme can utilize free 
                     23S rRNA as the substrate, but not the fully assembled 
                     large ribosomal subunit |CITS: [20184321]|. RlmN is also 
                     responsible for methylation of certain tRNAs at the C2 
                     position of A37 |CITS: [22891362]|. RlmN substrates and 
                     modification sites within the substrates have been 
                     determined |CITS: [29782154]|.
                     RlmN belongs to the Cfr/RlmN family of the ""radical SAM"" 
                     superfamily of proteins |CITS: [16225687][20007606]|. The 
                     reaction requires two molecules of SAM, one as the methyl 
                     group donor, and the second as the source of the 
                     5'-deoxyadenosyl radical |CITS: [21368151]|. The cysteine 
                     residues of the 4Fe-4S cluster-binding motif are essential 
                     for activity of RlmN |CITS: [20184321]| and coordinate one 
                     4Fe-4S cluster |CITS: [21916495]|. The reaction proceeds 
                     via a ping-pong mechanism whereby the conserved C355 
                     residue or RlmN is methylated using SAM as a donor in a 
                     typical S<sub>N</sub>2 displacement reaction |CITS: 
                     [21415317]|. S-methylation of C355 requires the presence of
                     the 4Fe-4S cluster, but not the presence of the substrate 
                     |CITS: [21916495]|. A transient covalent linkage between 
                     the methylated C355 and the methyl recipient adenine in the
                     RNA substrate is formed, and C118 is required for its 
                     resolution |CITS: [23088750][24806349]|. Reductive cleavage
                     of a second molecule of SAM generates the 5'-deoxyadenosyl 
                     radical that is required for transfering the methyl residue
                     to the C2 position of A2503 |CITS: [21415317]|.
                     Crystal structures of wild-type and C118A mutant RlmN in 
                     the absence and presence of SAM or the tRNA substrate have 
                     been solved |CITS: [21527678][24806349][27081063]|. The 
                     location of the bound SAM supports the proposed ping-pong 
                     reaction mechanism |CITS: [21527678]|. The crystal 
                     structure of the C118A mutant with the tRNA<sup>Glu</sup> 
                     substrate captures a reaction intermediate where A37 of the
                     tRNA is covalently linked to C355 of RlmN. The anticodon 
                     stem-loop is unfolded, which enables access to the 
                     nucleobase target; RlmN also contacts the sugar-phosphate 
                     backbone of the D-stem-loop and the 3' end of the tRNA 
                     |CITS: [27081063]|. Protein-Protein Interaction (PPI) 
                     networks have been examined with algebraic topology 
                     analysis showing that most interacting proteins with YfgB 
                     (RlmN) are related to the critical cellular processes such 
                     as protein translation |CITS: [35560988]|.
                     Probing the specificity of RlmN for the C2 position of 
                     adenosine showed that even small changes in the RlmN 
                     sequence towards that of Cfr (which methylates the C8 
                     position) result in loss of enzymatic activity |CITS: 
                     [26700482]|.
                     In an <i>rlmN</i> null mutant strain, 23S rRNA A2503 and 
                     tRNA A37 are not C2-methylated |CITS: 
                     [18025251][22891362]|. Although the null mutant alone does 
                     not show any obvious growth defect, it is outcompeted by 
                     wild type in a growth competition experiment |CITS: 
                     [18025251]|. <i>rlmN</i> inactivation increases UAG 
                     readthrough levels and thus leads to an error-prone 
                     translation phenotype, most likely due to the loss of A2503
                     methylation of 23S rRNA |CITS: [19402753][22891362]|. An 
                     <i>rlmN</i> null mutant shows slightly increased 
                     susceptibility to certain peptidyl transferase-targeting 
                     antibiotics |CITS: [18025251][18554609]|. A knockout of 
                     <i>rlmN</i> in combination with <i>rluE</i> was viable at 
                     both 37 and 20 &deg;C but resulted in large defects on 
                     ribosome assembly and peptidyl transferase activity at 20 
                     &deg;C |CITS: [35260421]|.
                     A study that used a &Delta;10 ribosomal modification 
                     deletion strain lacking nucleoside modifications around the
                     peptidyl-transferase center (PTC) due to deletions of 
                     |FRAME: EG11118|, |FRAME: G6488|, |FRAME: EG12401|, |FRAME:
                     EG11794|, |FRAME: G6581|, |FRAME: EG12433|, |FRAME: 
                     EG11921|, |FRAME: G7845|, |FRAME: G6746| and |FRAME: 
                     EG11507| found that RlmE is the most effective at 
                     alleviating the severe growth defect phenotype of the 
                     &Delta;10 strain and that RlmN's methylation activity of 
                     A2503 can partially complement the RlmE-containing mutant 
                     with respect to large ribosomal subunit assembly in late 
                     exponential phase cultures as determined by sucrose 
                     gradient ribosome profile assay |CITS: [38554109]|.
                     RlmN: ""<b>r</b>RNA <b>l</b>arge subunit 
                     <b>m</b>ethyltransferase <b>N</b>"" |CITS: [18025251]| 
                     Reviews: |CITS: 
                     [27375676][25009947][22097883][21527702][40210524]|"
