     gene            complement(2649895..2650095)
                     /gene="iscX"
                     /locus_tag="b2524"
                     /label=iscX
     CDS             complement(2649895..2650095)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="iscX"
                     /locus_tag="b2524"
                     /product="accessory [Fe-S] cluster assembly protein IscX"
                     /label=iscX
                     /note="IscX appears to act as a regulator of iron-sulfur
                     cluster assembly.  IscX physically interacts with |FRAME: 
                     CPLX0-248 IscS| |CITS: [11983079]| and |FRAME: 
                     G7324-MONOMER IscU| |CITS: [24810328]|.  It was suggested 
                     that IscX functions as a molecular adaptor that is able to 
                     modulate the function of IscS in iron-sulfur cluster 
                     formation |CITS: [16698547]|.  IscX addition to the 
                     IscU-IscS binary complex reduces the cysteine desulfurase 
                     activity of the ternary complex and inhibits assembly of 
                     Fe-S clusters on IscU <i>in vitro</i> |CITS: [24810328]|. 
                     <i>In vivo</i>, IscX has a positive effect on Fe-S cluster 
                     biogenesis |CITS: [25430730]|.
                     The residues involved in binding Fe<sup>2+</sup> and 
                     Fe<sup>3+</sup> are also involved in the interaction of 
                     IscX with IscS |CITS: [16698547]|.  IscX, |FRAME: 
                     EG11653-MONOMER CyaY|, and |FRAME: FERREDOXIN-MONOMER Fdx| 
                     compete for overlapping binding sites on IscS |CITS: 
                     [24810328]|.  The presence of Fe<sup>2+</sup> strengthens 
                     the interaction between IscX and IscU |CITS: [24810328]|. 
                     IscX may be involved in the assembly of the [2Fe-2S] 
                     cluster of Fdx |CITS: [10544286]|.
                     A crystal structure of IscX has been solved at 1.75 &Aring;
                     resolution |CITS: [15937904]|, and a solution structure is 
                     available |CITS: [16698547]|.
                     An <i>iscX</i> mutant exhibits no obvious phenotype, 
                     compared to wild type |CITS: [11432781]|.  Only a 
                     competitive growth experiment revealed that a 
                     &Delta;<i>iscX</i> mutant has a growth disadvantage 
                     compared to wild type |CITS: [25430730]|."
