     gene            complement(2650107..2650442)
                     /gene="fdx"
                     /locus_tag="b2525"
                     /label=fdx
     CDS             complement(2650107..2650442)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="fdx"
                     /locus_tag="b2525"
                     /product="bifunctional reduced ferredoxin / ferredoxin"
                     /label=fdx
                     /note="Ferredoxin (Fdx) contains a [2Fe-2S] cluster |CITS: 
                     [4375562][11551196]| and functions in Fe-S cluster assembly
                     |CITS: [10544286][11432781]|. Fdx interacts directly with 
                     |FRAME: G7325-MONOMER IscS| and supplies one of the two 
                     electrons needed for reduction of S<sup>0</sup> to IscS. 
                     Fdx and |FRAME:G7324-MONOMER IscU| compete for overlapping 
                     binding sites on IscS |CITS: [23682711]|. Holo-IscA |CITS: 
                     [11319236]|, holo-GrxD, and the GrxD-BolA heterodimer 
                     |CITS: [21899261]| can transfer an [2Fe-2S] cluster to 
                     apo-Fdx <i>in vitro</i>.
                     A crystal structure of Fdx has been solved at 1.7 &Aring; 
                     resolution. The [2Fe-2S] cluster is located near the 
                     surface of the protein and is coordinated by the S&gamma; 
                     atoms of Cys42, Cys48, Cys51, and Cys87; another cysteine 
                     residue, Cys46, is exposed on the surface near the Fe-S 
                     cluster |CITS: [11551196]|.
                     Fdx is synthesized under both aerobic and anaerobic growth 
                     conditions |CITS: [4375562]|. An <i>fdx</i> null mutant 
                     strain grows with a significantly increased doubling time 
                     compared to wild type |CITS: [11432781]|.
                     Review: |CITS: [23298813]|."
