     gene            complement(2652311..2652826)
                     /gene="hscB"
                     /locus_tag="b2527"
                     /label=hscB
     CDS             complement(2652311..2652826)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="hscB"
                     /locus_tag="b2527"
                     /product="bifunctional [Fe-S] cluster biosynthesis
                     co-chaperone HscB / [Fe-S] cluster biosynthesis 
                     chaperone/co-chaperone system"
                     /label=hscB
                     /note="The |FRAME: EG12130-MONOMER| together with |FRAME: 
                     EG12131-MONOMER| comprises a chaperone/cochaperone system 
                     similar to DnaK/DnaJ |CITS: [9144776][9852006]| that is 
                     involved in iron-sulfur cluster assembly |CITS: 
                     [11432781]|. Models for chaperone-facilitated Fe-S cluster 
                     transfer have been proposed. One model involves an exchange
                     of Fe-S cluster ligands in the iron-sulfur cluster scaffold
                     protein |FRAME: G7324-MONOMER IscU| upon chaperone binding 
                     that facilitates cluster transfer |CITS: [21977977]|; 
                     another involves chaperone-mediated disordering of IscU 
                     that promotes the transfer of the Fe-S cluster to an 
                     acceptor protein |CITS: [22782893]|.
                     A crystal structure of HscB has been solved at 1.8 &Aring; 
                     resolution |CITS: [9300502][11124030]|. HscB consists of an
                     N-terminal J-domain that is similar to the J-domain of 
                     DnaJ, and a compact three-helix bundle C-terminal domain 
                     |CITS: [11124030]|. A solution structure indicates that the
                     crystal structure is representative of the solution state 
                     |CITS: [18702525]|.
                     HscB is a co-chaperone that stimulates HscA (Hsc66) ATPase 
                     activity |CITS: [9144776][10869428]|. HscB physically 
                     interacts with HscA and with IscU |CITS: 
                     [11983079][18702525]| and aids in targeting IscU to HscA 
                     |CITS: [10869428][11983079]|. The J-domain of HscB 
                     interacts primarily with full-length ATP-bound HscA |CITS: 
                     [15485839][25080945]|. The <i>in vivo</i> turnover rate of 
                     the HscA chaperone cycle may be determined by the 
                     availability of the IscU-HscB complex |CITS: [15485839]|. 
                     In the presence of HscA and HscB, conformational changes in
                     the [2Fe-2S] cluster of IscU appear to be coupled to ATP 
                     hydrolysis by HscA |CITS: [18986169]|.
                     Results from site-directed mutagenesis suggest that the 
                     C-terminal domain HscB interacts with IscU |CITS: 
                     [18702525][21269500]|. HscB binds to and stabilizes the 
                     ordered state of apo-IscU |CITS: [19492851][22782893]| and 
                     appears to modulate the formation and transfer of [2Fe-2S] 
                     clusters by IscU |CITS: [26246371]|. Suppressor mutations 
                     in <i>iscU</i> can bypass the requirement for the HscA-HscB
                     chaperone system |CITS: [26560204]|.
                     HscB also interacts with the cysteine desulfurase IscS via 
                     an exposed patch of residues in the C-terminal domain; this
                     interaction does not interfere with the HscB-IscU 
                     interaction |CITS: [27730125]|.
                     HscA and HscB are constitutively produced; HscB shows a 
                     cellular concentration of 6-12 &micro;M |CITS: [9144776]|. 
                     HscB expression is slightly induced by cold shock, but not 
                     heat shock |CITS: [7665466][9144776]|. An <i>hscB</i> 
                     mutant has increased doubling time in rich media and has 
                     lower activity of the Fe-S enzymes GltS and SDH than wild 
                     type |CITS: [11432781]|. Overexpression of the <i>isc</i> 
                     gene cluster, containing nine genes including <i>hscB</i>, 
                     increases iron-sulfur cluster assembly in overproduced 
                     ferredoxins |CITS: [10393315]|.
                     An <i>hscB</i> mutant loses selenate reductase activity 
                     |CITS: [25307727]|. Under anaerobic conditions, a 
                     &Delta;<i>hscB</i> mutant lacks nitrate reductase, formate 
                     dehydrogenases FDH-N and FDH-O, and hydrogenases 1 and 2 
                     activities |CITS: [28640740]|.
                     <i>hscB</i> belongs to a network of genes which facilitate 
                     stress-induced mutagenesis (SIM) in <i>E. coli</i> K-12 
                     |CITS: [23224554]|.
                     Reviews: |CITS: [30194723][23333622][23660107][17919282][1 
                     6952052][17453917][15987899][35611886]|"
