     gene            complement(2655942..2656682)
                     /gene="trmJ"
                     /locus_tag="b2532"
                     /label=trmJ
     CDS             complement(2655942..2656682)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="trmJ"
                     /locus_tag="b2532"
                     /product="trifunctional tRNA Cm32/Um32 methyltransferase /
                     tRNA Um32 methyltransferase / tRNA Cm32 methyltransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.1.1.200"
                     /label=trmJ
                     /note="TrmJ is the tRNA:Cm32/Um32 methyltransferase which 
                     introduces methyl groups at the 2'-<i>O</i> position of C32
                     and U32 of several tRNAs <i>in vitro</i>. The tRNAs 
                     2'-<i>O</i>-methylated at the C/U32 position <i>in vivo</i>
                     are |FRAME: glnW-tRNA| and |FRAME: glnX-tRNA| (at the U32 
                     position), and |FRAME: metZ-tRNA|, |FRAME: metY-tRNA|, 
                     |FRAME: serT-tRNA| and |FRAME: trpT-tRNA| (at the C32 
                     position) |CITS: [16848900][26202969]|.
                     TrmJ belongs to the SPOUT superfamily of methyltransferases
                     |CITS: [11763972]|. Sequence analysis suggests that the 
                     active sites of TrmH and TrmJ are conserved, and the 
                     enzymes may thus use a similar reaction mechanism |CITS: 
                     [16848900]|. TrmJ does not show specificity for the 
                     nucleotide at the 32 position and can also methylate 
                     tRNA<sup>Pro</sup>(GGG) <i>in vitro</i> |CITS: [24951554]|.
                     Crystal structures of the N-terminal SPOUT domain of TrmJ 
                     as well as the full-length enzyme in complex with SAH have 
                     been solved |CITS: [24951554][26202969]|. The enzyme forms 
                     an unusual asymmetric dimer in which the N- and C-terminal 
                     domains associate separately. SAH is bound to the trefoil 
                     knot within the SPOUT domain |CITS: [26202969]|. 
                     Mutagenesis of the predicted catalytic Arg23 residue 
                     results in loss of activity |CITS: [24951554]|. Mutants in 
                     conserved residues within the C-terminal domain have 
                     reduced catalytic activity |CITS: [26202969]|.
                     TrmJ requires the full-length tRNA for activity and 
                     recognizes identity elements within the D stem-loop for 
                     distinguishing substrate from non-substrate tRNAs |CITS: 
                     [24951554]|. The tertiary L-shaped structure of the tRNA is
                     required for TrmJ activity |CITS: [26202969]|. Residues 
                     required for binding of tRNA reside in both the N-and 
                     C-terminal domain of TrmJ; neither the isolated domains nor
                     mixtures of isolated N- and C-terminal domains are able to 
                     bind substrate tRNA |CITS: [26202969]|.
                     Review: |CITS: [22905870][40210524]|"
