                     /locus_tag="b2536"
                     /product="bifunctional putative 3-phenylpropionate
                     transporter / 3-phenylpropionate transport"
                     /label=hcaT
                     /note="HcaT is a member of the major facilitator
                     superfamily (MFS) of transporters |CITS: [9529885]|. HcaT 
                     is a putative 3-phenylpropionate transporter. The 
                     <I>hcaT</I> gene is located immediately downstream of the 
                     <I>hcaR</I> gene, whose product regulates expression of the
                     <I>hcaA-D</I> operon responsible for catabolism of 
                     3-phenylpropionic acid |CITS: [9603882]|. HcaT is predicted
                     to be an inner membrane protein with 12 transmembrane 
                     domains; topology analysis suggests the C-terminus is 
                     located in the cytoplasm |CITS:[15044727]|."
