     CDS             2664267..2664587
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="hcaC"
                     /locus_tag="b2540"
                     /product="multifunctional putative
                     3-phenylpropionate/cinnamate dioxygenase ferredoxin subunit
                     / putative 3-phenylpropionate/cinnamate dioxygenase / 
                     cinnamate dioxygenase / 3-phenylpropionate dioxygenase"
                     /EC_number="1.14.12.19"
                     /label=hcaC
                     /note="Based on sequence similarity, HcaC is thought to
                     encode the ferredoxin component of the 3-phenylpropionate 
                     dioxygenase system |CITS: [9603882]|.  Partially purified 
                     HcaC protein was shown to contain a [2Fe-2S] iron-sulfur 
                     cluster that can be reduced by dithionite, but not 
                     ascorbate, identifying it as a low-potential Rieske 
                     iron-sulfur cluster protein |CITS: [18286376]|. 
                     3-phenylpropionate dioxygenase has not been biochemically 
                     characterized.
                     <i>E. coli</i> is able to utilize certain aromatic acids as
                     carbon and energy sources.  A meta-cleavage pathway 
                     involving HcaC is used for the catabolism of 
                     3-phenylpropionate |CITS: [6345502][9603882]|.
                     HcaC: ""<b>h</b>ydroxy<b>c</b>innamic <b>a</b>cid"" |CITS: 
