                     carbon and energy sources.  A meta-cleavage pathway 
                     involving HcaB is used for the catabolism of 
                     3-phenylpropionate |CITS: [6345502][9603882]|.
                     An <i>hcaB</i> mutant does not grow on 
                     <i>m</i>-hydroxyphenylpropionate (MHP) as the sole source 
                     of carbon |CITS: [3531186]|.
                     HcaB: ""<b>h</b>ydroxy<b>c</b>innamic <b>a</b>cid"" |CITS: 
                     [9603882]|
                     "
