     gene            complement(2682152..2682865)
                     /gene="qseG"
                     /locus_tag="b2555"
                     /label=qseG
     CDS             complement(2682152..2682865)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="qseG"
                     /locus_tag="b2555"
                     /product="outer membrane lipoprotein QseG"
                     /label=qseG
                     /note="QseG is a periplasmic facing outer membrane
                     lipoprotein which physically interacts with the |FRAME: 
                     G7345-MONOMER ""GlrK histidine kinase""| and activates the 
                     |FRAME: PWY0-1503|.
                     <i>qseG</i> is a multicopy inducer of |FRAME: RPOE-MONOMER 
                     ""<i>rpoE</i>""|; transcription is significantly pronounced
                     from the RpoN regulated P2 promoter (<i>rpoE</i>P2) and is 
                     abrogated in a &Delta;<i>glrR</i> strain |CITS: 
                     [27629414]|. QseG activates the |FRAME: PWY0-1503| (also 
                     known as QseEF) which regulates transcription of  
                     <i>rpoE</i> - it is one of the multiple systems which 
                     regulate transcription of <i>rpoE</i> in response to a 
                     variety of stress conditions |CITS: [27629414]|.
                     QseG is present in the cell envelope of <i>E. coli</i> 
                     K-12; levels of the |FRAME: TKE1-RNA| are significantly 
                     reduced in a &Delta;<i>qseG</i> strain and QseG is required
                     for efficient transcription from the 
                     &sigma;<sup>54</sup>-dependent promoter of <i>glmY</i>; it 
                     has no role in transcription from the 
                     &sigma;<sup>70</sup>-dependent promoter of <i>glmY</i> 
                     |CITS: [30040820]|. QseG binds the periplasmic N-terminal 
                     domain of dimeric GlrK <i>in vivo</i>; QseG and GlrK are 
                     both required for efficient phosphorylation of aspartate56 
                     in the GlrR response regulator; a single substitution 
                     mutation (S58N) in GlrK impairs the physical interaction 
                     between QseG and GlrK and results in a 3-fold decrease in 
                     <i>glmY</i> expression |CITS: [30040820]|. |FRAME: 
                     L-EPINEPHRINE ""Epinephrine""| induces moderate stimulation
                     of GlrK phosphorylation in the stationary growth phase and 
                     QseG is required for this effect |CITS: [30040820]|.
                     In enterohemorrhagic <i>E. coli</i> the homologous gene 
                     encodes an outer membrane protein and virulence factor 
                     which (along with <i>qseE</i> and <i>qseF</i>) is 
                     implicated in AE (attaching and effacing) lesion formation 
                     in the large intestine |CITS: [19289831]|.
                     <i>qse</i>: quorum sensing |CITS: [17220220][27629414]|
                     "
