                     /gene="shoB"
                     /locus_tag="b4687"
                     /product="toxic peptide ShoB"
                     /label=shoB
                     /note="The small hydrophobic peptide ShoB is encoded
                     within the small RNA sequence of <i>ryfB</i> |CITS: 
                     [15718303][18710431]|. RyfB was identified in a 
                     cloning-based screen for small RNAs and shown to be 
                     expressed during exponential growth |CITS: [15718303]|. 
                     Overexpression of ShoB is toxic to the cell by disrupting 
                     membrane integrity. Whole-genome gene expression analysis 
                     after induction of ShoB expression shows changes in 
                     expression of many stress response and membrane proteins 
                     |CITS: [18710431]|. Overexpression of ""RyfB"" decreases 
                     swimming and swarming motility |CITS: [26469694]|.
                     ShoB is predicted to be a bitopic inner membrane protein 
                     |CITS: [27510400]|.
                     Regulatory elements are highly conserved across pathogenic 
                     and commensal <i>E. coli</i> |CITS: [38856235]|.
                     ShoB: ""<b>s</b>mall <b>h</b>ydrophobic <b>O</b>RF"" |CITS:
                     [18710431]|
                     Reviews: |CITS: [19210615][21342783][23182878]|"
                     /translation="MTDCRYLIKRVIKIIIAVLQLILLFL"
                     /go_component="plasma membrane [goid 0005886] [evidence
