     gene            complement(2695840..2696745)
                     /gene="era"
                     /locus_tag="b2566"
                     /label=era
     CDS             complement(2695840..2696745)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="era"
                     /locus_tag="b2566"
                     /product="bifunctional 30S ribosomal subunit maturation
                     GTPase Era / GTPase"
                     /EC_number="3.6.5.3"
                     /label=era
                     /note="Era is a GTPase |CITS: [2105934]| that interacts
                     with the 30S ribosomal subunit |CITS: [10527840][27382067]|
                     and is involved in its maturation |CITS: [20188109]|, 
                     specifically folding of helices 23 and 24 in the platform 
                     region |CITS: [31265110]|. The GTP binding and GTPase 
                     activities |CITS: [8919456]| and the C-terminal RNA binding
                     domain |CITS: [10510227]| of Era are required for its 
                     function. Native Era protein co-purifies with 16S rRNA 
                     |CITS: [10832634]|.
                     The kinetics of guanine nucleotide binding and exchange 
                     have been measured |CITS: [10852878]|.
                     Crystal structures of Era have been solved |CITS: 
                     [10094501][10411886][19706445]|. Era is composed of an 
                     N-terminal GTPase domain and a C-terminal domain with an 
                     RNA binding motif |CITS: [10411886]|.
                     |FRAME: EG10572-MONOMER MazG| and Era associate <i>in 
                     vitro</i> and by yeast two-hybrid test. Nucleotide 
                     influences the association; binding is weaker with 
                     GTP&gamma;S than with GDP added |CITS: [12218018]|. Era 
                     also interacts with |FRAME: G6362-MONOMER YbeY| |CITS: 
                     [27834201]| and binds (p)ppGpp |CITS: [29511080]|. 
                     <i>era</i> is essential for viability |CITS: 
                     [2838786][2540151][1537799][1901053][1906969][12936988]|. A
                     temperature-sensitive lethal allele contains a C-terminal 
                     deletion and a point mutation resulting in a Tyr8Cys change
                     |CITS: [2527846]|. Depletion of Era leads to accumulation 
                     of precursors of 16S rRNA |CITS: [12753192]|. |FRAME: 
                     EG10523 <i>rsmA</i>| is a multicopy suppressor of a ts 
                     <i>era</i> mutant |CITS: [9748462]|; suppressor activity 
                     does not depend on RsmA's methyltransferase activity |CITS:
                     [17890303]|. A suppressor mutation for the 
                     temperature-sensitive ts118 allele of |FRAME: EG10911 
                     <i>rpsL</i>| maps to <i>era</i> |CITS: [3162077]|. 
                     Overexpression of Era also partially suppresses the 
                     cold-sensitive phenotype of a &Delta;|FRAME: EG11178 
                     <i>rbfA</i>| mutant |CITS: [12753192]|, the slow growth 
                     phenotype of a &Delta;|FRAME: G7841 <i>rsgA</i>| mutant 
                     |CITS: [18223068]|, and the growth defect of a 
                     &Delta;|FRAME: G6362 <i>ybeY</i>| mutant |CITS: 
                     [29914987]|. A T99I point mutation, which might affect 
                     GTP/GDP binding to Era due to structural changes, results 
                     in suppression of some pleiotropic phenotypes of 
                     &Delta;<i>ybeY</i> but not the temperature sensitivity or 
                     16S rRNA stability phenotypes. The suppression is specific 
                     to the &Delta;<i>ybeY</i> mutant as the <i>era(T99I)</i> 
                     mutant does not suppress loss of other 16S rRNA maturation 
                     factors, such as KsgA, RimM, RsgA, and RbfA |CITS: 
                     [35663862]|.
                     <i>era</i> is co-transcribed with the upstream <i>rnc</i> 
                     gene encoding RNase III, which autoregulates expression of 
                     the operon |CITS: [2583104][2085545][8971718][8972772]|. 
                     Expression of Era appears to be translationally coupled to 
                     that of RNase III |CITS: [2105934]| and is growth-rate 
                     regulated |CITS: [9515700]|.
                     RbaA: ""<b>r</b>i<b>b</b>osomal <b>a</b>ssembly <b>A</b>"" 
                     |CITS: [3162077]|
                     SdgE: ""<b>s</b>uppressor of <i><b>d</b>na<b>G</b></i> 
                     <b>E</b>"" |CITS: [9093842][9226268]|
                     Era: ""<i><b>E</b>. coli</i> <b>RA</b>S-like protein"" 
                     |CITS: [3097637]|
                     Reviews: |CITS: [1640828][11200227][11489118][11551179][12 
                     732302][16890019][21529161][21675921][21885683][28132488][ 
                     37860580]|"
