     gene            complement(2700681..2701160)
                     /gene="rseC"
                     /locus_tag="b2570"
                     /label=rseC
     CDS             complement(2700681..2701160)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rseC"
                     /locus_tag="b2570"
                     /product="bifunctional regulatory protein RseC / SoxR
                     [2Fe-2S] reducing system"
                     /label=rseC
                     /note="RseC is encoded as the fourth protein of the 
                     <i>rpoE-rseABC</i> operon |CITS: [9159522][9159523]|. RseC,
                     along with proteins encoded by the <i>rsxABCDGE</i> operon,
                     may play a role in reduction of the SoxR iron-sulfur 
                     cluster |CITS: [12773378]|. The periplasmic flavin 
                     transferase |FRAME: EG12073-MONOMER ApbE| (renamed Ftp 
                     |CITS: [26626129]|) is also a component of this system; the
                     RsxABCDGE, RseC and AbpE proteins likely form a complex 
                     that uses NAD(P)H to reduce SoxR |CITS: [35344189]|. RseC 
                     may have additional SoxR-independent roles |CITS: 
                     [39631780]|.
                     RseC is predicted to be an inner membrane protein with two 
                     transmembrane domains; experimental topology analysis 
                     suggests that both the N-terminal and C-terminal domains 
                     are located in the cytoplasm |CITS: 
                     [15919996][35344189][39631780]|. The N-terminal region of 
                     RseC contains a conserved cysteine motif 
                     (CX<sub>2</sub>CX<sub>5</sub>C); the purified N-terminal 
                     domain (residues 1-70) can form an oxygen-sensitive Fe-S 
                     cluster |CITS: [39631780]|.
                     Genetic evidence suggests that RseC has a subtle positive 
                     effect on &sigma;<sup>E</sup> activity |CITS: [9159522]| 
                     and a minor positive role in the regulation of cell lysis 
                     |CITS: [19549168]|. However, an <i>rseC</i> mutant is also 
                     reported to show wild-type &sigma;<sup>E</sup> activity 
                     under inducing or non-inducing conditions |CITS: 
                     [9159523]|. An <i>rseC</i> mutant exhibits constitutive 
                     <i>soxS</i> expression mediated by oxidized SoxR protein 
                     |CITS: [12773378]|, as well as increased motility and 
                     biofilm formation compared to wild type |CITS: [18344336]|.
                     Membranes purified from a &Delta;<i>rseC</i> mutant do not 
                     exhibit NADH-dependent SoxR-reducing activity |CITS: 
                     [35344189]|.
                     <i>Salmonella typhimurium</i> RseC is involved in thiamine 
                     synthesis |CITS: [9335303]|.
                     <i>rseC</i> shows differential codon adaptation, resulting 
                     in differential translation efficiency signatures, in 
                     aerotolerant compared to obligate anaerobic microbes. It 
                     was therefore predicted to play a role in the oxidative 
                     stress response. An <i>rseC</i> deletion mutant was shown 
                     to be more sensitive than wild-type specifically to 
                     hydrogen peroxide exposure, but not other stresses |CITS: 
                     [24580753]|.
                     RseC: ""<b>r</b>egulator of <b>s</b>igma <b>E</b> 
                     <b>C</b>"" |CITS: [9159523]|"
