     gene            complement(2702113..2702763)
                     /gene="rseA"
                     /locus_tag="b2572"
                     /label=rseA
     CDS             complement(2702113..2702763)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rseA"
                     /locus_tag="b2572"
                     /product="anti-sigma-E factor RseA"
                     /label=rseA
                     /note="RseA is an anti-sigma factor that inhibits 
                     &sigma;<sup>E</sup> |CITS: [9159522]|.  RseA is the major 
                     regulator of &sigma;<sup>E</sup> |CITS: [10500101]|.  RseA 
                     associates with the region of &sigma;<sup>E</sup> that 
                     interacts with DNA and may interfere with promoter binding 
                     |CITS: [12016219]|.  Structural studies indicate that RseA 
                     interferes with binding of &sigma;<sup>E</sup> to core 
                     polymerase |CITS: [12718891]|.  RseA binding to 
                     &sigma;<sup>E</sup> may be regulated by phosphorylation 
                     |CITS: [12657060]|.
                     Upon extracytoplasmic stress, misfolded/unfolded porins 
                     interact with the DegS PDZ domain, releasing an inhibitory 
                     interaction and activating DegS protease |CITS: 
                     [12679035]|. DegS and RseP then sequentially catalyze 
                     proteolytic cleavage of RseA, thereby relieving repression 
                     of &sigma;<sup>E</sup> and activating the 
                     &sigma;<sup>E</sup>-mediated stress response |CITS: 
                     [12183368][12183369]|.
                     The &sigma;<sup>E</sup> system is also involved in the 
                     response to hyperosmotic shock |CITS: [10594827]| and in 
                     release of nutrients from dead cells during long periods of
                     stationary phase |CITS: [10960110]|.
                     A crystal structure of &sigma;<sup>E</sup> in complex with 
                     the RseA amino-terminal, cytoplasmic domain is presented at
                     2 &Aring; resolution |CITS: [12718891]|.
                     RseA resides in the inner membrane.  The cytoplasmic 
                     amino-terminal domain has the anti-sigma activity |CITS: 
                     [9159522][9159523]|.  Residue Y38 is phosphorylated |CITS: 
                     [12657060]|. RseA is predicted to be a bitopic inner 
                     membrane protein with the N-terminus in the cytoplasm 
                     |CITS: [27510400]|.
                     Mutations cause increased &sigma;<sup>E</sup> activity 
                     |CITS: [9159522][9159523]|.  Overproduction causes 
                     decreased &sigma;<sup>E</sup> activity |CITS: [9159522]|. 
                     RseA and &sigma;<sup>E</sup> physically interact |CITS: 
                     [9159522][9159523]|.  RseA also interacts with the 
                     periplasmic RseB protein |CITS: [9159522][9159523]|, which 
                     acts to stimulate binding of RseA to &sigma;<sup>E</sup> 
                     |CITS: [11777003]|.
                     <i>E. coli</i> and mammalian cells exhibit analogous 
                     responses to unfolded protein stress |CITS: [12183369]|.
                     A potential RNA G-quadruplex structure, formed by 
                     guanine-rich sequences located in the coding sequence 
                     region of the gene, was identified  for <i>rseA</i>. This 
                     structure  could regulate the expression of the gene, as 
                     observed for <i>hemL</i> gene expression |CITS: 
                     [31964733]|.
                     The Keio collection <i>rseA</i> mutant is sensitive to 
                     lithium (<90% growth at 200mM Li) |CITS: [39983623]|. RseA:
                     ""<b>r</b>egulator of <b>s</b>igma <b>E</b>"" |CITS: 
                     [9159523]|"
