     CDS             complement(2705386..2706123)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yfiC"
                     /locus_tag="b2575"
                     /product="tRNA m(6)A37 methyltransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.1.1.223"
                     /label=yfiC
                     /note="The 37th position of tRNA, located in the anticodon 
                     stem-loop 3'-adjacent to the third nucleotide of the 
                     anticodon, is generally occupied by a purine and is often 
                     modified. The YfiC protein, also known as TrmM, is 
                     responsible for methylation of the A37 nucleotide of 
                     tRNA<sup>Val</sup><sub>1</sub> at the N<sup>6</sup> 
                     position |CITS: [19383770]|.
                     The m<sup>6</sup>A modification is relatively rare in tRNA 
                     and mostly observed in bacteria. Under standard growth 
                     conditions, a <i>yfiC</i> null mutant has no significant 
                     growth defect. However, under osmotic or oxidative stress 
                     conditions, the <i>yfiC</i> mutant shows decreased survival
                     |CITS: [19383770]|.
                     X-ray crystal structures of the protein with and without 
                     |FRAME: ADENOSYL-HOMO-CYS| were published for the 
                     orthologous protein from |FRAME: TAX-2095|, which can 
                     substitute for YfiC. That protein was shown to require a 
                     divalent metal ion for activity |CITS: [35481631]|."
