     gene            2706255..2707589
                     /gene="srmB"
                     /locus_tag="b2576"
                     /label=srmB
     CDS             2706255..2707589
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="srmB"
                     /locus_tag="b2576"
                     /product="bifunctional ATP-dependent RNA helicase SrmB / 
                     ATP-dependent RNA helicase"
                     /EC_number="5.6.2.7"
                     /label=srmB
                     /note="SrmB is a DEAD-box protein with RNA helicase
                     activity that facilitates an early step in the assembly of 
                     the 50S subunit of the ribosome |CITS: 
                     [12787353][30219894]|.  Recent data suggest that SrmB 
                     facilitates ribosome assembly by acting both as an RNA 
                     chaperone to resolve misfolded and trapped RNA structures 
                     and by stabilizing early ribosomal protein and rRNA binding
                     events |CITS: [31877323]|.
                     The SrmB protein was found to be associated with a pre-50S 
                     ribosomal particle |CITS: [12787353]| and forms a complex 
                     with ribosomal proteins L4, L24, and the region of 23S rRNA
                     that interacts with L4 and L24 |CITS: [19734346]|. The site
                     of SrmB action is different from its binding site; models 
                     for SrmB activity during 50S ribosomal subunit assembly are
                     presented |CITS: [21859437]|.  SrmB positively regulates 
                     expression of the ribosomal proteins |FRAME: 
                     EG10874-MONOMER L13| and |FRAME: EG10908-MONOMER S9| by 
                     preventing premature transcription termination; thus, the 
                     role of SrmB in ribosome assembly may be to ensure the 
                     synthesis of adequate levels of L13 and S9 |CITS: 
                     [31188443]|.  SrmB activates expression of the |FRAME: 
                     CSRB-RNA| |CITS: [24708042]| by promoting normal binding of
                     UvrY to <i>csrB</i> |CITS: [26673755]|.
                     The ATPase and helicase activities of SrmB are stimulated 
                     by long single-stranded RNAs |CITS: [15196029][18165229]|. 
                     SrmB can directly interact with |FRAME: EG10690-MONOMER| 
                     |CITS: [10361280]|, |FRAME: EG10859-MONOMER RNase E| |CITS:
                     [15554979]|, and |FRAME: CPLX0-1642 RraA| |CITS: 
                     [24045937]| and can stabilize overexpressed mRNAs |CITS: 
                     [7526223]|.  SrmB has a relatively non-specific RNA strand 
                     annealing, RNA strand displacement, and RNA chaperone 
                     activities |CITS: [21378185]|.
                     The interaction of RraA with SrmB modulates the ATPase 
                     activity of SrmB.  Crystal and solution structures of the 
                     RraA-SrmB complex have been analyzed |CITS: [24045937]|. 
                     The protein inventory, rRNA modification state, and 
                     structures of 40S ribosomal assembly intermediates that 
                     form in a &Delta;<i>srmB</i> mutant have been studied 
                     |CITS: [31877323]|.
                     Deletion of the <i>srmB</i> gene causes a growth defect at 
                     low temperature |CITS: [12787353][20166751][20484467]|, 
                     while overexpression supresses a temperature sensitive 
                     lethal mutation in ribosomal protein L24 |CITS: [2461520]|.
                      Overexpression of <i>srmB</i> also improves the fitness of
                     an evolved &Delta;<i>mutH E. coli</i> strain |CITS: 
                     [25806682]|.  Extragenic suppressors of the 
                     &Delta;<i>srmB</i> growth defect identify two 
                     heptanucleotide repeats in domain II of 23S rRNA and a site
                     in 5S rRNA as the sites of SrmB action |CITS: [21859437]|. 
                     Expression of <i>rplM</i> as well as ribosomal protein L13 
                     and S9 levels are decreased in the &Delta;<i>srmB</i> 
                     mutant compared to wild type. Suppressors of the 
                     cold-sensitive growth phenotype of &Delta;<i>srmB</i> were 
                     found in the 5' UTR of the <i>rplM-rpsI</i> operon and lead
                     to mostly normalized expression of L13 and S9 |CITS: 
                     [31188443]|.
                     The C-terminal domain of SrmB is not required for function 
                     |CITS: [19734346]|.  A strain containing deletions of all 
                     five DEAD-box genes (<i>deaD</i>, <i>srmB</i>, <i>rhlB</i>,
                     <i>rhlE</i>, and <i>dbpA</i>), &Delta;5, is viable and 
                     shows a cumulative growth defect at low temperature.  
                     Growth in minimal medium alleviates the growth defect of 
                     &Delta;5 |CITS: [20484467]|.  An <i>srmB rnr</i> double 
                     deletion strain shows a growth defect and enhanced 
                     accumulation of rRNA degradation products |CITS: 
                     [30219894]|.
                     Reviews: |CITS: [1552844][16935881][21529161][21923767][24 
                     635478][25907111]|
                     "
