     CDS             complement(2707798..2708679)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yfiE"
                     /locus_tag="b2577"
                     /product="putative LysR-type DNA-binding transcriptional
                     regulator YfiE"
                     /label=yfiE
                     /note="YfiE contains a helix-turn-helix motif to bind DNA
                     in its N-terminal domain and it was predicted that this 
                     protein regulates genes related to cysteine and 
                     O-acetylserine export and HOCl resistance |CITS: [35880217]
                     [34428301]|.
                     Genome-wide YfiE binding sites were determined <i>in 
                     vivo</i> by the chromatin immunoprecipitation method 
                     combined with lambda exonuclease digestion (ChIP-exo) in 
                     glucose M9 minimal medium |CITS: [34428301]|.
                     Upstream of the <i>yfiE</i> gene, a sequence was found that
                     could work as a transcriptional promoter, and the 
                     transcription of the <i>yfiE</i> gene is affected by 
                     cadmium and conditions that lead to biofilm formation 
                     |CITS: [35880217]|.
                     The YfiE binding landscape was globally mapped in vivo by 
                     standardized ChIP-seq and quantitatively modeled using 
                     BoltzNet, a biophysically informed neural network that 
                     infers binding energy from sequence data |CITS:[40335485]|.
                     The resulting ChIP-seq binding regions are available in 
                     RegulonDB (<a href=""https://regulondb.cc 
                     g.unam.mx/ht/dataset/TFBINDING/source=GALAGAN"">Galagan 
                     collection</a>), and the corresponding energy matrix and 
                     genomic binding profiles can be accessed at <a 
                     href=""http://boltznet.bu.edu"">boltznet.bu.edu</a> 
                     |CITS:[40335485]|."
