     gene            2712582..2713280
                     /gene="tapT"
                     /locus_tag="b2583"
                     /label=tapT
     CDS             2712582..2713280
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="tapT"
                     /locus_tag="b2583"
                     /product="tRNA 3-amino-3-carboxypropyltransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.5.1.25"
                     /label=tapT
                     /note="tRNA-uridine aminocarboxypropyltransferase
                     catalyzes the transfer of the aminocarboxypropyl group from
                     <i>S</i>-adenosylmethionine to the N3 position of uridine 
                     within tRNAs |CITS: [4597321][31804502][31863583]|.  The 
                     physiological significance of the 
                     3-(3-amino-3-carboxypropyl)uridine (acp<sup>3</sup>U) 
                     modification is so far unknown |CITS: [378998][31863583]|.
                     The acp<sup>3</sup>U modification of tRNAs is widely 
                     conserved |CITS: [31804502][31863583]|; in <i>E. coli</i>, 
                     it resides in nucleotide 47 of the variable loop of eight 
                     specific tRNAs |CITS: [31863583]| and appears to increase 
                     their thermal stability |CITS: [31804502]|.  Depending on 
                     the specific tRNA, lack of prior m<sup>7</sup>G 
                     modification at position 46 reduces acp<sup>3</sup>U 
                     modification |CITS: [31863583]|.
                     A structural model of TapT suggests the presence of a 
                     trefoil knot that is characteristic of the &alpha;/&beta; 
                     knot methyltransferase superfamily |CITS: [26335199]|. TapT
                     binds Zn<sup>2+</sup> <i>in vitro</i>; the N-terminal 
                     domain of TapT with a putative zinc-binding motif is 
                     required for catalytic activity.  Mutations in the 
                     conserved DTW motif strongly reduce activity |CITS: 
                     [31863583]|.
                     A &Delta;<i>tapT</i> mutant has no obvious defect under 
                     normal growth conditions |CITS: [31804502][31863583]|; when
                     cultured under continuous heat stress, it develops a 
                     motility defect due to secondary mutations |CITS: 
                     [31804502]|.
                     TapT: ""<b>t</b>RNA 
                     <b>a</b>minocarboxy<b>p</b>ropyl<b>t</b>ransferase"" |CITS:
                     [31804502]|
                     TuaA: ""<b>t</b>RNA <b>U</b>47 <b>a</b>cp transferase 
                     <b>A</b>"" |CITS: [31863583]|"
