                     /label=kgtP
     CDS             complement(2717807..2719105)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="kgtP"
                     /locus_tag="b2587"
                     /product="bifunctional alpha-ketoglutarate:H(+) symporter
                     / transport of 2-oxoglutarate"
                     /label=kgtP
                     /note="KgtP is a proton-driven transporter for 
                     &alpha;-ketoglutarate. <i>kgtP</i> mutants show greatly 
                     impaired growth on &alpha;-ketoglutarate which can be 
                     complemented by the cloned <i>kgtP</i> gene |CITS: 
                     [2053984]|. KgtP-dependent &alpha;-ketoglutarate/proton 
                     symport activity has been demonstrated in membrane vesicles
                     |CITS: [1556144]|.
                     KgtP displays a Km for &alpha;-ketoglutarate of 13-46 
                     &mu;M. KgtP-mediated &alpha;-ketoglutarate transport could 
                     be partially inhibited by fumarate, malate and succinate 
                     |CITS: [1556144]|. Consistent with its function as an 
                     &alpha;-ketoglutarate/proton symport, KgtP is a member of 
                     the major facilitator superfamily |CITS: [1419050]|. 
                     Alkaline phosphatase fusions have demonstrated that KgtP 
                     consists of twelve transmembrane spanning segments |CITS: 
                     [8419306]|. Arg-92 and Asp-88 have been shown to be 
                     essential residues in the KgtP transporter |CITS: 
                     [1554735]|.
                     <i>kgtP</i> appears to be constitutively expressed |CITS: 
                     [1556144]|.
                     KgtP has been implicated in arabinose efflux |CITS: 
                     [22952739]|."
