                     /label=ryfD
     misc_RNA        complement(2727512..2727654)
                     /gene="ryfD"
                     /locus_tag="b4609"
                     /product="small regulatory RNA RyfD"
                     /note="RyfD was identified in a cloning-based screen for
                     small RNAs.  RyfD is highly abundant under all conditions 
                     tested |CITS: [15718303]|.  In an RNA-RNA interactome 
                     screen, the RyfD-RaiZ small RNA pair was found to be 
                     associated with the RNA chaperone ProQ |CITS: [31761494]|. 
                     RyfD appears to have some genetic interactions with other 
                     sRNAs under different growth conditions |CITS: [35920556]|.
                     Overexpression of RyfD decreases biofilm formation and 
                     swarming motility |CITS: [26469694]|.
                     Review: |CITS: [32213244]|"
     gene            complement(2727662..2728393)
                     /gene="pgeF"
                     /locus_tag="b2593"
                     /label=pgeF
     CDS             complement(2727662..2728393)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="pgeF"
                     /locus_tag="b2593"
                     /product="multifunctional purine nucleoside phosphorylase
                     PgeF / adenosine phosphorylase / S-methyl-5'-thioadenosine 
                     phosphorylase / inosine phosphorylase / adenosine deaminase
                     / polyphenol oxidase"
                     /EC_number="2.4.2.28; 1.10.3.2"
                     /label=pgeF
                     /note="YfiH is a purine nucleoside phosphorylase; <i>in 
                     vitro</i> activity was tested with adenosine, 
                     <i>S</i>-methyl-5'-thioadenosine and inosine. The enzyme 
                     can also act as an adenosine deaminase |CITS: [31978345]|. 
                     Earlier research showed that YfiH is a multicopper oxidase 
                     with polyphenol oxidase activity. Cyclic voltammetry 
                     measurements show that YfiH is a laccase with low redox 
                     potential |CITS: [16740638]|.
                     A <i>yfiH</i> deletion strain is more sensitive to 
                     ampicillin, cephradine and cephoxitin than wild type |CITS:
                     [20065048][28612943]|. Overexpression of |FRAME: 
                     LSERINEDEAM1-MONOMER SdaA| or deletion of |FRAME: EG12142 
                     <i>sdaC</i>| suppresses the &beta;-lactam sensitivity 
                     |CITS: [28612943]|. A cell morphology-altering mutation was
                     mapped to <i>yfiH</i> |CITS: [26593043]|. A 
                     &Delta;<i>yfiH</i> mutant shows altered cell morphology and
                     incorporates L-serine or glycine in place of L-alanine 
                     within the crosslinking peptides of peptidoglycan |CITS: 
                     [28612943]|. Further analysis of the &Delta;<i>pgeF</i> 
                     found that cells accumulate misincorporated peptidoglycan 
                     precursors in the cytoplasm and expression of heterologous 
                     L-lysine or glycine ligases results in cell death, 
                     indicating that PgeF has the ability to edit 
                     misincorporated L-serine or glycine residues in place of 
                     L-alanine. This function is also found in other organisms 
                     as evidenced by homologs from various bacterial species 
                     complementing the &Delta;<i>pgeF</i> mutant |CITS: 
                     [40632566]|.
                     PgeF: <b>p</b>eptido<b>g</b>lycan <b>e</b>diting 
                     <b>f</b>actor |CITS: [28612943]|"
