     gene            2730513..2730854
                     /gene="raiA"
                     /locus_tag="b2597"
                     /label=raiA
     CDS             2730513..2730854
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="raiA"
                     /locus_tag="b2597"
                     /product="ribosome-associated inhibitor A"
                     /label=raiA
                     /note="The hibernation factors |FRAME: EG11681-MONOMER
                     HPF|, |FRAME: EG50004-MONOMER RMF| and RaiA protect 
                     ribosomes, likely by protecting ribonuclease target sites 
                     within the ribosome |CITS: [33503254]|.  RaiA associates 
                     with 70S ribosomes at stationary phase and participates in 
                     the modulation of ribosome activity that is observed at 
                     stationary phase |CITS: [11168583]|.  RaiA binds to the 30S
                     ribosomal subunit and stabilizes the association of the 
                     subunits in the 70S ribosome |CITS: [10535924]|. Binding of
                     RaiA interferes with translation initiation |CITS: 
                     [15502846]| and elongation |CITS: [11375931]| by blocking 
                     mRNA-dependent tRNA binding in the P site and inhibiting 
                     tRNA binding to the A site |CITS: [15502846]|. RaiA blocks 
                     dissociation of the 70S ribosome by IF3 |CITS: [15502846]|.
                     At physiological Mg<sup>2+</sup> concentrations during 
                     <i>in vitro</i> poly(U) translation, RaiA inhibits 
                     misincorporation of leucine more strongly than 
                     incorporation of phenylalanine, the appropriate amino acid,
                     suggesting an anti-miscoding activity |CITS: [15219834]|.
                     NMR structural characterization has been performed |CITS: 
                     [12392550][12398359][12470636][17968439]|.  Crystal 
                     structures of RaiA within the ribosome show that RaiA 
                     overlaps the binding sites of both P- and A-site tRNAs 
                     |CITS: [15502846]|.  Crystal structures of RaiA associated 
                     with a <i>Thermus thermophilus</i> 70S ribosome showed that
                     both RaiA and HPF bind in the channel between the head and 
                     body of the 30S ribosomal subunit, apparently blocking the 
                     sites for tRNA and mRNA binding during protein synthesis.  
                     The extended C-terminal tail of RaiA presumably blocks the 
                     binding of RMF and thereby also RMF-induced ribosome dimer 
                     formation.  The binding site also overlaps with the binding
                     sites for IF1 and IF3 as well as EF-G, which are all 
                     involved in dissociation of the ribosomal subunits |CITS: 
                     [22605777]|.
                     RaiA protein production is induced during stationary phase 
                     or at cold temperatures |CITS: [11375931]|, during nitrogen
                     limitation stress |CITS: [27939605]|, and during 
                     HipA-induced persistence |CITS: [34427514]|.  Under 
                     anaerobiosis, expression of <i>raiA</i> is repressed by 
                     FNR, and a predicted FNR binding site was identified 
                     upstream of <i>raiA</i> |CITS: [12754220]|.
                     In an <i>raiA</i> deletion mutant, a larger number of 100S 
                     ribosomal particles are formed in stationary phase than in 
                     wild type |CITS: [16324148][26290418]|.  An <i>raiA</i> 
                     mutant shows reduced persister cell formation and increased
                     persister cell resuscitation |CITS: [32007277]|. A 
                     &Delta;<i>rmf hpf raiA</i> mutant is defective in regrowth 
                     from starvation; mutants accumulate increased amounts of 
                     fragmented rRNA |CITS: [33503254]|.
                     RaiA: ""<b>r</b>ibosome-<b>a</b>ssociated <b>i</b>nhibitor 
                     <b>A</b>"" |CITS: [11375931]|
                     Reviews: |CITS: [12762053][15523473][15884656][30476446]|"
