     misc_RNA        2730740..2730901
                     /gene="raiZ"
                     /locus_tag="b4805"
                     /product="small RNA RaiZ"
                     /note="RaiZ is a small RNA encoded within the 3' end and
                     3' UTR of <i>raiA</i>.  RaiZ binds both Hfq and ProQ; 
                     potential regulatory targets of RaiZ were identified |CITS:
                     [31761494]|.  RaiZ and 29 potential targets were also 
                     identified by applying a small RNA prediction algorithm to 
                     RIL-seq data |CITS: [34093460]|.
                     The RaiZ small RNA was initially detected in <i>Salmonella 
                     enterica</i> and <i>E. coli</i> (data was not shown); 
                     further characterization was done with the 
                     <i>Salmonella</i> gene product.  There, RaiZ is produced by
                     RNase E processing from the <i>raiA</i> primary transcript;
                     it binds the ProQ chaperone and negatively regulates 
                     <i>hupA</i> expression |CITS: [28336682]|.
                     RaiZ is expressed during both exponential and stationary 
                     phase |CITS: [34093460]|.
                     Reviews: |CITS: [28370625][32213244]|"
