     gene            2734719..2735084
                     /gene="yfiL"
                     /locus_tag="b2602"
                     /label=yfiL
     CDS             2734719..2735084
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yfiL"
                     /locus_tag="b2602"
                     /product="DUF2799 domain-containing lipoprotein YfiL"
                     /label=yfiL
                     /note="YfiL is a verified lipoprotein according to
                     unpublished data by S. Matsuyama et al. (cited in |CITS: 
                     [12876315]|).
                     Expression of <i>yfiL</i> is significantly decreased in 
                     populations adapted to the presence of ampicillin or 
                     tetracycline |CITS: [28217741]|."
                     /translation="MMKKFIAPLLALLVSGCQIDPYTHAPTLTSTDWYDVGMEDAISGS
                     AIKDDDAFSDSQADRGLYLKGYAEGQKKTCQTDFTYARGLSGKSFPASCNNVENASQLH
                     EVWQKGADENASTIRLN"
     gene            2735234..2735752
                     /gene="yfiR"
                     /locus_tag="b2603"
                     /label=yfiR
     CDS             2735234..2735752
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yfiR"
                     /locus_tag="b2603"
                     /product="DUF4154 domain-containing protein YfiR"
                     /label=yfiR
                     /note="An in-frame <i>yfiR</i> deletion mutant loses
                     swarming motility, but only mildly affects swimming 
                     motility.  A <i>yfiR</i> mutation partially suppresses the 
                     motility defect of a <i>yhjH</i> mutant.  Deletion of 
                     <i>yfiN</i> suppresses the swarming defect of the 
                     <i>yfiR</i> deletion mutant |CITS: [17941710]|.  YfiR 
                     counteracts relocation of |FRAME: EG12880-MONOMER DgcN| to 
                     the Z ring; reductive stress inactivates this YfiR function
                     |CITS: [27507823]|.
                     In uropathogenic <i>E. coli</i> UTI89, YfiR is a 
                     periplasmic protein that represses the diguanylate cyclase 
                     YfiN. YfiR is a substrate of the DsbA/DsbB disulfide bond 
                     forming system in <i>E. coli</i> UTI89 |CITS: [25112475]|. 
                     <i>yfiR, yfiN</i> and <i>yfiB</i> may form an operon in 
                     <i>E. coli</i> K-12. In <i>Pseudomonas aeruginosa</i>, this
                     operon is involved in exopolysaccharide synthesis |CITS: 
                     [20300602]|; in uropathogenic <i>E. coli</i>, YfiR and YfiN
                     were shown to have a role in cellulose production, but no 
                     evidence implicating YfiB in this process was obtained 
                     |CITS: [25112475]|. <i>E. coli</i> K-12 does not produce 
                     cellulose due to a mutation in the <i>bcs</i> operon (see 
                     |FRAME: EG12261|)."
                     /translation="MRFSHRLFLLLILLLTGAPILAQEPSDVAKNVRMMVSGIVSYTRW
                     PALSGPPKLCIFSSSRFSTALQENAATSLPYLPVIIHTQQEAMISGCNGFYFGNESPTF
                     QMELTEQYPSKALLLIAEQNTECIIGSAFCLIIHNNDVRFAVNLDALSRSGVKVNPDVL
                     MLARKKNDG"
                     /go_component="periplasmic space [goid 0042597] [evidence
                     IEA] [GO_REF 0000044]"
                     /go_component="cytosol [goid 0005829] [evidence IEA] [PMID
                     19054114]"
                     /go_process="bacterial-type flagellum-dependent swarming
                     motility [goid 0071978] [evidence IMP] [PMID 17941710]"
     gene            2735742..2736968
                     /gene="dgcN"
                     /locus_tag="b2604"
                     /label=dgcN
     CDS             2735742..2736968
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="dgcN"
                     /locus_tag="b2604"
                     /product="bifunctional diguanylate cyclase DgcN /
                     diguanylate cyclase"
                     /EC_number="2.7.7.65"
                     /label=dgcN
                     /note="DgcN is a diguanylate cyclase (DGC) that
                     dynamically relocates to the division site in response to 
                     envelope stress. DgcN localizes to the Z ring in an FtsZ- 
                     and ZipA-dependent manner in the presence of high levels of
                     c-di-GMP. |FRAME: G7354-MONOMER YfiR| counteracts 
                     relocation of DgcN to the Z ring |CITS: [27507823]|. During
                     growth on gluconeogenic carbon sources (glycerol, mannitol,
                     sorbitol) DgcN activity depletes cellular GTP and promotes 
                     growth arrest - this function of DgcN is also associated 
                     with an increased tolerance to various antibiotics |CITS: 
                     [37036337]|
                     DgcN is an inner membrane protein with two predicted 
                     transmembrane domains. The C terminus is located in the 
                     cytoplasm |CITS: [15919996]|. DgcN contains an N-terminal 
                     CHASE (<u>c</u>yclases/<u>h</u>istidine kinases 
                     <u>a</u>ssociated <u>se</u>nsory) domain |CITS: 
                     [26148715]|.
                     Deletion of <i>dgcN</i> partially restores motility of a 
                     <i>pdeH</i> mutant, suggesting that DgcN is one of four 
                     diguanylate cyclases that adjust c-di-GMP concentration for
                     motility control |CITS: [20303158]|. Deletion of 
                     <i>dgcN</i> also suppresses the swarming defect of a 
                     <i>yfiR</i> deletion mutant |CITS: [17941710]|. A 
                     <i>dgcN</i> deletion mutant shows 18-fold increased early 
                     biofilm formation and 10-fold increased swimming motility. 
                     Deletion of <i>dgcN</i> does not alter the concentration of
                     c-di-GMP inside the cell |CITS: [21181144]|. Overexpression
                     of <i>dgcN</i> increases resistance to polymyxin B |CITS: 
                     [27507823]|.
                     In uropathogenic <i>E. coli</i> UTI89, YfiN encodes a 
                     diguanylate cyclase that contributes to a cellulose 
                     production pathway. YfiN is inhibited by the periplasmic 
                     protein YfiR |CITS: [25112475]|. <i>yfiR, yfiN</i> and 
                     <i>yfiB</i> may form an operon in <i>E. coli</i> K-12. In 
                     <i>Pseudomonas aeruginosa</i>, this operon is involved in 
                     exopolysaccharide synthesis |CITS: [20300602]|; in 
                     uropathogenic <i>E. coli</i>, YfiR and YfiN were shown to 
                     have a role in cellulose production, but no evidence 
                     implicating YfiB in this process was obtained |CITS: 
                     [25112475]|. <i>E. coli</i> K-12 does not produce cellulose
                     due to a mutation in the <i>bcs</i> operon (see |FRAME: 
                     EG12261|).
                     DgcN: ""<b>d</b>i<b>g</b>uanylate <b>c</b>yclase <b>N</b>""
                     |CITS: [26148715]|.
                     Related review: |CITS: [33640237]|"
