     gene            2736984..2737466
                     /gene="yfiB"
                     /locus_tag="b2605"
                     /label=yfiB
     CDS             2736984..2737466
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yfiB"
                     /locus_tag="b2605"
                     /product="lipoprotein YfiB"
                     /label=yfiB
                     /note="YfiB is a verified lipoprotein according to
                     unpublished data by S. Matsuyama et al. (cited in |CITS: 
                     [12876315]|).
                     Under the conditions examined, <i>yfiB</i> is not essential
                     for viability of <i>E. coli</i> |CITS: [7559342]|.  A 
                     <i>yfiB</i> deletion mutant shows increased early biofilm 
                     formation |CITS: [21181144]|.  Under conditions when the 
                     <i>C. elegans</i> gut microbiota consists of a single <i>E.
                     coli</i> &Delta;<i>yfiB</i> mutant strain, the life span of
                     the nematode increases by 20% compared to colonization with
                     wild-type <i>E. coli</i> |CITS: [28622510]|.
                     <i>yfiR, yfiN</i> and <i>yfiB</i> may form an operon in 
                     <i>E. coli</i> K-12. In <i>Pseudomonas aeruginosa</i> this 
                     operon is involved in exopolysaccharide synthesis |CITS: 
                     [20300602]|; in uropathogenic <i>E. coli</i> YfiR and YfiN 
                     were shown to have a role in cellulose production, but no 
                     evidence implicating YfiB in this process was obtained 
                     |CITS: [25112475]|. <i>E. coli</i> K-12 does not produce 
                     cellulose due to a mutation in the <i>bcs</i> operon (see 
                     |FRAME: EG12261|)."
