     gene            complement(2738729..2739277)
                     /gene="rimM"
                     /locus_tag="b2608"
                     /label=rimM
     CDS             complement(2738729..2739277)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rimM"
                     /locus_tag="b2608"
                     /product="ribosome maturation factor RimM"
                     /label=rimM
                     /note="RimM is an assembly factor for the 30S ribosomal
                     subunit.  Ribosome assembly intermediates isolated from a 
                     <i>rimM</i> deletion strain have been characterized, 
                     showing that RimM promotes assembly of 3'-head domain 
                     proteins and stabilizes rRNA tertiary structure |CITS: 
                     [23293003]|.  The effect of RimM during <i>in vitro</i> 
                     reconstitution of the 30S ribosomal subunit has been 
                     investigated |CITS: [20188109]|.
                     RimM has affinity for the 30S ribosomal subunit, but not 
                     the 70S ribosome |CITS: [9226267]|.  Two conserved tyrosine
                     residues in the proposed PRC &beta;-barrel domain of RimM 
                     are responsible for specific interactions with the |FRAME: 
                     EG10918-MONOMER| |CITS: [15496525]|.  RimM is not directly 
                     required for wild-type 16S rRNA processing |CITS: 
                     [15496525]|.
                     A <i>rimM</i> deletion mutant accumulates 17S rRNA |CITS: 
                     [9422595][23611982]|, and the levels of polysomes decreases
                     while levels of free 30S and 50S subunits increase |CITS: 
                     [15496525]|.  The structure of the 30S ribosomal subunit of
                     a &Delta;<i>rimM</i> mutant was solved by cryo-EM 
                     reconstruction, showing the absence of some tertiary 
                     ribosomal proteins; similar structural defects exist in an 
                     <i>rsgA</i> mutant |CITS: [23611982]|. <i>rimM</i> mutants 
                     exhibit defects in growth and a slower rate of translation,
                     compared to wild type, and these phenotypes are suppressed 
                     by some <i>rpsM</i> (30S ribosomal subunit protein S13) and
                     <i>rpsS</i> (30S ribosomal subunit protein S19) mutations 
                     |CITS: [9226267][15496525]| or by RbfA overproduction 
                     |CITS: [9422595][11567010]|.  Mutations causing decreased 
                     RimM interaction with the 30S ribosomal subunit result in a
                     growth defect that is suppressed by mutations that increase
                     RimM production |CITS: [11514519]|.
                     Transcription of the operon containing the <i>rimM</i> gene
                     increases with the growth rate |CITS: [3290194]|.  A 
                     sequence element located between codons 18 and 50 of 
                     <i>rimM</i> appears to reduce the efficiency of <i>rimM</i>
                     translation |CITS: [2516239]|.  An mRNA secondary structure
                     which sequesters the <i>rimM</i> Shine-Dalgarno sequence is
                     thought to be responsible for this posttranscriptional 
                     regulation |CITS: [1569581]|. Deletion of <i>rimM</i> 
                     increases the growth defect of a <i>rsgA</i> mutant strain 
                     |CITS: [18223068]|.
                     Reviews: |CITS: [21529161][16890019]|"
