     CDS             complement(2739296..2739544)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rpsP"
                     /locus_tag="b2609"
                     /product="trifunctional 30S ribosomal subunit protein S16
                     / 30S ribosomal subunit / ribosome"
                     /label=rpsP
                     /note="The S16 protein is a component of the 30S subunit
                     of the ribosome and is essential for viability |CITS: 
                     [7559342]|.
                     S16 interacts with the 5' domain of 16S rRNA |CITS: 
                     [3373529][7916699]|.  Binding of S16 to 16S rRNA is 
                     dependent on prior binding of S4 and S20 |CITS: [4598121]|.
                      Subsequent binding of S16 suppresses non-native assembly 
                     intermediates and drives a conformational switch at helix 3
                     of 16S rRNA, stabilizing the decoding center of the 30S 
                     subunit |CITS: [19343072]|. Ensemble FRET experiments 
                     confirmed that S16 destabilizes the non-native S4-rRNA 
                     conformation |CITS: [26354770]|. S16 was also shown to be a
                     DNA-binding protein with 
                     Mg<sup>2+</sup>-Mn<sup>2+</sup>-dependent endonuclease 
                     activity |CITS: [8730873]|.  S16 preferentially binds to 
                     cruciform DNA structures; its endonuclease activity appears
                     to be sequence-specific |CITS: [9288907]|.  S16 may bind 
                     Zn<sup>2+</sup> |CITS: [11985624]|.
                     Expression of <i>rpsP</i> is induced 16-fold upon exposure 
                     of cells to the biocide polyhexamethylene biguanide |CITS: 
                     [16549663]|.
                     "
