     gene            2744190..2745068
                     /gene="nadK"
                     /locus_tag="b2615"
                     /label=nadK
     CDS             2744190..2745068
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="nadK"
                     /locus_tag="b2615"
                     /product="NAD kinase"
                     /EC_number="2.7.1.23"
                     /label=nadK
                     /note="NAD kinase appears to be an allosteric enzyme, with 
                     activity tightly coupled to the NADPH/NADP<sup>+</sup> and 
                     NADH/NAD<sup>+</sup> ratios present in the cell.  That 
                     suggests that NAD kinase may play an important role in the 
                     regulation of NADP turnover and size of the NADP pool 
                     |CITS: [3025169][11488932]|.
                     <i>nadK</i> is likely essential for growth |CITS: 
                     [12142426][16738554]|.
                     Site-directed mutagenesis studies of the <i>E. coli</i> 
                     enzyme showed that a R175G mutation relaxed the strict NAD 
                     substrate specificity of the enzyme, resulting in a low 
                     level of ATP-dependent NADH kinase activity |CITS: 
                     [15855156]|.
                     Structure-function relationships in NAD kinases from 
                     archaea, bacteria (including <i>E. coli</i>) and eukaryotes
                     have been reviewed |CITS: [16842123] [18391451] 
                     [19430699]|.
                     "
