     CDS             2746964..2747305
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="bamE"
                     /locus_tag="b2617"
                     /product="bifunctional outer membrane protein assembly
                     factor BamE / outer membrane protein assembly complex"
                     /label=bamE
                     /note="Sequence analysis indicates that BamE is a
                     lipoprotein in the outer membrane of <I>Escherichia 
                     coli</I> |CITS:[15126489]|. Affinity purification 
                     experiments have shown BamE copurifies with BamA, BamD, 
                     BamB, and BamC. These experiments also show BamE interacts 
                     with BamD, BamC, and BamA independently of BamB 
                     |CITS:[17404237]|.
                     Deletion of <i>bamE</i> results in increased sensitivity to
                     rifampin, cholate, and SDS/EDTA. Deletion of <i>bamE</i> 
                     results in reduced levels of the outer membrane proteins 
                     (OMPs) LamB and OmpA and an elevated level of DegP 
                     suggesting the presence of misfolded OMPs. Large quantities
                     of unfolded LamB monomer accumulate in <I>bamE degP</I> 
                     double mutants |CITS:[17404237]|. <i>bamE</i> null mutants 
                     show only slight defects in OMP assembly and membrane 
                     permeability |CITS: [22178970]|. BamE is implicated in the 
                     assembly of |FRAME: RCSF-MONOMER ""RcsF|-OmpA complexes; 
                     RcsF-OmpA complexes are almost undetectable and RcsF-BamA 
                     cross-linking is increased in <i>bamE</i> null strains 
                     |CITS: [27282389]| (see further |CITS: 
                     [31113900][31113901][37455652]|).
                     Genetic analysis and biochemical studies suggest that BamE 
                     has a function in stabilising the interaction between the 
                     BamA and BamD proteins |CITS: [17404237][22178970]| (see 
                     also |CITS: [37196764]|). Deletion of BamE results in 
                     increased protease sensitivity of BamA |CITS: [22178970]|. 
                     Purified BamE exists in both monomeric and dimeric forms 
                     which adopt different structures |CITS: [21207987]|. Whole 
                     cell purification of overexpressed BamE yields a mixture of
                     monomeric and dimeric BamE; when expressed in the 
                     periplasm, purified BamE is monomeric |CITS: [21212804]|. 
                     Purified monomeric BamE consists of two N-terminal 
                     &alpha;-helices and a C-terminal &beta;-sheet containing 3 
                     &beta;-strands |CITS: [21207987], [21212804]|.
                     <i>bamE</i> is a member of the &sigma;<sup>E</sup> regulon 
                     |CITS:[12900013]|. <I>bamE</I> expression is upregulated by
                     the presence of autoinducer 2 |CITS:[11514505]|. 
                     Cardiolipin binds to the Bam complex through BamE |CITS: 
                     [30442809]|.
                     Comment: |CITS: [21252940]|"
