                     /product="ribosome association toxin RatA"
                     /label=ratA
                     /note="RatA is a toxic protein that inhibits initiation of 
                     translation by specifically associating with the free 50S 
                     subunit of the ribosome and inhibiting 70S ribosome 
                     formation.  RatA is unable to dissociate 70S ribosomes and 
                     has no effect on cellular mRNAs |CITS: [21323758]|. 
                     Inducing expression of RatA causes inhibition of cell 
                     growth |CITS: [14594833][21323758]|.  Deletion of the 
                     orthologous <i>pasTI</i> locus alone in the uropathogenic 
                     <i>E. coli</i> CFT073 causes a defect in colonizing the 
                     kidneys of a mouse UTI model system and a defect in 
                     persister cell formation.  In contrast, deletion of 
                     <i>ratAB</i> does not affect persister cell formation in 
                     <i>E. coli</i> K-12 MG1655 and does not increase 
                     sensitivity to nitrosative stress caused by acidified 
                     sodium nitrite (ASN).  However, low-level expression of 
                     RatA does increase resistance to ASN |CITS: [23055930]|. 
                     RatA: ""<b>r</b>ibosome <b>a</b>ssociation <b>t</b>oxin 
                     <b>A</b>"" |CITS: [21323758]|"
