     CDS             2760343..2760714
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rnlB"
                     /locus_tag="b2631"
                     /product="bifunctional CP4-57 prophage; antitoxin RnlB /
                     RnlA-RnlB toxin-antitoxin complex"
                     /label=rnlB
                     /note="RnlB is the antitoxin of the RnlA-RnlB
                     toxin-antitoxin system.  Overexpression of RnlA in 
                     &Delta;<i>rnlAB</i> cells inhibits cell growth and causes 
                     mRNA degradation, while overexpression of RnlB in wild-type
                     cells suppresses the growth defect of the T4 <i>dmd</i> 
                     mutant |CITS: [20980243]|.  The RnlB protein is extremely 
                     unstable |CITS: [24112600]| and is stabilized in 
                     <i>clpX</i> or <i>lon</i> mutants |CITS: [20980243]|.
                     RnlB interacts with the DBD domain of RnlA and suppresses 
                     its RNase LS activity |CITS: [20980243][24112600]|. 
                     Reviews: |CITS: [22060041][26780368][31932311]|, Comments: 
                     |CITS: [22283468][22307030]|"
