                     /note="YfjR, which contains a helix-turn-helix motif to
                     bind DNA in its N-terminal domain, appears to belong to the
                     DeoR family of transcription factors, and it was predicted 
                     to regulate genes involved in processes related with phages
                     |CITS: [35880217]| and with biofilm formation |CITS: 
                     [16385049]|.
                     The transcription of the <i>yfjR</i> gene is affected by 
                     conditions that lead to biofilm formation |CITS: 
                     [35880217]|, and it increases 16-fold upon deletion of 
                     <i>tqsA</i> |CITS: [16385049]|.
                     "
