     gene            2769278..2769736
                     /gene="lfgA"
                     /locus_tag="b2643"
                     /label=lfgA
     CDS             2769278..2769736
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="lfgA"
                     /locus_tag="b2643"
                     /product="CP4-57 prophage; putative antirestriction
                     protein"
                     /label=lfgA
                     /note="Excision of CP4-57 prophage which includes 
                     <i>lfgABCDE</i> operon (formerly the <i>yfjXY ypjJ 
                     yfjZF</i> operon) increases biofilm formation primarily 
                     early in biofilm development |CITS: [19458652]|. 
                     Single-cell transcriptomic studies revealed that the 
                     <i>lfgABCDE</i> operon was transcribed when subjected to 
                     oxidative, acid and heat stress in wild-type strain BW25113
                     compared to an inactivated <i>mqsRA</i> mutant; the results
                     are not detected in population studies. |FRAME: 
                     G7571-MONOMER MqsA| binds to a putative palindromic 
                     sequence upstream of the operon repressing it's 
                     transcription. The |FRAME: G7379| protease but not LfgA 
                     prevents repression by MgsA under oxidative stress through 
                     degradation of MqsA |CITS: [38206055]|. <i>lfgA</i>, 
                     <U>l</U>ess <U>f</U>atality <U>g</U>ene <U>A</U> |CITS: 
                     [38206055]|."
                     /translation="MTTQTQYDLVPANGSEFELSVTQVPDEQHIRFWPQHFGTIPQWIT
                     LEPRIFAWMDRFCDEYCGGIWSFYTLSNGGAFMAPDADGDDKWHLLNGMNGNGAEMSAE
                     AAGIAVCLIEYSHHACLTECDAMTEHYYRLRDYALQHPESSAIMRIID"
                     /go_component="cytosol [goid 0005829] [evidence IEA] [PMID
                     19054114]"
     gene            2769745..2770227
                     /gene="lfgB"
                     /locus_tag="b2644"
                     /label=lfgB
     CDS             2769745..2770227
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="lfgB"
                     /locus_tag="b2644"
                     /product="CP4-57 prophage protease"
                     /label=lfgB
                     /note="LfgB (previously YfjY) is a protease that
                     selectively degrades the |FRAME: G7571-MONOMER| under 
                     stress conditions |CITS: [38206055]|.
                     Overexpression of <i>yfjY</i> from a multicopy plasmid 
                     results in a mutator phenotype |CITS: [15225322]|. 
                     Deletions in <i>lfgB</i> and excision in CP4-57 prophage 
                     increase biofilm formation primarily early in biofilm 
                     development |CITS: [19458652]|.
                     Single-cell transcriptomic studies revealed that the 
                     <i>lfgABCDE</i> operon (formerly the <i>yfjXY ypjJ 
                     yfjZF</i> operon) was transcribed when subjected to 
                     oxidative, acid and heat stress in wild-type strain BW25113
                     compared to an inactivated <i>mqsRA</i> mutant; the results
                     are not detected in population studies. The impact of LfgB 
                     on catalase activity was reduced upon deletion of |FRAME: 
                     RPOS-MONOMER|. Thus, LfgB degradation of MqsA results in 
                     derepression of |FRAME: EG10510|, activation of |FRAME: 
                     G7572-MONOMER|, and facilitation of the stress response 
                     |CITS: [38206055]|.
                     <i>lfgB</i>, <U>l</U>ess <U>f</U>atality <U>g</U>ene 
                     <U>B</U> |CITS: [38206055]|."
                     /translation="MMEQSLIPQTPVLPLTAQRTVKRALTLLDRHLRETGVAFTSTQAA
