     gene            complement(2789696..2790145)
                     /gene="kbp"
                     /locus_tag="b2665"
                     /label=kbp
     CDS             complement(2789696..2790145)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="kbp"
                     /locus_tag="b2665"
                     /product="K(+) binding protein"
                     /label=kbp
                     /note="Kbp is a potassium-binding protein that is required
                     for normal growth in the presence of high external 
                     concentrations of potassium and under salt-induced osmotic 
                     stress conditions.  Upon association with K<sup>+</sup>, 
                     Kbp undergoes a conformational change that results in 
                     compaction of the tertiary structure |CITS: [27112601]|. 
                     Kbp contains a BON domain that is thought to function as a 
                     membrane-binding domain, and a LysM domain that is 
                     associated with bacterial cell wall degradation |CITS: 
                     [17015655]|.  The BON domain is required for K<sup>+</sup> 
                     binding, while the LysM domain appears to stabilize the 
                     K<sup>+</sup>-bound complex |CITS: [27112601]|.
                     A solution structure of K<sup>+</sup>-bound Kbp has been 
                     determined |CITS: [27112601]|.
                     A <i>kbp</i> deletion mutant shows impaired growth in media
                     with elevated K<sup>+</sup> concentration |CITS: 
                     [27112601]|.  Both deletion and overexpression of 
                     <i>kbp</i> (<i>ygaU</i>) impact peptidoglycan structure; 
                     deletion of <i>kbp</i> individually and in combination with
                     |FRAME: EG11253-MONOMER <i>ldtD</i>| activates the |FRAME: 
                     PWY0-1485 ""Cpx two component pathway""|.  |FRAME: G7396 
                     ""<i>yqaE</i>""| and <i>kbp</i> may form a Cpx-P induced 
                     transcription unit |CITS: [25422305]|.
                     Expression of <i>kbp</i> is slightly induced under osmotic 
                     stress imposed by NaCl in both aerobic and anaerobic 
                     conditions |CITS: [17015655]|.  <i>kbp</i> belongs to the 
                     &sigma;<sup>S</sup> |CITS: [15716429]| and Cpx |CITS: 
                     [23564175][25422305]| regulons.
                     In <i>E. coli</i> BL21, downregulation of Kbp plays a role 
                     in enhancing tolerance to phenylpropanoids |CITS: 
                     [25277045]|.
                     Kbp: ""<b>K<sup>+</sup></b> <b>b</b>inding <b>p</b>rotein""
                     |CITS: [27112601]|
                     "
