     gene            2790570..2790869
                     /gene="ygaV"
                     /locus_tag="b2667"
                     /label=ygaV
     CDS             2790570..2790869
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ygaV"
                     /locus_tag="b2667"
                     /product="DNA-binding transcriptional regulator YgaV"
                     /label=ygaV
                     /note="YgaV is a transcriptional regulator involved in 
                     H<sub>2</sub>S-dependent antioxidative stress responses and
                     antibiotic resistance |CITS:[39324809]|. YgaV is 
                     responsible for upregulating the expression of iron uptake 
                     genes in response to intracellular H<sub>2</sub>S 
                     |CITS:[39324809]|.
                     Inhibition of <i>ygaV</i> expression by CRISPRi enhanced 
                     cellular fitness under treatment with the antibiotics 
                     erythromycin or methyl methanesulfonate (MMS) 
                     |CITS:[40352728]|.
                     YgaV binding to its genomic targets is enhanced when 
                     intracellular  reactive sulfur species increase, including 
                     H<sub>2</sub>S-derived polysulfides/supersulfides 
                     |CITS:[39324809][40763654]|. Polysulfidation of YgaV by 
                     polysulfides/supersulfides (including species generated 
                     from sulfide) alters its DNA-binding affinity 
                     |CITS:[39324809][40763654]|. In vitro, apo-YgaV responds 
                     preferentially to polysulfides rather than H2S itself 
                     |CITS:[40763654]|. Heme binding confers oxygen-dependent 
                     sulfide responsiveness to YgaV, enhancing cysteine 
                     oxidation by sulfide under aerobic but not anaerobic 
                     conditions |CITS:[40763654]|. Heme coordination depends on 
                     cysteine redox status, and DNA binding does not markedly 
                     alter heme binding |CITS:[40763654]|.
                     It has been proposed that YgaV may autoregulate its own 
                     expression |CITS: [18245262]|.
                     Genome-wide YgaV binding sites were determined <i>in 
                     vivo</i> by the chromatin immunoprecipitation method 
                     combined with lambda exonuclease digestion (ChIP-exo) in 
                     glucose M9 minimal medium |CITS: [34428301]|.
                     A knockout mutant of this gene was sensitive to boric acid 
                     exposure compared to most other gene knockouts; a 
                     complementation assay restored its intrinsic boric acid 
                     resistance |CITS: [38466471]|."
