     gene            2805975..2807513
                     /gene="emrB"
                     /locus_tag="b2686"
                     /label=emrB
     CDS             2805975..2807513
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="emrB"
                     /locus_tag="b2686"
                     /product="multifunctional multidrug efflux pump membrane
                     subunit EmrB / multidrug efflux pump EmrAB-TolC / 
                     deoxycholate efflux pump / CCCP efflux pump / nalidixate 
                     efflux pump"
                     /label=emrB
                     /note="EmrB is the inner membrane subunit of a tripartite
                     efflux pump that is implicated in the export of a variety 
                     of mainly hydrophobic compounds  - carbonylcyanide 
                     <i>m</i>-chlorophenylhydrazone (CCCP), 
                     tetrachlorosalicyanide (TSA), nalidixate, phenylmercury 
                     acetate and others (see |FRAME: CPLX0-2121| for more 
                     details).
                     <i>emrB</i> encodes a predicted integral inner membrane 
                     protein with 14 transmembrane domains; <i>emrB</i> is 
                     co-transcribed with <i>emrA</i> - predicted to encode a 
                     membrane fusion protein |CITS: [1409590][8021163]|. 
                     <i>emrB</i> is one of 35 efflux-encoding genes that have 
                     been deleted or inactivated in 'Efflux KnockOut-35' 
                     (EKO-35) -  a K-12 BW25133-derived strain that lacks 35 
                     efflux pumps and can be used as a platform to study their 
                     function |CITS: [36065018][36318669]|. Swimming motility is
                     increased in the <i>emrB</i> Keio collection mutant 
                     (BW25113 &Delta;<i>emrB::kan</i>) |CITS: [39529380]|.
                     EmrB is a member of the Drug:H<sup>+</sup> Antiporter-2 
                     family within the major facilitator superfamily |CITS: 
                     [8987357][26546518]|.
                     <i>emr</i>: <i><u>E</u>. coli</i> <u>m</u>ultidrug 
                     <u>r</u>esistance"
