     CDS             complement(2809871..2810299)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yqaA"
                     /locus_tag="b2689"
                     /product="DedA family protein YqaA"
                     /label=yqaA
                     /note="YqaA is predicted to be an inner membrane protein
                     with four transmembrane domains; topology analysis suggests
                     the C-terminus is located in the cytoplasm |CITS: 
                     [15919996]|.
                     YqaA ia a member of the DedA family of proteins |CITS: 
                     [23086209]|. <i>E. coli</i> K-12 contains 7 other DedA 
                     family members, namely |FRAME: EG10216 ""DedA""|, |FRAME: 
                     EG11824 ""YghB""|, |FRAME: EG11571 ""YabI""|, |FRAME: 
                     EG12017 ""YohD""|, |FRAME: G7609-MONOMER ""YqjA""|, |FRAME:
                     G6945-MONOMER ""YdjX""| and |FRAME: G6947 ""YdjZ""|.  
                     Collectively, the DedA family is essential in <i>E. 
                     coli</i> K-12 |CITS: [22301910]|.
                     A <i>yqaA</i> mutant has a defect in swarming, but not 
                     swimming motility |CITS: [17122336]|."
