     gene            complement(2831613..2832623)
                     /gene="ascG"
                     /locus_tag="b2714"
                     /label=ascG
     CDS             complement(2831613..2832623)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ascG"
                     /locus_tag="b2714"
                     /product="DNA-binding transcriptional repressor AscG"
                     /label=ascG
                     /note="The AscG, 
                     ""<b>A</b>rbutin-<b>s</b>alicin-<b>c</b>ellibiose,"" 
                     transcriptional regulator represses the expression of a 
                     cryptic operon (<i>ascFB</i>) whose genes are involved in 
                     transport and utilization of the &beta;-glucoside sugars 
                     arbutin, salicin, and cellibiose. This operon is activated 
                     only when the repressor is inactivated through the 
                     interruption of the gene by an insertion sequence 
                     |CITS:[1630307]|. AscG also regulates <i>prpBC</i> for 
                     propionate catabolism |CITS:[19633077]|.
                     Consistent with a broader in vivo model for many 
                     transcription factors (including AscG), regulation is 
                     compatible with primary stabilization of RNAP at promoters,
                     with fold-changes scaling approximately as the reciprocal 
                     of promoter basal activity and buffering 
                     promoter-to-promoter variability across contexts and 
                     perturbations |CITS: [40934320]|.
                     AscG is a GalR-type transcription factor and has a 
                     helix-turn-helix motif |CITS:[1630307][19633077]|. AscG 
                     recognizes and binds the consensus palindromic sequence 
                     TGAAACCGGTTTCA |CITS:[19633077]|.
                     A high level of AscG is always present in wild-type 
                     <i>Escherichia coli</i> cells |CITS:[19633077]|.  A 
                     positive correlation between cellular growth and the copy 
                     number of the protein AscG has been reported |CITS: 
                     [35694815]|.
                     The <i>ascG</i> gene is transcribed divergently from the 
                     operon it regulates |CITS:[1630307]|. <i>ascG</i> is 
                     paralogous to <i>galR</i> |CITS:[19633077]|.
                     The AscG binding landscape was globally mapped in vivo by 
                     standardized ChIP-seq and quantitatively modeled using 
                     BoltzNet, a biophysically informed neural network that 
                     infers binding energy from sequence data |CITS:[40335485]|.
                     The resulting ChIP-seq binding regions are available in 
                     RegulonDB (<a href=""https://regulondb.cc 
                     g.unam.mx/ht/dataset/TFBINDING/source=GALAGAN"">Galagan 
                     collection</a>), and the corresponding energy matrix and 
                     genomic binding profiles can be accessed at <a 
                     href=""http://boltznet.bu.edu"">boltznet.bu.edu</a> 
                     |CITS:[40335485]|."
