     gene            complement(2835932..2836402)
                     /gene="hycI"
                     /locus_tag="b2717"
                     /label=hycI
     CDS             complement(2835932..2836402)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="hycI"
                     /locus_tag="b2717"
                     /product="hydrogenase 3 maturation protease"
                     /label=hycI
                     /note="HycI is an endopeptidase that belongs to the M52 
                     peptidase family; it cleaves 32 amino acids off the 
                     carboxy-terminus of |FRAME: HYCELARGE-MONOMER HycE|, 
                     modifying it into its final form as the large subunit of 
                     hydrogenase 3 |CITS: [7851435][8756471][17150961]|.
                     The substrate HycE must have nickel bound in its center for
                     the processing step to take place |CITS: 
                     [8125094][10727938]|.  When nickel uptake is blocked, zinc 
                     can disrupt HycI proteolysis of HycE, possibly by binding 
                     in the nickel site of HycE |CITS: [11418115]|.  HycI shows 
                     a somewhat relaxed specificity for amino acid residues at 
                     the HycE cleavage site; however, HycI does not cleave a 
                     substrate where the C-terminal extension of HycE is swapped
                     for that of HybC |CITS: [10795682]|.  The HycI homolog HyfK
                     from <i>Pectobacterium atrosepticum</i> is able to process 
                     the <i>E. coli</i> HycE protein |CITS: [32731905]|.
                     A high resolution solution structure of the apo form of 
                     recombinant HycI was determined by nuclear magnetic 
                     resonance spectroscopy |CITS: [17150961]|.  In addition, 
                     recombinant HycI was crystallized in the presence of 
                     Ca<sup>2+</sup> and its crystal structure was determined at
                     1.70 &Aring; resolution.  Three specific metal binding 
                     sites were identified that might be involved in the 
                     C-terminal cleavage of HycE |CITS: [19720045]|.
                     Mutation of conserved residues in HycI which match 
                     cadmium-binding residues in the related endopeptidase HybD 
                     reduces HycI protease activity |CITS: [10727938]|.
                     A potential fourth hydrogenase enzyme is encoded by the 
                     <i>hyf</i> operon; it does not encode a HycI homolog or 
                     other protease.
                     HycI: |CITS: [7851435]|
                     Review: |CITS: [17091562]|"
