                     /product="multifunctional hydrogenase 3 [Fe-S] protein
                     HycG / hydrogenase 3 / hydrogenase / formate hydrogenlyase 
                     complex"
                     /EC_number="1.12.7.2"
                     /label=hycG
                     /note="The <i>hycBCDEFG</i> genes in <i>E. coli</i> K-12
                     encode the hydrogenase component (hydrogenase 3) of  the 
                     formate hydrogenlyase complex. HycG has similarity to small
                     subunits of hydrogenases |CITS: [1625581]|.
                     HycG is absent in extracts of a <i>slyD</i> mutant strain 
                     grown anaerobically in the absence of nickel; however, this
                     phenotype was restored upon addition of nickel to the 
                     growth medium |CITS:[ 25620052]|.
                     The HycG protein was undetectable in a <i>hypA</i> mutant 
                     and a <i>hypA</i> <i>slyD</i> double mutant |CITS:[ 
                     25620052]|."
