     gene            2845223..2845495
                     /gene="hypC"
                     /locus_tag="b2728"
                     /label=hypC
     CDS             2845223..2845495
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="hypC"
                     /locus_tag="b2728"
                     /product="bifunctional hydrogenase maturation factor HypC
                     / HypCD complex involved in hydrogenase maturation"
                     /label=hypC
                     /note="HypC is an accessory protein primarily involved in
                     the maturation of the |FRAME: HYDROG3-CPLX| isoenzyme and 
                     also participates in the maturation of |FRAME: 
                     FORMHYDROGI-CPLX hydrogenase 1| |CITS: 
                     [1482271][29996137]|.  Current data suggests that HypC 
                     delivers Fe-CO<sub>2</sub> to HypD, where CO<sub>2</sub> is
                     reduced to CO |CITS: [23851071]|.
                     The precursor of mature HycE (pre-HycE), the large subunit 
                     of hydrogenase 3, interacts directly with HypC, while the 
                     processed form of HycE is not associated with HypC |CITS: 
                     [9485446]|.  The amino-terminal methionine residue of HypC 
                     appears to be post-translationally removed, and the second 
                     amino acid residue, cysteine, is required for interaction 
                     of HypC with HypD as well as pre-HycE |CITS: 
                     [10783387][12441107][15504408]|.  HypC has low intrinsic 
                     ATPase activity; the purified HypC-HypD complex catalyzes 
                     hydrolysis of ATP with a 5-fold higher k<sub>cat</sub> of ~
                     0.85 s<sup>-1</sup> |CITS: [31614069]|.
                     A solution structure of HypC shows an OB-fold &beta;-barrel
                     with two C-terminal helixes |CITS: [17669368]|.  
                     Anaerobically purified HypC contains iron and 
                     CO<sub>2</sub> |CITS: [23851071]|.
                     A <i>hypC</i> mutation abolishes hydrogenase 3 activity and
                     reduces hydrogenase 1 activity |CITS: [1482271]|. HybG, a 
                     paralog of HypC, is required for maturation of hydrogenase 
                     2 |CITS: [11292801]|.  The specificity of HypC for 
                     maturation of hydrogenases 3 and 1, but not hydrogenase 2, 
                     was investigated.  The C-terminal &alpha;-helix of HypC is 
                     important for discriminating against hydrogenase 2, while 
                     changes in variable regions 1 and 2 negatively affect 
                     maturation of hydrogenase 1 by HypC |CITS: [29996137]|.
                     A potential RNA G-quadruplex structure, formed by 
                     guanine-rich sequences located in the coding sequence 
                     region of the gene, was identified for <i>hypC</i>.  This 
                     structure could regulate the expression of the gene, as 
                     observed for <i>hemL</i> expression |CITS: [31964733]|. 
                     Overexpression of the HypB and HypC accessory proteins 
                     improves the survivability of <i>E. coli</i> when grown 
                     under lethal acid stress from |FRAME: D-LACTATE| |CITS: 
                     [35271275]|.
                     HypC: ""<b>hy</b>drogenase, <b>p</b>leiotropic"" |CITS: 
                     [1849603]|
                     Reviews: |CITS: [17216401][26919691][27735784]|"
