     gene            complement(2860973..2862112)
                     /gene="nlpD"
                     /locus_tag="b2742"
                     /label=nlpD
     CDS             complement(2860973..2862112)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="nlpD"
                     /locus_tag="b2742"
                     /product="murein hydrolase activator NlpD"
                     /label=nlpD
                     /note="NlpD is a divisome associated, outer membrane
                     lipoprotein which activates the peptidoglycan (PG) 
                     hydrolase |FRAME: G7458-MONOMER ""AmiC""| involved in 
                     septal splitting |CITS: [20300061]|.
                     An NlpD-Mcherry fusion protein localises to the septal ring
                     division site; <i>envC nlpD</i> double null mutants show 
                     significant defects in cell separation resulting in very 
                     long chain formation due to a defect in septal 
                     peptidoglycan splitting |CITS: [19525345]|. NlpD contains a
                     lipoprotein signal sequence, a LysM (lysin motif) domain 
                     (associated with peptidoglycan binding |CITS: 
                     [18430080][24978025]|) and a LytM (lysostaphin/M23 
                     peptidase) domain (also found in |FRAME: EG12297-MONOMER 
                     EnvC|, |FRAME: G7484-MONOMER YgeR| and |FRAME: 
                     EG10013-MONOMER MepM|) |CITS: [19525345]|. NlpD (and EnvC) 
                     contain a degenerate LytM domain (dLytM) which is missing 
                     metal-binding and catalytic residues conserved in active 
                     LytM metallopeptidases |CITS: [20300061][23796240]|. The 
                     LysM domain of NlpD is both required and sufficient for 
                     proper localization to the septal ring; the dLytM domain is
                     required (but not sufficient) for amidase activation and 
                     cell separation <i>in vivo</i>; outer membrane localization
                     is required for proper NlpD activity |CITS: [28708841]|.
                     NlpD contains an N-terminal, unstructured linker domain 
                     which is implicated in targeting to the outer membrane 
                     |CITS: [34326538]|.
                     NlpD incorporates radiolabeled palmitic acid and 
                     accumulates as an uncleaved precursor in the presence of 
                     globomycin, an inhibitor of the lipoprotein signal 
                     peptidase; disruption of <i>nlpD</i> 
                     (<i>nlpD</i>::Km<sup>r</sup>) results in decreased 
                     stationary-phase survival after 7 days |CITS: [8132457]|. 
                     Genetic interaction analysis implicates |FRAME: 
                     G7644-MONOMER ""YraP""| and the Tol-Pal system in the 
                     NlpD-mediated activation of AmiC |CITS: [28708841]|. Cells 
                     lacking proper NlpD function 
                     (<sup>&Delta;SS</sup><i>nlpD</i>) have a phenotype that is 
                     indicative of outer membrane defects |CITS: [28708841]|. 
                     <i>nlpD</i>: new lipoprotein D |CITS: [8132457]|]"
