     CDS             complement(2863614..2864663)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="truD"
                     /locus_tag="b2745"
                     /product="tRNA pseudouridine(13) synthase"
                     /EC_number="5.4.99.27"
                     /label=truD
                     /note="TruD is responsible for biosynthesis of the 
                     pseudouridine13 modification of tRNA(Glu) |CITS: 
                     [12756329]|.
                     TruD is a member of a widely conserved fifth family of 
                     pseudouridine synthases that is unrelated to any previously
                     characterized pseudouridine synthases |CITS: [12756329]|.  
                     Crystal structures of TruD have been solved |CITS: 
                     [14999002][15039583][15135053][15208439]|.  The enzyme has 
                     an overall V-shaped structure; one arm is structurally 
                     similar to the catalytic domain of other pseudouridine 
                     synthases, while the other arm has a novel fold and has 
                     been named the TRUD domain |CITS: 
                     [14999002][15135053][15208439]|.  The conserved Glu31 
                     residue may act as the general base for proton abstraction 
                     |CITS: [19664587]|.
                     A <i>truD</i> mutant lacks the pseudouridine13 modification
                     at tRNA(Glu), but shows no growth defect |CITS: 
                     [12756329]|.  The conserved Asp80 is required for catalysis
                     |CITS: [12756329]|.
                     Reviews: |CITS: 
                     [17113994][17085441][22905870][25616362][40210524]|"
