     CDS             complement(2898106..2898777)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="queE"
                     /locus_tag="b2777"
                     /product="bifunctional putative 7-carboxy-7-deazaguanine
                     synthase QueE / 7-carboxy-7-deazaguanine synthase"
                     /EC_number="4.3.99.3"
                     /label=queE
                     /note="The QueE ortholog of <i>Bacillus subtilis</i>
                     catalyzes the 7-carboxy-7-deazaguanine synthase reaction of
                     the |FRAME: PWY-6703| pathway |CITS: [19354300]|. Deletion 
                     of <i>queE</i> results in absence of queuosine and 
                     epoxyqueuosine from cellular RNA |CITS: [21502530]|. A 
                     transposon insertion mutant or in-frame deletion of 
                     <i>queE</i> suppresses the filamentation phenotype due to a
                     strongly stimulated PhoQ/PhoP two-comPonent system |CITS: 
                     [27471053]|, and overexpression of <i>queE</i> leads to 
                     cell filamentation |CITS: [12900028][27471053]|. 
                     Transcription of <i>queE</i> is regulated by PhoP |CITS: 
                     [27471053]|.
                     QueE is cytoplasmic, but also shows specific localization 
                     to the Z ring in filamentous cells |CITS: [27471053]|."
