     gene            2921588..2922877
                     /gene="sdaC"
                     /locus_tag="b2796"
                     /label=sdaC
     CDS             2921588..2922877
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="sdaC"
                     /locus_tag="b2796"
                     /product="L-serine:H(+) symporter"
                     /label=sdaC
                     /note="<i>sdaC</i> encodes a (probable) L-serine:proton 
                     symporter which mediates the uptake of L-serine.
                     Early studies in K-12 strains characterized a specific, 
                     threonine insensitive, leucine inducible, L-serine uptake 
                     system which was energized by proton co-transport |CITS: 
                     [3129404][1331028]|.
                     <I>sdaC</I> is located in a operon with <I>sdaB</I>, 
                     encoding a serine deaminase |CITS: [8026499]|. <i>sdaC</i> 
                     has high sequence similarity with <i>tdcC</i> encoding a 
                     threonine transporter; over-expression of <i>sdaC</i> 
                     significantly increases the rate of (threonine insensitive)
                     serine uptake; <i>sdaC</i> encodes a protein with six 
                     predicted transmembrane domains |CITS: [8026499]|. SdaC is 
                     implicated in the adaption to glucose limitation; in the 
                     absence of exogenous serine, cells lacking the <i>sdaCB</i>
                     operon lyse upon glucose depletion and SdaC has a dominant 
                     role in this effect |CITS: [31680488]|.
                     In the Transporter Classification Database |CITS: 
                     [26546518]| SdaC is a member of the hydroxy/aromatic amino 
                     acid permease (HAAAP) family within the APC superfamily. An
                     <i>sdaC</i> insertion mutant (<i>dcrA60</i>::CAT) is 
                     deficient in phage C1 adsorption |CITS: [8752353]| (see 
                     further |CITS: [12558182]|). An <i>sdaC</i>::Tn<i>10</i> 
                     mutant is resistant to the peptide antibiotic, Colicin V 
                     |CITS:[15743941]|.
                     <i>dcrA</i>: see |CITS: [8752353]|"
