     gene            2922935..2924302
                     /gene="sdaB"
                     /locus_tag="b2797"
                     /label=sdaB
                     /note="By making use of micro arrays analysis it was
                     concluded that anarobiosis do not affect the expression of 
                     the sdaB gene, although FNR appears to activate it.  A 
                     putative FNR binding site, which is not shown in the paper,
                     was identified upstream of this operon |CITS: [12754220]|."
     CDS             2922935..2924302
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="sdaB"
                     /locus_tag="b2797"
                     /product="bifunctional L-serine deaminase II / L-serine
                     deaminase"
                     /EC_number="4.3.1.17"
                     /label=sdaB
                     /note="L-serine deaminase II (SdaB) is one of three
                     enzymes carrying
                     out the sole step in the
                     pathway of L-serine degradation, converting serine into a 
                     basic
                     cellular building block, pyruvate.
                     SdaB catalyzes the conversion of L-serine into pyruvate and
                     ammonia |CITS: [2013569]|.
                     Much like its companion enzyme |FRAME: 
                     LSERINEDEAM1-MONOMER|, purified
                     SdaB requires activation <i>in vitro</i> with iron
                     and dithiothrietol, suggesting that it, too, has
                     a catalytically important iron-sulfur cluster |CITS: 
                     [2013569]|.
                     Like fellow serine deaminase gene |FRAME: G7624|, 
                     <i>sdaB</i>
                     is transcribed under glucose-limited conditions in complex 
                     medium |CITS: [8385012]|."
