     gene            complement(2926400..2927047)
                     /gene="fucA"
                     /locus_tag="b2800"
                     /label=fucA
     CDS             complement(2926400..2927047)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="fucA"
                     /locus_tag="b2800"
                     /product="bifunctional L-fuculose-phosphate aldolase / 
                     D-ribulose-phosphate aldolase"
                     /EC_number="4.1.2.17"
                     /label=fucA
                     /note="FucA can function as both an L-fuculose-phosphate 
                     aldolase and a D-ribulose-phosphate aldolase, the third 
                     enzyme of the L-fucose and D-arabinose degradation 
                     pathways, respectively.  However, production of FucA is 
                     only
                     induced by L-fucose |CITS: [4323967][4928018]|.
                     The substrate specificity of the enzyme was tested with a 
                     partially purified preparation from an unnamed <i>E. 
                     coli</i>
                     strain |CITS: [OZAKI90]|.
                     Crystal structures of the enzyme and a number of point 
                     mutants have been solved.  The combination of structural 
                     data and enzymatic activity of mutants allowed modelling 
                     and refinement of the catalytic mechanism of the enzyme. 
                     |CITS: [8515438][15299567][8676381][10821675][11054289]| 
                     The enantiomeric selectivity of the enzyme has been studied
                     |CITS: [10821675]|.
                     A <i>fucAO</i> deletion mutant colonizes the mouse 
                     intestine and maintains its population at a lower level 
                     than wild
                     type; the accumulation of fuculose-1-phosphate appears to 
                     enable the mutant to switch to utilization of ribose for 
                     growth |CITS: [17709419]|.
                     "
