                     /label=fucI
     CDS             2928943..2930718
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="fucI"
                     /locus_tag="b2802"
                     /product="bifunctional L-fucose isomerase / D-arabinose
                     isomerase"
                     /EC_number="5.3.1.25; 5.3.1.3"
                     /label=fucI
                     /note="FucI can function as both an L-fucose isomerase and
                     a D-arabinose isomerase, the first enzymes of the L-fucose 
                     and D-arabinose degradation pathways, respectively. 
                     However, production of FucI is only induced by L-fucose 
                     |CITS: [4928018]|.
                     Between the two anomers of L-fucose,only the &alpha;-form 
                     adopts a position suitable for the ring opening reaction 
                     |CITS: [9367760]|.
                     A crystal structure of the enzyme has been solved at 2.5 
                     &Aring; resolution |CITS: [9367760]|.
                     An amber mutation has been generated |CITS: [12853150]|."
