                     /product="bifunctional L-fuculokinase / D-ribulokinase"
                     /EC_number="2.7.1.51"
                     /label=fucK
                     /note="FucK can function as both an L-fuculokinase and a 
                     D-ribulokinase, the second enzyme of the L-fucose and 
                     D-arabinose degradation pathways, respectively.  However, 
                     production of FucK is only induced by L-fucose |CITS: 
                     [4323967][4928018]|.
                     An <i>fucK</i> deletion mutant colonizes the mouse 
                     intestine as well as wild type, but is defective in 
                     maintenance of the population |CITS: [15123798]|.
                     "
