     gene            complement(2933502..2934602)
                     /gene="rlmM"
                     /locus_tag="b2806"
                     /label=rlmM
     CDS             complement(2933502..2934602)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rlmM"
                     /locus_tag="b2806"
                     /product="23S rRNA 2'-O-ribose C2498 methyltransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.1.1.186"
                     /label=rlmM
                     /note="RlmM is the methyltransferase responsible for
                     methylation of 23S rRNA at the 2'-<i>O</i> position of the 
                     ribose at the C2498 nucleotide within the peptidyl 
                     transferase loop. <i>In vitro</i>, the enzyme is active on 
                     naked 23S rRNA |CITS: [19400805][22923526]| and unmodified 
                     domain V alone |CITS: [22923526]|, but not assembled 50S 
                     ribosomal subunits or ribosomes |CITS: [19400805]|. Crystal
                     structures of RlmM have been solved |CITS: 
                     [22923526][23722841]|, showing the presence of an 
                     N-terminal THUMP domain and aC-terminal Rossmann-like fold 
                     methyltransferase domain |CITS: [22923526]|.
                     RlmM was predicted to be an RNA 2'-O-ribose 
                     methyltranserase by sequence similarity. The extended 
                     N-terminus may act in target recognition |CITS: 
                     [11293658]|. Phylogenetic analysis of this protein family 
                     has been performed |CITS: [12527203]|. Phylogenetic 
                     profiling shows an unexplained link between RlmM and RdgC 
                     |CITS: [22411911]|.
                     An <i>rlmM</i> mutant has a slightly longer doubling time 
                     in rich medium than wild type and is slowly out-competed by
                     wild type in a growth competition experiment |CITS: 
                     [19400805]|. A knockout of <i>rlmM</i> in combination with 
                     <i>rluE</i> was viable at both 37 and 20&deg;C but resulted
                     in large defects on ribosome assembly and peptidyl 
                     transferase activity at 20&deg;C |CITS: [35260421]|.
                     RlmM: ""<b>r</b>RNA <b>l</b>arge subunit 
                     <b>m</b>ethyltransferase <b>M</b>"" |CITS: [19400805]|"
