                     /product="DUF423 domain-containing inner membrane protein
                     YgdD"
                     /label=ygdD
                     /note="YgdD is an inner membrane protein with four
                     predicted transmembrane domains.  The C terminus is located
                     in the cytoplasm |CITS: [15919996]|.  Structural modeling 
                     of YgdD predicts that it will form a homotrimer |CITS: 
                     [26335199]|.  YgdD has been implicated in the response to 
                     the antimicrobial peptide, arasin |CITS: [26860543]|."
