     gene            2937901..2938344
                     /gene="csdE"
                     /locus_tag="b2811"
                     /label=csdE
     CDS             2937901..2938344
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="csdE"
                     /locus_tag="b2811"
                     /product="sulfur acceptor protein CsdE"
                     /label=csdE
                     /note="CsdA and CsdE combine to form the CSD sulfur
                     transfer system.  CsdA activity doubles in the presence of 
                     CsdE, which contains a cysteine residue (C61) that acts to 
                     accept sulfur liberated via the desulfinase activity of 
                     CsdA |CITS: [15901727]|.  A physiologically relevant sulfur
                     acceptor from CsdE has not been identified yet. CsdE also 
                     interacts with and may be able to transfer sulfur to TcdA 
                     |CITS: [20054882]|; a transient physical interaction 
                     between CsdE and TcdA was also shown by NMR and 
                     crosslinking experiments |CITS: [25897750]|. Additional 
                     proteins that interact with CsdE have been identified 
                     |CITS: [20734996]|.
                     The p<i>K<sub>a</sub></i> of the C61 residue was determined
                     to be 6.5 |CITS: [20734996]|.
                     An NMR solution structure of CsdE has been solved |CITS: 
                     [15930006]|.  CsdE migrates as a dimer on a gel filtration 
                     column |CITS: [15901727]|, but both the solution |CITS: 
                     [15930006]| and crystal |CITS: [26944665]| structures show 
                     it as a monomer.  A crystal structure of the CsdA-CsdE 
                     complex shows a CsdA dimer in which each subunit 
                     independently interacts with one CsdE subunit, for an 
                     overall stoichiometry of CsdA<sub>2</sub>CsdE<sub>2</sub>. 
                     The structure suggests that conformational flexibility of 
                     the C61-containing loop in CsdE enables sulfur transfer 
                     |CITS: [23913692]|.
                     A <i>csdE</i> mutant contains only 2% of the 
                     ct<sup>6</sup>A modification in tRNAs and has lower 
                     decoding efficiency than wild type |CITS: [23242255]|. 
                     CsdE: ""<b>c</b>ysteine <b>s</b>ulfinate 
                     <b>d</b>esulfinase"" |CITS: [15901727]|"
