     gene            complement(2939440..2940537)
                     /gene="mltA"
                     /locus_tag="b2813"
                     /label=mltA
     CDS             complement(2939440..2940537)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="mltA"
                     /locus_tag="b2813"
                     /product="bifunctional membrane-bound lytic murein
                     transglycosylase A / peptidoglycan lytic 
                     exotransglycosylase"
                     /label=mltA
                     /note="<i>mltA</i> encodes a membrane bound lytic murein 
                     transglycosylase which cleaves the &beta;-1,4 glycosidic 
                     bond between <i>N</i>-acetylglucosamine (GlcNAc) and 
                     <i>N</i>-acetylmuramic acid (MurNAc) residues of 
                     peptidoglycan with the concomitant formation of a 
                     1,6-anhydro ring at the MurNAc residue.
                     MltA is an outer membrane lipoprotein |CITS: 
                     [8288527][9287002]|. Purifed MltA degrades insoluble murein
                     sacculi to produce soluble muropeptides and degrades 
                     isolated linear glycan strands (poly GlcNAc-MurNAc) to 
                     produce anhydro-disaccharide units |CITS: 
                     [8405923][8288527]|. Purified MltA degrades the purified 
                     cell wall sacculus to produce the following major products 
                     (in order of abundance): tetra-A1 
                     (GlcNAc-1,6-anhydro-MurNAc monomer with tetrapeptide stem);
                     tetra2-A2 (a GlcNAc-1,6-anhydro-MurNAc dimer with 
                     crosslinked tetrapeptide stems); tri-A1 
                     (GlcNAc-1,6-anhydro-MurNAc monomer with tripeptide stem) 
                     plus other variations in smaller amounts. The reaction 
                     generates both cross-linked and non-crosslinked products; 
                     it does not generate products that are indicative of an 
                     endolytic transglycosylase reaction |CITS: [23421439]|. 
                     Purified MltA interacts with |FRAME: EG10605-MONOMER 
                     ""PBP1B""|, |FRAME: G7322-MONOMER ""PBP1C""|, |FRAME: 
                     EG10606-MONOMER ""PBP2""|, |FRAME: EG10341-MONOMER 
                     ""PBP3""|, |FRAME: EG10748-MONOMER ""PBP1A""| (through an 
                     unknown periplasmic factor), and |FRAME: G6968-MONOMER 
                     ""MipA""| |CITS: [10037771]|. MltA, PBP1B and MipA form a 
                     trimeric complex <i>in vitro</i> |CITS: [10037771]|. 
                     Purified, crystallized MltA (lacking its lipid anchor) is a
                     'kidney bean' shaped monomer; the protein contains two 
                     domains separated by a large groove which may constitute 
                     the substrate binding site |CITS: [16139297][16618494]|. 
                     Crystal structures have also been obtained for an inactive 
                     MltA mutant, in apo form and in complex with chitohexaose -
                     a substrate analog |CITS: [17502382]|.
                     Induced overexpression of MltA results in spheroblasting 
                     and lysis of cells grown at 30&deg; C, the optimal 
                     temperature for enzymatic activity |CITS: [9287002]|. A 
                     strain lacking three lytic transglycosylases, MltA, MltB 
                     and Slt70 shows no change in morphology or growth but 
                     significant changes to peptidoglycan composition including 
                     decreased anhydromuropeptide content and an increase in L-D
                     peptide cross links |CITS: [9287002]|. A strain lacking 
                     MltA, MltB and Slt70 shows a significant reduction in 
                     murein turnover without affecting growth |CITS: 
                     [10572120]|.
                     <i>E. coli</i> K-12 contains other lytic murein 
                     transglycosylases including |FRAME: G7410-MONOMER 
                     ""MltB""|, |FRAME: G7533-MONOMER ""MltC""|, |FRAME: 
                     EG10246-MONOMER ""MltD|, |FRAME: EG11373-MONOMER ""MltF""|,
                     |FRAME: G6622-MONOMER ""EmtA""| and |FRAME: EG10950-MONOMER
                     ""Slt70""|. |FRAME: EG11494 ""MltG""|, an inner membrane 
                     protein and potential PG terminase, also has lytic murein 
                     transglycosylase activity.
                     Related reviews:  |CITS: [8765311][18266855][22126997]|"
