                     /product="trifunctional exodeoxyribonuclease V subunit
                     RecD / 5' to 3' ATP-dependent DNA helicase / 
                     exodeoxyribonuclease V"
                     /EC_number="3.1.11.5; 5.6.2.3"
                     /label=recD
                     /note="RecD is one of three proteins of the heterotrimeric 
                     helicase/nuclease complex known as Exonuclease V or RecBCD 
                     that promotes homologous recombination in the repair of 
                     double-strand DNA breaks and during bacterial conjugation. 
                     RecD is essential for the ATP-dependent double-stranded DNA
                     exonuclease activity of Exonuclease V |CITS: [3526335]|. 
                     Over-expressed, purified RecD (his-RecD) possesses ssDNA 
                     dependent ATPase activity and 5' to 3' DNA helicase 
                     activity |CITS: [9092551][12815438]|. RecD is a superfamily
                     1 (SF1) helicase (see |CITS: [20456941]|)."
