     gene            complement(2945820..2949362)
                     /gene="recB"
                     /locus_tag="b2820"
                     /label=recB
     CDS             complement(2945820..2949362)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="recB"
                     /locus_tag="b2820"
                     /product="trifunctional exodeoxyribonuclease V subunit
                     RecB / 3' to 5' ATP-dependent DNA helicase / 
                     exodeoxyribonuclease V"
                     /EC_number="3.1.11.5; 5.6.2.4"
                     /label=recB
                     /note="RecB is one of three proteins of the heterotrimeric 
                     helicase/nuclease complex known as Exonuclease V or RecBCD 
                     that promotes homologous recombination in the repair of 
                     double-strand DNA breaks and during bacterial conjugation. 
                     Over-expressed, purified RecB has DNA-dependent ATPase 
                     activity but no exonuclease activity; the ATPase activity 
                     of RecB is stimulated by both single-stranded (ss) DNA and 
                     double-stranded (ds) DNA; when combined together purified 
                     RecB and RecC exhibit ATP-dependent exonuclease activity on
                     dsDNA |CITS: [3155726]|. Purified RecB has ATP-dependent 
                     DNA helicase activity - it displaces oligonucleotides 
                     annealed to ss phage DNA |CITS: [1311326]|. RecB is a 
                     superfamily 1 (SF1) helicase (see |CITS: [20456941]|).
                     Purified RecB lacking the C-terminal 251 amino acids is an 
                     ATP-dependent helicase and a ssDNA dependent ATPase; when 
                     reconstituted with RecC and a histidine-tagged RecD the 
                     complex is a processive DNA helicase but has no nuclease 
                     activity |CITS: [9448271]|. The C-terminal domain of RecB 
                     (RecB30) is responsible for the nuclease activity 
                     associated with the RecBCD complex; purified RecB30 
                     degrades linear ssDNA and dsDNA and can cleave cleave 
                     circular ssDNA and dsDNA; Mg<sup>2+</sup> is required for 
                     RecB30 nucleolytic activity |CITS: [16388588][9790841]|. 
                     The C-terminal domain of RecB is required for the 
                     constitutive (Chi-independent) RecA protein loading that 
                     occurs in a RecBC complex |CITS: [10731409]|.
                     Purified RecB is an ATP-dependent 3' to 5' ssDNA 
                     translocase/helicase; it can displace 20-mer 
                     oligonucleotides annealed at the 5' end or the middle of a 
                     60 base oligonucleotide |CITS: [9150267]|.
                     <i>recB</i> belongs to a network of genes which facilitate 
                     stress-induced mutagenesis (SIM) in <i>E. coli</i> K-12 
                     |CITS: [23224554]|.
                     Reviews: |CITS: [25131811]|"
