     gene            complement(2949355..2952243)
                     /gene="ptrA"
                     /locus_tag="b2821"
                     /label=ptrA
     CDS             complement(2949355..2952243)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ptrA"
                     /locus_tag="b2821"
                     /product="bifunctional protease 3 / protease"
                     /EC_number="3.4.24.55"
                     /label=ptrA
                     /note="Protease III is a periplasmic protein that rapidly 
                     degrades small proteins and peptides <i>in vitro</i> |CITS:
                     [7037737][374413][15502359][7680857]|.
                     Protease III is partially responsible for degrading 
                     A-&beta;-lactamase as well as misfolded MalE31 |CITS: 
                     [2013581][9535871]|.
                     Protease III is a zinc metalloendopeptidase with a 
                     nontraditional zinc-binding motif, featuring the consensus 
                     sequence HXXEH rather than the more traditional HEXXH 
                     |CITS: [1733942][1570301]|. In addition to the two 
                     histidines in the zinc-binding motif, glutamate162 is also 
                     required for zinc coordination |CITS: [8099278]|.
                     A 50 kDa polypeptide with no apparent protease function 
                     derived from the N-terminal end of protease III can be 
                     found in the periplasm under some circumstances |CITS: 
                     [2993229]|."
