     gene            complement(2958521..2959396)
                     /gene="lgt"
                     /locus_tag="b2828"
                     /label=lgt
     CDS             complement(2958521..2959396)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="lgt"
                     /locus_tag="b2828"
                     /product="phosphatidylglycerol--prolipoprotein
                     diacylglyceryl transferase"
                     /EC_number="2.5.1.145"
                     /label=lgt
                     /note="Lgt catalyses the transfer of an 
                     <i>sn</i>-1,2-diacylglyceryl group from 
                     phosphatidylglycerol to the sulfhydryl group of the 
                     prospective N-terminal cysteine of a proliporotein |CITS:[ 
                     8051048]|. It is the first of 3 sequential reactions 
                     (catalysed by Lgt, |FRAME: EG10548-MONOMER| and |FRAME: 
                     EG10168-MONOMER| respectively) that result in the formation
                     of mature triacylated lipoproteins, including |FRAME: 
                     EG10544-MONOMER|.
                     Lgt is an essential inner membrane protein |CITS: 
                     [2644208][22287519][35938851]|. <i>lgt</i> (formerly 
                     <i>umpA</i>) mutants are defective in diacylglycerol 
                     modification of prolipoprotein <i>in vitro</i> and <i>in 
                     vivo</i> |CITS: [7896715]|.
                     Lgt contains 7 transmembrane segments; the N-terminus faces
                     the periplasm and the C-terminus faces the cytoplasm |CITS:
                     [22287519]|. Lgt is a peripheral membrane protein 
                     associating loosely with the cytoplasmic face of the inner 
                     membrane |CITS: [18602442]|.
                     A conserved histidine residue, His-103, is essential for 
                     enzyme activity |CITS:[7592473][9139912]|; His-103 is not 
                     essential for enzyme activity |CITS: [22287519]| <i>lgt</i>
                     and <i>thyA</i> form an operon |CITS: [7896715]|.
                     Lgt is a target for the development of novel antibiotics 
                     |CITS: [33875545]|. Cells depleted of Lgt become rounder 
                     and wider, lose DNA, display a membrane defect and 
                     eventually lyse; deletion of |FRAME: EG10544 <i>lpp</i>| 
                     only partially restores growth of an Lgt depletion strain 
                     suggesting that Lgt is essential independently of Lpp and 
                     other lipoproteins are important for cell viability |CITS: 
                     [35938851]|.
                     <i>umpA</i>:  <U>u</U>nidentified <U>m</U>embrane 
                     <U>p</U>rotein |CITS: [2644208]|<BR><i>lgt</I>: 
                     pro<U>l</U>ipoprotein diacyl<U>g</U>lycerol 
                     <U>t</U>ransferase (see |CITS: [7896715]|)
                     Comment: |CITS: [22366420]|
                     "
