     CDS             2964956..2965996
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="tas"
                     /locus_tag="b2834"
                     /product="putative NADP(H)-dependent aldo-keto reductase
                     Tas"
                     /label=tas
                     /note="Tas is a protein with similarity to aldo-keto
                     reductases |CITS: [9560382][14517983][23103600]|.  The 
                     physiological substrate is unknown.
                     A crystal structure of Tas has been solved, showing a 
                     canonical (&beta;/&alpha;)<sub>8</sub> barrel with an 
                     NADP(H) molecule bound to the protein |CITS: [14517983]|. 
                     Re-evaluation of the structural data led |CITS: [23103600]|
                     to suggest that the protein is a homodimer.
                     In experiments with an auxotrophic <i>E. coli</i> B/r 
                     strain, Tas was required for starvation-associated 
                     mutational suppression of a <i>tyrA14</i>(oc) allele. 
                     Multicopy <i>tas</i> expression suppressed the tyrosine 
                     auxotrophy of a <i>tyrA14</i>(oc) <i>leu308</i>(am) mutant,
                     which has a prephenate dehydrogenase defect |CITS: 
                     [9560382]|.
                     Sequence differences between <i>E. coli</i> strains B and 
                     K-12 have been noted |CITS: [11470487]|.
                     Tas: ""<b>t</b>yrosine <b>a</b>uxotrophy 
                     <b>s</b>uppressor"" |CITS: [9560382]|
                     Review: |CITS: [23103600]|"
