     gene            complement(2974123..2975541)
                     /gene="araE"
                     /locus_tag="b2841"
                     /label=araE
     CDS             complement(2974123..2975541)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="araE"
                     /locus_tag="b2841"
                     /product="bifunctional arabinose:H(+) symporter /
                     transport of arabinose"
                     /label=araE
                     /note="AraE is an arabinose/proton symporter responsible
                     for the uptake of arabinose. Studies in membrane vesicles 
                     have shown that AraE can transport L-arabinose with low 
                     affinity (140-320 &mu;M) and arabinose transport is coupled
                     with proton transport |CITS: [6282256]|. The AraE protein 
                     has been overproduced and reconstituted in liposomes as an 
                     arabinose/proton symporter |CITS: [3520228]|. AraE is a 
                     member of the major facilitator superfamily (MFS) of 
                     transporters |CITS: [1419050]|. Arabinose is the sole 
                     inducer of <i>araE</i> expression |CITS: [6282256]|, which 
                     is controlled by the AraC regulator. An inhibitory effect 
                     on <i>araE</i> induced by arabinose appeared in the 
                     presence of xylose |CITS:[ 29140539]|. Imported arabinose 
                     is catabolized to xylulose-5-phosphatel, which then enters 
                     the pentose phosphate pathway."
