     gene            complement(2976647..2977483)
                     /gene="kduI"
                     /locus_tag="b2843"
                     /label=kduI
     CDS             complement(2976647..2977483)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="kduI"
                     /locus_tag="b2843"
                     /product="trifunctional 5-dehydro-4-deoxy-D-glucuronate
                     isomerase / 5-dehydro-4-deoxy-D-glucuronate isomerase / 
                     glucose-6-phosphate isomerase"
                     /EC_number="5.3.1.17; 5.3.1.9"
                     /label=kduI
                     /note="KduI was a predicted 5-keto 4-deoxyuronate
                     isomerase due to its high sequence similarity to the enzyme
                     from <i>Erwinia chrysanthemi</i>.  In unpurified form, the 
                     enzyme appeares to be able to utilize both glucuronate and 
                     galacturonate, perhaps catalyzing the same reaction as 
                     |FRAME: UXAC-MONOMER ""UxaC""|.  While UxaC expression is 
                     repressed under osmotic stress conditions, KduI expression 
                     appears to be unaffected, and it could therefore substitute
                     for UxaC |CITS: [23437267]|.  The purified protein was 
                     recently shown to catalyze the activity of |FRAME: 
                     EC-5.3.1.17| in coupled assays with KduD from 
                     <i>Pectobacterium carotovorum</i> or <i>Streptococcus 
                     agalactiae</i> |CITS: [25605731]|.
                     Based on its structural similarity to the <i>Pyrococcus 
                     furiosus</i> phosphoglucose isomerase, catalytic activity 
                     of KduI was tested with a panel of substrates; the enzyme 
                     showed activity with glucose-6-phosphate, glucuronate, and 
                     fructose-6-phosphate.  The enzyme binds zinc, but catalytic
                     activity is metal-independent |CITS: [32179131]|.
                     Crystal |CITS: [9761873][16152643]| and solution |CITS: 
                     [27227414]| structures of KduI have been solved.  The 
                     enzyme binds a metal ion tentatively identified as 
                     Zn<sup>2+</sup> and is structurally similar to members of 
                     the cupin superfamily of proteins |CITS: [16152643]|. <i>In
                     vivo</i> homomultimeric KduI interaction can be detected in
                     cross-linking experiments |CITS: [21697552]|. Solution 
                     structure data obtained by SAXS suggests the existence of a
                     mixture of high- and low-MM oligomers |CITS: [27227414]|.  
                     Catalytic activity at different enzyme concentrations 
                     suggest that the active form of the enzyme is the homodimer
                     |CITS: [32179131]|.
                     KduI was identified as a protein whose expression is 8-fold
                     lower in E. coli found in the cecum of mice that were fed a
                     casein diet compared to mice fed a starch diet |CITS: 
                     [22427493]|.  Expression of <i>kduI</i> is increased in the
                     presence of galacturonate and glucuronate |CITS: 
                     [23437267]|.
                     "
