     gene            complement(2987819..2988262)
                     /pseudo
                     /gene="ygeK"
                     /locus_tag="b2855"
                     /label=ygeK
     CDS             complement(2987819..2988262)
                     /pseudo
                     /gene="ygeK"
                     /locus_tag="b2855"
                     /product="putative DNA-binding transcriptional regulator
                     YgeK"
                     /label=ygeK
                     /note="YgeK is a predicted member of the NarL family of
                     response regulators of two-component regulatory systems. 
                     The protein lacks the receiver domain, which usually 
                     contains an Asp residue that is phosphorylated by the 
                     cognate histidine kinase. However, expressed and purified 
                     YgeK can be phosphorylated <i>in vitro</i> by the 
                     noncognate histidine kinases BarA and UhpB |CITS: 
                     [15522865]|.
                     On the other hand, it was suggested that YgeK belongs to 
                     the LuxR family of transcription factors |CITS: 
                     [35880217]|. This protein contains a helix-turn-helix motif
                     to bind DNA in its C-terminal domain |CITS: [35880217]|.
                     Upstream of the <i>ygeK</i> gene, a sequence was found that
                     could work as a transcriptional promoter, and the 
                     transcription of the <i>ygeK</i> gene is affected by 
                     conditions that generate general transcriptional 
                     termination and it is also affected by <i>hupA</i>,<i> 
                     hupB</i> and <i>rpoS</i> mutants |CITS: [35880217]|.
                     "
