     CDS             3000869..3002065
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ygeX"
                     /locus_tag="b2871"
                     /product="2,3-diaminopropionate ammonia-lyase"
                     /EC_number="4.3.1.15"
                     /label=ygeX
                     /note="Unlike <i>Salmonella typhimurium</i>, <i>E.
                     coli</i> only shows weak growth on 2,3-diaminopropionate as
                     the sole source of carbon.  This difference may be due to 
                     the very low expression levels of 2,3-diaminopropionate 
                     ammonia-lyase in <i>E. coli</i> |CITS: [22904288]|. 
                     2,3-Diaminopropionate ammonia-lyase is not stereospecific 
                     and catalyzes the &alpha;,&beta;-elimination of both the D 
                     and L stereoisomer of 2,3-diaminopropionate |CITS: 
                     [12596860][12821154]|.  The enzyme also exhibits weak 
                     activity toward D-serine, and does not exhibit activity 
                     toward L-serine, D-&beta;-Cl-alanine, or 
                     L-&beta;-Cl-alanine |CITS: [12596860]|.
                     The enzyme is homodimeric and contains a pyridoxal 
                     5'-phosphate prosthetic group |CITS: [12596860][12821154]|,
                     belonging to the fold-type II family of PLP-containing 
                     enzymes |CITS: [12596860]|. Crystal structures of the apo- 
                     and holoenzyme and the enzyme in complex with a reaction 
                     intermediate and substrate have been solved |CITS: 
                     [12925808][22505717]|. Kinetic properties of mutants in 
                     active site residues were analyzed, and a reaction 
                     mechanism was proposed |CITS: [22505717]|.
                     "
                     /translation="MSVFSLKIDIADNKFFNGETSPLFSQSQAKLARQFHQKIAGYRPT
