     CDS             3003387..3004772
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="hyuA"
                     /locus_tag="b2873"
                     /product="phenylhydantoinase"
                     /label=hyuA
                     /note="Phenylhydantoinase is a novel enzyme exhibiting
                     activity toward hydantoin derivatives with an aromatic side
                     chain at the 5' position, with phenylhydantoin and 
                     hydroxyphenylhydantoin having the highest activity level. 
                     It is not active on dihydropyrimidines.  The enzyme has a 
                     stereospecific preference for D-enantiomers.  The 
                     physiological role of the enzyme is not yet known |CITS: 
                     [11092864]|.
                     HyuA has similarity to allantoinase enzymes |CITS: 
                     [10986234]|, including AllB |CITS: [11092864]|.  The enzyme
                     is a homotetramer |CITS: [11092864]|.
                     HyuA: <b>hy</b>dantoin-<b>u</b>tilizing enzyme <b>A</b> 
                     |CITS: [11092864]|
                     "
