     gene            3012520..3013848
                     /gene="ssnA"
                     /locus_tag="b2879"
                     /label=ssnA
     CDS             3012520..3013848
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ssnA"
                     /locus_tag="b2879"
                     /product="putative aminohydrolase SsnA"
                     /label=ssnA
                     /note="SsnA has similarity to allantoinase enzymes |CITS: 
                     [10986234]|.  Purified SsnA does not have isoguanine 
                     deaminase activity |CITS: [21604715]|.
                     An <i>ssnA</i> mutant retains a higher number of viable 
                     cells upon entry into stationary phase in rich media than 
                     wild type |CITS: [10074077]|.  Strains harboring high-copy 
                     episomal <i>ssnA</i> show aberrant cell morphology and 
                     growth defects, and induction of <i>ssnA</i> expression 
                     correlates with decreased viability |CITS: [10074077]|. 
                     Increased expression of &sigma;<sup>E</sup> suppresses 
                     <i>ssnA</i>-dependent growth inhibition |CITS: [10960110]|.
                     Expression of <i>ssnA</i> increases upon entry into 
                     stationary phase; expression is negatively regulated by 
                     RpoS |CITS: [10074077]|.
                     SsnA: <b>s</b>ubject to Rpo<b>S</b>-dependent 
                     <b>n</b>egative regulation in stationary phase <b>A</b> 
                     |CITS: [10074077]|
                     "
