     gene            3017710..3019110
                     /gene="xanQ"
                     /locus_tag="b2882"
                     /label=xanQ
     CDS             3017710..3019110
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="xanQ"
                     /locus_tag="b2882"
                     /product="xanthine:H(+) symporter XanQ"
                     /label=xanQ
                     /note="XanQ (formerly YgfO) is a member of the NCS2 
                     (Nucleobase-Cation Symport-2) family of transporters. XanQ 
                     is a specific, high-affinity, proton motive force-dependent
                     xanthine transporter; XanQ is unable to transport guanine, 
                     hypoxanthine, uric acid, and uracil, or to efficiently 
                     recognize certain xanthine or uric acid analogues |CITS: 
                     [16096267]|.
                     XanQ is predicted to contain 12-14 transmembrane (TM) 
                     regions and contains a nucleobase-ascorbate transporter 
                     (NAT) signature motif |CITS: 
                     [17077086][20802252][21917919]|. XanQ has been subject to 
                     extensive cysteine scanning and site-directed mutagenesis 
                     |CITS: [17077086][18359771][19581302][20802252][21917919][ 
                     26192456]|.
                     <i>xanQ</i> is located within a cluster of genes that have 
                     putative purine catabolic functions |CITS: [10986234]|. 
                     Xanthine is converted to xanthosine-5-phosphate as part of 
                     the |FRAME: SALVPURINE2-PWY ""xanthine salvage pathway""|. 
                     Review: |CITS: [23097742]|"
