     CDS             3019125..3020444
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="guaD"
                     /locus_tag="b2883"
                     /product="guanine deaminase"
                     /EC_number="3.5.4.3"
                     /label=guaD
                     /note="Guanine deaminase is an aminohydrolase that
                     converts guanine to xanthine and ammonia.  This reaction 
                     removes guanine from the pool of guanine-containing 
                     metabolites, which helps to regulate cellular GTP and the 
                     guanylate nucleotide pool.
                     Ammeline is an intermediate in the metabolism of melamine 
                     (see the MetaCyc pathway for |FRAME: PWY-5170|).  <i>E. 
                     coli</i> is able to metabolize ammeline to ammelide, but 
                     does not metabolize either melamine or ammelide.  A 
                     <i>guaD</i> deletion mutant is deficient in ammeline 
                     deaminase activity |CITS: [20023034]|.
                     "
