                     /product="trifunctional guanine/hypoxanthine transporter
                     GhxQ / hypoxanthine transport / guanine transport"
                     /label=ghxQ
                     /note="GhxQ mediates the uptake of guanine and
                     hypoxanthine (but not adenine, xanthine, uric acid nor 
                     uracil) when overexpressed in strains (&Delta;<i>yjcD</i> 
                     or &Delta;<i>purP</i>) which lack significant background 
                     activity; GhxQ transports guanine and hypoxanthine with 
                     high affinity |CITS: [24214977]|. GhxQ is a member of the 
                     nucleobase:cation symporter 2 (NCS2) family of transporters
                     |CITS: [19022853]|.
                     GhxQ is part of a putative purine catablic operon |CITS: 
                     [10986234]|.  Expression of <I>ghxQ</I> is significantly 
                     induced under acidic growth conditions (pH 5.5 and 4.5) 
                     |CITS: [12426343]|.
                     <i>ghxQ</i>: <U>g</U>uanine / <U>h</U>ypo<U>x</U>anthine 
                     permease Q
