                     /product="putative oxidoreductase YgfT"
                     /label=ygfT
                     /note="Under anaerobic and microaerobic conditions, <i>E. 
                     coli</i> is able to utilize urate as its sole source of 
                     nitrogen.  YgfT or AegA play a role in the 
                     formate-dependent catabolism of urate. Like AegA, YgfT 
                     contains an N-terminal Fe-S cluster domain and C-terminal 
                     pyridine nucleotide-disulfide oxidoreductase domain |CITS: 
                     [30885932]|.
                     An <i>aegA ygfT</i> double mutant lacks urate degradation 
                     activity |CITS: [30885932]|.
                     Expression of <i>ygfT</i> is induced under anaerobic and 
                     microaerobic conditions; expression is also increased in 
                     the presence of dimethyl sulfoxide, trimethylamine 
                     <i>N</i>-oxide, fumarate, hypoxanthine, xanthine, or urate 
                     and reduced in the presence of nitrate or nitrite under 
                     anaerobic conditions |CITS: [30885932]|."
