     CDS             3033214..3033735
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="fldB"
                     /locus_tag="b2895"
                     /product="flavodoxin 2"
                     /label=fldB
                     /note="Flavodoxin 2 (FldB) was discovered by sequence
                     similarity to |FRAME: FLAVODOXIN1-MONOMER|.  Flavodoxins 
                     are small, acidic electron transfer proteins which contain 
                     FMN as a prosthetic group.  The physiological role of FldB 
                     is so far unknown |CITS: [10714981]|.
                     Solution structures of apo- and holo-FldB have been 
                     obtained, showing a typical flavodoxin fold |CITS: 
                     [25380767]|.
                     <i>fldB</i> is a member of the SoxRS regulon.  <i>fldB</i> 
                     expression is induced by paraquat, but an <i>fldB</i> 
                     mutant does not show increased sensitivity to paraquat.
                     An <i>fldB</i> mutant has no obvious growth defect, and 
                     overexpression of <i>fldB</i> does not rescue the lethality
                     of an <i>fldA</i> mutation |CITS: [10714981]|."
