     gene            complement(3033775..3034182)
                     /gene="ygfX"
                     /locus_tag="b2896"
                     /label=ygfX
     CDS             complement(3033775..3034182)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ygfX"
                     /locus_tag="b2896"
                     /product="protein YgfX"
                     /label=ygfX
                     /note="YgfX is a membrane-associated protein that
                     interacts with MreB and FtsZ, inhibiting their 
                     polymerization <i>in vitro</i> |CITS: [22239607]|.
                     In one set of experiments, overexpression of YgfX caused 
                     growth arrest; elongated cells began to form after 1 h, 
                     followed by the formation of lemon-shaped cells. 
                     Simultaneous overexpression of SdhE neutralized the effect 
                     of YgfX overexpression |CITS: [22239607]|.  However, in 
                     subsequent experiments, overexpression of YgfX alone had no
                     effect on growth |CITS: [23657679]|.
                     YgfX has two predicted N-terminal transmembrane domains and
                     a soluble C-terminal domain that is involved in its 
                     interaction with MreB and FtsZ |CITS: [22239607]|. 
                     YgfX-SdhE was first identified as a potential 
                     toxin-antitoxin pair by |CITS: [14594833]|.
                     CptA: ""<b>c</b>ytoskeleton <b>p</b>olymerization 
                     inhibiting <b>t</b>oxin"" |CITS: [22239607]|"
