     gene            complement(3034163..3034429)
                     /gene="sdhE"
                     /locus_tag="b2897"
                     /label=sdhE
     CDS             complement(3034163..3034429)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="sdhE"
                     /locus_tag="b2897"
                     /product="FAD assembly factor"
                     /label=sdhE
                     /note="SdhE is a small protein that facilitates the 
                     autocatalytic assembly of the essential covalent flavin 
                     linkage in respiratory complex II flavoprotein subunits 
                     |CITS: [29514959]| and is involved in utilization of 
                     succinate as a carbon and energy source |CITS: [22474332]|.
                      It was first shown in <i>Serratia</i> sp. strain ATCC 
                     39006 that SdhE acts as an FAD assembly factor for SdhA 
                     |CITS: [24070374]| and FrdA |CITS: [24374335]|. SdhE 
                     interacts with the flavoprotein subunits |FRAME: FUM-FLAVO 
                     FrdA| and |FRAME: SDH-FLAVO SdhA| of the fumarate reductase
                     |FRAME: FUMARATE-REDUCTASE QFR| and succinate dehydrogenase
                     |FRAME: CPLX0-8160 SQR| complexes. The SdhE binding site in
                     these proteins resembles the site of interaction between 
                     the N terminus of the iron-sulfur subunits SdhB/FrdB and 
                     SdhA/FrdA in the mature QFR/SQR enzymes |CITS: [26644464]|.
                      SdhE is not essential for FAD attachment to FrdA; however,
                     under aerobic conditions, covalent FAD attachment to FrdA 
                     is significantly lower in the absence of SdhE |CITS: 
                     [28615448]|.
                     |FRAME: G7509-MONOMER YgfX/CptA| was initially identified 
                     as a membrane-associated toxin that interacts with MreB and
                     FtsZ, inhibiting their polymerization <i>in vitro</i>. SdhE
                     (CptB) was thought to act as the cognate antitoxin |CITS: 
                     [22239607]|.  A subsequent publication did not confirm a 
                     toxic effect of overexpression of YgfX alone |CITS: 
                     [23657679]|.
                     Crystal structures of SdhE have been solved at 1.2 and 2 
                     &Aring; resolution.  The crystals show dimeric packing, but
                     the protein exists primarily as a monomer in solution 
                     |CITS: [15593094]|.  A crystal structure of SdhE 
                     crosslinked to FAD-bound FrdA suggests that the interaction
                     with SdhE stabilizes a conformation of FrdA that enables 
                     autocatalytic covalent flavinylation |CITS: [29348404]|.  A
                     co-crystal structure of the SdhA-SdhE complex shows that 
                     SdhE interacts directly with the FAD-linked His45 residue 
                     in SdhA and maintains an open, catalytically inactive 
                     conformation of SdhA |CITS: [29514959]|.
                     An <i>sdhE</i> deletion mutant is defective in the 
                     utilization of succinate as the sole source of carbon and 
                     energy due to severely reduced succinate dehydrogenase 
                     activity |CITS: [22474332]| and shows reduced anaerobic 
                     growth in glycerol-fumarate (GF) medium as well as reduced 
                     fumarate reductase activity |CITS: [24374335]|.
                     CptA-SdhE was first identified as a potential 
                     toxin-antitoxin pair by |CITS: [14594833]|.
                     CptB: ""<b>c</b>ytoskeleton <b>p</b>olymerization 
                     inhibiting <b>t</b>oxin"" |CITS: [22239607]|
                     SdhE: ""<b>s</b>uccinate <b>d</b>e<b>h</b>ydrogenase 
                     protein <b>E</b>"" |CITS: [22474332]|
                     Review: |CITS: [22985599]|"
                     /translation="MDINNKARIHWACRRGMRELDISIMPFFEHEYDSLSDDEKRIFIR
                     LLECDDPDLFNWLMNHGKPADAELEMMVRLIQTRNRERGPVAI"
