     gene            complement(3035848..3036507)
                     /gene="trhA"
                     /locus_tag="b2899"
                     /label=trhA
     CDS             complement(3035848..3036507)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="trhA"
                     /locus_tag="b2899"
                     /product="transmembrane homeostasis protein A"
                     /label=trhA
                     /note="TrhA (formerly YqfA) modulates the ability to
                     maintain optimal cell membrane energetics possibly via an 
                     effect on unsaturated fatty acid metabolism. A 
                     &Delta;<i>trhA</i> mutant shows pleiotropic physiological 
                     changes consistent with dysregulated membrane energetics; 
                     mechanism not known |CITS: [35285724]|. Deletion of 
                     <i>trhA</i> and site-specific mutations of <i>trhA</i> 
                     alter cell morphology; &Delta;<i>trhA</i> cells contain 
                     fewer long unsaturarated fatty acids and an increased 
                     abundance of saturated fatty acids compared to wild type; 
                     TrhA modulates the relative abundance of membrane 
                     unsaturated fatty acids |CITS: [38054739]|.
                     TrhA is related to the progestin and AdipoQ receptor (PAQR)
                     family of proteins which function to maintain membrane 
                     fluidity and membrane fatty acid composition in eukaryotes 
                     |CITS: [35285724]|.
                     <i>trhA</i> is part of the FabR regulon; <i>trhA</i> is 
                     coregulated with genes of unsaturated fatty acid synthesis 
                     |CITS: [11160901][35285724]|. <i>trhA</i> is upregulated 
                     under multiple stress conditions (heat, cold, oxidative 
                     stress, nitrosative stress, and antibiotic treatment) 
                     |CITS: [36144394]|.
                     TrhA is an inner membrane protein with seven predicted 
                     transmembrane domains; the C terminus is located in the 
                     periplasm |CITS: [15919996][38054739]|. TrhA structure has 
                     been modeled |CITS: [26335199]|.
                     <i>trhA</i>: <U>tr</U>ansmembrane <U>h</U>omeostasis 
                     protein A |CITS: [35285724]|."
