     CDS             complement(3036671..3036982)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yqfB"
                     /locus_tag="b2900"
                     /product="N(4)-acetylcytidine amidohydrolase"
                     /EC_number="3.5.1.135"
                     /label=yqfB
                     /note="YqfB hydrolyzes a variety of 
                     <i>N</i><sup>4</sup>-modified cytosine/cytidine compounds, 
                     including <i>N</i><sup>4</sup>-acetylcytidine (ac4C), its 
                     likely physiological substrate |CITS: [31964920]|.
                     Amino acid residues conserved between closely related 
                     proteins were identified and mutagenized; the Arg26Ala, 
                     Thr24Ala and Lys21Ala mutants lacked catalytic activity.
                     A catalytic mechanism has been proposed |CITS: [31964920]|.
                     A solution structure of YqfB has been determined |CITS: 
                     [15969587]|.  However, this structure may differ 
                     significantly from the native structure of the protein 
                     |CITS: [31964920]|."
