     gene            3037021..3038460
                     /gene="bglA"
                     /locus_tag="b2901"
                     /label=bglA
     CDS             3037021..3038460
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="bglA"
                     /locus_tag="b2901"
                     /product="6-phospho-beta-glucosidase A"
                     /label=bglA
                     /note="BglA is a 6-phospho-&beta;-glucosidase with a high 
                     affinity for phosphorylated aromatic &beta;-glucosides and 
                     a low affinity for phosphorylated &beta;-methyl-glucoside 
                     |CITS: [4576407]|.  BglA is one of several 
                     6-phospho-&beta;-glucosidases in <i>E. coli</i>; 
                     transporters for these compounds are present, but appear to
                     be not expressed.  Because its potential phosphorylated 
                     substrates are not commercially available, the true 
                     substrate range of BglA is unknown.
                     Mutants that are able to utilize &beta;-methyl-glucoside as
                     the source of carbon and energy have increased levels of 
                     6-phospho-&beta;-glucosidase |CITS: [4897109]|.
                     A crystal structure of BglA has been solved at 2.3 &Aring; 
                     resolution.  BglA likely forms a homomultimer and has an 
                     8-strand alpha/beta TIM barrel structure |CITS: 
                     [22393408]|."
