     CDS             complement(3052025..3052684)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rpiA"
                     /locus_tag="b2914"
                     /product="ribose-5-phosphate isomerase A"
                     /EC_number="5.3.1.6"
                     /label=rpiA
                     /note="There are two physically and genetically distinct 
                     ribose-5-phosphate isomerases present in <i>E. coli</i> 
                     |CITS: [4909663][11945603]|.  The constitutive 
                     ribose-5-phosphate isomerase A (RpiA) normally accounts for
                     more than 99% of the ribose-5-phosphate isomerase activity 
                     in the cell and functions in the |FRAME: NONOXIPENT-PWY| 
                     |CITS: [11945603]|.  The inducible ribose-5-phosphate 
                     isomerase B can substitute for RpiA's function if its 
                     expression is induced |CITS: [4598000][8576032]|.  There is
                     no sequence similarity between the two enzymes |CITS: 
                     [8576032]|.
                     Crystal structures of RpiA have been solved and active site
                     residues and an acid-base catalytic mechanism were 
                     predicted |CITS: [12211039][12517338]|.
                     An <i>rpiA</i> mutant requires ribose for growth |CITS: 
                     [11945603][8576032]|.
                     RpiA: ""<b>r</b>ibose<b>p</b>hosphate <b>i</b>somerase 
                     <b>A</b>"" |CITS: [4598000]|
                     Review:  |CITS: [8572885]|
                     "
