     CDS             3056346..3057341
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="argK"
                     /locus_tag="b2918"
                     /product="bifunctional methylmalonyl-CoA
                     mutase-interacting GTPase YgfD / GTPase"
                     /label=argK
                     /note="YgfD is a member of the G3E family of P-loop
                     GTPases |CITS: [11916378]|.
                     The YgfD protein and |FRAME: CPLX0-7741| (encoded upstream 
                     of YgfD) interact both <i>in vivo</i> and <i>in vitro</i>; 
                     detection of the interaction depends on the presence of a 
                     non-hydrolyzable GTP analog |CITS: [18950999]|.
                     YgfD was first identified as an ATPase, ArgK, that appeared
                     to phosphorylate the periplasmic binding proteins of the 
                     lysine, arginine, ornithine transport system as well as the
                     arginine, ornithine transport system |CITS: [2136858]|.  
                     However, the kinase activity of ArgK did not affect 
                     transport activity |CITS: [9733684]|.  Neither the 
                     molecular weight nor the pI of ArgK are similar to that of 
                     the protein kinase that was purified based on its activity 
                     |CITS: [2104851]|.
                     Overexpression of YgfD contributes to increased production 
                     of 1-propanol in an engineered <i>E. coli</i> strain |CITS:
                     [24074355]|."
