     gene            complement(3060699..3061439)
                     /gene="yggE"
                     /locus_tag="b2922"
                     /label=yggE
     CDS             complement(3060699..3061439)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yggE"
                     /locus_tag="b2922"
                     /product="DUF541 domain-containing protein YggE"
                     /label=yggE
                     /note="Proteomic analysis of membrane preparations
                     suggests that YggE forms a homo-oligomeric complex |CITS: 
                     [21210718]|.  The C-terminus of YggE is in the periplasm 
                     and thus YggE may be a periplasmic protein that associates 
                     with the inner membrane |CITS: [21210718]|.
                     Expression of <i>yggE</i> is upregulated in a superoxide 
                     dismutase-deficient strain that is exposed to oxidative 
                     stress |CITS: [15870370]| and by UVA irradiation and 
                     elevated temperature |CITS: [18800193]|.  In microarray 
                     experiments, <i>yggE</i> expression was found to be 
                     &sigma;<sup>S</sup>-dependent |CITS: [15489429]|, 
                     upregulated by AI-2 quorum signaling |CITS: [11514505]|, 
                     and belonging to the Rcs regulon |CITS: [13129944]|. 
                     Overexpression of <i>yggE</i> from a plasmid increases the 
                     maximum specific growth rate in paraquat-containing medium 
                     and decreases ROS (reactive oxygen species) levels |CITS: 
                     [15870370]|.  A <i>yggE</i> mutant shows increased levels 
                     of intracellular ROS and reduced tolerance to oxidative 
                     stress generated by exposure to potassium tellurite |CITS: 
                     [19330318]|.  In a large genetic interaction screen, 
                     <i>yggE</i> showed genetic interactions with a number of 
                     proteins involved in translation and ribosome biogenesis; a
                     &Delta;<i>yggE</i> mutant shows increased levels of stop 
                     codon readthrough |CITS: [27732863]|.
                     "
