     gene            3075272..3076030
                     /gene="loiP"
                     /locus_tag="b2936"
                     /label=loiP
     CDS             3075272..3076030
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="loiP"
                     /locus_tag="b2936"
                     /product="bifunctional metalloprotease LoiP /
                     metalloprotease"
                     /label=loiP
                     /note="LoiP is an outer membrane metalloprotease that 
                     preferentially cleaves between Phe/Phe residues |CITS: 
                     [22491786]|.
                     LoiP is predicted to be a lipoprotein with a type II signal
                     peptide |CITS: [15174130]|. The protein is associated with 
                     the membrane fraction |CITS: [17909889]|. LoiP is an outer 
                     membrane lipoprotein |CITS: [22491786]|. LoiP has one 
                     intramolecular S-S bond plus one additional cysteine that 
                     mediates lipid attachment |CITS: [22491786]|.
                     Expression of <i>loiP</i> is upregulated in response to 
                     stress (heat shock, UV irradiation) and in an <i>era-1</i> 
                     mutant background |CITS: [17651431][17909889]|. <i>loiP</i>
                     is upregulated and increased amounts of LoiP are produced 
                     when cells are grown in low osmolarity media |CITS: 
                     [22491786]|. Overexpression of full-length <i>loiP</i> 
                     inhibits growth |CITS: [17909889]|. There is no significant
                     difference in growth between wild-type and a <i>loiP</i> 
                     deletion strain when grown in low osmolarity media |CITS: 
                     [22491786]|.
                     LoiP and |FRAME: G7311-MONOMER ""BepA""| interact and LoiP 
                     is not detected in the outer membrane fraction of a 
                     <i>bepA</i> null mutant (tested at 42<sup>o</sup>C in rich 
                     media containing 0.5M NaCl) |CITS: [22491786]|.
                     LoiP interacts directly with |FRAME: EG10270-MONOMER 
                     ""Era""|, an essential GTPase |CITS: [17651431]|. LoiP 
                     appears to enhance expression of |FRAME: AGMATIN-CPLX| 
                     |CITS: [1310091]|.
                     Deletion of <i>loiP</i> decreases permeabilty of the outer 
                     membrane and reduces plasmid transformation efficiency in 
                     competent cells of <i>E. coli</i> DH5&alpha; prepared by 
                     calcium chloride treatment |CITS: [36708165]|.
                     <i>loiP</i> may be a member of the Rcs regulon |CITS: 
                     [13129944]|.
                     <i>loiP</i>: <U>l</U>ow <U>o</U>smolarity <U>i</U>nduced 
                     <U>P</U>rotease |CITS: [22491786]|"
