     CDS             complement(3076236..3077156)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="speB"
                     /locus_tag="b2937"
                     /product="agmatinase"
                     /EC_number="3.5.3.11"
                     /label=speB
                     /note="Agmatinase (SpeB) catalyzes the hydrolysis of
                     agmatine to yield urea and putrescine, the product of the 
                     |FRAME: PWY-40| pathway |CITS: 
                     [4908780][4908781][3081491]|.
                     Crystal stuctures of SpeB have been solved |CITS: 
                     [33857156][33946272]|.  While the enzyme was initially 
                     thought to be homodimeric in solution |CITS: [3081491]|, 
                     the crystal structures and gel filtration data agree on a 
                     homohexameric quarternary structure |CITS: 
                     [33857156][33946272]|.  One molecule of Mn<sup>2+</sup> is 
                     present per SpeB monomer |CITS: [10329468]|.  The His163Phe
                     |CITS: [10527864]|, Asp153Asn |CITS: [12423350]|, 
                     His126Asn, His151Asn |CITS: [15149812]| and Glu174Ala 
                     |CITS: [15369817]| mutations leads to loss of activity.  
                     Based on the structural and mutant data, a catalytic 
                     mechanism was proposed |CITS: [33946272]|. Agmatinase 
                     activity is induced by the presence of its substrate, 
                     agmatine |CITS: [6319366]|, as well as L-arginine |CITS: 
                     [3897202]|.  Experiments determining regulation of 
                     agmatinase activity by cAMP yielded contradictory results 
                     |CITS: [6319366][3897202]|.  |CITS: [1310091]| later showed
                     that the effect of cAMP on SpeB expression is indirect.  
                     Agmatinase synthesis is also controlled by nitrogen 
                     availability |CITS: [3897202]|.
                     The |FRAME: EG11291-MONOMER| appears to enhance expression 
                     of agmatinase |CITS: [1310091]|.
                     A strain lacking the polyamines putrescine, spermidine and 
                     cadaverine due to deletion of <i>speA</i>, <i>speB</i>, 
                     <i>speC</i>, <i>speD</i> |CITS: [159306]| and <i>cadA</i> 
                     |CITS: [7002915]| has a reduced growth rate compared to 
                     wild type.  The presence of the <i>rpsL9</i> (streptomycin 
                     resistance) allele leads to a requirement for polyamines 
                     for growth |CITS: [7021537]|.  A &Delta;<i>speA speB speC 
                     speD speE speF cadA ldcC</i> mutant is completely deficient
                     in polyamine production and is able to grow under aerobic 
                     conditions with a decreased growth rate; however, both 
                     under anaerobic and 95% oxygen conditions, it requires 
                     polyamines for growth |CITS: [19542271]|. Deletion of 
                     <i>speB</i> impairs pili-dependent surface motility (PDSM) 
                     in <i>E. coli</i> strain W3110 |CITS: [40178519]|.
                     SpeB: ""<b>spe</b>rmidine biosynthesis <b>B</b>"" |CITS: 
                     [4564714]|
                     Review: |CITS: [3157043]|"
