     CDS             3083706..3084413
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="endA"
                     /locus_tag="b2945"
                     /product="bifunctional DNA-specific endonuclease I /
                     endonuclease I"
                     /EC_number="3.1.21.1"
                     /label=endA
                     /note="Endonuclease I is a periplasmic enzyme that cleaves 
                     within duplex DNA. Its cellular role is unknown. 
                     Endonuclease I cleaves within duplex DNA, producing 
                     oligonucleotides that are on average 7 bp long and contain 
                     5' phosphate groups |CITS: [14463751]|. It is inhibited by 
                     tRNA and rRNA |CITS: [14463750]|.
                     Even though it was originally reported that mutants lacking
                     <i>endA</i> show no apparent difference from wild type 
                     cells |CITS: [4938550][4105037]|, several phenotypes were 
                     reported later. An <i>endA</i> deletion strain is sensitive
                     to |FRAME: CPD0-1392| |CITS: [29769716]|, and deletion of 
                     <i>endA</i> was found to facilitate plasmid isolation from 
                     <i>E. coli</i> strains |CITS: [36317996]|. A UV-resistant 
                     mutant increased DNA polymerase I and endonuclease I 
                     activity |CITS: [6252282]|.
                     EndA: <b>end</b>onuclease I |CITS: [4105037]|."
                     /translation="MYRYLSIAAVVLSAAFSGPALAEGINSFSQAKAAAVKVHADAPGT
