                     /locus_tag="b2959"
                     /product="putative ribosome assembly factor YggL"
                     /label=yggL
                     /note="YggL interacts with both the intact ribosome and
                     the 50S subunit and may be involved in ribosome assembly 
                     |CITS: [32813020]|.
                     <i>yggL</i> is transcribed during exponential growth; 
                     transcription decreases during early stationary phase. 
                     Converseley, YggL protein levels remain stable during 
                     stationary phase |CITS: [32813020]|.
                     A &Delta;<i>yggL</i> mutant does not show a growth defect 
                     in rich or minimal medium at 37&deg;C, but grows 
                     significantly slower than wild type at 25&deg;C. The mutant
                     also contains more free 50S ribosomal subunits than wild 
                     type |CITS: [32813020]|."
