     gene            3096372..3097424
                     /gene="mutY"
                     /locus_tag="b2961"
                     /label=mutY
     CDS             3096372..3097424
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="mutY"
                     /locus_tag="b2961"
                     /product="bifunctional adenine DNA glycosylase / adenine 
                     glycosylase"
                     /EC_number="3.2.2.31"
                     /label=mutY
                     /note="MutY is a novel base excision repair (BER)
                     glycosylase which catalyses the removal of adenine when it 
                     is paired with the oxidatively damaged form of guanine, 
                     |FRAME: CPD-12427| (GO; 8-oxoG); MutY activity prevents 
                     deleterious G:C &rarr; T:A transversion mutations.
                     Strains defective in MutY function stimulate G:C &rarr; T:A
                     transversion |CITS: [3128795]| (see also |CITS: 
                     [2974159]|).
                     Purified MutY is an A:G specific adenine glycosylase; MutY,
                     a 5' endonuclease, and DNA polymerase I are able to 
                     reconstitute A:G &rarr; C:G mismatch correction <i>in 
                     vitro</i> |CITS: [2682664]|. MutY removes adenines from 
                     8-oxoG:A mispairs that result from trans-lesion DNA 
                     replication past 8-oxoG; MutY also removes adenine from 
                     A:C, and A:8-oxo-7,8-dihydrodeoxyadenine mispairs; MutY 
                     remains bound to the repair site which may prevent MutM 
                     from removing the 8-oxoG lesion with subsequent double 
                     strand break |CITS: [1495996][1445834]|. MutY may |CITS: 
                     [1382298][7559523][ 9287157]| or may not |CITS: [1495996] 
                     [9730810][7642635][ 8855952]| have associated 
                     apurinic/apyrimidinic endonuclease activity (see also 
                     |CITS: [10506150][10955998][9846876]|).
                     Purified MutY removes guanine from 8-oxoG:G mispairs; 
                     strains defective in MutY function accumulate G:C &rarr; 
                     C:G transversions |CITS: [9753736]|. Strains lacking MutY 
                     show decreased accumulation of A:T &rarr; C:G 
                     transversions; MutY may promote spontaneous mutagenesis 
                     when 8-oxodGTP is inserted opposite template (correct) 
                     adenine |CITS: [12531387]|. MutY does not excise adenine 
                     residues opposite UV induced adducts in oligoDNA substrates
                     |CITS: [30568855]|.
                     MutY contains a [4Fe-4S] cluster |CITS: [1382298][9846876]|
                     (see also |CITS: [9572864][11900536][10353811][12667065]|).
                     The cluster is not implicated in protein folding or 
                     stability but is important for specific recognition of 
                     damaged and mismatched DNA |CITS: [ 9572864]|. The [4Fe-4S]
                     cluster is redox active in the presence of DNA; MutY may 
                     use DNA-mediated charge transfer (CT) to detect genome 
                     damage |CITS: [14559969]| (see further |CITS: 
                     [15938629][16505354][17599416]|. The [4Fe-4S] 
                     cluster-containing DNA repair proteins MutY and |FRAME: 
                     EG10662-MONOMER  Endo III| use DNA-mediated CT 
                     cooperatively to search for DNA damage |CITS: 
                     [19720997][21651304]|. MutY, Endo III, and |FRAME: 
                     EG11357-MONOMER DinG| can use DNA-mediated CT to cooperate 
                     with one another to localize to regions of genome damage 
                     |CITS: [24738733]|.
                     Crystal structures of the catalytic domain of MutY 
                     (MutY<sub>1-225</sub> with adenine bound and designed 
                     mutants) have been used to define the structural and 
                     chemical basis of DNA binding, substrate specificity and 
                     glycosyl bond cleavage |CITS: [9846876]| (see also |CITS: 
                     [11554310][18026095]|).
                     MutY is one of three enzymes of the 'GO' system which 
                     counters the incorporation and accumulation of 8-oxoG in 
                     the genome (see |CITS: [1328155][11554297]|).
                     Purified MutY excises |FRAME: CPD0-2060| (Z base) from 
                     Z:8-oxoG and Z:G duplexes inefficiently; the GO system does
                     not efficiently repair oxidative DNA damage when |FRAME: 
                     CPD0-2060 Z base| is present in DNA |CITS: [38042029]|.
                     MutY is a member of the helix-hairpin-helix (HhH)/GPD 
                     superfamily of DNA glycosylases |CITS: [8805338]|. 
                     <i>mutY</i> is part of a complex operon; expression and 
                     regulation have been studied |CITS: 
                     [10400579][10986244][14567447]|
                     <i>mutY</i>: <U>mut</U>ator locus Y |CITS: [3128795]| 
                     Reviews: |CITS: [25771731]|<BR>Related reviews:  |CITS: 
                     [9224623][11554297][15811798][17599416][31220976]|"
