     gene            3097452..3097727
                     /gene="yggX"
                     /locus_tag="b2962"
                     /label=yggX
     CDS             3097452..3097727
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yggX"
                     /locus_tag="b2962"
                     /product="putative Fe(2+)-trafficking protein"
                     /label=yggX
                     /note="YggX belongs to a subclass of the treble clef (TC)
                     domain family that appears to have lost zinc binding 
                     ability |CITS: [27562564]|.  YggX is proposed to play a 
                     role in oxidation resistance of iron-sulfur clusters |CITS:
                     [14594836]|.  YggX is found at high abundance <i>in 
                     vivo</i> |CITS: [9298646]|.
                     A solution structure of YggX has been determined |CITS: 
                     [15883188]|.  C7 of YggX is redox-sensitive |CITS: 
                     [18287020]|.
                     A <i>yggX</i> mutant shows paraquat sensitivity, a 
                     paraquat-induced aconitase defect |CITS: [14594836]| and 
                     increased sensitivity to redox stress |CITS: [18287020]|. 
                     Multicopy <i>yggX</i> expression results in elevated 
                     aconitase activity, compared to wild type |CITS: 
                     [14594836]|.  A <i>yggX</i> null mutant produces a higher 
                     extracellular thiamine diphosphate titer |CITS: 
                     [28768189]|.
                     Transcription of <i>yggX</i> is induced by SoxS 
                     overproduction or by oxidative stress |CITS: [14594836]|. 
                     YggX is upregulated under glucose-limited fed-batch 
                     conditions |CITS: [16180237]| and in response to plumbagin 
                     |CITS: [16385035]|.
                     "
                     /translation="MSRTIFCTFLQREAEGQDFQLYPGELGKRIYNEISKEAWAQWQHK
