                     /product="putative type II secretion system M-type protein
                     YghD"
                     /label=yghD
                     /note="YghD has homology to the GspM Type II secretion
                     system protein from enterotoxigenic <i>E. coli</i> strain 
                     H10407 |CITS: [12011463]|. In pathogenic (and some 
                     commensal) <i>E. coli</i> strains, GspM functions as part 
                     of a virulence associated type II secretion pathway - known
                     as T2SS<sub>&beta;</sub> or T2SS <sub>H10407</sub>; 
                     examination of T2SS<sub>&Beta;</sub> encoding loci in 
                     various strains indicates that <i>E. coli</i> K-12 carries 
                     remnants of the pathway but has experienced a deletion 
                     which removed a large internal region of the 
                     T2SS<sub>&beta;</sub> encoding operon |CITS: [12011463][17 
                     085567][22585966][22451516][23758679][24478067][24809621]|.
                      YghD is predicted to be a bitopic inner membrane protein 
                     |CITS: [27510400]|.
                     Ecf: ""extracytoplasmic function"" |CITS: [11274153]|"
