     gene            complement(3107909..3112471)
                     /gene="yghJ"
                     /locus_tag="b4466"
                     /label=yghJ
     CDS             complement(3107909..3112471)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yghJ"
                     /locus_tag="b4466"
                     /product="putative mayloidogenic protein"
                     /label=yghJ
                     /note="YghJ is a potentially amyloidogenic protein |CITS: 
                     [26885581]|; the metalloprotease domain (aa 1081-181) of 
                     YghJ (YghJ<sub>M</sub>) contains 3 short amyloidogenic 
                     regions; purified YghJ<sub>M</sub> forms detergent- and 
                     protease-resistant aggregates with fibrillar morphology; 
                     YghJ<sub>M</sub> aggregates have amyloidogenic properties 
                     <i>in vitro</i>; YghJ<sub>M</sub> forms amyloid-like 
                     fibrils <i>in vivo</i> |CITS: [29381728]|.
                     In pathogenic (and some commensal) <i>E. coli</i> strains, 
                     YghJ (renamed SslE) is a virulence factor secreted by a 
                     type II system (known as T2SS<sub>&Beta;</sub>); <i>E. 
                     coli</i> K-12 does not contain the full set of 
                     T2SS<sub>&beta;</sub> encoding genes - an examination of 
                     T2SS<sub>&Beta;</sub> encoding loci in various strains 
                     suggests that in K-12, the T2SS<sub>&Beta;</sub> - encoding
                     operon experienced an internal deletion |CITS: [1 
                     7085567][22585966][22451516][23758679][24478067][24809621]|
                     . YghJ is detected in in the whole-cell lysate of MG1655 
                     but not in the secreted fraction |CITS: [27598999]|. 
                     <i>yghJ</i> contains a predicted lipoprotein signal |CITS: 
                     [15174130]|."
