     CDS             3123573..3124553
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="insH9"
                     /locus_tag="b2982"
                     /product="IS5 transposase and trans-activator"
                     /label=insH9
                     /note="InsH is believed to be the transposase for the
                     insertion sequence element IS<i>5</i>.
                     <i>insH</i> spans the length of IS<i>5</i> |CITS: 
                     [6269958][6327289][6269959][2846516]|. IS<i>5</i> can 
                     enhance gene transcription when it is placed on either side
                     of the promoter for a target gene. This enhancement depends
                     specifically on InsH and its interaction with the termini 
                     of the IS<i>5</i> sequence |CITS: [1311089]|.
                     The consensus target for IS<i>5</i> insertion is 
                     C(T/A)A(G/A) |CITS: [6269958][6269959]|.
                     Many copies of IS<i>5</i>, and thus InsH, are present in 
                     typical <i>E. coli</i> strains |CITS: [6269959]|."
