     gene            complement(3133075..3133323)
                     /gene="hybG"
                     /locus_tag="b2990"
                     /label=hybG
     CDS             complement(3133075..3133323)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="hybG"
                     /locus_tag="b2990"
                     /product="hydrogenase maturation factor HybG"
                     /label=hybG
                     /note="HybG is a chaperone-like protein which is
                     specifically required for the generation of active |FRAME: 
                     FORMHYDROG2-CPLX| (Hyd-2) and can also function in the 
                     maturation of |FRAME: FORMHYDROGI-CPLX| (Hyd-1) |CITS: 
                     [11292801]|.  HybG appears to be the carrier that delivers 
                     the Fe(CN)<sub>2</sub>CO group to |FRAME: HYBC-MONOMER 
                     large subunit of hydrogenase 2| (pre-HybC) |CITS: 
                     [34934150]|.
                     HybG and pre-HybC interact.  The amino-terminal methionine 
                     residue of HybG appears to be removed, and the second amino
                     acid residue, cysteine, is required for interaction of HybG
                     with HybC and for Hyd-1 and Hyd-2 maturation |CITS: 
                     [11292801][34934150]|.  Co-purification assays confirmed 
                     interactions between HybG and the large subunits of Hyd-1 
                     and Hyd-2 (HyaB and HybC), as well as HypD and HypE |CITS: 
                     [16412426]|.  The C-terminal 15 amino acids of HybC are 
                     required for interaction with HybG |CITS: [28539366]|.  
                     Addition of pre-HybC titrates HybG away from the 
                     HybG-|FRAME: EG10486-MONOMER HypD| complex |CITS: 
                     [34934150]|.
                     Anaerobically purified HybG contains iron and 
                     CO<sub>2</sub> |CITS: [23851071]| and was shown to carry 
                     the Fe(CN)<sub>2</sub>CO group |CITS: [34934150]|. 
                     Maturation of Hyd-1 and Hyd-2 can be reconstituted <i>in 
                     vitro</i> with anaerobically purified HybG-HypDE under 
                     reducing conditions in the presence of ATP, 
                     carbamoylphosphate, and nickel |CITS: [25184670]|.  <i>In 
                     vitro</i> maturation of |FRAME: FORMHYDROG2-CPLX| with 
                     protein components including HybG has been achieved |CITS: 
                     [28539366]|.
                     HybG has low intrinsic ATPase activity; the purified 
                     HybG-HypD complex catalyzes hydrolysis of ATP with a 
                     10-fold higher k<sub>cat</sub> of ~ 0.85 s<sup>-1</sup> 
                     |CITS: [31614069]|.
                     <i>hybG</i> is required for wild-type levels of Hyd-1 and 
                     Hyd-2 |CITS: [8021226]|.
                     Review: |CITS: [17216401]|"
