     gene            complement(3133336..3133677)
                     /gene="hybF"
                     /locus_tag="b2991"
                     /label=hybF
     CDS             complement(3133336..3133677)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="hybF"
                     /locus_tag="b2991"
                     /product="hydrogenase maturation protein HybF"
                     /label=hybF
                     /note="HybF and its homolog, HypA, are involved in the 
                     maturation of hydrogenase isozymes.  HybF is required for 
                     maturation of hydrogenase isozymes 1 and 2, while HypA is 
                     involved in the maturation of hydrogenase 3; HypA and HybF 
                     can only partially substitute for each other |CITS: 
                     [12081959]|.  The presence of high levels of nickel can 
                     phenotypically rescue <i>hypA</i> and <i>hybF</i> mutants 
                     and a triple <i>hypA hypB hybF</i> mutant to a low level 
                     |CITS: [12081959][15090500]|.
                     Purified HybF contains Zn<sup>2+</sup> in stoichiometric 
                     amounts.  However, C89 in the C-terminal zinc finger motif 
                     is not essential for function of HybF.  The protein is able
                     to bind Ni<sup>2+</sup> <i>in vitro</i> with a 
                     K<sub>D</sub> of 1.87 &micro;M; a H2Q mutation drastically 
                     reduces Ni<sup>2+</sup> binding.  The H2 and E3 residues 
                     are also required for the hydrogenase maturation activity 
                     of HybF |CITS: [15090500]|.
                     Reviews: |CITS: [17216401][26919691]|
                     "
