     gene            complement(3134151..3134645)
                     /gene="hybD"
                     /locus_tag="b2993"
                     /label=hybD
     CDS             complement(3134151..3134645)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="hybD"
                     /locus_tag="b2993"
                     /product="hydrogenase 2 maturation protease"
                     /label=hybD
                     /note="HybD is an endopeptidase involved in the maturation
                     of the large subunit of hydrogenase 2, |FRAME: HYBC-MONOMER
                     HybC| |CITS: [20807532]|.  Processing of HybC by HybD is 
                     dependent on prior insertion of Fe(CN)<sub>2</sub>CO.  
                     Processing of the HybC C terminus is required for assembly 
                     of the catalytically active HybC-HybO heterodimer |CITS: 
                     [28539366]|.
                     HybD was predicted to be the endopeptidase involved in the 
                     maturation of HybC based on its similarity to the 
                     processing enzyme for hydrogenase 3, HycI |CITS: 
                     [7851435]|.  <i>In vitro</i> maturation of |FRAME: 
                     FORMHYDROG2-CPLX| with protein components including HybD 
                     has been achieved |CITS: [28539366]|.
                     Purified HybD does not contain stoichiometric amounts of 
                     bound metal ion |CITS: [10727938]|.  The crystal structure 
                     of HybD has been determined at 2.2 &Aring; resolution 
                     |CITS: [10331925]|.
                     A &Delta;<i>hybD</i> mutant contains unprocessed HybC 
                     |CITS: [20807532]|.
                     Reviews: |CITS: [15667279][17216401]|"
