     CDS             complement(3136345..3137523)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="hybB"
                     /locus_tag="b2995"
                     /product="bifunctional hydrogenase 2 membrane subunit /
                     hydrogenase 2"
                     /EC_number="1.12.5.1"
                     /label=hybB
                     /note="The HybB protein is predicted to be an integral
                     membrane component of hydrogenase 2 |CITS: [8021226]|. 
                     <i>hybB</i> contains a HXXH conserved motif associated with
                     cytochrome <i>b</i> type proteins |CITS: [8021226]|. HybB 
                     contains no conserved histidines that would serve as heme 
                     iron ligands |CITS: [DUBINI02]|. HybB may act as a proton 
                     pump during H(2):quinone oxidoreductase activity |CITS: 
                     [25368299]| (and see |CITS: [29555844][31260099]|). A 
                     <i>hybB</i> in-frame deletion mutant cannot grow on 
                     glycerol and fumarate as the sole energy sources.
                     However,
                     the HybOHybC complex is correctly targeted to the membrane 
                     and active with the artificial electron acceptor benzyl 
                     viologen (BV) |CITS: [DUBINI02]|."
