     gene            complement(3144177..3144602)
                     /gene="exbD"
                     /locus_tag="b3005"
                     /label=exbD
     CDS             complement(3144177..3144602)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="exbD"
                     /locus_tag="b3005"
                     /product="multifunctional Ton complex subunit ExbD /
                     energy transducing Ton complex / pyrroloquinoline quinone 
                     outer membrane transport complex / ferric catecholate outer
                     membrane transport complex II / ferric catecholate outer 
                     membrane transport complex I / ferric catecholate outer 
                     membrane transporter / ferric coprogen outer membrane 
                     transport complex / transport of ferric coprogen / ferric 
                     citrate outer membrane transport complex / transport of 
                     ferric citrate / ferrichrome outer membrane transport 
                     complex / transport of ferrichrome / ferric enterobactin 
                     outer membrane transport complex / ferric enterobactin 
                     outer membrane transporter / cobalamin outer membrane 
                     transport complex"
                     /label=exbD
                     /note="ExbD is a component of the energy transducing Ton
                     system which functions to harness the energy of the proton 
                     motive force (pmf) at the cytoplasmic membrane to support 
                     active transport of iron-siderophore complexes and certain 
                     cofactors across the outer membrane.
                     ExbD is an inner membrane protein |CITS: [2670903]|; 
                     topology analysis suggests that it contains a single 
                     transmembrane region with the N-terminus located in the 
                     cytoplasm and a larger C-terminal domain located in the 
                     periplasm |CITS: [1644779]|. ExbD interacts with TonB and 
                     with ExbB and forms homodimers <i>in vivo</i>; ExbD and 
                     TonB interact through their periplasmic domains; ExbD-TonB 
                     interaction requires PMF |CITS: [19627500]|. ExbD binds to 
                     the TonB ""D-box"" motif and this interaction is suggested 
                     to be critical for force transduction between the membranes
                     |CITS: [38311172]|.
                     Over-expressed ExbBD purifies in multiple stoichiometries; 
                     the principle complex, ExbB<sub>4</sub>ExbD<sub>2</sub>, 
                     contains a TM region expected to consist of 14 TM helices 
                     (12 from ExbB and two from ExbD), a periplasmic domain 
                     comprised of the ExbD C-terminus and a cytoplasmic domain 
                     |CITS: [24657092][24862870]|. Crystallized 
                     ExbBExbD<sub>&Delta;peri</sub> contains a pentamer of ExbB 
                     which forms a transmembrane pore that is filled by the 
                     transmembrane helix of ExbD |CITS: [27654919]| (see also 
                     |CITS: [29661272][30442809]|). ExbBD is a heteroheptameric 
                     5:2 rotary motor (see |CITS: [35992645]|).
                     The <i>exb</i> locus consists of <i>exbB</i> and 
                     <i>exbD</i>; the products of both genes contribute to the 
                     activity of TonB |CITS: [2670904][2670903][12193634]|. 
                     Cross complementation is observed between ExbBD and TolQR 
                     |CITS: [8316079]|.
                     <i>exb</i> mutants hyper-excrete enterochelin and are 
                     defective in the uptake of ferrichrome and vitamin B12 
                     |CITS: [4576403][HANTKE81]|.
                     Overexpression of <i>exbD</i> from an ASKA plasmid leads to
                     a more than 3-fold increase in the MIC of hypochlorous acid
                     |CITS: [34072091]|.
                     <i>exb</i>: excretes an inhibitor of colicin B |CITS: 
                     [4891106]|"
