     gene            complement(3144609..3145343)
                     /gene="exbB"
                     /locus_tag="b3006"
                     /label=exbB
     CDS             complement(3144609..3145343)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="exbB"
                     /locus_tag="b3006"
                     /product="multifunctional Ton complex subunit ExbB /
                     energy transducing Ton complex / pyrroloquinoline quinone 
                     outer membrane transport complex / ferric catecholate outer
                     membrane transport complex II / ferric catecholate outer 
                     membrane transport complex I / ferric catecholate outer 
                     membrane transporter / ferric coprogen outer membrane 
                     transport complex / transport of ferric coprogen / ferric 
                     citrate outer membrane transport complex / transport of 
                     ferric citrate / ferrichrome outer membrane transport 
                     complex / transport of ferrichrome / ferric enterobactin 
                     outer membrane transport complex / ferric enterobactin 
                     outer membrane transporter / cobalamin outer membrane 
                     transport complex"
                     /label=exbB
                     /note="ExbB is a component of the energy transducing Ton
                     system which functions to harness the energy of the proton 
                     motive force (pmf) at the cytoplasmic membrane to support 
                     active transport of iron-siderophore complexes and certain 
                     cofactors across the outer membrane.
                     ExbB affects the stability of TonB and disruption of 
                     <i>exbB</i> (<i>exbB</i>::Tn10) results in decreased TonB 
                     function |CITS: [1809832][7642501]|.
                     ExbB is an inner membrane protein |CITS: [3295484]|. ExbB 
                     interacts with ExbD and TonB |CITS: [8631671]|. Topology 
                     analysis suggests that ExbB contains three transmembrane 
                     (TM) regions with the N-terminus in the periplasm and the 
                     C-terminus in the cytoplasm |CITS: [8449962]|. ExbB forms 
                     multimers <i>in vitro</i> and <i>in vivo</i> |CITS: 
                     [9811664][20799747][21840979]|.  A large cytoplasmic loop 
                     (residues 40-129) is essential for Ton system function; 
                     expression of ExbB proteins with sequential 10-residue 
                     deletions in the cytoplasmic loop results in (reversible) 
                     growth arrest (that is not due to collapse of the PMF) 
                     |CITS: [23913327]|. ExbB transmembrane domains do not 
                     participate in a proton translocation pathway |CITS: 
                     [23603742]|.
                     Over-expressed ExbBD purifies in multiple stoichiometries; 
                     the principle complex, ExbB<sub>4</sub>ExbD<sub>2</sub>, 
                     contains a TM region expected to consist of 14 TM helices 
                     (12 from ExbB and two from ExbD), a periplasmic domain, and
                     a cytoplasmic domain containing the loops and C-termini of 
                     ExbB molecules |CITS: [24657092][24862870]|. Crystallized 
                     ExbBExbD<sub>&Delta;peri</sub> (the Ton subcomplex) 
                     contains a pentamer of ExbB; the ExbB monomer consists of 7
                     &alpha; helices which form a transmembrane domain (helices 
                     2, 6 and 7) that extends into the cytoplasm to form a helix
                     bundle with the cytoplasmic loop and C-terminal domain; the
                     pentameric structure contains a transmembrane pore (filled 
                     by the transmembrane helix of ExbD) and a large enclosed 
                     cytoplasmic cavity containing 5 openings (possibly for 
                     solvent or ion passage) |CITS: [27654919]|. ExbB is a 
                     pentamer in the Ton complex |CITS: [27654919]|. Channels of
                     the Ton subcomplex are cation selective and channel 
                     activity is pH dependent; channels of the ExbB pentamer 
                     alone are anion selective |CITS: [27654919]|. ExbBD is a 
                     heteroheptameric 5:2 rotary motor (see |CITS: [35992645]|).
                     The <i>exb</i> locus consists of <i>exbB</i> and 
                     <i>exbD</i>; the products of both genes contribute to the 
                     activity of TonB |CITS: [2670904][2670903][12193634]|. 
                     Cross complementation is observed between ExbBD and TolQR 
                     |CITS: [8316079]|.
                     <i>exb</i> mutants hyper-excrete enterochelin and are 
                     defective in the uptake of ferrichrome and vitamin B12 
                     |CITS: [4576403][HANTKE81]|.
                     <i>exb</i>: excretes an inhibitor of colicin B |CITS: 
                     [4891106]|"
