     gene            3146922..3147581
                     /gene="yghB"
                     /locus_tag="b3009"
                     /label=yghB
     CDS             3146922..3147581
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yghB"
                     /locus_tag="b3009"
                     /product="DedA family protein YghB"
                     /label=yghB
                     /note="YghB is predicted to be an inner membrane protein
                     with four transmembrane domains; topology analysis suggests
                     the C-terminus is located in the cytoplasm 
                     |CITS:[15919996]|.
                     A <I>yghB yqjA</I> double null strain has a synthetic 
                     growth defect at elevated temperatures, forms chains of 
                     cells at permissive temperatures, and can be complemented 
                     by <I>yghB, yqjA, yohD,</I> or <I>yabI</I> expressed from a
                     plasmid |CITS:[18456815]|. The double and single mutants 
                     displayed altered phospholipid compositions 
                     |CITS:[18456815]|.
                     An <i>E. coli &Delta;yghB &Delta;yqjA</i> strain is 
                     hypersensitive to a number of structurally diverse drugs 
                     and dyes including ethidium bromide, methyl viologen, 
                     acriflavine, nalidixic acid and &beta;-lactam antibiotics. 
                     A wild-type response is restored by expression of 
                     <i>yghB</i> from a plasmid |CITS: [24277026]|. Mutation of 
                     the membrane embedded acidic amino acids E39 (glutamic 
                     acid) or D51 (aspartic acid) in plasmid-expressed YghB 
                     compromises its ability to restore wild-type resistance 
                     |CITS: [24277026]|. Overexpression of <i>yghB</i> in a 
                     wild-type background does not result in increased 
                     resistance to any of the compounds tested. Overexpression 
                     of the |FRAME: G6440 ""<i>mdfA</i>""| antiporter restores 
                     the wild-type resistance of an <i>E. coli &Delta;yghB 
                     &Delta;yqjA</i> strain to all componds tested as does 
                     growth in the presence of 400mM NaCl or with increased 
                     amounts of cations or at pH 6 |CITS: [24277026], 
                     [18456815]|. Deletion of <i>yghB</i> and <i>yqjA</i> may 
                     indirectly cause drug sensitivity due to impairment of the 
                     proton-motive force (PMF) |CITS: [24277026]|.
                     The <I>yghB</I> gene has a possible FNR binding site 
                     upstream of its coding sequence |CITS:[17164287]|. 
                     Expression of <I>yghB</I> is significantly induced in 
                     response to autoinducer-2 (AI-2) |CITS:[11514505]|.
                     YghB is a member of the DedA family of inner membrane 
                     proteins |CITS: [18456815], [23086209]|. <i>E. coli</i> 
                     K-12 contains 7 other DedA family members, namely |FRAME: 
                     EG10216 ""DedA""|, |FRAME: G7609-MONOMER ""YqjA""|, |FRAME:
                     EG11571 ""YabI""|, |FRAME: EG12017 ""YohD""|, |FRAME: G7407
                     ""YqaA""|, |FRAME: G6945-MONOMER ""YdjX""| and |FRAME: 
                     G6947 ""YdjZ""|.  Collectively, the DedA family is 
                     essential in <i>E. coli</i> K-12 |CITS: [22301910]|."
