     CDS             complement(3159470..3161077)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ygiS"
                     /locus_tag="b3020"
                     /product="putative deoxycholate binding periplasmic
                     protein"
                     /label=ygiS
                     /note="YgiS has 44% identity with OppA - the periplasmic
                     binding protein of an oligopeptide ABC transporter |CITS: 
                     [25534751]|.  The mRNA interferase, |FRAME: G7572-MONOMER 
                     ""MqsR""|, degrades <i>ygiS</i> mRNA <i>in vitro</i>; 
                     <i>ygiS</i> mRNA contains 43 potential MqsR cleavage sites 
                     (5'GCU) |CITS: [25534751]|. YgiS reduces cell fitness 
                     against deoxycholate; YgiS is associated with increased 
                     intracellular deoxycholate concentrations |CITS: 
                     [25534751]|.
                     In the Transporter Classification Database YgiS is 
                     annotated as a probable deoxycholate binding periplasmic 
                     protein that may interact with the membrane and ATP-binding
                     components of the oligopeptide ABC transporter (OppBCDF) to
                     mediate deoxycholate uptake |CITS: [26546518]|.
                     <i>ygiS</i> is upregulated under glucose-limited fed-batch 
                     conditions |CITS: [16180237]|. <i>ygiS</i> is significantly
                     induced in a &Delta;<i>mqsRA</i> strain exposed to 
                     deoxycholate |CITS: [25534751]|."
