     gene            3163843..3165192
                     /gene="qseC"
                     /locus_tag="b3026"
                     /label=qseC
     CDS             3163843..3165192
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="qseC"
                     /locus_tag="b3026"
                     /product="bifunctional sensor histidine kinase QseC / 
                     protein-histidine autokinase"
                     /EC_number="2.7.13.3"
                     /label=qseC
                     /note="QseC is the sensor kinase component of the
                     QseB-QseC two-component system which is involved in the 
                     activation of flagella and motility genes; QseBC modulates 
                     transcription of <i>flhDC</i>, the master regulator for 
                     flagella and motility genes |CITS: [11929534][16352847]|. 
                     QseC contains two predicted transmembrane helices, a 
                     dimerization domain which contains the predicted site 
                     (His-246) of autophosphorylation and an 'orthodox-type' 
                     ATP-binding kinase domain (see |CITS: [11320123]|). QseC is
                     predicted to have both histidine autokinase and 
                     phosphotransferase activity; the QseBC system has been well
                     studied in enterohemorrhagic (EHEC) and uropathogenic 
                     (UPAC) <i>E. coli</i> strains (see |CITS: [11929534][16803 
                     956][16135237][19696934][26426681][26589223]|); QseC 
                     (purified from EHEC and reconstituted into liposomes) 
                     autophosphorylates in response to an external signal 
                     (epinephrine/norepinephrine and autoinducer-3) and 
                     transfers its phosphate to QseB <i>in vitro</i> |CITS: 
                     [16803956]| (and see further |CITS: [28396353]|). QseC of 
                     EHEC O157:H7 and <i>E. coli</i> K-12 MG1655 differ by eight
                     amino acids |CITS: [11929534]|.
                     <i>qseBC</i> null mutants show hypersensitivity to several 
                     toxic cations |CITS: [12897016]|. &Delta;<i>qseC</i> cells 
                     are longer and wider than wild-type; loss of QseB reverses 
                     the shape defect of &Delta;<i>qseC</i> cells |CITS: 
                     [32979869]|.
                     qseC: ""quorum-sensing <i>E. coli</i> regulator C"" |CITS: 
                     [11929534]|
                     <i>Note</i>: bacterial histidine kinases function as 
                     homodimers; both <i>cis</i>- and 
                     <i>trans</i>-autophosphorylation mechanisms have been 
                     documented (see |CITS: [19575571][25982528]|). In the 
                     absence of experimental evidence QseC is represented as a 
                     monomer in the EcoCyc database.
                     Reviews: |CITS:[36849330]|"
                     /translation="MKFTQRLSLRVRLTLIFLILASVTWLLSSFVAWKQTTDNVDELFD
