     gene            join(3179384..3179454,3180791..3183224)
                     /pseudo
                     /gene="yqiG"
                     /locus_tag="b3046"
                     /label=yqiG
                     /note="The <i>yqiG</i> gene is interrupted by an IS
                     element.  Sequence similarity suggests that its ancestral 
                     product is a member of the Fimbrial Usher Protein (FUP) 
                     family |CITS: [12192075]|.
                     The <i>yqiG</i> null mutant of the Keio collection was 
                     reported to produce less hydrogen than wild type under 
                     fermentation conditions.  A <i>yqiG</i> expression clone 
                     from the ASKA library complements the phenotype |CITS: 
                     [24025676]|. The BW25113 strain used in these experiments 
                     does not contain the IS element which interrupts the gene 
                     in MG1655.
                     <i>E. coli</i> K-12 contains 12 chaperone-usher fimbrial 
                     operons, including <i>ygiLyqiGHI</i>; a fimbria-lacking 
                     mutant - strain WQM026 - created by deleting all 12 operons
                     has been characterised |CITS: [33863704]|.
                     Comment in ASAP: The coordinates of yqiG have been changed 
                     from those reported in the GenBank entry (GBAN:U00096.3), 
                     adding 36 nucleotides to the N-terminus and including the 
                     repeat at the end of the N-terminal fragment."
