     CDS             3183991..3185055
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yqiI"
                     /locus_tag="b3048"
                     /product="putative fimbrial protein YqiI"
                     /label=yqiI
                     /note="YqiI may play a role in detoxification of
                     methylglyoxal (MG) and dihydroxyacetone (DHA).
                     A <i>yqiI</i> insertion mutant increases the sensitivity of
                     a |FRAME: G6891 <i>gloA</i>| mutant to MG and DHA; a strain
                     containing only the <i>yqiI</i> insertion mutation does not
                     show increased sensitivity to MG or DHA |CITS: [17846588]|.
                     The <i>yqiI</i> insertion mutant appears to lack flagellin 
                     and shows impaired motility on swarm plates |CITS: 
                     [17846588]|.
                     <i>E. coli</i> K-12 contains 12 chaperone-usher fimbrial 
                     operons, including <i>ygiLyqiGHI</i>; a fimbria-lacking 
                     mutant - strain WQM026 - created by deleting all 12 operons
                     has been characterised |CITS: [33863704]|.
