     gene            complement(3185098..3185298)
                     /gene="glgS"
                     /locus_tag="b3049"
                     /label=glgS
     CDS             complement(3185098..3185298)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="glgS"
                     /locus_tag="b3049"
                     /product="surface composition regulator"
                     /label=glgS
                     /note="GlgS negatively regulates flagellar motility and 
                     production of biofilm polysaccharides |CITS: [23537328]|. 
                     Since a <i>glgS</i> null mutation inhibits glycogen 
                     synthesis and overproduction of GlgS stimulates synthesis 
                     of glycogen |CITS: [1324388][19702577]|, GlgS was thought 
                     to be involved in the regulation of glycogen biosynthesis 
                     |CITS: [1324388]|. However, because motility and 
                     biosynthesis of extracellular polysaccharides normally 
                     compete with glycogen biosynthesis for the same metabolite 
                     pools, the effect of GlgS on glycogen biosynthesis is now 
                     thought to be indirect |CITS: [23537328]|.
                     Expression of <i>glgS</i> is dependent on RpoS and induced 
                     in stationary phase |CITS: [1324388][8416901]|.  CsrA 
                     negatively regulates <i>glgS</i> expression |CITS: 
                     [8576033]|.
                     <i>glgS</i> mutants accumulate high levels of AMP |CITS: 
                     [19702577]|, are hyperflagellated and hyperfimbriated, and 
                     show elevated swarming motility and increased biofilm 
                     formation |CITS: [23537328]|.
                     Solution structures of GlgS have been obtained |CITS: 
                     [9208918][15161493]|.  GlgS shows similarity to proteins 
                     involved in protein-protein interactions, suggesting a 
                     similar role for GlgS |CITS: [15161493]|.
                     ScoR: ""<b>s</b>urface <b>co</b>mposition 
                     <b>r</b>egulator"" |CITS: [23537328]|"
