     gene            3186223..3187884
                     /gene="yqiK"
                     /locus_tag="b3051"
                     /label=yqiK
     CDS             3186223..3187884
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yqiK"
                     /locus_tag="b3051"
                     /product="flotillin family inner membrane protein YqiK"
                     /label=yqiK
                     /note="<i>yqiK</i> encodes a flotillin-like protein |CITS: 
                     [19138386][20713508]|. YqiK is a prokaryotic member of the 
                     stomatin, prohibitin, flotillin, and HflK/C (SPFH) protein 
                     superfamily |CITS: [19138386]|; SPFH domain proteins 
                     localize in eukaryotic lipid rafts and the function and 
                     localization of <i>E. coli</i> SPFH proteins, including 
                     YqiK has been investigated |CITS: [37347165]| (see also 
                     |CITS: [31603938][27984012]|).
                     YqiK is predicted to be a bitopic inner membrane protein 
                     with its C-terminus located in the cytoplasm |CITS: 
                     [15919996][27510400]|. YqiK fluorescent fusion proteins 
                     (YqiK-GFP and Yqik-YFP) localize to discrete foci in the 
                     membrane |CITS: [25118250][20713508]|. The YqiK fusion 
                     protein with enhanced green fluorescent protein (YqiK-EGFP)
                     distributes throughout the cytoplasm |CITS: [17272300]|.
                     A &Delta;<i>yqiK</i> strain shows enhanced resistance to 
                     ampicillin and enhanced swimming behaviour |CITS: 
                     [31062059]|."
