     gene            complement(3188456..3188599)
                     /gene="sibE"
                     /locus_tag="b4611"
                     /label=sibE
     misc_RNA        complement(3188456..3188599)
                     /gene="sibE"
                     /locus_tag="b4611"
                     /product="small RNA SibE"
                     /note="The SibE small RNA is located in the
                     <i>yqiK-rfaE</i> intergenic region.  In the updated and 
                     corrected version of the <i>E. coli</i> genome sequence, 
                     this region contains two copies of a repeat sequence 
                     element (initially termed QUAD1 and later renamed SIB) that
                     occurs five times in the <i>E. coli</i> K-12 genome |CITS: 
                     [10673004][18710431]|.  Many sequence regions conserved 
                     between the SIB elements are predicted to form stem-loop 
                     structures |CITS: [18710431]|.
                     Two RNA products arising from <i>sibE</i> have been 
                     detected; the shorter RNA product may be derived by 
                     processing of the longer transcript |CITS: [18710431]|.  A 
                     small open reading frame encoding the toxic peptide IbsE is
                     located on the opposite strand |CITS: [18710431]|.
                     SibE interacts with the protein |FRAME: EG12866-MONOMER| 
                     |CITS: [36328526]|.
                     SibE is expressed at varying levels throughout growth; the 
                     RNA level is generally higher in minimal medium than in 
                     rich medium |CITS: [18710431]|.
                     Deletion of <i>sibE</i> has no detectable effect on cell 
                     growth.  However, in a <i>sibE</i> deletion strain, 
                     expression of SibE from a plasmid must be highly induced to
                     yield viable cells; this appears to be due to 
                     overexpression of the toxic peptide IbsE |CITS: 
                     [18710431]|. On the other hand, a double mutant 
                     <i>sgrS</i>-<i>sibE</i>, the <i>sibE</i> mutant appears to 
                     suppress the effect of a <i>sgrS</i> mutant on growth 
                     |CITS: [35920556]|.
                     Ryx: ""RNA of unknown function at X position (10 minute) in
                     the genome"" |CITS: [11445539]|
                     SibE: ""<b>s</b>hort, <b>i</b>ntergenic, a<b>b</b>undant 
                     sequence"" |CITS: [18710431]|
                     Reviews: |CITS: [12762038][12654996][32213244]|"
