     gene            complement(3193023..3194324)
                     /gene="ygiF"
                     /locus_tag="b3054"
                     /label=ygiF
     CDS             complement(3193023..3194324)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ygiF"
                     /locus_tag="b3054"
                     /product="inorganic triphosphatase"
                     /EC_number="3.6.1.25"
                     /label=ygiF
                     /note="YgiF belongs to the CYTH
                     (<b>Cy</b>aB-<b>Th</b>iamine triphosphatase) family of 
                     proteins.  The enzyme was shown to be a specific inorganic 
                     triphosphatase.  However, the majority of inorganic 
                     triphosphatase activity in <i>E. coli</i> cells may be due 
                     to the activity of |FRAME: CPLX0-243| |CITS: [22984449]|. 
                     The <i>ygiF</i> gene was amplified from <i>E. coli</i> 
                     Mach1<sup>TM</sup> cells (Thermo Fisher Scientific, derived
                     from <i>E. coli</i> W, not K-12; the Mach1<sup>TM</sup> 
                     gene is 98% identical to the K-12 gene), and crystal 
                     structures of the protein were solved. The structures show 
                     a conserved triphosphate tunnel metalloenzyme (TTM) fold 
                     and a second &alpha;-helical domain  Two metal ion binding 
                     sites suggested a two-metal catalytic mechanism, where one 
                     metal ion provides substrate coordination and the other 
                     enables a nucleophilic attack on the triphosphate 
                     substrate. Site-directed mutagenesis of the Glu6 and Glu60 
                     residues showed that the proper arrangement of both metal 
                     binding sites is required for catalytic activity and that 
                     Arg56 may have a role as the proton donor |CITS: 
                     [26221030]|. Review: |CITS: [24021036]|
                     "
