                     /gene="ttdB"
                     /locus_tag="b3062"
                     /product="bifunctional L(+)-tartrate dehydratase subunit
                     beta / L(+)-tartrate dehydratase"
                     /EC_number="4.2.1.32"
                     /label=ttdB
                     /note="The <i>ttdB</i> gene encodes the &beta; subunit of 
                     L-tartrate dehydratase |CITS: [8371115]|.  Expression may 
                     be translationally coupled to TtdA |CITS: [8371115]|. 
                     <i>ttdB</i> shows differential codon adaptation, resulting 
                     in differential translation efficiency signatures, in 
                     thermophilic microbes.  It was therefore predicted to play 
                     a role in the heat shock response.  A <i>ttdB</i> deletion 
                     mutant was shown to be more sensitive than wild-type 
                     specifically to heat shock, but not other stresses |CITS: 
                     [24580753]|.
                     TtdB: ""L-<b>t</b>ar<b>t</b>rate <b>d</b>ehydratase 
                     <b>B</b>"" |CITS: [8371115]|"
