                     /label=mug
     CDS             complement(3208326..3208832)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="mug"
                     /locus_tag="b3068"
                     /product="bifunctional stationary phase mismatch/uracil
                     DNA glycosylase / DNA containing a base with lesion 
                     hydrolase"
                     /EC_number="3.2.2.28"
                     /label=mug
                     /note="Mug is a glycosylase that acts in DNA repair |CITS: 
                     [8878487]|.  Mug shows activity toward G:U and G:T base 
                     mismatches |CITS: [9489705]|.  Mug also shows activity 
                     toward epsilonC (3,N4-ethenocytosine) |CITS: [9671708], 
                     [10521502]|, 8-HM-epsilondC 
                     (8-(hydroxymethyl)-3,N4-etheno-2'-deoxycytidine) |CITS: 
                     [11841206]|, 1,N(2)-epsilonG (1,N(2)-ethenoguanine) lesions
                     |CITS: [12016206]|, and 5-formyluracil |CITS: [12531390]| 
                     lesions.
                     Structural models for the specificity of the enzyme for G:U
                     and G:T base mispairings |CITS: [9489705]| and for the G:U 
                     preference of the enzyme |CITS: [10581234]| are presented. 
                     The substrate specificity of the enzyme is discussed in 
                     detail |CITS: [12184783], [12482242], [12668677]|.
                     Mug activity reduces mutation during stationary phase 
                     |CITS: [11555290]|, whereas it does not play a large role 
                     in DNA repair during cell growth |CITS: [10521502]|.
                     A mug mutant exhibits increased mutagenesis during 
                     stationary phase, compared to wild type and to an ung 
                     mutant |CITS: [11555290]|.
                     Crystal structures of Mug are presented |CITS: [9489705], 
                     [10581234]|.
                     Regulation has been described |CITS: [11555290]|.  Mug 
                     production is upregulated upon stationary phase entry 
                     |CITS: [11555290]|.
                     Mug: ""<U>m</U>ismatch-specific <U>u</U>racil 
                     DNA-<U>g</U>lycosylase"" |CITS: [9489705]|.
                     dsUDG: ""<U>d</U>ouble-<U>s</U>trand-specific 
                     <U>u</U>racil-<U>D</U>NA <U>g</U>lycosylase"" |CITS: 
                     [10521502]|."
