                     /product="bifunctional glycoside hydrolase / nigerose
                     hydrolase"
                     /label=ygjK
                     /note="YgjK belongs to the glycoside hydrolase family 63
                     and was shown to possess &alpha;-1,3-glucosyl hydrolase 
                     activity.  Of the tested substrates, nigerose was the best;
                     however, it is unlikely to be the natural substrate of the 
                     enzyme |CITS: [18586271]|.  YgjK is able to hydrolyze 
                     2-<i>O</i>-&alpha;-D-glucopyranosyl-D-galactopyranose 
                     |CITS: [23826932]|.
                     The point mutations E727A and D324N convert the enzyme to a
                     glycosynthase |CITS: [23826932]|.
                     Crystal structures of YgjK alone and in complex with 
                     various sugars have been solved |CITS: 
                     [15213393][18586271][23826932]|."
