     gene            complement(3227500..3227814)
                     /gene="higB"
                     /locus_tag="b3083"
                     /label=higB
     CDS             complement(3227500..3227814)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="higB"
                     /locus_tag="b3083"
                     /product="trifunctional ribosome-dependent mRNA
                     interferase toxin HigB / mRNA interferase / HigB-HigA 
                     toxin/antitoxin complex and DNA-binding transcriptional 
                     repressor"
                     /label=higB
                     /note="HigB is the toxin of the HigB-HigA toxin-antitoxin 
                     system, acting as a translation-dependent mRNA interferase.
                     HigB inhibits protein synthesis by cleaving translated 
                     mRNAs within the coding region |CITS: [19943910]|. It also 
                     is a BECR-fold toxin in the RelE/ParE superfamily of type 
                     II toxin-antitoxin systems |CITS: [39998207]|.
                     An analysis of the targets and site specificity showed that
                     HigB favors a G nucleotide downstream of the cleavage site 
                     and shows strong codon position preference. Like other 
                     <i>E. coli</i> endoribonuclease toxins, HigB activity does 
                     not affect mature ribosomes, but inhibits ribosome 
                     biogenesis, likely by affecting the translation of a 
                     specific set of ribosomal proteins |CITS: [34544284]|.
                     The crystal structure of the HigBA toxin-antitoxin complex 
                     suggests that the putative HigB active site is not occluded
                     in the complex |CITS: [27601326]|.
                     Ectopic expression of HigB causes inhibition of cell growth
                     |CITS: [19943910]|. Overexpression of any one of three RNA 
                     interferase toxins HicA, HigB and YafQ suppresses the 
                     essentiality of |FRAME: RPOE-MONOMER &sigma;<sup>E</sup>| 
                     |CITS: [25917909]|.
                     The promoter upstream of <i>higB</i> appears to be 
                     autorepressed by HigA; Lon protease is required for 
                     activation of transcription. Transcription is induced by 
                     chloramphenicol treatment as well as amino acid starvation 
                     induced by serine hydroxamate |CITS: [19943910]|.
                     Review: |CITS: [22060041][31932311]|"
                     /translation="MHLITQKALKDAAEKYPQHKTELVALGNTIAKGYFKKPESLKAVF
                     PSLDNFKYLDKHYVFNVGGNELRVVAMVFFESQKCYIREVMTHKEYDFFTAVHRTKGKK
                     "
