     gene            complement(3228098..3229234)
                     /gene="rlmG"
                     /locus_tag="b3084"
                     /label=rlmG
     CDS             complement(3228098..3229234)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rlmG"
                     /locus_tag="b3084"
                     /product="23S rRNA m(2)G1835 methyltransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.1.1.174"
                     /label=rlmG
                     /note="RlmG is the methyltransferase responsible for
                     methylation of 23S rRNA at the N2 position of the G1835 
                     nucleotide.  <i>In vitro</i>, recombinant RlmG is able to 
                     methylate naked 23S rRNA, but not 23S rRNA assembled into 
                     the 50S ribosomal subunit |CITS: [17010380]|.  Methylation 
                     of G1835 occurs during the early stages of ribosome 
                     assembly |CITS: [20719918]| and enhances association of the
                     ribosomal subunits |CITS: [21237242]|.
                     Phylogenomic analysis revealed sequence similarities and 
                     conserved architecture of the predicted active sites; at 
                     that time, RlmG was thought to be a candidate for the RsmD 
                     16S rRNA methyltransferase |CITS: [11053259][11929612]|. 
                     Crystal and solution structures of RlmG in complex with 
                     S-adenosylmethionine have been determined, allowing 
                     modeling of the catalytic mechanism of the enzyme |CITS: 
                     [22753782]|.  The N-terminal domain of RlmG was shown to be
                     able to bind RNA independently |CITS: [22753782]|.
                     An <i>rlmG</i> null mutation leads to loss of methylation 
                     at G1835 of the 23S rRNA.  A strain lacking <i>rlmG</i> 
                     shows reduced fitness in growth competition assays, 
                     especially under sub-optimal growth conditions |CITS: 
                     [17010380]|.
                     RlmG: ""<b>r</b>RNA <b>l</b>arge subunit 
                     <b>m</b>ethyltransferase <b>G</b>"" |CITS: [17010380]| 
                     Review: |CITS: [17389639]|"
