     gene            3233303..3234547
                     /gene="sstT"
                     /locus_tag="b3089"
                     /label=sstT
     CDS             3233303..3234547
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="sstT"
                     /locus_tag="b3089"
                     /product="serine/threonine:Na(+) symporter"
                     /label=sstT
                     /note="Early studies characterized a
                     Na<sup>+</sup>-dependent serine-threonine transport system 
                     in the K-12 derived <i>E. coli</i> strain W3133-2 |CITS: 
                     [2825778]|. Purified His-tagged SstT, reconstituted into 
                     liposomes mediates serine uptake which is dependent on an 
                     inwardly directed Na<sup>+</sup> gradient and membrane 
                     potential |CITS: [12097162]|. Serine transport in 
                     reconstituted proteoliposomes is inhibited by L-threonine, 
                     but not by other amino acids |CITS: [12097162]|.
                     In the Transporter Classification Database |CITS: 
                     [33170213]| SstT is a member of the Dicarboxylate/Amino 
                     Acid:Cation Symporter (DAACS) Family."
