                     /product="trifunctional D-glucoronate/D-galacturonate
                     isomerase / D-glucuronate isomerase / D-galacturonate 
                     isomerase"
                     /EC_number="5.3.1.12"
                     /label=uxaC
                     /note="Uronate isomerase catalyzes the initial step of 
                     isomerization of the alduronic to the keturonic acid in the
                     glucuronate
                     and galacturonate degradation pathways.
                     Cofactor requirements of the enzyme are unclear; one of the
                     earlier reports on purification of the enzyme states that
                     Zn<sup>2+</sup> inhibits the enzyme |CITS: [13794771]|, 
                     while a later report states that uronate isomerase is a 
                     metalloenzyme, with Zn<sup>2+</sup> as the likely 
                     physiologically relevant cofactor |CITS: [15358357]|. 
                     Tagaturonate and fructuronate act as inducers |CITS: 
                     [6997263]|; production of the enzyme is under catabolite 
                     repression |CITS: [7026975]|."
