     gene            3238583..3239881
                     /gene="exuT"
                     /locus_tag="b3093"
                     /label=exuT
     CDS             3238583..3239881
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="exuT"
                     /locus_tag="b3093"
                     /product="trifunctional hexuronate transporter /
                     D-galacturonate transporter / D-glucuronate transporter"
                     /label=exuT
                     /note="ExuT is a transporter for aldohexuronates such as 
                     D-galacturonate and D-glucuronate. Mutations affecting the 
                     transport of hexuronates have been shown to map to the 
                     <I>exuT</I> gene |CITS: [6343797]|. ExuT is a member of the
                     major facilitator superfamily (MFS) of transporters |CITS: 
                     [9529885]| and probably functions as an 
                     aldohexuronate/proton symporter. The <I>exuT</I> gene 
                     constitutes a hexuronate-inducible single gene operon, 
                     whose expression is controlled
                     by the ExuR regulator |CITS: [6997263]|. Imported 
                     hexuronates are initially metabolised to 
                     2-keto-3-deoxy-D-gluconate."
