                     /label=yqiM
                     /note="YqiM was identified as a previously unannotated
                     small protein; its expression is higher during exponential 
                     phase than during stationary phase in rich media |CITS: 
                     [30837344]|.
                     "
                     /translation="MLMYQTRRTYQNSNNIAVVHLLKPAWR"
     gene            3241132..3241794
                     /gene="yqjA"
                     /locus_tag="b3095"
                     /label=yqjA
     CDS             3241132..3241794
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yqjA"
                     /locus_tag="b3095"
                     /product="DedA family protein YqjA"
                     /label=yqjA
                     /note="A <I>yghB yqjA</I> double null strain has a
                     synthetic growth defect at elevated temperatures, forms 
                     chains of cells at permissive temperatures, and can be 
                     complemented by <I>yghB, yqjA, yohD,</I> or <I>yabI</I> 
                     expressed from a plasmid |CITS:[18456815]|. The double and 
                     single mutants displayed altered phospholipid compositions 
                     |CITS:[18456815]|.
                     An <i>E. coli &Delta;yqjA &Delta;yghB</i> strain is 
                     hypersensitive to a number of structurally diverse drugs 
                     and dyes including ethidium bromide, methyl viologen, 
                     acriflavine, nalidixic acid and &beta;-lactam antibiotics. 
                     A wild-type response is restored by expression of 
                     <i>yqjA</i> from a plasmid |CITS: [24277026]|. Mutation of 
                     the membrane embedded acidic amino acids E39 (glutamic 
                     acid) or D51 (aspartic acid) in plasmid-expressed YqjA 
                     compromises its ability to restore wild-type resistance 
                     |CITS: [24277026]|. Overexpression of <i>yqjA</i> in a 
                     wild-type background does not result in increased 
                     resistance to any of the compounds tested. Overexpression 
                     of the |FRAME: G6440 ""<i>mdfA</i>""| antiporter restores 
                     the wild-type resistance of an <i>E. coli &Delta;yqjA 
                     &Delta;yghB</i> strain to all componds tested as does 
                     growth in the presence of 400mM NaCl or with increased 
                     amounts of cations or at pH 6 |CITS: [24277026], 
                     [18456815]|. Deletion of <i>yqjA</i> and <i>yghB</i> may 
                     indirectly cause drug sensitivity due to impairment of the 
                     proton motive force (PMF) |CITS: [24277026]|.
                     <i>yqjA</i> is necessary for bacterial cell survival at 
                     alkaline pH |CITS:[ 28591809]|.
                     YqjA is a member of the DedA family of inner membrane 
                     proteins |CITS:[18456815], [23086209]|. <i>E. coli</i> K-12
                     contains 7 other DedA family members, namely |FRAME: 
                     EG10216 ""DedA""|, |FRAME: EG11824 ""YghB""|, |FRAME: 
                     EG11571 ""YabI""|, |FRAME: EG12017 ""YohD""|, |FRAME: G7407
                     ""YqaA""|, |FRAME: G6945-MONOMER ""YdjX""| and |FRAME: 
                     G6947 ""YdjZ""|.  Collectively, the DedA family is 
                     essential in <i>E. coli</i> K-12 |CITS: [22301910]|. 
                     Transcription of <I>yqjA</I> is regulated by RpoE 
                     (&sigma;<sup>E</sup>) |CITS:[11274153]|. The <i>yqjA</i> 
                     promoter activity is high at alkaline pH and this activity 
                     requires the presence of the transcriptional regulator CpxR
                     and extracellular sodium or potassium salts |CITS:[ 
                     28591809]|.
                     <i>ecfL</i>:  <U>e</U>xtra<U>c</U>ytoplasmic 
                     <U>f</U>unction |CITS:[11274153]|.
                     "
                     /translation="MELLTQLLQALWAQDFETLANPSMIGMLYFVLFVILFLENGLLPA
                     AFLPGDSLLVLVGVLIAKGAMGYPQTILLLTVAASLGCWVSYIQGRWLGNTRTVQNWLS
