                     /label=mzrA
     CDS             3241798..3242181
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="mzrA"
                     /locus_tag="b3096"
                     /product="modulator protein MzrA"
                     /label=mzrA
                     /note="The MzrA protein functions to regulate the
                     EnvZ/OmpR osmoregulatory two-component signal transduction 
                     system. Overexpression of <i>mzrA</i> suppresses the 
                     conditionally lethal phenotype of a <i>degP bamB</i> double
                     deletion mutant |CITS:[19432797]| and results in reduced 
                     levels of OmpF, LamB and to a smaller extent MalE. This 
                     effect was OmpR and EnvZ dependent |CITS:[19432797]|. MzrA 
                     interacts with EnvZ <i>in vivo</i> |CITS:[19432797], 
                     [20889743]|. Constitutively activated CpxA/CpxR strains 
                     regulate EnvZ/OmpR in an MzrA dependent manner suggesting 
                     that MzrA links these two signal transduction systems 
                     |CITS:[19432797]|
                     MzrA is an inner membrane protein with its C-terminus 
                     exposed to the periplasm and its N-terminus exposed to the 
                     cytoplasm |CITS:[19432797]|.
                     Transcription of <i>mzrA</i> is regulated by RpoE 
                     (&sigma;<sup>E</sup>) |CITS: [11274153]|.
                     MzrA: ""<b>m</b>odulator of Env<b>Z</b> and Omp<b>R</b> 
                     <b>A</b>"" |CITS: [19432797]|"
