     gene            3242734..3243039
                     /gene="yqjD"
                     /locus_tag="b3098"
                     /label=yqjD
     CDS             3242734..3243039
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yqjD"
                     /locus_tag="b3098"
                     /product="ribosome- and membrane-associated DUF883 
                     domain-containing protein YqjD"
                     /label=yqjD
                     /note="YqjD is an inner membrane protein that associates
                     with the 30S subunit of 70S and 100S ribosomes during 
                     stationary phase |CITS: [22661687]|. The YqjD protein 
                     localizes to clusters of various sizes that are 
                     predominantly located at a cell pole, especially during 
                     stationary phase; the Min system is involved in 
                     localization of the protein |CITS: [22380631]|. A YqjD-YFP 
                     fusion protein localizes mainly at the cell poles; the tail
                     anchor domain of YqjD localizes to regions enriched in 
                     phosphatidic acid |CITS: [34644400]||
                     Overexpression of <i>yqjD</i> inhibits cell growth |CITS: 
                     [22661687]|. A <i>yqjD</i> mutant shows increased biofilm 
                     formation compared to wild type, but decreased biofilm 
                     formation when the derepressed conjugative plasmid 
                     R1<i>drd</i>19 is present |CITS: [18344336]|. A 
                     &Delta;<i>yqjD</i> mutant also shows slightly decreased 
                     persister cell formation |CITS: [28431088]|.
                     <i>yqjD</i> is expressed during stationary phase, and 
                     expression is dependent on RpoS |CITS: [22661687]|. 
                     Polyamines stimulate expression of <i>yqjD</i> |CITS: 
                     [28431088]|. |FRAME: EG11447-MONOMER CsrA| directly 
                     regulates <i>yqjD</i> expression post-transcriptionally; 
                     CsrA represses translation of <i>yqjD</i> during 
                     exponential growth |CITS: [37943032]|.
                     YqjD belongs to the heterogeneous group of C-tail-anchored 
                     membrane proteins |CITS: [20406421]|. YqjD, |FRAME: G7173 
                     ElaB|, and |FRAME: B0899-MONOMER ""YgaM""| are paralogs 
                     |CITS: [22661687]|. YqjD, ElaB, and YgaM are 
                     ribosome-associated factors implicated in stress-associated
                     translation modulation (see |CITS: [30476446]|)"
                     /translation="MSKEHTTEHLRAELKSLSDTLEEVLSSSGEKSKEELSKIRSKAEQ
                     ALKQSRYRLGETGDAIAKQTRVAAARADEYVRENPWTGVGIGAAIGVVLGVLLSRR"
