     gene            complement(3250038..3251369)
                     /gene="cyuP"
                     /locus_tag="b3110"
                     /label=cyuP
     CDS             complement(3250038..3251369)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="cyuP"
                     /locus_tag="b3110"
                     /product="L-cysteine importer"
                     /label=cyuP
                     /note="CyuP is an L-cysteine-specific importer that,
                     together wih |FRAME: G7622-MONOMER|, supports anaerobic 
                     growth with cysteine as either the sole nitrogen or the 
                     sole carbon/energy source |CITS: [35377168]|. CyuP-mediated
                     [<sup>14</sup>C]cysteine import can be detected (after 
                     cysteine induction) using an engineered strain that lacks 
                     other interfering transporters |CITS: [35377168]|.
                     A &Delta;<i>cyuP</i> strain has decreased growth in the 
                     presence of cysteine and produces significantly less 
                     hydrogen sulfide than wild type |CITS: [27435271]|. A 
                     &Delta;<i>cyuP</i> mutant does not show anaerobic cysteine 
                     sensitivity (10 mM cysteine) and does not show 
                     cysteine-dependent production of sulfide |CITS: 
                     [28607157]|.
                     <i>cyuP</i> forms an operon with <i>cyuA</i>; expression is
                     activated by |FRAME: G6247-MONOMER ""DecR""| in the 
                     presence of L-cysteine |CITS: [27435271]| (see further 
                     |CITS: [28607157][35377168]|).
                     In the Transporter Classification Database |CITS: 
                     [33170213]|, CyuP is a member of the Hydroxy/Aromatic Amino
                     Acid Permease (HAAAP) Family within the Amino 
                     Acid-Polyamine-Organocation (APC) Superfamily.
                     In enterohaemorrhagic <i>E. coli</i> (EHEC) the CyuP 
                     homolog, known as DlsT, is implicated in proton-dependent 
                     serine transport |CITS: [26727373]|
                     <i>cyuP</i>: <U>cy</U>steine <U>u</U>tilization 
                     <U>p</U>ermease |CITS: [28607157]|"
