     gene            complement(3257045..3258376)
                     /gene="tdcC"
                     /locus_tag="b3116"
                     /label=tdcC
     CDS             complement(3257045..3258376)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="tdcC"
                     /locus_tag="b3116"
                     /product="trifunctional threonine/serine:H(+) symporter
                     TdcC / L-serine:H(+) symporter / L-threonine:H(+) 
                     symporter"
                     /label=tdcC
                     /note="TdcC is a threonine transport system, likely to
                     function as a threonine/proton symporter. Disruption of 
                     <I>tdcC</I> reduced threonine uptake under anaerobic 
                     conditions, and this defect could be complemented by the 
                     cloned <I>tdcC</I> gene |CITS: [2115866]|. The TdcC 
                     transport system displayed a Km of approx 6 &mu;M and 
                     threonine transport was inhibited by uncouplers, suggesting
                     it is a high affinity threonine/proton symporter |CITS: 
                     [2115866]|. TdcC has also been shown to be a proton-driven 
                     serine transporter |CITS: [9498571]|. TdcC is a member of 
                     the hydroxy/aromatic amino acid permease (HAAAP) family of 
                     transporters, and is homologous to the serine transporter 
                     SdaC. The <I>tdcC</I> gene is located in the <I>tdcABC</I> 
                     operon, which also codes for threonine dehydratase |CITS: 
                     [3053659]|. Expression of <I>tdc-lacZ</I> fusions has 
                     indicated that this operon is expressed under anaerobic 
                     conditions |CITS: [2115866]|. Threonine and serine imported
                     under anaerobic conditions are degraded to ammonia and the 
                     corresponding &alpha;-keto acids."
