                     /note="Tartronate semialdehyde reductase (GarR) catalyzes
                     the reduction of tatronate semialdehyde to yield glycerate 
                     |CITS: [9772162]|.  GarR is one of two tartronate 
                     semialdehyde reductase isozymes in <I>E. coli</i>. 
                     Enzymatic activity of tartronate semialdehyde reductase is 
                     induced by growth on <i>D</i>-glucarate, 
                     <i>D</i>-galactarate, and <i>D</i>-glycerate |CITS: 
                     [10762278]|."
