     gene            complement(3266932..3268266)
                     /gene="garP"
                     /locus_tag="b3127"
                     /label=garP
     CDS             complement(3266932..3268266)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="garP"
                     /locus_tag="b3127"
                     /product="multifunctional galactarate/D-glucarate
                     transporter GarP / D-glucarate transporter / D-galactarate 
                     transporter / D-glycerate transporter"
                     /label=garP
                     /note="GarP is a putative substrate:proton symporter which
                     is implicated in uptake of the diacid sugars, galactarate 
                     and D-glucarate.
                     <i>garP</i> is located in a polycistronic operon along with
                     genes whose products are involved in galactarate and 
                     D-glucarate metabolism; <i>garP</i> encodes a potential 
                     D-glucarate or galactarate transporter |CITS: [9772162]|. A
                     &Phi;(<i>garP-lacZ</i>) transcriptional fusion is induced 
                     in cultures grown in the presence of galactarate, 
                     D-glucarate or D-glycerate; a polar <i>garP</i>::Tn5 
                     insertion mutant has 'impaired' D-glucarate and D-glycerate
                     utilization |CITS: [10762278]|.
                     In the Transporter Classification Database GarP is a member
                     of the Anion:Cation Symporter (ACS) Family within the Major
                     Facilitator Superfamily (MFS) |CITS: [9529885][26546518]|.
                     GarP may function as a proton-driven glucarate symporter 
                     and perhaps a glucarate:glycerate antiporter; it may form 
                     part of a membrane transport metabolon linking the 
                     transport of glucarate with the enzymes responsible for its
                     metabolism |CITS: [22705263]|.
                     The genes encoding enzymes involved in galactarate and 
                     D-glucarate metabolism are organized in three 
                     transcriptional units |CITS: [9772162]|; during aerobic 
                     growth with galactarate, D-glucarate or D-glycerate 
                     expression of these genes is coordinately regulated by the 
                     transcription factor CdaR |CITS: [10762278]|.
                     A knockout mutant of this gene was sensitive to boric acid 
                     exposure; a complementation assay restored its intrinsic 
                     boric acid resistance. Double and triple knockout mutants 
                     (<i>&Delta;garP&Delta;|FRAME: G6253|, 
                     &Delta;ylaC&Delta;garP&Delta;|FRAME: G7261|, 
                     &Delta;ylaC&Delta;garP&Delta;|FRAME: G6994| and 
                     &Delta;yfeS&Delta;yoaC&Delta;garP</i>) exhibited increasing
                     sensitivity, respectively |CITS: [38466471]|."
                     /translation="MILDTVDEKKKGVHTRYLILLIIFIVTAVNYADRATLSIAGTEVA
                     KELQLSAVSMGYIFSAFGWAYLLMQIPGGWLLDKFGSKKVYTYSLFFWSLFTFLQGFVD
