     CDS             3275335..3276489
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="agaS"
                     /locus_tag="b3136"
                     /product="bifunctional putative galactosamine-6-phosphate 
                     deaminase/isomerase / galactosamine-6-phosphate 
                     deaminase/isomerase"
                     /label=agaS
                     /note="AgaS has been predicted to be an isomerase involved
                     in <i>N</i>-acetylgalactosamine (GalNAc) utilization in 
                     some strains of <i>E. coli</i> |CITS: [10931310]|.
                     Because <i>E. coli</i> K-12 contains a partial deletion of 
                     the <i>aga</i> gene cluster and does not utilize GalNAc, 
                     functional studies have been carried out in <i>E. coli</i> 
                     C.  There, a &Delta;<i>agaS</i> mutant becomes unable to 
                     utilize GalNAc |CITS: [22711537][23634833]|.
                     Expression of the <i>agaS</i> operon is induced by 
                     galactosamine and <i>N-</i>-acetylgalactosamine and 
                     repressed by AgaR |CITS: [14731281]|."
