     CDS             3277529..3278005
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="agaB"
                     /locus_tag="b3138"
                     /product="bifunctional galactosamine-specific PTS enzyme
                     IIB component / galactosamine-specific PTS enzyme II"
                     /label=agaB
                     /note="Sequence analysis indicates that <i>agaB</i>
                     encodes a protein with similarity to the IIB domain of the 
                     PTS Enzymes II specific for mannose.  <i>agaB</i> has 
                     sequence similarity with |FRAME: G7632 ""<i>agaV</i>""|. 
                     <i>agaB</i> contains a conserved histidine residue (His17) 
                     |CITS: [8932697]|.
                     <i>agaB</i> encodes the Enzyme IIB domain of a predicted 
                     galactosamine (Gam or GalN) transporting PEP-dependent 
                     phosphotransferase system. <i>E. coli</i> K-12 cannot 
                     transport galactosamine as it is lacking an Enzyme IIA 
                     domain for this PTS (encoded by the <i>agaF</i> gene in 
                     <i>E. coli</i> strains B and C). Providing <I>agaF</I> on a
                     plasmid results in a Gam<sup>+</sup> phenotype 
                     |CITS:[10931310]|."
