     CDS             3279629..3280384
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="agaI"
                     /locus_tag="b3141"
                     /product="putative deaminase AgaI"
                     /label=agaI
                     /note="Unlike other <i>E. coli</i> strains, K-12 is unable
                     to grow on N-acetylgalactosamine as a source of carbon and 
                     energy.  This phenotype is apparently due to a deletion of 
                     genes essential for transport and metabolism of 
                     N-acetylgalactosamine.  AgaI was predicted to catalyze the 
                     deaminase step if the pathway were functional |CITS: 
                     [10931310]|, but that reaction was later shown to be 
                     catalyzed by AgaS |CITS: [22711537]|.
                     AgaI was also predicted to be a galactosamine-6-phosphate 
                     isomerase by |CITS: [11574054]|.  Based on sequence 
                     similarity, AgaI might have 6-phosphogluconolactonase 
                     activity |CITS: [12952533]|.
                     AgaI: ""N-<b>a</b>cetyl<b>ga</b>lactosamine degradation"" 
                     |CITS: [8932697]|"
