                     /note="<i>yraHIJK</i> is a putative chaperone-usher
                     fimbrial operon in <i>E.coli K-12</i> |CITS: [12192075], 
                     [20345943]|. The operon is cryptic under normal laboratory 
                     conditions but when constitutive expression is induced in a
                     strain that lacks the type 1 fimbrial complex the 
                     <i>yra</i> operon promotes adhesion to eukaryotic 
                     epithelial cells (T<sub>4</sub> bladder cells) |CITS: 
                     [20345943]|. Expression of the <i>yra</i> operon is 
                     regulated by the global regulators |FRAME: PD00288 
                     ""H-NS""| and |FRAME: CPLX0-226 ""CRP cAMP""| |CITS: 
