     gene            3289168..3289758
                     /gene="diaA"
                     /locus_tag="b3149"
                     /label=diaA
     CDS             3289168..3289758
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="diaA"
                     /locus_tag="b3149"
                     /product="DnaA initiator-associating protein DiaA"
                     /label=diaA
                     /note="Proper amounts of DiaA are required for the timely 
                     initiation of chromosomal replication.  DiaA interacts 
                     directly with the N-terminal domains I-II of |FRAME: 
                     PD03831 DnaA| in a DNA-independent manner |CITS: 
                     [15326179]| and stimulates the assembly of DnaA on |FRAME: 
                     G0-10506 <i>oriC</i>|, conformational changes in the 
                     initiation complex, and unwinding of <i>oriC</i> |CITS: 
                     [17699754]|.  Both DnaA binding and homotetramerization of 
                     DiaA are required for stimulation of replication |CITS: 
                     [17699754]|.
                     A crystal structure of DiaA has been solved at 1.8 &Aring; 
                     resolution, showing that DiaA forms a homotetramer |CITS: 
                     [17699754]|.  Residues required for tetramerization or DnaA
                     binding were identified by mutagenesis |CITS: [17699754]|. 
                     DnaA F46 is the crucial residue that is required for 
                     interaction with DiaA as well as DnaB |CITS: [19632993]|.
                     Timing of replication initiation is disrupted in both a 
                     <i>diaA</i> mutant and a DiaA overexpression strain |CITS: 
                     [15326179]|.
                     DiaA: ""<b>D</b>naA <b>i</b>nitiator-<b>a</b>ssociating 
                     factor <b>A</b>"" |CITS: [15326179]|
                     Reviews: |CITS: [17459114][20157337][29357054]|"
