     gene            3289768..3290343
                     /gene="dolP"
                     /locus_tag="b3150"
                     /label=dolP
     CDS             3289768..3290343
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="dolP"
                     /locus_tag="b3150"
                     /product="division and outer membrane stress-associated 
                     lipid-binding lipoprotein"
                     /label=dolP
                     /note="DolP (formerly YraP) is an outer membrane
                     lipoprotein; a DolP-mCherry fusion protein localizes to the
                     septal ring division site |CITS: [28708841]|. DolP is a 
                     dual BON (bacterial OsmY and nodulation)-domain containing 
                     protein; DolP binds specifically to anionic phospholipids 
                     via its C-terminal BON domain - this interaction is 
                     required for localization to the cell division site and is 
                     important for DolP function |CITS: [33315009]|.
                     Genetic interaction analyses implicate DolP in the |FRAME: 
                     EG12111-MONOMER ""NlpD""|-mediated activation of AmiC 
                     |CITS: [28708841]|. DolP has a role in cell divivion but it
                     is not an upstream regulator of NlpD; DolP does not iteract
                     with NlpD nor activate amidases <i>in vitro</i> |CITS: 
                     [35604759]|.
                     Deletion of <I>dolP</I> results in sensitivity to SDS and a
                     slight induction of &sigma;<sup>E</sup> activity; 
                     &Delta;<i>dolP</i> exhibits a synthetic phenotype with 
                     <i>surA::Cm</i>  |CITS:[15968066]|. &Delta;<i>dolP</i> 
                     cells show an increase in membrane fluidity |CITS: 
                     [33315009]|.
                     <i>dolP</i> is a member of the RpoE (&sigma;<sup>E</sup>) 
                     regulon |CITS: [11274153][16336047]|.
                     <i>dolP</i>: <U>d</U>ivision and <U>o</U>uter membrane 
                     stress-associated <U>l</U>ipid-binding protein |CITS: 
                     [33315009]|"
