                     /product="bifunctional DNA damage response nuclease YhbQ / 
                     exodeoxyribonuclease 3' -> 5"""
                     /EC_number="3.1.11.1"
                     /label=yhbQ
                     /note="Purified YhbQ has metal dependent nuclease
                     activity; genetic interaction screening suggests that YhbQ 
                     functions during DNA damage repair |CITS: [26774489]|. 
                     Purified YhbQ has metal dependent 3' to 5' exonuclease 
                     activity on ssDNA; purified YhbQ has metal dependent 
                     endonuclease activity on circular ssDNA and linear dsDNA 
                     but not on circular dsDNA or RNA; the divalent cations 
                     Mg<sup>2+</sup>, Mn<sup>2+</sup> and Co<sup>2+</sup> all 
                     support enzyme activity |CITS: [26774489]|. Purified YhbQ 
                     is active on several substrates related to nucleotide 
                     excision repair (NER), including dsDNA substrates 
                     containing a single nucleotide mismatch or ssDNA loops, and
                     on DNA recombination intermediates |CITS: [26774489]|. A 
                     strain lacking <i>yhbQ</i> shows hypersensitivity to UV 
                     irradiation and to the DNA damaging agents mitomycin C and 
                     4-nitroquinoline-1-oxide |CITS: [26774489]|. 
                     Affinity-tagged YhbQ co-purifies with |FRAME: PD03831 
                     ""DnaA""|, |FRAME: EG10823-MONOMER ""RecA""|, |FRAME: 
                     G7656-MONOMER ""ObgE""| and |FRAME: EG11062-MONOMER 
                     ""UvrB""| |CITS: [26774489]|."
