                     /gene="ubiT"
                     /locus_tag="b3157"
                     /product="anaerobic ubiquinone biosynthesis accessory
                     factor UbiT"
                     /label=ubiT
                     /note="UbiT, like |FRAME: EG11474-MONOMER UbiJ|, is an
                     SCP2 domain-containing protein.  It may similarly function 
                     as an accessory factor in the oxygen-independent pathway 
                     for ubiquinone biosynthesis |CITS: [31289180]|.
                     UbiT is a cytoplasmic protein that is expressed in early 
                     exponential phase and is degraded by the essential 
                     membrane-bound protease |FRAME: EG11506-MONOMER FtsH| 
                     |CITS: [27766750]|.
                     A &Delta;<i>ubiT</i> mutant is deficient in ubiquinone-8 
                     biosynthesis under anaerobic growth conditions |CITS: 
                     [31289180]|.  Expression of <i>ubiT</i> is repressed by the
                     biofilm regulator CsgD |CITS: [21421764]|.
                     UbiT: ""<b>ubi</b>quinone biosynthesis <b>T</b>"" |CITS: 
                     [31289180]|"
