                     /product="trifunctional ubiquinone biosynthesis protein
                     UbiU / 2-(all-trans-polyprenyl)phenol 6-hydroxylase 
                     (prephenate) / 2-octaprenylphenol 6-hydroxylase 
                     (prephenate)"
                     /EC_number="1.97.1.15"
                     /label=ubiU
                     /note="UbiU together with UbiV functions in the three 
                     hydroxylation reactions in the oxygen-independent pathway 
                     for ubiquinone biosynthesis |CITS: [31289180]|.
                     UbiU contains a 4Fe-4S iron-sulfur cluster; mutagenesis of 
                     the cysteine residues C169, C176, C193, and C232 identified
                     them as the iron-chelating residues.  UbiU and UbiV can be 
                     purified as a heterodimer |CITS: [31289180]|. A 
                     &Delta;<i>ubiU</i> mutant is deficient in ubiquinone-8 
                     biosynthesis under anaerobic growth conditions |CITS: 
                     [31289180]|.
                     UbiU: ""<b>ubi</b>quinone biosynthesis <b>U</b>"" |CITS: 
                     [31289180]|"
