     gene            complement(3297932..3299176)
                     /gene="mtr"
                     /locus_tag="b3161"
                     /label=mtr
     CDS             complement(3297932..3299176)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="mtr"
                     /locus_tag="b3161"
                     /product="bifunctional tryptophan:H(+) symporter Mtr / 
                     tryptophan:H(+) symporter"
                     /label=mtr
                     /note="Early studies in <i>E. coli</i> K-12 identified
                     several systems for aromatic amino acid transport including
                     one specific for tryptophan with an apparent Michealis 
                     constant of 3 &mu;M |CITS: [4919744][4323966]|. 
                     5-<U>m</U>ethyl-<U>t</U>ryptophan <U>r</U>esistant 
                     (<i>mtr</i>) mutations described initially by |CITS: 
                     [4882032]| result in loss of this tryptophan-specific 
                     transport system (see |CITS: [334742][1917834]|). 
                     Mtr-mediated tryptophan transport is influenced by the 
                     growth medium and Mtr is also able to transport indole 
                     |CITS: [1917834][22426114]| although this capability has 
                     been disputed |CITS: [21296966]|. Deletion of <i>mtr</i> 
                     negates the indole-induced enhancement of antimicrobial 
                     (malachite green) uptake |CITS: [35297612]|.
                     Membrane topology analysis, together with sequence data, 
                     suggests that Mtr contains 11 transmembrane domains with 
                     its N-terminus located in the cytoplasm |CITS: 
                     [2022620][7814318][15919996]|.
                     Expression of <I>mtr</I> is repressed by tryptophan via the
                     |FRAME: CPLX-125 Trp repressor| and induced by 
                     phenylalanine or tyrosine via |FRAME: PD00413 TyrR| |CITS: 
                     [1904443] [2061290]|.
                     In the Transporter Classification Database (|CITS: 
                     [33170213]|) Mtr is a member of the Hydroxy/Aromatic Amino 
                     Acid Permease (HAAAP) family within the Amino 
                     Acid-Polyamine-Organocation (APC) superfamily.
                     Tryptophan can also be imported into cells by the 
                     low-affinity transporter |FRAME: TNAB-MONOMER TnaB| and by 
                     the general aromatic amino acid transporter |FRAME: 
                     AROP-MONOMER AroP|."
