     CDS             complement(3310913..3311365)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rimP"
                     /locus_tag="b3170"
                     /product="ribosome maturation factor RimP"
                     /label=rimP
                     /note="RimP assists in the maturation of the 30S subunit
                     of the ribosome.  The protein associates with free 30S 
                     ribosomal subunits |CITS: [19150615]|.  The effect of RimP 
                     during <i>in vitro</i> reconstitution of the 30S ribosomal 
                     subunit has been investigated |CITS: [20188109]|.  RimP 
                     plays an important role in stabilization of the central 
                     pseudoknot structure of 16S rRNA and influences the 
                     assembly kinetics of certain ribosomal protein subunits 
                     |CITS: [25313868]|.
                     The secondary structure of RimP has been predicted from NMR
                     data |CITS: [32303998]|.
                     Contrary to results reported earlier (|CITS: [17921263]|, 
                     see below), a <i>rimP</i> in-frame deletion mutant has a 
                     reduced growth rate compared to the wild type, especially 
                     at higher temperatures, and shows a defect in 30S ribosomal
                     subunit maturation |CITS: [19150615]|.  A <i>rimP</i> 
                     insertion mutant shows a more than 1000-fold increased 
                     level of transposition of IS<i>903</i> |CITS: [16135227]|.
                     Expression of <i>rimP</i> decreased in a recombinant 
                     xylitol-producing strain; introduction of a <i>rimP</i> 
                     deletion into that strain increased production of xylitol. 
                     <i>rimP</i> deletion in a wild type background resulted in 
                     better growth during early log phase.  The authors 
                     postulated that deletion of <i>rimP</i> may enhance the 
                     availability of NADPH |CITS: [17921263]|.
                     RimP: ""<b>ri</b>bosome <b>m</b>aturation"" |CITS: 
                     [19150615]|
                     Review: |CITS: [21529161]|"
                     /translation="MSTLEQKLTEMITAPVEALGFELVGIEFIRGRTSTLRIYIDSEDG
