     gene            complement(3320394..3321023)
                     /gene="rlmE"
                     /locus_tag="b3179"
                     /label=rlmE
     CDS             complement(3320394..3321023)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rlmE"
                     /locus_tag="b3179"
                     /product="23S rRNA 2'-O-ribose U2552 methyltransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.1.1.166"
                     /label=rlmE
                     /note="RlmE is the methyltransferase responsible for
                     methylation of 23S rRNA at the 2'-<i>O</i> position of the 
                     ribose at the universally conserved U2552 nucleotide |CITS:
                     [10748051]|. <i>In vitro</i>, the enzyme is active on 
                     ribosomes and the 50S ribosomal subunit, but not free rRNA 
                     |CITS: [10748051][10983982]|. The 45S ribosomal subunit 
                     precursor that accumulates in an <i>rlmE</i> mutant is a 
                     true intermediate on the pathway of 50S subunit assembly. 
                     2'-<i>O</i>-methylation of U2552 promotes association 
                     between helices 92 and 71 of 23S rRNA; together with 
                     incorporation of |FRAME: EG11232-MONOMER|, it promotes late
                     steps of 50S ribosomal subunit assembly |CITS: [26261349]|.
                     Cryo-EM structures and biochemical assays show that 
                     2'-<i>O</i>-methylation of U2552 plays a role in ribosome 
                     biogenesis and protein translation |CITS: [32571953]|.
                     A crystal structure of RlmE has been solved at 1.5 &Aring; 
                     resolution |CITS: [10983982]|. Site-directed mutagenesis 
                     has identified possible active site and substrate binding 
                     residues, and a reaction mechanism has been proposed |CITS:
                     [12181314][15375145]|.
                     A mutant strain lacking RlmE has a decreased growth rate at
                     all temperatures tested and shows reduced protein synthesis
                     activity and accumulation of free ribosomal subunits and 
                     assembly intermediates |CITS: 
                     [10814528][10983982][32174967]| that are unstable at low 
                     Mg<sup>2+</sup> concentrations |CITS: [20172997]|. A 
                     &Delta;<i>rlmE</i> &Delta;<i>rpmJ</i> double mutant 
                     exhibits a severe synthetic growth defect at 37&deg;C and 
                     is unable to grow at 30 or 22&deg;C |CITS: [26261349]|. 
                     Overexpression of the small GTPases ObgE or Der |CITS: 
                     [11976298][16980477][20172997]| suppresses the ribosomal 
                     assembly or stability defect of an <i>rlmE</i> mutant 
                     without restoring the methylation of U2552 |CITS: 
                     [11976298]|. An <i>rlmE</i>-deficient strain shows a 
                     decrease in -1 and +1 frameshifting and a decrease in UAA 
                     and UGA stop codon readthrough, suggesting that the U2552 
                     base may interact with aminoacyl-tRNAs at the ribosomal A 
                     site |CITS: [15715963]|. The effect of a &Delta;<i>rlmE</i>
                     mutation on the proteome has been investigated |CITS: 
                     [32174967]|.
                     A study that used a &Delta;10 ribosomal modification 
                     deletion strain lacking nucleoside modifications around the
                     peptidyl-transferase center (PTC) due to deletions of 
                     |FRAME: EG11118|, |FRAME: G6488|, |FRAME: EG12401|, |FRAME:
                     EG11794|, |FRAME: G6581|, |FRAME: EG12433|, |FRAME: 
                     EG11921|, |FRAME: G7845|, |FRAME: G6746| and |FRAME: 
                     EG11507| found that addition of ectopically produced RlmE 
                     (or genome produced RlmE in &Delta;9 mutant) is the most 
                     effective at alleviating the severe growth defect phenotype
                     of the &Delta;10 strain under different growth temperatures
                     from 37 &deg;C down to 25 &deg;C, pointing to its ability 
                     to rescue ribosome assembly defects of the other ribosome 
                     PTC modification enzymes, though to a lesser degree at 25 
                     &deg;C. RlmB, RlmL, RlmN, and RluC, but not the other 
                     genes, can partially complement the RlmE mutant with 
                     respect to large ribosomal subunit assembly in late 
                     exponential phase cultures as determined by sucrose 
                     gradient ribosome profile assay |CITS: [38554109]|.
                     An <i>rlmE</i> mutant is more sensitive to lincomycin 
                     |CITS: [10814528]|, clindamycin, hygromycin A and 
                     sparsomycin |CITS: [18554609]| than wild-type.
                     Review: |CITS: [24261569]|"
                     /translation="MTGKKRSASSSRWLQEHFSDKYVQQAQKKGLRSRAWFKLDEIQQS
