     gene            3321149..3321442
                     /gene="yhbY"
                     /locus_tag="b3180"
                     /label=yhbY
     CDS             3321149..3321442
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yhbY"
                     /locus_tag="b3180"
                     /product="ribosome assembly factor YhbY"
                     /label=yhbY
                     /note="YhbY is a ribosome assembly factor that is involved
                     in both 30S and 50S ribosomal subunit assembly |CITS: 
                     [27732863]|.
                     YhbY belongs to the CRM domain family of proteins.  It was 
                     found to associate with the 50S subunit of the ribosome 
                     |CITS: [16980477][17105995]| and was also found to 
                     cosediment with a pre-50S ribosomal subunit |CITS: 
                     [17105995]|.
                     The crystal structure of YhbY has been solved at 1.5 
                     &Aring; resolution.  The structure of YhbY is similar to 
                     that of the C-terminal domain of the translation initiation
                     factor IF3, with a basic exterior surface that is predicted
                     to bind RNA |CITS: [12429100]|.
                     A &Delta;<i>yhbY</i> mutant grows more slowly than wild 
                     type, accumulates increased levels of pre-50S ribosomal 
                     subunits |CITS: [17105995]|, and is cold-sensitive |CITS: 
                     [17337586]|.  In a large genetic interaction screen, 
                     <i>yhbY</i> showed genetic interactions with a number of 
                     RNases involved in rRNA maturation as well as several 
                     ribosome biogenesis factors and ribosomal subunit proteins.
                      A &Delta;<i>yhbY</i> mutant shows decreased translational 
                     fidelity and decreased 5' end processing of rRNAs |CITS: 
                     [27732863]|.
                     "
