     gene            complement(3325129..3326094)
                     /gene="yhbE"
                     /locus_tag="b3184"
                     /label=yhbE
     CDS             complement(3325129..3326094)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yhbE"
                     /locus_tag="b3184"
                     /product="putative transporter YhbE"
                     /label=yhbE
                     /note="YhbE is predicted to be an inner membrane protein
                     with 10 transmembrane domains; experimental topology 
                     analysis suggests the C terminus is located in the 
                     cytoplasm |CITS: [15919996]|.
                     <i>yhbE</i> is expressed from an operon along with 
                     <i>rplU</i>, <i>rpmA</i>, and <i>obgE</i> under control of 
                     the <i>rplU</i> promoter. This operon is mainly expressed 
                     during exponential growth and is probably indirectly 
                     regulated by ppGpp/DksA |CITS:[ 27137500]|. Furthermore, 
                     the amount of YhbE is affected by the presence of a 
                     terminator between <i>rpmA</i> and <i>yhbE</i> |CITS:[ 
                     27137500]|.
                     Deletion of <i>yhbE</i> does not affect persister cell 
                     formation |CITS: [26051177]|.
                     In the Transporter Classification Database |CITS: 
                     [24225317]| YhbE is a member of the Drug/Metabolite 
                     Exporter (DME) family within the Drug/Metabolite 
                     Transporter (DMT) superfamily."
