     gene            complement(3331269..3331820)
                     /gene="mlaD"
                     /locus_tag="b3193"
                     /label=mlaD
     CDS             complement(3331269..3331820)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="mlaD"
                     /locus_tag="b3193"
                     /product="bifunctional intermembrane phospholipid
                     transport system, substrate binding protein MlaD / 
                     intermembrane phospholipid transport system"
                     /label=mlaD
                     /note="<i>mlaD</i> encodes an inner membrane anchored
                     subunit of the MlaFEDB transporter complex which functions 
                     as part of a retrograde |CITS: [19383799]| and/or 
                     anterograde |CITS: [31235958]| intermembrane phospholipid 
                     trafficking system.
                     MlaD is implicated in a retrograde phospholipid trafficking
                     pathway; a &Delta;<i>mlaD</i> mutant displays increased 
                     SDS-EDTA sensitivity |CITS: [19383799]|. MlaD is predicted 
                     to be a periplasmic facing, inner membrane protein |CITS: 
                     [19383799]|. MlaD is a member of the mammalian cell entry 
                     (MCE) family of proteins; MlaD consists of a predicted 
                     membrane-anchoring N-terminal &alpha;-helix, followed by an
                     MCE domain and a C-terminal &alpha;-helical domain, both 
                     located in the periplasm |CITS: [28388411]|. MlaD forms a 
                     stable complex with MlaF, MlaE and MlaB; MlaD exists as an 
                     oligomer in the complex; the periplasmic, substrate binding
                     domain of MlaD (sMlaD) forms hexamers <i>in vitro</i>; 
                     hexameric sMlaD binds phospholipids (phosphatidylglycerol 
                     and phosphatidylethanolamine) |CITS: [27529189]|. In the 
                     MlaFEDB cryo-EM structures determined by |CITS: 
                     [33199922]|, MlaD forms a hexameric disc on the periplasmic
                     side of the membrane and interacts with dimeric MlaE in the
                     membrane (see also |CITS: [33236984][32884137][38347327]|).
                     <i>mla</i>: <U>m</U>aintenance of outer membrane 
                     <U>l</U>ipid <U>a</U>symmetry |CITS: [19383799]|
                     Comments: |CITS: [28461688]|"
