     gene            complement(3331825..3332607)
                     /gene="mlaE"
                     /locus_tag="b3194"
                     /label=mlaE
     CDS             complement(3331825..3332607)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="mlaE"
                     /locus_tag="b3194"
                     /product="bifunctional intermembrane phospholipid
                     transport system, integral membrane subunit MlaE / 
                     intermembrane phospholipid transport system"
                     /label=mlaE
                     /note="<i>mlaE</i> encodes an inner membrane subunit of
                     the MlaFEDB transporter complex which functions as part of 
                     a retrograde |CITS: [19383799]| and/or anterograde |CITS: 
                     [31235958]| intermembrane phospholipid trafficking system. 
                     MlaE is the predicted permease component of a retrograde 
                     phospholipid trafficking pathway; a &Delta;<i>mlaE</i> 
                     mutant displays increased SDS-EDTA sensitivity |CITS: 
                     [19383799]|. MlaE forms a stable complex with MlaF, MlaD, 
                     and MlaB |CITS: [27529189]|. In the MlaFEDB cryo-EM 
                     structures determined by |CITS: [33199922]|, dimeric MlaE 
                     forms the transmembrane core of the complex interacting 
                     with both the periplasmic MlaD hexamer and the cytoplasmic 
                     MlaF dimer; each MlaE subunit consists of five 
                     transmembrane domains plus an N-terminal 'elbow helix' 
                     which runs parallel to the plane of the membrane; in the 
                     phospholipid-bound MlaFEDB structure, dimeric MlaE binds 
                     phospholipid within a V-shaped cavity that extends into the
                     periplasm and forms a continuous pathway with the central 
                     channel of the MlaD hexamer (see also |CITS: 
                     [33236984][32884137]|).
                     The doxycycline resistance is diminished in cells lacking 
                     <i>mlaE</i>; also, these cells have an increased surface 
                     hydrophobicity |CITS: [29133912]|.
                     A potential RNA G-quadruplex structure, formed by 
                     guanine-rich sequences located in the coding sequence 
                     region of the gene, was identified in <i>mlaE</i>. This 
                     structure could regulate the expression of the gene, as 
                     observed for <i>hemL</i> gene expression |CITS: 
                     [31964733]|.
                     <i>mla</i>: <u>m</u>aintenance of outer membrane 
                     <u>l</u>ipid <u>a</u>symmetry |CITS: [19383799]|
                     "
