     gene            complement(3332615..3333424)
                     /gene="mlaF"
                     /locus_tag="b3195"
                     /label=mlaF
     CDS             complement(3332615..3333424)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="mlaF"
                     /locus_tag="b3195"
                     /product="bifunctional intermembrane phospholipid
                     transport system, ATP binding subunit MlaF / intermembrane 
                     phospholipid transport system"
                     /label=mlaF
                     /note="<i>mlaF</i> encodes the ATP-binding protein of an
                     inner membrane complex (MlaFEDB) which functions as part of
                     a retrograde |CITS: [19383799]| and/or anterograde |CITS: 
                     [31235958]| intermembrane phospholipid trafficking system.
                     MlaF contains signature motifs conserved in ATP-binding 
                     cassette (ABC) proteins |CITS: [9593292]|. MlaF is 
                     implicated in a retrograde phospholipid trafficking 
                     pathway; a &Delta;<i>mlaF</i> mutant displays increased 
                     SDS-EDTA sensitivity |CITS: [19383799]| (also |CITS: 
                     [32602838]|). MlaF forms a stable complex with MlaE, MlaD 
                     and MlaB; an MlaFEB complex containing an MlaF variant 
                     (MlaF<sub>K47R</sub>) has no intrinsic ATPase activity 
                     <i>in vitro</i> |CITS: [27529189]|. Purified, recombinant 
                     MlaFB (co-expressed from a single transcript) forms a 
                     complex with 1:1 stoichiometry and structures of both 
                     MlaF<sub>1</sub>B<sub>1</sub> - the inactive 
                     'half-transporter' - and MlaF<sub>2</sub>B<sub>2</sub> - 
                     the fully assembled complex - have been solved |CITS: 
                     [32602838]|. In the MlaFEDB cryo-EM structures determined 
                     by |CITS: [33199922]|, dimeric MlaF in the cytoplasm 
                     associates with the auxiliary MlaB subunits and the MlaE 
                     transmembrane core (see also |CITS: [33236984][32884137]|).
                     <i>mla</i>: <U>m</U>aintenance of outer membrane 
                     <U>l</U>ipid <U>a</U>symmetry |CITS: [19383799]|"
