                     /locus_tag="b3196"
                     /label=yrbG
     CDS             3333634..3334611
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yrbG"
                     /locus_tag="b3196"
                     /product="putative transport protein YrbG"
                     /label=yrbG
                     /note="YrbG is an uncharacterized member of the CaCA
                     family of metal cation exchangers |CITS: [10082980], 
                     [11259419]|.  Sequence similarity suggests it may function 
                     as a sodium ion/calcium ion exchanger. However direct 
                     measurement of cytosolic calcium levels using the 
                     Ca<sup>2+</sup> activated photoprotein, aequorin, suggests 
                     that it does not play a role in regulating cytosolic 
                     Ca<sup>2+</sup> |CITS: [18342619]|.
                     YrbG is predicted to be an inner membrane protein; sequence
                     alignment and experimental topology analysis suggest that 
                     the protein has a two-domain structure each with five 
                     transmembrane segments and with opposite orientation in the
                     membrane |CITS: [11259419]|. <i>yrbG</i> is not essential 
                     for growth |CITS: [16765569]|."
