     gene            3336195..3336770
                     /gene="lptC"
                     /locus_tag="b3199"
                     /label=lptC
     CDS             3336195..3336770
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="lptC"
                     /locus_tag="b3199"
                     /product="bifunctional lipopolysaccharide transport system
                     protein LptC / lipopolysaccharide transport system"
                     /EC_number="7.5.2.5"
                     /label=lptC
                     /note="LptC is a component of the Lpt lipopolysaccharide
                     (LPS) transport system in <i>E. coli</i> K-12.
                     <i>lptC</i> is essential for growth |CITS: 
                     [16738554][16765569]|. Depletion of <i>lptC</i> leads to 
                     growth arrest and irreversible cell damage; sensitivity to 
                     SDS and bile salts indicates a defective outer membrane 
                     |CITS: [16765569]|. LptC contains a single N-terminal 
                     membrane spanning domain and a large soluble periplasmic 
                     domain |CITS: [17056748][20720015]|. LptC forms a complex 
                     with LptF, LptG and LptB |CITS: [19500581]|; LptC interacts
                     with LptA |CITS: [21169485][22668317]|. LptC lacking the 
                     transmembrane (TM) region is functional and can bind the 
                     LptBFG inner membrane complex |CITS: [23292770]|. LptC 
                     binds rough and smooth LPS <i>in vitro</i> |CITS: 
                     [20720015]| (see also |CITS: [23138981][29024084]|). LptA 
                     can displace LPS from the purified periplasmic domain of 
                     LptC <i>in vitro</i> but not vice versa |CITS: [20720015]|.
                     The soluble domain of LptC is a dimer <i>in vitro</i> 
                     |CITS: [21169485][29024084]|.
                     LptC inhibits the ATPase activity of LptB<sub>2</sub>FG 
                     complexes <i>in vitro</i> |CITS: [30894744]|. In the 
                     cryo-EM structure of LptB<sub>2</sub>FGC, the N-terminal 
                     helix of LptC lies within the LPS binding cavity (formed by
                     TMs 1, 2 and 5 of LptF and LptG) and this positioning may 
                     explain the observed inhibition of LptB<sub>2</sub>FG 
                     ATPase activity; LptC is implicated in regulating 
                     LptB<sub>2</sub>FG mediated extraction of LPS |CITS: 
                     [30894744]| (see also |CITS: 
                     [35678757][38131105][38645307][40260908]|."
