     gene            3336739..3337296
                     /gene="lptA"
                     /locus_tag="b3200"
                     /label=lptA
     CDS             3336739..3337296
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="lptA"
                     /locus_tag="b3200"
                     /product="bifunctional lipopolysaccharide transport system
                     protein LptA / lipopolysaccharide transport system"
                     /EC_number="7.5.2.5"
                     /label=lptA
                     /note="LptA is an essential periplasmic component of the
                     Lpt lipopolysaccharide (LPS) transport system.
                     Depletion of LptA results in impaired lipopolysaccharide 
                     transport to the outer membrane |CITS: [17056748]|; a 
                     conditional mutant which contains inactivating point 
                     mutations in LptA rapidly stops growing when incubated at 
                     the restrictive temperature and newly synthesized LPS 
                     appears trapped on the periplasmic side of the inner 
                     membrane |CITS: [18768814]|. LptA drives a specific, 
                     protein mediated, long lived association between 
                     proteoliposomes containing LptBFGC and LPS and 
                     proteliposomes containing LptDE |CITS: [29449493]|. 
                     Purified LptA binds smooth and rough LPS; purified LptA 
                     binds to the lipid A domain of LPS |CITS: [18480051]|. 
                     Over-expressed His-tagged LptA is found in the soluble 
                     periplasmic fraction of whole cell lysates |CITS: 
                     [17056748]|. Untagged LptA, expressed at native levels 
                     fractionates with the outer membranes whilst His-tagged 
                     LptA fractionates with the inner membranes |CITS: 
                     [20446753]|. LptA interacts with LptC but does not interact
                     with LptE |CITS: [21195693]|. Purified LptA forms 
                     end-to-end arranged, concentration dependent, oligomers 
                     |CITS: [22109962]| (see also |CITS: [23897621]|)
                     Crystal structures of LptA in the presence and absence of 
                     LPS have been determined to 2.15 &Aring; and 3.25 &Aring; 
                     resolution, respectively. The LptA structure showed a novel
                     protein fold consisting of 16 consecutive anti-parallel 
                     &beta;-strands with resemblance to a &beta;-jellyroll. The 
                     structure of LptA crystallized in the presence of LPS 
                     consists of two sets of four LptA molecules, with monomers 
                     stacked in a head-to-tail fashion |CITS: [18534617]|. LPS 
                     binds on the inside of the &beta;-jellyroll of LptA |CITS: 
                     [23138981]|.
                     LptA is unusually tolerant to alanine scanning mutagenesis 
                     |CITS: [37417889]|.
                     LptA is implicated in a trafficking pathway for surface 
                     exposed lipoproteins; LptA may mediate transfer of |FRAME: 
                     MONOMER0-2693 LptM| from |FRAME: ABC-62-CPLX LolCDE| to 
                     |FRAME: CPLX0-7628 LptDE| |CITS: [40348743]|."
