                     /label=hpf
     CDS             3339532..3339819
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="hpf"
                     /locus_tag="b3203"
                     /product="ribosome hibernation-promoting factor"
                     /label=hpf
                     /note="The hibernation factors HPF, |FRAME:
                     EG50004-MONOMER RMF| and |FRAME: EG11151-MONOMER RaiA| 
                     protect ribosomes, likely by protecting ribonuclease target
                     sites within the ribosome |CITS: [33503254]|.  HPF binds to
                     100S ribosome dimers at stationary phase |CITS: 
                     [11168583]|.  RMF alone promotes dimerization of 70S 
                     ribosomes to 90S ribosome particles; binding of HPF then 
                     promotes formation of stable 100S ribosome dimers |CITS: 
                     [18174192][19170772]|.
                     In cyro-EM structures of the hibernating ribosome, HPF 
                     interacts with the anticodon stem-loop of deacylated tRNA 
                     in the E site and masks the binding site for mRNA as well 
                     as A- and P-site tRNAs |CITS: [30177741]|.  Earlier work 
                     using <i>Thermus thermophilus</i> ribosomes also showed 
                     that both HPF and RaiA bind in the channel between the head
                     and body of the 30S ribosomal subunit, apparently blocking 
                     the sites for tRNA and mRNA binding during protein 
                     synthesis.  The binding site also overlaps with the binding
                     sites for IF1 and IF3 as well as EF-G, which are all 
                     involved in dissociation of the ribosomal subunits |CITS: 
                     [22605777]|.  An NMR solution structure of HPF alone is 
                     also available |CITS: [19747895]|.
                     Binding of HPF to the ribosome inhibits translation in some
                     <i>in vitro</i> assays |CITS: [18174192]|.
                     Expression of <i>hpf</i> is induced by the autoinducer 2 
                     (AI-2) quorum sensing pheromone |CITS: [11514505]|. 
                     Expression increases at the onset of stationary phase 
                     |CITS: [33503254]|.
                     A &Delta;<i>hpf</i> mutant shows reduced persister cell 
                     formation and increased persister cell resuscitation |CITS:
                     [32007277]|.  In a <i>hpf raiA</i> double deletion mutant, 
                     only 90S ribosome particles are found in stationary phase 
                     |CITS: [16324148]|.  A &Delta;<i>rmf hpf raiA</i> mutant is
                     defective in regrowth from starvation; mutants accumulate 
                     increased amounts of fragmented rRNA |CITS: [33503254]|.
                     Hpf: ""<b>h</b>ibernation <b>p</b>romoting <b>f</b>actor"" 
                     |CITS: [16324148]|
                     Reviews: |CITS: [15884656][26443727][24944100][30476446][3 
                     1230411][31867037]|"
