     gene            3341325..3341597
                     /gene="npr"
                     /locus_tag="b3206"
                     /label=npr
     CDS             3341325..3341597
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="npr"
                     /locus_tag="b3206"
                     /product="phosphorelay protein NPr"
                     /label=npr
                     /note="NPr is the second phosphotransfer protein of the
                     nitrogen phosphoenolpyruvate (PEP)-dependent 
                     phosphotransferase system (PTS<sup>Ntr</sup>) in <i>E. 
                     coli</i> K-12. The exact function of the PTS<sup>Ntr</sup> 
                     is not clear - it has been implicated in the regulation of 
                     nitrogen metabolism |CITS: [23517463]| and in potassium 
                     homeostasis (reviewed in |CITS: [20202847]| but see also 
                     |CITS: [21742895]|).
                     |FRAME: EG12188-MONOMER ""PtsP""|, also known as enzyme 
                     I<sup>Ntr</sup>, phosphorylates NPr <i>in vitro</i>. This 
                     reaction occurs at an optimum pH of 8.0, is dependent on 
                     Mg<sup>2+</sup>, is stimulated by high ionic strength, and 
                     has two Km values for Npr of 2 and 10 &mu;M |CITS: 
                     [10473571]|. Purified Npr is active as a phosphoryl 
                     acceptor from EI<sup>Ntr</sup> and is capable of 
                     phosphotransfer to |FRAME: EG11682-MONOMER ""PtsN""| (also 
                     known as EIIA<sup>Ntr</sup>); a solution structure of Npr 
                     has been obtained |CITS: [18421563]|. PtsP and NPr 
                     contribute to the phosphorylation of PtsN <i>in vivo</i>, 
                     but in the absence of these two phosphotransfer proteins 
                     PtsI and HPr of the canonical PTS<sup>sugar</sup> can 
                     substitute. The absence of all four of these 
                     phosphotransfer proteins results in extremely limited 
                     phosphorylation of EIIA<sup>Ntr</sup> |CITS: [18625021]|. 
                     |FRAME: G7211-MONOMER| dephosphorylates phospho-NPr <i>in 
                     vitro</i>; phospho-NPr dephosphorylation proceeds via a 
                     transient SixA phosphohistidine intermediate; NPr-SixA 
                     interaction (in the <i>E. coli</i> commensal isolate MP1) 
                     is important for colonization of the mouse intestinal tract
                     |CITS: [30482831][33199374]|.
                     Efficient transfer of phosphate to Npr, from a number of 
                     enzyme IIAs of the PTS<sup>sugar</sup> system and from 
                     EIIA<sup>Ntr</sup> can be observed <i>in vitro</i> |CITS: 
                     [7876255]|.
                     <i>npr</i> forms part of the sigma54 operon in <i>E. 
                     coli</i> K-12 |CITS: [7876255]|.
                     <i>npr</i> mutants have been show through phenotype 
                     microarray analysis to be more resistant than wild-type to 
                     leucine-containing peptides |CITS:[16164569]|."
