     gene            complement(3364443..3365933)
                     /gene="nanT"
                     /locus_tag="b3224"
                     /label=nanT
     CDS             complement(3364443..3365933)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="nanT"
                     /locus_tag="b3224"
                     /product="N-acetylneuraminate:H(+) symporter"
                     /label=nanT
                     /note="<i>E. coli K-12</i> is able to use the common
                     sialic acid, N-acetylneuramic acid, as a carbon source and 
                     possesses a transporter, NanT, with high specificity for 
                     this sugar acid |CITS: [3902799][7592358]|. NanT recognizes
                     the abundant &beta;-anomer of  N-acetylneuramic acid; 
                     expression of a periplasmic |FRAME: CPLX0-7658| supports 
                     the ability to use the less abundant &alpha;-anomer <i>in 
                     vivo</i> |CITS: [18063573]|.
                     Purified NanT, reconstituted into liposomes, mediates the 
                     uptake of labeled <i>N</i>-acetylneuraminate <i>in 
                     vitro</i> and transport is energised by the proton gradient
                     alone |CITS: [22167185]|. NanT facilitates both substrate 
                     counterflow and substrate exchange <i>in vitro</i> |CITS: 
                     [22167185]| (see also |CITS: [19179287]|). NanT transports 
                     the related sialic acids, |FRAME: CPD-273| and |FRAME: 
                     CPD-21259 ""3-deoxy-D-glycero-D-galactonononate""| (KDN) 
                     |CITS: [23848303]| and the anhydro-sialic acid |FRAME: 
                     CPD-23638| |CITS: [38488830]|. NanT transports exogenous 
                     3-deoxy-D-<i>manno</i>-oct-2-ulosonic acid (Kdo) and its 
                     experimentally useful azido analog, 
                     8-azido-3,8-dideoxy-D-<i>manno</i>-oct-2-ulosonic acid 
                     (Kdo-N3) |CITS: [30076772]|.
                     Expression of <I>nanT</I> is induced by sialic acid |CITS: 
                     [3902799]|; <i>nanT</i> is a member of the |FRAME: 
                     G7678-MONOMER NanR| 'sialoregulon' |CITS: 
                     [12897000][23935044][33790291]|.
                     NanT is an archetypal member of the bacterial sialic acid 
                     transporter 1 (ST1) family |CITS: [34184979]|.
                     <i>nan</i>: <u><i>N</i>-a</u>cyl<u>n</u>euraminate |CITS: 
                     [3902799]|
                     Related reviews: |CITS: [27284039][29222808]|"
