     CDS             3368228..3369595
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="dcuD"
                     /locus_tag="b3227"
                     /product="putative transporter DcuD"
                     /label=dcuD
                     /note="In the Transporter Classification Database, DcuD is
                     a member of the C<sub>4</sub>-dicarboxylate Uptake C (DcuC)
                     family |CITS: [26546518]|.
                     DcuD has high sequence similarity to the anaerobic 
                     C<sub>4</sub>-dicarboxylate transporter, DcuC |CITS: 
                     [8955408]|.
                     DcuD is not essential for C<sub>4</sub>-dicarboxylate 
                     transport during aerobic or anaerobic growth and a 
                     <i>dcuD</i> null mutant strain shows no significant growth 
                     impairment when tested with a large number of substrates; 
                     expression of <i>dcuD</i> is very low or absent under most 
                     conditions |CITS: [10525738]| (see also |CITS: 
                     [11511871]|). DcuD may be active during glycerol 
                     fermentation |CITS: [30862913]|; DcuD is implicated in the 
                     generation of PMF during glucose fermentation at pH7.5 
                     |CITS: [34118553]|"
