     gene            complement(3371174..3371566)
                     /gene="rpsI"
                     /locus_tag="b3230"
                     /label=rpsI
     CDS             complement(3371174..3371566)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rpsI"
                     /locus_tag="b3230"
                     /product="trifunctional 30S ribosomal subunit protein S9 /
                     30S ribosomal subunit / ribosome"
                     /label=rpsI
                     /note="The S9 protein is a component of the 30S subunit of
                     the ribosome.
                     S9 was shown to crosslink to domains 3 and 4 of 16S rRNA 
                     |CITS: [2423965][2429836]| and increases protection against
                     ribunuclease digestion of the hairpin loop 41 near the 3' 
                     terminus of 16S rRNA by a mixture containing S7, S14, and 
                     S19 |CITS: [2438658]|.  The effect of S9 may be dependent 
                     on the presence of S14 |CITS: [3279390]|.  S7 is required 
                     for and accelerates binding of S9 to the 16S rRNA |CITS: 
                     [20207951]|.  S9 crosslinks to tRNA at the P site of the 
                     ribosome and weakly to tRNA at the A site |CITS: 
                     [8524654]|.  The assembly cofactors Era, RimM and RimP 
                     accelerate the binding rate of S9 during 30S assembly 
                     |CITS: [20188109]|.
                     Structural modelling suggested that the C-terminal region 
                     of S9 interacts with the P-site tRNA.  Studies with 
                     <i>rpsI</i> mutants lacking this region show that the 
                     C-terminal tail is not essential for the function of S9, 
                     but such mutants have slower growth rates.  <i>In 
                     vitro</i>, deletion of the C-terminal tail of S9 affects 
                     binding of tRNAs with anticodon stem sequences that are 
                     most divergent from initiator tRNAs |CITS: [15308780]|. 
                     Deletion of three C terminal amino acids of S9 results in 
                     altered translation initiation from various codons |CITS: 
                     [23530111]|.
                     S9 is one of the subunits required for the 
                     ribosome-dependent GTPase activity of EF-G |CITS: 
                     [4346030]|.  A decreased amount of S9 in the cell may cause
                     a defect in ribosome maturation |CITS: [15126466]|. |FRAME:
                     EG10975-MONOMER SrmB| positively regulates expression of 
                     L13 and S9 by preventing premature transcription 
                     termination; thus, the role of SrmB in ribosome assembly 
                     may be to ensure the synthesis of adequate levels of L13 
                     and S9 |CITS: [31188443]|.
                     SHAPE probing showed that the 5' UTR of the 
                     <i>rplM-rpsI</i> mRNA folds into five hairpin helices; 
                     |FRAME: EG10874-MONOMER L13| binds to mRNA containing the 
                     entire region and is predicted to inhibit translation by 
                     stabilizing helix 4, which occludes the <i>rplM</i> 
                     ribosome binding site.  <i>rpsI</i> is structurally linked 
                     to <i>rplM</i>, suggesting a mechanism for coregulation of 
                     the two genes |CITS: [29551268]|.
                     An <i>rpsI</i> null mutant is viable, but has a slow growth
                     phenotype |CITS: [17277072][21945294]|."
