     gene            complement(3371582..3372010)
                     /gene="rplM"
                     /locus_tag="b3231"
                     /label=rplM
     CDS             complement(3371582..3372010)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rplM"
                     /locus_tag="b3231"
                     /product="trifunctional 50S ribosomal subunit protein L13
                     / 50S ribosomal subunit / ribosome"
                     /label=rplM
                     /note="The L13 protein is an early assembly component of
                     the 50S subunit of the ribosome |CITS: [3541786]|.
                     The RNA helicase |FRAME: EG10975-MONOMER SrmB| was 
                     initially proposed to be necessary for the assembly of L13 
                     into the ribosome |CITS: [12787353]|.  However, it was 
                     recently shown that SrmB positively regulates expression of
                     L13 and S9 by preventing premature transcription 
                     termination; thus, the role of SrmB in ribosome assembly 
                     may be to ensure the synthesis of adequate levels of L13 
                     and S9 |CITS: [31188443]|.
                     L13 interacts with 23S rRNA |CITS: 
                     [800986][823048][6163479][1702198][8308887]| and crosslinks
                     to it in both free ribosomes and the initiation complex 
                     |CITS: [2495985]|.  L13 is located within 21 &Aring; of 
                     nucleotide C2475 of 23S rRNA, near the peptidyltransferase 
                     center |CITS: [7529559]|.  L13 binds to 5S rRNA |CITS: 
                     [3301408]| and can be crosslinked to L2 |CITS: [813873]|, 
                     L3 |CITS: [2665813]|, L20 |CITS: 
                     [813873][2653827][2665813]| and L21 |CITS: 
                     [3314578][2645289][2665813]|.  L13 interacts with tRNA in 
                     the P site |CITS: [2660905]|.
                     |FRAME: EG50004-MONOMER Ribosome modulation factor| binds 
                     near L2, L13, and S13 |CITS: [12473202]|.  A puromycin 
                     analog |CITS: [354931]|, a tobramycin analog |CITS: 
                     [6341055]|, and a pactamycin analog |CITS: [3899171]| can 
                     be crosslinked to L13.
                     L13 has RNA chaperone-like activity in an <i>in vitro 
                     trans</i> splicing assay |CITS: [15525706]| and binds zinc 
                     |CITS: [11985624]|.  L13 was found to be phosphorylated 
                     |CITS: [19469554]|.
                     L13 inhibits translation of its own mRNA |CITS: 
                     [27381917]|.  SHAPE probing showed that the 5' UTR of the 
                     <i>rplM-rpsI</i> mRNA folds into five hairpin helices; L13 
                     binds to mRNA containing the entire region and is predicted
                     to inhibit translation by stabilizing helix 4, which 
                     occludes the <i>rplM</i> ribosome binding site. <i>rpsI</i>
                     is structurally linked to <i>rplM</i>, suggesting a 
                     mechanism for coregulation of the two genes |CITS: 
                     [29551268]|."
