                     /locus_tag="b3258"
                     /product="pantothenate:Na(+) symporter"
                     /label=panF
                     /note="PanF is a pantothenate transporter which probably 
                     functions as a pantothenate/cation symporter. Whole cell 
                     transport assays have shown that the cloned <I>panF</I> 
                     gene can complement <I>panF</I> mutants with pantothenate 
                     transport defects |CITS: [2193919]|. Overexpression of 
                     <I>panF</I> lead to increased pantothenate accumulation. 
                     Whole cell transport experiments have shown that PanF 
                     mediates high affinity pantothenate transport with a Km of 
                     approx 0.4 &mu;M and pantothenate uptake was stimulated by 
                     the presence of sodium ions |CITS: [3888959]|. PanF is a 
                     member of the
                     SSS family of sodium/solute symporters, supporting the 
                     notion that it functions as a sodium/pantothenate symporter
                     |CITS: [8031825]|. Imported pantothenate is phosphorylated 
                     by pantothenate kinase, a key step in Coenzyme A 
                     synthesis."
