                     /product="ribosomal protein L11 methyltransferase"
                     /label=prmA
                     /note="PrmA is the methyltransferase responsible for the 
                     multiple methylation of |FRAME: EG10872-MONOMER|.  Free L11
                     is a better substrate than assembled 50S ribosomal subunits
                     |CITS: [241395]|.
                     <i>prmA</i> mutants are deficient in the methylation of 
                     ribosomal protein L11 |CITS: [331082][7715456]|.  A strain 
                     containing a <i>prmA</i> null mutation is viable and shows 
                     no growth defect, indicating that lack of methylation of 
                     L11 does not affect its function in the ribosome |CITS: 
                     [7715456]|.
                     PrmA: ""<b>pr</b>otein <b>m</b>ethylation <b>A</b>"" |CITS:
