     CDS             3408392..3411496
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="acrF"
                     /locus_tag="b3266"
                     /product="bifunctional multidrug efflux pump RND permease
                     AcrF / multidrug efflux pump AcrEF-TolC"
                     /label=acrF
                     /note="AcrF shares 77% amino acid sequence identity with
                     |FRAME: ACRB-MONOMER ""AcrB""| of the AcrAB multidrug 
                     efflux system |CITS:[1720861], [8407802]|. <i>acrEF</i> is 
                     not expressed at significant levels in wild-type K-12 
                     strains (see |CITS: [7889326][8830678]|) but is expressed 
                     upon integration of IS<i>1</i> or IS<i>2</i> into the 
                     upstream region of the operon |CITS: [11274125]| or upon 
                     deletion of the |FRAME: PD00288 ""H-NS repressor protein""|
                     |CITS: [14973023]|; when expressed AcrF functions in 
                     <i>Escherichia coli</i> as part of a drug efflux system 
                     with the AcrE membrane fusion protein and the TolC outer 
                     membrane protein |CITS: [11274125]| (see |FRAME: 
                     CPLX0-2141| for more details).
                     <i>acrF</i> is one of 35 efflux-encoding genes that have 
                     been deleted or inactivated in 'Efflux KnockOut-35' 
                     (EKO-35) -  a K-12 BW25133-derived strain that lacks 35 
                     efflux pumps and can be used as a platform to study their 
                     function |CITS: [36065018][36318669]|. The <i>acrF</i> Keio
                     collection mutant (BW25113 &Delta;<i>acrF::kan</i>) shows a
                     significant increase in swimming motility |CITS: 
                     [39529380]|."
