     CDS             3422595..3423149
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yrdA"
                     /locus_tag="b3279"
                     /product="hexapeptide repeats-containing protein YrdA"
                     /label=yrdA
                     /note="YrdA belongs to the &gamma; class of carbonic
                     anhydrases (&gamma;-CA).  During cloning, a point mutation,
                     Arg6His, and a C-terminal His tail were introduced; when 
                     purified, this protein only has little detectable carbonic 
                     anhydrase activity |CITS: [22868757]|. An N-terminally 
                     His-tagged recombinant &gamma;-CA based on accession 
                     WP_009008373.1, which contains an additional 72 N-terminal 
                     amino acids and is identical to YrdA in its C-terminal 184 
                     amino acids, is able to catalyze hydration of 
                     CO<sub>2</sub> with a k<sub>cat</sub> of 5.7 x 
                     10<sup>5</sup> s<sup>-1</sup> |CITS: [32746656]|.
                     Crystal structures of YrdA have been solved; the protein 
                     forms a homotrimer in the crystal |CITS: [22868757]|.
                     The expression of YrdA protein is induced by the addition 
                     of spermine to the growth media at pH 8.5 |CITS: 
                     [16223443]|.
                     Using a method that distinguishes N-phosphorylation from 
                     O-phosphorylation, N-phosphorylation was detected <i>in 
                     vitro</i> |CITS: [35636362]|.
                     The Keio collection <i>yrdA</i> mutant exhibits a 'low 
                     level' of resistance to lithium exposure |CITS: 
                     [39983623]|."
