                     /product="protein Smf"
                     /label=smf
                     /note="The <i>smf</i> gene can partially complement the 
                     transformation defect of a <i>Haemophilus influenzae 
                     dprA</i> mutant.  However, in <i>E. coli</i>, <i>smf</i> 
                     does not appear to have a role in transformation, 
                     conjugation, DNA repair, or recombination |CITS: 
                     [16978360]|.  <i>smf</i> is not required for spontaneous 
                     plasmid transformation on nutrient plates with high agar 
                     concentration |CITS: [19011021]|.
                     <i>smf</i>: inverse of <i>fms</i> |CITS: [8432722]|"
