                     /label=rsmB
     CDS             3428566..3429855
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rsmB"
                     /locus_tag="b3289"
                     /product="16S rRNA m(5)C967 methyltransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.1.1.176"
                     /label=rsmB
                     /note="RsmB is the methyltransferase responsible for
                     methylation of 16S rRNA at the C967 nucleotide |CITS: 
                     [10026269][10194318]|.  <i>In vitro</i>, the enzyme is 
                     active on free 16S rRNA, but not 30S ribosomal subunits 
                     |CITS: [2662188][10026269][10194318]|.  Methylation of G966
                     and C967 in 16S rRNA appears to stabilize the binding of 
                     initiator tRNA to the 30S pre-initiation complex prior to 
                     recognition of the start codon, thus modulating the early 
                     stages of translation initiation |CITS: [22649054]|. The 
                     crystal structure of the apoenzyme has been solved at 1.65 
                     &Aring; resolution, and that of the enzyme complexed with 
                     AdoMet at 2.1 &Aring; resolution |CITS: [14656444]|. A null
                     mutation in <i>rsmB</i> has no significant effect on the 
                     growth rate in rich or minimal media |CITS: [10194318]|, 
                     although competitive growth experiments reveal a fitness 
                     defect |CITS: [22649054]|.  Deletion of <i>rsmB</i> alters 
                     the initiation frequency from certain translation 
                     initiation codons |CITS: [23530111]|.  A C375A mutant is 
                     catalytically inactive, while a C325A mutant retains 
                     activity |CITS: [10899996]|.
                     RsmB: ""<b>r</b>RNA <b>s</b>mall subunit 
                     <b>m</b>ethyltransferase <b>B</b>""
                     Review: |CITS: [20007150]|
                     "
