     gene            complement(3433399..3434388)
                     /gene="rpoA"
                     /locus_tag="b3295"
                     /label=rpoA
     CDS             complement(3433399..3434388)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rpoA"
                     /locus_tag="b3295"
                     /product="multifunctional RNA polymerase subunit alpha /
                     RNA polymerase, core enzyme / RNA polymerase / RNA 
                     polymerase sigma 24 / RNA polymerase sigma 19 / RNA 
                     polymerase sigma 28 / RNA polymerase sigma S / RNA 
                     polymerase sigma 32 / RNA polymerase sigma 54 / RNA 
                     polymerase sigma 70"
                     /EC_number="2.7.7.6"
                     /label=rpoA
                     /note="RpoA is the &alpha; subunit of the RNA polymerase
                     core enzyme. It consists of two domains connected by a 
                     flexible linker.
                     The RpoA amino-terminus is both necessary and sufficient 
                     for dimerization of RpoA and subsequent assembly of the RNA
                     polymerase core complex |CITS: [9657722]|. The 
                     amino-terminus has been analyzed both by NMR and via a 2.5 
                     &Aring; resolution crystal structure |CITS: 
                     [10920271][9657722]|. Protein-Protein Interaction (PPI) 
                     networks have been examined with algebraic topology 
                     analysis showing that most interacting proteins with RpoA 
                     are related to the protein translation |CITS: [35560988]|. 
                     The amino-terminal and carboxy-terminal domains of RpoA are
                     connected by a flexible linker, which has been shown to 
                     affect transcription in a promoter-dependent fashion |CITS:
                     [9135123][10821700][10747024]|.
                     The carboxy-terminal domain of RpoA is involved in 
                     antitermination, rho-dependent termination, and is a target
                     for interactions with |FRAME: EG10665-MONOMER| that control
                     termination and pausing |CITS: [8878045][9878357]|. 
                     Interaction with the RpoA carboxy-terminal domain activates
                     RNA binding by |FRAME: EG10665-MONOMER| |CITS: [11040219]|.
                     The RpoA carboxy-terminal domain is also required for some 
                     kinds of transcriptional activation and plays a role in 
                     some transcriptional initiation |CITS: 
                     [9112442][10198440]|. RpoA accumulates recurrent mutations 
                     under glucose limitation, notably clustered at residue 
                     Pro322, affecting its interaction with OmpR and altering 
                     transcription of porin genes |CITS:[40830465]|."
