     gene            complement(3435068..3435457)
                     /gene="rpsK"
                     /locus_tag="b3297"
                     /label=rpsK
     CDS             complement(3435068..3435457)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rpsK"
                     /locus_tag="b3297"
                     /product="trifunctional 30S ribosomal subunit protein S11
                     / 30S ribosomal subunit / ribosome"
                     /label=rpsK
                     /note="The S11 protein is a component of the 30S subunit
                     of the ribosome.
                     S11 is a component of the ribosomal P site |CITS: 
                     [2459389]| and crosslinks to the D loop and anticodon loop 
                     of tRNA |CITS: [386278][2660905][8440251][9292501]|.  S11 
                     was also shown to crosslink to IF2 |CITS: [805140]| and IF3
                     |CITS: [7000779][7020604][6755396][6349681]|.
                     However, IF3 can interact with ribosomes lacking S11 |CITS:
                     [764867]|.  Footprinting of IF3 on 16S rRNA and modelling 
                     of IF3-30S subunit interactions suggested that IF3 is 
                     located near S7 and S11 |CITS: [11684020]|.
                     S11 binds to or can be crosslinked to 16S rRNA |CITS: 
                     [331074][2437527][2437528][3311162][2505863]|; S11, S6, and
                     S18 interact cooperatively with two loop regions of 16S 
                     rRNA |CITS: [2459389]|.  S11 crosslinks to S21 |CITS: 
                     [6351913]|.  S11 and S7 physically and functionally 
                     interact; disruption of this interaction by mutagenesis 
                     results in error-prone translation |CITS: [12937172]|.
                     S11 interacts with the endoribonuclease YbeY |CITS: 
                     [27834201]|.
                     S11 is methylated at the amino terminal alanine residue 
                     |CITS: [337304][7007074][10094780]| and contains 
                     isoaspartate |CITS: [10217780]|.  S11 was also found to be 
                     Ser/Thr-phosphorylated |CITS: [19469554]|.
                     <i>rpsK</i> is encoded within the so-called &alpha; operon;
                     its expression is regulated at the translational level by 
                     the S4 ribosomal subunit |CITS: [3309351]|. Review: |CITS: 
                     [22649682]|
                     "
