     gene            complement(3435977..3436093)
                     /gene="rpmJ"
                     /locus_tag="b3299"
                     /label=rpmJ
     CDS             complement(3435977..3436093)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rpmJ"
                     /locus_tag="b3299"
                     /product="trifunctional 50S ribosomal subunit protein L36
                     / 50S ribosomal subunit / ribosome"
                     /label=rpmJ
                     /note="The L36 protein is a component of the 50S subunit
                     of the ribosome |CITS: [3298224]|. L36 is highly conserved 
                     in bacteria, mitochondria and chloroplasts, but not present
                     in archaea and eukarya |CITS: [16246363]|. Ribosomes 
                     lacking L36 are correctly assembled. However, chemical 
                     protection experiments suggest that rRNA tertiary 
                     interactions are disrupted in ribosomes lacking L36, thus 
                     arguing that L36 plays a significant role in organizing 23S
                     rRNA structure |CITS: [16246363]|. 2'-<i>O</i>-methylation 
                     of U2552 by |FRAME: EG11507-MONOMER| promotes association 
                     between helices 92 and 71 of 23S rRNA; together with 
                     incorporation of L36, it promotes late steps of 50S 
                     ribosomal subunit assembly |CITS: [26261349]|. Profiles of 
                     ribosomes isolated from a &Delta;<i>rpmJ</i> mutant show a 
                     minor peak at 40S that lacks the late assembly proteins L16
                     and L35 |CITS: [32559334]|. Ribosomes isolated from a 
                     &Delta;|FRAME: EG11507 <i>rlmE</i>| strain lack L16, L35 
                     and L36 |CITS: [32571953]|.
                     L36 has been shown to crosslink to 23S rRNA |CITS: 
                     [7556101]|.
                     Deletion of <i>rpmJ</i> causes a temperature-sensitive 
                     growth defect |CITS: [16116291][16246363][32559334]| and 
                     increased sensitivity to hydroxyurea |CITS: [23292777]|. 
                     <i>rpmJ</i> deletion led to decreased expression of 
                     <i>secY</i>, located immediately upstream of <i>rpmJ</i>. 
                     <i>rpmJ</i> does not appear to be essential for protein 
                     synthesis |CITS: [16116291]|. A &Delta;<i>rlmE</i> 
                     &Delta;<i>rpmJ</i> double mutant exhibits a severe 
                     synthetic growth defect at 37&deg;C and is unable to grow 
                     at 30 or 22&deg;C |CITS: [26261349]|. The Keio collection 
                     <i>rpmJ</i> mutant is sensitive to lithium (<90% growth at 
                     200mM Li) |CITS: [39983623]|.
                     |FRAME: MONOMER0-2656 YkgO| is a paralog of L36 |CITS: 
                     [19121005]|; it is the prevalent paralog present in 
                     stationary phase ribosomes |CITS: [30359641]|."
