                     /product="trifunctional 50S ribosomal subunit protein L15
                     / 50S ribosomal subunit / ribosome"
                     /label=rplO
                     /note="The L15 protein is a component of the 50S subunit
                     of the ribosome.
                     L15 is a late assembly protein |CITS: [2204629]| that 
                     appears to be required for 5S rRNA incorporation
                     |CITS: [7038683]|.  L15 interacts with domain II of 23S 
                     rRNA in a partially assembled ribosomal particle
                     |CITS: [321250][9878356]|.  L15 appears to be dispensible 
                     for protein synthesis and cell growth |CITS: [6389119]|, 
                     and ribosomes lacking L15 are translationally active |CITS:
                     [2204629]|.
                     L15 is a component of the binding site for erythromycin on 
                     the ribosome |CITS: [3275651]|.
                     L15 has RNA chaperone-like activity in an <i>in vitro 
                     trans</i> splicing assay |CITS: [15525706]|."
