     gene            complement(3438603..3438956)
                     /gene="rplR"
                     /locus_tag="b3304"
                     /label=rplR
     CDS             complement(3438603..3438956)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rplR"
                     /locus_tag="b3304"
                     /product="trifunctional 50S ribosomal subunit protein L18
                     / 50S ribosomal subunit / ribosome"
                     /label=rplR
                     /note="The L18 protein is a component of the 50S subunit
                     of the ribosome and is required for incorporation of 5S 
                     rRNA into the ribosome |CITS: [7038683]|.
                     L18 interacts with both 23S rRNA |CITS: [1702198]| and 5S 
                     rRNA |CITS: [6364140][353728][354687][7015289]|.  L18 
                     together with L5 can associate into a quaternary complex 
                     with 5S and 23S rRNAs |CITS: [109811]|.  The binding 
                     determinants of the 5S rRNA-L5-L18-L25 complex have been 
                     mapped |CITS: [7038676][6159586][6278442] 
                     [6354252][2990903][2429677][3060848][2472486][2479908][154 
                     1273][8925931][9813114]|. Both L5 and L18 are essential for
                     viability |CITS: [17198710]|.  Iodination at a tyrosine 
                     residue abolishes binding of L18 to 5S rRNA |CITS: 
                     [7011398]|.
                     L18 is posttranslationally modified by phosphorylation, 
                     most likely at the Ser45 residue |CITS: [19469554]|.
                     L18 has RNA chaperone-like activity in an <i>in vitro 
                     trans</i> splicing assay |CITS: [15525706]| as well as 
                     <i>in vitro</i> protein chaperone activity |CITS: 
                     [19071121]|.
                     L18 is photoaffinity labeled by puromycin, an analog of the
                     3' end of aminoacylated tRNA |CITS: [8034577]|.  L18 can 
                     also be crosslinked to the spiramycin derivative 
                     dihydrospiramycin and may thus be located near the peptidyl
                     transferase center |CITS: [7559446]|."
