                     /gene="rpsN"
                     /locus_tag="b3307"
                     /product="trifunctional 30S ribosomal subunit protein S14
                     / 30S ribosomal subunit / ribosome"
                     /label=rpsN
                     /note="The S14 protein is a component of the 30S subunit
                     of the ribosome.
                     S14 has a role in tRNA binding |CITS: 
                     [1107046][2578985][3542041][2660905]|.  S14 is 
                     photoaffinity labeled by streptomycin |CITS: [775293]|, 
                     puromycin, an analog of the 3' end of aminoacylated tRNA 
                     |CITS: [341968][375969][3888269][8034577]|, and 
                     dihydrospiramycin |CITS: [7559446]|.  S14 may be required 
                     for <i>in vitro</i> assembly of the small subunit |CITS: 
                     [3533932]|; it assembles late in the biogenesis of the 30S 
                     subunit |CITS: [10376881][23228329]|.
                     S14 can be crosslinked to S19 |CITS: [4213326][6351913]| 
                     and L7/L12 |CITS: [9430711]|.  A mixture containing S7, 
                     S14, and S19 protects the hairpin loop 41 near the 3' 
                     terminus of 16S rRNA against ribonuclease digestion |CITS: 
                     [2438658]|.  S14 can also be crosslinked to 16S rRNA |CITS:
                     [361396][7002551][6163479][16617474]| and mRNA |CITS: 
                     [1397315]|.  The sites of interaction of S14 with 16S rRNA 
                     have been identified by hydroxyl radical probing |CITS: 
                     [2459390]|.
                     <i>rpsN</i> is part of the <i>spc</i> operon |CITS: 
                     [6182899]|.  An amber mutation in <i>rpsN</i> exerts a 
                     polar effect on the genes distal to the <i>rpsN</i> gene in
                     the <i>spc</i> operon |CITS: [6986365]|.
                     "
