     gene            complement(3440258..3440797)
                     /gene="rplE"
                     /locus_tag="b3308"
                     /label=rplE
     CDS             complement(3440258..3440797)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rplE"
                     /locus_tag="b3308"
                     /product="trifunctional 50S ribosomal subunit protein L5 /
                     50S ribosomal subunit / ribosome"
                     /label=rplE
                     /note="The L5 protein is a component of the 50S subunit of
                     the ribosome.  The crystal structure of the ribosome |CITS:
                     [16272117]|, cryo-EM reconstructions |CITS: [12809609]|, 
                     and crosslinking experiments |CITS: [7031269]| show that 
                     the L5 protein contacts the S13 protein of the small 
                     subunit of the ribosome, forming the only protein-protein 
                     bridge between the subunits.  During the ratchet-like 
                     motion of the ribosome, L5 and S13 reorganize in different 
                     constellations |CITS: [20643101]|. L5, L15 and L18 are 
                     required for 5S RNA incorporation into the 50S subunit of 
                     the ribosome |CITS: [7038683]|, and L5 was shown to be 
                     required for the assembly of the central protuberance of 
                     the 50S subunit |CITS: [22821559]|.
                     L5 binds to 5S rRNA |CITS: [827440][321249][353489][354687 
                     ][365228][6181508][6364140]|. The association of L5 with 5S
                     rRNA is cooperatively stimulated by L18 |CITS: [354687]|, 
                     and the binding regions of the 5S rRNA-L5-L18 complex were 
                     mapped |CITS: [9813114]|.  Both L5 and L18 are essential 
                     for viability |CITS: [17198710]|.  A crystal structure of 
                     the <i>Thermus thermophilus</i> L5 in complex with a 
                     fragment of 5S RNA has been solved |CITS: [12515387]|.  L5 
                     also crosslinks to IF-3 |CITS: [6755396]| and uncharged 
                     tRNA in the P site of the ribosome |CITS: 
                     [2205514][1708125][8524654]|. Molecular dynamics 
                     simulations suggest that L5 facilitates tRNA translocation 
                     |CITS: [24186064]|.
                     L5 is altered in a thiopeptin-resistant mutant |CITS: 
                     [1098662]|.  L4, L5, and L21 bind to erythromycin 
                     cooperatively |CITS: [2256953]|.  Inhibition of the 
                     EF-G-ribosome complex by thiostrepton involves 
                     destabilization of 5S RNA-protein (L5 and L18) interactions
                     |CITS: [12409297]|.
                     Expression of L5 is regulated at the translational level by
                     |FRAME: EG10907-MONOMER S8| |CITS: 
                     [6445562][6262737][3049533][2464692][15146079]|. 
                     Overexpression of <i>rplE</i> suppresses the growth defect 
                     of a |FRAME: G7841 &Delta;<i>rsgA</i>| mutant |CITS: 
                     [18223068]|."
