     gene            complement(3440812..3441126)
                     /gene="rplX"
                     /locus_tag="b3309"
                     /label=rplX
     CDS             complement(3440812..3441126)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rplX"
                     /locus_tag="b3309"
                     /product="trifunctional 50S ribosomal subunit protein L24
                     / 50S ribosomal subunit / ribosome"
                     /label=rplX
                     /note="The L24 protein is a component of the 50S subunit
                     of the ribosome.  L3 and L24 are the two proteins that 
                     initiate assembly of the 50S subunit; L24 is not thought to
                     be involved in ribosomal function |CITS: 
                     [357435][6760192]|.  L24 contacts the M domain finger loop 
                     of the signal recognition particle |CITS: [25775537]|.
                     L24 binds directly to 23S rRNA |CITS: [4577133][4591618][8 
                     00986][788777][404143][386275][2443713][3278299][1702198][8
                     308887][9813114][10781065]|; binding of L24 together with 
                     L4 to 23S rRNA leads to a change in tertiary structure of 
                     the RNA |CITS: [11345438]|.  L4 and L24 cooperatively bind 
                     and stabilize the structure of an rRNA fragment containing 
                     their binding site |CITS: [30705137]|.
                     <i>rplX</i> mutants are temperature sensitive and show a 
                     very slow growth rate |CITS: [6757660][2993250][3308860]|. 
                     The defect is in the assembly of 50S subunits |CITS: 
                     [3526091]|.  Suppressors of certain temperature sensitive 
                     <i>rplX</i> mutations map to 23S rRNA |CITS: [3525151]| or 
                     the Lon protease |CITS: [3287098]|.  SrmB is a high-copy 
                     suppressor of a ts lethal <i>rplX</i> mutation |CITS: 
                     [2461520]| and interacts with L4, L24 and the region of 23S
                     rRNA that interacts with L4 and L24 |CITS: [19734346]|.  
                     Unlike previous work, |CITS: [21945294]| were able to 
                     generate an <i>rplX</i> deletion mutant.
                     L20 can replace L24 for the initiation of assembly of the 
                     50S subunit at permissive temperatures in an L24 mutant 
                     |CITS: [2461735]|.
                     Retroregulation of L24 expression by |FRAME: 
                     EG10907-MONOMER S8| likely occurs via mRNA degradation 
                     |CITS: [2643112]|."
