     gene            complement(3441673..3441927)
                     /gene="rpsQ"
                     /locus_tag="b3311"
                     /label=rpsQ
     CDS             complement(3441673..3441927)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rpsQ"
                     /locus_tag="b3311"
                     /product="trifunctional 30S ribosomal subunit protein S17
                     / 30S ribosomal subunit / ribosome"
                     /label=rpsQ
                     /note="The S17 protein is a component of the 30S subunit
                     of the ribosome |CITS: [344065]|.
                     S17 stabilizes the tertiary structure of the entire 5' 
                     domain of 16S rRNA, including non-native folding 
                     intermediates |CITS: [19616559]|.  An S17-stabilized 
                     non-native folding intermediate appears to be the preferred
                     substrate for |FRAME: EG12044-MONOMER| |CITS: [32486254]|. 
                     S17, S4 and S20 together pre-organize the binding site for 
                     S16 |CITS: [19343072]|.  Molecular dynamics simulations 
                     indicate that binding of S16 rescues the structure of the 
                     helix 17 internal loop that is disrupted by previous 
                     binding of S17 |CITS: [23972210]|. The 30S subunit assembly
                     defect due to depleting S17 was analyzed <i>in vivo</i> 
                     |CITS: [24792169][25884162]|.
                     S17 binds directly to the 5' domain of 16S rRNA |CITS: [45 
                     98121][7002551][7029472][6186486][6354253][3005967][2437528
                     ][3279390][3373529][7916699]|. Specific contact sites have 
                     been identified |CITS: [7556101][9169412][9246617]|.  S17 
                     can also be crosslinked to tRNA in the A site |CITS: 
                     [2578985][2660905]| and to the release factor RF-2 |CITS: 
                     [6802827]|.
                     S17 is encoded as part of the S10 operon |CITS: [3892488]|.
                      The initiating methionine of S17 is cleaved |CITS: 
                     [9868784][10094780]|.
                     A conditionally lethal point mutation in <i>rpsQ</i> leads 
                     to impaired assembly of the 30S ribosomal subunit |CITS: 
                     [108517]|.  Depletion of RpsQ leads to reduced levels of 
                     70S ribosomes and a 30S assembly defect |CITS: [24792169]|.
                      An <i>rpsQ</i> null mutant is viable |CITS: 
                     [17277072][21945294]|, but has a slow growth phenotype 
                     |CITS: [17277072]|.  Strains carrying the <i>neaA301</i> 
                     allele of <i>rpsQ</i> exhibit neamine resistance |CITS: 
                     [765484][781296]| and decreased misreading by the ribosome 
                     <i>in vitro</i> |CITS: [325371][7005621]|.  An evolved 
                     allele of <i>rpsQ</i>, selected for increased ethanol 
                     tolerance, increases ribosome accuracy |CITS: [24927582]|. 
                     NeaA: ""neamine resistance"" |CITS: [765484]|"
