                     /product="trifunctional 50S ribosomal subunit protein L29
                     / 50S ribosomal subunit / ribosome"
                     /label=rpmC
                     /note="The L29 protein is a component of the 50S subunit
                     of the ribosome .
                     L29 interacts with 23S rRNA |CITS: [8722036][7556101]| and 
                     is photoaffinity labeled by puromycin, an analog of the 3' 
                     end of aminoacylated tRNA |CITS: [8034577]|.  L29 
                     crosslinks to Trigger Factor (TF) |CITS: [12226666]| and 
                     contacts
                     the Signal Recognition Particle |CITS: [12756233]|, but is 
                     not required for the association of TF with the ribosome 
                     |CITS: [12226666]|.
                     L29 together with ACP stimulates the binding of 
                     Tn<i>7</i>-encoded TnsD to <i>attTn7</i>, the insertion 
                     site for
                     Tn<i>7</i> in the <i>E. coli</i> chromosome.  L23 also 
                     stimulates Tn<i>7</i> transposition <i>in vitro</i>.  A 
                     mutation
                     in L29 decreases Tn<i>7</i> transposition <i>in vivo</i> 
                     |CITS: [9755182]|."
