                     /gene="rplP"
                     /locus_tag="b3313"
                     /product="trifunctional 50S ribosomal subunit protein L16
                     / 50S ribosomal subunit / ribosome"
                     /label=rplP
                     /note="The L16 protein is a late assembly component of the
                     50S subunit of the ribosome; ribosomes lacking L16 are 
                     translationally active |CITS: [2204629]|.  L2 is required 
                     for assembly of L16 into the 50S subunit |CITS: [2211695]|.
                     L16 interacts with tRNA |CITS: [6352325][6363130][2182127]|
                     and can be crosslinked to aminoacylated tRNA in the A and P
                     site |CITS: [386278][8524654]|.  Conserved residues within 
                     L16 were shown to be involved in the translocation of tRNA 
                     from the A to the P site |CITS: [24186064]|.  L16 is 
                     located within 21 &Aring; of nucleotide C2475 of 23S rRNA, 
                     near the peptidyltransferase center |CITS: [7529559]|.  L16
                     and a histidine residue within the N-terminal domain of L16
                     may be important for the correct conformation of the 
                     peptidyltransferase center |CITS: 
                     [6254759][3549294][3297687]|.  L16 is important for release
                     factor 2-dependent peptidyl-tRNA hydrolysis |CITS: 
                     [6355096]|.  The antibiotics chloramphenicol |CITS: 
                     [4365366][4599619]|, virginiamycin S |CITS: [95947]|, 
                     avilamycin and evernimicin |CITS: [27330110]| interact with
                     L16 within the ribosome.
                     Ribosomes that lack |FRAME: EG10885-MONOMER L25| contain an
                     inactive fraction of dissociated subunits in which the 50S 
                     subunit also lacks L16.  Mutations in the C-terminal tail 
                     of L16 affect its retention in the ribosome |CITS: 
                     [26885579]|.  Pre-50S ribosomal subunits isolated from a 
                     &Delta;<i>rlmE</i> strain lack L16, L35 and L36 |CITS: 
                     [32571953]|.
                     L16 is one of six ribosomal proteins that is completely 
                     lost from ribosomes in post-stationary cells |CITS: 
                     [6201363]|.
                     The N-terminal methionine of L16 appears to be methylated 
                     |CITS: [786730][323502]|, and additional posttranslational 
                     modifications of the protein are present |CITS: 
                     [10094780][22649682]|.  These include phosphorylation 
                     |CITS: [17938405][19469554]| as well as hydroxylation of 
                     the Arg81 residue by |FRAME: CPLX0-8112| |CITS: 
                     [23103944]|.
                     L16 has RNA chaperone-like activity in an <i>in vitro 
                     trans</i>-splicing assay |CITS: [15525706]| as well as 
                     protein chaperone activity |CITS: [19071121]|."
