                     /product="trifunctional 30S ribosomal subunit protein S3 /
                     30S ribosomal subunit / ribosome"
                     /label=rpsC
                     /note="The S3 protein, a component of the small subunit of
                     the ribosome, is surface-accessible and located on the head
                     of
                     the 30S subunit |CITS: [6394951]|.  It can be crosslinked 
                     to rRNA |CITS: [7556101]| and nascent peptides
                     |CITS: [9716382]| as well as to IF3 |CITS: [7020604]|.  S3 
                     is the main target of modification by reaction with 
                     pyridoxal
                     phosphate |CITS: [6336745]|.
                     The ribosome was found to have mRNA helicase activity, and 
                     mutations in the S3 and S4 subunits impair this activity 
                     |CITS: [15652481]|.
                     A low-resolution cryo-electron microscopy map of the 
                     ribosome containing S3 has been analyzed |CITS: 
                     [12809609]|."
