     gene            complement(3443260..3443592)
                     /gene="rplV"
                     /locus_tag="b3315"
                     /label=rplV
     CDS             complement(3443260..3443592)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rplV"
                     /locus_tag="b3315"
                     /product="trifunctional 50S ribosomal subunit protein L22
                     / 50S ribosomal subunit / ribosome"
                     /label=rplV
                     /note="The L22 protein is a component of the 50S subunit
                     of the ribosome; it can interact with nascent translation 
                     products in the exit tunnel |CITS: [11893334]| and provides
                     one of the earliest contacts with a nascent peptide chain 
                     past the peptidyl transferase center |CITS: [15983062]|.
                     L22 is an early assembly protein and binds to the 5' end of
                     23S rRNA |CITS: [4934681][386275][6153613][6998892][329 
                     8242][2495985][8308887]|; it can be crosslinked to 23S rRNA
                     in both free ribosomes and the initiation complex |CITS: 
                     [2495985]|. L22 also crosslinks to L32 |CITS: [2645289]| 
                     and L18 |CITS: [2653827]|. L22 does not appear to be 
                     required for the structural integrity of the 50S subunit 
                     |CITS: [18695246]|.
                     L22 that lacks part of its extended loop that lines the 
                     peptide exit tunnel is functional in ribosome assembly 
                     |CITS: [13130133]|. The K90H or K90W mutations in L22 
                     affect ribosome stalling during translation of the TnaC 
                     leader peptide |CITS: [16061180]|. A K90D mutation in L22 
                     resulted in cells with altered growth and additional 
                     physiological changes, such as increased ability to survive
                     in low pH conditions and form biofilms |CITS: [35311583]|. 
                     The effect of L22 on ribosome pausing depends on the 
                     peptide being translated |CITS: [18586934]|.
                     In addition to preventing elongation of the peptide chain, 
                     the antibiotic erythromycin inhibits the assembly of the 
                     50S ribosomal subunit |CITS: [7766155]|. L22 is a component
                     of the binding site for erythromycin on the ribosome |CITS:
                     [3275651]|. A 9 bp deletion in <i>rplV</i>, removing codons
                     82-84 of L22, leads to erythromycin resistance; the mutant 
                     phenotype is recessive |CITS: [7928988]|. 
                     Erythromycin-resistant L22 mutants show a perturbed 
                     conformation of 23S rRNA |CITS: [10369764]| and affect the 
                     topology of the nascent polypeptide exit tunnel |CITS: 
                     [11511371]|. Additional L22 mutants that confer 
                     erythromycin resistance have been isolated |CITS: 
                     [17956547]|.
                     Temperature-sensitive <i>rplV</i> mutants are defective in 
                     protein synthesis |CITS: [6159923][7729693]|.
                     EryB: ""<b>ery</b>thromycin resistance <b>B</b>"" |CITS: 
                     [4589347][353516]|"
