     CDS             complement(3443902..3444723)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rplB"
                     /locus_tag="b3317"
                     /product="trifunctional 50S ribosomal subunit protein L2 /
                     50S ribosomal subunit / ribosome"
                     /label=rplB
                     /note="The L2 protein is a component of the 50S subunit of
                     the ribosome and is part of the peptidyltransferase center.
                     L2 is highly evolutionarily conserved |CITS: 
                     [6209167][9531480]|.
                     L2 is required for the association of the 30S and 50S 
                     subunits |CITS: [11013226]|; one end of the elongated L2 
                     protein is located at the intersubunit interface of the 50S
                     subunit |CITS: [11114255]|. L2 is involved in binding of 
                     tRNA to both the A and P sites, and the His229 residue 
                     appears to be important for peptidyl-transferase activity 
                     of the ribosome |CITS: [11013226]|. A conserved region 
                     within L2 is required for assembly of L16 into the 50S 
                     ribosomal subunit |CITS: [2211695]|. Ribosome modulation 
                     factor binds near L2, L13, and S13 |CITS: [12473202]|.
                     L2 interacts with domains II and IV of 23S rRNA |CITS: 
                     [1960726][3061801][9693099][9813114]| and with 5S rRNA 
                     |CITS: [11094158]|. L2 also interacts with aminoacyl-tRNA 
                     |CITS: [6170527][2412896][2182127]|. Protein-Protein 
                     Interaction (PPI) networks have been examined with 
                     algebraic topology analysis showing that most interacting 
                     proteins with L2 protein are related to the protein 
                     translation |CITS: [35560988]|."
