     gene            complement(3444741..3445043)
                     /gene="rplW"
                     /locus_tag="b3318"
                     /label=rplW
     CDS             complement(3444741..3445043)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rplW"
                     /locus_tag="b3318"
                     /product="trifunctional 50S ribosomal subunit protein L23
                     / 50S ribosomal subunit / ribosome"
                     /label=rplW
                     /note="The L23 protein is a component of the 50S subunit
                     of the ribosome and provides a chaperone docking site that 
                     links
                     protein biosynthesis with protein folding.  L23 is 
                     essential for growth of <i>E. coli</i> |CITS: [12226666]|. 
                     L23 crosslinks to Trigger Factor (TF), a protein that 
                     interacts with nascent polypeptides on the ribosome, and is
                     essential for the association of TF with the ribosome 
                     |CITS: [12226666][12756233]|.  It also crosslinks to the 
                     Ffh
                     component of the Signal Recognition Particle (SRP) |CITS: 
                     [12702815][12756233]|.  K<sub>d</sub> values for binding of
                     TF and SRP to the ribosome under various conditions have 
                     been estimated, and TF and SRP are thought to have separate
                     binding sites on L23 |CITS: [15308339]|.  L23 can also be 
                     crosslinked to a nascent peptide chain
                     |CITS: [15983062]|.
                     L23 is an early assembly protein that interacts with 23S 
                     rRNA
                     |CITS: [386275][1702198][1960726][2495985][8308887][969309 
                     9][6163479][6392564][9693099]|. L23
                     crosslinks to tRNA in the A site |CITS: [2660905]|.  L23 
                     can also be crosslinked to L34 |CITS: [2645289][2665813]| 
                     and L29 |CITS: [2665813]|.
                     L23 is photoaffinity labeled by puromycin, thus placing it 
                     within the A-site domain of the peptidyl transferase center
                     |CITS: [1103130][341968][3888269]|.  Puromycin-crosslinked 
                     L23 interferes with tRNA binding, but 50S subunits 
                     containing it retain peptidyl transferase activity |CITS: 
                     [2191716]|.
                     Reviews: |CITS: [12352951][15978066]|"
