     gene            complement(3445656..3446285)
                     /gene="rplC"
                     /locus_tag="b3320"
                     /label=rplC
     CDS             complement(3445656..3446285)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rplC"
                     /locus_tag="b3320"
                     /product="trifunctional 50S ribosomal subunit protein L3 /
                     50S ribosomal subunit / ribosome"
                     /label=rplC
                     /note="The L3 protein is a component of the 50S subunit of
                     the ribosome.  L3 and L24 are the two proteins that 
                     initiate
                     assembly of the 50S subunit |CITS: [6760192]|.
                     The L3 protein is methylated at the glutamine residue in 
                     position 150 |CITS: [331083][10094780 ]|.  A <i>prmB</i> 
                     mutant which lacks methylation of L3 has a cold-sensitive 
                     growth phenotype and accumulates abnormal ribosomal 
                     particles; however, lack of L3 methylation does not appear 
                     to affect ribosome function once the ribosome is
                     assembled |CITS: [6173216]|.
                     L3 interacts with 23S rRNA |CITS: [9873002]|; this 
                     interaction appears to be cooperative with L6 |CITS: 
                     [9873002]|.
                     An L3 mutant strain is resistant to the antibiotics 
                     tiamulin (a peptidyl transferase inhibitor) and 
                     pleuromutilin, but not
                     valnemulin |CITS: [12936991][16569865]|.  An amber mutation
                     in <i>rplC</i> exerts a polar effect on the genes distal
                     to the <i>rplC</i> gene in the S10 operon |CITS: 
                     [6986365]|."
