     CDS             3449736..3451688
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="gspD"
                     /locus_tag="b3325"
                     /product="bifunctional type II secretion system secretin
                     GspDalpha / type II secretion system"
                     /EC_number="7.4.2.8"
                     /label=gspD
                     /note="<i>E. coli</i> K-12 contains a cluster of genes 
                     (<i>gsp</i>) predicted to encode the components of a type 
                     II secretion system; the cluster consists of two divergent 
                     operons |FRAME: TU0-14374 <i>gspC-O</i>| and |FRAME: 
                     TU-8433 <i>gspAB</i>| which are transcriptionally repressed
                     by |FRAME: PD00288 nucleoid-structuring protein H-NS| under
                     standard laboratory conditions |CITS: [8655552][11118204]|.
                     Overexpression of the full cluster supports secretion of 
                     (plasmid expressed) |FRAME: EG11237-MONOMER| and (plasmid 
                     expressed) |FRAME: G7706-MONOMER pseudopilin GspG| in a 
                     <i>hns</i> mutant strain |CITS: [11118204][12754241]|.
                     <i>gspD</i> encodes the outer membrane channel or 
                     'secretin' of gram-negative type II secretion systems (see 
                     |CITS: [21565514][22466878][30767847]|). Purified GspD 
                     adopts a pentadecameric structure forming a cylindrical 
                     channel; the K-12 GspD protomer consists of five domains: 3
                     N domains (N1, N2, N3) which form the periplasmic chamber 
                     plus the secretin and S domain which form the pore 
                     structure in the OM |CITS: [ 28067918]|. <i>gspD</i> in 
                     <i>E. coli</i> K-12 encodes a <i>Klebsiella</i>-type 
                     GspD<sub>&alpha;</sub> secretin; cryo-ET in-situ structures
                     of GspD<sub>&alpha;</sub> on the inner and outer membrane 
                     have been obtained and a model of secretin translocation 
                     proposed |CITS: [37563200]|.
                     <i>gsp</i>: <U>g</U>eneral <U>s</U>ecretory <U>p</U>athway 
                     |CITS: [8655552]|"
