                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="gspM"
                     /locus_tag="b3334"
                     /product="bifunctional type II secretion system protein
                     GspM / type II secretion system"
                     /EC_number="7.4.2.8"
                     /label=gspM
                     /note="<i>E. coli</i> K-12 contains a cluster of genes 
                     (<i>gsp</i>) predicted to encode the components of a type 
                     II secretion system; the cluster consists of two divergent 
                     operons |FRAME: TU0-14374 <i>gspC-O</i>| and |FRAME: 
                     TU-8433 <i>gspAB</i>| which are transcriptionally repressed
                     by |FRAME: PD00288 nucleoid-structuring protein H-NS| under
                     standard laboratory conditions |CITS: [8655552][11118204]|.
                     Overexpression of the full cluster supports secretion of 
                     (plasmid expressed) |FRAME: EG11237-MONOMER| and (plasmid 
                     expressed) |FRAME: G7706-MONOMER pseudopilin GspG| in a 
                     <i>hns</i> mutant strain |CITS: [11118204][12754241]|.
                     GspM is predicted to be a bitopic inner membrane protein 
                     |CITS: [27510400]|.
                     <i>gspM</i> encodes a component of the inner membrane 
                     platform of gram-negative type II secretion systems (see 
                     |CITS: [22466878][30767847]|).
                     <i>gsp</i>: <U>g</U>eneral <U>s</U>ecretory <U>p</U>athway 
                     |CITS: [8655552]|<BR><i>pshM</i>: <U>p</U>rotein 
                     <U>s</U>ecretion <U>h</U>omolog |CITS: [7959070]|)"
