     gene            3458902..3459579
                     /gene="gspO"
                     /locus_tag="b3335"
                     /label=gspO
     CDS             3458902..3459579
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="gspO"
                     /locus_tag="b3335"
                     /product="bifunctional type II secretion system prepilin
                     peptidase / leader peptidase"
                     /EC_number="3.4.23.43"
                     /label=gspO
                     /note="In <i>Escherichia coli</i>, <i>gspO</i> is a member
                     of an operon of genes (<i>gspC-O</i>) which are not 
                     normally expressed |CITS: [11118204]| but are homologous to
                     those encoding the secreton, or type II secretion machinery
                     in <i>Klebsiella oxytoca</i> and <i>Aeromonase 
                     hydrophila</i>, among others |CITS: [8655552]|. Although 
                     <i>Escherichia coli</i> K-12 does not secrete endogenous 
                     proteins, the <i>gsp</i> genes of <i>E. coli</i> are 
                     orthologs of those in other secretons |CITS: [8655552]|, 
                     including those of the pullulanase (<i>pul</i>) secretion 
                     pathway of <i>Klebsiella oxytoca</i>.
                     GspO encodes a protein similar to type IV prepilin 
                     peptidases, like <i>pulO</i> gene in <i>K. oxytoca</i>. 
                     Though it is under the control of a promoter that has very 
                     poor basal expression under laboratory growth conditions, 
                     when expressed from a stronger promoter, GspO promotes 
                     cleavage of prepilin peptidase substrates such as type IV 
                     prepilin from <i>Neisseria gonorrhoaea</i> and prePulG as 
                     well as PulH, PulI and PulJ from <i>K. oxytoca </i>, 
                     referred to as pseudopilins |CITS: 
                     [8655552][8412682][8057924][10735856]|. <i>gspO</i> is 
                     capable of complementing the processing function in a 
                     <i>pulO</i> deletion mutant |CITS: [8655552]|.
                     <i>gsp</i>: <U>g</U>eneral <U>s</U>ecretory <U>p</U>athway 
                     |CITS: [8655552]|<BR><i>hopD</i>: <U>ho</U>mologous to 
                     <U>p</U>ilC |CITS: [7959070]|"
