     gene            complement(3460519..3463212)
                     /gene="chiA"
                     /locus_tag="b3338"
                     /label=chiA
     CDS             complement(3460519..3463212)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="chiA"
                     /locus_tag="b3338"
                     /product="endochitinase"
                     /EC_number="3.2.1.14"
                     /label=chiA
                     /note="ChiA is a large soluble protein with five predicted 
                     chitin-binding domains and a C-terminal catalytic domain 
                     that is similar to the family 18 glycohydrolases |CITS: 
                     [10760150]|.  The purified N-terminal chitin-binding domain
                     binds to chitin with high affinity, but binds only poorly 
                     to cellulose |CITS: [10419961]|.  Purified ChiA exhibits 
                     endochitinase activity, releasing diacetyl-chitobiose and 
                     triacetyl-chitotriose from colloidal chitin |CITS: 
                     [33794535]|.
                     Under standard growth conditions, <i>chiA</i> expression is
                     low and is negatively controlled by H-NS |CITS: 
                     [10760150]|.  In mutants lacking H-NS, expression of the 
                     <i>gsp</i> locus is derepressed, and a type II secretion 
                     machinery can be produced.  This allows secretion of ChiA 
                     into the culture medium |CITS: [11118204]|.  Expression of 
                     <i>chiA</i> is activated by BglJ-RcsB, which may function 
                     as an H-NS antagonist |CITS: [24335284]|.  Artificially 
                     induced expression of <i>chiA</i> enables growth on 
                     pentaacetyl-chitopentaose |CITS: [33794535]|.
                     ChiA: ""<b>chi</b>tinase"" |CITS: [10760150]|
                     Review: |CITS: [21938682]|"
