     gene            complement(3483625..3484188)
                     /gene="pabA"
                     /locus_tag="b3360"
                     /label=pabA
     CDS             complement(3483625..3484188)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="pabA"
                     /locus_tag="b3360"
                     /product="bifunctional aminodeoxychorismate synthase
                     subunit 2 / 4-amino-4-deoxychorismate synthase"
                     /EC_number="2.6.1.85"
                     /label=pabA
                     /note="PabA (component 2) provides the glutamine 
                     amidotransferase activity of the aminodeoxychorismate 
                     synthase complex |CITS: [1637823]|.
                     PabA functions as a glutaminase, but only when in complex 
                     with PabB |CITS: [1637823]|.  The reaction proceeds via 
                     formation of a covalent PabA-&gamma;-glutamyl intermediate 
                     |CITS: [1637823][15770625]|.  Titration of PabA with PabB 
                     showed a gain of glutaminase activity that reached a 
                     plateau at a 1:1 ratio of PabA/PabB, suggesting that the 
                     effect of PabB is as a stoichiometric positive allosteric 
                     effector on the PabA subunit |CITS: [1637823]|.  The 
                     presence of chorismate allosterically stimulates the 
                     glutaminase activity of PabA further |CITS: [31121180]|. 
                     Analysis of PabA by site-directed mutagenesis suggested a 
                     role for the conserved Cys79, His168 and Glu170 as part of 
                     the catalytic triad |CITS: [8096767]|.  The crystal 
                     structure of a predicted ancestral PabA protein has been 
                     solved, and a homology model for the PabA-PabB complex was 
                     derived |CITS: [31121180]|.  Alanine scanning mutagenesis 
                     revealed residues within an interdomain hydrogen bonding 
                     network that are important for PabA-PabB complex formation,
                     residues involved in allosteric signaling between the 
                     subunits, as well as residues involved in ammonia 
                     channeling from the PabA- to the PabB active site |CITS: 
                     [31121180]|.
                     Expression of <i>pabA</i> is constitutive |CITS: 
                     [2050628]|.  <i>pabA</i> appeared to be transcribed from 
                     two promoters, one upstream of <i>yhfG</i> and another 
                     upstream of <i>pabA</i> itself |CITS: [2403545]|.
                     However, it appears that transcription from the <i>yhfG</i>
                     promoter is normally terminated by a stable secondary 
                     structure upstream of <i>pabA</i> |CITS: [2050628]|.
                     A <i>pabA</i> mutant requires supplementation with 
                     <i>p</i>-aminobenzoate for growth |CITS: [5337773]|.
                     PabA: ""<b><i>p</i>-a</b>mino<b>b</b>enzoate"" |CITS: 
                     [5337773]|"
                     /translation="MILLIDNYDSFTWNLYQYFCELGADVLVKRNDALTLADIDALKPQ
