     gene            complement(3484220..3484822)
                     /gene="fic"
                     /locus_tag="b3361"
                     /label=fic
     CDS             complement(3484220..3484822)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="fic"
                     /locus_tag="b3361"
                     /product="bifunctional putative adenosine
                     monophosphate--protein transferase Fic / FicT-FicA complex"
                     /label=fic
                     /note="The Fic protein is the founding member of a
                     widespread family of proteins.  It is related to the phage 
                     P1 toxin Doc |CITS: [14659018]| and contains a sequence 
                     motif required for AMPylation activity in related proteins 
                     |CITS: [19503829]|.  A |FRAME: EG12374-MONOMER small 
                     protein| encoded upstream of Fic is homologous to the 
                     cognate antitoxins |CITS: [26299961]|.  However, the <i>E. 
                     coli</i> Fic belongs to a set of enterobacterial FicT 
                     homologs with an altered FIC domain signature motif, where 
                     a hydrophobic residue is substituted for a conserved 
                     arginine residue that is involved in ATP binding in the 
                     FicT proteins with AMP transferase activity |CITS: 
                     [26299961][27657533]|.  Unlike other FicT proteins, 
                     expression of the wild-type <i>E. coli</i> protein does not
                     cause a detectable growth defect |CITS: [26299961]|. 
                     Crystal structures of the Fic-FicA complex have been 
                     solved.  Combined with phylogenetic analysis, the crystal 
                     structures show a conserved potential ligand-binding 
                     pocket; the ligand awaits identification |CITS: 
                     [27657533]|.
                     A strain containing the <i>fic-1</i> allele, which encodes 
                     a G55R change |CITS: [2546924]|, exhibits heat-sensitive 
                     CRP-dependent cell filamentation in the presence of cAMP 
                     |CITS: [6284712]|.  Filamentation of the <i>fic-1</i> 
                     mutant is associated with production of a 40 kD membrane 
                     protein |CITS: [6305918]|, and the phenotype can be rescued
                     by NaCl |CITS: [2842288]| or by folate |CITS: [1656497]|.  
                     The mutation does not appear to affect the structure of the
                     protein |CITS: [27657533]|.
                     A <i>fic</i> null mutant exhibits a PAB (p-aminobenzoate) 
                     or folate requirement at high growth temperatures |CITS: 
                     [1656497]|.  Unlike the <i>fic-1</i> point mutant, a null 
                     mutant does not exhibit heat-sensitive, cAMP-induced 
                     filamentation |CITS: [2842288]|.
                     <i>fic</i> is transcribed at stationary phase by RpoS 
                     (&sigma;<sup>S</sup>)-containing RNA polymerase holoenzyme 
                     |CITS: 
                     [8475100][8270191][7708499][7549107][7665531][8825088]|. 
                     Fic: ""<b>fi</b>lamentation induced by <b>c</b>AMP"" |CITS:
                     [6284712]|
                     (FicT: ""<b>FIC</b> domain <b>t</b>oxin"" |CITS: 
                     [26299961]|)
                     Review: |CITS: [26299785 ]|"
                     /translation="MSDKFGEGRDPYLYPGLDIMRNRLNIRQQQRLEQAAYEMTALRAA
