     gene            3489910..3490236
                     /gene="nirD"
                     /locus_tag="b3366"
                     /label=nirD
     CDS             3489910..3490236
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="nirD"
                     /locus_tag="b3366"
                     /product="bifunctional nitrite reductase (NADH) small
                     subunit / nitrite reductase - NADH dependent"
                     /EC_number="1.7.1.15"
                     /label=nirD
                     /note="NirD may be a subunit of the NADH-dependent nitrite 
                     reductase.  Presence of <i>nirD</i> is required for nitrite
                     reductase activity in cell extracts, and the NirD protein 
                     appears to be present in partially purified nitrite 
                     reductase |CITS: [1435259]|.  NirD interacts directly with 
                     NirB in a BACTH experiment |CITS: [34323689]|.  However, 
                     the function of NirD in enabling nitrite reductase activity
                     has not been determined.
                     NirD interacts directly with the catalytic domain of 
                     |FRAME: RELA-MONOMER RelA|, thereby inhibiting the 
                     synthesis of (p)ppGpp and the stringent response.  The E50K
                     mutation eliminates the interaction with RelA, but does not
                     affect the interaction with NirB |CITS: [34323689]|.
                     Overexpression of <i>nirD</i> leads to a decrease of the 
                     intracellular levels of (p)ppGpp |CITS: [34323689]|. 
                     Expression of <i>nirD</i> is upregulated upon exposure to 
                     silver nanoparticles |CITS: [22771582]|.
                     NirD: ""<b>n</b>itr<b>i</b>te <b>r</b>eductase"""
