                     /label=nirC
     CDS             3490362..3491168
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="nirC"
                     /locus_tag="b3367"
                     /product="nitrite transporter NirC"
                     /label=nirC
                     /note="NirC, encoded within the 4-gene <i>nir</i> operon
                     |CITS: [2200672][1435259]|, is an inner membrane nitrite 
                     channel that contributes to both nitrite uptake and nitrite
                     efflux under anaerobic growth conditions |CITS: 
                     [11967075][15667293]| (and see further |CITS: [18691156]|).
                     Purified NirC, incorporated into liposomes, is permeable to
                     nitrite, nitrate, and formate; it has low permeability to 
                     acetate and is impermeable to ammonium and magnesium 
                     cations. A pentameric structure has been modeled |CITS: 
                     [36918441]|.
                     In the Transporter Classification Database, NirC is a 
                     member of the Formate-Nitrate Transporter (FNT) family 
                     |CITS: [33170213]| (see also |CITS: [28738779]|).
                     Related review: |CITS: [23380538]|"
