     CDS             3494627..3495649
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="frlB"
                     /locus_tag="b3371"
                     /product="fructoselysine 6-phosphate deglycase"
                     /label=frlB
                     /note="Fructoselysine 6-phosphate deglycase, which acts in 
                     fructoselysine degradation, is an FrlB dodecamer |CITS: 
                     [12147680]|.  The fructoselysine 6-phosphate deglycase 
                     reaction is reversible <i>in vitro</i>, but is catalyzed in
                     the direction of formation of glucose 6-phosphate and 
                     lysine <i>in vivo</i> |CITS: [12147680]|.  A detailed 
                     reaction mechanism is discussed |CITS: [12147680]|. 
                     Fructoselysine 6-phosphate deglycase activity is 
                     undetectable when cells are grown on glucose; stationary 
                     phase extract of cells grown on fructoselysine or 
                     psicoselysine have a deglycase activity of 20 nmol/min per 
                     mg of protein |CITS: [14641112]|.
                     An <i>frlA</i> mutant is unable to grow on 20mM 
                     fructoselysine or psicoselysine as the sole source of 
                     carbon |CITS: [14641112]|.
                     FrlB: ""<b>fr</b>uctose<b>l</b>ysine"" |CITS: [12147680]|"
