     gene            3496526..3497311
                     /gene="frlD"
                     /locus_tag="b3374"
                     /label=frlD
     CDS             3496526..3497311
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="frlD"
                     /locus_tag="b3374"
                     /product="fructoselysine 6-kinase"
                     /EC_number="2.7.1.218"
                     /label=frlD
                     /note="FrlD is a monomeric fructoselysine 6-kinase |CITS: 
                     [12147680]|.  FrlD is a member of the PfkB family of 
                     kinases and has similarity to the glucosamine-6-phosphate 
                     synthase isomerase domain |CITS: [12147680]|.
                     A structure model of FrlD was used to identify potential 
                     residues involved in substrate recognition, and 
                     site-directed mutants were tested for enzymatic activity. 
                     Most of the mutants showed significantly decreased 
                     activity.  A Met220Leu mutant has decreased activity with 
                     fructoselysine, but increased activity with fructosevaline 
                     as the substrate |CITS: [23076362]|.
                     Fructoselysine 6-kinase activity is undetectable when cells
                     are grown on glucose; stationary phase extracts of cells 
                     grown on fructoselysine or psicoselysine have a kinase 
                     activity of 100 nmol/min per mg of protein |CITS: 
                     [14641112]|.
                     Experiments in |CITS: [12147680][14641112]| were done with 
                     proteins from <i>E. coli</i> BL21(DE3).
                     FrlD: ""<b>fr</b>uctose<b>l</b>ysine"" |CITS: [12147680]|"
