                     /product="putative hydrolase"
                     /label=php
                     /note="The Php protein is similar to phosphotriesterase
                     from <i>Pseudomonas diminuta</i>, but unlike that enzyme, 
                     it does not catalyze the hydrolysis of nonspecific 
                     phosphotriesters.  Its physiological function is unknown 
                     |CITS: [9548740]|.
                     Php is a monomer in solution.  A crystal structure has been
                     solved at 1.7 &Aring; resolution.  The structure, an 
                     &alpha;/&beta; barrel, is similar to that of 
                     phosphotriesterase and contains a binuclear zinc center at 
                     the presumed active site |CITS: [9548740]|.
                     Php: ""<b>p</b>hosphotriesterase <b>h</b>omology 
                     <b>p</b>rotein"" |CITS: [9548740]|"
