     gene            complement(3506990..3507748)
                     /gene="gph"
                     /locus_tag="b3385"
                     /label=gph
     CDS             complement(3506990..3507748)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="gph"
                     /locus_tag="b3385"
                     /product="phosphoglycolate phosphatase"
                     /EC_number="3.1.3.18"
                     /label=gph
                     /note="The <i>gph</i> gene encodes a haloacid dehalogenase 
                     (HAD)-like phosphatase family enzyme with 
                     2-phosphoglycolate phosphatase activity 
                     |CITS:[7603433],[10572959],[16990279]|.
                     2-phosphoglycolate phosphatase is an enzyme of the Calvin 
                     Cycle for assimilation of CO<sub>2</sub>, and it was thus 
                     not clear why it would be found in <i>E. coli</i> 
                     |CITS:[7603433],[10572959]|.  However, 2-phosphoglycolate 
                     is formed during repair of DNA strand breaks with 
                     3'-phosphoglycolate ends; such breaks can be caused by 
                     radiomimetic drugs like bleomycin |CITS:[13129953]|.  Gph 
                     was shown to be involved in the recovery of glycolate from 
                     2-phosphoglycolate released by the activity of DNA repair 
                     enzymes after bleomycin treatment |CITS:[13129953]|. 
                     Deletion of <I>gph</I> resulted in loss of induction of the
                     <I>glc</I> operon by glycolate after bleomycin treatment 
                     |CITS:[13129953]|.  <I>gph</I> mutants also failed to 
                     recover as quickly as wild type after bleomycin treatment 
                     |CITS:[13129953]|.  In a previous study <i>gph</i> deletion
                     mutation had no apparent physiological effect 
                     |CITS:[10572959]|.
                     Expression of <i>gph</i> appears to be constitutive 
                     |CITS:[13129953]|.
                     Overexpression of the |FRAME: EG11871| gene is able to 
                     rescue a mutation in the |FRAME: EG10945| gene |CITS: 
                     [17884825][36920032]|.
                     Gph: ""phospho<b>g</b>lycolate <b>ph</b>osphatase"" |CITS: 
                     [7603433]|"
                     /translation="MNKFEDIRGVAFDLDGTLVDSAPGLAAAVDMALYALELPVAGEER
                     VITWIGNGADVLMERALTWARQERATQRKTMGKPPVDDDIPAEEQVRILRKLFDRYYGE
