                     /product="DNA utilization protein HofP"
                     /label=hofP
                     /note="The <i>yrfA</i> gene product is required for
                     utilization of DNA as the sole source of carbon and energy;
                     <i>yrfA</i> is homologous to genes involved in natural 
                     competence and genetic transformation in other bacteria 
                     |CITS: [11591672][16707682]|.  YrfA is predicted to be 
                     located in the inner membrane |CITS: [16707682]|.
                     A <i>yrfA</i> null mutant has a normal growth phenotype in 
                     complex media, but has a stationary phase 
                     competition-defective (SPCD) phenotype in co-culture with 
                     the wild-type strain.  A <i>yrfA</i> null mutant can not 
                     utilize DNA as the sole source of carbon and energy |CITS: 
                     [16707682]|.
                     <i>yrfA</i> is poorly expressed |CITS: [10633126]|.
                     "
