     gene            3519828..3521963
                     /gene="igaA"
                     /locus_tag="b3398"
                     /label=igaA
     CDS             3519828..3521963
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="igaA"
                     /locus_tag="b3398"
                     /product="inner membrane protein involved in phosphorelay
                     system"
                     /label=igaA
                     /note="IgaA is an essential inner membrane protein which 
                     inhibits the |FRAME: PWY0-1493|; IgaA acts downstream of 
                     RcsF in the Rcs signaling pathway; current models suggest 
                     that IgaA interacts physically with either RcsC or RcsD to 
                     regulate kinase/phosphatase activity (see |CITS: 
                     [29897834]|).
                     <i>igaA</i> is essential in <i>E. coli</i> K-12; an 
                     <i>igaA</i> deletion is viable when combined with deletions
                     of <i>rcsB, rcsC</i> or <i>rcsD</i>; IgaA forms a complex 
                     with RcsF <i>in vivo</i>; depletion of IgaA activates the 
                     Rcs signaling pathway independently of RcsF; IgaA exerts an
                     inhibitory effect on the Rcs signaling cascade |CITS: 
                     [25525882]|. RcsF-IgaA complex levels increase in response 
                     to peptidoglycan stress (mecillinam treatment); under 
                     stress conditions RcsF interacts with the periplasmic 
                     domain of IgaA resulting in activation of the Rcs system 
                     |CITS: [29852010]|.
                     IgaA is an inner membrane protein predicted to contain 5 
                     transmembrane domains with two cytosolic domains at the 
                     N-terminus and one large periplasmic domain close to the 
                     C-terminus |CITS: [29852010]|.
                     The <i>mrcA</i> deletion strain characterised by |CITS: 
                     [10383966]| was later found to be an <i>mrcA nudE igaA</i> 
                     triple mutant (more specifically the deletion covered 
                     'most' of <i>mrcA</i>, all of <i>nudE</i> and the promoter 
                     and 5' end of <i>igaA</i>) |CITS: [11567017]|.
                     <i>igaA</i> was included in a pilot study examining genetic
                     interactions of essential genes |CITS: [24463526]|.
                     IgaA was first characterised in <i>Salmonella 
                     typhimurium</i> |CITS: 
                     [11553591][12524328][15387821][15516559]|; the gene from 
                     <i>E. coli</i> has 80% sequence identity with its homolog 
                     from Salmonella |CITS: [11553591]|."
