     CDS             3526177..3527799
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="pck"
                     /locus_tag="b3403"
                     /product="phosphoenolpyruvate carboxykinase (ATP)"
                     /EC_number="4.1.1.49"
                     /label=pck
                     /note="Phosphoenolpyruvate (PEP) carboxykinase (Pck) is an 
                     enzyme involved in gluconeogenesis.  Growth on succinate as
                     the carbon and energy source is limited by the level of Pck
                     in the cell |CITS: [8226637]|.
                     PEP carboxykinase is unusual in that it appears to be a 
                     monomeric enzyme with an allosteric site |CITS: [6986370]|.
                     Crystal structures of the enzyme have been solved |CITS: 
                     [2056527][8609605][8599762][11724534][12837799]|, providing
                     insight into the mechanistic details of the enzymatic 
                     reaction |CITS: [8599762][11724534]| and into the mechanism
                     of activation by Ca<sup>2+</sup> |CITS: [12837799]|.
                     Transcription of <i>pck</i> is regulated by catabolite 
                     repression and is induced at the onset of stationary phase 
                     |CITS: [6988403][6434512][2183002]| and is regulated by 
                     CsrA |CITS: [8393005]|.  Overexpression of <i>pck</i> 
                     during growth on glucose leads to reduced growth yield and 
                     increased excretion of fermentation products such as 
                     acetate |CITS: [8285716]|.  Expression of Pck is 
                     upregulated when acetate is used as the source of carbon 
                     |CITS: [12655459]|.
                     A double mutant defective in both PEP carboxykinase and 
                     |FRAME: PEPSYNTH-CPLX| is unable to utilize C4-dicarboxylic
                     acids such as succinate and malate as the sole source of 
                     carbon and energy |CITS: [4370531]|. Reviews: |CITS: 
                     [7832509][8599751][9139042][15023367]|
                     "
