     gene            3533522..3533749
                     /gene="feoA"
                     /locus_tag="b3408"
                     /label=feoA
     CDS             3533522..3533749
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="feoA"
                     /locus_tag="b3408"
                     /product="Fe(2+) transport protein A"
                     /label=feoA
                     /note="FeoA is part of a conserved ferrous iron transport 
                     system. The function of this protein has not yet been 
                     determined in <i>E. coli</i>; however, in a number of 
                     orthologous systems, FeoA was shown to form a complex with 
                     the FeoB transmembrane transporter component.
                     A solution structure of FeoA shows a Src-homology 3 
                     (SH3)-like fold; the protein forms a &beta;-barrel with two
                     &alpha;-helices, one of which is positioned over the 
                     barrel. FeoA does not appear to act as a GTPase-activating 
                     protein for FeoB |CITS: [23104801]|.
                     A <i>feoA</i>::Tn<i>5</i> mutant shows partially reduced 
                     uptake of ferrous iron |CITS: [8407793]|.
                     Fe<sup>2+</sup> uptake is regulated by Fur; a Fur binding 
                     site is located upstream of the <i>feo</i> locus |CITS: 
                     [Hantke87][8407793]|. <i>feo</i> expression is low under 
                     aerobic condtions and increases under anaerobic conditions 
                     under the positive control of transcription factors ArcA 
                     and FNR; Feo-mediated import of Fe<sup>2+</sup> promotes 
                     Fur-Fe<sup>2+</sup> occupancy amd contributes to Fur 
                     regulation under anaerobic conditions |CITS: [29087312]|. 
                     Overexpression of <i>feoA</i> increases the tolerance of 
                     <i>E. coli</i> to n-butanol |CITS: [21408113]|.
                     Expression of <i>feoA</i>, along with that of other genes 
                     also regulated by Fur,  is reduced under Zn excess |CITS: 
                     [31586033] |.
                     Feo: <b>fe</b>rr<b>o</b>us iron uptake |CITS: [Hantke87]| 
                     Reviews: |CITS: [16718600][16718601][26684538]|"
                     /translation="MQYTPDTAWKITGFSREISPAYRQKLLSLGMLPGSSFNVVRVAPL
                     GDPIHIETRRVSLVLRKKDLALLEVEAVSC"
                     /go_component="cytoplasm [goid 0005737] [evidence IEA]
                     [GO_REF 0000044]"
                     /go_function="transition metal ion binding [goid 0046914]
                     [evidence IEA] [GO_REF 0000002]"
                     /go_process="monoatomic ion transport [goid 0006811]
                     [evidence IEA] [GO_REF 0000043]"
                     /go_process="iron ion transport [goid 0006826] [evidence
                     IEA] [GO_REF 0000043]"
                     /go_process="DNA damage response [goid 0006974] [evidence
