     gene            3533766..3536087
                     /gene="feoB"
                     /locus_tag="b3409"
                     /label=feoB
     CDS             3533766..3536087
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="feoB"
                     /locus_tag="b3409"
                     /product="bifunctional Fe(2+) transporter FeoB / Fe(2+) 
                     transporter"
                     /label=feoB
                     /note="FeoB is the inner membrane component of a ferrous
                     iron uptake system which is active under anaerobic growth 
                     conditions |CITS: [8407793]|. FeoB is composed of a 
                     hydrophilic N-terminal domain which specifically binds GTP 
                     (the G protein domain; residues 1-170), a GDP dissociation 
                     inhibitor-like (GDI-like) domain (residues 171-274) and a 
                     C-terminal integral membrane domain which may act as a 
                     permease |CITS: [12446835][18068722]|. FeoB's G protein 
                     catalyses slow GTP hydrolysis and fast GDP release and is 
                     required for Fe(II) uptake |CITS: [12446835][18068722]|. 
                     The mechanism of ferrous iron uptake by FeoB may represent 
                     an early prototype of the eukaryotic G protein cycle |CITS:
                     [18068722]|.
                     Crystal structures of the soluble domain of FeoB (nFeoB 
                     comprising residues 1-270) in both an apo and GTP-bound 
                     conformation have been reported: nFeoB assembles as a 
                     funnel-shaped trimer with 3-fold symmetry between the 
                     protomers; the trimer binds a single molecule of the 
                     nonhydrolysable GTP analogue mGTP and a putative 
                     Mg<sup>2+</sup> ion; a comparative analysis of the 
                     structures suggests that GTP binding leads to opening of a 
                     central cytoplasmic pore and a mechanism of G-protein 
                     coupled gating of FeoB has been proposed |CITS: 
                     [19629046]|. Conformational change in the nucleotide 
                     binding G5 loop is implicated in GDP release |CITS: 
                     [19629046][25374115][25517170]|. The GTPase activity of 
                     nFeoB (residues 1-274) is stimulated by potassium |CITS: 
                     [30760591]|.
                     Early studies in <i>Escherichia coli</i> K-12 strains 
                     characterized <i>feo</i> mutants which were defective in 
                     the import of ferrous iron |CITS: [Hantke87][8407793]|. The
                     <i>feo</i> operon consists of three co-regulated genes 
                     <i>feoABC</i> |CITS: [8407793][16718600]|. <i>feo</i> is a 
                     member of the Fur regulon; expression is repressed by 
                     Fur-Fe<sup>2+</sup>; <i>feo</i> expression is activated by 
                     FNR under anaerobic conditions |CITS: [Hantke87][8407793]|.
                     <i>feo</i> expression is low under aerobic conditions and 
                     increases under anaerobic conditions under the positive 
                     control of transcription factors ArcA and FNR; Feo-mediated
                     import of Fe<sup>2+</sup> promotes Fur-Fe<sup>2+</sup> 
                     occupancy amd contributes to Fur regulation under anaerobic
                     conditions |CITS: [29087312]|.
                     FeoB is a member of the 'TrmE-Era-EngA-YihA-Septin like' 
                     superfamily within the GTPase superclass of P-loop NTPases 
                     |CITS: [11916378]| and a member of the Ferrous Iron Uptake 
                     Family in the Transporter Classification Database |CITS: 
                     [26546518]|.
                     <i>feo</i>: <u>fe</u>rr<u>o</u>us iron uptake |CITS: 
                     [Hantke87]|
                     Reviews: |CITS: [12781516][16718600][26684538][29953152]|"
                     /translation="MKKLTIGLIGNPNSGKTTLFNQLTGSRQRVGNWAGVTVERKEGQF
