     gene            3538241..3538924
                     /gene="yhgH"
                     /locus_tag="b3413"
                     /label=yhgH
     CDS             3538241..3538924
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yhgH"
                     /locus_tag="b3413"
                     /product="DNA utilization protein YhgH"
                     /label=yhgH
                     /note="The <i>yhgH</i> gene product is required for
                     utilization of DNA as the sole source of carbon and energy;
                     <i>yhgH</i> is homologous to genes involved in natural 
                     competence and genetic transformation in other bacteria 
                     |CITS: [11591672][16707682]|.
                     Based on complementation experiments, YhgH/GntX is also 
                     thought to be involved in high-affinity gluconate transport
                     |CITS: [9871335]|.
                     A <i>yhgH</i> null mutant has a normal growth phenotype in 
                     complex media, but has a stationary phase 
                     competition-defective (SPCD) phenotype in co-culture with 
                     the wild-type strain.  A <i>yhgI</i> null mutant can not 
                     utilize DNA as the sole source of carbon and energy |CITS: 
                     [16707682]|.
                     "
