     gene            complement(3562706..3564679)
                     /gene="glgX"
                     /locus_tag="b3431"
                     /label=glgX
     CDS             complement(3562706..3564679)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="glgX"
                     /locus_tag="b3431"
                     /product="limit dextrin alpha-1,6-glucohydrolase"
                     /EC_number="3.2.1.196"
                     /label=glgX
                     /note="GlgX is a glycogen debranching enzyme.  The
                     purified enzyme shows only low activity toward |FRAME: 
                     Glycogens glycogen| itself, but hydrolyzes 
                     1,6-&alpha;-glucosidic linkages in |FRAME: CPD0-971 ""limit
                     dextrins""| prepared from glycogen and amylopectin by 
                     treatment with phosphorylase and &beta;-amylase |CITS: 
                     [779849]|.  Recombinant GlgX efficiently hydrolyzes 
                     &alpha;-1,6-glucosidic linkages with degrees of 
                     polymerization of three or four glucose residues, and has 
                     very low or no activity with longer chains |CITS: 
                     [15687211]|.
                     The crystal structure of the enzyme has been determined at 
                     2.25 &Aring; resolution. The enzyme was found to be a 
                     monomer consisting of three major domains. A structural 
                     feature at the substrate binding groove suggests the basis 
                     of its unique specificity for G4 phosphorylase-limit 
                     dextrin and its discrimination toward substrates of varying
                     length |CITS: [20187119]|.
                     GlgX has similarity to glycogen branching enzymes, glucan 
                     hydrolases and glucan transferases from other organisms 
                     |CITS: [2975249]|.  Overexpression of <i>glgX</i> leads to 
                     increased glycogen debranching activity |CITS: [8576033]|. 
                     A <i>glgX</i> mutant strain lacks debranching activity and 
                     accumulates 2-3 times higher amounts of glycogen than the 
                     wild-type strain |CITS: [15687211]|.
                     Regulation has been described |CITS: 
                     [779849][2975249][8576033]|.  Expression <i>glgX</i> was 
                     induced by treatment with |FRAME: CPD-17518| |CITS: 
                     [11967071]|."
