                     /product="putative oxidoreductase YhhX"
                     /label=yhhX
                     /note="Based on sequence similarity, YhhX was predicted to
                     be a D-galactose 1-dehydrogenase |CITS: [12952533]|. 
                     However, this is not consistent with the known biochemistry
                     of <i>E. coli</i> K-12, which metabolizes galactose via the
                     |FRAME: PWY-6317|.
                     Transcription of <i>yhhX</i> was thought to be regulated by
                     Fur |CITS: [11101675]|, but the measured gene expression 
                     was due to a transcriptional fusion to <i>ryhB</i> |CITS: 
                     [11917098]|.
                     A transposon insertion mutant in <i>yhhX</i> is more 
                     sensitive to chloramphenicol than wild type |CITS: 
                     [18807027]|."
