                     /note="YhhY is an acetyltransferase that is able to
                     detoxify nonhydrolyzable aminoacyl adenylates.  <i>In 
                     vitro</i>, YhhY is able to acetylate the synthetic 
                     aminoacyl sulfamoyl adenylates LSA and ISA, but not DSA and
                     ESA |CITS: [25002546]|.
                     Transcription of <i>yhhY</i> is regulated by Fur |CITS: 
                     [11101675]|."
