                     /gene="ugpQ"
                     /locus_tag="b3449"
                     /product="multifunctional glycerophosphodiester
                     phosphodiesterase UgpQ / glycerophosphodiester 
                     phosphodiesterase / glycerophosphoglycerol 
                     phosphodiesterase / glycerophosphoserine phosphodiesterase 
                     / L-1-glycerophophorylethanolamine phosphodiesterase"
                     /EC_number="3.1.4.46"
                     /label=ugpQ
                     /note="UgpQ is a cytosolic glycerophosphodiester 
                     phosphodiesterase with broad substrate specificity |CITS: 
                     [18083802]|.
                     Initial experiments suggested that cytoplasmic 
                     glycerophosphodiesters are not substrates of UgpQ, and that
                     they are hydrolyzed only when transported by the Ugp system
                     |CITS: [2842304]|.  However, recent purification and 
                     characterization of the enzyme contradicts those results 
                     |CITS: [18083802]|.  Moreover, purified UgpQ does not 
                     affect the activity of the UgpB-EAC<sub>2</sub> transporter
                     complex <i>in vitro</i> |CITS: [23013274]|. Expression of 
                     UgpQ is induced by phosphate starvation |CITS: [18083802]|.
                      The <i>ugp</i> operon is induced by carbon starvation 
                     during the late logarithmic growth phase |CITS: [1745236]|.
                     UgpQ: ""<b>u</b>ptake of <b>g</b>lycerol <b>p</b>hosphate""
                     |CITS: [363686]|"
