     gene            3591344..3591727
                     /gene="panZ"
                     /locus_tag="b3459"
                     /label=panZ
     CDS             3591344..3591727
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="panZ"
                     /locus_tag="b3459"
                     /product="PanD maturation factor"
                     /label=panZ
                     /note="Coenzyme A-bound PanZ promotes activation of the
                     |FRAME: ASPDECARBOX-MONOMER ""PanD""| proenzyme |CITS: 
                     [23170229][25910242]| and negatively regulates the 
                     aspartate &alpha;-decarboxylase activity of activated PanD 
                     |CITS: [25910242]|.  PanZ is not an enzyme but a 
                     stoichiometric facilitator of PanD activation. Formation of
                     a PanD-PanZ complex stabilizes a conformation of PanD in 
                     which the serine-25 hydroxyl group moves to a close 
                     proximity to the adjacent carbonyl group, thus facilitating
                     an attack on the G24-S25 peptide bond |CITS: 
                     [22940551][25910242]|. Addition of PanZ to an assay of 
                     &beta;-alanine synthesis by PanD enhances activity 24-fold 
                     |CITS: [22497218]|.
                     Coenzyme A is a pantothenate metabolite; regulation of 
                     |FRAME: PANTO-PWY| by feedback inhibition of the committed 
                     input, |FRAME: PWY-5155 &beta;-alanine|, via the 
                     CoA-binding protein PanZ is a novel form of regulation 
                     |CITS: [25910242]|.
                     PanZ has micromolar affinity for both coenzyme A and 
                     acetyl-CoA and nanomolar affinity for the PanD proenzyme. 
                     The interaction of PanZ with PanD is dependent on the 
                     presence of CoA; titration experiments suggest that PanZ, 
                     PanD and CoA bind in a 1:1:1 ratio (a PanZ molecule binds 
                     to each of the PanD monomers that make up the PanD 
                     tetramer, with one molecule of CoA or acetyl-Coa bound to 
                     each PanZ-PanD complex) |CITS: [22940551]|.  Crystal 
                     structures of the PanZ-PanD complex elucidate the CoA 
                     dependency of the PanZ-PanD interaction and the structural 
                     basis for activation of PanD by PanZ |CITS: [25910242]|.
                     A site-directed mutant in a conserved residue of the 
                     acetyltransferase domain of PanZ, N45A, does not rescue the
                     &beta;-alanine requirement of a &Delta;<i>panZ</i> mutant 
                     and loses the ability to activate PanD |CITS: [23170229]|.
                     The N45 residue forms a hydrogen bond with the PanD 
                     main-chain amide of residue D23, which is located next to 
                     the cleavage site between G24 and S25 |CITS: [25910242]|. A
                     strain carrying a deletion of <i>livJ</i>, <i>panZ</i> and 
                     <i>livK</i> is auxotrophic for pantothenate; the 
                     auxotrophic phenotype can be complemented by a plasmid 
                     carrying the <i>panZ</i> gene alone |CITS: [2195019]|. 
                     Overexpression of <i>panZ</i> also leads to &beta;-alanine 
                     auxotrophy due to inhibition of ADC activity by PanZ |CITS:
                     [25910242]|.  <i>panZ</i> is essential for growth on 
                     glycerol minimal medium |CITS: [17012394]|.
                     |FRAME: CPD0-1152| (N5-Pan), a pantothenate analogue, is a 
                     potent inhibitor of <i>E. coli</i> growth.  The compound 
                     and its derivatives are accepted with high efficiency 
                     (10-fold faster than pantothenate) by the last five enzymes
                     of |FRAME: COA-PWY CoA biosynthesis| pathway, forming 
                     |FRAME: CPD-26636|, an analogue of |FRAME: CO-A| |CITS: 
                     [12372838]|.
                     The main mechanism by which N5-Pan inhibits growth of <i>E.
                     coli</i> is by binding of |FRAME: CPD-26636| to PanZ, which
                     results in loss of its ability to activate self-cleavage by
                     |FRAME: ASPDECARBOX-MONOMER PanD|, resulting in inhibition 
                     of |FRAME: B-ALANINE| synthesis and as a result, a 
                     defficiency of CoA |CITS: [28832133]|. <i>panZ</i> belongs 
                     to a network of genes which facilitate stress-induced 
                     mutagenesis (SIM) in <i>E. coli</i> K-12 |CITS: 
                     [23224554]|.
                     PanZ: ""<b>pan</b>thothenate"" |CITS: [23170229]|"
                     /translation="MKLTIIRLEKFSDQDRIDLQKIWPEYSPSSLQVDDNHRIYAARFN
                     ERLLAAVRVTLSGTEGALDSLRVREVTRRRGVGQYLLEEVLRNNPGVSCWWMADAGVED
                     RGVMTAFMQALGFTAQQGGWEKC"
