     gene            3602577..3603242
                     /gene="yhhQ"
                     /locus_tag="b3471"
                     /label=yhhQ
     CDS             3602577..3603242
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yhhQ"
                     /locus_tag="b3471"
                     /product="bifunctional queuosine precursor transporter / 
                     7-cyano-7-deazaguanine transporter"
                     /label=yhhQ
                     /note="YhhQ is an inner membrane protein implicated in the 
                     uptake of queuosine (Q) precursors - 7-cyano-7-deazaguanine
                     (|FRAME: 7-CYANO-7-DEAZAGUANINE ""preQ<sub>0</sub>""|) and 
                     7-aminomethyl-7-deazaguanine (|FRAME: 
                     7-AMINOMETHYL-7-DEAZAGUANINE ""preQ<sub>1</sub>""|) - for Q
                     salvage.
                     Q-modified tRNA is absent in &Delta;|FRAME: G7431 
                     ""<i>queD</i>""| and &Delta;<i>queD</i> &Delta;<i>yhhQ</i> 
                     strains grown in minimal media with glycerol; Q-modified 
                     tRNA is detected when a &Delta;<i>queD</i> strain is grown 
                     in minimal media plus 10 nM preQ<sub>0</sub> or 
                     preQ<sub>1</sub> but is absent when a &Delta;<i>queD</i> 
                     &Delta;<i>yhhQ</i> strain is grown under these conditions 
                     |CITS: [28208705]|. <i>yhhQ</i> expressed from a plasmid 
                     restores the presence of Q-modified tRNA in a 
                     &Delta;<i>queD</i> &Delta;<i>yhhQ</i> strain |CITS: 
                     [28208705]|.
                     Cleavage of <i>yhhQ</i> mRNA by |FRAME: CPLX0-3281| appears
                     to accelerate its degradation |CITS: [28351917]|; a 5' UTR 
                     antisense RNA |CITS: [24453212]| might be required to show 
                     cleavage <i>in vitro</i> |CITS: [28351917]|.
                     A class I type III pre-Q<sub>1</sub> 
                     (preQ<sub>1</sub>-I<sub>III</sub>)-sensing riboswitch in 
                     the 5' leader region of <i>yhhQ</i> mRNA is implicated in 
                     translation control |CITS: [37660906]|.
                     YhhQ is prediced to be an inner membrane protein with six 
                     transmembrane domains; topology analysis suggests the 
                     C-terminus is located in the cytoplasm |CITS: [15919996]|. 
                     <i>yhhQ</i> is predicted to be a member of the purine 
                     (PurR) regulon |CITS: [12391881]|.
                     In the Transporter Classification Database, YhhQ is a 
                     member of the Vitamin Uptake Transporter (VUT) family 
                     |CITS: [26546518]|."
                     /translation="MNVFSQTQRYKALFWLSLFHLLVITSSNYLVQLPVSILGFHTTWG
                     AFSFPFIFLATDLTVRIFGAPLARRIIFAVMIPALLISYVISSLFYMGSWQGFGALAHF
