     gene            complement(3603876..3605093)
                     /gene="yhhS"
                     /locus_tag="b3473"
                     /label=yhhS
     CDS             complement(3603876..3605093)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yhhS"
                     /locus_tag="b3473"
                     /product="putative transporter YhhS"
                     /label=yhhS
                     /note="The YhhS protein is an uncharacterised member of
                     the major facilitator superfamily (MFS) of transporters 
                     |CITS: [9529885][26546518]|.
                     Overexpression of both a full-length <i>yhhS</i> and a 
                     truncated <i>yhhS</i> (containing 7 of the putative 12 
                     membrane spanning domains) confers resistance to the 
                     herbicide, glyphosate and permits growth of cells in the 
                     presence of 15mM glyphosate |CITS: [22089966]|. 
                     Overexpression of <i>yhhS</i> reduces the intracellular 
                     accumulation of labeled glyphosate |CITS: [22089966]|. YhhS
                     has been implicated in arabinose efflux |CITS: [22952739]|.
                     Accumulation of the cationic fluorescent dye 
                     3,3'-dipropylthiadicarbocyanine iodide (diS-C3) is greater 
                     in <i>yhhS</i> knockout cells compared to wild type |CITS: 
                     [31438868]|.
                     This partially characterized enzyme was found to interact 
                     with the |FRAME: PGK| enzyme in glycolysis in a large 
                     assessment of protein-protein interactions (PPIs) |CITS: 
                     [33917325]|."
