     CDS             3606329..3606916
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="acpT"
                     /locus_tag="b3475"
                     /product="bifunctional holo-[acyl carrier protein]
                     synthase 2 / holo-[acyl carrier protein] synthase"
                     /EC_number="2.7.8.7"
                     /label=acpT
                     /note="The carrier protein substrates of AcpT have been 
                     identified in <I>E. coli</I> O157:H7
                     strain EDL933 as Z4853 and Z4854, two proteins in O-island 
                     138 which appears to
                     contain genes for fatty-acid biosynthesis 
                     |CITS:[16824108]|.  O-island 138 has been
                     deleted from a K-12 ancestor,  but <I>acpT</I> has been 
                     retained possibly because
                     AcpT allows slow growth in the absence of AcpS activity 
                     |CITS:[16824108]|.
                     Overexpression of <I>acpT</I> suppresses an <I>acpS</I> 
                     mutation
                     |CITS:[10625633]|.  Overexpression of <I>acpT</I> also 
                     suppresses the lethality of
                     <I>yejM</I> null mutants, as well as the temperature 
                     sensitivity of
                     <I>yejM</I>G570A mutants 
                     |CITS:[18245839],[9168603],[9025280]|.  This
                     suppression does not require phosphopantetheinyl 
                     transferase activity because a
                     mutant lacking this activity was still able to suppress the
                     temperature sensitivity of
                     the <I>yejM</I>G570A mutant |CITS:[18245839]|.
                     "
