     CDS             3628201..3629253
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yhiM"
                     /locus_tag="b3491"
                     /product="inner membrane protein YhiM"
                     /label=yhiM
                     /note="Expression of <i>yhiM</i> is negatively regulated
                     by trimethylamine N-oxide (TMAO) via the TorR 
                     transcriptional regulator |CITS: [12657056]|. Expression of
                     <i>yhiM</i> is induced under acid stress |CITS: 
                     [12426343]|.  Transposon insertion mutants of <i>E.coli 
                     yhiM</i> are unable to grow at pH 2.5 |CITS: [22327802]|. 
                     YhiM is necessary for RpoS, glutamine and lysine-dependent 
                     acid resistance but is not required for arginine-dependent 
                     acid resistance |CITS: [22327802]|.
                     YhiM is predicted to be an inner membrane protein with ten 
                     membrane spanning domains; experimental topology analysis 
                     suggests the C terminus is located in the cytoplasm |CITS: 
                     [15919996]|."
