                     /product="bifunctional ribosomal dihydrouridine synthase A
                     / dihydrouridine synthase"
                     /label=rdsA
                     /note="The RdsA is responsible for the dihydrouridylation
                     of uridine 2449 in |FRAME: 23S-rRNAs|.
                     Using the rhodamine labelling method (Rho-seq) for 
                     detecting dihydrouridine (D) in position 2449 of 23S rRNAs 
                     and rRNA from various mutant <i>E. coli</i> strains, only 
                     the &Delta;<i>rdsA</i> BW25113 strain lacked D2449. 
                     Characterization of RdsA using an AlphaFold model and 
                     homologous structures found it to be a flavoprotein with a 
                     conserved FAD binding pocket that binds FAD noncovalently 
                     |CITS: [39078675]|.
                     Kinetic analyses measured NADH rather than NADPH oxidase 
                     activity with hydride transfer being the likely chemical 
                     mechanism |CITS: [39078675]|.
                     RdsA = <u>r</u>ibosomal <u>d</u>ihydrouridine 
                     <u>s</u>ynthase <u>A</u>"
