     gene            complement(3632745..3633080)
                     /gene="uspB"
                     /locus_tag="b3494"
                     /label=uspB
     CDS             complement(3632745..3633080)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="uspB"
                     /locus_tag="b3494"
                     /product="universal stress protein B"
                     /label=uspB
                     /note="UspB plays a role in the RuvABC recombination
                     repair pathway |CITS: [20817623]| and is required for 
                     wild-type ethanol tolerance in stationary phase |CITS: 
                     [9829921]|.
                     UspB is an inner membrane protein with two predicted 
                     transmembrane domains.  The C terminus is located in the 
                     periplasm |CITS: [15919996]|.
                     A <i>uspB</i> mutant exhibits ethanol sensitivity, but not 
                     heat sensitivity, in stationary phase |CITS: [9829921]|.
                     A <i>uspB</i> mutant shows increased sensitivity to DNA 
                     damaging agents and phenocopies a <i>ruvC</i> mutant; 
                     overexpression of <i>ruvC</i> suppresses the UV-sensitive 
                     growth phenotype of the <i>uspB</i> mutant |CITS: 
                     [20817623]|.  Overproduction of UspB results in stationary 
                     phase inviability |CITS: [9829921]|.
                     <i>uspB</i> is transcribed under stress conditions 
                     including starvation; it depends on &sigma;<sup>S</sup> and
                     is influenced by H-NS |CITS: [9829921]|.  Expression also 
                     requires the presence of ppGpp |CITS: [10747855]|, but is 
                     not induced by UV stress |CITS: [20817623]|. <i>uspB</i> 
                     mRNA stability during glucose starvation is diminished in 
                     the absence of |FRAME: CPLX0-3281| function |CITS: 
                     [16309817]|.  In a long-term evolution experiment under 
                     freeze-thaw-growth (FTG) conditions, an IS<i>150</i> 
                     insertion in the 5' UTR of <i>uspB</i> was recovered 
                     multiple times and shown to be beneficial under the FTG 
                     regime.  The IS<i>150</i> insertion reduces <i>uspB</i> 
                     transcription |CITS: [18757947]|.  In a long-term evolution
                     experiment growing on lactose, an IS<i>150</i> insertion 
                     upstream of <i>uspB</i> appears to cause a reduced benefit 
                     of <i>lacI</i> mutations on fitness |CITS: [33744956]|.
                     The <i>uspB</i> promoter has been evaluated for expression 
                     of heterologous genes |CITS: 
                     [12740005][12764564][12827701]|.
                     UspB: ""<b>u</b>niversal <b>s</b>tress <b>p</b>rotein 
                     <b>B</b>"" |CITS: [9829921]|
                     Review: |CITS: [16159755]|
                     "
