     CDS             3634222..3635691
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="dtpB"
                     /locus_tag="b3496"
                     /product="trifunctional dipeptide/tripeptide:H(+)
                     symporter DtpB / transport of a tripeptide / transport of a
                     dipeptide"
                     /label=dtpB
                     /note="The DtpB protein is a member of the POT
                     (proton-dependent oligopeptide transporter) family of 
                     peptide transporters |CITS:[7817396]|. DtpB is responsible 
                     for proton-dependent transport of di- and tripeptides as 
                     well as some structurally related peptidomimetics like 
                     B-lactam antibiotics |CITS: [18485005]|.  DtpB transports 
                     the tetrapeptide, tetraalanine <i>in vitro</i> |CITS: 
                     [24440353]| however tetraalanine does not function as an 
                     inhibitor in competitive transport assays |CITS: 
                     [18485005]|. DtpB shows a preference for di- and 
                     tripeptides composed of L amino acids and for peptides 
                     containing a positively charged side chain in the 
                     N-terminal position |CITS: [18485005]|.
                     YhiP is predicted to contain 14 transmembrane regions with 
                     the C-terminus located in the cytoplasm |CITS: [15919996]|.
                     The dipeptide/tripeptide:proton symporters DtpB and |FRAME:
                     B1634-MONOMER DtpA| are receptors for the group 6 
                     contact-dependent growth inhibition (CDI) ionophore toxins 
                     |CITS: [39591464]|.
                     <i>dtpB</I>: <U>d</U>ipeptide and <U>t</U>ripeptide 
                     <U>p</U>ermease B |CITS: [18485005]|"
