                     /product="16S rRNA m(2)G1516 methyltransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.1.1.242"
                     /label=rsmJ
                     /note="RsmJ is the methyltransferase responsible for
                     methylation of 16S rRNA at the N2 position of the G1516 
                     nucleotide.  <i>In vitro</i>, the enzyme can methylate 16S 
                     rRNA within the 30S ribosomal subunit, but not free 16S 
                     rRNA |CITS: [22079366]|.
                     <i>prlC-rsmJ</i> is a heat shock operon regulated by RpoH 
                     |CITS: [16818608]|.  An <i>rsmJ</i> mutant strain is cold 
                     sensitive, showing a growth defect at 16&deg;C |CITS: 
                     [22079366]|."
