     gene            complement(3641065..3641148)
                     /gene="dinQ"
                     /locus_tag="b4613"
                     /label=dinQ
     CDS             complement(3641065..3641148)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="dinQ"
                     /locus_tag="b4613"
                     /product="membrane toxin DinQ"
                     /label=dinQ
                     /note="<i>dinQ</i> encodes a small (27 amino acid) toxic
                     protein that localises to the inner membrane in <i> E. 
                     coli</i> K-12. DinQ is predicted to contain a single 
                     transmembrane region. <i>dinQ-agrAB</I> may be a type I 
                     toxin-antitoxin system in <i>E.coli</i> K-12 |CITS: 
                     [23408903]|.
                     <i>dinQ</i> expression is controlled by the |FRAME: 
                     RNA0-380 ""AgrB small RNA""|. The <i>agrB</i> transcript 
                     counteracts the UV sensitivity induced by <i>dinQ</i> 
                     expression. The two small non-coding RNAs - <i>agrA</i> and
                     <i>agrB</i> - both contain a region of antisense 
                     complementarity to <i>dinQ</i> |CITS: [23408903]|.
                     The phenotype of augmented DinQ in an <i>agrB</i> deleted 
                     strain has been studied. DinQ is involved in nucleoid 
                     compaction and reorganisation during UV exposure. DinQ 
                     modulates conjugal recombination. Overexpression of 
                     <i>dinQ</i> depolarises the cell membrane and decreases the
                     intracellular ATP concentration |CITS: [23408903]|.
                     A <i>dinQ</i> ORF of 150 bp was previously annotated. 
                     |CITS: [23408903]| later reported that biologically active 
                     DinQ is translated from post-transcriptionally modified 
                     <i>dinQ</i> RNA. <i>dinQ</i> is translated from an 
                     alternate GTG start codon |CITS: [23408903]|.
                     Expression of <i>dinQ</i> is DNA damage-inducible and 
                     appears to be regulated by LexA |CITS: [10760155]|. 
                     <i>dinQ</i>: <U>d</U>amage <U>in</U>ducible protein
                     "
                     /translation="MIDKAIIVLGALIALLELIRFLLQLLN"
                     /go_component="plasma membrane [goid 0005886] [evidence
                     IEA] [GO_REF 0000044]"
                     /go_component="membrane [goid 0016020] [evidence IDA]
                     [PMID 23408903]"
                     /go_process="DNA damage response [goid 0006974] [evidence
                     IEP] [PMID 10760155]"
     gene            3641423..3641504
                     /gene="agrA"
                     /locus_tag="b4712"
                     /label=agrA
     misc_RNA        3641423..3641504
                     /gene="agrA"
                     /locus_tag="b4712"
                     /product="small RNA AgrA"
                     /note="AgrA is one of two small RNAs encoded in the 
                     <i>arsR-gor</i> intergenic region.  The second small RNA, 
                     AgrB, appears to be the antitoxin for the DinQ toxin |CITS:
                     [23408903]|.
                     <i>agrA</i> expression is increased in an <i>agrB</i> 
                     mutant |CITS: [23408903]|.
                     AgrA: <i><b>a</b>rsR-<b>g</b>or</i> <b>r</b>egion gene 
                     <b>A</b> |CITS: [23408903]|
                     Review: |CITS: [32213244]|"
     gene            3641654..3641735
                     /gene="agrB"
                     /locus_tag="b4713"
                     /label=agrB
     misc_RNA        3641654..3641735
                     /gene="agrB"
                     /locus_tag="b4713"
                     /product="small regulatory RNA AgrB"
                     /note="AgrB is one of two small RNAs encoded in the 
                     <i>arsR-gor</i> intergenic region and appears to be the 
                     antitoxin of the type I DinQ-AgrB toxin-antitoxin system 
                     |CITS: [23408903][27651528]|.  AgrB interaction with the 
                     +44 processed transcript of <i>dinQ</i> stabilizes an 
                     alternative secondary structure of the <i>dinQ</i> mRNA 
                     that occludes the ribosome binding site, inhibits 
                     translation, and mediates processing by RNase III |CITS: 
                     [27651528]|.
                     The AgrB small RNA appears to negatively regulate DinQ 
                     accumulation.  An <i>agrB</i> mutant shows increased 
                     sensitivity to UV light and has a lower growth rate than 
                     wild type; in addition, a shorter processed <i>dinQ</i> 
                     mRNA accumulates |CITS: [23408903]|.
                     AgrB: <i><b>a</b>rsR-<b>g</b>or</i> <b>r</b>egion gene 
                     <b>B</b> |CITS: [23408903]|
                     Review: |CITS: [32213244]|"
