     gene            3642295..3643584
                     /gene="arsB"
                     /locus_tag="b3502"
                     /label=arsB
     CDS             3642295..3643584
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="arsB"
                     /locus_tag="b3502"
                     /product="trifunctional arsenite/antimonite:H(+)
                     antiporter / antimonite:H(+) antiporter / arsenite:H(+) 
                     antiporter"
                     /label=arsB
                     /note="Based on sequence similarity with the R773-plasmid 
                     encoded arsenite resistance operon, ArsB is a transporter 
                     and ArsC is an arsenate reductase |CITS:[7860609]|.  The 
                     chromosomally encoded operon, however, lacks <I>arsA</I>, 
                     which encodes a putative ATP-binding protein 
                     |CITS:[7860609]|.  Transport through ArsB occurs through a 
                     metalloid:proton antiport mechanism |CITS:[14970228]|. 
                     Expression of <I>arsA</I> from the R773 plasmid increases 
                     resistance to As(III) and Sb(III) showing ArsB can act 
                     alone in metalloid:proton antiport or as part of an 
                     ATP-dependent ABC transporter |CITS:[14970228]|. Antimonite
                     stimulates uptake of arsenite, but arsenite inhibits uptake
                     of antimonite suggesting co-transport of the two compounds 
                     possibly as six-membered, co-polymer rings 
                     |CITS:[14970228]|.
                     Deletion mutants of the chromosomal <I>arsRBC</I> operon 
                     exhibit 10-20 times more sensitivity to arsenite and 5-10 
                     times more sensitivity to antimonite and arsenate than the 
                     parental strain |CITS:[7860609]|.  Expression of the cloned
                     <I>arsRBC</I> conferred increased arsenite, arsenate, and 
                     antimonite resistance compared with wild-type as well as 
                     when expressed in an <I>arsRBC</I> deletion strain 
                     |CITS:[7860609],[7721697]|.  Accumulation of arsenite in 
                     cells increased upon deletion of <I>arsRBC</I> and then 
                     decreased upon expression of <I>arsRBC</I> from a plasmid 
                     |CITS:[7860609]|.
                     Expression of <I>arsRBC</I> is induced by antimonite 
                     |CITS:[7860609]|, arsenate, and arsenite 
                     |CITS:[7721697],[7860609],[9342883]|.  ArsR acts as the 
                     repressor for the <I>arsRBC</I> operon |CITS:[8764681]|.
                     "
