     gene            3652352..3652442
                     /gene="gadF"
                     /locus_tag="b4718"
                     /label=gadF
     misc_RNA        3652352..3652442
                     /gene="gadF"
                     /locus_tag="b4718"
                     /product="small regulatory RNA GadF"
                     /note="GadF is a 91 nt small regulatory RNA that is
                     expressed in stationary phase and is generated by 
                     processing of the 3' end of the <i>gadE</i> mRNA. 
                     Overexpression of GadF leads to increased expression of 
                     <i>acrB</i> and <i>cfa</i> |CITS: [27588604]|.
                     Additional potential targets for GadF were identified by 
                     Hfq CLASH |CITS: [32356726]|.  The Hfq-dependent GadF and 
                     24 potential targets were also identified by applying a 
                     small RNA prediction algorithm to RIL-seq data |CITS: 
                     [34093460]|. The interaction of GadF with Hfq has been 
                     demonstrated |CITS: [36328526]|.
                     Review: |CITS: [32213244]|"
     gene            3652592..3653749
                     /gene="mdtE"
                     /locus_tag="b3513"
                     /label=mdtE
     CDS             3652592..3653749
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="mdtE"
                     /locus_tag="b3513"
                     /product="multifunctional multidrug efflux pump membrane
                     fusion protein MdtE / multidrug efflux pump MdtEF-TolC / 
                     deoxycholate efflux pump / erthromycin efflux pump / 
                     ethidium efflux pump"
                     /label=mdtE
                     /note="MdtE is the membrane fusion protein of a putative 
                     tripartite efflux pump complex; production of the complex 
                     (through expression of cloned <i>mdtEF</i> genes) confers 
                     some degree of resistance to various toxic compounds in 
                     laboratory strains of <i>E. coli</i> K-12 (see |FRAME: 
                     TRANS-CPLX-204| for more detail).
                     Production of MdtE does not complement the efflux defect of
                     <i>E. coli</i> strain HNCE3 (nonpolar &Delta;<i>acrA</i>) 
                     (|CITS: [12949086]|.
                     MdtE is a member of the Membrane Fusion Protein (MFP) 
                     family |CITS: [26546518]|.
                     MdtE was isolated as a homotrimer in inner membrane 
                     vesicles purified from <i>E. coli</i> strain BL21 |CITS: 
                     [16079137]|.
                     Exposure to synthetic reactive oxygen species (ROS) 
                     generated from synthetron radiation (X-ray) results in 
                     oxidation of methionine residues <i>in vivo</i> in hundreds
                     of proteins. The % modification was highest in MdtE, 
                     |FRAME: EG11009-MONOMER TolC| and |FRAME: EG10855-MONOMER| 
                     and increased as the X-ray oxidation dose increased |CITS: 
                     [40199130]|."
