     CDS             3653774..3656887
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="mdtF"
                     /locus_tag="b3514"
                     /product="multifunctional multidrug efflux pump RND
                     permease MdtF / multidrug efflux pump MdtEF-TolC / 
                     deoxycholate efflux pump / erthromycin efflux pump / 
                     ethidium efflux pump"
                     /label=mdtF
                     /note="MdtF is the inner membrane subunit of a putative 
                     tripartite efflux complex; production of the complex 
                     (through expression of cloned <i>mdtEF</i> genes) confers 
                     some degree of resistance to various toxic compounds in 
                     laboratory strains of <i>E. coli</i> K-12 (see |FRAME: 
                     TRANS-CPLX-204| for more detail).
                     MdtF can function with the AcrA membrane fusion protein for
                     efflux of bile salts (cholate, taurocholate), dyes (crystal
                     violet, ethidium bromide) and antibiotics (novobiocin, 
                     ciprofloxacin, eerythromycin) |CITS: [12949086]|. 
                     <i>mdtF</i> expressed from a plasmid can complement the 
                     steroid hormone efflux deficient phenotype of a strain 
                     lacking both AcrB and EmrAB |CITS: [16428427]| MdtF was 
                     isolated as a homotrimer in inner membrane vesicles 
                     purified from <i>E. coli</i> strain BL21 |CITS: [16079137]|
                     MdtF belongs to the Hydrophobe/Amphiphile Efflux-1 (HAE1) 
                     family of transporters within the 
                     resistance-nodulation-cell division (RND) superfamily 
                     |CITS: [11566977][26546518]|.
                     A &Delta;<i>mdtF</i> mutant shows increased persister cell 
                     formation under antibiotic stress |CITS: [22221537]|. The 
                     <i>mdtF</i> Keio collection mutant (BW25113 
                     &Delta;<i>mdtF::kan</i>) shows a significant increase in 
                     swimming motility |CITS: [39529380]|.
                     <i>mdtF</i> is one of 35 efflux-encoding genes that have 
                     been deleted or inactivated in 'Efflux KnockOut-35' 
                     (EKO-35) -  a K-12 BW25133-derived strain that lacks 35 
                     efflux pumps and can be used as a platform to study their 
                     function |CITS: [36065018][36318669]|."
