                     /product="bifunctional cytoplasmic trehalase / trehalase"
                     /EC_number="3.2.1.28"
                     /label=treF
                     /note="<i>E. coli</i> contains two trehalases: the
                     cytoplasmic TreF (discussed here) and the periplasmic 
                     |FRAME: TREHALAPERI-MONOMER ""TreA""|.  Both enzymes 
                     catalyze the hydrolysis of trehalose into two molecules of 
                     D-glucose.
                     Transcription of <i>treF</i> is only weakly induced by high
                     osmolarity and partially dependent on the stationary-phase 
                     alternative sigma factor RpoS |CITS: [8892826]|.  Under 
                     aerobic conditions, TreF protein is induced more than 
                     20-fold by high osmolarity |CITS: [17015655]|."
