     CDS             complement(3664652..3665254)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yhjB"
                     /locus_tag="b3520"
                     /product="putative DNA-binding transcriptional regulator
                     YhjB"
                     /label=yhjB
                     /note="YhjB belongs to the NarL family of response
                     regulators of two-component regulatory systems; no cognate 
                     histidine kinase has been identified.  <i>In vitro</i>, 
                     YhjB enhanced the dephosphorylation of several non-cognate 
                     histidine kinase proteins |CITS: [15522865]|.
                     On the other hand, it was suggested that YhjB belongs to 
                     the LuxR family of transcription factors, and it was 
                     predicted to regulate genes related to metabolism |CITS: 
                     [35880217]|.
                     Genome-wide YhjB binding sites were determined <i>in 
                     vivo</i> by the chromatin immunoprecipitation method 
                     combined with lambda exonuclease digestion (ChIP-exo) in 
                     glucose M9 minimal medium |CITS: [34428301]|.
                     Upstream of the <i>yhjB</i> gene, a sequence was found that
                     could work as a transcriptional promoter, and the 
                     transcription of the <i>yhjB</i> gene is affected by 
                     oxidative stress and glucose-lactose shift |CITS: 
                     [35880217]|.
                     "
