     CDS             3665774..3666673
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rcdB"
                     /locus_tag="b3521"
                     /product="putative DNA-binding transcriptional regulator
                     YhjC"
                     /label=rcdB
                     /note="YhjC was predicted to be a LysR-type transcription
                     factor |CITS: [34428301] [35880217]|. This protein contains
                     a helix-turn-helix motif to bind DNA in its N-terminal 
                     domain, and it was predicted that this protein regulates 
                     genes related to metabolism and antibiotic sensitivity 
                     |CITS: [35880217]|.
                     Genome-wide YhjC binding sites were determined <i>in 
                     vivo</i> by the chromatin immunoprecipitation method 
                     combined with lambda exonuclease digestion (ChIP-exo) in 
                     glucose M9 minimal medium |CITS: [34428301]|.
                     The YhjC binding landscape was globally mapped in vivo by 
                     standardized ChIP-seq and quantitatively modeled using 
                     BoltzNet, a biophysically informed neural network that 
                     infers binding energy from sequence data |CITS:[40335485]|.
                     The resulting ChIP-seq binding regions are available in 
                     RegulonDB (<a href=""https://regulondb.cc 
                     g.unam.mx/ht/dataset/TFBINDING/source=GALAGAN"">Galagan 
                     collection</a>), and the corresponding energy matrix and 
                     genomic binding profiles can be accessed at <a 
                     href=""http://boltznet.bu.edu"">boltznet.bu.edu</a> 
                     |CITS:[40335485]|.
                     Transcription of the <i>yhjC</i> gene is affected by 
                     temperature |CITS: [35880217]|."
