                     /product="putative transporter YhjE"
                     /label=yhjE
                     /note="In the Transporter Classification Database |CITS: 
                     [33170213][9529885]|, YhjE is an uncharacterised member of 
                     the Metabolite:H+ Symporter (MHS) Family within the Major 
                     Facilitator Superfamily (MFS). Deletion of <i>yhjE</i> in a
                     strain (&Delta;<i>cydB</i>::Km<sup>S</sup>/&Delta;<i>app 
                     B</i>::Km<sup>R</sup>) that is dependent solely on |FRAME: 
                     CYT-O-UBIOX-CPLX| for respiratory growth, results in an 
                     aerobic growth defect; cytochrome <i>bo</i><sub>3</sub> 
                     oxidase activity is significantly reduced and its <i>b</i>-
                     and <i>o</i>-type hemes cannot be detected |CITS: 
                     [37862358]|. |CITS: [37862358]|. Deletion of <i>yhjE</i> in
                     an otherwise wild-type background perturbs iron (but not 
                     copper) homeostasis |CITS: [37862358]|.
                     ArcA appears to activate <i>yhjE</i> expression under 
                     anaerobiosis. A putative ArcA binding site is located 202 
                     bp upstream of this gene |CITS: [15699038]|"
