     gene            complement(3671780..3672547)
                     /gene="pdeH"
                     /locus_tag="b3525"
                     /label=pdeH
     CDS             complement(3671780..3672547)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="pdeH"
                     /locus_tag="b3525"
                     /product="bifunctional cyclic di-GMP phosphodiesterase
                     PdeH / cyclic di-GMP phosphodiesterase"
                     /EC_number="3.1.4.52"
                     /label=pdeH
                     /note="Curli amyloid fibers are thin, coiled surface
                     structures composed of a polymer of a single type of 
                     subunit, |FRAME: EG11489-MONOMER|, encoded by the |FRAME: 
                     EG11489| gene |CITS: [2649795][8459772]|. Curli are the key
                     component of the extracellular matrix produced during 
                     biofilm formation by <i>Escherichia coli</i> and related 
                     <i>Enterobacteriaceae</i> and are involved in inert surface
                     colonization, biofilm formation, and bacterial binding to a
                     variety of extracellular matrix and serum proteins |CITS: 
                     [1357528][9457880][11823641][12819107][30305312]|.
                     PdeH is a c-di-GMP phosphodiesterase involved in regulation
                     of the switch from flagellar motility to sessile behavior 
                     and curli expression at the end of exponential growth 
                     |CITS: [18765794]|. PdeH belongs to the core set of eight 
                     GGDEF/EAL domain proteins that is absolutely conserved in a
                     set of 61 <i>E. coli</i> genomes containing pathogenic, 
                     commensal and probiotic strains |CITS: [26303830]|.
                     Curli production is controlled by a complex signaling 
                     cascade, with the |FRAME: EG12396 DgcE|/|FRAME: EG12252 
                     PdeH| diguanylate cyclase (DGC)/phosphodiesterase (PDE) 
                     pair acting upstream of |FRAME: G6639 PdeR|, which itself 
                     is upstream of the DGC |FRAME: G6673 DgcM|, and all acting 
                     upstream of the |FRAME: EG12008 ""MlrA transcription 
                     factor""|. MlrA controls expression of |FRAME: G6546 ""CsgD
                     transcriptional regulator""|, which controls the 
                     transcription of the |FRAME: TU00390| operon, encoding 
                     curli production |CITS: [23708798]|.
                     Curli expression is heterogeneous - it does not occur 
                     within all cells that occupy the same position within a 
                     biofilm |CITS: [23359678][23512962][27761132][30954572]|. 
                     This bimodal expression was also observed in a well-stirred
                     planktonic culture, indicating that it is not due to 
                     microenvironmental gradients |CITS: [37186613]|. Removal of
                     the regulatory network does not abolish the bimodality of 
                     curli gene expression |CITS: [37186613]|. Overexpression of
                     PdeH suppresses the flagellar motility defect of an 
                     <i>hns</i> mutant |CITS: [11031114]|. A <i>pdeH</i> mutant 
                     shows strongly reduced motility on soft agar |CITS: 
                     [18765794][17941710]| and increased curli expression |CITS:
                     [18765794]|. Depending on the growth temperature, mutations
                     in <i>dgcE</i>, <i>dgcQ</i> and <i>dgcJ</i> partially 
                     suppress the motility defect of a <i>pdeH</i> mutant; 
                     double or triple mutants are required to fully restore 
                     motility to the <i>pdeH</i><sup>-</sup> mutant |CITS: 
                     [18765794]|. A screen for suppressors of the motility 
                     defect of a &Delta;<i>pdeH</i> mutant identified activating
                     mutations in <i>E. coli</i>'s alternative c-di-GMP 
                     phosphodiesterases (PDEs). This supports a model whereby 
                     the signaling specificity of PDEs is the result of 
                     environmental signals required for their activation |CITS: 
                     [26553851]|.
                     Deletion of <i>pdeH</i> resulted in different effects on 
                     swimming vs swarming |CITS: [20346719]|. An RNAseq 
                     experiment found that expression of <i>pdeH</i> was 
                     significantly downregulated during swarming |CITS: 
                     [40326769]|.
                     Transcription is regulated by FlhDC |CITS: [11031114]|. 
                     Expression of <i>pdeH</i> is highest during late 
                     exponential growth and is negatively regulated by 
                     &sigma;<sup>S</sup>. Expression of <i>pdeH</i> is lower 
                     during growth on solid medium than in liquid medium |CITS: 
                     [19332833]|.
                     PdeH: ""<b>p</b>hospho<b>d</b>i<b>e</b>sterase <b>H</b>"" 
                     |CITS: [26148715]|
                     Review: |CITS: [22226726][23057745]|"
                     /translation="MIRQVIQRISNPEASIESLQERRFWLQCERAYTWQPIYQTCGRLM
