     gene            complement(3688593..3689345)
                     /pseudo
                     /gene="bcsQ"
                     /locus_tag="b3534"
                     /label=bcsQ
                     /note="In the commensal cellulose-producing <i>E. coli</i> 
                     strain 1094, BcsQ is required for cellulose production and 
                     localizes to the cell poles |CITS: [19400787]|.
                     In <i>E. coli</i> K-12 strains such as W3110 and MG1655, a 
                     ""domesticating SNP"" consists of a point mutation that 
                     introduces a stop codon after the first 5 amino acids of 
                     the wild-type <i>bcsQ</i> ORF.  Additionally, the 
                     domesticating SNP lowers expression of both <i>bcsQ</i> and
                     the downstream <i>bcsA</i> gene.  After repairing the SNP, 
                     the resulting ""de-domesticated"" W3110 derivative produces
                     cellulose and has dramatically altered biofilm morphology. 
                     A &Delta;<i>bcsQ</i> mutation introduced into this strain 
                     leads to loss of cellulose biosynthesis |CITS: [24097954]| 
                     (see also |CITS: [31604608]|).
                     BcsQ belongs to the ParA family of ATPases which also 
                     includes MinD.  The N-terminal predicted ATP-binding domain
                     of BcsQ (in strain 1094) is required for function, but not 
                     for the polar localization of the protein, while the 
                     C-terminal domain contributes to both localization and 
                     function in cellulose biosynthesis |CITS: [19400787]|. In 
                     the cellulose producing strain <i>E. coli</i> 1094, the 
                     inner membrane and cytosolic Bcs proteins - BcsA, BcsB, 
                     BscQ, BcsG, BcsE, BcsR and BcsF - organize in a 
                     multisubunit, stable macrocomplex; two-hybrid assays 
                     identified multiple direct interactions between the 
                     subunits and a low resolution structure has been obtained 
                     |CITS: [29234007]| (see also |CITS: [33712813]|).
                     A <i>bcsQ</i> mutant was seen to exhibit filamentous 
                     morphology, heterogeneous cell size, and a defect in 
                     chromosome partitioning |CITS: [12382054]|, but |CITS: 
                     [19400787]| was unable to reproduce these phenotypes. BcsQ:
                     ""<b>b</b>acterial <b>c</b>ellulose <b>s</b>ynthesis""
                     Related review: |CITS: [26077867]|"
     CDS             complement(3688593..3689345)
