     gene            complement(3699458..3701065)
                     /gene="dppA"
                     /locus_tag="b3544"
                     /label=dppA
     CDS             complement(3699458..3701065)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="dppA"
                     /locus_tag="b3544"
                     /product="bifunctional dipeptide ABC transporter
                     periplasmic binding protein / dipeptide ABC transporter"
                     /EC_number="7.4.2.9"
                     /label=dppA
                     /note="DppA is the periplasmic binding protein of a
                     dipeptide ABC transport system.
                     <i>dppA</i> mutation results in the inability of a proline 
                     auxotroph to utilize Pro-Gly as a proline source; DppA 
                     accumulates to high levels when <i>E. coli</i> K-12 strain 
                     JM101 is grown in minimal medium; osmotic shock treatment 
                     releases DppA into the supernatant |CITS: [1702779]|. 
                     Purified DppA binds ala-ala and ala-phe dipeptides with a 
                     1:1 stoichiometry and substrate specificity has been tested
                     through competitive binding assays; tripeptides are poor 
                     substrates as are dipeptides containing one or more D 
                     residues |CITS: [10537211]|. Purified DppA binds heme 
                     |CITS: [16905647]|.
                     Crystal structures of 'open', unliganded DppA (two 
                     &alpha;/&beta; domains separated by a cleft and connected 
                     by two hinge segments) and 'closed' DppA with bound 
                     glycyl-L-leucine (three &alpha;/&beta; domains; domains I 
                     and III connected by 2 strands; dipeptide ligand buried 
                     completely) have been reported |CITS: 
                     [8496961][8527431][8563629]|. The DppA binding site 
                     recognizes the peptide backbone while allowing for 
                     accommodation of various side chains |CITS:[8563629]|. DppA
                     is required for dipeptide chemotaxis |CITS: 
                     [3520334][1956284]|.
                     Overproduction of DppA stabilises a highly unstable MBP 
                     mutant; purified DppA inhibits the aggregation of 
                     &alpha;-lactalbumin |CITS: [26003922]|.
                     <i>dppA</i> expression is regulated by the small, 
                     non-translated RNA |FRAME: GCVB-RNA ""GcvB""| |CITS: 
                     [10972807][18312576][19118352]|. DppA levels increase in 
                     response to glucose-limitation |CITS: [11683869]|; DppA 
                     levels decrease after 4 hours exposure to zinc stress 
                     |CITS: [17122063]|.  DppA levels decrease in response to 
                     phosphate limitation; a putative Pho box is located 
                     upstream of <i>dppA</i> |CITS: [1478454]|."
