     gene            complement(3704159..3705367)
                     /gene="yhjX"
                     /locus_tag="b3547"
                     /label=yhjX
     CDS             complement(3704159..3705367)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yhjX"
                     /locus_tag="b3547"
                     /product="putative transporter YhjX"
                     /label=yhjX
                     /note="Expression of <i>yhjX</i> is induced in cells 
                     over-producing the |FRAME: G7244-MONOMER| |CITS: 
                     [23222720]|. A <i>yhjX-lux</i> reporter construct is not 
                     expressed in a <i>pyrSRypdC</i> deletion mutant; 
                     <i>yhj-lux</i> expression is induced in response to 
                     pyruvate and in medium containing gluconate or glucuronate 
                     as the sole carbon source |CITS: [23222720]|. <i>yhjX</i> 
                     is expressed transiently at the onset of stationary phase 
                     during growth in an amino acid rich medium |CITS: 
                     [24659770]|. <i>yhjX</i> shows heterogeneous activation at 
                     the onset of stationary phase during growth in LB medium; 
                     the degree of heterogeneity is influenced by external 
                     pyruvate concentration |CITS: [29038258]|. The PyrR binding
                     site in the <i>yhjX</i> promoter has been characterised 
                     |CITS: [23222720]|.
                     In the Transporter Classification Database, YhjX is a 
                     member of the Oxalate:Formate Antiporter (OFA) Family 
                     within the Major Facilitator Superfamily (MFS) |CITS: 
                     [9529885][26546518]|. YhjX is implicated in pyruvate 
                     reassimilation in an <i>n</i>-butanol producing strain of 
                     <i>E. coli</i> |CITS: [28363967]|.
                     YhjX interacts with the sensor kinases |FRAME: 
                     G7243-MONOMER ""PyrS""| and |FRAME: EG12007-MONOMER 
                     ""BtsS""| and with the pyruvate:proton symporter |FRAME: 
                     G7942-MONOMER ""BtsT""|. YhjX is capable of 
                     homo-oligomerisation |CITS: [24659770]|.
                     <i>yhjX</i> is subject to CsrA derived post-transcriptional
                     regulation; <i>yhjX</i> mRNA contains a CsrA binding site 
                     and deletion of <i>csrA</i> prevents expression of a 
                     <i>yhjX</i> translational fusion |CITS: [24659770]|.
                     Expression of <i>yhjX</i> is highly induced upon 
                     overexpression of the toxic peptides ShoB, LdrD or IbsC 
                     |CITS: [18710431]|; expression is upregulated in response 
                     to cytoplasmic acid stress (generated by benzoate 
                     treatment) |CITS: [18302792]|.  A <i>yhjX-lux</i> reporter 
                     construct is not expressed under any of the aforementioned 
                     conditions |CITS: [23222720]|."
