     gene            complement(3707421..3709754)
                     /gene="bisC"
                     /locus_tag="b3551"
                     /label=bisC
     CDS             complement(3707421..3709754)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="bisC"
                     /locus_tag="b3551"
                     /product="bifunctional methionine-S-sulfoxide reductase /
                     biotin sulfoxide reductase"
                     /EC_number="1.8.4.13"
                     /label=bisC
                     /note="BisC was first identified as a biotin sulfoxide
                     reductase that reduces a spontaneous oxidation product of 
                     biotin, biotin-<i>d</i>-sulfoxide (BDS), back to biotin. 
                     The enzyme allows scavenging of BDS as a biotin source and 
                     may also protect the cell from oxidation damage |CITS: 
                     [2180922]|.
                     The other genes which were originally identified to be 
                     required for biotin sulfoxide reductase activity |CITS: 
                     [4579877]| are likely involved in the biosynthesis and 
                     insertion of the molybdenum cofactor |CITS: [6460021]|.  A 
                     small, heat-stable, thioredoxin-like protein functions as a
                     source for reducing equivalents and is required for biotin 
                     sulfoxide reductase activity |CITS: [6460021]|. BisC also 
                     exhibits methionine-<i>S</i>-sulfoxide reductase activity, 
                     acting specifically on the <i>S</i> enantiomer in the free,
                     but not the protein-bound form.  It thus plays a role in 
                     assimilation of oxidized methionines |CITS: [15601707]|.  
                     BisC was also found to make a minor contribution to 
                     detoxification of <i>N</i>-hydroxylated base analogs |CITS:
                     [18312271]|.
                     BisC: ""<b>bi</b>otin-<i>d</i>-<b>s</b>ulfoxide"" |CITS: 
                     [4579877]|
                     Review: |CITS: [17322183]|"
