                     /label=glyQ
                     /note="A crystal structure of GlyRS has been solved at
                     2.68 &Aring; resolution, revealing an unusual X-shaped 
                     architecture with an &alpha; subunit dimer at the center. 
                     The &alpha; subunit contains binding sites for glycine and 
                     ATP, while the &beta; subunit interacts with the 
                     &gamma;-phosphate of ATP.  Site-directed mutagenesis 
                     supported the proposed roles for the &alpha; and &beta; 
                     subunits |CITS: [34390350]|.
                     CfcA: ""<b>c</b>ontrol the <b>f</b>requency of <b>c</b>ell 
                     division"" |CITS: [2651881]|"
