     gene            3724491..3725483
                     /gene="xylF"
                     /locus_tag="b3566"
                     /label=xylF
     CDS             3724491..3725483
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="xylF"
                     /locus_tag="b3566"
                     /product="trifunctional xylose ABC transporter periplasmic
                     binding protein / xylose ABC transporter / transport of 
                     D-xylose"
                     /EC_number="7.5.2.10"
                     /label=xylF
                     /note="XylF is the periplasmic binding protein of an 
                     ATP-dependent, high-affinity xylose uptake system. Purified
                     XylF binds a sngle molecule of D-xylose with high affinity 
                     (K<sub>d</sub> = 0.6 &micro;M); XylF binds D-xylose 
                     specifically - in a wide range of sugars tested only 
                     methyl-&alpha;-D-xylofuranoside showed some inhibition of  
                     D-xylose binding |CITS: [7037773]|.
                     XylF consists of two similar globular domains connected by 
                     a three-stranded hinge; xylose (as the chair form 
                     &beta;-pyranose) binds in the cleft between the two domains
                     |CITS: [20678502]|. Based on the comparison of 
                     XylF-open-apo, XylF-open-xyl and XylF-closed-xyl crystal 
                     structures, a description of the conformational change that
                     accompanies ligand binding to XylF is available |CITS: 
                     [20678502]|."
