     gene            3733065..3734318
                     /gene="avtA"
                     /locus_tag="b3572"
                     /label=avtA
     CDS             3733065..3734318
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="avtA"
                     /locus_tag="b3572"
                     /product="bifunctional valine--pyruvate aminotransferase / 
                     2-oxobutanoate aminotransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.6.1.66"
                     /label=avtA
                     /note="Valine-pyruvate aminotransferase (transaminase C) 
                     catalyzes the transamination reaction that converts 
                     &alpha;-keto-isovalerate to valine and alanine to pyruvate 
                     |CITS: [4616947][7040341]|.  This makes it the effective 
                     last step in potential synthetic routes to both alanine and
                     valine.  Transaminase C may also catalyze the 
                     interconversion of &alpha;-ketobutyrate and 
                     &alpha;-aminobutyrate |CITS: [7040341]|.
                     A homology model of the enzyme based on the crystal 
                     structure of AlaA has been generated |CITS: [25014014]|. An
                     <i>ilvE avtA</i> double mutant requires isoleucine and 
                     valine for growth |CITS: [7040341]|.  <i>avtA</i> is a 
                     multicopy suppressor of the isoleucine requirement of an 
                     <i>ilvE</i> mutant |CITS: [3040683]|.  An <i>alaA avtA</i> 
                     double mutant forms small colonies on agar plates.  An 
                     <i>alaA avtA alaC</i> triple mutant has a slow growth 
                     phenotype in liquid medium.  The defects of the double and 
                     triple mutants can be rescued by addition of alanine |CITS:
                     [20729367][21597182]|.  Under competitive growth conditions
                     in rich media, the &Delta;<i>avtA</i> mutation does not 
                     confer a disadvantage compared to wild type |CITS: 
                     [25014014]|.
                     AvtA expression is suppressed by excess alanine and leucine
                     |CITS: [396446][7040341][6373721][20729367]|. AvtA: 
                     ""<b>a</b>lanine-<b>v</b>aline <b>t</b>ransaminase"" |CITS:
                     [396446]|"
                     /translation="MTFSLFGDKFTRHSGITLLMEDLNDGLRTPGAIMLGGGNPAQIPE
                     MQDYFQTLLTDMLESGKATDALCNYDGPQGKTELLTLLAGMLREKLGWDIEPQNIALTN
