                     /locus_tag="b3580"
                     /product="bifunctional L-xylulose kinase /
                     3-keto-L-gulonate kinase"
                     /EC_number="2.7.1.53"
                     /label=lyxK
                     /note="L-xylulose kinase is the product of an apparently
                     silent gene, <i>lyxK</i>.  Once expression is activated 
                     through a mutation in the transcriptional repressor YiaJ 
                     |CITS: [9525947]|, the kinase specifically phosphorylates 
                     L-xylulose.  This allows <i>E. coli</i> to utilize the 
                     uncommon sugar, L-lyxose, using enzymes of the rhamnose 
                     degradation system.  The product of the L-xylulose kinase 
                     reaction, L-xylulose 5-P, is further metabolized by the 
                     pentose phosphate pathway |CITS: [7961955]|.
                     LyxK is also able to catalyze the phosphorylation of 
                     3-keto-L-gulonate |CITS: [11741871]|.
                     "
