                     /product="bifunctional 3-keto-L-gulonate-6-phosphate
                     decarboxylase SgbH / 3-keto-L-gulonate-6-phosphate 
                     decarboxylase"
                     /EC_number="4.1.1.85"
                     /label=sgbH
                     /note="YiaQ/SgbH is one of two known 
                     3-keto-L-gulonate-6-phosphate decarboxylases in <i>E. 
                     coli</i> |CITS: [11741871]|.
                     Expression from the <i>yiaK</i> promoter is moderately 
                     induced by fucose and ascorbate |CITS: 
                     [10913096][17906139]|, and increased amounts of YiaQ 
                     protein are detected after aerobic growth on ascorbate 
                     |CITS: [17906139]|.  The presence of the amino acids 
                     proline, threonine, glutamate, glutamine or aspartate in 
                     the medium is required for <i>yiaK</i> promoter activity. 
                     Cells that overexpress the <i>yiaK</i> operon due to a 
                     mutation in the YiaJ repressor gain the ability to utilize 
                     L-ascorbate as the sole source of carbon |CITS: 
                     [17906139]|.
                     Review: |CITS: [14700544]|"
