     CDS             3773187..3774377
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="lldD"
                     /locus_tag="b3605"
                     /product="bifunctional L-lactate dehydrogenase / 
                     (S)-2-hydroxybutanoate dehydrogenase"
                     /label=lldD
                     /note="L-lactate dehydrogenase is an FMN-dependent 
                     membrane-associated dehydrogenase |CITS: [18473][8407843]|.
                      It functions in aerobic respiration and also has a role in
                     anaerobic nitrate respiration |CITS: 
                     [NISHIMURA83][8132465]|.  L-lactate dehydrogenase is 
                     associated with the inner membrane |CITS: 
                     [4554536][18473][15911532]|.
                     LldD is one of three lactate dehydrogenase enzymes which 
                     interconvert pyruvate and lactate in <i>E. coli</i>.  The 
                     other two enzymes are specific for D-lactate: the soluble 
                     |FRAME: DLACTDEHYDROGNAD-MONOMER ""LdhA""|, an NAD-linked 
                     fermentative enzyme, and |FRAME: DLACTDEHYDROGFAD-MONOMER 
                     ""Dld""|, a membrane-associated respiratory enzyme. 
                     L-lactate dehydrogenase is induced by aerobic growth on 
                     L-lactate and L-fucose |CITS: [4595205][18473][8407843]| 
                     and in the presence of lactate under nitrate, fumarate and 
                     TMAO respiration conditions |CITS: [NISHIMURA83]|. 
                     Repression of <i>lldD</i> expression under anaerobic 
                     conditions is mediated by ArcA |CITS: [8132465]|.  An 
                     <i>lldD</i> insertion mutant has lost the ability to grow 
                     on L-lactate as the sole source of carbon and energy, but 
                     can still utilize D-lactate |CITS: [8407843]|."
