     gene            complement(3782407..3783441)
                     /gene="waaH"
                     /locus_tag="b3615"
                     /label=waaH
     CDS             complement(3782407..3783441)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="waaH"
                     /locus_tag="b3615"
                     /product="UDP-glucuronate:LPS(HepIII) glycosyltransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.4.1.17"
                     /label=waaH
                     /note="WaaH is a glucuronic acid transferase involved in 
                     modification of the core oligosaccharide in <i>E. coli</i> 
                     K-12. WaaH catalyses the addition of glucuronic acid to the
                     third heptose of the inner core oligosaccharide |CITS: 
                     [23372159]|. This modified lipopolysaccharide (LPS) is 
                     produced when <i>E. coli</i> is grown under phosphate 
                     limiting conditions with sub millimolar concentrations of 
                     Zn<sup>2+</sup> and Fe<sup>3+</sup> |CITS: [23372159]|. The
                     glucuronic acid modification coincides with the absence of 
                     phosphate on the second heptose, is absent in the LPS of 
                     <i>waaC, waaO, waaP, waaG</i> or <i>waaQ</i> deletion 
                     mutants but can be identified in <i>waaR</i> and 
                     <i>waaB</i> deletion mutants |CITS: [22021036][23372159]|. 
                     The LPS of a <i>phoB</i> deletion mutant does not contain 
                     glucuronic acid |CITS: [23372159]|. WaaH is membrane 
                     associated |CITS: [23372159]|. Structural analysis of the 
                     modified LPS indicates that a &beta;-glucuronate residue is
                     attached to the O7 atom of the side chain heptose (heptose 
                     III) |CITS: [23372159]|.
                     Transcription of a <i>waaH-lacZ</i> promoter fusion is 
                     induced by growth in phosphate limited medium and abolished
                     in a <i>phoB</i> deleted strain but not in a <i>basR</i> 
                     deleted strain |CITS: [23372159]|. Two PhoB binding sites 
                     are located directly upstream of the <i>waaH</i> gene 
                     |CITS: [21538251]|. Transcription of a <i>ugd-lacZ</i> 
                     promoter fusion is also induced by growth in phosphate 
                     limited medium |CITS: [23372159]| - (|FRAME: UGD-MONOMER| 
                     catalyses the production of the nucleotide sugar 
                     UDP-glucuronate).
                     <i>waaH</i> levels are increased 2.7-fold by growth on 
                     ZnSO<sub>4</sub>-containing medium, and a <i>waaH</i> null 
                     mutant is hypersensitive to ZnSO<sub>4</sub> |CITS: 
                     [15659689]|.  Iron- and zinc-mediated induction of 
                     <i>waaH</i> expression is dependent on PmrA/BasR |CITS: 
                     [16428424]|.  Expression of <i>waaH</i> is activated by 
                     PhoB |CITS: [17020555]|.
                     Based on sequence similarity, WaaH is predicted to be an 
                     inosine triphosphate diphosphatase and/or a 
                     ribulose-bisphosphate carboxylase (2-phosphoglycolate 
                     forming) |CITS: [12952533]|.
                     "
