     gene            3788289..3789335
                     /gene="waaF"
                     /locus_tag="b3620"
                     /label=waaF
     CDS             3788289..3789335
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="waaF"
                     /locus_tag="b3620"
                     /product="bifunctional ADP-heptose--LPS
                     heptosyltransferase 2 / ADP-heptose--LPS 
                     heptosyltransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.4.99.24"
                     /label=waaF
                     /note="ADP-heptose:LPS heptosyltransferase II (HepII,
                     WaaF) is the enzyme responsible for transfer of the second 
                     heptose sugar onto the heptosyl-Kdo<sub>2</sub> moiety of 
                     the lipopolysaccharide inner core |CITS: 
                     [11054112][11717579]|. A kinetic and biophysical 
                     characterization of HepII has been reported by |CITS: 
                     [35861590]|.
                     Truncation of the LPS inner core by defined mutations in 
                     <i>hldD</i> (<i>rfaD</i>), <i>hldE</i> (<i>rfaE</i>) or 
                     <i>waaF</i> resulted in high-level <i>gab</i> operon 
                     expression and a mucoid colony phenotype resulting from a 
                     colanic acid capsule |CITS: [15576807]|. Production of 
                     colanic acid in the &Delta;<i>waaF</i> mutant is dependent 
                     on the RcsCDB phosphorelay system |CITS: [27002133]|. In 
                     <i>waaC</i>, <i>waaE</i>, <i>waaF</i> and <i>waaG</i> 
                     mutants, biofilm formation was significantly increased 
                     relative to the parental strain |CITS: [23284671]|.  A 
                     &Delta;<i>waaF</i> strain lacks flagella |CITS: 
                     [27214006]|. Selection for reduced susceptibility to 
                     tigecycline results in mutations in <i>waaF</i> and other 
                     genes of the LPS core biosynthesis pathway |CITS: 
                     [23843301]|.
                     The chromosomal <i>waa</i> region (formerly <i>rfa</i>) 
                     contains the major core-oligosaccharide assembly operons in
                     <i>E. coli</i> |CITS: [12045108][17362200]|. The current 
                     nomenclature system was proposed originally in |CITS: 
                     [9004408]| and |CITS: [9791168]| and followed thereafter.
                     Reviews: |CITS: [17362200][12045108][9791168][7504166]|"
