     gene            complement(3796418..3797497)
                     /gene="waaB"
                     /locus_tag="b3628"
                     /label=waaB
     CDS             complement(3796418..3797497)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="waaB"
                     /locus_tag="b3628"
                     /product="bifunctional UDP-D-galactose:(glucosyl)lipopolys 
                     accharide-1,6-D-galactosyltransferase / lipopolysaccharide 
                     1,6-galactosyltransferase"
                     /label=waaB
                     /note="The lipopolysaccharide (LPS) of <i>E. coli</i> K-12 
                     consists of two major components: the hydrophobic lipid A 
                     moiety inserted into the outer membrane and the 
                     phosphorylated core oligosaccharide |CITS: [12045108]|. 
                     UDP-galactose:(glucosyl)lipopolysaccharide 
                     1,6-D-galactosyltransferase (WaaB) adds galactose from 
                     UDP-galactose to the first glucose residue (GlcI) of the 
                     outer core of LPS |CITS: [24479701]|.
                     Early studies characterized the <i>waa</i> (<i>rfa</i>) 
                     locus and identified the <i>waaB</i> gene |CITS: 
                     [2168379][1938935][1348243][1577693]|.
                     In the absence of the lipid acceptor, WaaB can slowly 
                     hydrolyze the UDP-galactose sugar donor. It cannot 
                     hydrolyze UDP-glucose |CITS: [24479701]|.
                     WaaB is not able to utilize other sugar nucleotide donors 
                     such as UDP-glucose, UDP-glucuronate, UDP-galacturonate, 
                     GDP-mannose, ADP-glucose and GDP-glucose. Unphosphorylated 
                     heptosyl<sub>2</sub>-Kdo<sub>2</sub>-lipid A cannot serve 
                     as an acceptor |CITS: [24479701]|.
                     <i>waaB</i> was identified by its ability to complement a 
                     <i>Salmonella typhimurium waaB</i> mutant |CITS: 
                     [1624461]|.  A <i>waaB</i> deletion mutant has a lower 
                     ciclopirox minimum inhibitory concentration than wild type 
                     |CITS: [23936064]|.
                     In an <i>E. coli</i> K-12 <i>rfaBIJ</i> deletion mutant, 
                     complementation analysis showed that <i>rfaB</i> is 
                     necessary for the synthesis of LPS capable of serving as a 
                     co-receptor for bacteriphage K20 binding |CITS: 
                     [10564794]|.
                     A recombinant <i>E. coli</i> K-12 strain containing a 
                     deletion of the glycosyltransferases encoded by <i>waaB</i>
                     and <i>waaO</i> resulted in a truncated lipid A core which 
                     was used as a scaffold for antigen display |CITS: 
                     [21286806][20574043]|.
                     The <i>Salmonella</i> enzyme has also been biochemically 
                     characterized |CITS: [6403519][4553445][4898284]|.
                     The chromosomal <i>waa</i> region (formerly <i>rfa</i>) 
                     contains the major core-oligosaccharide assembly operons in
                     <i>E. coli</i> |CITS: [12045108][17362200]|.  The current 
                     gene nomenclature system was proposed originally in |CITS: 
                     [9004408]| and |CITS: [9791168]| and followed thereafter.
                     Reviews: |CITS: [12045108][9791168][7504166]|"
