     gene            complement(3804610..3804777)
                     /gene="rpmG"
                     /locus_tag="b3636"
                     /label=rpmG
     CDS             complement(3804610..3804777)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rpmG"
                     /locus_tag="b3636"
                     /product="trifunctional 50S ribosomal subunit protein L33
                     / 50S ribosomal subunit / ribosome"
                     /label=rpmG
                     /note="The L33 protein is a component of the 50S subunit
                     of the ribosome.  L33 is found in substoichiometric amounts
                     and appears to require the presence of L3 and L28 for 
                     assembly |CITS: [3298242]|.
                     L33 is located within 21 &Aring; of nucleotide C2475 of 23S
                     rRNA, near the peptidyltransferase center |CITS: 
                     [7529559]|.  L33 had previously been shown to crosslink to 
                     23S rRNA |CITS: [1702198]| and to tRNA in the P site |CITS:
                     [3889589][2660905][2685749][2182127][1708125][76808 
                     05][8524654]| and E site |CITS: 
                     [8440251][8524654][10961994][11904182]|. L33 also 
                     crosslinks to L1 and L27 |CITS: 
                     [2645289][2653827][2665813]| and can be isolated in a 
                     complex with 5S rRNA, tRNA, and other proteins of the large
                     ribosomal subunit |CITS: [6174328][7047160]|.  L33 can be 
                     exchanged between ribosomes; however, it is unclear whether
                     this occurs <i>in vivo</i> |CITS: [340925][342903]|.  L33 
                     is not exposed on the ribosomal surface |CITS: [9371771]|.
                     In ~ 25% of L33 proteins, the initiator methionine residue 
                     is monomethylated |CITS: [326752]|.  In the remainder of 
                     L33 proteins, the initiating methionine is removed |CITS: 
                     [10094780]|, and the first alanine residue is methylated 
                     |CITS: [5324303][786732][326752][10094780]|.
                     A strain containing an IS element insertion in <i>rpmG</i> 
                     shows no major defect in ribosome assembly |CITS: 
                     [7685806]|; L33 appears to have no significant role in 
                     ribosome synthesis or function |CITS: 
                     [9044258][9098043][9294008]|.  Overexpression of 
                     <i>rpmG</i> causes increased resistance to mitomycin C. The
                     effect is dependent on the DNA glycosylase |FRAME: 
                     EG10329-MONOMER MutM|, which is encoded directly downstream
                     of <i>rpmG</i> |CITS: [26704888]|.
                     Review: |CITS: [22649682]|"
