                     /label=rpmB
     CDS             complement(3804798..3805034)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rpmB"
                     /locus_tag="b3637"
                     /product="trifunctional 50S ribosomal subunit protein L28
                     / 50S ribosomal subunit / ribosome"
                     /label=rpmB
                     /note="The L28 protein is a component of the 50S subunit
                     of the ribosome and is required for ribosome assembly 
                     |CITS: [9044258][9098043][9294008]|.
                     L28 interacts with 23S rRNA |CITS: 
                     [6163479][3298242][2495985][1702198][7556101][8722036]| and
                     crosslinks to L9 |CITS: [2645289][2653827][2665813]|. L15 
                     and L17 stimulate the interaction of L28 with 23S rRNA 
                     |CITS: [3298242]|.  L28 is phosphorylated at Thr8 |CITS: 
                     [19469554]|.
                     L28 is labeled by the macrolides carbomycin A, niddamycin 
                     and tylosin, which inhibit ribosomal activity |CITS: 
                     [3884043][4055551]|.
                     Expression of <i>rpmBG</i> is under ppGpp/DksA-dependent 
                     negative stringent control during amino acid starvation 
                     |CITS: [27381917]|."
