                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="setC"
                     /locus_tag="b3659"
                     /product="putative exporter SetC"
                     /label=setC
                     /note="SetC has significant sequence similarity with the
                     sugar efflux transporters SetA and SetB from the major 
                     facilitator superfamily; glucose, galactose and lactose 
                     transport activities are not observed in everted membrane 
                     vesicles prepared from cells overexpressing <i>setC</i> 
                     |CITS:[10209755][10438463]|.
                     Deletion of <i>setC</i> increases intracellular arabinose 
                     concentration (measured indirectly using a fluorescent 
                     transcriptional reporter) and overexpression of <i>setC</i>
                     reduces intracellular arabinose concentration compared to 
                     wild type |CITS: [22952739]|.
                     A SetC-GFP fusion protein localizes in a helical pattern in
                     the cell |CITS:[14617174]|.
                     In the Transporter Classification Database |CITS: 
                     [26546518]|, SetC is a member of the Sugar Efflux 
                     Transporter (SET) family within the Major Facilitator 
                     Superfamily."
