     CDS             3831608..3832531
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yicL"
                     /locus_tag="b3660"
                     /product="putative transporter YicL"
                     /label=yicL
                     /note="YicL is an inner membrane protein with ten
                     predicted transmembrane domains.  The C terminus is located
                     in the cytoplasm |CITS: [15919996]|. Overexpression of YicL
                     or the ORF296 protein from <i>Glycine max</i> (soybean) 
                     inhibits growth of <i>E. coli</i> and leads to slightly 
                     increased accumulation of |FRAME: 5-AMINO-LEVULINATE 
                     &delta;-aminolevulinic acid| (ALA).  The authors proposed 
                     that YicL may inhibit the biosynthesis of heme, possibly by
                     inhibiting HemB |CITS: [11817648]|.
                     In the Transporter Classification Database <i>E. coli</i> 
                     YicL is a member of the Drug/Metabolite Transporter (DMT) 
                     superfamily |CITS: [24225317]|.
                     "
