     gene            complement(3832535..3833353)
                     /gene="nlpA"
                     /locus_tag="b3661"
                     /label=nlpA
     CDS             complement(3832535..3833353)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="nlpA"
                     /locus_tag="b3661"
                     /product="lipoprotein-28"
                     /label=nlpA
                     /note="NlpA is an inner membrane lipoprotein in
                     <I>Escherichia coli</I>; NlpA is non-essential for growth 
                     |CITS: [2841301]|.
                     NlpA may serve as an L and D-methionine receptor, feeding 
                     inefficiently into the |FRAME: METNIQ-METHIONINE-ABC-CPLX 
                     ""methionine ABC transporter""|. Compared to a wild type 
                     strain and a <i>&Delta;metQ</i> single mutant, a 
                     <i>&Delta;metQ &Delta;nlpA</i> double mutant grows poorly 
                     with D-methionine (and to a lesser extent with 
                     L-methionine) as sole sulfur source and takes up labeled 
                     L-methionine and labeled D-methionine poorly |CITS: 
                     [12819857]|. NlpA expressed from a plasmid can complement a
                     &Delta;<i>nlpA</i> &Delta;<i>metQ</i> &Delta;<i>metE</i> 
                     triple mutation for growth on D-methionine |CITS: 
                     [23852867]|.
                     NlpA may play a role in virulence of enteropathogenic 
                     strains of <I>E. coli</I> |CITS: [1317383]|.
                     An <i>E. coli</i> DH5&alpha; <i>nlpA</i>::Tn5 mutant 
                     produces significantly less outer membrane vesicles than 
                     the wild type |CITS: [16855227]|.  This phenotype is most 
                     severe in late log phase and stationary phase |CITS: 
                     [23852867]|. <i>E. coli</i> &Delta;<i>nlpA</i> 
                     &Delta;<i>degP</i> double mutants have a severe stress 
                     dependent synthetic growth defect |CITS: [23852867]|."
