     gene            complement(3840665..3841984)
                     /gene="uhpC"
                     /locus_tag="b3667"
                     /label=uhpC
     CDS             complement(3840665..3841984)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="uhpC"
                     /locus_tag="b3667"
                     /product="inner membrane protein sensing
                     glucose-6-phosphate"
                     /label=uhpC
                     /note="UhpC belongs to the phosphorelay system
                     UhpB-UhpC-UhpA |CITS [8349544], [3042748], [11325944]| 
                     which regulates the uptake of hexose phosphates |CITS 
                     [11325944]| (see |FRAME: PWY0-1492| ).
                     UhpC is a membrane-bound protein that senses external 
                     glucose-6-phosphate (G-6-P) and interacts with the 
                     histidine kinase UhpB. Interaction of UhpC with UhpB 
                     stimulates the kinase activity of UhpB with subsequent 
                     phosphorylation of the response regulator UhpA |CITS 
                     [11739766], [11053370], [12107138], [11325944]|. 
                     Phosphorylated UhpA increases the affinity for its specific
                     DNA binding sites and controls the transcriptional 
                     expression of the hexose phosphate transporter UhpT |CITS 
                     [12107138], [11325944 ]|. <i>uhpB</i> insertion mutants 
                     which are consititutive for expression of <i>uhpT</i> are 
                     dependent on the presence of <i>uhpC</i> suggesting that 
                     UhpB and UhpC may act as a complex in the signalling 
                     pathway |CITS: [8349544]|. Deletion of <i>uhpC</i> results 
                     in the elevated expression of a <i>uhpT-lacZ</i> reporter 
                     construct that is not further induced by G-6-P |CITS: 
                     [1569007]|. UhpC is predicted to contain 12 trans-membrane 
                     regions with the N and C-terminus located in the cytoplasm 
                     |CITS: [1569007]|. UhpC has approximately 30% amino acid 
                     sequence identity with UhpT. This degree of identity is 
                     similar to that shared between UhpT and the transport 
                     proteins GlpT and PgtP |CITS: [1569007]|.
                     In the Transporter Classification Database UhpC is a member
                     of the Major Facilitator Superfamily (MFS) of transporters 
                     |CITS: [24225317]|.
                     "
