     gene            complement(3841994..3843496)
                     /gene="uhpB"
                     /locus_tag="b3668"
                     /label=uhpB
     CDS             complement(3841994..3843496)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="uhpB"
                     /locus_tag="b3668"
                     /product="bifunctional sensor histidine kinase UhpB / 
                     protein-histidine autokinase"
                     /EC_number="2.7.13.3"
                     /label=uhpB
                     /note="UhpB belongs to the phosphorelay system
                     UhpB-UhpC-UhpA  which is involved in the regulation of the 
                     uptake of hexose phosphates. UhpB is a membrane bound 
                     histidine kinase with eight predicted transmembrane helices
                     and a C-terminal cytoplasmic domain containing the 
                     characteristic histidine kinase sequence motifs |CITS: 
                     [3042748], [1569007]|. UhpB autophosphorylates on a 
                     conserved histidine residue (His313) and transfers the 
                     phosphoryl group its cognate response regulator, UhpA 
                     |CITS: [11739766]|. The Uhp signal transduction system is 
                     responsible for sensing and transport of the metabolic 
                     intermediate, glucose-6-phosphate. The membrane protein, 
                     UhpC senses glucose-6-phosphate in the periplasm and 
                     subsequently interacts with UhpB stimulating its kinase 
                     activity |CITS: [8349544], [11053370]|. Dephosphorylation 
                     of phosphorylated UhpA by membrane-bound UhpB has been 
                     demonstrated <i>in vitro</i> |CITS: [11739766]|."
