     gene            complement(3844162..3844452)
                     /gene="ilvN"
                     /locus_tag="b3670"
                     /label=ilvN
     CDS             complement(3844162..3844452)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ilvN"
                     /locus_tag="b3670"
                     /product="trifunctional acetohydroxy acid synthase I
                     subunit IlvN / acetohydroxybutanoate synthase / 
                     acetolactate synthase"
                     /EC_number="2.2.1.6"
                     /label=ilvN
                     /note="IlvN is the small regulatory subunit of AHAS I, the 
                     bifunctional acetohydroxybutanoate synthase/acetolactate 
                     synthase which carries out both the first step in valine 
                     biosynthesis and the second step in isoleucine 
                     biosynthesis.
                     IlvN was shown to bind close to the FAD binding site of 
                     IlvB |CITS: [18193896]|.  The interactions between the 
                     large and small subunits from different isozymes were 
                     investigated |CITS: [19653643]|.
                     Wild type cells are sensitive to exogenous valine due to 
                     inhibition of the enzymatic activity of IlvB/N |CITS: 
                     [14463257]|.  <i>ilvN</i> mutants, however, while still 
                     able to grow in the absence of valine and isoleucine, are 
                     no longer sensitive in this manner to exogenous valine 
                     |CITS: [3011751]|.
                     The solution structure of IlvN in both the free and 
                     valine-bound form was determined by NMR methods.  In its 
                     free form, IlvN exists as a mixture of conformational 
                     states, while in its bound form, IlvN exists as a single 
                     conformer |CITS: [23205845]|.  The backbone and side-chain 
                     assignments of IlvN in the valine bound form was reported 
                     |CITS: [20383786]|."
