                     /locus_tag="b3671"
                     /label=ilvB
     CDS             complement(3844456..3846144)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ilvB"
                     /locus_tag="b3671"
                     /product="trifunctional acetohydroxy acid synthase I
                     subunit IlvB / acetohydroxybutanoate synthase / 
                     acetolactate synthase"
                     /EC_number="2.2.1.6"
                     /label=ilvB
                     /note="IlvB is the large catalytic subunit of AHAS I, the 
                     bifunctional acetohydroxybutanoate synthase/acetolactate 
                     synthase which carries out both the first step in valine 
                     biosynthesis and the second step in isoleucine 
                     biosynthesis.
                     The IlvB subunit can catalyze the reaction in isolation and
                     is not inhibited by valine in the manner of the holoenzyme.
                      However, the V<sub>max</sub> for the reaction as catalyzed
                     by IlvB alone is sharply reduced, as is the enzyme's 
                     affinity for the required FAD cofactor |CITS: 
                     [1512191][3011751]|.  Both activities are catalyzed by the 
                     same active site on IlvB |CITS: [3294793]|.  The 
                     interactions between the large and small subunits from 
                     different isozymes were investigated |CITS: [19653643]|.
                     "
