     gene            complement(3854533..3855347)
                     /pseudo
                     /gene="glvG"
                     /locus_tag="b4556"
                     /label=glvG
                     /note="<i>glvG</i> is designated a pseudogene that encodes
                     the N-terminal half of a 6-phospho-&alpha;-glucosidase. The
                     <i>glvG</i> ORF in <i>E. coli</i> K-12 MG1655 has suffered 
                     a 508 bp deletion between 8 bp direct repeats (GAACCACT), 
                     which would be located between nucleotides 3861387 and 
                     3861388 in the current genome sequence.  The formerly 
                     annotated <i>ysdC</i> ORF represents the C terminus of the 
                     ancestral gene.  An intact version of <i>glvG</i> is 
                     present in <i>E. coli</i> HS; see <a href="" 
                     ""https://biocyc.org/gene?orgid=GCF_000017765&id=ECHS_RS191
                     80"""">6-phospho-alpha-glucosidase</a>. UniProt ID of the 
                     truncated GlvG ORF: P31450
                     glvG: """"<b>gl</b>ucoside-like"""" |CITS: [8019415]|
                     "
