                     /gene="dgoD"
                     /locus_tag="b4478"
                     /product="bifunctional L-galactonate dehydratase /
                     D-galactonate dehydratase"
                     /EC_number="5.5.1.25; 4.2.1.6"
                     /label=dgoD
                     /note="D-galactonate dehydratase catalyzes the first step
                     in the degradation of D-galactonate, the dehydration of 
                     D-galactonate to form 2-dehydro-3-deoxygalactonate |CITS: 
                     [324806][211976]|.
                     D-galactonate dehydratase belongs to the mandelate racemase
                     (MR) subgroup of the enolase superfamily |CITS: 
                     [7855594][15581566]|. A reaction mechanism for the 
                     &beta;-elimination of OH<sup>-</sup> involving His185 as a 
                     general acid/base catalyst has been proposed and is 
                     supported by analysis of point mutants |CITS: 
                     [WIECZOREK99]|.
                     Production of galactonate dehydratase is induced by growth 
                     on galactonate |CITS: [324806]|. The inducer is 
                     D-galactonate, and expression is subject to catabolite 
                     repression |CITS: [211976][30455279]|.
                     The enantiomer |FRAME: CPD-12349| alone cannot be used by 
                     <i>E. coli</i> as a sole carbon source, however a mixture 
                     of 2-dehydro-3-deoxy-L-galactonate and |FRAME: 
                     D-GALACTURONATE| enables the utilization of both compounds 
                     |CITS: [37812254][38954014]|."
