     CDS             complement(3866355..3866972)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="dgoA"
                     /locus_tag="b4477"
                     /product="2-dehydro-3-deoxy-6-phosphogalactonate aldolase"
                     /EC_number="4.1.2.21"
                     /label=dgoA
                     /note="2-oxo-3-deoxygalactonate 6-phosphate aldolase
                     (KDPGal aldolase) catalyzes the final reaction in the 
                     degradation of D-galactonate, an aldol cleavage resulting 
                     in GA3P and pyruvate which enter central metabolism |CITS: 
                     [324806][211976]|.
                     Crystal structures of KDPGal aldolase have been determined.
                      Comparison to the crystal structure of KDPG aldolase led 
                     to the hypothesis that the V154 residue was involved in 
                     stereoselectivity of the enzyme.  A V154T mutant shows 
                     reduced stereoselectivity, but also reduced catalytic 
                     efficiency |CITS: [17981470]|.
                     Although KDPG aldolase (the <i>eda</i> gene product) and 
                     KDPGal aldolase (the <i>dgoA</i> gene product) catalyze 
                     nearly identical reactions that differ only at a single 
                     stereocenter, they show only a low level of sequence 
                     similarity |CITS: [17981470]|.
                     Production of KDPGal aldolase is induced by growth on 
                     galactonate |CITS: [324806]|.  The inducer is 
                     D-galactonate, and expression is subject to catabolite 
                     repression |CITS: [211976][30455279]|.
                     DgoA: ""<b>D</b>-<b>g</b>alact<b>o</b>nate"" |CITS: 
                     [211976]|"
