     CDS             complement(3869500..3870312)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yidA"
                     /locus_tag="b3697"
                     /product="bifunctional sugar phosphatase YidA / sugar
                     phosphatase"
                     /EC_number="3.1.3.23"
                     /label=yidA
                     /note="YidA is a promiscuous sugar phosphatase belonging
                     to the superfamily of haloacid dehalogenase (HAD)-like 
                     hydrolases.  Its preferred substrate is 
                     erythrose-4-phosphate |CITS: [16990279]|.  YidA selectively
                     hydrolyzes &alpha;-D-glucose-1-phosphate and has no 
                     activity with the &beta; form |CITS: [16990279][25527541]|.
                      The reaction proceeds via the canonical phosphomonoester 
                     hydrolase mechanism, which involves breakage of the P-O 
                     bond, not the C1-O bond |CITS: [25527541]|.  The 
                     phosphatase activity of YidA was first discovered in a 
                     high-throughput screen of purified proteins |CITS: 
                     [15808744]|.
                     Mutagenesis of the predicted catalytic Asp residue in YidA 
                     results in loss of phosphatase activity |CITS: [16990279]|.
                      YidA does not catalyze phosphoryl transfer to a sugar 
                     acceptor |CITS: [25527541]|.
                     "
