     CDS             3877696..3877836
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rpmH"
                     /locus_tag="b3703"
                     /product="trifunctional 50S ribosomal subunit protein L34
                     / 50S ribosomal subunit / ribosome"
                     /label=rpmH
                     /note="The L34 protein is a component of the 50S subunit
                     of the ribosome.
                     L34 can be isolated in a complex with 5S rRNA, tRNA, and 
                     other proteins of the large ribosomal subunit |CITS: 
                     [7047160][6174328]|.  Assembly of L34 into the 50S 
                     ribosomal subunit is dependent on L4, L22 and L24 |CITS: 
                     [3298242]|.  L34 can be crosslinked to L23 |CITS: 
                     [2645289][2665813]|.  L34 is one of six proteins that is 
                     completely lost from ribosomes in post-stationary cells 
                     |CITS: [6201363]|.
                     L34 was identified as ""antizyme 2"", an inhibitor of the 
                     biosynthetic ornithine and arginine decarboxylases; these 
                     enzymes are involved in the biosynthesis of polyamines 
                     |CITS: [6351053][6392292]|.  <i>In vitro</i> and outside 
                     the context of the ribosome, L34 and a number of additional
                     ribosomal proteins show ""antizyme"" inhibition of 
                     ornithine decarboxylase |CITS: [3542048]|.  L34 physically 
                     interacts with ornithine and arginine decarboxylase, and 
                     overexpression of L34 decreases the production of 
                     polyamines <i>in vivo</i> |CITS: [7539334]|. Levels of L34 
                     increase in response to polyamines; the effect is thought 
                     to be due to an increase in the level of transcription of 
                     <i>rpmH</i> |CITS: [2185470]|.  SHAPE probing showed that 
                     the 5' UTR of the <i>rpmH-rnpA</i> mRNA folds into three 
                     major hairpin helices; |FRAME: EG10862-MONOMER| binds 
                     tightly to helix 2 and may induce a conformational change 
                     in the 5' UTR |CITS: [29551268]|. The <i>rimA</i> mutant, 
                     likely an allele of <i>rpmH</i> |CITS: [6329723]|, has a 
                     cold-sensitive growth and ribosome assembly defect |CITS: 
                     [4591943]|.  An <i>rpmH</i> null mutant is viable |CITS: 
                     [21945294]|. RimA: ""<b>ri</b>bosome <b>m</b>aturation 
                     <b>A</b>"" |CITS: [4591943]|<br>
                     SsaF: ""<b>s</b>uppressor of <i><b>s</b>ec<b>A</b></i> 
                     <b>F</b>"" |CITS: [3881390]|<br>
                     RpmH: |CITS: [6329723]|
                     Reviews: |CITS: [3893559][3076320]|"
