                     /gene="mdtL"
                     /locus_tag="b3710"
                     /product="bifunctional efflux pump MdtL /
                     chloramphenicol:H(+) antiporter"
                     /label=mdtL
                     /note="MdtL (formerly YidY) is a member of the 
                     Drug:H<sup>+</sup> Antiporter-1 (12 Spanner) (DHA1) family 
                     within the Major Facilitator Superfamily (MFS) |CITS: 
                     [8987357][26546518]|. Overexpression of <I>mdtL</I> in a 
                     K-12 strain which lacks the major efflux pump permease AcrB
                     (<i>E. coli</i> KAM3; see |CITS: [12618449]|) results in a 
                     two-fold increase in resistance to chloramphenicol but does
                     not impact the resistance to a range of other antibiotics 
                     and toxic compounds |CITS:[11566977]|. <i>mdtL</i> is one 
                     of 35 efflux-encoding genes that have been deleted or 
                     inactivated in 'Efflux KnockOut-35' (EKO-35) -  a K-12 
                     BW25133-derived strain that lacks 35 efflux pumps and can 
                     be used as a platform to study their function |CITS: 
                     [36065018][36318669]|.
                     "
