                     /product="PF03691 family colicin E2 tolerance protein
                     CbrC"
                     /label=cbrC
                     /note="Overexpression of CbrC causes a Colicin E2 tolerant 
                     (""Cet2"") phenotype |CITS: [20418396]|.
                     Transcription of <i>cbrB</i>, the first gene of the 
                     predicted <i>cbrBC</i> transcription unit, is induced by 
                     the CreBC two-component system by minimal media growth 
                     conditions |CITS: [11350954]|.
                     Certain <i>cbrBC</i> mutants show hypersensitivity to 
                     nitrofurzone |CITS: [12897016]|.  <i>cbrC</i> insertion or 
                     deletion mutants are more susceptible to colicin E2 than 
                     wild type in the CreC hyperactive mutant background |CITS: 
                     [20418396]|.
                     CbrC: ""<i><b>c</b>re<b>B</b></i>-<b>r</b>egulated gene 
                     <b>C</b>"" |CITS: [12897016]|"
