                     transporter"
                     /EC_number="7.3.2.1"
                     /label=pstB
                     /note="PstB is the ATP-binding subunit of a high affinity 
                     phosphate specific uptake system; PstB contains signature 
                     motifs conserved in ATP binding cassette (ABC) proteins 
                     |CITS: [3926486][9593292]|. PstB interacts directly with 
                     PhoU and this interaction is implicated in signal 
                     transduction to PhoR; PstB, PhoU and PhoR may form a 
                     phosphate-sensing complex at the cell membrane |CITS: 
                     [24563032]|.
                     <i>pstB</i> belongs to a network of genes which facilitate 
                     stress-induced mutagenesis (SIM) in <i>E. coli</i> K-12 
                     |CITS: [23224554]|."
