     gene            complement(3903845..3904885)
                     /gene="pstS"
                     /locus_tag="b3728"
                     /label=pstS
     CDS             complement(3903845..3904885)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="pstS"
                     /locus_tag="b3728"
                     /product="trifunctional phosphate ABC transporter
                     periplasmic binding protein / phosphate ABC transporter / 
                     phsophate ABC transporter"
                     /EC_number="7.3.2.1"
                     /label=pstS
                     /note="PstS is the periplasmic, phosphate binding protein
                     of the ATP dependent, high affinity phosphate transport 
                     sytem in <i>E. coli</i> K-12.
                     PstS consists of two globular domains separated by a deep 
                     cleft which forms the phosphate binding site |CITS: 
                     [2215649]|. PstS binds monobasic 
                     (H<sub>2</sub>PO<sub>4</sub><sup>-</sup>) and dibasic 
                     (H<sub>2</sub>PO<sub>4</sub><sup>2-</sup>) phosphates but 
                     discriminates against sulphate |CITS: [2215649][7929197]|. 
                     The aspartate residue at position 81 forms a short (low 
                     barrier) hydrogen bond with phosphate |CITS: [9228942]|. 
                     PstS can discriminate phosphate from arsenate up to an 800 
                     fold molar excess of arsenate |CITS: [23034649]|. A 
                     <i>pstS</i> D81N mutant has no effect on phosphate binding 
                     but disturbs the discrimination against arsenate 
                     approximately 10-fold and the discrimination against 
                     sulfate about 100-fold |CITS: [23034649]|.
                     <i>pstS</i> insertion mutants were identified in a screen 
                     for genes that are important for surviving exposure to 
                     ionizing radiation (IR).  A <i>pstS</i> deletion mutant has
                     a substantial decrease in survival upon exposure to 
                     increasing doses of IR |CITS: [25049088]|.
                     It was determined by Genomic SELEX screening that the 
                     upstream region of the gene <i>pstS</i> is a target of the 
                     transcriptional factor CusR  |CITS: [34220787]|."
                     /translation="MKVMRTTVATVVAATLSMSAFSVFAEASLTGAGATFPAPVYAKWA
