     gene            complement(3910762..3911625)
                     /gene="atpG"
                     /locus_tag="b3733"
                     /label=atpG
     CDS             complement(3910762..3911625)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="atpG"
                     /locus_tag="b3733"
                     /product="multifunctional ATP synthase F1 complex subunit
                     gamma / ATP synthase F1 complex / ATP synthase / thiamin 
                     triphosphate synthase"
                     /EC_number="7.1.2.2"
                     /label=atpG
                     /note="The gamma subunit appears to play an important role
                     in coupling the catalytic site events with proton 
                     translocation in association with the epsilon subunit. The 
                     coupling involves conformational changes and probable 
                     translocations of one or both subunits |CITS: [8621695]|. 
                     The rate limiting rotation step carried out by this subunit
                     has been investigated and residues involved in this 
                     rotation process have been identified |CITS: [18628203]|.
                     ArcA appears to repress <i>atpG</i> gene expression under 
                     anaerobiosis. Two putative ArcA binding sites were 
                     identified  upstream of this gene |CITS: [15699038]|, but 
                     no promoter upstream of it has been identified. Instead, 
                     <i>atpG</i> is transcribed from three promoters: one of 
                     them is located usptream of <i>atpI</i> gene and the others
                     are located upstream of <i>atpB</i> gene."
