     gene            complement(3916417..3917040)
                     /gene="rsmG"
                     /locus_tag="b3740"
                     /label=rsmG
     CDS             complement(3916417..3917040)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rsmG"
                     /locus_tag="b3740"
                     /product="16S rRNA m(7)G527 methyltransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.1.1.170"
                     /label=rsmG
                     /note="RsmG is the methyltransferase responsible for
                     methylation of 16S rRNA at the N7 position of the G527 
                     nucleotide.  <i>In vitro</i>, the enzyme is able to 
                     methylate 16S rRNA within the 30S ribosomal subunit, but 
                     not naked 16S rRNA |CITS: [17238915]|.  RsmG is highly 
                     conserved in Gram-negative as well as Gram-positive 
                     bacteria |CITS: [17238915]|.
                     A crystal structure of RsmG has been solved at 2.4 &Aring; 
                     resolution |CITS: [12001236]|.
                     Amino acids that are important for catalytic activity of 
                     RsmG were identified by site-directed mutagenesis of 
                     conserved residues |CITS: [22337945]|.
                     An <i>rsmG</i> mutation has no apparent growth defect and 
                     confers low-level resistance to streptomycin.  <i>rsmG</i> 
                     mutations are found at high frequency in 
                     streptomycin-resistant clinical isolates of 
                     <i>Mycobacterium tuberculosis</i> |CITS: [17238915]|. GidB:
                     ""<b>g</b>lucose-<b>i</b>nhibited <b>d</b>ivision"" |CITS: 
                     [6185823]|
                     RsmG: ""<b>r</b>RNA <b>s</b>mall subunit 
                     <b>m</b>ethyltransferase <b>G</b>"" |CITS: [17238915]| 
                     Review: |CITS: [36986305]|"
