     gene            complement(3921512..3922963)
                     /gene="viaA"
                     /locus_tag="b3745"
                     /label=viaA
     CDS             complement(3921512..3922963)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="viaA"
                     /locus_tag="b3745"
                     /product="protein ViaA"
                     /label=viaA
                     /note="RavA and ViaA together may function as a regulatory 
                     chaperone for |FRAME: FUMARATE-REDUCTASE| (Frd) during 
                     anaerobic fumarate respiration |CITS: [27979649]|.  ViaA 
                     stimulates the ATPase activity of RavA.  The ViaA protein 
                     contains a VWA (Von Willebrand Factor Type A) domain |CITS:
                     [16301313]|.
                     Analysis of microarray and synthetic genetic array data 
                     suggests a functional link between ViaA and Fe-S cluster 
                     protein homeostasis as well as bacterial respiration |CITS:
                     [24454883]|.  ViaA interacts with a number of subunits of 
                     |FRAME: NADH-DHI-CPLX| |CITS: [24454883]| as well as 
                     |FRAME: FUM-FLAVO FrdA| |CITS: [27979649]|.  The N-terminal
                     domain of ViaA is responsible for interaction with RavA, 
                     while the C-terminal VWA domain is required for interaction
                     with with FrdA |CITS: [27979649]|.  Together with RavA, it 
                     negatively modulates the activity of the Frd complex |CITS:
                     [27979649]|.
                     A <i>viaA</i> deletion mutant shows increased production of
                     outer membrane vesicles, a phenotype that is associated 
                     with improved bacterial survival under stress |CITS: 
                     [17163978][22133164]|.  A <i>viaA</i> mutant reaches a 
                     higher cell density in stationary phase than wild type in 
                     the presence of sublethal levels of the aminoglycosides 
                     kanamycin or streptomycin; conversely, overexpression of 
                     RavA together with ViaA sensitizes cells to kanamycin. 
                     Deletion of certain subunits of |FRAME: NADH-DHI-CPLX|, 
                     |FRAME: SUCC-DEHASE SDH| and |FRAME: CYT-O-UBIOX-CPLX 
                     cytochrome bo| suppress this effect |CITS: [24454883]|. 
                     Expression of <i>ravA-viaA</i> is induced by FNR under 
                     oxygen-limited conditions |CITS: [27979649]|.
                     ViaA: ""<b>V</b>WA <b>i</b>nteracting with <b>A</b>AA+ 
                     <b>A</b>TPase"" |CITS: [16301313]|
                     "
