     gene            3929638..3930528
                     /gene="rbsB"
                     /locus_tag="b3751"
                     /label=rbsB
     CDS             3929638..3930528
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rbsB"
                     /locus_tag="b3751"
                     /product="trifunctional ribose ABC transporter periplasmic
                     binding protein / ribose ABC transporter / transport of 
                     D-ribose"
                     /EC_number="7.5.2.7"
                     /label=rbsB
                     /note="RbsB is the periplasmic ribose binding protein of
                     an ATP-dependent ribose uptake system; ligand bound RbsB 
                     also interacts with the |FRAME: EG11018 ""Trg""| sensory 
                     protein to mediate taxis to ribose.
                     The ribose binding protein is required for chemotaxis 
                     towards ribose; mutants lacking this protein do not 
                     demonstrate ribose mediated taxis |CITS: 
                     [4927373][339843]|. The RbsB molecule consists of two 
                     similar structured domains linked by a hinge region 
                     consisting of three short peptide stretches; bound 
                     &beta;-D-ribopyranose is completely enclosed in a cleft 
                     between the domains |CITS: [1583688]|. Non-liganded (open) 
                     structures of RbsB have also been obtained and 
                     conformational changes that the molecule undergoes during 
                     ligand binding and release are proposed |CITS: 
                     [9641984][8951381]|. Regions/residues of RbsB involved in 
                     interaction with RbsC and with the chemosensory receptor 
                     have been identified |CITS: [1304894][8878033]|
                     RbsB has been used in the development of a TNT bioreporter 
                     |CITS: [25005019]|.
                     <i>rbsB</i> was found to be downregulated in a MG1655 
                     lysogen carrying the Stx2a phage PA8 |CITS: 31208335|."
