     gene            complement(3932545..3933972)
                     /gene="hsrA"
                     /locus_tag="b3754"
                     /label=hsrA
     CDS             complement(3932545..3933972)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="hsrA"
                     /locus_tag="b3754"
                     /product="putative transporter HsrA"
                     /label=hsrA
                     /note="The HsrA protein is an uncharacterised member of
                     the Drug:H<sup>+</sup> Antiporter-2 (14 Spanner) (DHA2) 
                     Family within the Major Facilitator Superfamily (MFS) of 
                     transporters |CITS: [9529885][26546518]|.
                     Overexpression of cloned <I>hsrA</I> in a K-12 strain which
                     lacks the major efflux pump permease AcrB (<i>E. coli</i> 
                     KAM3; see |CITS: [12618449]|) does not impact resistance to
                     a range of toxic compounds (dyes, detergents, antibiotics 
                     and others) compared to the mutant parent 
                     |CITS:[11566977]|. Potential substrate candidates 
                     identified using an untargeted metabolomics approach 
                     include |FRAME: SER serine|, |FRAME: 2-HYDROXYGLUTARIC_ACID
                     hydroxyglutarate|, |FRAME: OROTATE|, and others |CITS: 
                     [38535289]|.
                     Overexpression of <i>hsrA</i> relieves the effect of 
                     overexpression of <i>rspA</i> on sigmaS expression.  HsrA 
                     is not a repressor of <i>rspA</i> expression or a direct 
                     activator of sigmaS expression |CITS: [10754234]|.] 
                     <i>hsrA</i> (<i>yieO</i>) is one of 35 efflux-encoding 
                     genes that have been deleted or inactivated in 'Efflux 
                     KnockOut-35' (EKO-35) -  a K-12 BW25133-derived strain that
                     lacks 35 efflux pumps and can be used as a platform to 
                     study their function |CITS: [36065018][36318669]|. HsrA: 
                     ""high copy suppressor of RspA"" |CITS: [10754234]|"
