     CDS             3941446..3941784
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="maoP"
                     /locus_tag="b3764"
                     /product="macrodomain Ori protein"
                     /label=maoP
                     /note="The MaoP protein and the |FRAME: MAOS <i>maoS</i>|
                     site, which is located in the intergenic region upstream of
                     <i>maoP</i>, are involved in the organization of the Ori 
                     macrodomain.  Together, they constrain the mobility of the 
                     Ori macrodomain |CITS: [27627105]|.
                     MaoP was identified in a phylogenetic screen that found 
                     proteins containing domains that only occur in organisms 
                     that also contain a |FRAME: EG10204-MONOMER Dam| 
                     methyltransferase |CITS: [16787973]|.
                     <i>maoP</i> belongs to a network of genes which facilitate 
                     stress-induced mutagenesis (SIM) in <i>E. coli</i> K-12 
                     |CITS: [23224554]|.  In a large-scale TraDIS screen, loss 
                     of <i>maoP</i> appeared to be beneficial for biofilm 
                     formation.  However, a <i>maoP</i> deletion mutant was 
                     deficient in biofilm formation |CITS: [34783647]|. 
                     Expression may be positively regulated by the small RNA 
                     RybB |CITS: [25891076]|.
                     MaoP: ""<b>ma</b>crodomain <b>O</b>ri <b>p</b>rotein"" 
                     |CITS: [27627105]|"
