     gene            complement(3952892..3953173)
                     /gene="ppiC"
                     /locus_tag="b3775"
                     /label=ppiC
     CDS             complement(3952892..3953173)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ppiC"
                     /locus_tag="b3775"
                     /product="bifunctional peptidyl-prolyl cis-trans isomerase
                     C / peptidyl-prolyl cis-trans isomerase"
                     /EC_number="5.2.1.8"
                     /label=ppiC
                     /note="<i>ppiC</i> encodes a peptidyl-prolyl
                     <i>cis-trans</i> isomerase (PPIase), parvulin, which 
                     defines a new family of PPIases |CITS: 
                     [7878731][7878732][8163020][7925971]|.  Unlike other 
                     PPIases, the enzymatic activity of parvulin is not 
                     inhibited by FK506 or cyclosporin A |CITS: [8163020]|.
                     The natural compound juglone specifically and irreversibly 
                     inactivates parvulin by covalent modification |CITS: 
                     [9558330]|.
                     |FRAME: EG11384-MONOMER AhpC| has been identified as a 
                     specific interaction partner of PpiC |CITS: [20806779]|. 
                     Additional substrates were identified by pull-down assays 
                     and co-IP |CITS: [32545723]|.
                     The stereospecificity of the enzyme has been studied |CITS:
                     [9720925]|, and a solution structure of PpiC has been 
                     determined |CITS: [15322281]|.  Mutants in predicted active
                     site residues were assayed for potential substrate binding 
                     and PPIase activity |CITS: [32545723]|.
                     A <i>ppiC</i> mutant is more sensitive to oxidative stress 
                     than wild type |CITS: [20806779]|.  A strain containing 
                     non-polar deletions of all six cytoplasmic PPIases 
                     (&Delta;6<i>ppi</i>) shows a growth defect at 37&deg;C in 
                     rich media and at 43&deg;C in both rich and minimal media 
                     |CITS: [32545723]|.
                     Resequencing of multiple isolates of the MG1655 strain has 
                     identified several genetic variations compared to the 
                     reference sequence, including a single-nucleotide 
                     polymorphism in the <i>yifO-ppiC</i> intergenic region 
                     |CITS: [22081388]|.  <a href=""http://ecoliwiki.net/colipe 
                     dia/index.php/Category:Strain:MG1655#Resequencing_of_MG1655
                     _and_comparison_to_the_reference_strain"">This EcoliWiki 
                     page</a> summarizes these sequence differences. PpiC: 
                     |CITS: [7878731]|
                     "
