     gene            3963493..3964623
                     /gene="wecB"
                     /locus_tag="b3786"
                     /label=wecB
     CDS             3963493..3964623
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="wecB"
                     /locus_tag="b3786"
                     /product="UDP-N-acetylglucosamine 2-epimerase"
                     /EC_number="5.1.3.14"
                     /label=wecB
                     /note="UDP-<i>N</i>-acetylmannosaminuronate (UDP-ManNAcUA)
                     is one of the building blocks for the cell surface 
                     polysaccharide enterobacterial common antigen (ECA). 
                     UDP-<i>N</i>-acetylglucosamine 2-epimerase catalyzes the 
                     first step in UDP-ManNAcUA biosynthesis, the reversible 
                     epimerization at the C-2 position between 
                     UDP-<i>N</i>-acetylglucosamine (UDP-GlcNAc) and 
                     UDP-<i>N</i>-acetylmannosamine (UDP-ManNAc) |CITS: 
                     [SALA96][MORGAN97]|.  Enzymatic activity requires the 
                     presence of UDP-GlcNAc as an activator |CITS: [MORGAN97]|. 
                     UDP-ManNAc synthesized by WecB is proposed to be the 
                     precursor for biosynthesis of a novel surface glycan that 
                     is required for bacteriophage N4 infection |CITS: 
                     [34903045][34903052]|.  Experiments with the BASEL 
                     collection of bacteriophages that infect <i>E. coli</i> 
                     showed that certain families of phages depend on the 
                     presence of WecB for infectivity |CITS: [34784345]|.
                     The reaction mechanism in the UDP-GlcNAc to UDP-ManNAc 
                     direction involves the <i>anti</i>-elimination of UDP from 
                     UDP-GlcNAc, generating the intermediate 2-acetamidoglucal, 
                     and followed by a <i>syn</i>-addition of UDP |CITS: 
                     [SALA96][MORGAN97]|.  A crystal structure of the enzyme has
                     been solved.  Each subunit of the homodimeric enzyme only 
                     contains a single substrate binding site, thus ruling out 
                     the possibility that regulation by UDP-GlcNAc is 
                     allosteric.  An interdomain rotation may be involved in 
                     regulation of catalytic activity |CITS: [11106477]|. 
                     Predicted active site residues were mutagenized, and their 
                     effect on substrate binding, catalysis, and regulation was 
                     analyzed |CITS: [15210128]|.
                     A <i>wecB</i> (<i>rffE</i>) mutation was isolated in a 
                     search for mutants that are defective in bacteriophage N4 
                     adsorption |CITS: [2670887][8226648]|.  A Tn<i>10</i> 
                     insertion mutant in <i>wecB</i> does not produce ECA |CITS:
                     [2166030]|.  Loss-of-function <i>wecB</i> mutations 
                     partially rescue the vancomycin sensitivity of |FRAME: 
                     CPLX0-2201 <i>tol-pal</i>| mutants |CITS: [32808719]|. 
                     Deletion of <i>wecB</i> partially suppresses the motility 
                     defect of a <i>pdeH ycgR</i> double mutant and confers 
                     resistance to infection by N4 |CITS: [34903052][34903045]|.
                     NfrC: ""<b>N</b> <b>f</b>our <b>r</b>esistance <b>C</b>"" 
                     |CITS: [2670887]|"
