     gene            3969638..3970888
                     /gene="wzxE"
                     /locus_tag="b3792"
                     /label=wzxE
     CDS             3969638..3970888
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="wzxE"
                     /locus_tag="b3792"
                     /product="lipid IIIECA flippase"
                     /label=wzxE
                     /note="The assembly of enterobacterial common antigen
                     (ECA) occurs by a Wzx/Wzy-dependent pathway (see |CITS: 
                     [32788387][25358682]|).
                     <i>wzxE</i> encodes lipid III<sub>ECA</sub> flippase - an 
                     inner membrane protein that mediates translocation, or 
                     'flipping', of the undecaprenyl pyrophosphate-linked 
                     trisaccharide repeating unit 
                     (Fuc4NAc-ManNAcA-GlcNAc-P-P-undecaprenol) of ECA across the
                     membrane bilayer |CITS: [12621029]|.
                     Null mutations in <i>wzxE</i> (<i>wzxE::cm</i>) result in 
                     accumulation of lipid III<sub>ECA</sub> which is lethal in 
                     the absence of the flippases |FRAME: G7097-MONOMER WzxC| 
                     for Und-PP-linked repeat units of colanic acid and |FRAME: 
                     RFBX-MONOMER WzxB| for Und-PP-linked repeat units of 
                     O-antigen |CITS: [12621029][16199561]| (and see |CITS: 
                     [40207904]|). WzxE mediates transport of the water soluble 
                     compound, N-acetylglucosaminylpyrophosphorylnerol 
                     (GlcNAc-P-P-Ner) into everted membrane vesicles; a 
                     pyrophosphoryl-linked saccharide and an unsaturated 
                     &alpha;-isoprene unit appear to be critical for 
                     WzeE-mediated transport |CITS: [12621029]|. Lipid 
                     III<sub>ECA</sub> flippase, ECA polymerase |FRAME: 
                     FUC4NACTRANS-MONOMER WzyE|, and co-polymerase |FRAME: 
                     EG11295 WzzE| may function as a multiprotein complex 
                     |CITS:[16816184]|. A <i>wzxE</i> knockout mutant (<i>E. 
                     coli</i> BW25113 &Delta;<i>wzxE</i>) is sensitive to acidic
                     growth media (< pH 6.7), to low-temperature (19 &Deg;C), 
                     and to high salt (300mM) stress, in a colanic acid 
                     synthesis-dependent manner |CITS: [40207904]|.
                     In the Transporter Classification Database |CITS: 
                     [26546518]|, Wzx flippases are part of the Polysaccharide 
                     Transporter (PST) family, within the 
                     Multidrug/Oligosaccharidyl-lipid/Polysaccharide (MOP) 
                     Flippase superfamily. Wzx flippases may translocate their 
                     substrate via a cation-dependent antiport mechanism (see 
                     |CITS: [28696276]|)."
