     CDS             3973316..3974056
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rffM"
                     /locus_tag="b3794"
                     /product="UDP-N-acetyl-D-mannosaminuronic acid
                     transferase"
                     /EC_number="2.4.1.180"
                     /label=rffM
                     /note="UDP-N-acetyl-D-mannosaminuronic acid transferase
                     (RffM) is involved in the biosynthesis of enterobacterial 
                     common antigen (ECA) catalyzing the transfer of Fuc4NAc 
                     (4-acetamido-4,6-dideoxy-D-galactose) from TDP-Fuc4NAc to 
                     ManNAcA-GlcNAc-pyrophosphorylundecaprenol, also known as 
                     ECA-lipid II |CITS: [3275612][2166030][3078744][ColiSalII]|
                     Mutants of rffM are defective in the synthesis of ECA-lipid
                     II |CITS: [2166030]|. Strains lacking WecG accumulate ECA 
                     intermediates, including novel diacylglycerol 
                     pyrophosphoryl (DAG-PP)-linked species |CITS: [32808719]|. 
                     The Keio collection <i>rffM</i> mutant exhibits a 'low 
                     level' of resistance to lithium exposure |CITS: 
                     [39983623]|."
