     CDS             3974247..3975632
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="thrP"
                     /locus_tag="b3795"
                     /product="threonine/serine:H(+) symporter ThrP"
                     /label=thrP
                     /note="ThrP (formerly YifK) is a proton-dependent, 
                     serine/threonine symporter - one of multiple known systems 
                     that mediate serine and threonine uptake |CITS: 
                     [37025642]|. ThrP contributes to threonine uptake in a 
                     threonine auxotrophic strain that lacks the threonine 
                     transporters |FRAME: YGJU-MONOMER SstT| and |FRAME: 
                     TDCC-MONOMER TdcC|; growth of an engineered MG1655-derived 
                     strain which contains ThrP as the single threonine carrier 
                     is inhibited by an excess of serine |CITS: [37025642]|. 
                     ThrP is a member of the Amino Acid Transporter (AAT) Family
                     within the Amino Acid-Polyamine-Organocation (APC) 
                     Superfamily |CITS: [10931886][24225317]|."
