                     /product="uroporphyrinogen-III synthase"
                     /EC_number="4.2.1.75"
                     /label=hemD
                     /note="Uroporphyrinogen III synthase catalyzes the
                     cyclization of hydroxymethylbilane with inversion of ring D
                     to form uroporphyrinogen III, the last common intermediate 
                     in the heme and corrin (B-12) pathways |CITS: 
                     [3040684][ColiSalII]|. Uroporphyrinogen III synthase forms 
                     a complex with hydroxymethylbilane synthase |CITS: 
                     [1747120][ColiSalII]|.
                     The <i>hemD</i> gene which encodes uroporphyrinogen III 
                     synthase has been cloned, and the product has been 
                     overexpressed, purified and characterized |CITS: [2557837 
                     ][3277628]|.  The <i>hemD</i> gene is adjacent to 
                     <i>hemC</i> and both genes appear to be transcribed by the 
                     same promoter |CITS: [3054815][3040684]|.
                     A group of hemin requiring mutants had defects in 
                     uroporphyrinogen III synthase |CITS: [387909]|."
