     gene            3987882..3988085
                     /gene="lptM"
                     /locus_tag="b4558"
                     /label=lptM
     CDS             3987882..3988085
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="lptM"
                     /locus_tag="b4558"
                     /product="LptD oxidative maturation-associated
                     lipoprotein"
                     /label=lptM
                     /note="<i>lptM</i> (formerly <i>yifL</i>) encodes a
                     lipoprotein that interacts with the |FRAME: CPLX0-7628 
                     outer membrane lipopolysaccharide (LPS) translocon| and 
                     promotes its efficient assembly at the BAM complex |CITS: 
                     [37821449][40674207]|. LptM promotes |FRAME: 
                     EG11569-MONOMER LptD| oxidative maturation; LptM acts 
                     synergistically with |FRAME: DISULFOXRED-MONOMER DsbA| in 
                     promoting proper oxidative maturation of LptD. LptM stably 
                     associates with LptDE forming a 1:1:1 heterotrimeric 
                     complex; LptM binds to sites in both LptD and |FRAME: 
                     EG10855-MONOMER LptE| that are important in coordinating 
                     LPS insertion into the outer membrane |CITS: [37821449]|. 
                     LptM interacts with LptD to facilitate the later stages of 
                     LptD maturation |CITS: [40674207]|.
                     LptM is a surface-exposed lipoprotein (SLP) that likely 
                     uses the periplasmic chaperone |FRAME: YHBN-MONOMER LptA| 
                     and the outer membrane translocon LptDE for surface 
                     translocation; cross-talk between lipoprotein and 
                     lipopolysaccharide trafficking pathways may be responsible 
                     for targeting a subset of SLPs (including LptM) to the 
                     outer membrane |CITS: [40348743]|.
                     Deletion of <i>lptM</i> impairs the oxidative maturation of
                     LptD and prolongs residence of LptD and LptE at the BAM 
                     complex |CITS: [37821449]|.
                     LptM is a lipoprotein conserved in <i>Enterobacteriacea</i>
                     |CITS: [37821449]|.
                     <i>lptM</i>: <U>Lpt</U>D oxidative 
                     <U>m</U>aturation-associated lipoprotein |CITS: 
                     [37821449]|."
