     CDS             3990543..3991259
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yigB"
                     /locus_tag="b3812"
                     /product="bifunctional
                     5-amino-6-(5-phospho-D-ribitylamino)uracil phosphatase / 
                     FMN phosphatase"
                     /EC_number="3.1.3.104; 3.1.3.102"
                     /label=yigB
                     /note="The identity of the enzyme(s) catalyzing the 
                     dephosphorylation of |FRAME: CPD-1086| in the riboflavin 
                     biosynthesis pathway was long unknown |CITS: 
                     [416855][colisalII]|.  |CITS: [24123841]| have now shown 
                     that at least two enzymes, YigB and YbjI, can catalyze this
                     reaction.
                     YigB was initially identified as an FMN phosphatase that 
                     belongs to the superfamily of haloacid dehalogenase 
                     (HAD)-like hydrolases |CITS: [16990279]|.
                     <i>yigB</i> is important for formation of dormant persister
                     cells; overexpression of <i>yigB</i> leads to increased 
                     tolerance to ofloxacin |CITS: [18519731]|. Deletion of 
                     <i>yigB</i> alone does not result in riboflavin auxotrophy 
                     |CITS: [16738554]|."
