     gene            3994786..3995736
                     /gene="corA"
                     /locus_tag="b3816"
                     /label=corA
     CDS             3994786..3995736
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="corA"
                     /locus_tag="b3816"
                     /product="multifunctional Ni(2+)/Co(2+)/Mg(2+) transporter
                     / Ni(2+) transporter / Co(2+) transporter / Mg(2+) 
                     transporter"
                     /label=corA
                     /note="CorA is an inner membrane magnesium ion transporter 
                     |CITS: [780341]|.
                     Kinetic analyses indicate that CorA is a constitutive 
                     magnesium, cobalt and manganese ion transport protein 
                     |CITS: [780341]|. A plasmid expressing <i>corA</i> from 
                     <i>E.coli</i> can complement a <i>Salmonella enterica 
                     corA</i> mutation and restore uptake of Co<sup>2+</sup> and
                     Mg<sup>2+</sup> |CITS: [3536881]|.
                     CorA is comprised of a large periplasmic domain and three 
                     membrane spanning helices |CITS: [8314774]|. The purified 
                     periplasmic domain of CorA functions as a homotetramer and 
                     is able to bind magnesium, cobalt and nickel ions |CITS: 
                     [16835234]|.
                     The well characterised CorA homolog from <i>Salmonella 
                     enterica</i> (which has 98% amino acid identity with <i>E. 
                     coli</i> CorA) mediates Mg<sup>2+</sup> - Mg<sup>2+</sup> 
                     exchange in addition to the import of magnesium, cobalt and
                     nickel ions |CITS: [2670893]|.
                     CorA is dependent on the Sec pathway for membrane 
                     integration |CITS: [8314774]|"
