                     /label=rarD
     CDS             complement(3996648..3997538)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rarD"
                     /locus_tag="b3819"
                     /product="putative transporter RarD"
                     /label=rarD
                     /note="RarD is predicted to be an inner membrane protein
                     with nine transmembrane domains; topology analysis suggests
                     the C- terminus is located in the cytoplasm |CITS: 
                     [15919996]|. RarD structure has been modelled |CITS: 
                     [26335199]|.
                     <i>rarD</i> expression increases under anaerobiosis |CITS: 
                     [12754220][15699038]| and decreases in an <i>fnr</i> 
                     deficient strain |CITS: [12754220]| and in an <i>arcA</i> 
                     deficient strain |CITS: [15699038]|.  A putative ArcA 
                     binding site is located 560 bp upstream of <i>rarD</i> 
                     |CITS: [15699038]| but no promoter has been identified.
                     In the Transporter Classification Database, RarD is a 
                     member of the Chloramphenicol-Sensitivitiy Protein (RarD) 
                     Family within the Drug/Metabolite Transporter (DMT) 
                     superfamily |CITS: [26546518]|. A variety of potential 
                     substrates have been identified using an untargeted 
                     metabolomics approach |CITS: [38535289]|."
