     gene            4001117..4001737
                     /gene="rhtC"
                     /locus_tag="b3823"
                     /label=rhtC
     CDS             4001117..4001737
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rhtC"
                     /locus_tag="b3823"
                     /product="bifunctional L-threonine exporter /
                     L-threonine:H(+) antiporter"
                     /label=rhtC
                     /note="RhtC can mediate the export of L-threonine; the 
                     physiological role of the transporter remains uncertain. 
                     Multicopy expression of <I>rhtC</I> confers resistance to 
                     high levels of threonine (50mg/mL) |CITS: [10386596]|. 
                     Multicopy expression of <i>rhtC</i> confers increased 
                     resistance to L-threonine but not to D-threonine, 
                     L-homoserine, D-homoserine, L-homoserine lactone nor a 
                     range of other amino acids |CITS: [12111147]| (see also 
                     |CITS: [12879215]|). Overexpression of <i>rhtC</i> 
                     increases threonine production in <i>E. coli</i> threonine 
                     producer strains |CITS: [12111147]|; heterologous 
                     expression of <i>rhtC</i> increases L-threonine production 
                     in <i>Corynebacterium glutamicum</i> threonine producing 
                     strains |CITS: [18594129]|.
                     RhtC is homologous to |FRAME: RHTB-MONOMER ""RhtB""|; 
                     proteins with homolgy to RhtB occur in a wide range of 
                     prokaryotes and form a family of putative transporters that
                     mediate metabolite export |CITS: [10322417]|. RhtC is a 
                     member of the Resistance to Homoserine/Threonine (RhtB) 
                     Family of transporters within the LysE superfamily; RhtC is
                     a probable substrate:H<sup>+</sup> antiporter |CITS: 
                     [26546518]|.
                     RhtC is predicted to be an inner membrane protein with 5 
                     transmembrane domains; experimental topology analysis 
                     suggests the C-terminus is located in the cytoplasm |CITS: 
                     [15919996]|
                     <i>rht</i>: <U>r</U>esistance to <U>h</U>omoserine and 
                     <U>t</U>hreonine |CITS: [10386596]|"
