     gene            complement(4001799..4002419)
                     /gene="rhtB"
                     /locus_tag="b3824"
                     /label=rhtB
     CDS             complement(4001799..4002419)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rhtB"
                     /locus_tag="b3824"
                     /product="multifunctional L-homoserine/L-homoserine 
                     lactone/L-threonine exporter / homoserine:H(+) antiport / 
                     L-homoserine lactone:H(+) antiport / L-threonine:H(+) 
                     antiport"
                     /label=rhtB
                     /note="RhtB can mediate the export of L-homoserine,
                     L-homoserine lactone and L-threonine; the physiological 
                     role of the transporter remains uncertain.
                     Multicopy expression of <i>rhtB</i> confers increased 
                     resistance to L-homoserine, L-homoserine lactone, 
                     L-threonine |CITS: [10386596][12111147][12879215]|, 
                     S-methyl methionine |CITS: [12111147]| and possibly 
                     L-serine |CITS: [10386596]|. Disruption or deletion of 
                     <i>rhtB</i> decreases resistance to L-homoserine and 
                     L-homoserine lactone |CITS: [10386596][12879215]|, L-serine
                     and DL-&beta;-hydroxynorvaline |CITS: [10386596]| and 
                     L-threonine |CITS: [12879215]|. Multicopy expression of 
                     <I>rhtB</I> increases homoserine production in homoserine 
                     producer strains of <i>E. coli</i>; disruption of 
                     <i>rhtB</i> (<i>rhtB::cat</i>) decreases production |CITS: 
                     [10386596]|. Multicopy expression of <i>rhtB</i> increases 
                     threonine production in a threonine producing strain of 
                     <i>E. coli</i> |CITS: [12111147]|.
                     RhtB contains 6 predicted transmembrane regions |CITS: 
                     [10386596]| and is the prototype member of the Resistance 
                     to Homoserine/Threonine (RhtB) family of transporters 
                     within the LysE superfamily |CITS: [10322417][26546518]|. 
                     <i>rht</i>: <U>r</U>esistance to <U>h</U>omoserine and 
                     <U>t</U>hreonine |CITS: [10386596]|."
