     gene            4003560..4004360
                     /gene="yigL"
                     /locus_tag="b3826"
                     /label=yigL
     CDS             4003560..4004360
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yigL"
                     /locus_tag="b3826"
                     /product="trifunctional phosphosugar phosphatase YigL /
                     pyridoxal phosphatase / phosphosugar phosphatase"
                     /EC_number="3.1.3.74; 3.1.3.23"
                     /label=yigL
                     /note="YigL is a phosphosugar phosphatase that is required
                     for response to phosphosugar stress under conditions of 
                     limited nutrient availability |CITS: [23873911]|. YigL 
                     belongs to the superfamily of haloacid dehalogenase 
                     (HAD)-like hydrolases. It shows a low level of 
                     discrimination between its preferred substrates  Purine and
                     pyrimidine nucleotides are secondary substrates |CITS: 
                     [16990279]|.
                     A <i>yigL</i> deletion mutant phenocopies the growth defect
                     of &Delta;<i>sgrS</i> in the presence of 
                     &alpha;-methylglucose (&alpha;MG) or 2-deoxyglucose |CITS: 
                     [23582330]|; in MOPS minimal medium with glycerol and 
                     &alpha;MG, a &Delta;<i>yigL</i> strain is significantly 
                     outcompeted by its wild type parent |CITS: [23873911]|. 
                     Direct upregulation of YigL expression by SgrS was 
                     initially shown in <i>Salmonella</i> |CITS: [23582330]| and
                     confirmed for <i>E. coli</i> |CITS: [23873911]|; SgrS 
                     appears to block RNase E from scanning for its cleavage 
                     site |CITS: [30852060]|."
