                     /label=bioP
     CDS             4004436..4005335
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="bioP"
                     /locus_tag="b3827"
                     /product="biotin transporter"
                     /label=bioP
                     /note="YigM is a biotin transporter in <i>E. coli</i> K-12
                     The uptake of labeled biotin is abolished in an <i>E. 
                     coli</i> &Delta;<i>yigM</i> strain (Keio collection strain 
                     K-12 BW25113); overexpression of YigM results in increased 
                     biotin uptake in both the wild type and in a 
                     &Delta;<i>yigM</i> strain; uptake assays in whole cells and
                     in membrane vesicles suggest biotin is taken up by 
                     facilitated diffusion |CITS: [RINGSLSTETTER10]|.
                     Biotin transport in <I>E. coli</I> K-12 (strains Y10-1 and 
                     54117-Pasteur collection) is an active process and  is 
                     inhibited by uncouplers |CITS:[4616949][3890946]|. Biotin 
                     transport is regulated by the concentration of biotin in 
                     the medium with reduced transport at higher biotin 
                     concentrations |CITS:[4583224]|. Biotinylated peptides up 
                     to 31 amino acids long can be taken up by <I>E. coli</I> 
                     through the biotin transport system |CITS:[15812011]|. YigM
                     is predicted to contain 10 transmembrane domains with the C
                     and N-termini located in the cytoplasm |CITS: 
                     [RINGSLSTETTER10]|.
                     Expression of a <i>yigM</i> promoter reporter decreases 
                     with increasing concentration of biotin; a putative 
                     truncated BirA binding site is located in the promoter 
                     region of YigM |CITS: [RINGSLSTETTER10]|. <I>yigM </I> may 
                     have a &sigma;<sup>54</sup>-dependent promoter 
                     |CITS:[11528004]|.  Expression of <I>yigM</I> is induced by
                     acivicin |CITS:[11344143]|.  Expression of <I>yigM</I> of 
                     <I>E. coli</I> O157:H7 Sakai strain is reduced upon entry 
                     into stationary phase |CITS:[17967175]|."
