     CDS             4009791..4010552
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="udp"
                     /locus_tag="b3831"
                     /product="uridine phosphorylase"
                     /EC_number="2.4.2.3"
                     /label=udp
                     /note="Uridine phosphorylase (Udp) catalyzes the
                     reversible phosphorolysis of uridine with the formation of 
                     ribose-1-phosphate and uracil |CITS: [16751]|.  Udp belongs
                     to the UP-1 subfamily of the nucleoside phosphorylase 
                     superfamily 1 |CITS: [22967797]|.  Udp is involved in 
                     utilization of nucleosides as a carbon and energy source 
                     |CITS: [4932245]| and is part of a process that degrades 
                     ""overflow"" UMP nucleotides |CITS: [23903661]|.
                     The main activity of Udp is towards uracil ribonucleotides,
                     but some activity is retained towards deoxyuridine and 
                     thymidine |CITS: [16751]|.  The substrate specificity of 
                     the enzyme has been evaluated using a large set of modified
                     nucleosides |CITS: [27846376]|.  The catalytic mechanism 
                     has been investigated |CITS: [7982499][7578229]|.  The Asp5
                     carboxyl group is important for catalysis |CITS: 
                     [7730307]|.
                     Various crystal structures of the enzyme alone or bound to 
                     substrates or inhibitors have been determined |CITS: [3546 
                     298][1610370][7796917][12499542][15003451][15983408][203648
                     33]|. The enzyme forms a toroidal homohexamer that can be 
                     described as a trimer of dimers.  The presence of substrate
                     induces conformational changes, closing the active site 
                     cleft |CITS: [15003451]|.  Putative substrate binding 
                     residues in the active site were investigated by 
                     site-directed mutagenesis |CITS: [15115774]|.
                     A proteomics approach identified Udp as an ATP-binding 
                     protein whose stability appears to be decreased in the 
                     presence of ATP |CITS: [22733688]|.  Both protein stability
                     and enzymatic activity are decreased by increasing levels 
                     of ATP <i>in vitro</i> |CITS: [28917600]|.
                     A <i>udp</i> mutant in a <i>upp deoA</i> mutant background 
                     can not utilize uridine as the sole source of carbon |CITS:
                     [4932245]|.  Increased Udp levels allow a <i>deoAB</i> 
                     mutant to grow on thymine |CITS: [1089630]|. Uridine 
                     phosphorylase is induced by the presence of cytidine |CITS:
                     [4559263]|.  Expression is regulated by cAMP-CRP and CytR 
                     |CITS: [10347150][12667072]|.
                     Comment: |CITS: [23903659]|
                     Review: |CITS: [11743878]|"
