     gene            4025852..4026466
                     /gene="yigZ"
                     /locus_tag="b3848"
                     /label=yigZ
     CDS             4025852..4026466
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yigZ"
                     /locus_tag="b3848"
                     /product="colonization factor YigZ"
                     /label=yigZ
                     /note="<i>yigZ</i> is a widely conserved gene; its
                     mammalian homolog is the imprinted (paternally expressed) 
                     mouse gene
                     <i>impact</i> |CITS: [9256468]|.
                     A crystal structure of YigZ has been solved at 2.8 &Aring; 
                     resolution. The C-terminal domain shows weak structural 
                     similarity to elongation factors and suggests that the 
                     protein may bind nucleic acids |CITS: 
                     [15103642][16021622]|.
                     In a large genetic interaction screen, <i>yigZ</i> showed 
                     genetic interactions with a number of proteins involved in 
                     translation and ribosome biogenesis. A &Delta;<i>yigZ</i> 
                     mutant shows increased levels of stop codon readthrough 
                     |CITS: [27732863]|. In a large-scale TraDIS screen, fewer 
                     <i>yigZ</i> mutants were found in biofilm conditions 
                     compared to planktonic growth |CITS: [34783647]|.
                     The <i>yigZ</i> ortholog from commensal <i>E. coli</i> M13 
                     strain has two amino acid differences from strain MG1655 at
                     residues 25 and 146. When this ortholog is overexpressed in
                     strain MG1655, the colonization in mice increased 
                     substantially indicating the allelic variation in YigZ that
                     confers colonization capacity. YigZ is found throughout 
                     major gut colonizing microbes and is considered a conserved
                     gut colonization factor |CITS: [40286794]|."
