     gene            complement(4034775..4035359)
                     /gene="mobA"
                     /locus_tag="b3857"
                     /label=mobA
     CDS             complement(4034775..4035359)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="mobA"
                     /locus_tag="b3857"
                     /product="bifunctional molybdenum cofactor
                     guanylyltransferase / bis(molybdenum cofactor) synthase"
                     /EC_number="2.7.7.77"
                     /label=mobA
                     /note="MobA is required for the biosynthesis of the 
                     molybdopterin guanine dinucleotide (MGD) cofactor |CITS: 
                     [1648082]|. The enzyme catalyzes the transfer of a GMP 
                     moiety from GTP to Mo-molybdopterin, forming MGD |CITS: 
                     [21081498]|. The MGD cofactor can be further modified to 
                     |FRAME: CPD-15873 ""bis-MGD""|. Formation of bis-MGD is 
                     proposed to involve formation of a |FRAME: CPD-15874 
                     ""bis-Mo-MPT""| intermediate followed by the addition of 
                     two GMP moieties by MobA. This cofactor is then transferred
                     to its target protein TorA |CITS: [24003231]|. MobA is 
                     monomeric in solution |CITS: [8020507]|. Crystal structures
                     of MobA have been solved |CITS: 
                     [10978347][11080634][12719427]|. Site-directed mutagenesis 
                     of conserved residues showed that Gly15 is essential for 
                     MobA function, and Gly82 stabilizes the product-bound form 
                     of the enzyme |CITS: [12719427]|. The enzyme's specificity 
                     for GTP was also investigated |CITS: [21081498]|.
                     MobA directly interacts with both MoeA and MobB |CITS: 
                     [12372836]|. In the presence of the enzyme-specific 
                     chaperone NarJ and the mature molybdenum cofactor, MobA, 
                     MobB, MoeA and MogA interact with apo-NarG |CITS: 
                     [15247236]|. TorD may act as the enzyme-specific chaperone 
                     for molybdenum cofactor insertion into TorA |CITS: 
                     [18522945]|.
                     A <i>mobA</i> mutant contains elevated levels of 
                     molybdopterin, but no detectable molybdopterin guanine 
                     dinucleotide (MGD) |CITS: [1648082]|.
                     The <i>mob</i> locus is expressed at a low level under both
                     aerobic and anaerobic growth conditions |CITS: [7551035]|.
                     <i>mobA</i> was initially identified as one of several 
                     genes that, when mutated, result in resistance to chlorate.
                     Chlorate resistance of the <i>chlB</i> mutants is the 
                     result of inactive nitrate reductase, which is a 
                     molybdoenzyme |CITS: [4404057][7026535]|.
                     ChlB: ""chlorate resistance""
                     MobA: ""<b>mo</b>lybdenum cofactor biosynthesis, 
                     <i>chl<b>B</b></i> group, gene <b>A</b> |CITS: [1484496]| 
                     Reviews: |CITS: [9388540][12504674][23201473][25268953]|"
