     gene            4035775..4036761
                     /gene="srkA"
                     /locus_tag="b3859"
                     /label=srkA
     CDS             4035775..4036761
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="srkA"
                     /locus_tag="b3859"
                     /product="bifunctional stress response kinase A /
                     serine/threonine protein kinase"
                     /EC_number="2.7.11.1"
                     /label=srkA
                     /note="SrkA is a serine/threonine protein kinase that
                     protects cells from several types of lethal stress |CITS: 
                     [17302814][23416055]|.  SrkA is able to autophosphorylate 
                     at serine and threonine, but not tyrosine residues |CITS: 
                     [17302814]|.  The protein kinase activity is required for 
                     stress protection by SrkA |CITS: [23416055]|.
                     SrkA is also able to phosphorylate a general kinase 
                     substrate, myelin basic protein, <i>in vitro</i>.  The 
                     native substrate for SrkA has not been identified yet 
                     |CITS: [17302814]|.
                     A crystal structure of SrkA has been determined at 2.8 
                     &Aring; resolution and shows structural similarity to 
                     protein kinases |CITS: [17302814]|.
                     A D217A mutation abolishes catalytic activity |CITS: 
                     [17302814]|.  A &Delta;<i>srkA</i> mutant is 
                     hypersusceptible to the lethal effects of UV light, 
                     hydrogen peroxide, nalidixic acid and certain other 
                     antibiotics, but does not affect their minimum inhibitory 
                     concentration (MIC).  Deletion of <i>mazEF</i> rescues the 
                     hypersusceptibility phenotype of the &Delta;<i>srkA</i> 
                     mutant |CITS: [23416055]|.
                     The <i>dsbA</i> gene is partly cotranscribed from the 
                     <i>srkA</i> promoter, which is activated by CpxR |CITS: 
                     [7881552][9159398]|.  A <i>yihE</i> insertion mutation 
                     decreases the abundance of periplasmic DsbA, but does not 
                     appear to affect periplasmic disulfide bond formation 
                     |CITS: [7881552]|.
                     RdoA is the YihE homolog in <i>Salmonella enterica</i> 
                     serovar Typhimurium |CITS: [12511488][17302814]| and 
                     <i>Shigella flexneri</i> |CITS: [11594757]|, where it is 
                     involved in cellular stress responses.
                     SrkA: ""<b>s</b>tress <b>r</b>esponse <b>k</b>inase 
                     <b>A</b>"" |CITS: [23416055]|"
