     gene            complement(4039030..4039962)
                     /gene="yihG"
                     /locus_tag="b3862"
                     /label=yihG
     CDS             complement(4039030..4039962)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yihG"
                     /locus_tag="b3862"
                     /product="bifunctional 1-acylglycerol-3-phosphate
                     O-acyltransferase YihG / 1-acylglycerol-3-phosphate 
                     O-acyltransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.3.1.51"
                     /label=yihG
                     /note="<i>yihG</i> encodes a membrane-bound 
                     1-acylglycerol-3-phosphate <i>O</i>-acyltransferase (also 
                     called lysophosphatidic acid acyltransferase or LPAAT for 
                     short) .
                     Analysis of the phospholipid composition of cells 
                     overproducing YihG suggests that the enzyme facilitates 
                     synthesis of phospholipids containing <i>cis</i>-vaccenoyl 
                     (18:1) and myristoyl (14:0) at the <i>sn</i>-2 position and
                     preferably introduces these groups into lysophospholipids 
                     containing <i>cis</i>-vaccenoyl (18:1) at the <i>sn</i>-1 
                     position |CITS: [32403425]|. Analysis of the phospholipid 
                     composition of &Delta;<i>yihG</i> cells grown at 37&deg;C 
                     suggests that the endogenous enzyme transfers 
                     <i>cis</i>-vaccenoyl (18:1) from acyl donor substrates 
                     (acyl-acyl carrier protein or coenzyme A) to the 
                     <i>sn</i>-2 position of membrane phospholipids |CITS: 
                     [32403425]|. Purified YihG prefers |FRAME: 
                     TETRADECANOYL-COA myristoyl-CoA| (14:0-CoA) as acyl-CoA 
                     donor but also uses both saturated and unsaturated fatty 
                     acyl-CoAs with other chain lengths (eg 12:0-CoA, 16:0-CoA 
                     and 16:1-CoA); the enzyme is active with |FRAME: 
                     Lysophosphatidates lysophosphatidates| but not with |FRAME:
                     Lysophosphatidylethanolamines 
                     lysophosphatidylethanolamines| nor with |FRAME: 
                     Lysophosphatidylglycerols lysophosphatidylglyerols| |CITS: 
                     [39727331]|.
                     Overexpression of <i>yihG</i> suppresses the the 
                     temperature-sensitive growth defect of the |FRAME: EG11377 
                     ""<i>plsC</i>""| mutation present in <i>E. coli</i> strain 
                     JC201 |CITS: [32403425][2211622]|. Overexpression of 
                     <i>yihG</i> suppresses the cold sensitivity of a 
                     &Delta;|FRAME: G7313 ""<i>hda</i>""| mutant |CITS: 
                     [28130843]|.
                     YihG is implicated in flagellar formation; loss of 
                     <i>yihG</i> (in the poorly motile |FRAME: TAX-679895|) is 
                     associated with high production of |FRAME: EG10321-MONOMER 
                     ""FliC""| and enhanced swimming motility |CITS: 
                     [32403425]|.
                     YihG was originally suggested to function as a second 
                     poly(A) polymerase |CITS: [8876178]|; later work refuted 
                     this |CITS: [10594834]|.
                     YihG is predicted to be a bitopic inner membrane protein 
                     |CITS: [27510400]|.
                     Transcription of <i>yihG</i> is induced during stationary 
                     phase; the gene is transcribed from a &sigma;<sup>S</sup> 
                     promoter |CITS: [10594834]|."
