     gene            complement(4043493..4044125)
                     /gene="yihA"
                     /locus_tag="b3865"
                     /label=yihA
     CDS             complement(4043493..4044125)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yihA"
                     /locus_tag="b3865"
                     /product="GTP-binding protein YihA"
                     /label=yihA
                     /note="YihA is essential for normal cell division |CITS: 
                     [9743119][10572302]|.  YihA is the founding member of a 
                     family of putative GTPases |CITS: [11200227]|.
                     Depletion causes late-stage cell cycle arrest with 
                     filamentous cell morphology, indicative of a defect in cell
                     division |CITS: [10572302]|.  This filamentation is 
                     partially suppressed by FtsZ overproduction and is 
                     suppressed by FtsQI,
                     FtsA, and FtsZ co-overproduction |CITS: [10572302]|.
                     YihA shows conserved GTPase motifs, indicating that YihA 
                     may have GTPase activity |CITS: [10572302]|.  Purified YihA
                     protein specifically binds guanine nucleotides and has 
                     extremely low GTPase activity; mutational studies confirm 
                     that the predicted GTP-binding domain is involved in 
                     nucleotide binding |CITS: [12880769]|.
                     Reviews: |CITS: [11200227][16333325][21675921][21885683]| "
