     gene            complement(4049788..4049981)
                     /gene="glnZ"
                     /locus_tag="b4836"
                     /label=glnZ
     misc_RNA        complement(4049788..4049981)
                     /gene="glnZ"
                     /locus_tag="b4836"
                     /product="small regulatory RNA GlnZ"
                     /note="GlnZ is a small regulatory RNA that is 
                     post-transcriptionally regulated by Hfq |CITS: 
                     [36062564][15718303]| and regulates genes related to 
                     nitrogen and carbon efflux |CITS: [36062564]|. GlnZ is 
                     cleaved by the endonuclease RNase III, which suggests that 
                     GlnZ forms double-stranded secondary structures creating 
                     stem loops |CITS: [36062564]|.
                     Operons that contain the genes <i>gln</i> produce two small
                     transcripts, GlnZ194 and GlnZ174, through RNA processing, 
                     but only GlnZ194 contains the putative sequence that 
                     recognizes the targets of GlnZ |CITS: [36062564]|.
                     Potential targets of GlnZ were identified by applying two 
                     technologies, RNA interaction by ligation and sequencing 
                     (RIL-seq) and MS2-affinity purification coupled with RNA 
                     sequencing (MAPS) |CITS: [36062564]|. Although the sequence
                     of GlnZ varies across bacterial species, it shows similar 
                     regulation and targets |CITS: [36062564]|.
                     The <i>glnZ</i> expression is induced by nitrogen 
                     starvation and diminished ketoglutarate and glutamine 
                     |CITS: [36062564]|. Glutamine affects the expression of 
                     GlnZ at a post-transcriptional level |CITS: [36062564]|. 
                     RIL-seq experiments with cells grown in various nitrogen 
                     (N) growth conditions found that the Hfq-dependent GlnZ-RNA
                     interactions were found under all four conditions tested 
                     (N-replete, N-starved, N-starved for 24 hrs, and 2 hrs 
                     after N added to 24 hr N-starved) and included new mRNA 
                     targets, in particular |FRAME: G7072|, under N-starvation 
                     conditions |CITS: [38142457]|.
                     Review: |CITS: [38061078]|"
