     CDS             4053807..4054517
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yihL"
                     /locus_tag="b3872"
                     /product="putative DNA-binding transcriptional regulator
                     YihL"
                     /label=yihL
                     /note="The YihL putative transcriptional regulator belongs
                     to the GntR family |CITS: [12582243][15608167][ 35880217]|.
                     This protein contains a helix-turn-helix motif to bind DNA 
                     in its N-terminal domain, and it was predicted to regulate 
                     genes related to metabolism |CITS: [35880217]|.
                     Genome-wide YihL binding sites were determined <i>in 
                     vivo</i> by the chromatin immunoprecipitation method 
                     combined with lambda exonuclease digestion (ChIP-exo) in 
                     glucose M9 minimal medium |CITS: [34428301]|.
                     The transcription of the <i>yihL</i> gene is affected by 
                     temperature and oxidative stress |CITS: [35880217]|.
                     YihL was transcriptionally upregulated in iron excess over 
                     iron limitation at 63% dissolved oxygen as determined by 
                     RNA-seq |CITS:[ 35777694]|."
