                     /gene="yihP"
                     /locus_tag="b3877"
                     /product="putative 2,3-dihydroxypropane-1-sulfonate export
                     protein"
                     /label=yihP
                     /note="<i>yihP</i> is part of a 10 gene cluster which is 
                     conserved across <i>E. coli</i> species and has been 
                     implicated in sulfoquinovose catabolism. The YihP protein 
                     may function to export |FRAME: 
                     2-3-dihydroxypropane-1-sulfonate| (an end-product of 
                     sulfoquinovose catabolism) but it has not been 
                     experimentally characterised |CITS: [24463506]|. The YihP 
                     protein is a member of the glycoside-pentoside-hexuronide 
                     (GPH) cation symporter family of transporters |CITS: 
                     [8830272], [24225317]|."
