     gene            complement(4060600..4062636)
                     /gene="yihQ"
                     /locus_tag="b3878"
                     /label=yihQ
     CDS             complement(4060600..4062636)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yihQ"
                     /locus_tag="b3878"
                     /product="sulfoquinovosidase"
                     /EC_number="3.2.1.199"
                     /label=yihQ
                     /note="Sulfoquinovosidase (YihQ) catalyzes the hydrolysis
                     of terminal non-reducing sulfoquinovoside residues in 
                     sulfoquinovosyl diacylglycerides and sulfoquinovosyl 
                     glycerol, releasing the &alpha; anomer of sulfoquinovose 
                     |CITS: [26878550]|.  Sulfoquinovosyl glycerol can serve as 
                     the sole source of carbon and energy via the |FRAME: 
                     PWY-7446| pathway |CITS: [30276262]|.
                     YihQ is a member of the glycosyl hydrolase 31 family.  The 
                     best tested substrate was &alpha;-glucosyl fluoride; the 
                     physiological substrate of the enzyme was unknown at the 
                     time |CITS: [15294295]|.
                     Crystal structures of the enzyme have been solved |CITS: 
                     [26878550][30276262]| and show an 
                     (&alpha;&beta;)<sub>8</sub> barrel followed by a 
                     &beta;-sheet domain.  Within the active site, D405 may 
                     serve as the catalytic nucleophile and D472 may serve as 
                     the catalytic acid-base residue.  Mutations in these 
                     residues (D405A, D405N, D472A and D472N) render the enzyme 
                     catalytically inactive.  The W304, R301 and Y508 residues 
                     may have roles in the specific recognition of the sulfonate
                     moiety |CITS: [26878550]|.
                     Expression of YihQ is induced by growth on |FRAME: 
                     CPD-10247| |CITS: [24463506]|.
                     Review: |CITS: [22146713]|"
                     /translation="MDTPRPQLLDFQFHQNNDSFTLHFQQRLILTHSKDNPCLWIGSGI
