     gene            complement(4063875..4065116)
                     /gene="yihS"
                     /locus_tag="b3880"
                     /label=yihS
     CDS             complement(4063875..4065116)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yihS"
                     /locus_tag="b3880"
                     /product="bifunctional sulfoquinovose isomerase / mannose 
                     isomerase"
                     /EC_number="5.3.1.31; 5.3.1.7"
                     /label=yihS
                     /note="Sulfoquinovose isomerase (YihS) catalyzes the 
                     isomerization to |FRAME: CPD-16501| |CITS: [24463506]|, a 
                     part of the |FRAME: PWY-7446| pathway.
                     YihS has mannose isomerase activity <i>in vitro</i>. 
                     Predicted active site residues were analyzed by 
                     site-directed
                     mutagenesis.  A crystal structure of the enzyme has been 
                     solved at 2.5 &Aring; resolution |CITS: [18328504]|.
                     YihS may be identical to the enzyme first identified by 
                     |CITS: [796410][7033464]|, although the quarternary 
                     structure
                     differs.  The mannose isomerase identified in |CITS: 
                     [7033464]| is a tetramer in solution, while YihS is a 
                     hexamer
                     |CITS: [18328504]|.
                     Expression of YihS is induced by growth on sulfoquinovose 
                     |CITS: [24463506]| and lactose |CITS: [29453395]|.  A 
                     <i>yihS</i> mutant is unable to grow on sulfoquinovose as 
                     the sole source of carbon |CITS: [24463506]|.
                     In the absence of ppGpp (&Delta;<i>relA spoT</i>), 
                     overproduction of YihS reduces the growth rate and 
                     increases persistence |CITS: [26837570]|."
                     /translation="MKWFNTLSHNRWLEQETDRIFDFGKNSVVPTGFGWLGNKGQIKEE
