     CDS             complement(4075217..4076119)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="fdoH"
                     /locus_tag="b3893"
                     /product="multifunctional formate dehydrogenase O subunit
                     beta / formate dehydrogenase O subcomplex / formate 
                     dehydrogenase O / formate dehydrogenase"
                     /EC_number="1.17.5.3"
                     /label=fdoH
                     /note="<i>fdoH</i> encodes the &beta; subunit of formate 
                     dehydrogenase O. It has 100% amino acid identity with FdnH,
                     the [4Fe-4S] containing &beta; subunit of formate 
                     dehydrogenase-N.
                     FdoH is essentially hydrophilic in nature with one 
                     predicted &alpha; helical region at the C-terminus. The 
                     topological orientation of FdoH appears to be the reverse 
                     of FdnH, with the bulk of the protein located in the 
                     cytoplasm |CITS: [9852007]| however the use or reporter 
                     fusions to determine toplogy of Tat-dependent proteins has 
                     been brought into question |CITS: [11929547]|."
