                     dehydrogenase O / formate dehydrogenase"
                     /EC_number="1.17.5.3"
                     /label=fdoG
                     /note="<i>fdoG</i> encodes the &alpha; subunit of formate 
                     dehydrogenase O. It has 75% amino acid identity with 
                     |FRAME: FDNG-MONOMER FdnG| - the catalytic, molybdopterin 
                     cofactor containing &alpha; subunit of formate 
                     dehydrogenase-N. It contains an in-frame TGA (opal) codon 
                     that specifies selenocysteine |CITS: [8346018]|.
                     Topology analysis suggests that FdoG is located in the 
                     cytoplasm |CITS: [9852007]|; however, the use or reporter 
                     fusions to determine toplogy of Tat-dependent proteins has 
                     been brought into question |CITS: [11929547]|."
