                     /product="peptidase M42 family protein FrvX"
                     /label=frvX
                     /note="<I>frvX</I> is a member of the <I>frvABXR</I>
                     operon which encodes a putative fructose-specific 
                     PEP-dependent sugar phosphotransferase system 
                     |CITS:[8019415]|. <I>frvX</I> is predicted to encode a 
                     water soluble protein of unknown function |CITS:[8019415]|.
                     Experiments with plasmid-borne <I>lux</I>-promoter fusions 
                     show <I>frvX</I> is upregulated
                     during growth with sulfometuron methyl, which inhibits the 
                     first enzyme of valine and isoleucine biosynthesis 
                     |CITS:[9473030]|. <I>frvX</I> was also shown to be 
                     upregulated during growth with nalidixic acid 
                     |CITS:[11544210]|."
