                     /gene="rhaM"
                     /locus_tag="b3901"
                     /product="L-rhamnose mutarotase"
                     /EC_number="5.1.3.32"
                     /label=rhaM
                     /note="Utilizing NMR techniques, RhaM was shown to
                     catalyze the anomeric conversion of rhamnose |CITS: 
                     [15060078]|.  The enzyme has a preference for binding the 
                     &beta;-anomer |CITS: [15876375]|.
                     A crystal structure of RhaM in complex with L-rhamnose was 
                     solved at 1.8 &Aring; resolution.  Analysis of the 
                     catalytic activity of mutants in predicted active site 
                     residues allowed the authors to propose a possible 
                     catalytic mechanism |CITS: [15876375]|.
                     A <i>rhaM</i> deletion mutant has a decreased growth rate 
                     when grown on low concentrations of L-rhamnose |CITS: 
                     [15876375]|."
