     gene            complement(4089419..4090453)
                     /gene="rhaT"
                     /locus_tag="b3907"
                     /label=rhaT
     CDS             complement(4089419..4090453)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rhaT"
                     /locus_tag="b3907"
                     /product="trifunctional rhamnose/lyxose:H(+) symporter /
                     transport of rhamnose / transport of L-lyxose"
                     /label=rhaT
                     /note="RhaT is the sole transporter for rhamnose in <I>E. 
                     coli</I> and functions as a rhamnose/proton symporter. 
                     <I>rhaT</I> mutants were unable to utilise or transport 
                     rhamnose, and this defect could be complemented by the 
                     cloned <I>rhaT</I> gene |CITS: [1551902]|. Studies in 
                     membrane vesicles have shown that RhaT can transport 
                     rhamnose with moderate affinity (20-40 &mu;M) and that 
                     rhamnose transport is coupled with proton transport
                     |CITS: [8384447]|. RhaT is also able to transport L-lyxose 
                     |CITS:[1650346]|. RhaT is the prototype member of the RhaT 
                     family of transporters. Analysis of RhaT-BlaZ fusions has 
                     indicated that the RhaT protein contains 10 transmembrane 
                     segments |CITS: [8262918]|. Expression of <I>rhaT</I> is 
                     induced by rhamnose in a process involving RhaS and RhaT 
                     |CITS: [8757746]|. An inhibitory effect on <i>rhaT</i> 
                     induced by rhamnose appears in the presence of a higher 
                     concentration of arabinose or xylose |CITS:[ 29140539]|."
