                     /label=kdgT
     CDS             4091618..4092601
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="kdgT"
                     /locus_tag="b3909"
                     /product="bifunctional 2-dehydro-3-deoxy-D-gluconate:H(+)
                     symporter / transport of 2-dehydro-3-deoxy-D-gluconate"
                     /label=kdgT
                     /note="KdgT is a probable 2-keto-3-deoxy-D-gluconate (KDG) 
                     uptake system. The cloned <I>kdgT</I> gene increased uptake
                     of KDG and to a lesser extent glucuronate |CITS: [6094479]|
                     and could complement the KDG transport defect in 
                     <I>kdgT</I> mutants. KDG transport has been shown in whole 
                     cells and membrane vesicles to be via proton symport |CITS:
                     [15555]|. KdgT is the prototype representative of the KdgT 
                     family of KDG transporters.  Expression of <I>kdgT</I> is 
                     inducible by KDG and is under the control of the KdgR 
                     repressor |CITS: [4359651]|. Imported KDG is subsequently 
                     degraded to pyruvate and triose-phosphate."
