     CDS             4099858..4100613
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="cdh"
                     /locus_tag="b3918"
                     /product="CDP-diacylglycerol diphosphatase"
                     /EC_number="3.6.1.26"
                     /label=cdh
                     /note="CDP-diacylglycerol pyrophosphatase (Cdh) catalyzes
                     the hydrolysis of CDP-diacylglycerol |CITS: 
                     [6361023][6147353][6370994]|.  The enzyme can also catalyze
                     the transfer of the CMP or dCMP moiety from 
                     (d)CDP-diacylglycerol to phosphate or a variety of 
                     phosphomonoesters |CITS: [6361023]|.  The true <i>in 
                     vivo</i> role of the enzyme is not known.
                     Cdh is not required for lipid A biosynthesis <i>in 
                     vivo</i>.  While the protein has UDP-2,3-diacylglucosamine 
                     pyrophosphatase activity <i>in vitro</i> and interferes 
                     with the assay of |FRAME: EG12666-MONOMER ""LpxH""| 
                     activity in crude cell extracts, the active site of the 
                     protein may be localized in the periplasm, explaining why 
                     it plays no role in the cytoplasmic steps of lipid A 
                     biosynthetic |CITS: [12000771]|.  |CITS: [11557141]| were 
                     unable to detect Cdh protein and suggested that the protein
                     is rapidly degraded in the cell. Cdh is predicted to be a 
                     bitopic inner membrane protein |CITS: [27510400]|. 
                     <i>cdh</i> mutants contain elevated levels of 
                     CDP-diacylglycerol compared to wild type, but have no 
                     obvious growth defect |CITS: [6147353]|.
                     Cdh: <b>C</b>DP-<b>d</b>iacylglycerol <b>h</b>ydrolase 
                     |CITS: [6147353]|"
