                     /locus_tag="b3930"
                     /product="1,4-dihydroxy-2-naphthoate
                     octaprenyltransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.5.1.74"
                     /label=menA
                     /note="1,4-dihydroxy-2-naphthoate octaprenyltransferase
                     (MenA) catalyzes the transfer of an octaprenyl side chain 
                     to DHNA, the reaction in menaquinone biosynthesis where the
                     pathway becomes associated with the membrane |CITS: 
                     [949474][9573170]|.
                     Site-directed mutagenesis of predicted active site residues
                     confirmed their importance for catalytic activity.  A 
                     reaction mechanism has been proposed |CITS: [25051182]|.
                     MenA is an inner membrane protein with nine predicted 
                     transmembrane domains.  The C-terminus is located in the 
                     periplasm |CITS: [15044727][15919996]|.
                     A <i>menA</i> mutant accumulates 1,4-dihydroxy-2-naphthoate
                     in the culture supernatant |CITS: [1091286]|.  <i>menA</i> 
                     transposon insertion mutants have increased resistance to 
                     the plant essential oils thymol and menthol |CITS: 
                     [17949301]|.
                     Review: |CITS: [11153266]|"
