     gene            4116941..4117153
                     /gene="rpmE"
                     /locus_tag="b3936"
                     /label=rpmE
     CDS             4116941..4117153
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rpmE"
                     /locus_tag="b3936"
                     /product="trifunctional 50S ribosomal subunit protein L31
                     / 50S ribosomal subunit / ribosome"
                     /label=rpmE
                     /note="The L31 protein is a component of the 50S subunit
                     of the ribosome.   An atomic model for L31 within the 70S 
                     ribosome was obtained by single-particle cryo-EM.  L31 
                     bridges the 30S and 50S subunits between the 30S head and 
                     the 50S central protuberance.  A flexible linker region in 
                     L31 accomodates large-scale rearrangements during 
                     ratcheting of the ribosome |CITS: [25707802]|.  L31 is 
                     involved in translation initiation, reading frame 
                     maintenance |CITS: [28238762]|, stabilization of subunit 
                     association |CITS: [28238762][28397381]|, and formation of 
                     100S ribosomes in stationary phase |CITS: [28397381]|.
                     L31 also counteracts intrinsic ribosome destabilization by 
                     certain nascent peptide sequences |CITS: [29100053]|.
                     L31 can be isolated in a complex with 5S rRNA and L5, L18, 
                     and L25 |CITS: [7015289]| and can be crosslinked to tRNA in
                     the P site |CITS: [2660905]|.  Modeling shows that L31 may 
                     participate in the formation, dynamics and stabilization of
                     the S13-L5 bridge |CITS: [20643101]|.
                     L31 may only be loosely associated with the ribosome |CITS:
                     [10556732]|.  An extensive crosslinking and mass 
                     spectrometry study of ribosomal proteins clarified the 
                     localization and flexibility of L31 within the ribosome 
                     |CITS: [32724211]|.
                     Expression of L31 is autoregulated. The N-terminal residues
                     2-8 of L31 are required for autoregulatory activity.  A 
                     conserved stem-loop structure upstream of the ribosome 
                     binding site is required for autoregulation and appears to 
                     separate two parts of a non-contiguous translation 
                     initiation region |CITS: [32209634]|.
                     L31 was found to be phosphorylated |CITS: [19469554]|. The 
                     |FRAME: EG12342-MONOMER| was shown to phosphorylate RpmE at
                     Ser69, which negatively affects its function and further 
                     impacts ribosome assembly |CITS: [36537800]|. Purified RpmE
                     binds Zn<sup>2+</sup> |CITS: [22196016]|. L31 was initially
                     thought to be C-terminally processed; a fragment lacking 
                     the C-terminal amino acids RFNIPGSK was identified in <i>E.
                     coli</i> B |CITS: [339950]| and later by mass spectrometry 
                     in K-12 |CITS: [10094780]|.  However, |CITS: [10556732]| 
                     isolated full-length protein from MRE600, B and K-12 
                     strains.  Ribosomes isolated from a strain lacking |FRAME: 
                     EG10673-MONOMER OmpT| only contain full-length L31, 
                     suggesting that OmpT cleaves L31 during ribosome 
                     purification |CITS: [28397381]|.
                     A &Delta;<i>rpmE</i> mutant has a slow growth phenotype 
                     |CITS: [32209634][32559334]|.  A strain lacking both 
                     <i>rpmE</i> and its paralog <i>ykgM</i> has a significantly
                     reduced growth rate at various temperatures. Ribosomes 
                     lacking L31 display increased frameshifting and miscoding 
                     and reduced efficiency of translation initiation <i>in 
                     vivo</i> and <i>in vitro</i> |CITS: [28238762]|. Similarly,
                     ribosomes containing the C-terminally truncated form of L31
                     dissociate more easily and show reduced translation 
                     activity |CITS: [28397381]|.
                     |FRAME: G6167-MONOMER YkgM| is a paralog of L31 |CITS: 
                     [11574053]|; it is the prevalent paralog present in 
                     stationary phase ribosomes |CITS: [30359641]|.  YkgM has 
                     lost the predicted metal-binding ""zinc ribbon"" motif 
                     |CITS: [11574053]| and was shown to lack bound 
                     Zn<sup>2+</sup>, in contrast to L31 |CITS: [22196016]|. The
                     authors propose a model where YkgM can provide the function
                     of L31 in the ribosome under zinc-limiting conditions.  
                     Under lower-temperature growth conditions and in growth 
                     competition experiments, L31 confers higher fitness than 
                     L31B |CITS: [32669635]|.
                     The expression of the gene <i>rpmE</i> is repressed by the 
                     protein YkgM, but it is not clear at which expression level
                     this regulation happens; it could be at the level of 
                     transcription, mRNA stability, or translation at more than 
                     one level |CITS:[36533433]|. This regulation involves a 
                     hairpin structure in the <i>rpmE</i> mRNA and the 
                     N-terminal domain of YkgM |CITS:[36533433]|.
                     Reviews: |CITS: [22649682][26880335]|"
