     gene            complement(4137394..4138245)
                     /gene="yijO"
                     /locus_tag="b3954"
                     /label=yijO
     CDS             complement(4137394..4138245)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yijO"
                     /locus_tag="b3954"
                     /product="putative DNA-binding transcriptional regulator
                     YijO"
                     /label=yijO
                     /note="YijO, which contains a helix-turn-helix motif to
                     bind DNA in its C-terminal domain, appears to belong to the
                     AraC family of transcription factors and it was predicted 
                     to regulate genes related to metabolism |CITS: [35880217]|.
                     Upstream of the <i>yijO</i> gene, a sequence was found that
                     could work as a transcriptional promoter, and the 
                     transcription of the <i>yijO</i> gene is affected by 
                     conditions that generate general transcriptional 
                     termination or lead to biofilm formation |CITS: 
                     [35880217]|.
                     A mutation affecting <i>yijO</i> was identified as one of 
                     several mutations in an evolved strain adapted to osmotic 
                     stress by growth in 0.3 M NaCl |CITS: [23385483]|.
                     The YijO binding landscape was globally mapped in vivo by 
                     standardized ChIP-seq and quantitatively modeled using 
                     BoltzNet, a biophysically informed neural network that 
                     infers binding energy from sequence data |CITS:[40335485]|.
                     The resulting ChIP-seq binding regions are available in 
                     RegulonDB (<a href=""https://regulondb.cc 
                     g.unam.mx/ht/dataset/TFBINDING/source=GALAGAN"">Galagan 
                     collection</a>), and the corresponding energy matrix and 
                     genomic binding profiles can be accessed at <a 
                     href=""http://boltznet.bu.edu"">boltznet.bu.edu</a> 
                     |CITS:[40335485]|."
                     /translation="MYHDVSYLLSRLINGPLSLRQIYFASSNGPVPDLAYQVDFPRLEI
