     CDS             4144929..4145933
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="argC"
                     /locus_tag="b3958"
                     /product="N-acetylglutamylphosphate reductase"
                     /EC_number="1.2.1.38"
                     /label=argC
                     /note="N-acetylglutamylphosphate reductase (ArgC) carries
                     out the third step in arginine biosynthesis
                     and its subpathway, ornithine biosynthesis.
                     ArgC catalyzes the NADPH-dependent reduction of 
                     <i>N</i>-acetylglutamyl-phosphate to
                     yield <i>N</i>-acetyl-L-glutamate 5-semialdehyde |CITS: 
                     [13863980][2851495][4365537]|.
                     Evolution and recruitment of promiscuous enzymes have been 
                     studied using ProA and its ability to replace ArgC |CITS: 
                     [25246702][35729117]|."
