                     /note="Argininosuccinate lyase catalyzes the final step in
                     the L-arginine biosynthesis pathway.
                     A crystal structure of argininosuccinate lyase has been 
                     solved at 2.44 &Aring; resolution; the enzyme appears to be
                     tetrameric, with a dimer as the asymmetric unit of this 
                     crystal form |CITS: [15502303]|.
                     ArgH expression is repressed by the addition of arginine or
                     ornithine to the medium |CITS: [770426]|."
