                     /label=murI
     CDS             4155356..4156213
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="murI"
                     /locus_tag="b3967"
                     /product="glutamate racemase"
                     /EC_number="5.1.1.3"
                     /label=murI
                     /note="Glutamate racemase (MurI) catalyzes the
                     racemization of L-glutamate to D-glutamate, an essential 
                     component that is unique to bacterial peptidoglycan |CITS: 
                     [1355768][8098327][8172902]|.
                     Physiological concentrations of 
                     UDP-<i>N</i>-acetylmuramyl-L-Ala, the second substrate of 
                     the subsequent reaction in peptidoglycan biosynthesis, 
                     specifically activates the enzyme |CITS: [8172902]|.  It 
                     was suggested that the unique N terminus of MurI is 
                     required for activation |CITS: [7873525]|; however, an 
                     N-terminally truncated enzyme is still activated by 
                     UDP-<i>N</i>-acetylmuramyl-L-Ala |CITS: [9158721]|. 
                     Site-directed mutagenesis of the two conserved cysteine 
                     residues showed that they are essential for enzymatic 
                     activity, suggesting that they are involved in the two-base
                     reaction mechanism |CITS: [7873525][9158721]|. Evidence 
                     regarding the quarternary structure of MurI was 
                     contradictory: |CITS: [7901215]| reported a homodimer, 
                     while |CITS: [8172902]| report that the enzyme is 
                     monomeric.  A crystal structure of MurI in complex with 
                     UDP-<i>N</i>-acetylmuramyl-L-Ala has been solved at 1.9 
                     &Aring; resolution and shows a monomer.  The activator 
                     binds in a hinge region opposite to the catalytically 
                     active site |CITS: [17568739]|.
                     Activated MurI appears to inhibit |FRAME: CPLX0-2425| 
                     activity |CITS: [12213801]|.
                     A D-glutamate-requiring strain first isolated in the <i>E. 
                     coli</i> B background carries two independent mutations, 
                     one in the glutamate transporter |FRAME: GLTS-MONOMER 
                     ""GltS""| and a second in MurI |CITS: [8093236][8098327]|. 
                     <i>murI</i> is an essential gene |CITS: 
                     [8098327][8407834]|.
                     Peptide inhibitors of glutamate racemase activity have been
                     identified |CITS: [11598461]|.
                     Dga: ""<b>D</b>-<b>g</b>lutamate <b>a</b>uxotrophy""
                     Glr: ""<b>gl</b>utamate <b>r</b>acemase"" |CITS: [7901215]|
                     Review: |CITS: [22203377]|"
