     CDS             4161985..4163013
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="murB"
                     /locus_tag="b3972"
                     /product="UDP-N-acetylenolpyruvoylglucosamine reductase"
                     /EC_number="1.3.1.98"
                     /label=murB
                     /note="UDP-<i>N</i>-acetylenolpyruvoylglucosamine
                     reductase (MurB) catalyzes the second committed step in the
                     biosynthesis of peptidoglycan. The enzyme is essential for 
                     growth |CITS: [16738554]| and is a target for development 
                     of new antibiotics |CITS: [20080587]|.
                     Crystal structures of the enzyme have been solved |CITS: 
                     [7552726][8805513][8634262][15299687][9020778]|, and the 
                     NADP<sup>+</sup> binding site has been localized by NMR and
                     appears to co-localize with the binding pocket for 
                     UDP-<i>N</i>-acetylenolpyruvoylglucosamine |CITS: 
                     [8946851][9150408]|. The kinetic mechanism of the enzyme 
                     has been investigated. The reaction appears to proceed as a
                     sequence of two half-reactions |CITS: 
                     [8448160][7727397][9020779]|.
                     MurA, MurB and MurC are capable of chemo-enzymatic labeling
                     and modifying of UDP-GlcNAc-RNA <i>in vitro</i> |CITS: 
                     [38716860]|.
                     Reviews: |CITS: [12492849][22203377]|"
