     gene            4168807..4169511
                     /gene="rplA"
                     /locus_tag="b3984"
                     /label=rplA
     CDS             4168807..4169511
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rplA"
                     /locus_tag="b3984"
                     /product="trifunctional 50S ribosomal subunit protein L1 /
                     50S ribosomal subunit / ribosome"
                     /label=rplA
                     /note="The L1 protein is a component of the 50S subunit of
                     the ribosome and also functions in the post-transcriptional
                     regulation of the ribosomal protein genes encoded in the 
                     L11 operon.  Ribosomes lacking L1 show a lower translation 
                     activity than wild type |CITS: [7007045]| and are defective
                     in binding of aminoacylated tRNA |CITS: [6350280]|.  L1 has
                     been identified within a 3-D map of the 70S ribosome 
                     constructed by cryo-electron microscopy |CITS: [9653034]|.
                     L1 interacts with a region in the 5' end of 23S rRNA |CITS:
                     [827439][6162152][1960726]|.  It also can be crosslinked to
                     a region near the central fold of aminoacylated tRNA in the
                     P and E site |CITS: [2685749][8251501][8524654]|.  L1 is 
                     located within 21 &Aring; of nucleotide C2475 of 23S rRNA, 
                     near the peptidyltransferase center |CITS: [7529559]|.
                     L1 is a translational repressor of the synthesis of L11 and
                     L1, the proteins encoded by the L11 operon |CITS: 
                     [7011209][3309351][7024735][6445562][6171646]|.  Synthesis 
                     of L1 is regulated by translational coupling to the 
                     synthesis of L11 |CITS: [7016337][6354472]|.  The target 
                     site for L1 binding to the mRNA is near the translation 
                     initiation site of L11 |CITS: [7016337][6354472][3104883]|,
                     and the presence of 23S rRNA relieves translational 
                     inhibition by L1 |CITS: [7016337]|. The predicted secondary
                     structure of the L1 binding region within 23S rRNA and 
                     <i>rplKA</i> mRNA is similar |CITS: [6162152][6265904]| and
                     has been studied experimentally |CITS: 
                     [6382263][2448590][3060846][11142372]|.
                     Both the growth rate control and stringent control of the 
                     synthesis of ribosomal proteins L11 and L1 are resulting 
                     from translational regulation by L1 |CITS: [3520566]|.
                     The Keio collection <i>rplA</i> mutant is sensitive to 
                     lithium (<90% growth at 100mM Li) |CITS: [39983623]|."
