     gene            4220282..4221154
                     /gene="rluF"
                     /locus_tag="b4022"
                     /label=rluF
     CDS             4220282..4221154
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rluF"
                     /locus_tag="b4022"
                     /product="trifunctional 23S rRNA pseudouridine(2604) and
                     tRNA(Tyr) pseudouridine(35) synthase / 23S rRNA 
                     pseudouridine(2604) synthase / tRNA(Tyr) pseudouridine(35) 
                     synthase"
                     /EC_number="5.4.99.21"
                     /label=rluF
                     /note="RluF is the pseudouridine synthase that catalyzes 
                     formation of pseudouridine at position 2604 in 23S rRNA 
                     |CITS: [11720289]| and position 35 within the anticodon of 
                     |FRAME: TYR-tRNAs tRNA<sup>Tyr</sup>| |CITS: [27551044]|. 
                     RluF belongs to the RsuA family of RNA pseudouridine 
                     synthases |CITS: [11720289]|.
                     Pseudouridine modification of tRNA<sup>Tyr</sup> appears to
                     increase the translation efficiency of mRNAs rich in Tyr 
                     codons |CITS: [27551044]|. Neither an <i>rluF</i> null 
                     mutant nor an <i>rluB rluF</i> double null mutant exhibit 
                     an obvious growth defect. The conserved active site residue
                     Asp107 is essential for activity |CITS: [11720289]|.
                     The crystal structure of RluF bound to the 23S rRNA 
                     stem-loop it modifies has been solved at 3.0 &Aring; 
                     resolution. The structure shows a conserved binding groove 
                     for the RNA stem-loop in the catalytic domain. The bulge 
                     normally located at A2602 is folded into the stem and 
                     causes U2604 to flip into the active site, accounting for 
                     the site specificity of RluF |CITS: [19298824]|. A crystal 
                     structure of the catalytic domain of RluF from <i>E. 
                     coli</i> O157:H7 has been solved at 2.6 &Aring; resolution.
                     Analytical ultracentrifugation showed that RluF is a 
                     monomer in solution |CITS: [16712869]|.
                     Reviews: |CITS: [17113994][25616362]|"
