     gene            4225834..4226076
                     /gene="yjbE"
                     /locus_tag="b4026"
                     /label=yjbE
     CDS             4225834..4226076
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yjbE"
                     /locus_tag="b4026"
                     /product="uncharacterized protein YjbE"
                     /label=yjbE
                     /note="The <i>yjbEFGH</i> operon is involved in the
                     production of an extracellular polysaccharide |CITS: 
                     [17379715][18997023]|.
                     Published reports disagree on whether YjbE is involved in 
                     biofilm formation.  A mutant with a deletion of <i>yjbE</i>
                     showed a significant decrease in biofilm formation |CITS: 
                     [16385049]|.  However, other experiments showed that a 
                     <i>yjbE</i> mutant had no effect on biofilm formation 
                     |CITS: [17379715]|.  Overexpression of <i>yjbEFGH</i> 
                     altered
                     colony morphology and led to increased binding of toluidine
                     blue-O and Congo red, indicating increased production
                     of an EPS that is distinct from colanic acid |CITS: 
                     [17379715]|.
                     Expression of <i>yjbE</i> is positively regulated by RcsC 
                     |CITS: [14651646]| and increases 7.5-fold upon deletion of 
                     <i>tqsA</i>, which increases biofilm formation |CITS: 
                     [16385049]|.  Disruption of <i>yjbE</i> has a polar effect 
                     on
                     expression of <i>yjbFGH</i>, indicating that these genes 
                     form an operon; however, a full-length mRNA could not be 
                     detected, possibly due to strong secondary structure in the
                     <i>yjbE-yjbF</i> intergenic region |CITS: [17379715]|. 
                     Expression of <i>yjbEFGH</i> is highest at slow growth 
                     rates, low cell density and high oxygen availability; 
                     expression is higher in an <i>rpoS</i> mutant |CITS: 
                     [17957352]| and induced by 0.7 M NaCl |CITS: [18997023]|. A
                     &Delta;<i>yjbE rpoS</i>::Tn10 double mutant shows extreme 
                     mucoidy and a filamentous phenotype |CITS: [18997023]|."
                     /translation="MKKVLYGIFAISALAATSAWAAPVQVGEAAGSAATSVSAGSSSAT
                     SVSTVSSAVGVALAATGGGDGSNTGTTTTTTTSTQ"
                     /go_component="extracellular region [goid 0005576]
                     [evidence IEA] [PMID 19054114]"
                     /go_process="polysaccharide biosynthetic process [goid
                     0000271] [evidence IMP] [PMID 18997023]"
                     /go_process="polysaccharide biosynthetic process [goid
                     0000271] [evidence IMP] [PMID 17379715]"
                     /go_process="single-species biofilm formation [goid
                     0044010] [evidence IMP] [PMID 16385049]"
     gene            4226190..4226828
                     /gene="yjbF"
                     /locus_tag="b4027"
                     /label=yjbF
     CDS             4226190..4226828
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yjbF"
                     /locus_tag="b4027"
                     /product="lipoprotein YjbF"
                     /label=yjbF
                     /note="The <i>yjbEFGH</i> operon is involved in the
                     production of an extracellular polysaccharide |CITS: 
                     [17379715][18997023]|.
                     Sequence similarity suggests that YjbF may be a lipoprotein
                     and/or an outer membrane porin |CITS: [12192075]|.  YjbF is
                     a verified lipoprotein according to unpublished data by S. 
                     Matsuyama et al. (cited in |CITS: [12876315]|).
                     Overexpression of <i>yjbEFGH</i> alters colony morphology 
                     and leads to increased binding of toluidine blue-O and 
                     Congo red, indicating increased production of an EPS that 
                     is distinct from colanic acid |CITS: [17379715]|. 
                     Expression of <i>yjbF</i> is positively regulated by RcsC 
                     |CITS: [14651646]|.  Disruption of <i>yjbE</i> has a polar 
                     effect on expression of <i>yjbFGH</i>, indicating that 
                     these genes form an operon; however, a full-length mRNA 
                     could not be detected, possibly due to strong secondary 
                     structure in the <i>yjbE-yjbF</i> intergenic region |CITS: 
                     [17379715]|.  Expression of <i>yjbEFGH</i> is highest at 
                     slow growth rates, low cell density and high oxygen 
                     availability; expression is higher in an <i>rpoS</i> mutant
                     |CITS: [17957352]| and induced by 0.7 M NaCl |CITS: 
                     [18997023]|."
