                     Overexpression of <i>yjbEFGH</i> alters colony morphology 
                     and leads to increased binding of toluidine blue-O and 
                     Congo red, indicating increased production of an EPS that 
                     is distinct from colanic acid |CITS: [17379715]|. 
                     Expression of <i>yjbG</i> is positively regulated by RcsC 
                     |CITS: [14651646]|.  Disruption of <i>yjbE</i> has a polar 
                     effect on expression of <i>yjbFGH</i>, indicating that 
                     these genes form an operon; however, a full-length mRNA 
                     could not be detected, possibly due to strong secondary 
                     structure in the <i>yjbE-yjbF</i> intergenic region |CITS: 
                     [17379715]|.  Expression of <i>yjbEFGH</i> is highest at 
                     slow growth rates, low cell density and high oxygen 
                     availability; expression is higher in an <i>rpoS</i> mutant
                     |CITS: [17957352]| and induced by 0.7 M NaCl |CITS: 
                     [18997023]|.  A &Delta;<i>yjbG rpoS</i>::Tn10 mutant does 
                     not show extreme mucoidy on LB plates, but does produce 
                     increased amounts of extracellular polysaccharides as 
                     measured by a pelleting assay |CITS: [19583986]|."
