     CDS             4239482..4240402
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="malM"
                     /locus_tag="b4037"
                     /product="maltose regulon periplasmic protein"
                     /label=malM
                     /note="<i>malM</i> is the last gene in the
                     <i>malK-lamB-malM</i> operon and is thus part of the 
                     maltose regulon.  A signal
                     sequence is cleaved, and the mature MalM protein localizes 
                     to the periplasm |CITS: [2434655][3102747]|.
                     The <i>malM</i> gene is conserved between species, but its 
                     function is unknown |CITS: [1730061]|."
