     CDS             4247670..4249049
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="dinF"
                     /locus_tag="b4044"
                     /product="DNA damage-inducible protein F"
                     /label=dinF
                     /note="DinF is a member of the Multi Antimicrobial
                     Extrusion (MATE) Family of transporters |CITS: 
                     [9987140][26546518]|; DinF is implicated in protection from
                     reactive oxygen species (ROS) possibly via the export of 
                     oxidizing species |CITS: [22523558]|.
                     Expression of <i>dinF</i> is DNA damage (UV or mitomycin C)
                     inducible |CITS: [6771759]|. <i>dinF</i> forms an operon 
                     with the SOS response regulator, <i>lexA</i> |CITS: 
                     [6298183]|.
                     DinF contains 12 predicted transmembrane domains |CITS: 
                     [22523558]|; multicopy expression of <i>dinF</i> decreases 
                     intracellular ROS (reactive oxygen species) levels and 
                     protects cells from H<sub>2</sub>O<sub>2</sub>-induced 
                     killing; DinF is implicated in protection against bile 
                     salts; multicopy expression of <i>dinF</i> confers a slight
                     resistance to bile salts |CITS: [22523558]|.
                     "
