     gene            4249165..4249374
                     /gene="yjbJ"
                     /locus_tag="b4045"
                     /label=yjbJ
     CDS             4249165..4249374
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yjbJ"
                     /locus_tag="b4045"
                     /product="putative stress response protein YjbJ"
                     /label=yjbJ
                     /note="YjbJ is a soluble protein with a four-helix bundle
                     domain |CITS: [11854485]|.  YjbJ is one of a number of 
                     proteins that interacts with the |FRAME: PROP-MONOMER|; 
                     however, it does not affect ProP localization or function 
                     |CITS: [29280215]|.
                     YjbJ is not required for growth on rich or minimal media. 
                     The effects of mutations on the rate of cell growth are 
                     observed to vary depending on the construction of the 
                     mutant allele |CITS: [9335267]|.
                     Structural characterization has been performed by NMR 
                     |CITS: [11854485][12001238]|.
                     YjbJ is found at high abundance <i>in vivo</i> |CITS: 
                     [9298646]|.  Expression is induced under osmotic stress 
                     imposed by NaCl in both aerobic and anaerobic conditions 
                     |CITS: [17015655]|, and by acidic pH in the presence of 
                     cadmium |CITS: [19220470]|.  <i>yjbJ</i> belongs to the 
                     &sigma;<sup>S</sup> regulon |CITS: [15716429]|."
                     /translation="MNKDEAGGNWKQFKGKVKEQWGKLTDDDMTIIEGKRDQLVGKIQE
