     CDS             4252768..4253010
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="pspG"
                     /locus_tag="b4050"
                     /product="phage shock protein G"
                     /label=pspG
                     /note="The PspG protein is predicted to be an inner
                     membrane protein.  PspG is conserved in all bacteria that 
                     contain the phage shock |FRAME: TU00326| operon.  The PspG 
                     protein appears to affect motility |CITS: [15485810]|. 
                     Expression of the <i>pspG</i> gene, like that of the 
                     |FRAME: TU00326| operon, is upregulated by pIV secretin 
                     stress.  Transcription by |FRAME: RPON-MONOMER 
                     &sigma;<sup>54</sup>|-containing RNA polymerase may be 
                     activated by |FRAME: EG12344 PspF|, and |FRAME: 
                     EG10776-MONOMER PspA| negatively regulates <i>pspG</i> 
                     expression, making <i>pspG</i> part of the PspF regulon 
                     |CITS: [15485810]|.
                     The |FRAME: EG10230-MONOMER| stimulated abortive synthesis 
                     of the <i>pspG</i> promoter |CITS: [26365052]|.
                     PspG self associates and interacts with |FRAME: 
                     EG10778-MONOMER PspC| <i>in vivo</i> |CITS: [20595257]|."
                     /translation="MLELLFVIGFFVMLMVTGVSLLGIIAALVVATAIMFLGGMLALMI
                     KLLPWLLLAIAVVWVIKAIKAPKVPKYQRYDRWRY"
