     gene            4268407..4269756
                     /gene="ghxP"
                     /locus_tag="b4064"
                     /label=ghxP
     CDS             4268407..4269756
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ghxP"
                     /locus_tag="b4064"
                     /product="trifunctional guanine/hypoxanthine transporter
                     GhxP / hypoxanthine transport / guanine transport"
                     /label=ghxP
                     /note="Cloned and overexpressed GhxP transports labelled
                     guanine and hypoxanthine, but not adenine, xanthine, uric 
                     acid or uracil in <i>E. coli </i> K-12 |CITS: [24214977]|. 
                     GhxP has been implicated in transport of the purine base 
                     analogs |FRAME: CPD-15922|, |FRAME: CPD-15921|, |FRAME: 
                     CPD-15916|, |FRAME: CPD-5721| and |FRAME: CPD-15920| |CITS:
                     [24169576]|. GhxP is a member of the nucleobase-cation 
                     symporter-2 (NCS2) family of transporters |CITS: 
                     [16381841]|.
                     A <i>ghxP</i> transposon mutation suppresses the 
                     sensitivity of a <i>&Delta;|FRAME: G6487 ""ycbX""|</I> 
                     strain to the purine analogues, 6-hydroxyaminopurine and 
                     2-amino-6-hydroxyaminopurine. A <i>&Delta;ghxP</i> strain 
                     is also less sensitive to 6-mercaptopurine and 
                     6-thioguanine than wild type |CITS: [24169576]|. 
                     <i>ghxP</i> contains a PurR binding motif |CITS: 
                     [21572102]| and PurR dependent repression of <i>ghxP</I> is
                     induced by exogenous adenine |CITS: [22796662]|. Membrane 
                     topology predictions using experimentally determined C 
                     terminus locations indicate that GhxP has 13 transmembrane 
                     helices and the C-terminus is located in the periplasm 
                     |CITS: [15044727], [15919996]|."
