     gene            complement(4287036..4289183)
                     /gene="fdhF"
                     /locus_tag="b4079"
                     /label=fdhF
     CDS             complement(4287036..4289183)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="fdhF"
                     /locus_tag="b4079"
                     /product="trifunctional formate dehydrogenase H / formate 
                     dehydrogenase / formate hydrogenlyase complex"
                     /label=fdhF
                     /note="Formate dehydrogenase-H is one of three 
                     membrane-associated formate dehydrogenase isoenzymes in 
                     <i>E. coli</i> |CITS: [7747941]|. All are functional in the
                     anaerobic metabolism of the organism. Formate 
                     dehydrogenase-H (FDH-H) is located in the cytoplasm and 
                     together with hydrogenase-3, FDH-H forms the 
                     formate-hydrogen lyase complex |CITS: [2211698][7747941]|. 
                     FDH-H plays a role in the formate-dependent catabolism of 
                     urate |CITS: [30885932]|.
                     The enzyme is oxygen sensitive and contains selenium as 
                     selenocysteine incorporated cotranslationally at the 
                     position of an in-frame UGA stop codon in the FdhF open 
                     reading frame |CITS: [2941757][3033637][2141170][1829362]|.
                     <i>fdhF</I> mRNA contains a <i>cis</i>-acting element - the
                     selenocysteine insertion sequence (SECIS) - which in 
                     combination with the specialized elongation factor |FRAME: 
                     CPLX0-8053 SelB| is required for UGA-directed 
                     selenocysteine incorporation |CITS: 
                     [1396569][8483932][8314089][9192624][9461445][12421 
                     564][11053373]| (and see |CITS: [11568441]|).
                     A crystal structure of FDH-H has been solved at 2.3 &Aring;
                     resolution, confirming the presence of a [4Fe-4S] cluster, 
                     the coordination of molybdenum (Mo) to two molybdopterin 
                     guanine dinucleotide (MGD) cofactors and to selenium of 
                     selenocysteine (Sec-140), and the position of the binding 
                     site for the inhibitor nitrate |CITS: [9036855][16830149]|.
                     Formate is oxidized to CO<sub>2</sub> at the 
                     Mo(MGD)<sub>2</sub> active site and electrons are then 
                     shuttled to a downstream acceptor (hydrogenase-3 <i>in 
                     vivo</i>) via the [4Fe-4S] cluster |CITS: [9036855]|. FdhF 
                     is loosely associated with the hydrogenase 3 complex |CITS:
                     [25157147][36104349]|; FdhF interacts with HycB via 
                     hydrophobic interactions and hydrogen bonds, and with HycF 
                     via electrostatic attraction |CITS: [36104349]|.
                     Expression of <i>fdhF</i> is induced by formate and the 
                     absence of external electron acceptors, and is repressed by
                     nitrate, nitrite, trimethylamine N-oxide, and oxygen |CITS:
                     [3118141][6360066][9274019]|. Formate can overcome 
                     repression by nitrate but not by oxygen |CITS: [6360066]|. 
                     Inhibition of DNA gyrase enhances expression of <i>fdhF</i>
                     |CITS: [2829213]|."
