                     /product="trifunctional putative multidrug efflux pump
                     outer membrane channel / putative multidrug efflux pump 
                     MdtNOP / sulfadiazine efflux pump"
                     /label=mdtP
                     /note="<i>mdtP</i> encodes a putative multidrug resistance 
                     protein; MdtP from <i>E. coli</i> K-12 W3110 has 26% 
                     sequence identity and 47% similarity (over 466 residues) 
                     with OprM - the <i>Pseudomonas aeruginosa</i> outer 
                     membrane component of the MexAB multidrug resistance pump; 
                     deletion of <I>mdtP</I> from strain W3110 results in 
                     increased susceptibility to acriflavin, puromycin and 
                     tetraphenylarsonium chloride |CITS: [11257026]|. MdtP is 
                     the outer membrane component of a putative efflux pump 
                     implicated in resistance to sulfonamide antibiotics |CITS: 
                     [19429622]|.
                     <i>sdsP</i>: <U>s</U>ulfa <U>d</U>rug <U>s</U>ensitivity 
                     |CITS: [19429622]|<BR><i>mdtP</i>: <U>m</U>ulti <U>d</U>rug
                     <U>t</U>ransporter"
