                     /product="trifunctional putative multidrug efflux pump
                     subunit MdtO / putative multidrug efflux pump MdtNOP / 
                     sulfadiazine efflux pump"
                     /label=mdtO
                     /note="MdtO is an uncharacterized component of a putative 
                     multidrug efflux pump |CITS: [19429622]|.
                     <i>mdtO</i> is one of 35 efflux-encoding genes that have 
                     been deleted or inactivated in 'Efflux KnockOut-35' 
                     (EKO-35) -  a K-12 BW25133-derived strain that lacks 35 
                     efflux pumps and can be used as a platform to study their 
                     function |CITS: [36065018][36318669]|.
                     In the Transporter Classification Database, MdtO is a 
                     member of the Aromatic Acid Exporter (ArAE) family |CITS: 
                     [26546518]|.
                     <i>sdsQ</i>: <U>s</U>ulfa <U>d</U>rug <U>s</U>ensitivity 
