                     /product="D-allose kinase"
                     /EC_number="2.7.1.55"
                     /label=alsK
                     /note="The <i>alsK</i> gene encodes a D-allose kinase.
                     Its role in the degradation of D-allose is unclear; AlsK is
                     not
                     required for utilization of a D-allose carbon source; this 
                     effect may be due to the presence of other ambiguous sugar 
                     kinases within <I>E. coli</I> K-12 |CITS: 
                     [9401019][10559180][16086580]|.  Expression of <i>alsK</i> 
                     appears to be
                     unaffected by allose |CITS: [10559180]|.
                     Overexpression of <i>alsK</i> rescues the auxotrophic 
                     phenotype of a glucokinase mutant |CITS: [16086580]|.  The 
                     low glucokinase activity of AlsK can be improved by 
                     experimental evolution |CITS: [17979299]|.
                     Als:  ""D-<b>al</b>lo<b>s</b>e"" |CITS: [9401019]|"
