                     /locus_tag="b4085"
                     /label=alsE
     CDS             complement(4297600..4298295)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="alsE"
                     /locus_tag="b4085"
                     /product="D-allulose-6-phosphate 3-epimerase"
                     /label=alsE
                     /note="Allulose-6-phosphate 3-epimerase catalyzes the
                     final step in the degradation of D-allose, the conversion 
                     of
                     D-allulose-6-phosphate to D-fructose-6-phosphate, which 
                     feeds into the glycolysis pathway
                     |CITS: [9401019][18700786]|.
                     Crystal structures of AlsE have been solved.  The enzyme 
                     has a (&beta;/&alpha;)<sub>8</sub> barrel
                     structure; the active site is located at the C-terminal end
                     of the &beta; strands.  Site-directed mutants that were 
                     predicted to alter substrate specificity have been purified
                     and analyzed |CITS: [18700786]|.
                     Expression of <i>alsE</i> is induced by allose, and an 
                     <i>alsE</i> mutant is unable to catabolize allose
                     |CITS: [10559180]|.
                     AlsE: ""<b>al</b>lulo<b>s</b>e 6-phosphate 
                     <b>e</b>pimerase"" |CITS: [10559180]|"
