     gene            4303167..4303616
                     /gene="rpiB"
                     /locus_tag="b4090"
                     /label=rpiB
     CDS             4303167..4303616
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rpiB"
                     /locus_tag="b4090"
                     /product="trifunctional allose-6-phosphate isomerase / 
                     ribose-5-phosphate isomerase B / allose-6-phosphate 
                     isomerase / ribose-5-phosphate isomerase"
                     /EC_number="5.3.1.6"
                     /label=rpiB
                     /note="There are two physically and genetically distinct 
                     ribose-5-phosphate isomerases present in <i>E. coli</i> 
                     |CITS: [4909663][11945603]|.  The constitutive 
                     ribose-5-phosphate isomerase A, encoded by the <i>rpiA</i> 
                     gene, functions in the |FRAME: NONOXIPENT-PWY|.  The 
                     inducible ribose-5-phosphate isomerase B can substitute for
                     RpiA's function if its expression is induced |CITS: 
                     [4598000][8576032]|.  There is no sequence similarity 
                     between the two enzymes |CITS: [8576032]|.
                     A crystal structure of RpiB has been solved at 2.2 &Aring; 
                     resolution.  The enzyme is present as a dimer of dimers in 
                     the crystal, and active site residues are located at the 
                     dimer interface |CITS: [14499611][16322579]|.  A crystal 
                     structure of the active site mutant H99N has been solved at
                     2.1 &Aring; resolution |CITS: [18640127]|.
                     Expression of <i>rpiB</i> is induced by allose, and an 
                     <i>rpiB</i> mutant is unable to catabolize allose |CITS: 
                     [10559180]|.
                     RpiB: ""<b>r</b>ibose<b>p</b>hosphate <b>i</b>somerase 
                     <b>B</b>"" |CITS: [4598000]|
                     AlsI: ""<b>al</b>lo<b>s</b>e 6-phosphate <b>i</b>somerase""
                     |CITS: [10559180]|
                     Review:  |CITS: [8572885]|"
