     gene            complement(4305342..4305899)
                     /gene="phnN"
                     /locus_tag="b4094"
                     /label=phnN
     CDS             complement(4305342..4305899)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="phnN"
                     /locus_tag="b4094"
                     /product="ribose 1,5-bisphosphate phosphokinase"
                     /EC_number="2.7.4.23"
                     /label=phnN
                     /note="PhnN was found to catalyze the ribose 
                     1,5-bisphosphokinase reaction |CITS: [12700258]| in the 
                     |FRAME: PWY-7805| pathway.
                     <i>phnN</i> is part of a phosphate starvation-inducible 
                     operon that is required for use of phosphonate and 
                     phosphite as phosphorous sources |CITS: 
                     [9650256][1846145][2155230]|.  It was initially suggested 
                     that PhnN might be a subunit |CITS: [1368181]| or an 
                     accessory factor |CITS: [8388873]| of a C-P lyase. 
                     <i>phnN</i> insertion mutants show reduced growth on 
                     phosphite and methylphosphonate as a source of phosphorous 
                     |CITS: [8388873]|.  Derepression of <i>phnN</i> expression 
                     suppresses the NAD requirement of a &Delta;<i>prs</i> 
                     mutant |CITS: [12700258]|.  The authors proposed a PRPP 
                     biosynthesis pathway involving phosphoribomutase (DeoB), a 
                     hypothesized ribose-1-phosphokinase, and PhnN. 
                     Overexpression of <i>phnN</i> increases the tolerance of 
                     <i>E. coli</i> to n-butanol |CITS: [21408113]|.
                     Reviews: |CITS: [24600043][28031352]|
                     "
