                     /product="multifunctional carbon-phosphorus lyase core
                     complex subunit PhnJ / carbon-phosphorous lyase / 
                     carbon-phosphorus lyase core complex / carbon-phosphorus 
                     lyase system"
                     /EC_number="4.7.1.1"
                     /label=phnJ
                     /note="PhnJ is a radical SAM enzyme that catalyzes the
                     cleavage of |FRAME: CPD0-2480| (PRPn) to |FRAME: CPD0-2463|
                     (PRcP).  Activity requires anaerobic reconstitution of a 
                     [4Fe-4S] cluster and the presence of dithionite |CITS: 
                     [22089136]|.
                     PhnJ was also found to be a component of a protein complex 
                     that was thought to catalyze the carbon-phosphorus lyase 
                     reaction |CITS: [21705661]|.
                     <i>phnJ</i> is part of an operon that is phosphate 
                     starvation-inducible and required for use of phosphonate 
                     and phosphite as phosphorous sources |CITS: 
                     [9650256][1846145][2155230]|.  PhnJ appears to be required 
                     for carbon-phosphorous lyase activity |CITS: [8388873]|.
                     A <i>phnJ</i> mutant accumulates presumed intermediates of 
                     the C-P lyase pathway of phosphonate degradation |CITS: 
                     [19854894]|.
                     "
