                     /label=phnI
     CDS             complement(4309416..4310480)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="phnI"
                     /locus_tag="b4099"
                     /product="multifunctional carbon-phosphorus lyase core
                     complex subunit PhnI / alpha-D-ribose 1-methylphosphonate 
                     5-triphosphate synthase / alpha-D-ribose-1-(2-N-acetamidom 
                     ethylphosphonate)-5-triphosphate synthase / 
                     carbon-phosphorus lyase core complex / carbon-phosphorus 
                     lyase system"
                     /EC_number="2.7.8.37"
                     /label=phnI
                     /note="The <i>phnI</i> gene is part of a 14-gene 
                     <i>phnCDEFGHIJKLMNOP</i> operon that is involved in 
                     phosphonate uptake and metabolism and is a member of the 
                     phosphate regulon |CITS: [2155230][1846145][9650256]|.  A 
                     <i>phnI</i> mutant accumulates presumed intermediates of 
                     the C-P lyase pathway of phosphonate degradation |CITS: 
                     [19854894]|.
                     The PhnI protein alone has nucleosidase activity, producing
                     D-ribose-5-triphosphate and the free base from GTP and ATP.
                      However, in a mixture together with PhnG, PhnH and PhnL it
                     catalyzes the nucleophilic attack of |FRAME: CPD0-1068| on 
                     the anomeric carbon of ATP to form adenine and |FRAME: 
                     CPD0-2479| |CITS: [22089136]|. Immucillin-A triphosphate 
                     mimics the transition state structure for the nucleosidase 
                     reaction and inhibits PhnI activity |CITS: [24111876]|.
                     PhnI is a component of the |FRAME: CPLX0-10309| |CITS: 
                     [21705661][25954983][26280334]|."
