                     /label=phnD
     CDS             complement(4313153..4314169)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="phnD"
                     /locus_tag="b4105"
                     /product="trifunctional phosphonate/phosphate ABC
                     transporter periplasmic binding protein / 
                     phosphonate/phosphate ABC transporter / cryptic 
                     phosphonate/phosphate ABC transporter"
                     /EC_number="7.3.2.2"
                     /label=phnD
                     /note="<i>phnD</i> encodes the periplasmic binding protein
                     of an ATP-dependent phosphonate/phosphate uptake system 
                     that is considered to be cryptic in <i>E. coli</i> K-12. 
                     Purified PhnD binds the naturally occurring phosphonates, 
                     2-aminoethylphosphonate, ethylphosphonate and 
                     methylphosphonate with high affinity (estimated 
                     K<sub>d</sub>s of <0.05&micro;M, 0.2&micro;M and 
                     1.3&micro;M respectively); it also binds phosphate 
                     (estimated K<sub>d</sub> of 50&micro;M) |CITS:[16751609]|. 
                     PhnD has been used in the development of a phosphonate 
                     biosensor |CITS: [16751609]|.
                     <i>psiD</i>: <U>p</U>hosphate <U>s</U>tarvation 
                     <U>i</U>nducible |CITS: [6813506]|"
