     gene            complement(4323764..4325407)
                     /gene="eptA"
                     /locus_tag="b4114"
                     /label=eptA
     CDS             complement(4323764..4325407)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="eptA"
                     /locus_tag="b4114"
                     /product="bifunctional phosphoethanolamine transferase
                     EptA / phosphoethanolamine transferase"
                     /EC_number="2.7.8.43"
                     /label=eptA
                     /note="EptA catalyses the addition of |FRAME: 
                     PHOSPHORYL-ETHANOLAMINE| (pEtN) to the glucosamine 
                     disaccharide of lipid A core oligosaccharide.  This 
                     modification promotes resistance to |FRAME: Polymyxins 
                     ""polymyxin antibiotics""| and antimicrobial peptides. 
                     |FRAME: L-1-PHOSPHATIDYL-ETHANOLAMINE 
                     Phosphatidylethanolamine| serves as the donor and transfer 
                     occurs to the 1-phosphate and/or 4'-phosphate position; the
                     reaction occurs on the outer surface of the inner membrane 
                     |CITS: [12184950][15659161]|. A side product of the 
                     reaction is |FRAME: DIACYLGLYCEROL 
                     ""1,2-diacyl-<i>sn</i>-glycerol""| (DAG), a potential 
                     inhibitor of EptA |CITS: [37070977]|. However, the DAG that
                     is produced in converted rapidly to |FRAME: L-PHOSPHATIDATE
                     phosphatidate| by |FRAME: DIACYLGLYKIN-CPLX| |CITS: 
                     [34843376]|.
                     Modification of <i>E. coli</i> LPS with pEtN is induced in 
                     cells grown under mild acidic conditions |CITS: [15659161]|
                     and in cells grown in LB with ammonium metavanadate 
                     (NH<sub>4</sub>VO<sub>3</sub>) |CITS: [10373459]|. 
                     <i>eptA</i> transcript levels are increased under growth 
                     conditions with low Mg<sup>2+</sup> concentrations, but 
                     these expression levels are decreased significantly in the 
                     <i>pmrD</i> mutant strain compared with the wild-type 
                     strain |CITS: [25605366]|.
                     The EptA (formerly YjdB) protein can be found in the 
                     membrane in a complex with ZipA and an unidentified 24 kDa 
                     protein |CITS: [16079137]|.
                     Related review: |CITS: [32353363]|"
