                     /gene="dtpC"
                     /locus_tag="b4130"
                     /product="trifunctional dipeptide/tripeptide:H(+)
                     symporter DtpC / transport of a tripeptide / transport of a
                     dipeptide"
                     /label=dtpC
                     /note="The DtpC protein is a member of the POT
                     (proton-dependent oligopeptide transporter) family of 
                     peptide transporters |CITS: [7817396]|. DtpC transports 
                     dialanine, trialanine, alanine and the lysine analogue, 
                     aminohexanoic acid <i>in vitro</i> |CITS: [24440353]|
                     DtpC has a higher specificity towards dipeptides compared 
                     to tripeptides |CITS: [19703419]| and displays a preference
                     for dipeptides with a C-terminal lysine residue |CITS: 
                     [24440353]|. Direct binding of Ala-Lys dipeptides to 
                     purified protein has been reported. Binding of the 
                     tripeptide Ala-Ala-Lys and the dipeptide Ala-Gln to the 
                     purified protein was not detected |CITS: [22940668]|. 
                     Binding of Ala-Lys to a DtpC<sub>E388Q</sub> variant could 
                     not be detected in agreement with the observation that 
                     glutamic acid 388 may play a role in ligand binding |CITS: 
                     [21933132], [22940668]|. A high resolution cryo-EM 
                     structure of DtpC provides insight into the basis for 
                     ligand preference |CITS: [35898305]|.
                     DtpC is predicted to contain 14 transmembrane regions with 
                     the C-terminus located in the cytoplasm |CITS: [15919996]|.
                     <i>dtpC</i>: <U>d</U>ipeptide <U>t</U>ripeptide 
                     <U>p</U>ermease C"
