     gene            complement(4353162..4354859)
                     /gene="dsbD"
                     /locus_tag="b4136"
                     /label=dsbD
     CDS             complement(4353162..4354859)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="dsbD"
                     /locus_tag="b4136"
                     /product="thiol-disulfide exchange protein DsbD"
                     /EC_number="1.8.4.16"
                     /label=dsbD
                     /note="DsbD is an inner membrane protein which acts within
                     a reductive pathway that maintains the periplasmic 
                     disulfide oxidoreductases DsbC and DsbG and the cytochrome 
                     c maturation protein CcmG in their catalytically active 
                     reduced form. DsbD mediates electron transfer from 
                     cytoplasmic thioredoxin to the periplasmic substrate 
                     proteins via inter and intra molecular disulfide exchange 
                     reactions
                     DsbD consists of three domains: a periplasmic N-terminal 
                     domain (nDsbD or DsbD&alpha;) which contains an 
                     immunoglobulin-like fold, a central transmembrane (TM) 
                     domain (tmDsbD or DsbD&beta;) with eight predicted TM 
                     helices and a periplasmic C-terminal domain (cDsbD or 
                     DsbD&gamma;) which contains a thioredoxin-like fold |CITS: 
                     [7628442] [7623667][12033924]|. Each domain contains a pair
                     of cysteines which are essential for function |CITS: 
                     [10545108]|.
                     The electron cascade is initiated with the reduction of 
                     tmDsbD by thioredoxin, cDsbD then shuttles electrons from 
                     tmDsbD to nDsbD and reduced nDsbD passes the electrons on 
                     to the periplasmic substrate proteins |CITS: [10760137] 
                     [10712691][11114333][12004064]|. DsbD shuffles electrons 
                     from the cytoplasm to the periplasm without the involvement
                     of additional cofactors such as quinone, FAD or heme |CITS:
                     [18571669]|; transfer of electrons across the membrane 
                     occurs via thiol disulfide exchange reactions involving the
                     two redox active cysteines contained in each of the three 
                     domains of DsbD and reaction intermediates containing mixed
                     disulfide complexes have been isolated 
                     |CITS:[11114333][12925743][17641688]|. Electron flow from 
                     thioredoxin to the periplasmic substrate proteins via DsbD 
                     is thermodynamically driven; redox potentials for all the 
                     cysteine pairs involved have been determined (see |CITS: 
                     [18571669]| and citations within).
                     <i>dsbD</i> is required for biogenesis of <i>c</i>-type 
                     cytochromes in the periplasm |CITS: [7623667][9003292]| 
                     (see also |CITS: [7957865][8187885]|. <i>dsbD</i> mutants 
                     (<i>dsbD</i>::mini-Tn<i>10</i>Cam) display defects in 
                     alkaline phosphatase folding which can be complemented by 
                     the addition of reduced dithiothreitol (DTT) |CITS: 
                     [8917542]|. <i>dsbD</i> mutants accumulate oxidised DsbC 
                     |CITS: [9352906]| and oxidised DsbG |CITS: [10075670]|. 
                     Overexpression of <i>dsbD</i> results in phenotypes (loss 
                     of alkaline phosphatase activity and loss of motility) that
                     are consistent with the misfolding/reduction of periplasmic
                     proteins containing disulfide bonds; the purified 
                     C-terminal domain of DsbD is able to reduce insulin in the 
                     presence of DTT; <i>dsbD</i> is essential for growth at 
                     temperatures above 42&deg;C |CITS: [7628442]|.
                     <i>dipZ</i>: <U>d</U>isulfide <U>i</U>somerase-like 
                     <U>p</U>rotein Z |CITS: [7623667]|<BR><i>cutA2</i>: |CITS: 
                     [7623666]|
                     Reviews: |CITS: [15380548][16786221]|<BR>Selected related 
                     reviews: |CITS: 
                     [9098040][10841975][20367276][22901060][24576574]|"
