                     /label=groL
                     /note="GroEL protein synthesis was stimulated both by heat
                     shock in vivo and by the heat shock-specific RNA polymerase
                     E&sigma;<sup>32</sup> |CITS: [8349564]|. Depletion of GroEL
                     via targeted protein degradation (TPD) results in reduced 
                     bacterial survival and dysregulation of the proteome |CITS:
                     [40562793]|.
                     GroEL was identified as a putative phosphohistidine 
                     acceptor using chemoproteomics analysis with a stable 
                     analogue of 3-pHis |CITS: [40201162]|."
