     gene            4366134..4366259
                     /gene="ecnA"
                     /locus_tag="b4410"
                     /label=ecnA
     CDS             4366134..4366259
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ecnA"
                     /locus_tag="b4410"
                     /product="entericidin A lipoprotein, antidote to
                     entericidin B"
                     /label=ecnA
                     /note="<i>ecnAB</i> encodes an antidote/toxin system which
                     may function as a starvation adaptation that supports 
                     further cell growth at the expense of dying subpopulations;
                     the functions of EcnAB are consistent with a programmed 
                     cell death system |CITS: [9677290]|.
                     The EcnA lipoprotein is predicted to localise to the outer 
                     membrane; EcnA may adopt an amphipathic &alpha;-helical 
                     conformation |CITS: [9677290]|.
                     The entericidin A lipoprotein (EcnA) functions as an 
                     antidote to the bacteriolytic |FRAME: MONOMER0-1563 
                     ""entericidin B""| lipoprotein. Deregulated expression of 
                     <i>ecnB</i> results in stationary phase bacteriolysis; this
                     phenotype is eliminated upon expression of <i>ecnA</i> 
                     |CITS:[9677290]|.
                     <i>ecnA</i> does not appear to have an assoicated promoter 
                     but a Rho-independent terminator, located upstream of 
                     <i>ecnA</i> may attenuate EcnA production |CITS: 
                     [9677290]|. The entericidin locus is non-essential in <i>E.
                     coli</i> K-12 |CITS: [9677290]|."
                     /translation="MMKRLIVLVLLASTLLTGCNTARGFGEDIKHLGNSISRAAS"
                     /go_component="plasma membrane [goid 0005886] [evidence
