     gene            complement(4367006..4367539)
                     /gene="blc"
                     /locus_tag="b4149"
                     /label=blc
     CDS             complement(4367006..4367539)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="blc"
                     /locus_tag="b4149"
                     /product="outer membrane lipocalin protein"
                     /label=blc
                     /note="The Blc protein is a globomycin-sensitive outer
                     membrane lipoprotein |CITS: [7559452]|. <i>blc</i> is a 
                     member of the RpoS regulon; expression is induced at the 
                     transition between exponential and stationary phase growth 
                     |CITS: [7559452]|. Blc contains a typical lipocalin fold 
                     consisting of an 8 stranded &beta;-barrel with an &alpha; 
                     helix at the C-terminus; the protein contains a long, flat,
                     narrow cavity and the interior walls contain hydrophobic, 
                     semi-polar and charged residues. Blc may play a role in 
                     lipid transport or storage under stress conditions |CITS: 
                     [15044022]|.
                     Blc binds fatty acids (myristic, palmitoleic, palmitic, 
                     <i>cis</i>-vaccenic and others) and phospholipids with 
                     micromolar affinities |CITS: [16920109]|. Blc is a 
                     functional dimer |CITS: [16920109]|; Blc is a monomer in 
                     both crystal form and in solution; the dimeric structure 
                     observed by |CITS: [16920109]| may form as a consequence of
                     the cloning strategy |CITS: [21123871]|.
                     Blc may bind heme |CITS: [33210733]|
                     <i>blc</i>: <U>b</U>acterial <U>l</U>ipo<U>c</U>alin |CITS:
                     [7559452]|"
