     gene            complement(4368824..4369183)
                     /gene="frdD"
                     /locus_tag="b4151"
                     /label=frdD
     CDS             complement(4368824..4369183)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="frdD"
                     /locus_tag="b4151"
                     /product="bifunctional fumarate reductase membrane protein
                     FrdD / fumarate reductase"
                     /EC_number="1.3.5.1"
                     /label=frdD
                     /note="This is one of two integral membrane proteins in
                     the four subunit fumarate reductase complex |CITS: 
                     [6754697]|. FrdC and FrdD each have three transmembrane 
                     helices connected by periplasmic loops; the N-terminus is 
                     located in the cytoplasm and the C-terminus is located in 
                     the periplasm. The transmembrane helices are positioned to 
                     form two menaquinone binding pockets |CITS: [10373108]| 
                     Despite similar function, hydrophobicity, and protein size,
                     the FrdC and FrdD subunits of fumarate reductase do not 
                     share significant sequence identity with the corresponding 
                     membrane-binding subunits of succinate dehydrogenase, SdhC 
                     and SdhD |CITS: [6383359]|.
                     In &Delta;|FRAME: EG10509|, &Delta;|FRAME: G6115| and 
                     wild-type <i>E. coli</i> exposed to sub-lethal 
                     concentrations of amoxicillin, multiple and consistent 
                     mutations were found in <i>|FRAME: EG10040|</i>, its direct
                     upstream gene <i>|FRAME: EG10333|</i> and in |FRAME: 
                     EG10896|, pointing to their roles in amoxicillin resistance
                     |CITS: [39970152]|."
