     CDS             complement(4370327..4372135)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="frdA"
                     /locus_tag="b4154"
                     /product="bifunctional fumarate reductase flavoprotein
                     subunit / fumarate reductase"
                     /EC_number="1.3.5.1"
                     /label=frdA
                     /note="FrdA is one of two catalytic subunits in the four
                     subunit fumarate reductase complex. This subunit contains 
                     the FAD cofactor |CITS: [381310][7037404]|.
                     This protein has similarity to the SdhA subunit of 
                     succinate dehydrogenase |CITS: [6383359]|. A 2.2 &Aring; 
                     crystal structure of L-aspartate oxidase suggests that an 
                     unusual tertiary structure is shared by L-aspartate 
                     oxidase, the SdhA subunit of succinate dehydrogenase, and 
                     the FrdA subunit of fumarate reductase |CITS: [10425677]|. 
                     FrdA interacts directly with the FliG subunit of the 
                     flagellar motor; subunit binding probably occurs within the
                     context of an intact fumarate reductase complex; FrdA 
                     preferentially binds to the clockwise state of FliG and 
                     enhances clockwise rotation likely by stabilising the 
                     motor's clockwise state |CITS: [31412261]|.
                     Redox proteomics indicates that Cys-381 is significantly 
                     oxidized in a &Delta;|FRAME: CPLX0-245 Ahp| strain compared
                     to wild type |CITS: [37725887]|."
