     gene            4399092..4399823
                     /gene="rlmB"
                     /locus_tag="b4180"
                     /label=rlmB
     CDS             4399092..4399823
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rlmB"
                     /locus_tag="b4180"
                     /product="23S rRNA 2'-O-ribose G2251 methyltransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.1.1.185"
                     /label=rlmB
                     /note="RlmB is the methyltransferase responsible for
                     methylation of 23S rRNA at the 2'-<i>O</i> position of the 
                     ribose at the G2251 nucleotide |CITS: [11698387]|.
                     RlmB is a 2'O-methyltransferase that belongs to the SPOUT 
                     superfamily |CITS: [12377117]|. A crystal structure of RlmB
                     has been solved at 2.5 &Aring; resolution. The N terminus 
                     is implicated in rRNA recognition, and the C-terminal 
                     domain contains a deep knot structure that encompasses the 
                     predicted SAM binding site |CITS: [12377117]|. 
                     Computational docking analysis of the SAM binding site 
                     allowed inference of functionally important residues and a 
                     reaction mechanism |CITS: [12689347]|.
                     An <i>rlmB</i> deletion mutant does not show growth defects
                     or defects in ribosome maturation |CITS: [11698387]|. 
                     Ribosomal RNA in a &Delta;<i>rlmB</i> mutant was more 
                     susceptible to reactive oxygen species (ROS) and UVA damage
                     than wild-type |CITS: [34277707]|.
                     A study that used a &Delta;10 ribosomal modification 
                     deletion strain lacking nucleoside modifications around the
                     peptidyl-transferase center (PTC) due to deletions of 
                     |FRAME: EG11118|, |FRAME: G6488|, |FRAME: EG12401|, |FRAME:
                     EG11794|, |FRAME: G6581|, |FRAME: EG12433|, |FRAME: 
                     EG11921|, |FRAME: G7845|, |FRAME: G6746| and |FRAME: 
                     EG11507| found that RlmE is the most effective at 
                     alleviating the severe growth defect phenotype of the 
                     &Delta;10 strain under different growth temperatures from 
                     37 &deg;C down to 25 &deg;C and that RlmB can partially 
                     complement the RlmE-containing mutant with respect to large
                     ribosomal subunit assembly in late exponential phase 
                     cultures as determined by sucrose gradient ribosome profile
                     assay. An E198A mutation in RlmB not involved in 
                     methylation activity can also alleviate some of the growth 
                     defect of the &Delta;10 strain at 30 &deg;C, pointing to a 
                     possible alternative function of RlmB |CITS: [38554109]|. 
                     RlmB: ""<b>r</b>RNA <b>l</b>arge subunit 
                     <b>m</b>ethyltransferase <b>B</b>"" |CITS: [11698387]|"
