     CDS             complement(4405834..4406109)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yjfN"
                     /locus_tag="b4188"
                     /product="protease activator YjfN"
                     /label=yjfN
                     /note="<i>yjfN</i> encodes a predicted small, periplasmic 
                     protein; YjfN is a simultaneous substrate and activator of 
                     DegP proteolysis.
                     Purified YjfN is degraded by DegP <i>in vitro</i>; YjfN 
                     binds to DegP and activates cleavage of a model reporter 
                     substrate; YjfN promotes the DegP-catalysed degradation of 
                     denatured OmpA and SurA-bound OmpA <i>in vitro</i> |CITS: 
                     [28947671]|.
                     Over-expression of <i>yjfN</i> suppresses the high 
                     temperature misfolded protein stress of cells producing a 
                     less active DegP variant (DegP<sub>A184S</sub>) |CITS: 
                     [28947671]|.
                     YjfN is a member of the <i>E. coli</i> YhcN family 
                     consisting of nine paralogous small (&le; 150 aa) proteins 
                     |CITS: [9588799]|.
                     An alternative translation initiation codon 9 nt upstream 
                     of the annotated codon has been found; both codons may be 
                     used, potentially leading to the expression of two isoforms
                     |CITS: [30904393]|.
                     Comment: |CITS: [29109189]|"
