     gene            4414935..4415330
                     /gene="rpsF"
                     /locus_tag="b4200"
                     /label=rpsF
     CDS             4414935..4415330
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rpsF"
                     /locus_tag="b4200"
                     /product="multifunctional 30S ribosomal subunit protein S6
                     / S6:S18 ribosomal subunit complex / 30S ribosomal subunit 
                     / ribosome"
                     /label=rpsF
                     /note="The S6 protein is a component of the 30S subunit of
                     the ribosome. S6 interacts with the central domain of 16S 
                     rRNA |CITS: [6208366][2459389]|.
                     Protein-Protein Interaction (PPI) networks have been 
                     examined with algebraic topology analysis showing that most
                     interacting proteins with S6 protein are related to the 
                     protein translation |CITS: [35560988]|.
                     The S6 protein contains glutamate residues at the 
                     C-terminus, only two of which are encoded by the 
                     <i>rpsF</i> gene |CITS: [386035][3528756]|; up to four 
                     additional glutamate residues are added 
                     post-translationally by the |FRAME: EG10852-MONOMER RimK| 
                     enzyme |CITS: [2570347]|. This form of S6 accumulates when 
                     the <i>soxR</i> regulon is activated |CITS: [1696718]|. In 
                     bacteriophage T7-infected cells, S6 is phosphorylated 
                     |CITS: [8022276]|.
                     Expression analysis of <i>rpsF</i>p indicates that it may 
                     be autoregulated by one or more of its operon components 
                     |CITS: [23292777]|. Coexpressed S6:S18 were found to bind 
                     to the <i>rpsF</i> 5'-UTR in a region with structural 
                     similarity to their binding site in 16S rRNA |CITS: 
                     [23980204]|. The S6:S18 complex was shown to repress 
                     translation of <i>rpsF</i> |CITS: [26447183]|.
                     A class of mutations in <i>rpsF</i> supresses the 
                     temperature-sensitive growth defect of certain <i>dnaG</i> 
                     alleles |CITS: [9093842]|. The <i>rpsF292</i> allele, which
                     introduces a stop codon in place of Glu98, is an effective 
                     suppressor of &Delta;<i>recG</i>. The effect is due to both
                     elimination of RpsF and lower expression of PriB |CITS: 
                     [22957744]|. Both <i>rimK</i> and <i>rpsF</i> deletion 
                     mutants reduce the basal level of SOS response and increase
                     resistance to hydroxyurea |CITS: [23292777]|. SdgH: 
                     ""<b>s</b>upressor of <b>d</b>na<b>G</b>"" |CITS: 
                     [9093842]|
                     Review: |CITS: [22649682]|"
