     gene            complement(4422981..4423841)
                     /gene="qorB"
                     /locus_tag="b4211"
                     /label=qorB
     CDS             complement(4422981..4423841)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="qorB"
                     /locus_tag="b4211"
                     /product="NAD(P)H:quinone oxidoreductase"
                     /label=qorB
                     /note="QorB is an NAD(P)H:quinone oxidoreductase.  EPR and 
                     kinetic studies suggest that the enzyme catalyzes the 
                     two-electron reduction of quinones using a ping-pong 
                     mechanism.  Crystal structures of the enzyme alone and in 
                     complex with NADPH have been solved |CITS: 
                     [14747727][18455185]|.
                     QorB shows very low flavin reductase activity and ferrous 
                     iron release activity in the presence of free FAD |CITS: 
                     [31281172]|.
                     A <i>qorB</i> mutant shows no significant growth phenotype,
                     while overexpression of <i>qorB</i> leads to growth 
                     retardation and lowered expression of a number of proteins 
                     involved in carbon metabolism |CITS: [18455185]|. The gene 
                     was identified by a computational analysis as a candidate 
                     for encoding resistance to the antiobiotic |FRAME: 
                     CPD-9195|. Resistance was confirmed by wet-lab experiments 
                     that compared the minimum inhibitory concentration (MIC) of
                     a knock-out strain to that of the wild-type strain |CITS: 
                     [35487919]|.
                     QorB: ""NAD(P)H-dependent <b>q</b>uinone 
                     <b>o</b>xido<b>r</b>eductase"" |CITS: [18455185]|"
                     /translation="MIAITGATGQLGHYVIESLMKTVPASQIVAIVRNPAKAQALAAQG
