     gene            4423930..4424310
                     /gene="ytfH"
                     /locus_tag="b4212"
                     /label=ytfH
     CDS             4423930..4424310
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ytfH"
                     /locus_tag="b4212"
                     /product="putative transcriptional regulator YtfH"
                     /label=ytfH
                     /note="YtfH, which contains a helix-turn-helix motif to
                     bind DNA in its N-terminal domain, appears to belong to the
                     RipR family of transcription factors, and it was predicted 
                     to regulate genes related to metabolism |CITS: [35880217]|.
                     YtfH was mentioned as a predicted inner membrane protein 
                     that may be a substrate for the periplasmic chaperone YfgM 
                     |CITS: [25403562]|.
                     Upstream of the <i>ytfH</i> gene, a sequence was found that
                     could work as a transcriptional promoter, and the 
                     transcription of the <i>ytfH</i> gene is affected by heat 
                     stress, oxidative stress, and glucose-lactose shift |CITS: 
                     [35880217]|.
                     The YtfH binding landscape was globally mapped in vivo by 
                     standardized ChIP-seq and quantitatively modeled using 
                     BoltzNet, a biophysically informed neural network that 
                     infers binding energy from sequence data |CITS:[40335485]|.
                     The resulting ChIP-seq binding regions are available in 
                     RegulonDB (<a href=""https://regulondb.cc 
                     g.unam.mx/ht/dataset/TFBINDING/source=GALAGAN"">Galagan 
                     collection</a>), and the corresponding energy matrix and 
                     genomic binding profiles can be accessed at <a 
                     href=""http://boltznet.bu.edu"">boltznet.bu.edu</a> 
                     |CITS:[40335485]|."
