     gene            4438509..4438859
                     /gene="chpB"
                     /locus_tag="b4225"
                     /label=chpB
     CDS             4438509..4438859
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="chpB"
                     /locus_tag="b4225"
                     /product="trifunctional endoribonuclease toxin ChpB /
                     tmRNA endonuclease / ChpB-ChpS complex"
                     /EC_number="4.6.1.22"
                     /label=chpB
                     /note="ChpB is the toxin component of the ChpB-ChpS 
                     toxin-antitoxin system.
                     ChpB inhibits cell growth when it is overexpressed, or when
                     its partner protein ChpS is absent |CITS: [8226627]|. This 
                     growth inhibition effect appears to result from ChpB's 
                     ability to cleave RNAs. Identified cleavage targets include
                     RNAs from <i>era</i>, <i>mazG</i>, and translated tmRNA 
                     |CITS: [15901733][12972253]|. Increased tmRNA abundance 
                     blocks the growth inhibition effects of ChpB, and loss of 
                     tmRNA leads to increased sensitivity to ChpB |CITS: 
                     [12972253]|.
                     An analysis of the targets and site specificity of ChpB 
                     showed cleavage site specificity, cleaving between the U 
                     and A nucleotides of a UAC motif.  Like other <i>E. 
                     coli</i> endoribonuclease toxins, ChpB activity does not 
                     affect mature ribosomes, but inhibits ribosome biogenesis, 
                     likely by affecting the translation of a specific set of 
                     ribosomal proteins |CITS: [34544284]|.
                     Review: |CITS: [31932311]|"
