     gene            4439779..4440735
                     /gene="ytfQ"
                     /locus_tag="b4227"
                     /label=ytfQ
     CDS             4439779..4440735
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="ytfQ"
                     /locus_tag="b4227"
                     /product="multifunctional galactofuranose ABC transporter 
                     periplasmic binding protein / galactofuranose ABC 
                     transporter / transport of beta-D-galactofuranose / 
                     transport of alpha-D-galactofuranose"
                     /EC_number="7.5.2.9"
                     /label=ytfQ
                     /note="YtfQ is the periplasmic binding component of a 
                     galactofuranose ABC transporter.
                     Purified YtfQ binds galactose with a K<sub>d</sub> of 
                     1.7&mu;M and arabinose with a K<sub>d</sub> of 1.3&mu;M; 
                     YtfQ exhibits selective binding of galactofuranose over 
                     galactopyranose; the inferred affinity of YtfQ for 
                     galactofuranose is 0.13&mu;M; YtfQ is able to recognise 
                     both &alpha; and &beta; forms of galactofuranose; YtfQ does
                     not bind glucose |CITS: [19744923]|.
                     The crystal structure of YtfQ with a single molecule of 
                     galactofuranose in its ligand binding pocket has been 
                     resolved at 1.2&Aring;. The binding protein has two 
                     &alpha;/&beta; domains linked by a hinge region; 
                     galactofuranose binds in a cleft between the two domains 
                     and is totally buried within the protein; a disulfide bond 
                     is present between cysteine residues 129 and 193 |CITS: 
                     [19744923]|.
                     YtfQ is upregulated in fed-batch phase (compared to 
                     exponential phase) during glucose-limited fermentation 
                     |CITS: [16180237]|."
