                     /product="trehalose-6-phosphate hydrolase"
                     /EC_number="3.2.1.93"
                     /label=treC
                     /note="<i>E. coli</i> can utilize trehalose as the sole
                     source of carbon.  Under low-osmolarity conditions, 
                     trehalose is imported into the cytoplasm by the 
                     trehalose-specific PTS transporter, converting it into 
                     trehalose-6-phoshate.  Trehalose-6-phosphate hydrolase 
                     (TreC) then hydrolyzes trehalose-6-phosphate into glucose 
                     and glucose-6-phosphate |CITS: [8083158][6370169]|.
                     TreC may be able to catalyze the conversion of maltose to 
                     maltose-1-phosphate, which may act as an inducer of 
                     <i>malK</i> expression |CITS: [10361281]|.
                     Expression of TreC is induced by trehalose, but only under 
                     low-osmolarity conditions |CITS: [6370169][7608078]|.
                     "
