                     /product="DUF386 domain-containing toxin-antitoxin biofilm
                     protein TabA"
                     /label=tabA
                     /note="The toxin-antitoxin biofilm protein TabA may
                     decrease biofilm dispersal in response to the combined 
                     activity
                     of several toxin-antitoxin (TA) systems.
                     Simultaneous deletion of five TA systems leads to increased
                     expression of <i>tabA</i>.  Overexpression of <i>tabA</i> 
                     leads to decreased biofilm formation at 8 hours, but 
                     increased biofilm formation by 24 hours; deletion of 
                     <i>tabA</i> has the opposite effect.  At 8 hours, deletion 
                     of <i>tabA</i> increases expression of fimbriae-associated 
                     genes |CITS: [19060153]|. Transcription of <i>tabA</i> was 
                     predicted to be regulated by KdgR |CITS: [11115104]|.
                     TabA: ""<b>t</b>oxin-<b>a</b>ntitoxin <b>b</b>iofilm 
                     protein"" |CITS: [19060153]|"
