                     replisome"
                     /label=holC
                     /note="HolC is the &chi; subunit of the &chi;-&psi; dimer.
                     &chi; has more recently been found to form a complex with 
                     |FRAME: G6992-MONOMER| <i>in vitro</i>. The YoaA-&chi; 
                     dimer has DNA-dependent helicase activity and requires a 5'
                     single-stranded overhang or ssDNA gap for DNA unwinding; 
                     YoaA-&chi; unwinds DNA with a 5' flap and various types of 
                     damaged DNA (see |CITS: [36509145]|). |FRAME: CPLX0-8165 
                     SSB| interacts with YoaA-&chi; and affects the helicase 
                     activity of YoaA-&chi; in a substrate-dependent manner; 
                     YoaA-&chi; may pull SSB along while it translocates on DNA 
                     |CITS: [40442115]|."
