     gene            4476035..4477135
                     /gene="lptF"
                     /locus_tag="b4261"
                     /label=lptF
     CDS             4476035..4477135
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="lptF"
                     /locus_tag="b4261"
                     /product="bifunctional lipopolysaccharide transport system
                     protein LptF / lipopolysaccharide transport system"
                     /EC_number="7.5.2.5"
                     /label=lptF
                     /note="LptF is an essential inner membrane component of
                     the Lpt lipopolysaccharide (LPS) transport system.
                     LptF contains six predicted transmembrane domains with the 
                     C-terminus located in the cytoplasm |CITS: [15919996]|. 
                     <i>lptF</i> is essential |CITS: [16738554][18375759]|. 
                     Depletion of LptF (and/or LptG) results in a filamenting 
                     phenotype, increased sensitivity to hydrophobic antibiotics
                     and an altered form of LPS; LptFG are required for LPS to 
                     reach the outer leaflet of the outer membrane |CITS: 
                     [18375759]|. LptF forms a complex with LptG, LptB and LptC 
                     |CITS: [19500581]|. LptF and LptG each contain a coupling 
                     helix which mediates their interaction with LptB; the LptFG
                     coupling helices likely coordinate ATPase activity with LPS
                     extraction from the inner membrane but each appears to have
                     a distinct role |CITS: [27795402]| (see further |CITS: 
                     [31431556][32236984]|).
                     <i>lptF</i> has been the subject of a pilot study to 
                     examine genetic interactions involving essential genes 
                     |CITS: [24463526]|."
