     gene            complement(4481023..4482342)
                     /gene="idnT"
                     /locus_tag="b4265"
                     /label=idnT
     CDS             complement(4481023..4482342)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="idnT"
                     /locus_tag="b4265"
                     /product="multifunctional
                     L-idonate/5-ketogluconate/gluconate transporter / 
                     5-ketogluconate transporter / gluconate transporter / 
                     L-idonate transporter"
                     /label=idnT
                     /note="IdnT is a probable L-idonate and D-gluconate
                     transporter. Originally thought to be a subsidiary 
                     gluconate uptake system, the primary role of IdnT appears 
                     to be in L-idonate transport.  The <I>idnT</I> gene is 
                     located in the <I>idnDOTR</I>
                     operon involved in metabolising L-idonate to D-gluconate 
                     |CITS:[9658018]|. Expression of this operon is induced by 
                     idonate or by 5-ketogluconate |CITS:[9658018]|. The cloned 
                     <I>idnT</I> gene was shown to confer gluconate transport in
                     a gluconate transport negative mutant in whole cell 
                     experiments with IdnT displaying a Km of 60 &mu;M for 
                     gluconate |CITS:[9119199]|.  While direct transport of 
                     L-idonate has not been shown experimentally, IdnT-mediated 
                     gluconate transport is strongly inhibited by idonate 
                     |CITS:[9658018]|.  IdnT is a member of the Gnt family of 
                     gluconate transporters
                     |CITS:[9119199]| and is homologous to the <I>E. coli</I> 
                     GntT and GntU gluconate transporters. Gluconate uptake has 
                     been reported to occur via a proton-symport mechanism in 
                     <I>E. coli</I> |CITS:[4585187]|.  It seems likely that IdnT
                     mediates L-idonate/proton and D-gluconate/proton symport.  
                     Mutant phenotype in growth assays and expression analysis 
                     show IdnT also transports 5-keto-D-gluconate 
                     |CITS:[17088549]|."
