     gene            4484440..4485003
                     /gene="idnK"
                     /locus_tag="b4268"
                     /label=idnK
     CDS             4484440..4485003
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="idnK"
                     /locus_tag="b4268"
                     /product="bifunctional D-gluconate kinase, thermosensitive
                     / D-gluconate kinase"
                     /EC_number="2.7.1.12"
                     /label=idnK
                     /note="<i>E. coli</i> encodes two D-gluconate kinases
                     which can be distinguished by their thermal sensitivity. 
                     The <i>idnK</i>-encoded enzyme, described here, is 
                     thermosensitive |CITS: [3040894]|, and its primary function
                     is in the L-idonate degradation pathway |CITS: [14973046]|.
                      When grown on D-gluconate, the <i>gntK</i>-encoded 
                     thermostable enzyme is prevalent |CITS: [1336799]|.
                     Gluconokinase activity is induced by growth on gluconate 
                     |CITS: [4574689]|.  Expression of <i>idnK</i> is catabolite
                     repressed and induced by L-idonate or 5-ketogluconate 
                     |CITS: [14973046]|.  An <i>idnK</i> insertion mutant is 
                     unable to grow on L-idonate or 5-ketogluconate as the sole 
                     source of carbon, and an <i>idnK gntK</i> double mutant is 
                     also unable to grow on D-gluconate as the sole source of 
                     carbon |CITS: [14973046]|.
                     GntV: ""<b>g</b>luco<b>n</b>a<b>t</b>e""
                     IdnK: ""<b>id</b>o<b>n</b>ate"" |CITS: [9658018]|
                     Review: |CITS: [9657988]|"
