     gene            4493875..4495092
                     /gene="nanX"
                     /locus_tag="b4279"
                     /label=nanX
     CDS             4493875..4495092
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="nanX"
                     /locus_tag="b4279"
                     /product="2,7-anhydro-N-acetylneuraminate transporter
                     NanX"
                     /label=nanX
                     /note="<i>nanX</i> encodes an inner membrane transporter
                     that appears specific for |FRAME: CPD-6182| (2,7-AN) - a 
                     dehydrated form of the abundant sialic acid |FRAME: 
                     N-ACETYLNEURAMINATE ""<i>N</i>-acetylneuraminate""|.
                     In an engineered strain lacking sialic acid transporters 
                     and expressing the sialic acid utilisation pathway 
                     constitutively (<i>E. coli</i> BW25113 
                     &Delta;<i>nanT</I>::FRT &Delta;<i>nanX</i>::F3 
                     &Delta;<i>nanR</i> &Delta;<i>nagC</i>), the expression of 
                     recombinant NanX supports growth with 
                     2,7-anhydro-<i>N</i>-acetylneuraminate as sole carbon 
                     source but does not support growth with |FRAME: CPD-23638| 
                     (2,3-EN) nor with <i>N</i>-acetylneuraminate |CITS: 
                     [38488830]|. Deletion of <i>nanX</i> (in strain BW25113) 
                     results in complete loss of <i>in vitro</i> growth on 
                     2,7-AN; NanX, functioning together with a co-expressed 
                     |FRAME: CPLX0-8544 hydratase|, likely supports scavenging 
                     of 2,7-AN in the human gut |CITS: [32669363]| (see also 
                     |CITS: [32542330]|).
                     NanX is a member of the Major Facilitator Superfamily of 
                     transporters and it has sequence homology (35% identity, 
                     55% similarity) with the |FRAME: NANT-MONOMER 
                     ""<i>N</i>-acetylneuraminate:H<sup>+</sup> symporter""| 
                     NanT |CITS: [32669363]|. NanX is an archetypal member of 
                     the bacterial sialic acid transporter 1 (ST1) family |CITS:
                     [34184979]|.
                     The <i>nanXY</i> operon is part of a 'sialoregulon'; 
                     <i>N</i>-acetylneuraminate induces expression of 
                     <i>nanXY</i> by directly inactivating the NanR 
                     transcriptional regulator |CITS: [23935044]| (see also 
                     |CITS: [23724337]|)."
