                     /locus_tag="b4290"
                     /label=fecB
     CDS             complement(4503223..4504125)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="fecB"
                     /locus_tag="b4290"
                     /product="trifunctional ferric citrate ABC transporter
                     periplasmic binding protein / ferric citrate ABC 
                     transporter / transport of ferric dicitrate"
                     /EC_number="7.2.2.18"
                     /label=fecB
                     /note="<i>fecB</i> encodes the periplasmic substrate
                     binding component of the iron dicitrate ABC transporter. 
                     FecB is a Class III periplasmic binding protein - it is 
                     predicted to be a bilobal protein with a single 
                     &alpha;-helical hinge connecting the two lobes |CITS: 
                     [26600288]|.
                     Purified FecB binds both iron-free and iron-loaded citrate 
                     at pH 5.5 and pH 8; purified FecB binds 
                     [Fe<sub>2</sub>(cit)<sub>2</sub>]<sup>2-</sup> (di-iron 
                     dicitrate) and [Fe(cit)<sub>2</sub>]<sup>5-</sup> (iron 
                     dicitrate) with similar affinity; purified FecB binds the 
                     tricarboxylates isocitrate and <i>cis</i>-aconitic acid and
                     the citric acid derivatives tricarballyic acid and 
                     hydroxycitrate; purified FecB binds with other 
                     metal-citrate complexes, including Ga<sup>3+</sup>-citrate,
                     Al<sup>3+</sup>-citrate and In<sup>3+</sup>-citrate |CITS: 
                     [26600288]|."
