     gene            complement(4504170..4506494)
                     /gene="fecA"
                     /locus_tag="b4291"
                     /label=fecA
     CDS             complement(4504170..4506494)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="fecA"
                     /locus_tag="b4291"
                     /product="trifunctional ferric citrate outer membrane
                     transporter / ferric citrate outer membrane transport 
                     complex / transport of ferric citrate"
                     /label=fecA
                     /note="FecA is an outer membrane (OM) protein which
                     mediates the citrate dependent import of ferric iron; FecA 
                     mediated transport across the OM is energized by the inner 
                     membrane proton gradient; energy transduction is 
                     facilitated by the |FRAME: CPLX0-1923| (reviewed in |CITS: 
                     [7654405]|). FecA also signals the extracellular presence 
                     of iron to the FecR/FecI anti-sigma factor/sigma factor 
                     pair in the Fec signaling pathway.
                     The outer membrane protein, FecA, is expressed under 
                     iron-limiting growth conditions in the presence of citrate 
                     |CITS: [7007312]|. <i>fecA</i> forms an operon with 
                     <i>fecBCDE</i> encoding a ferric dicitrate ABC transporter;
                     the operon responds to ferric citrate induction and 
                     Fur-Fe<sup>2+</sup> repression |CITS: 
                     [2254251][7557462][9575233]|. Ferric citrate does not have 
                     to enter the cell to induce transcription of the operon; 
                     FecA (and the Ton complex) are directly involved in 
                     <i>fec</i> operon induction independent of their role in 
                     transport; substrate binding to FecA initiates a signal 
                     that is transferred across the inner membrane by |FRAME: 
                     EG10292-MONOMER ""FecR""| to activate the the iron 
                     starvation responsive sigma factor |FRAME: PD00440 
                     ""FecI""|, which facilitates binding of RNA polymerase to 
                     the upstream region of <i>fecA</i> |CITS: 
                     [6376472][7729419][7752886][9044267]| (and see |CITS: 
                     [9148773]|). The N-terminal, periplasmic region of FecA 
                     interacts with the C-terminal portion of FecR |CITS: 
                     [10633096]| (see further |CITS: [12813067][16923915]|). 
                     FecA consists of three structural domains: a monomeric 
                     22-stranded &beta;-barrel in the membrane; a globular plug 
                     domain which occludes the channel, and an N-terminal 
                     flexible extension (also called the transcriptional domain)
                     which extends into the periplasm; crystal structures of 
                     unliganded FecA and its complex with ferric chloride 
                     suggest the protein mediates transport by a bipartite 
                     gating mechanism |CITS: [11872840][12196171]| (see also 
                     |CITS: [12948487][16313612][18178655]|). FecA interacts 
                     with TonB; this interaction does not require the PMF and is
                     enhanced in the presence of substrate; in-frame deletion of
                     the FecA 'TonB box' results in loss of both transport and 
                     signaling functions |CITS: [12618451]|. TonB-energy 
                     transduction serves to drive transport and bring the FecA 
                     N-terminal transcriptional domain into proximity of the 
                     inner membrane receptor FecR |CITS: [22982293]|.
                     Early studies characterized a citrate-dependent system of 
                     iron uptake in <i>E. coli</i> K-12 wild-type and mutant 
                     strains |CITS: [4919746][4587079][783142][6268411]|. 
                     <i>fec</i> mutants grow normally on low-iron media 
                     containing 2,3-dihydroxybenzoate but are unable to grow in 
                     the presence of citrate |CITS: [346580]|.
                     <i>fec</i>: <U>fe</U>rric <U>c</U>itrate"
