     gene            complement(4506581..4507534)
                     /gene="fecR"
                     /locus_tag="b4292"
                     /label=fecR
     CDS             complement(4506581..4507534)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="fecR"
                     /locus_tag="b4292"
                     /product="ferric citrate regulator FecR"
                     /label=fecR
                     /note="FecR is an inner membrane protein which
                     participates in a trans-envelope signaling pathway to the 
                     iron starvation responsive, extracytoplasmic function (ECF)
                     sigma factor, |FRAME: PD00440 FecI|; FecR transmits a 
                     signal that is initiated by ferric chloride binding to the 
                     TonB-dependent outer membrane transporter |FRAME: 
                     EG10286-MONOMER FecA|; FecR and FecI constitute a 
                     non-canonical anti-sigma factor/sigma factor pair; the 
                     molecular details of signal transmission remain unclear 
                     (see |CITS: [12732308][17673165]|).
                     FecR is required for FecI-mediated transcriptional 
                     regulation of the <i>fec</i>-encoded ferric citrate 
                     transport genes (<i>fecABCD</i>); |CITS: 
                     [2254251][7752886][7729419]|; (and see |CITS: [9148773]|). 
                     FecR is a bitopic inner membrane protein, with globular 
                     cytoplasmic and periplasmic domains; FecR interacts with 
                     the TonB dependent, outer membrane ferric citrate 
                     transporter, FecA |CITS: [9573190]|. The C-terminal portion
                     of FecR interacts with the N-terminal periplasmic portion 
                     of FecA; the N-terminus of FecR interacts with FecI |CITS: 
                     [10633096]| (see further |CITS: [12813067]|). FecR, in 
                     uninduced cells, decreases interaction of FecI with the 
                     |FRAME: RPOC-MONOMER ""&beta;' subunit""| of RNA 
                     polymerase; the N-terminal portion of FecR 
                     (FecR<sub>1-85</sub>) enhances the interaction of FecI with
                     the |FRAME: RPOC-MONOMER ""&beta;' subunit""| of RNA 
                     polymerase |CITS: [12618442]|. |FRAME: EG12436-MONOMER 
                     RseP| cleaves the transmembrane region of FecR and this is 
                     the last step in a sequential processing cascade that is 
                     required for FecI-mediated transcription of the <i>fec</i> 
                     operon |CITS: [33865858]|.
                     The mutant strain, WA176, contains a nonsense mutation in 
                     codon 19 of FecR and cannot use ferric citrate as the sole 
                     iron source; the missense mutation, S127F, and C-terminally
                     truncated foms of RecR lead to constitutive expression of 
                     the <i>fec</i> transport genes |CITS: [7752886]|.
                     The FecR protein contains an internal twin-arginine motif; 
                     membrane integration of FecR is dependent on the Tat 
                     pathway |CITS: [32015149]| (and see |CITS: [32015148]|). 
                     FecR was transcriptionally upregulated in iron limitation 
                     over iron excess independently of the dissolved oxygen 
                     concentration as determined by RNA-seq |CITS:[ 35777694]|. 
                     Related reviews: |CITS: [16333751][16718597][31187912]|
                     "
