                     /gene="yjhH"
                     /locus_tag="b4298"
                     /product="bifunctional KpLE2 phage-like element; putative 
                     2-dehydro-3-deoxy-D-pentonate aldolase / 
                     2-dehydro-3-deoxy-D-pentonate aldolase"
                     /EC_number="4.1.2.28"
                     /label=yjhH
                     /note="YjhH appears to be a 2-dehydro-3-deoxy-D-pentonate 
                     aldolase |CITS: [23233208]|.
                     A <i>yjhH yagE</i> double mutant can not use D-xylonate as 
                     the sole source of carbon, and crude cell extracts do not 
                     contain 2-dehydro-3-deoxy-D-pentonate aldolase activity. 
                     Both phenotypes are complemented by providing <i>yjhH</i> 
                     on a plasmid |CITS: [23233208]|. Overexpression of 
                     <i>yjhH</i> has been used for metabolic engineering of 
                     glycolate production |CITS: [29038973]|.
                     ArcA appears to activate <i>yjhH</i> gene expression under 
                     anaerobiosis. Two putative ArcA binding sites were 
                     identified 211 and 597 bp upstream of this gene |CITS: 
                     [15699038]|, but no promoter upstream of it has been 
                     identified."
