     gene            complement(4527476..4528582)
                     /gene="nanM"
                     /locus_tag="b4310"
                     /label=nanM
     CDS             complement(4527476..4528582)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="nanM"
                     /locus_tag="b4310"
                     /product="N-acetylneuraminate mutarotase"
                     /EC_number="5.1.3.24"
                     /label=nanM
                     /note="The periplasmic <i>N</i>-acetylneuraminate
                     mutarotase supports the efficient use of 
                     &alpha;-<i>N</i>-acetylneuraminate (&alpha;-NeuNAc) as the 
                     sole source of carbon.  Sialoglycoconjugates present in 
                     vertebrates are linked exclusively by &alpha;-linkages; 
                     once released by sialidases, spontaneous mutarotation 
                     converts the &alpha; anomer to &beta;-NeuNAc, which 
                     constitutes more than 90% of NeuNAc at equilibrium. 
                     However, the spontaneous rate of mutarotation is relatively
                     slow.  Thus, loss of <i>N</i>-acetylneuraminate mutarotase 
                     confers a small growth delay to cells grown on 
                     &alpha;-NeuNAc |CITS: [18063573]|.
                     A crystal structure of NanM has been solved at 1.5 &Aring; 
                     resolution, showing a homodimeric six-bladed 
                     &beta;-propeller.  Site-directed mutagenesis of conserved 
                     amino acids identified Glu209 and Arg215 (positions refer 
                     to the processed polypeptide) as potential active site 
                     residues |CITS: [18063573]|.
                     Addition of NanM increases the activity of |FRAME: 
                     ACNEULY-MONOMER| <i>in vitro</i>; however, the two enzymes 
                     are not colocalized <i>in vivo</i> |CITS: [33895133]|. 
                     <i>nanM</i> is expected to be transcribed in an operon 
                     together with <i>nanC</i> and <i>nanS</i>.  Expression of 
                     <i>nanC</i> is induced by NeuNAc and is modulated by 
                     <i>N</i>-acetylglucosamine |CITS: [15743943]|.
                     NanM: ""<i><b>N</b></i>-<b>a</b>cetyl<b>n</b>euraminate 
                     <b>m</b>utarotase"" |CITS: [18063573]|"
