                     /product="putative fimbrial protein FimI"
                     /label=fimI
                     /note="The <I>fimI</I> gene is located in the <I>fim</I>
                     gene cluster of <I>Escherichia coli</I> and has been shown 
                     to encode a 16.4 kDa noncytoplasmic protein product. 
                     Deletion mutations in <I>fimI</I> produced a 
                     piliation-negative phenotype, however the function of the 
                     FimI protein in pilus biosynthesis has not been determined 
                     |CITS:[12897022]|.
                     <i>E. coli</i> K-12 contains 12 chaperone-usher fimbrial 
                     operons, including <i>fimAICDFGH</i>; a fimbria-lacking 
                     mutant - strain WQM026 - created by deleting all 12 operons
                     has been characterised |CITS: [33863704]|."
