                     /product="bifunctional type 1 fimbriae minor subunit FimF
                     / fimbrial complex"
                     /label=fimF
                     /note="FimF is a minor component of the type 1 fimbriae in 
                     <i>Escherichia coli</i>. Two-dimensional gel 
                     electrophoresis indicated that FimF has a molecular weight 
                     of 18.0 kDa and exists in a 1:100 ratio with the major 
                     fimbrial subunit, FimA |CITS: [2904111]|.  FimF and FimG 
                     are subunits of the tip fibrillum which are thought to 
                     function as adaptor proteins, linking the helical rod 
                     composed of FimA subunits to the the adhesin FimH at the 
                     tip of the fibrillum |CITS: [12842468]|.
                     <i>E. coli</i> K-12 contains 12 chaperone-usher fimbrial 
                     operons, including <i>fimAICDFGH</i>; a fimbria-lacking 
                     mutant - strain WQM026 - created by deleting all 12 operons
                     has been characterised |CITS: [33863704]|."
