     gene            4542718..4544178
                     /gene="uxuB"
                     /locus_tag="b4323"
                     /label=uxuB
     CDS             4542718..4544178
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="uxuB"
                     /locus_tag="b4323"
                     /product="D-mannonate oxidoreductase"
                     /EC_number="1.1.1.57"
                     /label=uxuB
                     /note="D-mannonate oxidoreductase is an enzyme of the 
                     D-glucuronate degradation pathway, reducing D-fructuronate 
                     to
                     D-mannonate.
                     The reaction proceeds via a rapid-equilibrium random bi-bi 
                     + dead-end EBQ complex mechanism |CITS: [4351435]|. Reports
                     differ on whether |CITS: [195622]| or not |CITS: [4402996]|
                     the enzyme is able to use D-glucuronate as a substrate.  
                     Where it was measured, the reaction with D-glucuronate 
                     appears to proceed via a different mechanism |CITS: 
                     [195622]|.
                     The enzyme is induced by both glucuronate and fructuronate 
                     |CITS: [4402996]|; the internal inducer is fructuronate 
                     |CITS: [4603847]|."
