     gene            4546810..4547202
                     /gene="iraD"
                     /locus_tag="b4326"
                     /label=iraD
     CDS             4546810..4547202
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="iraD"
                     /locus_tag="b4326"
                     /product="anti-adaptor protein IraD"
                     /label=iraD
                     /note="IraD is one of several small anti-adaptor proteins;
                     it inhibits proteolysis of the stationary phase sigma 
                     factor |FRAME: RPOS-MONOMER &sigma;<sup>S</sup>| by 
                     interacting with |FRAME: EG12121-MONOMER RssB|, an adaptor 
                     protein that would normally target &sigma;<sup>S</sup> for 
                     degradation by the ClpXP protease |CITS: [18383615]|. Each 
                     anti-adaptor protein interacts with RssB in a unique way 
                     |CITS: [24352426][25988182]|. IraD is a major determinant 
                     of the steady-state level of RpoS |CITS: 
                     [19124769][19820090]|. Increased expression of IraD and 
                     IraP contributes to the stabilization of 
                     &sigma;<sup>S</sup> in <i>aceE</i> mutants |CITS: 
                     [25847996]|.
                     A crystal structure of the RssB-IraD complex has been 
                     solved at 2 &Aring; resolution; the data suggests that 
                     structural plasticity conferred by the flexible linker 
                     region between the N- and C-terminal domains of RssB is 
                     critical for its regulatory function. When bound to IraD, 
                     RssB assumes a compact conformation. The W64, R67, and R70 
                     residues of IraD are critical for interaction with RssB and
                     for <i>in vivo</i> function of IraD |CITS: [30975721]|. The
                     binding interface between IraD and RssB overlaps with the 
                     binding interface between &sigma;<sup>S</sup> and RssB, and
                     IraD outcompetes &sigma;<sup>S</sup> for RssB binding 
                     |CITS: [33346011]|. Expression of <i>iraD</i> is strongly 
                     induced following treatment with hydrogen peroxide; the 
                     induction is independent of the regulator OxyR |CITS: 
                     [11443091]|. Expression is also induced by DNA damage by a 
                     mechanism independent of the SOS response |CITS: 
                     [19124769]|. <i>iraD</i> transcription is upregulated 
                     during the transition from exponential growth to stationary
                     phase |CITS: [19820090]| and is inhibited by H-NS |CITS: 
                     [22408168]|. When placed on a multicopy plasmid, 
                     <i>iraD</i> creates a mutator phenotype |CITS: [15225322]|.
                     <i>iraD</i> was found in a screen designed to identify 
                     genes that improved heterologous lycopene biosynthesis when
                     overexpressed |CITS: [17509919]|. The complex regulatory 
                     mechanisms involved in <i>iraD</i> expression and activity 
                     are independent of |FRAME: PC00010 LexA|/|FRAME: 
                     EG10823-MONOMER RecA| but involve |FRAME: PD03831| and 
                     |FRAME: EG10977-MONOMER| |CITS: [35445706]|. Translation of
                     <i>iraD</i> is negatively regulated by the |FRAME: 
                     EG11447-MONOMER| CsrA. CsrA binding directly inhibits 
                     translation of the |FRAME: MONOMER0-4390| encoded upstream 
                     of <i>iraD</i>, which is translationally coupled to and 
                     thereby affects translation of <i>iraD</i> |CITS: 
                     [28851853]|.
                     <i>iraD</i> mutants are more sensitive to hydrogen peroxide
                     than wild type and are hypersensitive to the replication 
                     inhibitor azidothymidine |CITS: [19124769]|. IraD: 
                     ""<b>i</b>nhibitor of <b>R</b>ssB <b>a</b>ctivity in 
                     response to <b>D</b>NA damage"" |CITS: [18383615]|
                     Review: |CITS: [31197038]|"
                     /translation="MMRQSLQAVLPEISGNKTSSLRKSVCSDLLTLFNSPHSALPSLLV
                     SGMPEWQVHNPSDKHLQSWYCRQLRSALLFHEPRIAALQVNLKEAYCHTLAISLEIMLY
                     HDDEPLTFDLVWDNGGWRSATLENVS"
