     gene            4558815..4559735
                     /pseudo
                     /gene="rpnD"
                     /locus_tag="b4584"
                     /label=rpnD
     CDS             4558815..4559735
                     /pseudo
                     /gene="rpnD"
                     /locus_tag="b4584"
                     /product="putative inactive recombination-promoting
                     nuclease-like protein RpnD"
                     /label=rpnD
                     /note="RpnD (YjiP/YjiQ) is one of five proteins in <i>E. 
                     coli</i> that belong to the ""transposase_31"" family 
                     |CITS: [28096446]|, which is distantly related to the 
                     PD-(D/E)XK nuclease superfamily |CITS: [17584917]|.  It was
                     previously noted that YjiP/Q has similarity to RpnC, which 
                     is encoded within the <i>panBCD</i> gene cluster |CITS: 
                     [8837478]|.
                     YjiP is encoded near the so-called immigration control 
                     region (ICR), which is a variable genomic island that 
                     contains a number of restriction-modification systems 
                     |CITS: [11782494][1316984]|.  The YjiP protein encoded in 
                     <i>E. coli</i> K-12 appears to be prematurely terminated 
                     due to a point mutation that results in a stop codon at 
                     codon 104.  Experiments in |CITS: [26162088][28096446]| 
                     were performed with a repaired version of YjiP (re-named 
                     RpnD), consisting of a 306 amino acid ORF beginning at the 
                     <i>yjiP</i> start codon and ending at the <i>yjiQ</i> stop 
                     codon.  Overexpression of the full-length protein increases
                     RecA-independent recombination, reduces cell viability, and
                     induces expression of the DNA damage-inducible gene 
                     <i>dinD</i> |CITS: [26162088][26618540][28096446]|.
                     YjiP/Q contains a PD-(D/E)XK phosphodiesterase domain 
                     |CITS: [22638584]|, which suggests that the protein may 
                     have nuclease activity |CITS: [26162088][26618540]|.
                     YjiP appears to be involved in biofilm formation.  A mutant
                     with a deletion of <i>yjiP</i> shows a significant decrease
                     in biofilm formation |CITS: [16385049]|. Expression of 
                     <i>yjiP</i> increases 20-fold upon deletion of <i>tqsA</i>,
                     which increases biofilm formation |CITS: [16385049]|.
                     RpnD: ""<b>r</b>ecombination-<b>p</b>romoting 
                     <b>n</b>uclease <b>D</b>"" |CITS: [28096446]|"
