     gene            complement(4559979..4561391)
                     /gene="yjiR"
                     /locus_tag="b4340"
                     /label=yjiR
     CDS             complement(4559979..4561391)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yjiR"
                     /locus_tag="b4340"
                     /product="fused putative DNA-binding transcriptional 
                     regulator/putative aminotransferase YjiR"
                     /label=yjiR
                     /note="YjiR, which contains a helix-turn-helix motif to
                     bind DNA in its N-terminal domain, appears to belong to the
                     DeoR family of transcription factors, and it was predicted 
                     to regulate genes related to antibiotic sensibility |CITS: 
                     [35880217]|.
                     YjiR may have a positive role in <i>csgD</i> expression 
                     |CITS: [32649279]|.
                     Upstream of the <i>yjiR</i> gene, a sequence was found that
                     could work as a transcriptional promoter, and the 
                     transcription of the <i>yjiR</i> gene is affected by DNA 
                     damage |CITS: [35880217]|.
                     The YjiR binding landscape was globally mapped in vivo by 
                     standardized ChIP-seq and quantitatively modeled using 
                     BoltzNet, a biophysically informed neural network that 
                     infers binding energy from sequence data |CITS:[40335485]|.
                     The resulting ChIP-seq binding regions are available in 
                     RegulonDB (<a href=""https://regulondb.cc 
                     g.unam.mx/ht/dataset/TFBINDING/source=GALAGAN"">Galagan 
                     collection</a>), and the corresponding energy matrix and 
                     genomic binding profiles can be accessed at <a 
                     href=""http://boltznet.bu.edu"">boltznet.bu.edu</a> 
                     |CITS:[40335485]|."
