     CDS             complement(4566729..4567775)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="mcrC"
                     /locus_tag="b4345"
                     /product="trifunctional Type IV methyl-directed
                     restriction enzyme EcoKMcrBC subunit / McrBC restriction 
                     endonuclease / type IV deoxyribonuclease"
                     /label=mcrC
                     /note="McrC is the catalytic subunit responsible for DNA 
                     cleavage within the McrBC restriction endonuclease complex 
                     |CITS: [11955073]|.
                     McrC was initially proposed to modulate the specificity of 
                     McrB |CITS: [2203735]|.  McrC stimulates the GTPase 
                     activity of McrB 30-fold |CITS: [9299347]|.  Site-directed 
                     mutagenesis of proposed active site residues has shown that
                     the McrC protein harbors the DNA cleavage activity of the 
                     McrBC restriction endonuclease |CITS: [11955073]|.
                     The N-terminal amino acid sequence of purified McrC has 
                     been determined |CITS: [2050643]|.
                     McrC was thought to be required for the restriction of 
                     5-methylcytosine-containing DNA, but not for the 
                     restriction of nonglycosylated phage DNA by McrB |CITS: 
                     [2664457]|; this phenotype was likely due to the fact that 
                     the <i>mcrB-1</i> mutant allele also leads to reduced 
                     amounts of McrC |CITS: [1316864]|.
                     McrC = ""<b>m</b>odified <b>c</b>ytosine <b>r</b>estriction
                     <b>C</b>"" |CITS: [2664457]|
                     Reviews: |CITS: [1316984][23990325]|
                     "
