     gene            complement(4567775..4569154)
                     /gene="mcrB"
                     /locus_tag="b4346"
                     /label=mcrB
     CDS             complement(4567775..4569154)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="mcrB"
                     /locus_tag="b4346"
                     /product="multifunctional Type IV methyl-directed
                     restriction enzyme EcoKMcrB subunit / McrBC restriction 
                     endonuclease / type IV deoxyribonuclease / Type IV 
                     methyl-directed restriction enzyme EcoKMcrB"
                     /label=mcrB
                     /note="The McrB protein together with McrC forms the McrBC 
                     restriction system |CITS: [2664457]|. The McrB subunit 
                     mediates binding of the enzyme to hemi- and 
                     fully-methylated 5'PuC sites |CITS: [7781618]|. Sequence 
                     determinants for DNA binding have been studied |CITS: 
                     [1317461][9348106][9628366]|. McrB also binds |CITS: 
                     [7781618][9299347]| and hydrolyzes |CITS: [9299347]| the 
                     essential cofactor GTP.
                     McrB contains an N-terminal DNA binding domain |CITS: 
                     [10595586]|, a AAA<sup>+</sup> domain |CITS: [9927482]| and
                     GTP-binding motifs |CITS: [10497020]|. Cryo-EM shows 
                     hexameric ring structures formed by McrB |CITS: 
                     [30521042]|.
                     DNA binding is specific for methylcytosine-containing DNA 
                     and requires both Mg<sup>2+</sup> and GTP |CITS: 
                     [10788324]|. Crystal structures of the isolated DNA binding
                     domain in complexes with dimethylated, hemimethylated and 
                     unmethylated DNA show a novel fold recognizing the 
                     5-methyl-C nucleotide which is flipped out from the DNA 
                     duplex |CITS: [22570415]|. Additional crystal structures 
                     with DNA containing different modifications have been 
                     solved, and McrB's affinity towards these substrates was 
                     measured. Amino acid residues within the binding pocket for
                     the flipped-out modified nucleotide were mutated to 
                     identify specificity elements |CITS: [30194838]|.
                     Site-directed mutants in the predicted GTP binding motifs 
                     of McrB result in reduced GTPase activity and loss of 
                     restriction endonuclease activity of McrBC |CITS: 
                     [9299347][10497020]|. In the presence of GTP, McrB forms 
                     homomultimeric doughnut-shaped complexes |CITS: 
                     [11406597]|.
                     Two isoforms of McrB are produced by alternative 
                     translation initiation |CITS: 
                     [2649480][2203735][1312983][1316864]|. McrB-S, the shorter 
                     isoform, was suggested to bind to McrC and modulate McrBC 
                     activity |CITS: [9736625]|, or to stabilize the McrBC 
                     complex |CITS: [9401036]|.
                     RglB: ""<b>r</b>estriction of <b>g</b>lucose<b>l</b>ess 
                     phages""
                     McrB: ""<b>m</b>odified <b>c</b>ytosine 
                     <b>r</b>estriction"" |CITS: [3024165]|
                     Reviews: |CITS: [1316984][23990325]|"
