     gene            complement(4577726..4578682)
                     /gene="yjiA"
                     /locus_tag="b4352"
                     /label=yjiA
     CDS             complement(4577726..4578682)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yjiA"
                     /locus_tag="b4352"
                     /product="bifunctional P-loop guanosine triphosphatase
                     YjiA / GTPase"
                     /label=yjiA
                     /note="YjiA belongs to the COG0523 subfamily of G3E
                     NTPases.  The apoprotein has low GTPase activity that is 
                     inhibited by metal binding |CITS: [24449932]|.
                     A single metal-binding site within the GTPase domain of 
                     YjiA binds the transition metal ions Zn(II), Ni(II) and 
                     Co(II) with micromolar affinities.  Metal binding induces 
                     oligomerization of the protein |CITS: [24449932]|.
                     A crystal structure of YjiA was determined at 2.4 &Aring; 
                     resolution |CITS: [14696199]|.  The protein folds into two 
                     distinct domains; the structure of the N-terminal domain 
                     suggests the presence of a conserved NTP binding site with 
                     specificity for guanine, which was experimentally verified.
                      A GTP-dependent regulatory function is proposed for YjiA 
                     |CITS: [14696199]|.  Structural analysis of Zn(II)-bound 
                     YjiA shows that the protein binds zinc at four distinct 
                     sites, one of which is near the GTPase active site |CITS: 
                     [24449932]|.
                     <i>yjiA</i> expression is induced in response to mitomycin 
                     C treatment, which causes DNA damage |CITS: [11967071]|. 
                     The <i>yjiS</i> gene defines the left border of the 
                     Immigration Control Region (ICR), and <i>yjiA</i> defines 
                     the right
                     border |CITS: [14744977]|.
                     In a large genetic interaction screen, <i>yjiA</i> showed 
                     genetic interactions with a number of proteins involved in 
                     translation and ribosome biogenesis.  A &Delta;<i>yjiA</i> 
                     mutant shows increased levels of stop codon readthrough 
                     |CITS: [27732863]|."
