     gene            complement(4591441..4591914)
                     /gene="yjjB"
                     /locus_tag="b4363"
                     /label=yjjB
     CDS             complement(4591441..4591914)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="yjjB"
                     /locus_tag="b4363"
                     /product="putative succinate exporter YjjB"
                     /label=yjjB
                     /note="<i>yjjB</i> and <i>yjjP</i> are implicated in
                     succinate export.
                     Deletion of these genes in an <i>E. coli</i> K-12 strain 
                     that has been engineered for anaerobic succinate production
                     decreases succinate production significantly; heterologous 
                     expression of these genes in an engineered strain of 
                     <i>Pantoea ananatis</i> enhanced succinate production under
                     aerobic conditions; heterologous expression of these genes 
                     in an engineered strain of <i>Corynebacterium 
                     glutamicum</i> restored succinate production under 
                     anaerobic conditions |CITS: [28673128]| . YjjB contains 4 
                     predicted transmembrane regions, YjjP contains 5 predicted 
                     transmembrane regions and together these proteins may 
                     constitute a 'split-type' ThrE family transporter |CITS: 
                     [28673128][11881894]|. Homologs of YjjP and YjjB are 
                     present in other gram-negative succinate producing species 
                     such as <i>Enterobacter aerogenes</i>, <i>Actinobacillus 
                     succinogenes</i> and <i>Mannheimia succiniciproducens</i> 
                     |CITS: [28673128]|.
                     A YjjB-LacZ fusion protein is expressed <i>in vivo</i> 
                     |CITS: [2844800]|.
                     <i>yjjB</i> expression is upregulated in response to 
                     challenge by four cationic amphipathic antimicrobial 
                     peptides (AMPs). A <i>&Delta;yjjB</i> strain is more 
                     sensitive than wild type to the natural AMP Magainin 2 
                     |CITS: [24789011]|.
                     <i>yjjB</i> shows differential codon adaptation, resulting 
                     in differential translation efficiency signatures, in 
                     halophilic microbes.  It is therefore predicted to play a 
                     role in the osmotic stress response.  A <i>yjjB</i> 
                     deletion mutant is more sensitive than wild-type to osmotic
                     stress, but not other stresses |CITS: [24580753]|."
                     /translation="MGVIEFLLALAQDMILAAIPAVGFAMVFNVPVRALRWCALLGSIG
