                     /product="putative succinate exporter YjjP"
                     /label=yjjP
                     /note="<i>yjjP</i> and <i>yjjB</i> are implicated in
                     succinate export.
                     Deletion of these genes in an <i>E. coli</i> K-12 strain 
                     that has been engineered for anaerobic succinate production
                     decreases succinate production significantly; heterologous 
                     expression of these genes in an engineered strain of 
                     <i>Pantoea ananatis</i> enhances succinate production under
                     aerobic conditions; heterologous expression of these genes 
                     in an engineered strain of <i>Corynebacterium 
                     glutamicum</i> restores succinate production under 
                     anaerobic conditions |CITS: [28673128]| . YjjP contains 5 
                     predicted transmembrane regions, YjjB contains 4 predicted 
                     transmembrane regions and together these proteins may 
                     constitute a 'split-type' ThrE family transporter |CITS: 
                     [28673128]|. Based on a high-throughput reporter assay, the
                     carboxy-terminus of YjjP is in the periplasm |CITS: 
                     [15919996]|.
                     Homologs of YjjP and YjjB are present in other 
                     gram-negative succinate producing species such as 
                     <i>Enterobacter aerogenes</i>, <i>Actinobacillus 
                     succinogenes</i> and <i>Mannheimia succiniciproducens</i> 
                     |CITS: [28673128]|."
