     gene            4593977..4594654
                     /gene="bglJ"
                     /locus_tag="b4366"
                     /label=bglJ
     CDS             4593977..4594654
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="bglJ"
                     /locus_tag="b4366"
                     /product="bifunctional DNA-binding transcriptional
                     regulator BglJ / RcsB-BglJ DNA-binding transcriptional 
                     activator"
                     /label=bglJ
                     /note="BglJ is a positive DNA-binding transcriptional
                     regulator of transport and utilization of the aromatic 
                     &beta;-glucosides arbutin and salicin |CITS: 
                     [8725214][16207917]|.
                     The expression of the gene <i>bglJ</i> induces the 
                     <i>bglGFB</i> operon via unknown mechanisms. This suggests 
                     the possibility that BglJ controls, directly or indirectly,
                     the expression of the <i>bgl</i> operon |CITS: 
                     [8725214][16207917]|.
                     BglJ is a protein that belongs to the LuxR/UhpA family of 
                     transcriptional regulators |CITS: [8725214]|. It shows a 
                     potential helix-turn-helix motif in the carboxyl-terminal 
                     domain, which has 48% identity and 70% similarity to the 
                     corresponding domain of the RcsB protein |CITS: 
                     [16207917]|.
                     A negative correlation between cellular growth and the copy
                     number of the proteins BglJ has been reported |CITS: 
                     [35694815]|.
                     BglJ was transcriptionally upregulated in iron limitation 
                     over iron excess at 21% and 63% of dissolved oxygen as 
                     determined by RNA-seq |CITS:[ 35777694]|."
