     gene            complement(4594692..4595480)
                     /gene="fhuF"
                     /locus_tag="b4367"
                     /label=fhuF
     CDS             complement(4594692..4595480)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="fhuF"
                     /locus_tag="b4367"
                     /product="ferric-siderophore reductase FhuF"
                     /label=fhuF
                     /note="FhuF is a ferric-siderophore reductase that is able
                     to mobilize iron from ferrioxamine B, ferrichrome and 
                     coprogen |CITS: [14756576]|.
                     FhuF contains a 2Fe-2S iron sulfur cluster |CITS: 
                     [9990318][10322040][19309314][33559753]|. Residues C244, 
                     C245, C256, and C259 are involved in coordination of the 
                     cluster and are required for protein function. The 
                     Cys-Cys-Xaa10-Cys-Xaa2-Cys motif is unusual among 2Fe-2S 
                     proteins |CITS: [9990318]|. Purified FhuF can directly 
                     reduce ferrioxamine B-bound ferric ions <i>in vitro</i>. 
                     The reduced ferrous ion is not bound to the [2Fe-2S] 
                     cluster. The system that regenerates reduced FhuF is not 
                     known |CITS: [14756576]|.
                     His-tagged FhuF has been overproduced and purified |CITS: 
                     [9990318][10322040][14756576]| and structurally 
                     characterized by small-angle X-ray scattering and 
                     paramagnetic NMR spectroscopy |CITS: [33559753]|. The 
                     reduction potential of FhuF has been measured |CITS: 
                     [14756576][33559753]| and was found to be pH-dependent 
                     |CITS: [33559753]|. In a <i>sufD</i> mutant, the FhuF 
                     protein is unstable |CITS: [10322040]|.
                     An <i>fhuF</i> mutant exhibits a defect in the utilization 
                     of ferrioxamine B as an iron source |CITS: 
                     [1392471][9990318]|.  The removal of iron from ferric 
                     coprogen and ferrichrome is significantly decreased in 
                     <i>E. coli fhuF</i> mutants. In an <i>E. coli</i> K-12 
                     strain engineered for the efficient transport of 
                     ferrioxamine B (i.e. expressing the <i>Yersinia 
                     enterocolitica</i> outer membrane ferrioxamine B receptor 
                     <i>in trans</i>), <i>fhuF</i> mutants also show 
                     significantly decreased iron removal from ferrioxamine B 
                     |CITS: [14756576]|.
                     Expression of <i>fhuF</i> is upregulated by iron limitation
                     |CITS: [3323834][1804764]| and repressed by hydrogen 
                     peroxide via OxyR |CITS: [11443092]|.
                     A Fur titration assay (FURTA), which measures the 
                     disruption of Fur-mediated repression of <i>fhuF</i>, has 
                     been used to identify Fur-regulated genes |CITS: 
                     [8107138]|.
                     FhuF: |CITS: [3323834]|
                     Reviews: |CITS: [11931550][23443998]|"
