     gene            complement(4596486..4597517)
                     /gene="rsmC"
                     /locus_tag="b4371"
                     /label=rsmC
     CDS             complement(4596486..4597517)
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rsmC"
                     /locus_tag="b4371"
                     /product="16S rRNA m(2)G1207 methyltransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.1.1.172"
                     /label=rsmC
                     /note="RsmC is the methyltransferase responsible for
                     methylation of 16S rRNA at the N2 position of the G1207 
                     nucleotide.  <i>In vitro</i>, the enzyme can methylate 16S 
                     rRNA within the 30S ribosomal subunit, but not free 16S 
                     rRNA |CITS: [9873033]|.
                     RsmC appears to contribute to the correct duplex formation 
                     of helix 34 in 16S rRNA |CITS: [31972066]|.
                     The C-terminal domain of RsmC is conserved across many 
                     known and predicted <i>N</i>-methyltransferases.  The 
                     N-terminal domain also has some similarity with this 
                     conserved domain, but is missing all the residues predicted
                     to be required for methyltransferase activity |CITS: 
                     [11929612]|.  A crystal structure of RsmC has been solved 
                     at 2.1 &Aring; resolution, confirming structural similarity
                     of the N- and C-terminal domains, and thus domain 
                     duplication.  The C-terminal domain may require presence of
                     the N-terminal domain for proper folding |CITS: 
                     [17576679]|.
                     Point mutants in various predicted active site residues 
                     show reduced activity |CITS: [17576679]|.
                     Review: |CITS: [17389639]|"
