     gene            4598002..4598448
                     /gene="rimI"
                     /locus_tag="b4373"
                     /label=rimI
     CDS             4598002..4598448
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="rimI"
                     /locus_tag="b4373"
                     /product="trifunctional protein N-acetyltransferase RimI / 
                     ribosomal-protein-S18-alanine N-acetyltransferase / 
                     peptidyl-lysine N-acetyltransferase"
                     /EC_number="2.3.1.266"
                     /label=rimI
                     /note="RimI is an alanine acetyltransferase that is
                     specific for |FRAME: EG10917-MONOMER| |CITS: 
                     [6991870][2828880]|. It also functions as an 
                     <i>N&epsilon;</i>-lysine acetyltransferase that targets 14 
                     unique lysine residues in 11 unique proteins |CITS: 
                     [30352934]|.
                     A <i>rimI</i> mutant exhibits a defect in acetylation of 
                     the N-terminal alanine of ribosomal protein S18, but shows 
                     no defect in acetylation of ribosomal proteins S5 or L12 
                     |CITS: [6991870]|.
                     Overexpression of RimI in an acetylation-gutted strain 
                     (&Delta; <i>pta patZ acs cobB</i>) leads to the appearance 
                     of acetylated proteins in an anti-acetyllysine Western 
                     blot. Mutagenesis of a predicted catalytic residue in RimI,
                     Y115A, eliminates the acetylation signal observed with the 
                     wild-type protein |CITS: [30352934]|.
                     RimI and RimJ share C-terminal similarity |CITS: 
                     [2828880][34721364]|."
