     gene            4601213..4601818
                     /gene="osmY"
                     /locus_tag="b4376"
                     /label=osmY
     CDS             4601213..4601818
                     /codon_start=1
                     /gene="osmY"
                     /locus_tag="b4376"
                     /product="osmotically inducible protein Y"
                     /label=osmY
                     /note="OsmY is induced by hyperosmotic stress |CITS: 
                     [3015869][1317380]| and during entry into stationary phase 
                     |CITS: [7934831]|. <i>osmY</i>::Tn<i>phoA</i> mutants show 
                     slightly increased sensitivity to hyperosmotic stress 
                     |CITS: [1317380]|. OsmY confers a growth benefit at high 
                     osmolarity that is dependent on glycerol in the growth 
                     medium and the presence of |FRAME: CPLX0-7653 aquaporin Z| 
                     |CITS: [38908784]|. OsmY is a mobile, monomeric, 
                     periplasmic protein with two flexibly linked BON - 
                     bacterial OsmY and nodulation - domains |CITS: [12878000]| 
                     (BON1 and BON2); the BON1 domain is required for growth at 
                     high osmolarity |CITS: [38908784]|.
                     OsmY is induced by stresses known to cause protein 
                     misfolding (see |CITS: [26003922]| and references within). 
                     Overproduction of OsmY stabilises a highly unstable MBP 
                     mutant; purified OsmY inhibits the aggregation of lactate 
                     dehydrogenase, &alpha;-lactalbumin and, less effectively, 
                     luciferase |CITS: [26003922]|. OsmY is very resistant to 
                     aggregation under a variety of denaturing conditions |CITS:
                     [15033470]|. OsmY is important for the assembly of |FRAME: 
                     G7080-MONOMER Ag43|; purified OsmY promotes the refolding 
                     of the Ag43 &beta;-barrel domain <i>in vitro</i> and 
                     protects it from digestion by exogenous proteases |CITS: 
                     [31369167]|. OsmY affects Ag43 levels only in the absence 
                     of |FRAME: EG10985-MONOMER SurA| |CITS: [34995984]|.
                     A &Delta;<i>osmY</i> mutant shows increased persister cell 
                     formation under antibiotic stress |CITS: [22221537]|. 
                     <i>osm</i>: osmotically inducible |CITS: [1317380]|"
                     /translation="MTMTRLKISKTLLAVMLTSAVATGSAYAENNAQTTNESAGQKVDS
