                     /product="phosphoserine phosphatase"
                     /EC_number="3.1.3.3"
                     /label=serB
                     /note="Phosphoserine phosphatase catalyzes the last step
                     in serine biosynthesis.  The enzyme belongs to the 
                     superfamily of haloacid dehalogenase (HAD)-like hydrolases 
                     |CITS: [16990279]|.  Enzymatic studies were originally 
                     performed using partially purified enzyme from <i>E. 
                     coli</i> strain W |CITS: [14086727]|; assays of the 
                     purified enzyme were performed as part of an investigation 
                     of the HAD superfamily of enzymes |CITS: [16990279]|. 
                     <i>serB</i> is essential for growth on glycerol minimal 
                     medium; the growth defect can be rescued by addition of 
                     serine |CITS: [17012394][3108237]|.  |FRAME: GPH-MONOMER 
                     Gph|, |FRAME: IMIDHISTID-CPLX HisB| and |FRAME: 
                     PGAM2-MONOMER YtjC| were identified as multicopy 
                     suppressors of the conditional &Delta;<i>serB</i> phenotype
                     |CITS: [17884825]|.  Directed evolution experiments 
                     identified mutations that increased fitness and enzymatic 
                     activity of these suppressors |CITS: [23728795]|.
                     Review: |CITS: [26443363]|
                     "
